window.DISTILLED = {"-dfk-L0XFGg":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League's sixth race of the season, at Pocono, produced a sixth different winner in six races as Alan Vaught finally broke through in the No. 33, winning Stage 1, dominating the long middle stretch, and taking the victory when a caution froze the field on the lone green-white-checkered attempt. Pole-sitter Jonathan Osborne tumbled to 29th after a massive late wreck with about eight laps to go sent a truck flying into the catch fence and collected close to half of the 38-truck field. Turn 2 of the Tricky Triangle lived up to its reputation all night, with earlier big ones claiming Dave Mayberry, Greg Klein — who later launched Mike Sobanovski's 'Digital Cow' truck onto its roof — and fan favorite Albert Anderson. Tim Pope recovered from a mid-race steering wheel disconnect to finish second, with Josh Oxendine third, Jonah Long fourth, and hard-charger-of-the-day Chris Zofeld climbing 28 spots to seventh.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Josh Oxendine"],"moments":[{"t":1442,"title":"Booth declares war on Zoom meetings","summary":"While drivers qualify, Alan English goes on an anti-Zoom-meeting rant — 'just fight it out in the street' and 'give him a little blanket party' — as the booth riffs on working from home during qualifying.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1902,"title":"82 spins off Turn 2 — first caution flies","summary":"The No. 82 drifts up exiting Turn 2 and spins, collecting Dustin Wade, while the No. 20 slows to avoid it, goes into the grass, and slams the inside wall with major engine damage.","tags":["mike-everage","dustin-wade","jeffrey-johnson"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2300,"title":"Turn 2 got him again — Mayberry's wild ride","summary":"On the restart Dave Mayberry gets turned in Turn 2 and goes for a wild ride, with Charlie Herkis, John Gallagher, Josh Oxendine, Dustin Wade, Andrew Coffin, and Chandler Paul all tangled in the shenanigans.","tags":["dave-mayberry","charlie-herkis","john-gallagher","josh-oxendine","dustin-wade","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2940,"title":"Klein body-shoves Player into the wall","summary":"The race-long battle between the 92 of Greg Klein and the 18 of Andrew Player boils over in Turn 2 — a little body shove sends Player into the outside wall and out of contention, forcing him to burn his fast repair.","tags":["greg-cline","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3144,"title":"Hard impact in Turn 2 — Jones and the 82 pile it up","summary":"The 82 slides up the track in Turn 2 and triggers a multi-truck melee with Dion Jones' No. 4, trucks docking and diving to escape as Cody Tarrant gets swept in — the booth debates netcode versus dirty air.","tags":["mike-everage","dion-jones","cody-tarrant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4654,"title":"Vaught takes Stage 1 and the ten bonus points","summary":"The lap-40 competition caution ends Stage 1 with Alan Vaught the stage winner over Mike Adamson, Tim Pope, and Jeremiah Burke, while Russ Kilgore snags the last stage point in tenth.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5090,"title":"The Big One erupts off Turn 2","summary":"Right after the stage restart, contact between Greg Klein and the 18 stacks the field five and six wide off Turn 2 — trucks in the wall, one truck climbing on top of another, and a huge chunk of the field collected. Charlie Herkis, freshly interviewed, somehow slices through.","tags":["greg-cline","andrew-player","austin-reeves","andrew-cauthan","john-gallagher","charlie-herkis"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6560,"title":"Klein launches the Digital Cow onto its roof","summary":"A spin in Turn 2 leaves Greg Klein nowhere to go — he slaughters Mike Sobanovski's cow-print No. 34, knocking it 'into next Tuesday' and up onto its roof before it sticks the landing. The hard impact effectively ends Klein's brutal night.","tags":["greg-cline","mike-sobanovski","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6950,"title":"America's Driver runs out of room","summary":"On a late restart Albert Anderson — a top-10 fixture all night — finds the No. 66 crawling off Turn 1, has nowhere to go, and pinballs into the inside wall, wrecking a fan favorite's fantastic run.","tags":["albert-anderson","todd-smith"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7362,"title":"Truck in the catch fence — half the field wiped out","summary":"With about eight to go it all breaks loose: contact between the 01 and 753 snowballs, Robert Jordan's 74 is totaled, a truck goes flying up into the catch fence, and a secondary crash in Turn 3 collects Osborne, Kilgore, Dixon, Zofeld, Smith, Whittenburg, Emig, Kelly, and Endicott — meatball flags everywhere.","tags":["robert-jordan","kelly-keel","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","russ-kilgore","ricky-whittenburg","todd-smith"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7674,"title":"Pope's wheel dies while running up front","summary":"Tim Pope suddenly parks against the outside wall — his steering wheel lost power entirely — and he has to turn it off and back on, then chase the field down and survive a scoring mix-up to salvage his podium bid.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":8104,"title":"Green-white-checkered: Vaught seals it under yellow","summary":"On the only green-white-checkered attempt available, Alan Vaught leads them into Turn 1 before a caution for the spinning No. 25 freezes the field — Vaught wins under yellow for his first victory of the season, making it six different winners in six races and punching his playoff ticket.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","josh-oxendine","cody-tarrant","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1475,"quote":"I'm pretty much anti-everything I don't know if y'all noticed yeah if you have a problem with somebody just just fight it out in the street","context":"The booth's anti-meeting riff during qualifying","gold":4},{"t":6611,"quote":"92 of Klein absolutely just a Slaughter knocks him into next Tuesday sends him onto his roof","context":"The booth reacts as Greg Klein launches Mike Sobanovski's No. 34","gold":5},{"t":7431,"quote":"the 21 goes flying up into the catch fence thankfully he's not going to be mowing any pastures here in the Farmland of Pennsylvania","context":"The booth calls the airborne truck in the major late wreck; the truck's identity remains uncertain","gold":5},{"t":8209,"quote":"he is gonna walk away a race winner and punches his ticket and is secured now in those playoffs","context":"The booth confirms Alan Vaught's caution-frozen Pocono victory","gold":5},{"t":8692,"quote":"yeah my wheel just connected there I moved something on my steering wheel and it just lost all power for some reason then it came I turned it back on it came back on","context":"Tim Pope explains the steering-wheel failure that interrupted his late run","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race decided under caution: the only green-white-checkered attempt was frozen by a yellow (No. 25 spun), so Alan Vaught won without a green-flag finish. Uncertain names: the No. 82 driver is variously captioned 'Michael Edwards' / 'Everest' / 'Michael average' — 'Michael Everett' is a best guess only; the No. 1 driver 'David fight' (finished 8th) is best-guessed as 'David Feit'; the No. 20 is called both 'Jeffrey Johnson' and 'Ethan Johnson' (booth even jokes 'he's got two different names'). Josh Bittner (No. 84) was hyped pre-race but does not appear in the finishing rundown, so he likely did not race. The booth said 'the 21 goes flying up into the catch fence' during the big late wreck, but no No. 21 is in the field — the airborne truck's identity is uncertain (Robert Jordan's No. 74 was totaled in that crash). League is run by Alan Vaught's wife Lori. Full finishing order was read at ~2:37:23 (9443s): Vaught, Pope, Oxendine, Long, Robertson, Kuehl, Zofeld, Fite, Reeves, Chipman top 10. Chris Zofeld was hard charger of the day (+28 spots); Jack Dixon won the random lucky-draw award (finished 16th). Next race: Las Vegas.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"-eP4NsfI6zY":{"recap":"The VRL Truck Series kicked up dust at Kansas Speedway for 100 laps under the lights, and the night opened with a bang: a lap-one Big One triggered when Tim Pope tagged a loose Alan Vaught, sending Mike Everage's 82 sliding upside down along the fence. Pole-sitter Albert Anderson and Pope traded the lead early before long green-flag runs turned the race into a tire and fuel strategy chess match around the lap-50 stage break. A three-wide Big One with roughly 20 to go wrecked Dave Mayberry's night, and a five-wide restart melee later put Kyle Vaught into the outside wall to set up a six-lap dash. Pope held off Anderson's final-lap charge to take the win with one of the most animated celebrations the booth had ever seen from him, with Mike Adamson third and Alan Vaught completing a lap-one-to-fourth comeback. Behind the leaders, a white-flag wreck between Michael Taylor and Ricky Whittenburg collected Josh Bittner and Dion Jones, while Kelly Kuehl and Andrew Coffin tied as hard chargers of the night.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Albert Anderson","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1438,"title":"Lap-One Big One Flips Everage","summary":"Tim Pope tags a loose Alan Vaught off turn two on the opening lap, triggering a pileup that sends Mike Everage's 82 upside down along the outside fence like a turtle and collects Earl Evans and Sean McDonnell.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","mike-everage","earl-evans","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1900,"title":"Pope Dives Under America's Driver","summary":"After early slicing and dicing with pole-sitter Albert Anderson, Tim Pope makes the dive stick on the bottom to steal the lead while the tires still have grip.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3305,"title":"Killer Penguin Paint Job Gets an A++","summary":"The booth marvels at Trevor Robertson's Whittenburg-painted scheme — a toothy 'scariest penguin I ever seen' on the tail and a AAA Broadcasting logo on the truck earn Ricky an A++ from the commentators.","tags":["trevor-robertson","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3652,"title":"Osborne's Great Save Goes Three-Wide","summary":"Contact at the front on the second-half restart nearly wrecks Jonathan Osborne, who wrangles the 81 back under control three-wide between Kelly Kuehl and Greg Klein — 'he was puckerin' too, I guarantee you.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3950,"title":"Net Code Bites Gallagher and Vaught","summary":"John Gallagher's 123 snaps sideways in front of Kyle Vaught in a crash the booth chalks up to net code — the two never looked like they were going to touch — with the field diving low to squeeze underneath.","tags":["john-gallagher","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4090,"title":"Whittenburg's Freebie Pit-Stop Gamble","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg leads a wave of trucks topping off fuel for a shot at making it to the end without a green-flag stop — a signature play the booth notes has won him a race on fuel before: 'Ricky puts his homework in.'","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player","josh-bittner"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4588,"title":"The Big One With 20 To Go","summary":"Three-wide racing down the backstretch sends Andrew Coffin's 10 into the outside wall and touches off a multi-truck melee — Dave Mayberry gets the big end of the stick with Austin Paul, Jonathan Osborne and Greg Dobson swept up in the accordion.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry","austin-paul","jonathan-osborne","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4678,"title":"Anderson Parts the Seas","summary":"Replay from the 99's windshield shows Albert Anderson threading the gap through the Big One untouched — a '99 touchdown run' as the wreck parts in front of him.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5000,"title":"Five-Wide Restart Chaos","summary":"The restart with about 15 to go turns the action up to 11 — five-wide racing, Adamson and Kuehl banging for the lead, contact between the 98 and 07, and Kyle Vaught caught in the outside wall after a bad 'clear' call from his AI spotter brings out the yellow.","tags":["mike-adamson","kelly-keel","jess-vaught","mike-taylor","jack-dixon","josh-bittner","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5558,"title":"White-Flag Wreck Behind the Leaders","summary":"As the white flag flies, Michael Taylor and Ricky Whittenburg have a heavy meeting of the minds near the white line — the 55 loses brakes and suspension and slides up to collect his own teammate Josh Bittner, with Dion Jones snagged up as well.","tags":["mike-taylor","ricky-whittenburg","josh-bittner","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5580,"title":"Pope Takes the Checkers at Kansas","summary":"Albert Anderson gives it all she's got on the final lap but can't run down the 27 — Tim Pope crosses the line for the win at his favorite track with an uncharacteristically animated celebration, Anderson and Mike Adamson rounding out the podium.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6098,"title":"Anderson Dedicates P2 to Turner's 'Release'","summary":"In his podium interview, Albert Anderson dedicates second place to Adam Turner 'regaining his freedom' from a North Korean camp, thanks aunts Edith and Kathy, and celebrates getting the Microsoft Paint scheme off his truck.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3332,"quote":"That's the scariest penguin I ever seen it's got teeth and everything","context":"The booth studies Trevor Robertson's penguin-themed paint scheme","gold":4},{"t":3701,"quote":"he was pucker in too I guarantee you that","context":"The booth reacts to Jonathan Osborne saving the truck in three-wide traffic","gold":4},{"t":4157,"quote":"Ricky puts his homework in y'all better pay attention we'll see how it works out","context":"The booth sizes up Ricky Whittenburg's late fuel-top-off gamble","gold":4},{"t":5584,"quote":"Albert giv it all she's got here trying to kick in that NOS turbo but it's not going to be enough as Timothy Pope comes across the line picking up tonight's race win","context":"The checkered-flag call as Tim Pope holds off Albert Anderson","gold":5},{"t":6090,"quote":"it was a it was all and out brawl that's for sure from uh start to finish","context":"Albert Anderson reflects on finishing second after battling Pope all night","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Broadcast by Triple A (AAA) Broadcasting; race control was Lori Vought (mentioned in booth, not a competitor). 100-lap Truck race with a single stage break at lap 50. Auto-captions garble several names, so best-guess spellings were used: Darland/Darlin/Darling (25), Coffin/Cofin (10), Rancone/Ranone/Rancan (28), Bitner/Bidner (84), Kuehl/Kill (01), the Vought family spellings (33/16 plus race control), and Whittenburg/Wittenberg (55). Car numbers heard on tape: 27 Pope, 99 Anderson, 88 Adamson, 33 J. Vought, 07 Dixon, 01 Kuehl, 69 Dickerson, 6 Robertson, 92 Klein, 14 Eaton, 25 Darland, 10 Coffin, 13 Evans, 84 Bitner, 18 Player, 3 Paul, 28 Rancone, 4 Jones, 123 Gallagher, 98 Taylor, 55 Whittenburg, 16 K. Vought, 79 Gonzalez, 81 Osborne, 29 Mayberry, 23 McDonnell, 82 Everage, 085 Dobson, 7 Long. Finishing order beyond the podium read off the results screen near 1:48:15-1:52:30: 4th J. Vought, 5th Dixon, 6th Kuehl, 7th Dickerson, 8th Robertson, 9th Klein, 10th Eaton. Kelly Kuehl and Andrew Coffin tied for hard charger. 'Chan the Man' was mentioned as unable to make the race; Jeremiah Burke was mentioned only as an Allstar Racing teammate, not in this event. McDonnell, Osborne and Long disconnected late; Mayberry and Dobson were done after using their fast repairs.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"-HOctBLGfO8":{"recap":"In the penultimate round of the VRL Premiere Truck Series season, 22 trucks — most wearing patriotic special paint schemes — took on the 3.4-mile Naval Base Coronado road course in California. Pole sitter Jonathan Osborne and pre-race favorite Dustyn Eaton traded the early lead, but Eaton's missed chicane forced a stop-and-go, and wall contact on the mid-race restart ended his shot at the win. Chris Goans took control from there and, after a four-fresh-tires final stop, held off a furious two-tire charge from Mike Adamson, who spun in the chicane with three laps to go yet closed back to under a second at the line. Goans won ahead of Adamson and Jorge Rincon, flipping the championship: he left Coronado roughly 18 points up on Jacob Alesia heading into the Charlotte finale.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Mike Adamson","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1460,"title":"Goodenough and Alesia tangle on lap 3","summary":"Craig Goodenough and championship leader Jacob Alesia get together in a tight turn early; the booth debates whether it was intentional, and the front-end damage later contributes to Goodenough's blown engine.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":1635,"title":"Eaton bumps the leader — and gives the spot back","summary":"Dustyn Eaton gets into leader Jonathan Osborne, spinning him around, then checks up and hands the position back — a sportsmanship move the booth compares to that weekend's real NASCAR race.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1771,"title":"Osborne finds the wall, Eaton takes the lead","summary":"Jonathan Osborne misjudges a corner and slaps the wall with no contact involved; Dustyn Eaton sweeps by for the top spot six laps in.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2646,"title":"Chicane chaos: Eaton's stop-and-go, Player crashes","summary":"Leader Dustyn Eaton misses the chicane and must come to a complete stop, handing the lead to Chris Goans, while Andy Player crashes and limps to pit lane.","tags":["dustin-eaton","andrew-player","chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3421,"title":"Player's hard hit into the tire barrier","summary":"Replay shows Andy Player going wide and hammering the tire barrier so hard his steering is broken — he wrestles the truck back to pit lane practically steering with the rear wheels, and his night is done.","tags":["andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4441,"title":"Albert's runaway goldfish","summary":"Back from a caution break, guest commentator Albert Anderson claims he's out of breath because his goldfish jumped out of the tank and ran into the parking lot — a running gag for the rest of the broadcast.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5120,"title":"Restart disaster for Eaton","summary":"On the restart after the lap-23 competition caution, Dustyn Eaton surges inside but ends up in the wall with right-front damage, dropping the presumed favorite out of contention as Osborne, Adamson and Alesia pounce.","tags":["dustin-eaton","chris-goans","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5211,"title":"Osborne blasts past Goans for the lead","summary":"On four fresh tires, pole sitter Jonathan Osborne pressures a loose Chris Goans and takes the point, with points leader Jacob Alesia lurking right behind.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6787,"title":"Four tires vs. two: Goans wins the pit war","summary":"Chris Goans's four-fresh-tire stop pays off as the pit cycle shakes out — he blows by Mike Adamson (two right-side tires only) to assume a lead the booth calls 'his race to lose'.","tags":["chris-goans","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7344,"title":"Adamson spins with three to go","summary":"Closing to under two seconds of the lead, Mike Adamson clips the barrels and spins in the chicane, seemingly killing an epic finish — but he keeps the truck alive and holds second.","tags":["mike-adamson","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7456,"title":"Alesia and Klein bang doors late","summary":"Battling for fifth in the tightest section of the track, Jacob Alesia and Greg Klein come together — one off the wall, one squeezed right — in what the booth later calls the race's one truly contentious incident.","tags":["jacob-alicia","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7740,"title":"Goans survives Adamson's last-lap charge","summary":"Mike Adamson re-catches the leader and gets within a second on the final lap, but Chris Goans — 'balls to the wall' through lap traffic by his own account — holds on to win at Coronado.","tags":["chris-goans","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":4441,"quote":"Well, you know, I'm a little out of breath. My goldfish jumped out of the tank and took off running","context":"Albert Anderson explains his absence from the booth during the caution break","gold":5},{"t":6797,"quote":"He's got four fresh tires and he just assumed the lead, folks. I think this is his race to lose unless he hits something.","context":"The booth recognizes Chris Goans taking control after the final pit cycle","gold":4},{"t":7355,"quote":"Man, I thought we were going to have an epic race to the end here","context":"The booth reacts after Mike Adamson spins while closing on the leader","gold":4},{"t":7746,"quote":"The one machine of Chris goes is going to bring home the victory tonight","context":"The winning call for Chris Goans after Adamson's last-lap recovery attempt","gold":5},{"t":7969,"quote":"You can be about 18 points in front as leader going to the championship race. How does that feel?","context":"The booth frames the title swing in its winner interview with Goans","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is uncertain from auto-captions (heard as Gones/Gomes/Goins/Gollins/Owens); 'Chris Gones' used as best guess — he drives the Blackjack Racing #1 and calls Charlotte his home track. Lead announcer's surname is garbled ('Alan Ba...'); he is a Navy veteran married to Lori, the league's race director/tower official (Lori is not counted as a booth broadcaster). Kyle's surname is heavily garbled (Vaude/Vault/Valk/Watt); he drives the #16 Shokker scheme and appears to be Albert Anderson's son. Tim Pope and Russ Kilgore are league drivers mentioned on air but not in this race (22 starters, 16 finishers). Track is referred to as both Naval Base Coronado Raceway and 'Qualcomm Circuit' (3.4-mile road course, 45 laps, single competition caution at lap 23, local cautions otherwise). This was Round 17 (penultimate); the finale is Charlotte the following Wednesday, where Gones leads Alesia by ~18 points and Albert Anderson must serve a tail-of-field penalty. Points context stated on air: 55 to win, 35 for second, 1-point intervals after.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"0hNNYGrILfc":{"recap":"The VRL All-Star Race brought the league's race winners, last-chance qualifiers, and fan-vote entry Chad McCabe to Talladega for a 100-lap exhibition in Xfinity cars, run in four stages with 50% fuel loads and three fast repairs. Fuel strategy dominated the night: Albert Anderson ran out of gas while leading in each of the first two stages, and Alan Vaught picked through a green-white-checkered Big One that flipped Chandler Paul to steal stage 1. Austin Paul was declared the stage 2 winner after Mike Everedge was mistakenly announced first, and Anderson redeemed himself by winning stage 3 in a four-wide drag race to the line over Everedge. The final stage kept wrecking — Jorge Rincon was collected hard early, Austin Paul and Anderson tangled with no caution, and Chandler Paul was sent flying to bring out a yellow with 10 laps to go. The broadcast cuts off before the final restart, so the All-Star Race winner is never shown on the tape.","winner":null,"podium":[],"moments":[{"t":2755,"title":"Three-wide squeeze brings out the first yellow","summary":"Three-wide racing collapses when contact finds Greg Klein in the middle of the pack — Tony Polk takes hard contact and fan-vote winner Chad McCabe goes for a wild ride to bring out the night's first caution.","tags":["greg-cline","tony-polk","chad-mccabe","jonathan-osborne","mike-everage","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3208,"title":"The Big One flips Chandler Paul on the stage 1 shootout","summary":"Fuel gambles fail on the green-white restart — Dobson and Burke run dry, Tim Pope clips traffic trying to move up, and Chandler Paul goes over on his lid in absolute chaos while Alan Vaught sneaks through to steal stage 1.","tags":["chandler-paul","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","greg-dobson","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jeff-ottinger","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4635,"title":"Anderson runs dry again — Mayberry and Jones hammer the inside wall","summary":"Albert Anderson runs out of fuel from the lead for the second straight stage; the checked-up field wrecks behind him and Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry and Dion Jones go for a brutal ride into the inside wall approaching turn three.","tags":["albert-anderson","dave-mayberry","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5400,"title":"Osborne whips it three lanes in one move","summary":"Jonathan Osborne drops from the wall all the way to the bottom line in one clean sweep — called the most aggressive move of the race by the booth, 'quicker to Dallas.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5815,"title":"Stage 3 melee: Endicott's nasty ride, McCabe left smoking","summary":"The 221 of David Feit drifts up into Greg Dobson's 285 and half the field gets collected — Russ Endicott slams the outside wall, Chad McCabe turns down into Dion Jones, and McCabe comes away with a smoking engine.","tags":["david-fite","greg-dobson","russ-endicott","mike-everage","chad-mccabe","dion-jones","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6290,"title":"Anderson's NOS-button run from 12th to the top five","summary":"Albert Anderson rockets up the outside 'like he's got a NOS button in that car,' going from 12th to inside the top five in one run with Alan Vaught pushing from behind.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6550,"title":"Four-wide drag race decides stage 3","summary":"After contact between Vaught and Everedge the field fans out FOUR WIDE for the lead through the tri-oval; Albert Anderson wins the drag race to the line over Mike Everedge — America's Driver redeemed after running out of fuel twice.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-everage","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6930,"title":"Everedge corrects the booth: Austin Paul won stage 2","summary":"Mid-interview, Mike Everedge tells the broadcasters he didn't actually win stage 2 — race control's replay review gave it to Austin Paul, who confirms it himself in a later interview.","tags":["mike-everage","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":7360,"title":"Endicott turns Ottinger — Rincon's night likely done","summary":"The 57 comes down on the 76 and turns him up into the wall in turn four; Jorge Rincon has nowhere to go as the 76 comes sideways across him, hits hard, and appears out of fast repairs and done for the night.","tags":["russ-endicott","jeff-ottinger","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7878,"title":"'Go Team Limitless — and Dave Mayberry sucks'","summary":"Albert Anderson signs off his booth interview with shots fired at frenemy Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry, to the broadcasters' delight.","tags":["albert-anderson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":8172,"title":"Paul and Anderson tangle — and no caution comes out","summary":"Austin Paul's 3 snags the rear bumper of the 82 and bounces down into Albert Anderson's 2 — both stage winners go for a wild ride, but with only two cars involved iRacing keeps it green.","tags":["austin-paul","albert-anderson","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":9516,"title":"Chandler Paul sent flying — caution with 10 to go","summary":"An off-square bump draft from the 221 into the corner of the 76's bumper sends Chandler Paul's 72 flying with 10 laps left, tearing off his front cowling and setting up a final shootout the stream never shows.","tags":["chandler-paul","david-fite","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3216,"quote":"they're wrecking we're gonna have a big one oh man chandler paul up on his lid absolute chaos","context":"The booth calls the stage-one pileup and Chandler Paul's rollover","gold":5},{"t":6303,"quote":"flying up like he's got a nos button in that car man oh man flying up through that outside","context":"The booth reacts to Albert Anderson charging through the outside lane","gold":4},{"t":6563,"quote":"four wide for the lead here comes anderson in that third lane oh man we were four wide","context":"The stage-three drag race fans across the Talladega tri-oval","gold":5},{"t":7892,"quote":"go team limitless and dave mayberry sucks shots fired i love it","context":"Albert Anderson signs off his booth interview with a shot at Dave Mayberry","gold":5},{"t":9523,"quote":"big contact behind him the 72 goes flying and that's going to bring out the caution here with 10 laps to go","context":"The booth calls the final caution shown before the source broadcast ends","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Broadcast/transcript ends at 2:44:59 (matching the 9900s video duration) with roughly 8-10 laps remaining — the field had just made final pit stops after the caution with 10 to go — so no race winner is ever declared on the tape. Stage winners on tape: Alan Vaught (stage 1), Austin Paul (stage 2, initially mis-announced as Mike Everedge), Albert Anderson (stage 3). Name spellings for 'David Feit' (#221) and 'Jeff Ottinger' (#76) are best guesses from heavily garbled captions. Car numbers heard: Vaught 33, Anderson 2, Pope 728, Everedge 82, Burke 753, Dobson 285, Adamson 51, Mayberry 29, Rincon 28, Jones 4, A. Paul 3, C. Paul 72, Ottinger 76, Polk 222, Fight 221, Osborne 81, McCabe 211, Endicott 57, Klein 92, Kilgore 7, Klafka 11. Teams referenced: Limitless (Anderson, Pope, Burke, Dobson, Adamson), Goodwiser (Everedge, Rincon), Cult of Chaos (A. Paul, C. Paul), Vigilante Force (Vaught). Race admin: Lori/Laurie. A driver called 'Ellis' (described as last season's champion) was expected but never showed. Format: 100 laps at Talladega in Xfinity cars, stages of laps 1-20/21-40/41-60/61-100, 50% fuel, unlimited tires, three fast repairs; exhibition, not for points.","resultConfidence":"winner-unknown-or-multi-stage"},"0IrM09fCcbo":{"recap":"Race #4 of VRL Season 10 brought the Gen 6 cup cars to Talladega Superspeedway for 94 laps, and the 35-car field pulled off the near-impossible: green to checkered without a single caution. Scott Rooney took the pole at 52.511, but the night's only spin came early when Kyle Vaught grabbed the lead on lap 7 and was immediately turned off Rooney's nose, dropping him from the front row to a lap down. Alan Vaught controlled long stretches with Kelly Cole welded to his bumper until a pit-road tangle with Jeremiah Burke split them up, and Ricky Whittenburg and Albert Anderson also took turns at the point through three rounds of green-flag stops. With five to go, Alan Vaught rocketed back to the front off a push from lapped teammate Dave Mayberry, traded the lead with Anderson twice, and won a photo finish over Dustyn Eaton by 0.039 seconds — his second straight superspeedway win. Anderson settled for third after deciding not to risk wrecking the field on the final run to the stripe.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Dustyn Eaton","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":1956,"title":"Green flag on 94 caution-free laps","summary":"Rooney leads the field to green from the pole; nobody knows yet this one runs flag-to-flag without a yellow.","tags":["scott-rooney","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2252,"title":"Kyle Vaught leads, then gets spun","summary":"Kyle Vaught crosses over to take the lead on lap 7, then gets turned off Scott Rooney's nose just past start/finish — no wall contact, but he loses the draft and goes a lap down. The race's only spin.","tags":["kyle-vaught","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2497,"title":"Cole wears the paint off Vaught's bumper","summary":"Kelly Cole pushes race leader Alan Vaught relentlessly, 'wearing the paint off the back bumper' lap after lap in a tandem the booth keeps waiting to go wrong.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2574,"title":"Chandler Paul: 35th to 12th in 13 laps","summary":"Starting shotgun on the field, Chandler Paul gains 22 positions in the first 13 laps with a monster charge up the gut.","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2684,"title":"Triple tandem assault on the leader","summary":"Anderson, Klein and Everage go bumper-to-bumper-to-bumper — a dangerous triple tandem — but still can't pry the lead away from Alan Vaught's Mobil 1 Mustang.","tags":["albert-anderson","chris-klein","mike-everage","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3155,"title":"Land rush to pit lane turns to chaos","summary":"First green-flag stops at lap 25: Jeremiah Burke spins on pit lane and clips Albert Anderson, Kelly Cole loses eight seconds in an incident, and Chris Klein gets a speeding penalty that puts him a lap down.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson","chris-klein","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3943,"title":"Whittenburg takes the point","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg jumps out to the race lead past Alan Vaught as both lanes prove viable at the front.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4295,"title":"'One podcast, no championships'","summary":"After the booth compares the second pack's strategy to Denny Hamlin giving 70 percent, chat fires back: 'Denny Hamlin — one podcast, no championships.' The booth cracks up.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6194,"title":"Everage hammers the wall — and no yellow","summary":"Replays show Chandler Paul crashing and Mike Everage hitting the wall with a broken right front, yet the caution stays in the pocket — 'darn lucky we didn't get a yellow.'","tags":["mike-everage","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6525,"title":"Deals made: Vaught rockets to the front","summary":"With five to go, Alan Vaught blasts back to the race lead off the nose of lapped teammate Dave Mayberry, then trades the top spot with Anderson in a seesaw battle to the white.","tags":["jess-vaught","dave-mayberry","albert-anderson","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6686,"title":"Photo finish: Vaught by 0.039 seconds","summary":"Vaught and Anderson take the white flag side by side; a huge Mayberry push crosses Vaught up in turn three, but he beats Dustyn Eaton to the stripe by 0.039 seconds for his second straight win.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","albert-anderson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7013,"title":"'You got to let Jesus take the wheel'","summary":"In victory lane, Vaught credits lapped teammate Dave Mayberry — 'not always the most comfortable pusher' — saying he told him to let loose and let Jesus take the wheel, and reveals Kelly Cole's race unraveled after hitting Burke on pit road.","tags":["jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3155,"quote":"Del Co jumps out of line and here comes the field it's a land rush to pit Lane","context":"The booth calls the first green-flag pit cycle as the pack dives for service","gold":4},{"t":4295,"quote":"Denny Hamlin one podcast no championships he's not wrong","context":"The booth reads a chat-line jab during the long green run","gold":4},{"t":6535,"quote":"Allan V Rockets to the front off the nose of Dave Mayberry and just like that the outside Lane starting to come back together","context":"The booth calls Vaught's charge back to the lead with four laps remaining","gold":5},{"t":6745,"quote":"coming to the stripe it's going to be a photo finish at the line","context":"The booth calls the finish that the scoring screen recorded as Vaught over Eaton by 0.039 seconds","gold":5},{"t":7058,"quote":"he's not always the most comfortable Pusher but I said man you just got to let loose you got to let Jesus Take the Wheel","context":"Vaught credits lapped teammate Dave Mayberry for the decisive late push","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is a phonetic best guess: captions render it 'VA', 'vot', 'bot', 'VOD', 'B', and 'F' — 'Vaught' fits all variants and the family (wife Lori, son Kyle, Kyle's fiancee Taylor Provax all referenced). However, both Anderson and Eaton call the winner 'Jess' in interviews, so his real first name may be Jess/Jesse rather than Allen (Allen could be the iRacing account name). 'Kelly Cole', 'David Feit', 'Craig Goodenough', 'Joe Canales', and 'Dion Jones' are also caption-inferred spellings. Full finishing order was read on air at ~2:07:37 (7657s): Vaught, Eaton, Anderson, Player, Whittenburg, Robertson, Pope, Adamson, Dixon, Gallagher top 10; Mike Everage finished 35th, 23 laps down. Derek Welch and Zach Miller are league drivers mentioned in chat but did not race tonight; a 'Bitner' (Team Tang) was also named as absent. Video uploaded Dec 2024 but booth calls it Season 10 Race 4, an offseason series mixing trucks and Gen 6 cup cars. Race ran entirely caution-free; the lap 7 Kyle Vaught spin drew no yellow.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"0kkSeqC3mI8":{"recap":"Dustyn Eaton stuck the No. 14 on the pole at 1:17.60 and went essentially wire-to-wire to win Round 2 of Season 12 at Sonoma Raceway, a 57-lap, 113-mile road course battle. Team Tang played the strategy of the night, with Eaton, Craig Goodenough, and Chris Goans diving onto pit road at the last possible moment before the lap-29 competition caution — Eaton cycled out right behind the pace truck and never gave up the lead. The second half turned into a teammate duel, Goodenough hounding Eaton's sliding rear tires inside half a second over the closing laps before settling for second, the Team Tang pair finishing some 22 seconds clear of third-place David Feit, back from a league hiatus. Attrition was brutal: Jeremiah Burke and Mike Everidge both blew engines in the same corner, Scott Milner and Kevin Hunt tangled early, Greg Dobson pounded the wall, and Chris Goans wrecked out of third in the final laps moments after the booth praised his race.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Craig Goodenough","David Feit"],"moments":[{"t":985,"title":"The foot cam, 'just for Dustin'","summary":"Andrew Player debuts a foot cam with a shout-out to Dustyn Eaton; Ricky cracks 'I usually have to pay a lot of money for this' and the booth swaps SVG foot-cam stories.","tags":["andrew-player","dustin-eaton"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1375,"title":"Green flag: Eaton spins the tires, contact with the 81","summary":"Polesitter Dustyn Eaton lights up the tires on the start, makes contact with Jonathan Osborne's 81 up the hill, drifts the truck and still clears him to keep the lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1545,"title":"Milner and Hunt in a big one","summary":"Scott Milner gets off track before the final turn and comes back across the racing line into Kevin Hunt, who has nowhere to go — big early crash for both.","tags":["scott-milner","kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1680,"title":"Burke blows up into the tire barrier","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets loose, noses the barrier hard and the puff of smoke says it all — blown engine, night over. He joins the booth minutes later to talk it through from the couch.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2686,"title":"Fight takes the lead into turn five","summary":"During the pit cycle David Feit challenges Jonathan Osborne's 81 for the lead heading down into turn five and completes an impressive pass — neither truck had pitted yet.","tags":["david-fite","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3616,"title":"Team Tang's perfectly timed pit call","summary":"Eaton, Goodenough, and Goans duck onto pit road at the last second before the lap-29 competition caution; Eaton exits right behind the pace truck and retains the lead — the strategy call that decides the race.","tags":["dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4135,"title":"Dobson hard into the wall","summary":"Greg Dobson slams the wall hard — 'that's going to leave a mark on that Phoenix strip' — heavy left-front damage and nine minutes of repairs on pit lane.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4200,"title":"Everidge blows an engine in Burke's corner","summary":"Mike Everidge blows his engine in the exact same corner of the S's that ended Jeremiah Burke's night, parking a second truck with the same failure.","tags":["mike-everage","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5480,"title":"Pope crashes battling the No. 1","summary":"Tim Pope, up seven spots and running a shock top-five on a road course he hates, crashes while battling David Feit — contact in turn 11 that Fight later apologizes for on air.","tags":["timothy-pope","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5525,"title":"Teammate duel for the win turns spicy","summary":"Craig Goodenough closes within half a second and forces Dustyn Eaton to abuse his rear tires lap after lap; the booth splits their picks as the Team Tang teammates decide the race between themselves.","tags":["dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5737,"title":"Announcer's curse strikes Goans","summary":"Seconds after the booth notes Chris Goans' strategy has cycled him back out in third, he wrecks on cold tires — 'Oh my god, I just jinxed him.'","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6090,"title":"Eaton wins wire-to-wire in Wine Country","summary":"Goodenough concedes in the final laps rather than risk wrecking his teammate, and Dustyn Eaton brings the 14 home for the Sonoma win — a Team Tang 1-2 that beat the rest of the field by 22 seconds, with David Feit third.","tags":["dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":988,"quote":"I usually have to pay a lot of money for this. So, you're getting it free here","context":"Ricky Whittenburg reacts to Andrew Player's special foot-cam feed","gold":4},{"t":4138,"quote":"Greg Dobson hard into the wall. That's going to leave a mark on that Phoenix strip.","context":"The booth calls Dobson's heavy road-course impact","gold":4},{"t":5737,"quote":"This this may have worked out pretty well for Chris Gones, actually. He somehow has pitted and he's come back out in third. Oh my god, I just jinxed him. He wrecked.","context":"The announcer's praise lands immediately before Goans goes off on cold tires","gold":5},{"t":6093,"quote":"It's going to be your 14 truck winning at Soma here in Wine Country.","context":"The booth calls Dustyn Eaton's Sonoma victory","gold":5},{"t":6126,"quote":"beat the entire field by 22 seconds.","context":"The booth measures Team Tang's one-two dominance over the rest of the field","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions were heavily garbled. 'Chris Gomes' spelling uncertain — captions alternate Gomes/Gones/Goens. 'David Feit' spelling uncertain (could be Fite). 'Kyle Vault' appears as Vaude/Bot/Vot. The 14th qualifier heard as 'John McDonn' is assumed to be Sean McDonnell (#23 truck). Tom Barish qualified 31st but the booth suggested he did not take the green flag. Dillon Bryant (3rd in points) was watching from the chat while sick, not racing. Derek Welch and Scott Milner disconnected mid-race. 'Lori' is the race admin and league co-organizer (host Alan's wife), not a driver. Host's surname heard as 'Vaude' — spelling uncertain. Championship points entering the race: 1st Craig Goodenough, 2nd Jason Gaines, 3rd Dillon Bryant.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"0TYPJE8g5SY":{"recap":"Round 5 of the VRL Premiere Series Season 12 brought the trucks to Iowa Speedway for the Iowa 150 — 177 laps and 150 miles on freshly patched pavement. After a caution-free opening run of roughly 40 laps, the night dissolved into a spin-fest of some 13-14 cautions, most of them self-spins off the treacherous new-asphalt transition exiting turn four. Points leader Craig Goodenough looked like the truck to beat until rear-end damage in a mid-race restart wreck turned his truck evil and dropped him from contention, while three-time champion Tim Pope was collected late when Mike Everage's 82 snapped loose underneath him. Josh Bittner gambled on track position with tires roughly 20 laps older than his rivals and led deep into the closing stages, but Dillon Bryant ran him down and completed a slide-job pass for the lead with seven to go. Bryant survived one final restart to win in his No. 51 Superman truck, with Bittner second and Dustyn Eaton smacking the wall on the last lap yet still holding off Chris Goans for third.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Josh Bittner","Dustyn Eaton"],"moments":[{"t":1063,"title":"Green flag: Player and Pope duel for the lead","summary":"The race goes green with pole sitter Andy Player getting the jump over Tim Pope, the two fighting side by side out front while Derek Welch stalks in third.","tags":["andrew-player","timothy-pope","derek-welch"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2040,"title":"40-lap green run ends: Burke and Fight spin off turn four","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets loose on the top side entering turns three and four and he and David Feit both slide down through the infield, ending the caution-free opening run and triggering the first round of pit stops.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","david-fite"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2312,"title":"Three-wide restart chaos collects Kyle Vault","summary":"On the lap-46 restart it goes three wide for the lead behind them; Kyle Vault checks up hard, gets tagged from behind (Osborne apologized on comms), and the 84 and 01 pile in. Kyle jumps on the booth line afterward to explain.","tags":["kyle-vaught","jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2875,"title":"Kelly Kuehl hooked into the outside wall","summary":"A camouflaged light-gray truck stalled against the old asphalt causes a checkup; the 434 gets into Kelly Kuehl and turns him hard into the outside wall, leaving him roughly a minute of repairs on pit lane.","tags":["kelly-keel","kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2940,"title":"Ricky's wrong-mic rookie mistake","summary":"Ricky realizes he's been broadcasting through the wrong microphone all night — 'a rookie mistake from a broadcaster that's done this for 25 years' — and the chat piles on, with Josh Bittner asking if anyone has a bed pan to lend.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3925,"title":"Kyle's pick move backfires, Mayberry pays the price","summary":"Kyle Vault swings to the bottom using John Schoenbachler as a pick, misjudges it and clips him, sending Dave Mayberry into the wall — the incident Mayberry stews over for the rest of the night.","tags":["kyle-vaught","john-schoenbachler","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4719,"title":"Half the field gambles: tire strategy splits down the middle","summary":"The top 15 — including Goodenough, Pope, Bryant, Eaton and Osborne — all stay out on lap-84 tires banking on cautions, while Bittner, Wade, Adamson and the rest take fresh rubber. The booth calls it an unusual half-and-half split that will decide the race.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope","josh-bittner","dustin-wade","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5170,"title":"Points leader Goodenough crinkles the rear","summary":"A restart wreck erupts behind the leaders: Deion Jones goes around, Jack Dixon noses the outside retaining wall, and championship leader Craig Goodenough picks up rear-end damage that makes his truck 'evil' and drops him from third to 14th with no fast repairs available.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dion-jones","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5948,"title":"Pope junked as the 82 snaps loose off four","summary":"Mike Everage's 82 snaps loose coming off the turn-four pavement transition with Tim Pope underneath him; Everage backs into the inside retaining wall and Pope collects heavy right-rear damage, ending the three-time champion's shot at the win.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6135,"title":"Mayberry's 'Kyle Vault's getting a penalty' sign","summary":"Dave Mayberry tells the booth a 'relative of Ricky's' wrecked him, admits he's been driving up beside Kyle Vault revving his engine in protest, and holds up a homemade sign reading 'Kyle Vault's getting a penalty' to the camera.","tags":["dave-mayberry","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":7013,"title":"Bryant slide-jobs Bittner for the lead with seven to go","summary":"On the restart Dillon Bryant hounds leader Josh Bittner's 20-lap-older tires, drives to the inside, and completes a clean slide-drive pass for the lead with seven laps remaining — the race-winning move, done without contact.","tags":["dylan-bryant","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7330,"title":"Bryant survives the final restart to win the Iowa 150","summary":"Dillon Bryant holds off Josh Bittner over a final two-lap restart while Dustyn Eaton 'murders the wall' on the last lap and still holds off Chris Goans for third; Bryant crosses the stripe head in hands, then plows the cornfield in celebration.","tags":["dylan-bryant","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2946,"quote":"I just realized I had the wrong microphone on.","context":"Ricky discovers that the broadcast has been using the wrong microphone.","gold":2},{"t":5954,"quote":"Oh, and he's wrecked. He's getting wrecked.","context":"The booth reacts as the No. 82 snaps loose with Tim Pope underneath during the late caution sequence.","gold":4},{"t":7045,"quote":"51's getting by inches here. He's getting on those. He's going to be clear. He's going to do a slide drive. He is around.","context":"Dillon Bryant completes the decisive late pass on Josh Bittner with seven laps remaining.","gold":5},{"t":7361,"quote":"We're on board with Dylan Bryan as he's coming around to take the checkered flag. He's got it. Great win for the 51 there.","context":"The live call confirms Dillon Bryant taking the checkered flag at Iowa; the transcript renders his surname as Bryan.","gold":5},{"t":7372,"quote":"It looks like Josh Bidder comes in second. Dustin Eden comes home third.","context":"The booth calls second and third at the finish; the transcript spellings correspond to Josh Bittner and Dustyn Eaton.","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and full podium are explicitly stated on the tape (Bryant / Bitner / Eaton). Caution count is loose: the booth counts 'our 13th caution' late and Bitner's interview says 'about 14 cautions tonight.' Auto-captions garble many surnames, so several names are best guesses: Jorge Rincon (heard Vinccon/Rencon/RCON/Rome), Mike Everage (heard Ever/average/Ambridge — 82 truck), David Feit, Kelly Kuehl (heard Hely Kill — 01 truck), Kyle Vault (heard Va/Bot — 16 truck), Andrew Cawthon (heard Cawin/Cawan/Cawton — 10 truck), John Schoenbachler (many variants — 12 truck), Tony Benfield (heard Stony/Sony — 75 truck), lead broadcaster Alan Vaude (surname uncertain). Race admin Lori (Alan's wife) runs the league, posted on-screen messages, and set several single-file restarts; she is neither a driver nor a booth commentator. Albert Anderson entered but parked at the start for last-place points and did not race. Championship context stated pre-race: Goodenough leads with 81 points, Pope 77, rookie Goins one point back in third.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"1FRoEwSmjQM":{"recap":"Championship night at Auto Club Speedway closed out the VRL truck season, with rookie John Ellis arriving with the title already locked up and leaving as league champion. The real fight was for second in the standings, where defending champion Tim Pope and Alan Vaught entered separated by a single point. Vaught was collected in an early three-wide wreck that also ended pole sitter Jonathan Osborne's night, then clawed all the way back to finish second in the race. Pope won the season finale to lock down the runner-up spot in points, with Ellis crossing third and Albert Anderson charging to fourth on the final lap. Outside the scheduled lap-62 competition caution the race ran green all night, and the league moves to Xfinity cars next season.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Alan Vaught","John Ellis"],"moments":[{"t":963,"title":"Turner Finds Out He's Live","summary":"Pit reporter Adam Turner gets caught mid-conversation not knowing he's on air — 'am I live? is this thing on? we've only done 400 of these' — blaming the spaceship in New Hampshire running the broadcast.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2527,"title":"Billy Joel Just Wrecked the 33","summary":"Three-wide racing goes wrong: the No. 33 of title contender Alan Vaught gets wrecked with Jonathan Osborne involved, and it stays green under the admin-only caution rules. Vaught spends the rest of the night fighting back to second.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","john-ellis","dale-adamson","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2662,"title":"Pole Sitter Osborne Meatballed Out","summary":"Jonathan Osborne catches the tail end of the crash, takes heavy damage and a meatball flag, burns two fast repairs and is done for the night — his second straight championship race he's wrecked out of, as 'Chachi' laments from YouTube chat.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4182,"title":"Adamson Steals the Fake Stage Win","summary":"Mike Adamson's early short-pit strategy pays off as the competition yellow flies on lap 62 with the 51 out front, picking up the halfway 'fake stage win' over John Ellis.","tags":["mike-adamson","john-ellis"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4421,"title":"Dustin Misses His Pit Box Entirely","summary":"Under the competition caution, Dustin Riehle comes down pit road and blows straight past his pit box — 'he rolled snake eyes shooting dice in Waco' — forcing another trip around and dropping him to the back.","tags":["dustin-reilly"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4510,"title":"Boogity Boogity Restart, Two Lead Changes in One Lap","summary":"Spectator Greg Dobson calls 'boogity boogity boogity' from the iRacing client as the field goes back green after the competition caution — Pope and Ellis swap the lead twice on the restart lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-ellis","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4556,"title":"Three-Wide Squeeze Ends Dustin's Night","summary":"Right after the restart, trucks get squeezed three wide — Dustin Riehle is put as far into the wall as he can go, with Robert Jordan and a previously clean Dion Jones collected. Riehle tows to the pits and disconnects for the night.","tags":["dustin-reilly","robert-jordan","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4861,"title":"Kilgore Tagged Into the Wall, Somehow Saves It","summary":"The field nearly goes four wide, the No. 7 gets tagged and sent up into the wall, but Russ Kilgore and Jeff Ottinger both pull off huge saves — the booth notes that in next season's Xfinity cars that's a guaranteed pileup.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5109,"title":"Vaught Slide-Jobs the 51","summary":"Alan Vaught sends a dirt-track-style slide job down into the corner on Mike Adamson, trading a quarter-panel bump before finally clearing the Bass Pro Chevy on his charge back toward the front.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5770,"title":"Jordan Hard Into the Wall","summary":"Robert Jordan's No. 204 slams the wall hard right in front of leader John Ellis, who has to check up — letting Tim Pope close the gap with about 30 laps to go.","tags":["robert-jordan","john-ellis","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7038,"title":"Anderson's Final-Lap Charge to Fourth","summary":"America's Driver Albert Anderson, half a second a lap faster, runs down the Rincon–Adamson battle and slices past both on the last lap to steal fourth in the purple Shooting Dice in Waco Toyota.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-adamson","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7051,"title":"Pope Wins the Finale as Ellis Is Crowned Champion","summary":"Tim Pope takes the white flag with clean air and cruises home to win the last race at Auto Club, sealing second in the championship, while Alan Vaught and champion John Ellis complete the podium.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":986,"quote":"broadcasting am i live is this thing working is this thing on we've only done 400 of these","context":"Pit reporter Adam Turner realizes mid-conversation that he is already live on the championship broadcast.","gold":3},{"t":2542,"quote":"oh just wrecked the 33. oh we probably need a caution for that","context":"The booth reacts to the early three-wide incident involving Alan Vaught's No. 33.","gold":4},{"t":4510,"quote":"boogie boogie boogity let's go racing boys and here we go","context":"The field returns to green after the scheduled competition caution.","gold":3},{"t":5130,"quote":"that's essentially what you do you just send it on down into the inside just like jess is doing now","context":"Alan Vaught attempts a slide-job-style move on the No. 51 during the comeback drive.","gold":4},{"t":7096,"quote":"timothy pope changing his luck around to pick up a win here in the final race at auto club","context":"The finish call explicitly identifies Tim Pope as the Auto Club season-finale winner.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Transcript begins at ~12:03 into the stream (pre-race hold before that). Auto-captions garble names heavily: 'Alan Vaught' is a best guess assembled from variants like 'just fought'/'chest vault'/'vaughn'; 'Russ Kilgore' was read once as 'Kilbourne' in the initial rundown; Dustin Riehle's surname is uncertain (captions consistently say 'really'). John Ellis is the season champion but Tim Pope won the race itself — don't conflate the two. In his winner interview Pope names his new team as 'lemurs motorsports', almost certainly a caption garble of Limitless Motorsports (the 'big move' the booth teased, and its drivers all finished top five). Greg Dobson appears only as a spectator in this broadcast but is named as joining Limitless Motorsports next season. A 'big special announcement' was teased for after the interviews, but the transcript cuts off mid-way through the Alan Vaught (second-place) interview, so the announcement and full post-race are not captured. Next season the league switches from trucks to Xfinity cars, starting around June 1.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"1igBGoIDgt4":{"recap":"On Thanksgiving eve 2021, the Vigilante Racing League brought its trucks to Nashville Superspeedway for race 10 of 15, with 27 trucks taking the green on a bumpy, tire-eating concrete surface. Polesitter Mike Adamson controlled the race essentially flag to flag, trading the lead with Tyler Green early and sealing it with a daring apron crossover off turn four that the booth called the move of the race. The only yellow all night was a surprisingly early competition caution around lap 42, which turned the second half into a pure pit-strategy chess match. Josh Bittner short-pitted his way to second while Tim Pope gambled on late fresh tires and charged from 11th back to third. Adamson took the checkered flag with a healthy gap for the $25 win, with Tyler Green fourth and Alex Berube completing the top five.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Josh Bittner","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1592,"title":"Green flag — Berube tags the wall on lap one","summary":"Adamson launches from pole as front-row challenger Alex Berube looks outside and snags the wall on the opening lap, handing second to Tyler Green; behind them the 29 caves in Jablonski's rear bumper but everyone keeps rolling.","tags":["mike-adamson","alex-berube","tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2270,"title":"Pope and Tyler Green go a full lap side by side","summary":"Pope and Green run side by side for nearly an entire lap fighting for second before the 728 finally clears the 5 and shuts the door, with Berube tapping Green in the aftermath — and apologizing over the radio.","tags":["timothy-pope","tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2528,"title":"'Barack Obama' joins the YouTube chat","summary":"The booth announces the 44th president of the United States is in the chat saying 'eat or get eaten,' then spends the night fielding his questions, including how to sign up for the league.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2720,"title":"Bittner short-pits into the lead","summary":"The first green-flag pit cycle shakes the whole field up: Bittner's short-pit gamble nets him track position while Tim Pope nearly loses it on pit road, leaving a Bittner-Adamson-Berube top three.","tags":["josh-bittner","mike-adamson","alex-berube","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2933,"title":"Competition caution catches the field off guard","summary":"The pre-announced competition yellow lands on lap 42 — far earlier than anyone guessed — scrambling every pit strategy for the second half with Adamson, Bittner and Berube running 1-2-3.","tags":["mike-adamson","josh-bittner","alex-berube"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3160,"title":"Austin Paul: 'It's like Disney on Ice out here'","summary":"Mid-race booth interview with Austin Paul, up 12 spots, who sums up the slick tire-worn concrete perfectly: after three or four laps you're slipping and sliding like Disney on Ice — save, save, save.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3262,"title":"Adamson's apron crossover — the move of the race","summary":"On the competition-caution restart Tyler Green surges ahead on the inside, but Adamson crosses over off turn four, dives all the way to the apron and slides back into the lead — a move Adamson's winner interview later crowned the move of the race.","tags":["mike-adamson","tyler-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3540,"title":"Dixon and Whittenburg get together","summary":"Whittenburg catches a piece of the apron in turns one and two and slides up the track; he and Dixon make contact and get sideways, with the 15 clipping the 55, but everyone gathers it back up under green.","tags":["jack-dixon","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4238,"title":"Trucks in the wall — Osborne caught in the mess","summary":"A couple of trucks tag the wall and one spins with about 30 laps to go; everyone saves it, but Jonathan Osborne tries to split two slow trucks and is slow getting going, and Austin Paul picks up heavy damage in the aftermath — no caution flies.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4818,"title":"Pope's fresh-tire charge nets the final podium spot","summary":"After staying out longest and taking the freshest tires, Pope runs Berube down and wins a side-by-side drag race for third in the closing laps, capping a charge back from 11th.","tags":["timothy-pope","alex-berube"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4975,"title":"Adamson takes the checkered at Nashville","summary":"White flag flies with Adamson holding a healthy gap over Bittner, who catches lap traffic on the final lap; Adamson cruises across the line for the win and the $25 payout.","tags":["mike-adamson","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2280,"quote":"that's the 5 and the 7 28 still side by side here for almost an entire lap","context":"Tim Pope and Tyler Green sustain a side-by-side battle for nearly a full lap.","gold":4},{"t":2933,"quote":"this is going to be your competition caution it looks like i don't see anybody spinning","context":"The scheduled competition caution catches the booth and field without an incident on track.","gold":3},{"t":3185,"quote":"save your tires because it's like it's like disney on ice out here","context":"Austin Paul describes the rapidly fading grip during his mid-race booth interview.","gold":4},{"t":3299,"quote":"as the 51 looks to maybe cross over the five as the five drifts wide coming out of the corner","context":"Mike Adamson sets up the apron crossover that restores him to the lead.","gold":4},{"t":5012,"quote":"picking up the win here at nashville","context":"The checkered-flag call confirms Mike Adamson as the Nashville winner.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"First ~10 minutes of the stream are pre-race music (stray lyric captions). Race called race 10 of 15 by the booth after briefly saying 11. Full finishing order read at 1:40:47 (6047s): Adamson, Bittner, Pope, T. Green, Berube, Anderson, Oxendine, Wheeler, Burke, Klafka, Hutchinson, Everedge, Rincon, J. Green, Mayberry, Dixon, Whittenburg, Jablonski, Cobasriges, Kuehl, Osborne, Herzig, R. Green, Paul, Jones, Schneider, Riehle. Low-confidence names: #020 driver ('Simon Cobasriges') is heavily garbled in captions; #999 heard as both 'Just Schneider' and 'Jeff Snyder'; #37 heard as both 'Justin' and 'Dustin Really'; George #28 heard as both 'Rincon' and 'Mancone'. 'Mike Leverage' at 19:17 is assumed to be a caption garble of Mike Everedge. A points contender heard once as 'Robertson' (11:49) may be a garbled name of a driver not in tonight's field. Booth pit reporter Adam Turner also warned of a possible connection drop at 1:02:03 but the broadcast stayed up.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"1Q8ew-pLmLY":{"recap":"Round 6 of 18 in the VRL Premiere Series brought the trucks to Darlington for the Widow Maker 200 — 147 laps on throwback night, with just two extra sets of tires and 65% fuel tanks turning the whole race into a strategy chess match. Jacob Alesia snatched the lead from pole-sitter Sean McDonnell at the green, but Tim Pope and Chris Goans emerged as the fastest trucks on the night, trading the point through the pit cycles while Scott Ronnie gambled on early tires and built a huge lead. The race flipped with nine laps to go when Andrew Cauthorn's No. 10 bounced off the wall and collected Pope, and on the ensuing restart Goans was spun battling for the lead with Jonathan Osborne piling in. That set up a green-white-checker shootout in which Stoney Benfield ran down a tire-less Ronnie for his first career VRL win, with Ronnie second and John Schoenbachler third. Remarkably, the notoriously unforgiving Lady in Black produced only four cautions all night.","winner":"Stony Benfield","podium":["Stony Benfield","Scott Rooney","John Schoenbachler"],"moments":[{"t":974,"title":"Throwback night paint scheme parade","summary":"Qualifying doubles as a throwback showcase: Davey Allison, Steve Park Pennzoil, Baby Ruth, Wrangler, Raybestos and more tribute liveries get the booth tour.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","john-schoenbachler","aaron-warren"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1441,"title":"Alesia steals the lead at the green","summary":"Jacob Alesia hangs tough on the outside of pole-sitter Sean McDonnell and takes the lead in turn one on the opening lap.","tags":["jacob-alicia","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1547,"title":"Lap-5 chaos brings the first caution","summary":"Tim Pope comes off the wall, then John McAdam catches the outside wall and the inside wall to bring out the first yellow just five laps in.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2064,"title":"Gordon Spain spins into Dustin Wade","summary":"Gordon Spain loses grip and collects Dustin Wade, who takes significant left-front damage; Kelly Kildea catches a piece of it too. Caution number two.","tags":["gordon-spain","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2404,"title":"Pole-sitter McDonnell crippled by wheel damage","summary":"Sean McDonnell can't stay out of the wall, radios that he has wheel damage and can't turn, and his night unravels from the front row.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3502,"title":"Pope's dirt-track save on pit entry","summary":"Race leader Tim Pope comes to pit lane way too hot and drifts it to the pit entrance without spinning — 'most drivers would have went around.'","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3698,"title":"Robertson wall shot ends Dillon Bryant's night","summary":"Trevor Robertson hits the wall and Dillon Bryant, fourth in points, piles in behind him and is done for the night with wheel damage.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5198,"title":"Chandler Paul wrecks — and no caution flies","summary":"Chandler Paul crashes reacting to the No. 10 bobbling ahead of him as Scott Milner closes fast, but the spin doesn't register and the race stays green — classic VRL Darlington.","tags":["chandler-paul","scott-milner"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5581,"title":"Pope overshoots his pit stall in crunch time","summary":"Chasing down Scott Ronnie's strategy gamble, Tim Pope slides past his pit box on his final stop, giving away roughly two seconds he can't afford.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6163,"title":"Heartbreak: Pope collected with nine to go","summary":"Andrew Cauthorn's No. 10 bounces off the wall and clips race favorite Tim Pope out of contention just as he was reeling in the leaders — 'OH NO, POPE!' Caution changes everything.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6480,"title":"Goans spun from the lead battle, Osborne piles in","summary":"Battling Benfield for the win on the restart, Chris Goans goes around on the backstretch and Jonathan Osborne piles into him — the second race favorite eliminated in minutes, setting up a green-white-checker.","tags":["chris-goans","jonathan-osborne","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6726,"title":"GWC shootout: Benfield's first career win","summary":"On the green-white-checker, Stoney Benfield runs down Scott Ronnie on worn tires while Mike Adamson's charge ends in the wall — Benfield takes the checkers for his first VRL Premiere Series victory.","tags":["stony-benfield","scott-rooney","mike-adamson","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1454,"quote":"And he does. He takes the lead over from the 23 here in the first turn.","context":"Jacob Alesia clears pole-sitter Sean McDonnell for the lead on the opening lap.","gold":4},{"t":3515,"quote":"most drivers would have went around. That was a that was a piece of driving.","context":"The booth praises Tim Pope for saving an over-hot entry to pit road.","gold":4},{"t":6163,"quote":"OH, NO POPE. TURN. >> And caution is out. Oh, no.","context":"The booth reacts when Andrew Cauthorn's wall contact collects Tim Pope with nine laps remaining.","gold":5},{"t":6485,"quote":"What a what a race. Oh, NO HE GOES AROUND. BACKSTRETCH. GO GOINS.","context":"Chris Goans spins from the late lead battle on the backstretch, forcing another restart.","gold":5},{"t":6861,"quote":"And we have a first-time winner here in Stony Benfield","context":"The post-race recap explicitly identifies Stoney Benfield as a first-time winner; the transcript spells his first name Stony.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Captions heavily garbled on names. Third-place finisher's surname is very uncertain — heard as Scheinbachler/Bacqueler/Buckler/Barker; 'John Schoenbachler' is a best guess. Jorge Rincon vs 'George Rankin' also uncertain (both used by the booth). The 47's driver is read as 'John McCauley' in the pre-race penalty list but 'John McAdam' everywhere else including the finishing order — possibly the same driver, treated as one entry. 'Mike Allison' in the grid readout appears to be a garble of Mike Adamson. A driver 'Luis' is mentioned once during qualifying but never again — likely a caption garble, not listed. Lori (Allen Gordon's wife) served as race admin from the tower, not on the mic. Many real-NASCAR names in the transcript (Davey Allison, Steve Park, Jeff Burton, Rusty Wallace, Cale Yarborough, Hut Stricklin, Sterling Marlin, etc.) are throwback paint-scheme references, not participants. Full finishing order was read at ~2:07:37 (7657s); championship standings entering the race: Albert Anderson 138, Tim Pope 129, Chris Goins ('Gomes') 125, Dillon Bryant 100, Jacob Alesia 97.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"1uGYBDLCu4w":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson turned the VRL's 'Chicanes of Madness' at the Charlotte Roval into a one-truck show, wrestling the lead from polesitter Sean McDonnell inside the first handful of laps, sweeping the halfway stage, and even getting the No. 6 up on two wheels through the final chicane on the last lap before winning by about six and a half seconds. The green flag brought instant mayhem, with Jonathan Osborne sideways and a turn-one bottleneck that damaged Dustyn Eaton's No. 14 before the field completed a lap. McDonnell held off a stalking Jess Vogt for second, while Eaton — racing under his wife Annaleigh's name all night — recovered to fourth and drew the random-draw interview. The last lap delivered late fireworks as Andrew Player rode the outside wall and bounced off Mike Adamson, handing Tim Pope a two-for-one pass for sixth, and Greg Klein charged eight spots to ninth as the league heads to Las Vegas for the regular-season finale.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Sean McDonnell","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1457,"title":"Green flag, instant chaos in turn one","summary":"The field slips and slides off the start; Jonathan Osborne goes sideways across the track, the No. 14 finds the wall, and a bottleneck jams the first corners on lap one.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton","trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1764,"title":"Robertson takes the point from McDonnell","summary":"Using every inch of the racetrack, Trevor Robertson works past polesitter Sean McDonnell for the lead he would barely relinquish all night.","tags":["trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2036,"title":"Discord dies, Brown calls the race solo","summary":"The booth's Discord melts down mid-broadcast, leaving Alan Brown rolling through play-by-play alone until English and Turner reconnect and everyone realizes nobody could hear anybody.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3317,"title":"Dickerson dive sends the 10 spinning","summary":"Larry Dickerson dives inside the No. 10, Andrew Cin returns a bump into turn one, and the 10 goes around — things getting serious in the midfield.","tags":["larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4155,"title":"Halfway restart turns into a scrap","summary":"Back to green after the halfway break: Jess Vogt bogs on the curbing, then Mike Adamson gets spun hard after beating and banging with Jeremiah Burke.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4364,"title":"Pope in the tires, Burke spins alongside","summary":"Tim Pope slides through the grass into the tire barrier while Jeremiah Burke spins in the same section, with Greg Klein also in trouble.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4827,"title":"The Derek Welch Invitational forklift race","summary":"The booth dreams up a weaponized forklift race — chainsaws, flamethrowers, lose-a-leg elimination rules — christening it the Derek Welch Invitational as chat groans.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5700,"title":"Cin spins right in front of the leader","summary":"With three laps to go, Andrew Cin goes sideways directly in front of race leader Trevor Robertson in a narrow section, also stacking up Jess Vogt.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5825,"title":"The chicane claims Osborne again","summary":"Jonathan Osborne loops it with two to go as the booth notes the unforgiving curbs have claimed a few victims tonight.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5903,"title":"Two wheels, then victory burnouts for Robertson","summary":"Trevor Robertson bounces the No. 6 onto two wheels through the backstretch chicane on the final lap, saves it, and cruises home 6.5 seconds clear of Sean McDonnell and Jess Vogt for a dominant win.","tags":["trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5938,"title":"Last-lap wall ride gifts Pope a two-for-one","summary":"Racing for sixth on the final lap, Andrew Player slaps the outside wall and bounces off Mike Adamson through the chicane, letting Tim Pope steal both spots at the line.","tags":["andrew-player","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6138,"title":"\"You're not Annaleigh — you're Dustin!\"","summary":"The random-draw interview unmasks the fourth-place No. 14: it was Dustyn Eaton driving under wife Annaleigh's name all night, who insists 'it's all her, I just do the talking.'","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1469,"quote":"oh no this is causing absolute mayhem out here","context":"The booth reacts to the lap-one bottleneck and multiple trucks in trouble at the Roval.","gold":4},{"t":1764,"quote":"it looks like Trevor Robertson is going to take that first position","context":"Trevor Robertson takes the lead from Sean McDonnell early in the race.","gold":4},{"t":5903,"quote":"the final time into that first of two chicanes getting it up onto two wheels able to save it from hitting that infield wall","context":"Robertson gets the No. 6 onto two wheels and saves it in the final-lap chicane.","gold":5},{"t":5926,"quote":"as Trevor Robertson picks up the race win here tonight closely behind for second and third is going to be the 23 of Shawn McDonald followed by the 33 of","context":"The live finish call confirms Robertson winning, McDonnell second, and the No. 33 running third; the following transcript line names Jess Vogt.","gold":5},{"t":6150,"quote":"wait a minute you're not analie you're Dustin oh no it's her man it's all her it's all her I just I just do the","context":"The fourth-place interview reveals that Dustyn Eaton drove the No. 14 entered under Annaleigh Eaton.","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Full finishing order read on air (t~6820): Robertson, McDonnell, J. Vogt, D. Eaton, Burke, Pope, Player, Adamson, Klein, Rancan, Osborne, Kuehl, Dickerson, Mayberry, Cin, Dixon, Anderson, K. Vogt, Dobson, Bitner. Surname of the Vogt family is uncertain — captions render it vot/VA/fought/VOD (could be Vogt or Vought); same for 'Andrew Cin' (possibly Chin/Cain), 'George Rancan' (rancon/ranan), and 'Josh Bitner' (possibly Bittner). The No. 14 was entered under Annaleigh Eaton's name but driven by Dustyn Eaton (revealed in the post-race interview); both are listed in drivers. Lori Vogt was named 16th in the grid rundown but served as race control and does not appear in the finishing order — likely not a competitor. Race was 50 laps at the Charlotte Roval with a planned halfway caution/stage break at lap 25; Robertson won the first stage. Klein was called 'hard charger of the day' (+8 spots). Next race announced: Las Vegas Motor Speedway, regular-season finale. League sponsors read on air: Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry) and GC Cruise Travel (Greg Klein).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"1VX1YWoyH88":{"recap":"The Season 10 finale of the Vigilante Racing League brought the trucks to virtual Auto Club Speedway for 85 laps, and the first half was pure carnage: seven cautions, including a start-line pileup when polesitter Sean McDonnell failed to fire, Greg Dobson going airborne off turn four, and both Russ Kilgore and Anthony Williams landing on their roofs. Ricky Whittenburg's night ended with a monster nose-first hit into the outside wall that the booth said would have required a helicopter in real life. Once the race finally settled into long green runs, Josh Bittner, Albert Anderson, Alan Vaught, and Craig Goodenough traded slide jobs and crossovers for the lead lap after lap. Vaught, who started seventh, proved nearly impossible to dislodge out front and stretched his fuel to the checkers, winning his second race in a row and clinching the Season 10 VRL championship. Goodenough charged from 30th (after a qualifying penalty) to finish second, with Bittner third, and the league rolls straight into Season 11 at Daytona next week.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Craig Goodenough","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1690,"title":"Green Flag, Instant Carnage","summary":"Caution at the initial start — polesitter McDonnell apparently fires off in third gear, the inside lane stacks up, and a pack wrecks at the end of pit lane before turn one.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","andrew-cauthan","chris-klein","kevin-hunt","larry-dickerson","chandler-paul","dion-jones","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2495,"title":"Dobson Takes Flight off Turn Four","summary":"Three-wide with the lapped Everage, net-code contact turns Dobson; air gets under the truck and it nearly goes over on its roof before slamming back down on all four wheels.","tags":["greg-dobson","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2795,"title":"Pope Collected Head-On in Restart Pileup","summary":"Anderson taps Adamson's left rear on the restart, Tim Pope has nowhere to go off turn two, and McDonnell piles in head-on — heavy damage with no fast repairs available tonight.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-adamson","timothy-pope","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3105,"title":"Leader Doesn't Fire, McAdam Eats the Wall","summary":"Race leader Whittenburg fails to launch on the third restart; Burke checks up to avoid beating him to the line and John McAdam gets forced up the track into the wall.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jeremiah-burke","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3175,"title":"Kilgore Flipped While Battling for the Lead","summary":"Side by side with Vaught for the top spot, Kilgore gets clipped down the backstretch, the air gets underneath and he lands on his lid into turn three. Vaught apologized to Kilgore in his winner's interview.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3590,"title":"Williams Right-Hooked Onto His Roof","summary":"Hunt gets into Williams' right rear, contact with Gallagher follows, and the No. 5 goes over onto its lid — the second truck upside down on the night.","tags":["anthony-williams","john-gallagher","kevin-hunt"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4140,"title":"Whose Face Is on All These Trucks?","summary":"John Osborne ('Mr Chachi') pops into chat baffled to see his own face on so many trucks — the booth finally spots the 'inmate Osborne' hood art and it all makes sense.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4533,"title":"Monster Hit for Whittenburg","summary":"Another restart stack-up sends Whittenburg nose-first into the outside wall off turn two — 'if it was real life he'd be leaving here in a helicopter.' The booth follows with a full SAFER barrier explainer.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","dion-jones","chandler-paul","kevin-hunt","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5280,"title":"Slide Job Clinic at the Front","summary":"Bittner, Anderson and Vaught trade slide jobs and crossovers for the lead lap after lap — 'this is how you do it, boys and girls,' with the booth joking they must be John Smoltz fans throwing all those sliders.","tags":["josh-bittner","albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6033,"title":"Goodenough Grabs the Lead, Vaught Snatches It Back","summary":"Banging doors through the dogleg, Goodenough — up from 30th — takes the top spot into turn one, but Vaught crosses back over and reclaims the lead within a lap.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6590,"title":"Vaught Seals the Win and the Championship","summary":"Running 'perfect qualifying laps' and saving fuel to the very end, Vaught takes the checkers over Goodenough and Bittner for his second straight win and the Season 10 VRL championship.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7574,"title":"Peanuts and Coke Confession","summary":"In his podium interview Bittner reveals he ran out of shell peanuts — which he can only crack open under caution — and the booth blames the peanuts for the first-half caution fest, since they're racetrack bad luck.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3183,"quote":"oh and upside down on the roof Russ gilgore makes some contact and Big Time wreck into turn number three","context":"Russ Kilgore is launched onto his roof while battling Alan Vaught for the lead; the transcript renders the surnames as gilgore and VA.","gold":5},{"t":6048,"quote":"Allen VA trying to cross back over good enough just barely off the outside wall in turn number two","context":"Alan Vaught crosses back underneath Craig Goodenough during the decisive late fight for the lead.","gold":4},{"t":6606,"quote":"Allen VA looking for the win Allen VA across start finish he wins","context":"The live finish call explicitly confirms Alan Vaught as the Auto Club winner; the transcript renders his surname as VA.","gold":5},{"t":6946,"quote":"alen V with the championship and the race win here","context":"The post-race return confirms that Vaught paired the season-finale win with the Season 10 championship.","gold":5},{"t":7578,"quote":"I ran out of peanuts and Coke after the uh first half","context":"Craig Goodenough explains why he had to shift from caution-snacking to racing during the long green-flag second half.","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Race #12 was the Season 10 finale (85 laps, trucks) at virtual Auto Club Speedway; Season 11 opens at Daytona the following week. Solo booth: Steve of the 'Track Limits' show on the TLN network; an 'Earl' is addressed about calling cautions over the radio (likely race control/spotter, radio not working) — not counted as a booth commentator. Winner's surname is heavily garbled in captions (VA/vot/bot/fought/VOD); 'Alan Vaught' is a best guess from the caption 'Allen fought'. Other uncertain proper names: Kelly Cole ('Kelly Co/cool'), Joe Canales ('canel/caneles/Canalis'), Andrew Coffin ('cin/coffen/coffin'), Sean McDonnell (introduced once as 'Don McDonnell'). Finishing-order captions garble positions 19-25 ('Mike Adamson was 19 18 Russ Kilgore 20th', 'Dave Mayberry 25th fourth 25th was Chandler Paul'), so mid-pack results are approximate. Alan Vaught's interview also thanks teammates 'Greg Klein' and Mayberry and references his wife Lori and son Kyle (finished 9th); Vaught's win was his second in a row and clinched the Season 10 championship.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"27ODGnImLlI":{"recap":"Chris Goans put on a clinic in the COTA Bull Run 2026, Round 3 of the VRL Premiere Series on Circuit of the Americas' shortened 16-turn west layout, winning from the pole in a 40-lap, 29-truck fuel-strategy chess match. The broadcast's wildest twist came when the halfway competition caution flew roughly three laps early after a scoring-overlay mix-up between booth and admin Lori, reshuffling strategy for the second half. Jack Dixon recovered from a three-wide turn-1 shuffle to finish second, while Jorge Rincon stunned the booth by stretching a 20-lap fuel run — crossing the line with 0.1 laps of gas — to steal third. Points leader Albert Anderson, no road-course lover, started from the pits, parked mid-race to eat a turkey sandwich on pit road, and cruised home 25th, letting Goans close to within four points of the championship lead heading to Phoenix.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Jack Dixon","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1250,"title":"Green flag: three-wide chaos up the hill into turn 1","summary":"The field takes the green at COTA and immediately stacks up three-wide into turn 1; Jack Dixon gets shoved off track (his screen froze for 3 seconds, per his interview) while Chris Goans clears the mess and bolts to an early lead.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1400,"title":"Onboard with the field's only VR driver","summary":"The booth rides onboard with leader Chris Goans, the only driver in the field racing in virtual reality, watching his head trace through every apex.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1622,"title":"Lap 1-2 carnage replays: Shanebacher, Austin Paul, Mayberry","summary":"Replay tour of the opening-lap damage: John Shanebacher wrecks and Austin Paul piles in and destroys his truck, Dave Mayberry spins off the nose of Dion Jones, and the 12 of Chandler Paul looses it into Mike Everage's 82.","tags":["austin-paul","dave-mayberry","dion-jones","chandler-paul","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2615,"title":"Osborne on fresh tires can't shake Adamson","summary":"Fresh off pit lane, Jonathan Osborne hounds Mike Adamson's 88 for ninth, but Adamson defends brilliantly on worn tires for over a lap before Osborne finally uses the inside line to complete the pass.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3080,"title":"Caution flies three laps early","summary":"The halfway competition caution comes out around lap 18 instead of lap 21 — the scoring overlay flipped from laps-run to laps-to-go and fooled the booth, Alan hollered at admin Lori, and the flag flew early. The booth owns the blunder live: 'Chaos is better.'","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3570,"title":"Albert Anderson's turkey sandwich pit stop","summary":"Points leader Albert Anderson sits motionless on pit road under caution; the booth calls him up and he confirms he pulled in to take a couple bites of his turkey sandwich, then details the full recipe — lettuce, tomato, onion, American cheese, Dijon and mayo, with a bag of chips.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3746,"title":"Final restart with 19 to go","summary":"Goans controls the last restart of the night with the top 18 all on the lead lap; the field gets through turn 1 mostly clean and the second-half strategy race is on.","tags":["chris-goans","trevor-robertson","mike-adamson","andrew-cauthan","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3844,"title":"Cawthon and Alesia trade paint","summary":"Andrew Cawthon and Jacob Alesia make hard contact after the restart and keep banging on each other for several corners before sorting it out — neither wrecks, but the booth bets they're not happy with each other.","tags":["andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4070,"title":"Kevin Hunt's top-five run ends on the front stretch","summary":"Kevin Hunt, having a surprise top-five road-course run, gets unsettled over the rumble strip in the last turn and spins on the front stretch, undoing a night where he'd climbed eight spots on pace.","tags":["kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4981,"title":"Robertson's two-for-one pick pass on Alesia","summary":"Trevor Robertson uses lapped traffic from Scott Rooney as a pick to blow past Jacob Alesia — a two-for-one corner that puts him in position to chase the podium in the closing laps.","tags":["trevor-robertson","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5366,"title":"Rincon and Osborne roll the fuel-mileage dice","summary":"With four to go, Jorge Rincon and Jonathan Osborne refuse to pit and try to stretch 20 laps out of a 15-lap fuel tank. Rincon makes it with 0.1 to spare and steals a podium; Osborne's second-gear corner exits cost him and he fades to eighth.","tags":["george-rincon","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5741,"title":"Goans takes the checkers — a good old-fashioned butt whooping","summary":"Chris Goans caps a wire-to-wire clinic with the win and a victory burnout, sick with an ice pack down his shirt as a homemade cool suit. Jack Dixon beats Jorge Rincon to the line for second, and Goans closes to four points of Albert Anderson's championship lead.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3593,"quote":"Yeah, I just came down pit road to take a couple bites on my turkey sandwich. I'm about to pull back off now.","context":"Albert Anderson explains the unusually long pit stop during a live booth check-in.","gold":4},{"t":4981,"quote":"Oh, we got Robertson got by Alicia with using a pick from Scott Rooney.","context":"Trevor Robertson uses Scott Ronnie as a pick to clear Jacob Alesia late in the race.","gold":4},{"t":5366,"quote":"they're obviously not going to pit or they would have already pitted. So they're doing everything they can apparently to try to stretch the gas.","context":"The booth identifies the late fuel-mileage gamble by the trucks that stay on track.","gold":4},{"t":5753,"quote":"Going to take the checkered flag here tonight. Definitely going to help his championship hopes here in the series. And there's your winner, folks.","context":"Chris Goans completes the final corner and receives the checkered flag; his name is called in the immediately preceding transcript line.","gold":5},{"t":5763,"quote":"Jack Dixon's going to cross before Rencon. But what a run by Rencon on a fuel run like that. Brings it home third.","context":"The finish call places Jack Dixon second and Jorge Rincon third, with Rincon completing the fuel gamble.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption spellings are heavily garbled, so several proper names are best guesses: winner heard as Gones/Gomes/Gwens/Gins/Goens (rendered here as Chris Goins); third place heard as Rencon/Rancon/Rickon/Vidcon/Rink (rendered Jorge Rincon); Cawthon heard as Cawton/Cawin/Cawan; Alesia heard as Alesia/Alleian; Shanebacher heard six-plus different ways. Dillon Bryant (#51), Jason Kane, Tim Pope, and Craig Goodenough were mentioned only in points/absence talk and did not race tonight. Full 29-truck finishing order is read out at 1:52:36 (6756s). The competition caution was thrown ~3 laps early (lap 18 instead of 21) due to a scoring-overlay mix-up, acknowledged on air by Alan. Andrew Cawthon ran a windshield tribute to Captain Cody A. Cork, killed in an Iranian drone strike on a base in Kuwait (segment at 1:53:33 / 6813s).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"2fW5_INlzeE":{"recap":"Josh Buettner started on the pole and won the 203 at old-scan Atlanta, holding off a hard-charging Russ Kilgore by six hundredths of a second in a drag race to the line. On a 99-degree, tire-shredding surface, the 135-lapper turned into a strategy race: John Ellis stretched his fuel to stay out and win the stage break, while a wave of short pit stops before the competition caution trapped much of the field a lap down, leaving only seven trucks on the lead lap at the end. Kilgore climbed 21 spots from 23rd to take second as hard charger of the day, and Ellis's third place — a fourth straight podium after three wins in a row — vaulted him past Tim Pope into the championship lead. Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne finished fourth and Ricky Whittenburg quietly rounded out the top five. Outside a lap-one stack-up and scattered wall-bangers, the night ran remarkably clean with just one early caution plus the planned competition yellow.","winner":"Josh Buettner","podium":["Josh Buettner","Russ Kilgore","John Ellis"],"moments":[{"t":1414,"title":"Green flag, instant chaos","summary":"The field stacks up in the middle on the opening green flag — Dustin Riehle plunges through the grass all the way to pit lane, Russ Endicott goes off track, and Albert Anderson gets sideways, but everyone escapes without hitting the wall.","tags":["dustin-reilly","russ-endicott","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1960,"title":"Osborne dumps Austin Paul","summary":"The 81 of Jonathan Osborne drifts up into the 3, sending Austin Paul into the inside wall with front-end damage and a meatball black flag. Chachi apologizes on the radio; winner Josh Buettner later calls the contact 'pretty BS' in his interview.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2060,"title":"Kelly Kuehl's bucking bronco ride","summary":"Kelly Kuehl snags the outside wall and slows on the back straightaway, scattering trucks in every direction — several get doored at 180 mph but the field somehow threads through.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2446,"title":"The save of the night","summary":"Klafka and Rincon go 'full heat' side by side and somehow both save what the booth swears should have been a three-or-four-truck pileup, with the 28 pinching the 88 against the outside wall and actually helping him stay straight.","tags":["eric-klafka","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2838,"title":"Everage into the octopus arms","summary":"Mike Everage's Buffalo Trace Distillery Silverado goes hard into the inside wall and gets stuck, needing a tow to the pit box. He later disconnects, ending a strong night as the official last-place truck.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3692,"title":"Backmarker scramble turns ugly","summary":"A mid-pack squeeze around lapped traffic sends Kelly Kuehl and Justin French into hard impacts, while Dustin Riehle and Chandler Paul tandem-drift side by side through the dirt and miraculously gather it back up.","tags":["kelly-keel","justin-french","dustin-reilly","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3977,"title":"Ellis's fuel gamble wins the stage break","summary":"While most of the field short-pits ahead of the competition caution, John Ellis stretches his fuel, stays out, and takes the stage break 16-17 seconds clear — a cycle that traps a huge chunk of the field a lap down for the rest of the night.","tags":["john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4371,"title":"Second-half restart: Ellis vs Buettner","summary":"Ellis and Buettner go side by side across the line on cold tires to open the second half, with Russ Kilgore poking his nose in and threatening to make it three wide for the lead.","tags":["john-ellis","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5621,"title":"Buettner takes the lead with 21 to go","summary":"Josh Buettner looks to the inside of John Ellis and completes the pass for the lead, Ellis answers with a crossover move, and the two go back to two-by-two in a lead battle the booth calls a 'lazy Susan' of back and forth.","tags":["john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5990,"title":"Kilgore muscles past Ellis for second","summary":"Pushing it to the envelope, Russ Kilgore finally clears the 221 of Ellis for second and sets off after Buettner with eight tenths to make up and the laps running out.","tags":["russ-kilgore","john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6200,"title":"Dale Adamson passes two trucks while typing","summary":"After chiming into the YouTube chat from his second monitor mid-race, Dale Adamson passes two trucks in half a turn with one hand on the keyboard, leaving the booth in disbelief.","tags":["dale-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6252,"title":"Photo finish: Buettner by 0.06","summary":"White flag: Kilgore bumps the 84, looks outside then dives back inside, cutting across the grass in a drag race to the line — Josh Buettner wins by six hundredths of a second in a finish the booth calls the closest they've seen in a long time.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":680,"quote":"It looks like a Louisiana two-lane highway out there.","context":"Allen English describing the old abrasive Atlanta surface in the pre-race","gold":3},{"t":714,"quote":"I use a calculator, I'm actually civilized, unlike English.","context":"Pit reporter Adam Turner jabbing booth-mate Allen English's abacus in the intro","gold":3},{"t":1881,"quote":"I mean, even just the invisible grip goblins could grab you.","context":"The booth on how treacherous the slick old Atlanta surface is","gold":4},{"t":2446,"quote":"Oh, big wreck here... they saved it! How the heck did that happen?","context":"Klafka and Rincon pulling off the miracle no-contact save","gold":3},{"t":2838,"quote":"The 82 goes hard into the inside wall and he is stuck — the octopus arms has grabbed him.","context":"Mike Everage stuck against the inside wall, needing a tow","gold":4},{"t":5047,"quote":"I hope it's not the seven of Russ Kilgore — he's spent enough time up there to do a couple orbits.","context":"Reading a fan comment wishing for 'cars going into space', ribbing Kilgore's airborne history","gold":4},{"t":6200,"quote":"Just watch Dale Adamson pass two trucks in a half a turn with his hand on the keyboard, typing us.","context":"Dale Adamson chatting on YouTube from his second monitor mid-race","gold":4},{"t":6284,"quote":"Cutting across the grass, racing to the line is going to be Josh Buettner by six one-hundredths of a second!","context":"The photo-finish call as Kilgore comes up just short at the stripe","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is garbled across captions ('buettner'/'bittner'/'bentner') — Buettner is the best-guess spelling. 'Dustin Really' is almost certainly a caption garble; Riehle is a best guess. 'Ricky Wittenberg' in captions is Ricky Whittenburg (DND Race Graphix / Keller Williams sponsor). Albert Anderson Jr. (the III's father) appears only as a Facebook commenter, not a driver. Jeremiah Burke (#753) was absent this week and only mentioned. Alan Vaught is also the league owner/admin and Lori Vaught is the race steward who throws manual cautions. Broadcast has ~10 minutes of pre-show silence before commentary starts. Race = 135 laps at old-scan (pre-repave) Atlanta with a competition caution around lap 70; only one natural caution all night. Buettner's interview line about it 'probably being my last race in the league at this track' is ambiguous in the captions — likely refers to the last race on the old Atlanta scan, not leaving the league.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"2O9wP2yqsNM":{"recap":"VRL's trip to the Martinsville paperclip lived up to its 'Mayhem' billing: the 200-lap truck race produced at least 21 cautions, with pileups striking from the opening lap all the way to inside ten to go. Pole sitter Craig Goodenough controlled much of the first half before surrendering the lead during halfway pit stops and getting collected in a pit-cycle scrape, while multi-truck 'parking lot' wrecks on the backstretch and off turn two chewed through the 33-truck field — including a mid-race rage-disconnect from Dustin Wade. Dustyn Eaton's No. 14 emerged from the chaos, controlling the late restarts and holding off Nick Ramsey and Ricky Whittenburg on a three-lap dash to win in regulation, with Goodenough fourth and Tim Pope fifth — the top five separated by about a second. Alan Vaught and Andrew Coffin tied for hardest charger at 18 spots gained, and Goodenough took home the poll award and Spotlight Driver of the Day honors.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Nick Ramsey","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":1488,"title":"Mayhem on the opening lap","summary":"Barely a lap into the race, Nick Ramsey's No. 34 Rowdy Energy truck spins on its own off turn two to bring out the night's first caution — an omen of the 20-plus yellows to come.","tags":["nick-ramsey"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1979,"title":"Corner becomes a parking lot — Osborne threads the needle","summary":"Contact between the 01 and Chandler Paul's 72 stacks up the field into a full parking lot in the corner; the 3, 8, 16, and 68 all get collected while Jonathan Osborne somehow squirts straight through the wreckage untouched.","tags":["chandler-paul","kyle-vaught","edson-ochoa","dustin-wade","jonathan-osborne","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2255,"title":"Dickerson and Everage part the Red Sea","summary":"A helping bump from Josh Bittner's 84 sends Larry Dickerson's 69 sideways in turn three, collecting Mike Everage's 82 as the field parts around them — Bittner gains two spots in the bargain.","tags":["larry-dickerson","mike-everage","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2497,"title":"Pope snatches the lead; Young gets smoked","summary":"Tim Pope nails a restart to take the top spot away from Craig Goodenough for the first time, while behind them Jacob Young checks up from a three-wide threat and gets absolutely smoked from behind by pusher Kelly Keil.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","jacob-young"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3830,"title":"The Big One off turn two","summary":"The 434 of Kevin Hunt scrapes fenders and goes around off turn two, triggering the Big One: Chandler Paul, Jacob Young, Josh Bittner, Jack Dixon, and Zachary Henin all get swept into the pile.","tags":["kevin-hunt","nick-ramsey","chandler-paul","jacob-young","josh-bittner","jack-dixon","zachary-henin"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4500,"title":"Stranded on the apron — and an angry Canadian radio call","summary":"Kyle Vaught's 16 slides below the inside curb and loses two laps waiting for traffic while Dustin Wade high-centers the 68 on the same curb; the booth crowns John Curtis' radio outburst 'the best Canadian angry accent I've ever heard' — polite, of course.","tags":["kyle-vaught","dustin-wade","john-curtis"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4812,"title":"Goodenough's race turns during halfway pit stops","summary":"Leader Craig Goodenough surrenders the point to pit at halfway and gets caught up in right-side contact from Albert Anderson's 99 in the shuffle; Tim Pope later apologizes on the radio and Goodenough waves it off as 'that's short track racing.'","tags":["craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5041,"title":"Absolute parking lot on the backstretch — Wade rage-quits","summary":"Jacob Young's 77 gets hooked around out of nowhere and the backstretch becomes an 'absolute parking lot' — the 187, 18, 99, 28, 84, 43, and 79 all involved while Ricky Whittenburg bull-mooses his way through; Dustin Wade manually disconnects in disgust.","tags":["jacob-young","ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player","albert-anderson","george-rincon","josh-bittner","john-curtis","alejandro-gonzalez","scott-howell","dustin-wade","jess-vaught","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5703,"title":"Teammate-on-teammate violence: Klein 'clines' Vaught","summary":"Greg Klein's 92 drills teammate (and league boss) Alan Vaught's 33 right in the door under green — the booth dubs it 'the definition of a Klein-ing,' the worst teammate violence since Pocono 2020.","tags":["greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7329,"title":"Caution bet revealed at yellow number 21","summary":"Lori Vaught's fun fact drops: league members bet on tonight's caution count — Dave Mayberry guessed 14, Jess 25, Kelly 29, Kyle 27 — as the booth confirms this is caution number 21 for the record.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jess-vaught","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":7453,"title":"Late accordion pileup mauls the WWE truck","summary":"With the laps winding down, an accordion-effect stackup sweeps in the 123, 72, 92, 74, 01, and 19 — Chandler Paul's WWE-schemed 72 takes hits on three different sides like a cage match, while Scott Dehow's 187 'MDK' takes credit on the radio.","tags":["chandler-paul","john-gallagher","greg-cline","zachary-henin","jack-dixon","scott-howell"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8012,"title":"Eaton survives the meat grinder for the win","summary":"On a three-to-go restart, Dustyn Eaton launches clear while Nick Ramsey and Ricky Whittenburg trade paint for second; Eaton takes the checkered in regulation with the top five — Eaton, Ramsey, Whittenburg, Goodenough, Pope — covered by about a second.","tags":["dustin-eaton","nick-ramsey","ricky-whittenburg","craig-goodenough","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1979,"quote":"big big wrecking Osborne squeezed right through it","context":"Jonathan Osborne threads through a major early-race pileup at Martinsville.","gold":4},{"t":2510,"quote":"Pope might have taken first place away from Craig good enough there definitely got a great restart","context":"Tim Pope uses a strong restart to take the lead from Craig Goodenough.","gold":4},{"t":3830,"quote":"oh no big one coming out of turn number two","context":"The booth calls the multi-truck crash that erupts off turn two.","gold":5},{"t":5703,"quote":"oh no the 92 gets into his teammate the 33","context":"Greg Klein makes contact with teammate Alan Vaught during a green-flag run.","gold":4},{"t":8055,"quote":"picks up the race win here from Martinsville Nick Ramsey and Ricky Wittenberg make up your Podium","context":"The finish call confirms Dustyn Eaton winning, followed by Nick Ramsey and Ricky Whittenburg; Eaton is named in the immediately preceding transcript line.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Race: 200 laps at Martinsville (trucks), 33 starters, at least 21 cautions (caution #21 confirmed on air at ~2:02:45; the pre-race bet suggests the final count may have been higher). Winner's first name spelled 'Dustyn' per the booth's recurring 'Dustin with a Y' gag (vs. Dustin Wade, 'Dustin with an i') — spelling inferred, not shown on screen. Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: Jorge Rincon (ranone/Ranon/rancan/rencon), Scott Dehow (de how/how), Kelly Keil (Kuehl/keill/kill), Andrew Coffin (coffin/CN/cin/conin), Edson Ochoa (Ooa/oo), Zachary Henin (henin/hin). Lori Vaught is race control/league admin (not a driver or booth commentator). Full finishing order was read on air; Alan Vaught and Andrew Coffin tied for hardest charger (+18 spots each). Craig Goodenough won the poll award / Spotlight Driver of the Day. Post-race interviews: Goodenough (4th), Whittenburg (3rd), Ramsey (2nd), Eaton (winner).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"2TlufGts6Hk":{"recap":"The Season 8 finale at New Hampshire's Magic Mile put four championship contenders on stage: two-time champion Tim Pope against first-time hopefuls Jonathan Osborne, Dustyn Eaton, and Josh Bittner. After a caution-free 77-lap green stretch through the middle of the race, the second half descended into restart chaos — Jeremiah Burke slingshotted up into Eaton on a five-wide restart, eventually leaving the fan-poll favorite six laps down and out of contention. Pope and Osborne traded the lead door to door over the closing laps until a one-shot green-white-checkered decided everything: Bittner clipped Osborne's back bumper on the final restart, sending the 81 tumbling through the field, and the caution froze the field with Pope in front. Tim Pope took the race win and, after a race-control review, was confirmed on air as Season 8 champion — his third VRL title. Josh Bittner finished second and Albert Anderson charged 23 spots from a rear start to complete the podium as hard charger.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Josh Bittner","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":3360,"title":"Kyle Vaught finds the pit wall","summary":"On cold fresh tires, Kyle Vaught self-spins coming off turn 4 and noses hard into the inside wall, losing his front clip with the engine 'spraying for mosquitoes.'","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4692,"title":"Three-wide goes wrong for the milkdud","summary":"Dickerson gets sandwiched three-wide between Alan Vaught and Goodenough; his nose catches both at once, spinning them around while Whittenburg gets fenders banged up checking up behind.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","ricky-whittenburg","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4905,"title":"Championship four run 1-2-3-4","summary":"After the mid-race carnage, all four title contenders line up nose to tail at the very front of the field with a little over 50 laps to go — the cream rising to the top.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5290,"title":"Five-wide restart bites Eaton","summary":"Five wide down the backstretch on the restart: Burke loses traction on the apron and slingshots up into Eaton, who slams the outside wall hard — the YouTube poll favorite ultimately falls six laps down and out of title contention.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5585,"title":"Bittner tap sends Goodenough tumbling","summary":"The slightest touch from Bittner to Osborne's back bumper slips the 81 sideways into Goodenough, who goes tumbling down the frontstretch and draws a meatball flag; Keill, Klein and Coffin get collected in the aftermath.","tags":["josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne","craig-goodenough","kelly-keel","greg-cline","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5980,"title":"Booth goes full Area 51","summary":"During the caution parade, Turner and Brown pivot to F-22s escorting UFOs and bored aliens judging Facebook food photos on paper plates — while league admin Lori pleads with drivers to shape up after 77 clean green-flag laps.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6495,"title":"Netcode slingshot collects half the field","summary":"Gallagher appears to get slingshotted down into the corner with no actual contact, collecting Mayberry, Fite, Young, Coffin, Hunt and Burke — with the already-wounded Eaton tangled up yet again.","tags":["john-gallagher","dave-mayberry","david-fite","jacob-young","andrew-cauthan","kevin-hunt","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7215,"title":"Nine to go: Osborne and Pope door to door","summary":"The final restart sequence begins with Osborne and Pope side by side, door to door and bumper to bumper for the championship, until the 123's spin ends the run just before the white flag.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7570,"title":"Two to go: Pope snaps into Osborne","summary":"Pope snaps loose on corner exit and gets into Osborne's side with two laps left — the booth calls it 'weird' and 'strange' — and Dickerson's spin sets up a one-shot green-white-checkered for all the marbles.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7854,"title":"GWC heartbreak: Bittner spins Osborne, Pope takes it all","summary":"On the green-white-checkered restart, Bittner gets into the back of Osborne and sends the 81 tumbling down through the field; the caution freezes the field and Tim Pope picks up the win and season championship number three.","tags":["josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8710,"title":"Bittner apologizes — and announces a hiatus","summary":"In his runner-up interview Bittner insists the Osborne contact wasn't intentional, vows to reach out and apologize, then announces he's taking an indefinite break from league racing on iRacing to focus on real-world racing.","tags":["josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":9184,"title":"Official: Pope is Season 8 champion","summary":"After Lori initially withheld the call ('way too many incidents to call it'), breaking news arrives live on the broadcast: Tim Pope is your Season 8 champion — his third VRL title.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":4912,"quote":"we got all four Championship contenders all nose to tail up at the very front here","context":"All four title contenders line up together near the front with roughly 50 laps remaining.","gold":4},{"t":7220,"quote":"they go side by side even Steven down across the start finish line for the 81 and the Seven","context":"Jonathan Osborne and Tim Pope restart door to door with nine laps remaining.","gold":4},{"t":7866,"quote":"as the 84 gets into the back of the 81 that's going to send the 81 tumbling down through the field","context":"Josh Bittner contacts Jonathan Osborne on the green-white-checkered restart, deciding the race order pending review.","gold":5},{"t":9046,"quote":"Timothy Pope picks up the race win 84 Josh bner in second with the 99 of America's driver Albert Anderson finding his way onto that Podium","context":"The provisional finishing-order readout records Pope, Bittner, and Anderson as the top three.","gold":5},{"t":9184,"quote":"it will be Timothy Pope being your season champion picking up number three for him","context":"After incident review, the booth officially confirms Tim Pope as the Season 8 champion.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 8 championship finale (trucks) at New Hampshire; Season 9 announced to follow with no fast repairs. Auto-captions garble names heavily — best guesses uncertain for: #28 'Jorge Rincon' (heard Rota / ran con / ranan / ring con / rone), #74 Zachary Henin (heard henin / Howen), #01 Kelly Keill (heard keill / Kuehl / Keen), #1 David Feit (heard only 'fight'). #14's first name is likely spelled Dustyn — the booth repeatedly calls him 'Dustin with a Y.' Lori Vaught is league administrator/race control (heard as Lori bot / Lori V / Lori VOD / Lorie), not a driver or booth member; Alan Vaught co-runs the league per Bitner's interview. Championship result was initially withheld pending incident review, then confirmed on air (~2:33:17). Full finishing order read at ~2:30:46. Adam Turner served as pit/roving reporter alongside booth pair Alan Brown and Allen English.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"3d4ZswHV-Fg":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League opened its third season under the lights at Daytona with a 100-lap, 250-mile night race — the league's first in Xfinity cars after two seasons in trucks. Alan Vaught led much of the night, but the race was defined by carnage: a string of multi-car cautions built to a massive mid-race Big One, triggered when the 37 of Dustin Riehle wiggled down into Albert Anderson, that left a parking lot of destroyed cars and reportedly took out everyone behind the leaders. A second giant crash with two laps to go forced a green-white-checker, and with more carnage erupting at the white flag, Kelly Kuehl got the push from Vigilante Force teammate Alan Vaught to score his first career VRL win — a Vigilante Force 1-2 with newcomer Jim Ott third. Russ Kilgore earned hard charger and rally train driver of the day, up 24 spots to finish seventh, while Ricky Whittenburg and Russ Endicott were both disqualified on the 21x incident-point limit.","winner":"Kelly Kuehl","podium":["Kelly Kuehl","Alan Vaught","Jim Ott"],"moments":[{"t":2820,"title":"Pit-road chaos spins Osborne into his box","summary":"The second pit cycle goes helter-skelter: Jonathan Osborne gets clipped in the left rear and spun into his pit box (meatball flag), Chad McCabe gets busted for speeding, and Jason Harrison is trapped in his stall waiting for the mess to clear.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","chad-mccabe","jason-airson"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3107,"title":"Broadcaster's curse strikes Dion Jones","summary":"Moments after the booth praises his run, Dion Jones is collected on the backstretch when David Fate taps the wall and Chandler Paul dives down into traffic; Ricky Whittenburg gets snagged too and rides through the grass. First caution of the season.","tags":["dion-jones","chandler-paul","david-fite","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3349,"title":"Hot Rod fires shots: 'limited talent'","summary":"In an in-race booth interview, Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry trash-talks rival team Limitless Motorsports — 'more like limited talent' — with the booth cackling 'shots fired.'","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3660,"title":"Front-pack wreck collects America's Driver","summary":"Jim Ott and Albert Anderson touch at the front of the pack; Anderson goes hard into the outside wall (meatball flag) while teammates Tim Pope and Jeremiah Burke get collected in the scatter behind, along with Mike Everedge and Jack Dixon.","tags":["albert-anderson","jim-ott","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","mike-everage","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4505,"title":"Jordan pounds the wall as the field dives through the grass","summary":"Robert Jordan comes up on Derek Welch and spins himself, taking the brunt of a hard multi-car impact; Eric Klafka goes for a wild ride like a tumbleweed while Jonathan Osborne threads through the grass near the bus-stop chicane to escape.","tags":["robert-jordan","derek-welch","eric-klafka","mike-adamson","jonathan-osborne","russ-endicott"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5071,"title":"THE BIG ONE at Daytona","summary":"Dustin Riehle catches a wiggle and comes down into Albert Anderson, sending the 2 up into Kelly Kuehl and turning the field into a parking lot of destroyed cars — so much carnage that iRacing glitched rendering the damage. The booth reckoned not a single car behind the wreck made it through clean.","tags":["dustin-reilly","albert-anderson","kelly-keel","robert-jordan","george-rincon","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6160,"title":"Osborne takes out the pit cone on the money stop","summary":"In the mad dash to pit lane for the final green-flag stop, Jonathan Osborne wipes out the pit-entry cone and risks a black flag.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6769,"title":"Osborne snagged with nine to go","summary":"A three-wide squeeze in lap traffic goes wrong and Jonathan Osborne takes the brunt of a hard hit with nine laps remaining, bringing out a late caution and stacking the field back up.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7234,"title":"Second Big One forces the green-white-checker","summary":"Three-wide in the tri-oval, the No. 3 Budweiser machine of Kevin Haas gets the squeeze play and turns sideways — absolute carnage erupts behind with nowhere to go, Dustin Riehle shooting the gap and Jorge Rincon riding the wall in a 'Days of Thunder' smoke-drive. Sets up a green-white-checkered finish.","tags":["kevin-haas","dustin-reilly","george-rincon","mike-everage","timothy-pope","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7618,"title":"Carnage at the white flag","summary":"As the white flag flies on the green-white-checker, absolute carnage erupts behind the leaders, reducing the finish to a five-or-six-car sprint to the line.","tags":["mike-adamson","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7640,"title":"Kelly Kuehl breaks through for his first VRL win","summary":"Pushed to the line by teammate Alan Vaught, Kelly Kuehl survives the green-white-checker sprint to win the season opener — his first victory in three seasons of VRL — a Vigilante Force 1-2 with newcomer Jim Ott stealing third.","tags":["kelly-keel","jess-vaught","jim-ott","jack-dixon","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7673,"title":"Whittenburg and Endicott DQ'd on incident points","summary":"Both Ricky Whittenburg and Russ Endicott hit the 21x incident-point limit and are disqualified from the season opener.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","russ-endicott"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2105,"quote":"The sun never sucks on a badass — you always gotta have those sunglasses.","context":"Adam Turner defending wearing sunglasses at a night race","gold":3},{"t":2405,"quote":"Just in case the absolute poop hits the fan.","context":"Explaining why backmarkers were leaving extra car gaps","gold":3},{"t":3355,"quote":"They call themselves Limitless, but I think the more like limited talent.","context":"Dave Mayberry's in-race interview, trash-talking the rival team","gold":4},{"t":5071,"quote":"Here we go, this is the big one here boys!","context":"The massive mid-race crash erupting behind the leaders","gold":5},{"t":7015,"quote":"Once when that white flag waves and it gets taken, you know it's on like Donkey Kong.","context":"Previewing the green-white-checker shootout","gold":4},{"t":7115,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet, and throw inhibition out the window.","context":"Five laps to go before the final restart at Daytona","gold":4},{"t":7277,"quote":"That's a Days of Thunder, you know — drive through the smoke!","context":"Jorge Rincon driving blind through the second Big One","gold":3},{"t":7640,"quote":"Here goes Kelly Keel, for the first time picks up a win here at Vigilante, followed by teammate Jess Vaught!","context":"The checkered-flag call on Kuehl's breakthrough first win","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Several proper names never resolved on-air and are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: the No. 3 newcomer was called both 'Kevin Hayes' and 'Kevin Haas' (booth said they'd figure it out); the No. 244 was called Jason Ayers / Airson / Harrison (booth settled on 'Harrison' in the final rundown); the No. 1 was called David Fate / Feet; the No. 37 is consistently captioned 'Dustin Really' — spelled here as Riley but unconfirmed. Ricky Whittenburg (55) is also the league sponsor via DND Race Graphix and Keller Williams of Johnson City TN. Race control/admin is Lori Vaught (wife of Alan Vaught, referenced as 'Laurie/Lori' — not a driver). John Ellis raced last season (rookie champion) and was only mentioned, not racing tonight. Full finishing order read out starting ~8512s: Kuehl, Vaught, Ott, Dixon, Jones, Jordan, Kilgore, C. Paul, Polk, Rincon top 10; Whittenburg and Endicott DQ'd on the 21x incident limit. Jonathan Osborne is a paraplegic driver who races using his mouth — highlighted early in the broadcast (~1224s).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"3P-DDBiB69I":{"recap":"Rejoining Richmond race two mid-broadcast after a booth computer failure, the night belonged entirely to Jim Ott, who put the No. 205 on rails at the three-quarter-mile short track and lapped the entire field — a feat the booth said VRL had never seen. Jeremiah Burke brought the No. 753 home second, a lap down, while Alan Vaught recovered from an early incident and an off-cycle pit strategy to grab the final podium spot, turning Mike Adamson in the closing laps in a move he apologized for on air. Jason Airson finished fourth and Adamson held on for fifth after the contact, with only two cautions all night in a light 17-car summer field. Canadian Greg Dobson lost laps to a thunderstorm power outage yet salvaged 14th and won the random driver draw. It was Ott's second win of the season, sending VRL into All-Star week at Talladega.","winner":"Jim Ott","podium":["Jim Ott","Jeremiah Burke","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":133,"title":"Computer love triangle in the booth","summary":"After the stream blackout, the booth jokes that Brown's crashed PC went on a 'climate change strike' out of jealousy over his new build that could 'run the Tesla spaceships.'","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":360,"title":"Burke's bumper magic on Hot Rod","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets impatient behind the No. 29 and lays some bumper to Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry trying to move him out of line, but Mayberry holds him off.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":698,"title":"The four hooks the 57 into the wall","summary":"An 'absolute glob' erupts around the No. 57 — the 82 and 51 get together, and Dion Jones hooks Russ Endicott and sends him up into the concrete, with the booth wondering if it was payback.","tags":["dion-jones","russ-endicott","mike-adamson","mike-everage","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":985,"title":"Hot Rod's wild ride, three-wide escape","summary":"Mayberry tangles with lap traffic and goes for a wild ride, the field fans three wide across the line, and Jonathan Osborne rides the outside to pass all the mess again.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jeff-ottinger","russ-kilgore","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1272,"title":"Ott laps the field up to fifth","summary":"So many green-flag laps have run that Jim Ott has lapped everyone up to fifth place — only four cars on the lead lap — and stretches his lead to 13 seconds.","tags":["jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2025,"title":"Dobson's 40-degrees-sideways save","summary":"Greg Dobson gets big-time loose off turn four, 40 degrees sideways, and somehow gathers it up on the apron — 'great save by our friendly Canadian.'","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2568,"title":"Mayberry snaps loose and hammers the wall","summary":"Coming off turn four, the No. 29 snaps loose on Hot Rod Mayberry, who hits the wall hard and bunny-hops a bump in the infield, wrecking his night.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3040,"title":"Yahtzee! Ott laps the entire field","summary":"Jim Ott drives around second-place Jeremiah Burke to put the whole field a lap down — something the booth says has never happened in VRL — capping an on-rails clinic at Richmond.","tags":["jim-ott","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3190,"title":"'Jim Ott the Bot' is born","summary":"Searching for a nickname for the runaway leader, the booth lands on 'Jim Ott the Bot' — he's out there destroying everybody like an AI on this rhythm track.","tags":["jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3535,"title":"Vaught turns Adamson for the podium","summary":"Nose to tail for third in the closing laps, Alan Vaught and Mike Adamson get together and the 51 spins — a 'Ross Chastain deal' per the booth — handing Vaught P3; Vaught apologized on air afterward.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3720,"title":"White flag and the checkers for Ott","summary":"Jim Ott takes the white flag and cruises across the line with the entire field lapped to pick up his second win of the season.","tags":["jim-ott","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3800,"title":"Dobson wins the random draw","summary":"The random draw driver of the day lands on 14th-place Greg Dobson, who battled thunderstorm disconnects in Canada all night — 'that's what happens when you're Canadian nice.'","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":127,"quote":"here at richmond 115 of 267 done and out of the way","context":"The restored stream rejoins the race at lap 115, explicitly bounding what this part-two broadcast can prove.","gold":5},{"t":724,"quote":"four just hooks the 57 and sends him up into the wall","context":"The No. 4 hooks the No. 57 during a crowded short-track battle.","gold":4},{"t":2028,"quote":"coming out of four that thing was 40 degrees sideways nice save for the 285","context":"Greg Dobson catches a dramatic slide off turn four.","gold":4},{"t":3045,"quote":"here we go to put the field a complete lap down there goes jim on around that 753 of jeremiah burke","context":"Jim Ott passes Jeremiah Burke to put the entire field at least one lap down; the captions render Ott as on.","gold":5},{"t":3744,"quote":"down and across the line goes jim aunt to pick up his second win on this season","context":"The checkered-flag call confirms Jim Ott winning the Richmond race; the captions render his surname as aunt.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"This is part two of the Richmond 2 broadcast — the stream crashed and rejoined in progress around lap 115 of 267, so early-race action (including at least one caution and a solo Mayberry spin) happened off-tape. Full finishing order 1-17 was read on air: Ott, Burke, Vaught, Airson, Adamson, Kilgore, Osborne, Anderson, Jones, Ottinger, Everett, Mayberry, Evans, Dobson, Endicott, Chandler Paul (DC), David Feit (DC). Name uncertainties: 'Alan Vaught' could be 'Vaughn' (captions render both); 'Jason Airson' could be 'Ayerson/Erison'; 'Mike Everett' could be 'Everedge'; 'David Feit' (#221, disconnected) is almost certainly a caption garble of an unknown surname. Tim Pope and John Ellis were mentioned but did not race tonight. Booth is AAA Broadcasting — sign-off named Alan and Adam, with engineer/co-host Brown; one host is also addressed as 'English' (likely a nickname). Cars are fixed-setup Xfinity-class; next event stated as All-Star week at Talladega (qualifier Monday, race Wednesday).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"3qDLIu_OtW4":{"recap":"Mike Adamson scored his breakthrough VRL win in a caution-filled 150-lap night race at Bristol, surviving a green-white-checkered finish in which Tim Pope, battling side-by-side for the lead, got loose in the final corner and smacked the outside wall at the line. Alex \"4J\" Berube dominated the early going with a two-second lead before a poor pit stop and repeated tangles left him 16th, seven laps down. The night was a short-track slugfest — restart pileups, a full \"parking lot\" around lap 40, and Josh Oxendine famously dodging his way through the carnage on his way to a seventh-place finish. Josh Bittner came home second with Trevor Robertson third, while Adamson credited his Limitless Esports teammates for keeping him calm after an early iRacing glitch dropped him deep in the field. The booth also confirmed the story of the night: Jeremiah Burke's dad once threw hands with a young Robby Gordon at the finish line of the Baja 1000.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Josh Bittner","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":2056,"title":"Lap 37: the first yellow finally flies","summary":"Self dives to the apron, Mayberry gets looped in the pack, Snyder is collected and Oxendine has nowhere to go — the first caution of the night on lap 37.","tags":["zachary-self","dave-mayberry","jeff-snyder","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2376,"title":"Restart turns into a parking lot","summary":"Tyler Green gets loose off the apron, comes back up into the 2 of Kilgore, and the chain reaction stacks up the field — \"now we got a little bit of a parking lot going on.\"","tags":["tyler-green","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2481,"title":"Riding with Ox through the bumper cars","summary":"In-car replay of Josh Oxendine threading a restart pileup untouched — \"missed one car, missed two cars, missed three cars\" — the booth credits his carburetor-cup dodging practice.","tags":["josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2537,"title":"The Robby Gordon story","summary":"With Jeremiah Burke's dad Michael in the YouTube chat, the booth confirms the podcast legend: Burke's pop once threw hands with a young Robby Gordon at the Baja 1000 finish line.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3028,"title":"Self t-boned by the 55","summary":"Self gets snagged and spun in the middle of the track and Ricky Whittenburg, in an unfamiliar new paint scheme, catches him full broadside.","tags":["zachary-self","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3281,"title":"The 12-into-14 chain-reaction big one","summary":"Oxendine gets into the back of Robertson on the restart, then Anderson's 12 tags the loose 14 of Herzig in the middle of the track and the whole field piles in behind them.","tags":["josh-oxendine","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson","john-herzig","rob-green","tyler-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3892,"title":"Hutchinson's five-minutes-old debut goes sideways","summary":"The 01 washes up into the 21 and the 15 plows into him — rough welcome for Justin Hutchinson, who joined the league literally five minutes before race time.","tags":["justin-hutchinson","kelly-keel","jeffrey-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3959,"title":"Dixon: wrecked three times by the same driver","summary":"Jack Dixon posts in the YouTube chat that he's been wrecked three times by the same driver — the booth smells something brewing and promises to do some research.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4207,"title":"Berube's charge ends in turn two","summary":"Tyler Green calls \"wreck in one and two\" on the radio as Berube gets help from Kilgore's 7 and goes around — the early dominator gets the worst end of the stick.","tags":["alex-berube","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4438,"title":"Adamson's crossover for the lead","summary":"Pope commits to the outside line on the restart and Adamson completes the crossover move underneath him to take the lead he'd carry to the win.","tags":["mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4484,"title":"Wheeler collected, Ricky breaks the steering","summary":"Netcode plus contact from the 753 and the 7 finish off Zach Wheeler, and Whittenburg tags the outside wall dodging the wreck, breaking his steering — \"Ricky keeps breaking A-arms.\"","tags":["zach-wheeler","jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5086,"title":"GWC: Pope smacks the wall, Adamson wins","summary":"Green-white-checkered thriller: Pope and Adamson run side-by-side to the line, Pope gets loose and smashes the wall in the final corner while cars wreck everywhere behind — Adamson takes his breakthrough win over Bittner and Robertson.","tags":["mike-adamson","timothy-pope","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson","josh-oxendine","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":692,"quote":"I like to call this the old dump-the-chump routine, man — this is where you can turn them and burn them.","context":"Adam Turner previewing Bristol bump-and-run tactics before the green","gold":4},{"t":2147,"quote":"He's probably getting a hot dog and they're gonna trade drivers or something, I don't know.","context":"Jack Dixon limping the Laughing Clown car down pit road","gold":3},{"t":2481,"quote":"Oh — missed one car, missed two cars, missed three cars, oh my goodness!","context":"riding in-car as Josh Oxendine threads a restart pileup untouched","gold":4},{"t":2570,"quote":"So did you just tell me he threw hands with Robbie Gordon?","context":"reacting to the story of Jeremiah Burke's dad fighting Robby Gordon at the Baja 1000","gold":5},{"t":3759,"quote":"Go get some hot dogs, trade out your drivers — get you all Ricky Bobby in there. I want to go fast, yeah!","context":"Jack Dixon stopped on the apron for the second time","gold":3},{"t":4506,"quote":"Ricky keeps breaking A-arms, man — he's breaking all the ball joints and A-arms and all the important pieces.","context":"Whittenburg tags the wall dodging a wreck and breaks his steering","gold":3},{"t":5111,"quote":"That's gonna give Mike Adamson the win... what a crazy finish, what just happened? That was a big one!","context":"the green-white-checkered finish as Pope slaps the wall at the line","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names heavily; proper spellings are best guesses. The video chapter marker reads 'Josh Bittner' while captions alternate 'buettner'/'bittner' — chapter spelling used. Russ Kilgore's No. 7 truck was painted like a 2, confusing the booth all night. Josh Oxendine said in his interview that Jeremiah Burke's 753 was disqualified at the line (moving Ox from 8th to 7th), but the booth's final rundown still lists Burke 12th, one lap down — official result ambiguous below the podium. The 'Russell Endicott' chapter marker refers to a Facebook commenter segment, not an on-track driver. Angelica Timur (surname garbled) sat out this week working a shift. Race: 150 laps at Bristol Motor Speedway, VRL inaugural season, trucks, 21x incident limit, two fast repairs.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"3s7qXcOrlmA":{"recap":"Jess Vogt put the 33 on pole and controlled most of the Rocking Richmond 200, ripping away on nearly every restart of a caution-filled 200-lap night race. The wrecks came early and often, headlined by John Gallagher's 123 barrel-rolling over the frontstretch barrels in a mid-race pileup and Mike Adamson's engine letting go, before a late string of yellows set up a single green-white-checkered attempt. Jonathan Osborne, who served a pass-through penalty and was a lap down by lap 5, gambled on fresh tires under the caution with about ten to go and squeezed past Larry Dickerson on the final restart just before the caution flew and froze the field. Osborne took the win as hard charger of the day, up 32 spots, with Jeremiah Burke charging from 31st to second and Greg Klein rounding out the podium. Vogt gave up the lead with a late pit call and fell to 15th after leading much of the night.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Jeremiah Burke","Greg Cline"],"moments":[{"t":1430,"title":"Lap-one spin brings out the first caution","summary":"Green flag barely waves before the 123 of John Gallagher goes around off turn four, with Jeremiah Burke and Jorge Rincon catching pieces of the aftermath.","tags":["john-gallagher","jeremiah-burke","george-rincon"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2336,"title":"The Big One on the frontstretch","summary":"Mike Adamson's 88 gets sucked into Craig Goodenough's quarter panel on a restart and a parking lot builds up on the frontstretch — Larry Dickerson stops just in time to avoid T-boning the 88.","tags":["mike-adamson","craig-goodenough","larry-dickerson","jess-vaught","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2789,"title":"Adamson's engine lets go","summary":"The Silent Assassin's rough night gets worse — the 88 blows an engine mid-corner, gets spun by oncoming traffic, and picks up a meatball flag.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3496,"title":"\"We got dead people\" — Gallagher goes flipping","summary":"Burke gets into the back of Mayberry entering three, Kelly Kuehl is collected, and John Gallagher's 123 gets pinched into the barrels and goes flipping as a flood of traffic pours through the blocked track. The signature wreck of the night.","tags":["john-gallagher","dave-mayberry","jeremiah-burke","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4358,"title":"The funeral-song poll","summary":"Race director Lorie V's driver poll — what song plays at your funeral — takes over the booth: David Allan Coe, Weird Al, Green Day, AC/DC, and Albert Anderson's deep-cut Megadeth pick.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","greg-dobson","dion-jones","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5468,"title":"Mayberry checks up, chaos collects four","summary":"The 29 gets loose off turn four, Dustin Wade has nowhere to go and turns him, and Mike Everage and Andrew Player are swept into the infield grass.","tags":["dave-mayberry","dustin-wade","mike-everage","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5580,"title":"Vogt's restart masterclass","summary":"The booth marvels at the polesitter — Jess Vogt has Richmond's odd restart zone figured out, launching away from the field like a shot from a cannon on every green flag.","tags":["jess-vaught","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6121,"title":"Whittenburg and Burke duel for second","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg, who the booth crowns a NASCAR historian racing Richmond like a home track, battles hard charger Jeremiah Burke for second with Jonathan Osborne breathing down both their necks.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6838,"title":"Kyle Vogt hammers the inside wall","summary":"Three-wide off turn two goes wrong — the 16 gets clipped, slides across the track, and takes a hard impact into the inside wall, narrowly missing the angled emergency-vehicle opening.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7160,"title":"Whittenburg and Bittner wiped out racing for the front","summary":"Moments after a three-wide-in-the-turns highlight, Josh Bittner breaks loose up the track and Ricky Whittenburg follows him in — the podcast buddies are both taken out inside the final ten laps, Ricky hard into the inside wall.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7452,"title":"GWC chaos: Osborne steals it as the yellow flies","summary":"On the lone green-white-checkered, Dickerson spins the tires, Osborne rockets around the outside on fresh rubber, and the caution comes out to freeze the field — with the 33 and 84 flipping behind them. Osborne wins from a lap down, up 32 spots.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","larry-dickerson","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7776,"title":"Whittenburg's phantom fuel stop","summary":"Spotlight driver Ricky Whittenburg reveals a sim gremlin cost him a top five: the replay shows his crewman fueling the truck, but no gas went in, and he ran dry before reaching pit road after the late wreck.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":852,"quote":"I would rather run Sebring than run this one, and you know how much I hate Sebring.","context":"Alan English on how much he hates driving Richmond","gold":3},{"t":3208,"quote":"Sometimes you're the windshield, sometimes you're the bug.","context":"Summing up Mike Adamson's cursed night after his blown engine","gold":3},{"t":3504,"quote":"Oh big... oh, we got dead people! And the 123 goes flipping — oh my goodness!","context":"John Gallagher barrel-rolls over the frontstretch barrels in the mid-race pileup","gold":5},{"t":3841,"quote":"The newly dubbed — as I'm dubbing it here — fastest chicken in the South.","context":"Christening Jacob Young's Raising Cane's chicken paint scheme","gold":3},{"t":7156,"quote":"Look at the three wide in the turns, able to hold it — there's not another league that we broadcast that could do that. Nobody can do that.","context":"The leaders go three-wide through the corners in the final ten laps","gold":4},{"t":7452,"quote":"Time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets, throw inhibition out the window — green flag racing!","context":"Sending the field off on the lone green-white-checkered attempt","gold":4},{"t":8778,"quote":"It's kind of like the WWE of racing tonight.","context":"The booth wrapping up a beating-and-banging Richmond show","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Race ended under caution on the lone green-white-checkered attempt; the field was frozen and Osborne declared the winner, so there was no racing to the checkered flag. Surname of Jess and Kyle (#33/#16) is garbled throughout the captions (vot/VA/VOD/fot/bought) — 'Vogt' is a best guess; the league is run by Jess and race director Lorie V, who also produced the driver polls. #74's name is heard as both 'Henin/henon' and 'Howen' and may be conflated with #187 Scott Howe. 'David Feit' (#1, heard as 'fight') and 'Edson Ochoa' (#8, heard as 'Ooa/oo') are best guesses. Tim Pope (#7) entered but did not grid due to connection/update issues. Booth names come through captions as 'Ellen Brown' and 'Allen English'. Dickerson led the GWC but was scored 9th after the frozen-field scoring shook out, which the booth found confusing on air.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"45CmS-hr9v4":{"recap":"Race #3 of the Vigilante Racing League season brought the trucks to the virtual Circuit of the Americas for 43 caution-free laps on the shortened West layout. Polesitter Alan Vaught led early, but Dustyn Eaton pounced in Turn 20 on lap 6 and controlled most of the night, only surrendering the point when Vaught briefly stole the lead with a lap-27 undercut in the green-flag pit cycle. Eaton ran the 33 back down and retook the lead in Turn 20 with 10 laps to go, cruising to his second straight win while Vaught settled for second with the fastest lap of the race. Derek Welch outdueled David Feit in a long, clean fight for third to complete the podium, with only 11 trucks finishing on the lead lap. The winner's burnout celebration ended with the motor expiring on Eaton's Toyota Tundra as the league looked ahead to Phoenix Raceway.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Alan Vaught","Derek Welch"],"moments":[{"t":2483,"title":"Green flag at COTA","summary":"The field takes the green for 43 laps at the virtual Circuit of the Americas, polesitter Alan Vaught leading Dustyn Eaton and Trevor Robertson.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","trevor-robertson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2882,"title":"Eaton pounces in Turn 20 for the lead","summary":"After stalking Vaught's tailgate for laps, Dustyn Eaton jumps in at the final corner and takes the race lead on lap 6.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3581,"title":"Robertson spins away third place","summary":"Trevor Robertson locks it up with an apparent wheel hop, spins from third and falls to sixth, promoting David Feit and Derek Welch.","tags":["trevor-robertson","david-fite","derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3917,"title":"Vaught closes to within four tenths","summary":"Eaton keeps sliding the rear and catching the sausage curbs, and Alan Vaught reels the gap down to under four tenths for a battle for the lead.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5248,"title":"Welch and Fite drag race for third","summary":"Derek Welch throws it deep to the inside of David Feit, they run side by side through Turn 20 and keep it clean — 'what a finish that would have been.'","tags":["derek-welch","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5463,"title":"The undercut: Vaught steals the lead in the pits","summary":"Eaton finally pits from the lead, but Alan Vaught's earlier stop and a near 3-second-faster out-lap complete the undercut — the 33 cycles to the front with a 3.4-second cushion.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5828,"title":"Welch finally clears Fite for third","summary":"Using lap traffic (a slow Dillon Bryant to the inside), Derek Welch makes the pass on David Feit stick for the final podium spot.","tags":["derek-welch","david-fite","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5886,"title":"Eaton retakes the lead with 10 to go","summary":"The race-deciding move: Dustyn Eaton dives to the inside in Turn 20 and takes the point back from Alan Vaught, then drives away for good.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6399,"title":"Everage clobbers the second-place truck","summary":"Mike Everage, two laps down, gets into the back of Alan Vaught in the final corner with five to go — 'that could have been disaster for the 33.'","tags":["mike-everage","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6444,"title":"Austin Paul sent into the Armco","summary":"Contact with Vaught in lap traffic sends Austin Paul's No. 3 truck into the Armco barrier between Turns 12 and 13.","tags":["austin-paul","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6908,"title":"Checkered flag: Eaton goes back-to-back","summary":"Dustyn Eaton takes the checkered flag at COTA — his second win in a row — with Alan Vaught a hard-fought second and Derek Welch third.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7084,"title":"Victory burnout blows the motor","summary":"Eaton does his 'best Kevin Harvick impression' on the frontstretch, the booth compares it to Robbie Gordon in Montreal, and the motor expires on the Tundra mid-celebration.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":4991,"quote":"Looked like a Formula Drift race here at COTA.","context":"Kelly Kuehl loops it way deep on the brakes at the end of the main straight","gold":3},{"t":5680,"quote":"That was a Zach Millet victory slide there.","context":"Eaton hangs the truck sideways coming out of the stadium section","gold":3},{"t":6399,"quote":"Oh! Everage gets into the back of Allen Vaught — that could have been disaster for the 33!","context":"A truck two laps down clips the second-place machine with five to go","gold":3},{"t":6649,"quote":"Quick, Lori, throw the caution — there's a horse on the racetrack! We can do a green white checker, why not?","context":"Booth begging for a caution that doesn't exist as Eaton stretches his biggest lead of the night","gold":4},{"t":6908,"quote":"Dustin Eaton — beautiful performance here at Circuit of the Americas. He'll win it!","context":"The winning call at the checkered flag","gold":4},{"t":7506,"quote":"I told you guys last week, this was my great white buffalo — and I shot it in the head tonight, dude.","context":"Dustyn Eaton in the winner's interview after going back-to-back","gold":4},{"t":7913,"quote":"If that's him nervous, I'd hate to see what he looks like comfortable.","context":"After Derek Welch claimed he's scared to death of passing on road courses","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and podium explicitly stated on air and in interviews. Proper-name guesses from garbled captions: 'Alan Vaught' inferred from variants (vot/VA/vont/fought/VOD; league admin, wife Lori and son Kyle Vaught share the surname); 'David Feit' uncertain (captions: fight/pight/F fet); 'Jorge Rincon' uncertain (ranone/Ren con); 'Sean McDonnell' captioned as both Shawn and John. Zach Millet, Brian McCann and Connor Leech are only mentioned in booth talk about a different league's race the night before (Numb Thumbs Racing League) — not entrants tonight. No cautions were available (local yellows only), so there were no restarts. Eaton's 'great white buffalo' quote is captioned 'great wife Buffalo' — cleaned as an obvious caption error. Full finishing order read at ~2:12:04 (7924s). Race #4 next week at Phoenix Raceway, with the broadcaster noting he may miss it due to work travel.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"4_8SoFbeO84":{"recap":"Race #7 of Vigilante Racing League Season 11 sent the trucks to Martinsville Speedway for 200 laps and turned into a 27-caution marathon that the Track Limits booth could only laugh through. Pole sitter Craig Goodenough dominated the early running, while constant yellows and pit strategy cycled the lead through Tim Pope — up from 23rd — Chris Klein, Kyle Vaught, and Andrew Player, whose strong night was ruined late by a connection drop. Trevor Robertson drove back through the field after his pit stop and retook command with 25 laps to go. A Ricky Whittenburg–Dustin Wade tangle with six to go forced the league's one-and-only green-white-checkered attempt, and Robertson nailed the final restart to beat Whittenburg and Goodenough, who took third on his 35th birthday. Tim Pope recovered to fourth, a 19-position gain on the night.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Ricky Whittenburg","Craig Goodenough"],"moments":[{"t":2467,"title":"Vaught drilled on the restart, debris 50 feet high","summary":"On the lap-29 restart Alan Vaught spins the tires and misses a shift, goes around in front of traffic and gets drilled by Dustyn Eaton — pieces of debris 50 feet in the air.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2916,"title":"Gallagher blows the braking zone","summary":"John Gallagher totally misses his braking point into turn three and plows into the pack, collecting Anthony Williams, Alan Vaught and David Feight.","tags":["john-gallagher","anthony-williams","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3335,"title":"The Chad and Jimmy spotter pack goes rogue","summary":"Steve apologizes for foul language from the spotters on the broadcast — then admits it's his 'Chad and Jimmy' spotter pack with the cuss words switched on because he forgot to turn them off.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4259,"title":"Tim Pope leads from 23rd","summary":"Tim Pope, who started 23rd, cycles to the race lead through strategy and clean driving — the biggest mover on the track all night.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4330,"title":"'That's how it's done' — Robertson takes the point","summary":"Trevor Robertson, on roughly 10-lap fresher tires, runs down Tim Pope for the lead, and Pope smartly lets him go rather than burn up his truck fighting it.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5302,"title":"Hunt and Mayberry meet the wall hard","summary":"Kevin Hunt misses his braking point, dives to the bottom to avoid contact, then washes up into the path of Dave Mayberry — both trucks take a big smack. 'Good thing it is just a sim.'","tags":["kevin-hunt","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5974,"title":"Turn-four pileup collects the pack","summary":"A stackup in turn four sweeps up Everage, Mayberry and Jeremiah Burke, with Dobson driving into the aftermath. Burke's suspension damage ultimately forces him to park it.","tags":["mike-everage","dave-mayberry","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6215,"title":"Klein dumps Hunt — 'a pretty professional move'","summary":"Chris Klein waits until the last second to duck inside Kyle Vaught, runs out of room and drives into the back of a slowing Kevin Hunt. Steve calls it a bad decision; Chris compares it to Matt Kenseth on Joey Logano.","tags":["chris-klein","kevin-hunt","kyle-vaught","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7153,"title":"Renone roots Pope into the fence","summary":"On the first double-file restart in ages, Renone roots Pope up the track and into the fence; Pope then pancakes the wall again and bounces into Bittner, who is shoved down into Whittenburg with Osborne collected on the front stretch.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner","ricky-whittenburg","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7359,"title":"Player's connection dies while in contention","summary":"Andrew Player, running up front all night, drives into the back of Dustin Wade coming to the restart and then vanishes from the session — a connection issue that dooms his race. He returns three-plus laps down in 26th.","tags":["andrew-player","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7783,"title":"Whittenburg clips Wade — GWC time","summary":"With six to go, Ricky Whittenburg sends it in late on the brakes and clips the left rear of Dustin Wade, putting Wade in the fence. Caution number 27 forces the league's single green-white-checkered attempt.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","dustin-wade","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7942,"title":"Robertson wins the green-white-checkered","summary":"On the one-and-only overtime attempt, Robertson gets the jump with Whittenburg to his inside, takes the white flag with a healthy lead as trouble breaks out behind, and wins the Martinsville marathon over Whittenburg and Goodenough.","tags":["trevor-robertson","ricky-whittenburg","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2312,"quote":"Crashberry. Sorry. We're not still doing that. All right. Sorry, Dave. I think it's fair.","context":"Steve slips out Dave Mayberry's nickname after a wreck","gold":3},{"t":3348,"quote":"It's the Chad and Jimmy spotter pack, but I got the cuss words on cuz I like getting fired up when I race, but I forgot to switch it back.","context":"Steve explaining the spotter profanity heard on the broadcast","gold":4},{"t":4168,"quote":"At this rate, Steve, I don't think Craig Good Enough's gonna spill his caramel macchiato he's got in this car.","context":"Chris on the endless cautions keeping the leader comfortable","gold":4},{"t":5810,"quote":"No fast repairs, no yellows. Every man for himself. Let it happen.","context":"The booth brainstorming after the 18th caution","gold":3},{"t":6291,"quote":"It looked like a pretty professional move. I think I saw Matt Kenith do that to Joey Logano one time.","context":"Chris defending Chris Klein's last-second dive that dumped Kevin Hunt","gold":4},{"t":6850,"quote":"Can you imagine if we had a Martinsville hot dog every time we had a caution tonight? We'd be in an ambulance.","context":"The hot dog running gag is born deep into the caution count","gold":4},{"t":7153,"quote":"Time to put your big boy panties on and get after it.","context":"First double-file restart in ages, 24 laps to go","gold":4},{"t":7988,"quote":"Checker flag. Robertson wins it. Ricky Whittenberg comes home in second. Holds off Craig Good enough.","context":"The green-white-checkered finish call","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"27 cautions total — the booth confirmed it as a Track Limits record. Lead announcer identified only as Steve; color commentator captioned 'Chris Gones' (possibly Jones), who raced the prior night in the Num Thumbs league. Auto-captions heavily garble surnames: Goodenough appears as Gooduff/Goodnoff/Goodnuff, the Vaughts as VA/Bot/Vault/Vaughn (family name guessed from pronunciation; league admins Allan and Lori share it in variants Vodor/Vot/Va), Renone as Ren Con/Ringo/Rone, Everage as 'average', and 'David Feight' is a best guess from captions 'Fight'/'Fe'. Two Kleins raced (Greg #92 and Chris); the results read-out garbles which finished 5th vs 16th ('Craig Klein was fifth... Greg Klein, sorry, Chris Klene' for 16th). Full finishing order was read at ~2:26:29. Craig Goodenough took pole and finished third on his 35th birthday. Race ran the full 200 laps plus one green-white-checkered within the 2h05m session cap.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"4fgQLbPfftk":{"recap":"Round six of the VRL Premiere Series brought a 35-truck field to Watkins Glen International for the 55-lap, 135-mile Watkins Glen 135, run with a scheduled competition caution at lap 28. Polesitter Craig Goodenough controlled the first half, stretching his lead past seven seconds while penalized fast-movers like Dillon Bryant and Jeremiah Burke charged from the rear into the top ten. The night had its share of carnage: Kyle Vaught blew his engine against the barrier early, Chris Goans spun in a tangle with Dustyn Eaton — saving a full 360 before Josh Bittner collected him in the carousel — and John Gallagher's race ended in a pit-entry crash. Tim Pope out-timed Goodenough on the final pit cycle, took the lead with a door-to-door pass with 15 laps to go, and drove away to win by nearly three seconds. Goodenough held off a hard-charging Derek Welch on the last lap to finish second, with Welch completing the podium.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Craig Goodenough","Derek Welch"],"moments":[{"t":1017,"title":"Kyle just wants to send it","summary":"Pre-race interview: Kyle says Taylor texted him reminding him to be patient — but admits 'I just want to send it' before starting from the rear with a penalty.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1321,"title":"Klein's opening-lap bounce into the wall","summary":"Greg Klein catches a bad hop off the curb on cold tires on the opening lap, slams the wall hard and is towed to the pits.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1819,"title":"Premature acceleration: Vaught blows it up","summary":"Racing three-wide from the back, Kyle Vaught pulls a slick crossover move, then lights up the rear tires, spins into the barrier and blows the engine — night over for one of the fastest trucks in the field.","tags":["kyle-vaught","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3124,"title":"Pit-close chess hands Welch the lead","summary":"Leader Goodenough and Chris Goans dive onto pit lane just as the pits close before the lap-28 competition caution, while Derek Welch stays out and traps everyone behind him — inheriting the lead for the comp caution.","tags":["craig-goodenough","chris-goans","derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3798,"title":"Back to green with 24 to go","summary":"The one and only restart of the night: Goodenough gets a good launch but Goans stays glued to his bumper, with Welch, Osborne, Robertson and Adamson lurking on four-lap fresher tires.","tags":["craig-goodenough","chris-goans","derek-welch","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4046,"title":"Gallagher's pit-entry disaster","summary":"John Gallagher misses the pit entry, catches contact with the 023 and then tangles with the 01 — the booth calls it a race-ender.","tags":["john-gallagher","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4135,"title":"The 38's 360 save — then Bittner arrives","summary":"Chris Goans gets a nudge battling Dustyn Eaton and spins — keeps driving it all the way around for an incredible full-360 save, only for Josh Bittner to run wide in the carousel and nail him in the rear. Both trucks need extensive repairs.","tags":["chris-goans","dustin-eaton","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4475,"title":"Pope refuses the door-slam, takes the lead","summary":"Fifteen to go: Tim Pope, on fresher tires after out-foxing Goodenough on pit timing, gets alongside — Craig tries to slam the door, Pope doesn't lift, and the seven truck completes the race-winning pass. First driver to pass Goodenough all night.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4668,"title":"Lug Nut Gate","summary":"Albert Anderson posts in chat that all his lug nuts fell off and he's done; the booth suggests he think about replacing his crew, and admin Lori flashes 'Don't trust Albert' on the broadcast. 'It'll be debated for years to come.'","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5548,"title":"Welch sends it, Pope seals it","summary":"Last lap: Derek Welch, on much fresher tires, lunges at Goodenough for second and gets dead sideways through the S's while Tim Pope cruises home nearly three seconds clear for the win — breaking up the Team Orangutang dominance.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1048,"quote":"I got to send it. I just want to send it, you know.","context":"Kyle Vaught's pre-race interview, minutes after promising Taylor he'd be patient","gold":3},{"t":1300,"quote":"I still don't think he likes road courses. He just tolerates them.","context":"Ricky on Tim Pope early in the race — the man who went on to win it","gold":3},{"t":1868,"quote":"What they call that is a case of premature acceleration. You just hit the gas a little too hard, a little too quick.","context":"Kyle Vaught spins into the barrier trying to complete a three-wide pass","gold":4},{"t":4192,"quote":"He's still driving that truck as he flips all the way around. Completely saves it.","context":"replay of the 38 truck's full-360 save after contact with Eaton","gold":4},{"t":4489,"quote":"Craig tried to cut it off and Tim didn't let him slam that door.","context":"the live call of Pope's race-winning pass on Goodenough","gold":4},{"t":4701,"quote":"I think if I was Albert Anderson, I'd think about replacing my crew.","context":"after all five of Anderson's lug nuts fell off","gold":4},{"t":6405,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, stay vigilante, and we'll see you next time.","context":"the signature VRL sign-off to close the broadcast","gold":5},{"t":6418,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"the VRN outro tag after sign-off","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Round 6 of VRL Premiere Series Season 12 (iRacing NASCAR Trucks) at Watkins Glen, Aug 13 2025 broadcast. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: the #38 driver is captioned Gones/Gomes/Gins/Gles ('Chris Gomes' chosen; Welch's teammate shoutout 'Chris Owens' likely refers to the same driver); 'Kyle Vaught' inferred from Vaude/Walt/Vault/bought variants; 'Kelly Kills', 'Chandler Paul' (also captioned Jenner Paul), 'John Schoenbachler', 'Andrew Cawthon', and 'Mike Ever' spellings are uncertain. Jorge Rincon drew a penalty from the prior race but did not make the field. Lori (Alan's wife) is the league admin — she runs cautions, chat, and on-screen messages but is not a booth commentator. Pope stated in his winner interview this was his second road-course win in the league (first was the Chicago street course), contradicting the booth's guess that it was his first.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"5ESA0ThVfCU":{"recap":"The VRL trucks packed a 34-plus entry field into Richmond for a 200-lap Wednesday-night brawl, with polesitter Alan Vaught controlling the early going before Dale Adamson stole the Stage 1 win on pit strategy after starting 30th. The second half turned into a demolition derby: Dave Mayberry triggered the night's first Big One, Kelly Kuehl was flipped fully upside down late, and a three-to-go pileup that sent Andrew Coffin tumbling forced the race's single green-white-checkered attempt. That attempt ended in total chaos when leaders Mike Adamson and Jack Dixon tied up and spun racing for the win, freezing the field amid a storm of iRacing black flags that briefly scored Chandler Paul as the winner. After a lengthy admin review by Lori and Jess, Austin Paul was declared the official winner over Andrew Player and Eric Klafka.","winner":"Austin Paul","podium":["Austin Paul","Andrew Player","Eric Klafka"],"moments":[{"t":1810,"title":"Baker bowls into the 48 — Dale Adamson rides the wall","summary":"Early yellow as Daniel Baker's 90 comes straight down into Jack Dixon's 48, spinning it loose, then collects Dale Adamson's 746 for a wild ride into the wall with Earl Evans' bad-luck 13 left with nowhere to go.","tags":["daniel-baker","jack-dixon","dale-adamson","earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2895,"title":"Mike Taylor's miracle save","summary":"Racing tight in traffic, Mike Taylor hangs onto a wild moment — 'way to hang on to it Mike Taylor, incredible' — as the field narrowly avoids what the booth calls absolute calamity.","tags":["mike-taylor"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3852,"title":"Booth goes full Skynet over ChatGPT","summary":"During a caution the booth spirals into an all-time tangent about putting ChatGPT into iRacing, Skynet taking over the world, and killer toasters — with Turner insisting the 'CBD computer' is coming for us all.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4315,"title":"Dale Adamson wins Stage 1 from 30th","summary":"After starting 30th and getting caught in an early wreck, Dale Adamson rides an off-cycle pit strategy to the front and beats son/teammate Mike Adamson and Alan Vaught to the lap-100 stage break — up 30 spots on the night.","tags":["dale-adamson","mike-adamson","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5115,"title":"The Big One: Mayberry locks it up","summary":"The biggest wreck of the night to that point — Dave Mayberry gets the brakes locked going low, the truck goes squirrely three-and-four wide, and chaos collects Connor Hughes, David Feit, Dion Jones and Sean McDonnell, with Chandler Paul left with heavy damage and meatball flags flying.","tags":["dave-mayberry","connor-hughes","david-fite","dion-jones","shawn-mcdonald","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5505,"title":"Rincon tumbles through the air dryer","summary":"The 21 of Timmy Bates and the 28 of Jorge Rincon meet on the backstretch — Rincon goes for a tumble 'in the air dryer' and the pileup keeps growing behind, collecting Eric Klafka, Andrew Coffin and Sean McDonnell.","tags":["george-rincon","timmy-bates","eric-klafka","andrew-cauthan","shawn-mcdonald","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5800,"title":"Taylor sideways sparks another melee","summary":"Right after a restart Mike Taylor goes sideways off the corner and a big wreck erupts — John Gallagher and Dave Mayberry get tied up, with Dale Adamson, Andrew Player and the 58 all bounced around.","tags":["mike-taylor","john-gallagher","dave-mayberry","dale-adamson","andrew-player","robert-chipman"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6500,"title":"Leader Vaught nails the pit barrels","summary":"After battling Mike Adamson side-by-side for the lead for over a lap, Alan Vaught comes to pit road and slams the barrels at pit entry — a caution while he sat in his box becomes a blessing in disguise.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7160,"title":"Kelly Kuehl turtled upside down","summary":"On a late restart Albert Anderson can't get slowed from the low line and drifts up into Brayton Laster, spinning the 013 and sending Kelly Kuehl's 01 into the wall — Kuehl's truck flips and lands fully upside down, stuck turtled on the track.","tags":["kelly-keel","brayton-laster","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7785,"title":"Three to go: Coffin goes flying","summary":"With three laps left the 72 sends it in deep and a huge crash erupts — 'people tumbling and bumbling' — Andrew Coffin gets looped and airborne and Greg Klein's strong night is wrecked, forcing the one and only green-white-checkered attempt.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","greg-cline","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8070,"title":"Leaders wreck racing for the win — field frozen","summary":"On the green-white-checkered, leaders Jack Dixon and Mike Adamson race side-by-side for the win, tie up and spin just short of the line, triggering a massive pileup — the yellow freezes the field about 30 feet before the stripe and Austin Paul slips through the middle to steal the race.","tags":["jack-dixon","mike-adamson","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8268,"title":"Victory donuts while the wrong Paul is scored the winner","summary":"Austin Paul does victory donuts while iRacing's scoring melts down — brother Chandler Paul is briefly listed as the winner amid a flood of passing-under-yellow black flags. After a long admin review, officials confirm Austin Paul the winner with Andrew Player second and Eric Klafka third.","tags":["austin-paul","chandler-paul","andrew-player","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":875,"quote":"It's less than a mile track, we got about 30 trucks — you do like the Louisiana math, I'm thinking at least three fights tonight.","context":"Adam Turner sizing up the 34-truck short-track field before the green","gold":4},{"t":1190,"quote":"We continuously have to try to conquer that beast that is known as Mark Zuckerberg.","context":"The booth begging for likes and subscribes during qualifying","gold":3},{"t":2600,"quote":"Wow, what a save! We had about three or four trucks all hit the wall and pounce off of each other, playing billiards out there.","context":"A chain of near-misses off the turn-two wall somehow ends with everyone pointed straight","gold":3},{"t":3855,"quote":"What we need to do is put that ChatGPT into iRacing — and I mean it may take over the world at some point. It's coming, Skynet.","context":"Caution-lap tangent about AI taking over the world","gold":4},{"t":5419,"quote":"Adamson taking the lawnmower approach here at Richmond.","context":"Dale Adamson spins through the infield grass after leading the race","gold":3},{"t":7735,"quote":"Albert Anderson is like the John Cena of the VRL — he's a lifetime babyface, he's never the bad guy, everybody loves him.","context":"Booth reads Ricky Wittenberg's chat verdict during the great heel-vs-babyface wrestling debate","gold":4},{"t":7795,"quote":"Oh, huge crash! Oh Lord, we got people tumbling and bumbling!","context":"The three-to-go pileup that forced the green-white-checkered","gold":5},{"t":7820,"quote":"Well, I need to call some extra bambulances in there, Adam.","context":"Surveying the damage after the three-to-go wreck","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Finish decided under caution: yellow froze the field roughly 30 feet before the line on the lone green-white-checkered attempt, and iRacing's scoring cycled through several winners (including Chandler Paul) before admins Lori and Jess ruled the official top three on air at ~2:25:55 (8755s): Austin Paul, Andrew Player, Eric Klafka. Stage 1 (lap 100) won by Dale Adamson. 'David Feit' (#1) is a phonetic caption guess and may be misspelled; 'Eric Klafka' spelling inferred from repeated caption variants. Mike Everidge (#82) and Michael Edwards appear only briefly and may be caption-garbled. Ricky Wittenberg appears as a chat viewer, not a driver. Full finishing order beyond the podium was never read out due to the scoring chaos.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"5eZXql3ocAc":{"recap":"The VRL took its trucks road racing for the Texas Stampede at Circuit of the Americas, a 33-lap, no-yellows grind over COTA's 20 turns with 36 trucks taking the green. Polesitter Dustyn Eaton was in a class of his own, stretching his lead past 30 and toward 40 seconds before a packet-loss disconnect with about five laps to go ended his night in heartbreak. League owner Alan Vaught inherited the lead and calmly closed out his second win of the season ahead of teammate Greg Klein and hard-charger Trevor Robertson, who climbed 21 spots from deep in the field. Jonathan \"Chachi\" Osborne — racing with a mouth-operated controller and no force feedback — took fourth and spotlight-driver honors, while Craig Goodenough charged up 17 spots to sixth. The booth spent the closing laps running fan poll suggestions, and Albert Anderson's \"do you support public caning?\" became the running gag of the night.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Greg Cline","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1365,"title":"Green flag: five-wide into Turn 1","summary":"The field launches side by side at COTA and scatters three-, four-, even five-wide up the hill into Turn 1 with 'incidents galore', while Eaton and Henin duel for the lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","zachary-henin"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1425,"title":"Eaton charges back past Henin","summary":"After Henin squeezed ahead through the esses, Eaton gets a great launch back down the hill and retakes the lead into the hard braking zone on lap one.","tags":["dustin-eaton","zachary-henin"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2033,"title":"Anderson retires with a toothache","summary":"America's driver Albert Anderson parks the 99 early — not damage, a nasty toothache — with Kathy Anderson representing Team Albert in the chat.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2235,"title":"Eaton's clinic: 11 seconds and climbing","summary":"The booth admits they've stopped showing the leader because Eaton is 11 seconds clear and 'putting on an absolute clinic' — a gap that grows past 30 seconds and toward 40.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2490,"title":"Lori orders a 'nitrous' inspection","summary":"Race administrator Lori messages the booth that she's pulling Eaton's truck for post-race inspection because he must be running nitrous; the booth counters 'maybe the guy's just good, Lori.'","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2712,"title":"Osborne runs fourth with a mouth-operated controller","summary":"The booth marvels that Chachi is driving with his mouth on his controller, no force feedback, and sitting fourth — 'ESPN should do a story on him someday.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3354,"title":"Teammate tension: Klein hunts the boss for second","summary":"Klein runs down teammate — and team/league owner — Alan Vaught for second, the booth asking whether Klein will 'just destroy Jess' or play nice.","tags":["greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5365,"title":"The public caning poll takes over the broadcast","summary":"Albert Anderson's poll suggestion — 'do you support public caning?' — spawns the night's running gag, with the booth sentencing litterers, seat-pee-ers, non-tippers and high-beam abusers, and signing off promising a live caning of Adam Turner.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5528,"title":"Netcode chaos: Ramsey and Goodenough collide","summary":"Side by side into a tight braking zone, the 34 and 89 snap together — '100% netcode, wrecks everywhere' — replayed from the chopper camera.","tags":["nick-ramsey","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5789,"title":"Heartbreak: Eaton disconnects from a 40-second lead","summary":"With a handful of laps left and nearly 40 seconds in hand, the dominant 14 drops from the server due to packet loss, handing Alan Vaught a 12-second lead and instantly spawning conspiracy theories in the booth.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6106,"title":"Vaught nails the final corner for win No. 2","summary":"Smooth as butter through the arena section, Vaught absolutely nails the last corner to take his second win of the season, with Klein second and hard-charger Robertson third.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6203,"title":"Three-truck drag race to the line for ninth","summary":"Adamson looks inside Henin as three trucks sprint to the stripe; Ramsey holds ninth, Henin takes tenth, and Adamson settles for eleventh after Henin breaks the draft against the right-hand wall.","tags":["nick-ramsey","zachary-henin","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":956,"quote":"It's a decent track for something that they built on a landfill. This is a dump — literally, that's what they built it on.","context":"Adam Turner's scouting report on Circuit of the Americas","gold":4},{"t":1274,"quote":"I didn't get your numbers, but you're in my heart.","context":"Alan Brown racing the clock through the tail end of the 36-truck starting grid","gold":3},{"t":1794,"quote":"No Ricky, we shouldn't eat more Tide Pods... we don't condone that at AAA Broadcasting. Don't eat Tide Pods, guys.","context":"The booth riffing on Josh Bittner's Tide Pods paint scheme while Whittenburg struggled","gold":3},{"t":2498,"quote":"She's definitely going to pull Dustin Eaton's truck in for a post-race inspection — pretty sure he's running nitrous or something on that thing.","context":"Relaying race admin Lori's chat message about the runaway leader","gold":4},{"t":2712,"quote":"Driving with his mouth on his controller, with no force feedback, and he's in fourth place — that says volumes about how good of a driver this guy is.","context":"The booth on Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne running in the top five","gold":4},{"t":3354,"quote":"Here's the real fight: is Klein going to just destroy Jess, the owner of the team and league, to get second — or is he going to play nice today?","context":"Teammates Klein and Vaught closing in on each other for second","gold":3},{"t":5608,"quote":"I saw somebody throw one of those Sonic Route 44 full beverages out the window on an on-ramp — that's 10 canes, that's 10 right there.","context":"The public-caning poll segment in full swing","gold":4},{"t":5789,"quote":"Oh no, the 14 of Dustin Eaton — computer issue? What? Oh my God, packet loss. Dropped due to packet loss. No way.","context":"The dominant leader disconnects with about five laps to go","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is a best guess: captions render it 'vot/fought/vought/vau/vant'; 'Vought' appears literally once and matches Kyle ('Kyle Vault') and race administrator Lori ('Lori V'/'Lorie Vault' — she is staff, not a driver). Surnames Henin, Fight, Cin, Howe, Rincon and Kuehl are also caption best-guesses. Race ran with no yellows thrown (road-course format); only 14 trucks finished on the lead lap. Full finishing order was read on air: Vought, Klein, Robertson, Osborne, Fight, Goodenough, McDonnell, Rincon, Ramsey, Henin top ten; Eaton classified 27th after the disconnect. Robertson was hard charger (+21 spots) and had won the previous week at Bristol on an unaired night; Goodenough gained 17. Drivers 'Pope' and 'Burke' were mentioned only in historical anecdotes, and 'Zeth Hol' was mentioned as a triple-screen racer but not confirmed in the field. Next race stated as Richmond.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"5LZWTiIW7Vw":{"recap":"Albert Anderson went two-for-two to open Season 14 of the VRL Premiere Series, driving his No. 99 ToeCall machine to victory in the Peach State 200 at EchoPark Speedway one week after winning at Daytona. Polesitter Dillon Bryant controlled the opening stint of the 133-lap, 35-truck race until a rare green-flag pit cycle flipped the field — Bryant spun entering pit lane, Austin Paul was turned at pit entry, and Anderson emerged with the lead. The night's biggest wreck came just shy of lap 100 when Kelly Kuehl smacked the wall out of a three-wide battle and roughly a dozen trucks piled in, with Mike Everidge threading the wreckage untouched. Anderson survived six cautions and a three-wide charge for second on the final lap to beat Allstar Racing teammate Dillon Bryant and Chris Goans, with Tim Pope fourth and Scott Rooney fifth.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Dillon Bryant","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":714,"title":"Green flag on the Peach State 200","summary":"35 trucks take the green at EchoPark Speedway; polesitter Dillon Bryant jumps out front with Albert Anderson hanging tough on the outside line.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1210,"title":"First caution: the 16 and 31 tangle","summary":"Jacob Alesia bounces off the turn-one wall chasing Kelly Kuehl's draft, gathers it up, and turns himself off Kyle Vogt's nose for the night's first yellow.","tags":["jess-vaught","jacob-alicia","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1821,"title":"No brakes! Kyle's wall-ride save","summary":"With his pedals dead, Kyle Vogt pops the wall twice and downshifts through the gears to engine-brake the truck out of the field's way — his night later ends when the engine lets go.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2010,"title":"Everybody caught it — Klein's monster save","summary":"Adamson touches the apron at the front, a chain-reaction check-up ripples back through the pack, and Greg Klein hauls in a tremendous save — nobody wrecks, but the field splits into three packs.","tags":["mike-adamson","greg-cline","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2559,"title":"Green-flag pit stop chaos","summary":"A rare green-flag cycle bites hard: Bryant spins entering the pits, Austin Paul's No. 3 gets turned at pit entry, Everidge spins backwards on the front stretch with no caution, and Anderson cycles into the lead.","tags":["dylan-bryant","austin-paul","mike-everage","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2857,"title":"Camouflage carnage: Austin Paul hits the stalled 10","summary":"The black No. 10 sits stalled against the blacktop and Austin Paul never sees it — a vicious head-on hit that ends both of their nights.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3378,"title":"Big wreck ripples off turn one","summary":"Kelly Kuehl smacks the wall switching lanes at the front, the check-up ripples back through the pack, and Dave Mayberry gets shot in the rear despite doing everything right.","tags":["kelly-keel","dave-mayberry","kevin-hunt","dion-jones","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4538,"title":"The Big One","summary":"Three-wide near the century mark, Kelly Kuehl gets squirrelly into the wall and roughly a dozen trucks pile in behind — the biggest wreck of the night, with Osborne collecting Kill hard at the tail end.","tags":["kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player","mike-adamson","jason-gaines","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4716,"title":"Everidge threads the needle","summary":"Riding on board, Mike Everidge calmly backs his No. 82 down through the middle of the Big One — the replay shows you couldn't slide a piece of paper between him and the 434.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5563,"title":"Player spun with 11 to go","summary":"Sixth caution of the night as Andy Player gets spooked by contact ahead, dips low off turn four, and gets spun tangling with the 19.","tags":["andrew-player","scott-milner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5941,"title":"Heartbreak for Dion Jones","summary":"Racing three-wide inside the lead pack with four laps to go, Dion Jones gets wrecked out of a strong run — and the race stays green to the finish.","tags":["dion-jones","george-rincon","gordon-spain"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6050,"title":"Three wide to the checkers — Anderson goes two-for-two","summary":"The field goes three wide for second on the final lap, but Albert Anderson has it in the bag — he brings the 99 home for his second straight win, with teammate Dillon Bryant second and a fuel-saving Chris Goans third.","tags":["albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","chris-goans","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":441,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream. This is VRN, your trusted leader in e-motorsports.","context":"the channel's signature bumper opening the broadcast","gold":4},{"t":974,"quote":"51 Superman's got his cape out right now and he's looking to try and lead every lap of this race.","context":"Dillon Bryant dominating the opening stint from the pole","gold":3},{"t":1390,"quote":"I'm sure Jacob won't like that answer, but I didn't move down. I don't know what you want me to do, dude.","context":"Kyle Vogt's in-race booth interview after the first-caution contact with the 31","gold":4},{"t":2010,"quote":"Oh, wreck. Wreck. Are they catching it? Everybody caught it. Oh my goodness. What a save.","context":"the whole pack checks up off Adamson's apron slip and nobody crashes","gold":4},{"t":2967,"quote":"Man, you talk about the case of camouflage. I didn't even see it at first.","context":"replay of Austin Paul hitting the stalled black No. 10 that blended into the blacktop","gold":3},{"t":4768,"quote":"Does he have contact? You probably couldn't slide a piece of paper between him and the other truck.","context":"the money-shot replay of Mike Everidge threading the Big One untouched","gold":4},{"t":6050,"quote":"Three wide here, folks. Three wide for second place. They're all trying to get to that 99 machine. Are they going to wreck?","context":"the final-lap call as Anderson holds off a three-wide charge","gold":4},{"t":7170,"quote":"Until next time, race fans, remember: stay sharp, stay fast, and above all else, stay vigilante.","context":"the signature VRN broadcast signoff","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Booth host's surname is garbled by auto-captions ('Alan Vot', 'Allan') — 'Alan Vogt' is a best guess; his son Kyle (No. 16, 'Kyle Vault'/'Kyle Walton' in captions) raced until pedal/engine failure ended his night. 'Chris Gones' also appears as 'Gomes' — real spelling uncertain. The league owner confirms the canonical spelling Jorge Rincon, pronounced 'George'; Ren/Rencon/Rinkon/Ranc remain source-caption variants rather than competing identities. The stalled No. 10 that Austin Paul hit is inferred to be Andrew Cowan from context and the finishing order. Lori (Alan's wife) is the league admin/event manager, credited throughout but not a booth commentator. Winner confirmed on air and in the victory interview; full 35-truck results are read at 1:57:46 (7066s). Race: Peach State 200, VRL Premiere Series S14 R2, EchoPark Speedway (virtual Hampton, GA), 133 laps / 200 miles, 35 trucks, six cautions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"5T49iFdFlKM":{"recap":"David Emig dominated \"The Takedown\" at Texas Motor Speedway, sweeping the lone midway stage and the overall win in the No. 2 truck over a massive 42-truck field, saving his tires all night and pulling away at the end. Trevor Robertson closed to within six tenths on the final lap but ran out of time, finishing second ahead of Tim Pope, Albert Anderson, and Jeremiah Burke — putting every Limitless truck (3rd, 4th, 5th, and 9th) inside the top ten. Despite the huge field, the 100-lapper ran remarkably clean: a lap-one pileup off turn two, an Earl Evans pit-exit spin that sent Chad McCabe into the inside wall, and a stage-ending scramble at pit entrance were the only cautions, and 41 of 42 starters finished. Albert Anderson provided the late fireworks, charging up 19 spots on fresh rubber \"like they're standing still.\" League commissioner Alan Vaught capped the night in the booth, praising the new rules package — single stage break, 17x DQ limit, and per-incident review — after charging back from a lap down to finish 11th.","winner":"David Emig","podium":["David Emig","Trevor Robertson","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":815,"title":"Lap-one pileup off turn two","summary":"Cold tires bite on the opening lap — Dustin Riehle gets sideways off the turn-two exit and drops down into traffic, collecting Matt Beamer while Jeffrey Johnson 'got smoked,' bringing out the first caution seconds into the race.","tags":["dustin-reilly","matt-beamer","jeffrey-johnson","charlie-herkis","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1405,"title":"Osborne hammers the outside wall","summary":"Jonathan Osborne goes hard into the outside wall and then down into the inside wall, taking heavy aero damage that ends his shot at the front after starting second.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1642,"title":"Emig bops around Long for the lead","summary":"David Emig takes the lead for the first time, working around Jonah Long as the front three nearly go three wide in lap traffic — the start of Emig's run to the front.","tags":["david-emig","jonah-long"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2042,"title":"Wreck on pit lane during green-flag stops","summary":"Green-flag pit stops turn dicey — Andrew Coffin gets spun around on pit lane, and Kuehl bumps Player on pit road in the bumping and banging.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","kelly-keel","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2130,"title":"Evans spins off pit exit, McCabe pounds the wall","summary":"The 13 of Earl Evans kicks it loose coming out of the pits, and the blind corner catches Chad McCabe's No. 11, who hits the inside wall hard — Greg Klein just barely checks up in time to save his blue chrome machine.","tags":["earl-evans","chad-mccabe","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2496,"title":"Three-wide restart, Poke squeezes through","summary":"Jonah Long and Jorge Rincon restart side by side up front and the field goes three wide behind them, with Tony Pope squeezing through the middle in wild restart traffic.","tags":["jonah-long","george-rincon","tony-polk"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2685,"title":"Stage-ending scramble at pit entrance","summary":"A wreck erupts at the pit entrance grass to end stage one — the 63 and 92 bang doors, Dustyn Eaton checks up in the middle of near-three-wide traffic and gets tangled up as trucks scatter through the grass and down pit lane.","tags":["dustin-eaton","josh-oxendine","greg-cline","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2816,"title":"Emig wins stage one","summary":"David Emig takes the caution-shortened stage-one win under the new single-midway-stage format, banking the bonus points he would later pair with the race win.","tags":["david-emig"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3926,"title":"Anderson's fresh-tire rampage","summary":"Albert Anderson hits the 'money stop' and comes out flying on new tires, driving around everybody 'like they're standing still,' sending it three-and-four wide through slower traffic and rocketing up to fourth — up 19 spots on the night.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4580,"title":"Emig holds off Robertson at the line","summary":"White flag at Texas — Trevor Robertson claws to within six tenths but it's not enough, as David Emig crosses the line to sweep the stage and the race win, with Limitless teammates Pope, Anderson, and Burke rounding out the top five.","tags":["david-emig","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5455,"title":"The Commissioner takes the booth","summary":"League boss Alan Vaught, fresh off a lap-down comeback to 11th, joins the broadcast to grab a beer and explain the new rules package — IPL scrapped, every incident reviewed with points penalties, one stage break on trial — declaring he had more fun driving from the back than in the first two races of the season.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":425,"quote":"I am Alan Brown, and my boss is gonna find out that I do not make threats — I make promises.","context":"opening the broadcast after the national anthem","gold":3},{"t":1506,"quote":"You got a better chance of entering chicken crab bingo at Jenny's Little Longhorn in Austin on a Sunday afternoon than you could do of winning this thing.","context":"sizing up the 42-truck field early in the race","gold":5},{"t":2056,"quote":"You ain't ever been going down the road and a car in front of you is going slower than the speed limit? You want to give him a little bump, get him up to speed.","context":"defending the bumping on pit road during green-flag stops","gold":3},{"t":2707,"quote":"These boys are smoking that grass — they need to go about 75 miles north of Oklahoma, you can smoke that grass all you want.","context":"trucks scattering through the infield grass in the stage-ending wreck","gold":4},{"t":2806,"quote":"I've never adored Greg — I mean, I've been doored a lot by Greg.","context":"reviewing the Greg Klein door-banging replay from the stage-one wreck","gold":4},{"t":3575,"quote":"He must have put them James Bond slicks on and just run over his own oil slick.","context":"the 99 of 'bond villain' Chris Zofeld bouncing off the outside wall","gold":3},{"t":5530,"quote":"Whatever you did work, because these guys were racing their ass off tonight and nobody was getting too crazy out there.","context":"the booth telling commissioner Alan Vaught the new rules delivered","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"100-lap day race at Texas Motor Speedway (repaved quad oval), 42 trucks, 103F track conditions, single midway stage break at lap 50 (new format on trial), 17x incident DQ limit. Full finishing order was read on air; only top 3 listed as podium. Names are best-guess from heavy auto-caption garbling: 'David Emig' also rendered as 'Dave Emmett/David Emmett'; 'Jorge Rincon' had many variants; 'Dustin Riehle' is inferred from caption 'Dustin really'; the No. 20 is 'Jeffrey Johnson' in grid and results but called 'Ethan Johnson' once mid-race. 'Ricky Whittenburg' spelling per league sponsor DND Race Grafix owner (captions say Wittenberg). Chapter marker 'Dustyn Eaton' (2419s) does not correspond to an interview — post-race interviews were Cody Sanderson (random draw, 17th), Tim Pope (3rd), Trevor Robertson (2nd), David Emig (winner), and Alan Vaught (commissioner). Kale Turboville was mentioned only in reference to a different night's race, so he is excluded from the driver list. Next race announced: Richmond.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"6SMmRzlxoGM":{"recap":"The VRL trucks swapped ovals for the Watkins Glen Cup layout, and a full 36-truck field turned the Road Racing Rumble into a night of off-tracks, spins, and fuel-mileage poker. Polesitter Alan Vaught dominated the opening stage before turn-one contact on the restart after the lap-16 competition caution spun him from second back to 17th, and stage winner Jeremiah Burke controlled the second half until a bus-stop spin on the final lap dropped him from contention to fourth. That left the race to fuel gamblers Andrew Player and Todd Smith, who had stayed out since lap 25 — Smith ran dry exiting the final corner, both leaders spun in a drag race to the line, and Player's No. 18 squiggled across for his third win of the season. Smith coasted home second as hard charger of the day, up 31 spots, while Trevor Robertson's late splash-and-go netted third, up 24 spots, as blown-up trucks from a last-lap front-stretch melee littered the finish.","winner":"Andrew Player","podium":["Andrew Player","Todd Smith","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1387,"title":"Green at the Glen: who survives turn one?","summary":"The full field storms into turn one for the first time — the 66 takes a ride through the grass but everybody survives, with Vaught leading Osborne up through the Esses.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1762,"title":"Wittenberg clocks Poke Salad Tony","summary":"Ricky Wittenberg absolutely clocks Tony Polk in turn one, leaving an engine smoking and the No. 8 Craftsman pickup crab-walking with suspension damage.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","tony-polk"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3177,"title":"Burke bags the stage as the yellow flies","summary":"The lap-16 competition caution falls with Jeremiah Burke edging Alan Vaught for the stage win — while his crew sweats whether he has the fuel to make it back around to pit lane.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3285,"title":"Wade runs dry and shreds the bus-stop cone","summary":"Out of fuel under caution, Dustin Wade cuts the bus stop and vaporizes the cone — the booth nerds out over iRacing's new debris physics and a theory about a box of 16-penny nails.","tags":["dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3821,"title":"Polesitter Vaught spins on the restart","summary":"Right off the halfway restart, turn-one contact spins the dominant No. 33 of Alan Vaught from second all the way back to 17th — a heartbreaker that ends his shot at the win.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4038,"title":"Two trucks into the bus-stop tire barriers","summary":"The 123 and the 2 make contact entering the bus stop and slide together into the tire barriers in the race's biggest two-truck wreck.","tags":["john-gallagher","david-emig"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4070,"title":"'The greatest driver of all time'","summary":"Fan Drew Holland crowns hard-charging Trevor Robertson the GOAT in chat — 'he is a machine' — and the booth runs with the Muhammad Ali bit as the 64 climbs 22-plus spots.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4268,"title":"Wittenberg disconnects, dreams of vodka","summary":"Ricky Wittenberg's night ends with a disconnect; he resurfaces in YouTube chat wishing vodka came out of his shower head.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4797,"title":"Splash-and-go poker at the front","summary":"Robertson and then leader Burke dive in for late splash-and-gos, handing the front of the field to Andrew Player and Todd Smith — who last pitted on lap 25 in the ultimate fuel gamble.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","andrew-player","todd-smith"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5084,"title":"Burke's final-lap bus-stop heartbreak","summary":"Perfect all race long, Jeremiah Burke pushes too hard chasing the leaders and spins coming out of the bus stop on the final lap, tumbling from a possible win to fourth.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5107,"title":"Drag race, double spin — Player steals it","summary":"Todd Smith runs out of fuel exiting the final corner, both leaders spin in the drag race to the line, and Andrew Player squiggles around for his third win of the season — while the 63 pushes Smith's dead truck back to victory lane.","tags":["andrew-player","todd-smith"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5140,"title":"Last-lap melee on the front stretch","summary":"Osborne and Klein beat and bang out of the final turn in their own drag race, collecting Jorge Rincon and Dion Jones — blown-up trucks litter the front stretch at the checkers.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","greg-cline","george-rincon","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1399,"quote":"We send it off down into turn number one — who is going to survive and who is going to die?","context":"the green flag drops and the field funnels into turn one for the first time","gold":4},{"t":2033,"quote":"I don't know why they call them S's — is it shaped like an ass?","context":"the booth trying to sort out Watkins Glen corner names mid-race","gold":3},{"t":3318,"quote":"You know what somebody did? They put a box of 16 penny nails underneath the cone — that's what he just ran over.","context":"Dustin Wade, out of fuel, obliterates the bus-stop cone under caution","gold":4},{"t":4856,"quote":"Today's the kind of day where I just kind of wish vodka came out of my shower head.","context":"the booth reading Ricky Wittenberg's chat message after his mid-race disconnect","gold":4},{"t":4889,"quote":"One guy lost his internet, the other one had to go to the bathroom — so he won.","context":"recalling Josh Buettner's 'easiest race win ever' at the Red Bull Ring","gold":4},{"t":5117,"quote":"It's gonna be a drag race as both drivers spin out — the 18 gonna be able to squiggle on around — Andrew Player sneaks out a win, oh my goodness!","context":"the final-corner finish as Smith runs dry and both leaders spin","gold":5},{"t":5347,"quote":"We had people struggling on fuel, we had strategies, we had spin outs — we had just about everything happen on that final lap. That was unbelievable.","context":"the booth catching its breath right after the checkered flag","gold":3},{"t":6122,"quote":"You probably had about 12 ounces more of fuel than Todd Smith — a beer's worth of fuel got you across the line.","context":"winner's interview with Andrew Player after the fuel-mileage finish","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"45-lap race on the Watkins Glen Cup layout in NASCAR trucks, run 2022-12-07 (booth notes Pearl Harbor Remembrance Day, 81 years). Presented by Blue Fox Properties; broadcast by AAA Broadcasting. Auto-captions garble names heavily: 'David Feit' (#1) may be Feit/Fite; 'Charlie Harkison' (#83) is also read as 'Harkins' in the finish rundown; 'Tony Polk' (#8) is once read as 'Tony Pope'; 'Mike Sobanovsky' (#34) spelling is uncertain across four variants. The 23rd starting position was never announced (36 drivers gridded across 37 called slots). Ricky Wittenberg (#55) disconnected mid-race and was scored 35th. Random draw driver of the day: Austin Paul (16th). Booth mentions league organizers Jess and Lori; next week is Talladega.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"72Aj4TIu5Fg":{"recap":"VRL hit the three-quarter-mile Richmond Raceway for the Richmond 200 — 267 laps of tire-cooking short-track survival, with a 17-car field fighting 94-degree track temps during a nationwide heat wave. Pole-sitter Alan Vaught controlled the early laps before Jim Ott ran him down for the first lead change of the night, and a rare Vigilante caution flew when Russ Endicott and Chandler Paul tangled with Vaught left nowhere to go. The ensuing restart turned into chaos when the leaders never launched, triggering a pileup that swept up Mike Adamson, Jeff Ottinger, Jonathan Osborne, and Jason Airson. Adamson rebounded to grab the lead on a wild near-five-wide restart before Ott wrestled it back around lap 79. The broadcast cut off near the lap-100 mark with the finish unaired, Vaught fading to fifth on fast repairs and Ott back out front.","winner":null,"podium":[],"moments":[{"t":1194,"title":"Green flag on the Richmond 200","summary":"Pole-sitter Alan Vaught gets a great jump as the field piles into turn one, cars already kissing the outside wall on lap 1.","tags":["jess-vaught","jason-airson","jim-ott"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1387,"title":"Burke goes Tokyo drifting","summary":"Jeremiah Burke throws a massive slide down the backstretch, saves it, but coughs up every position he'd gained.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1857,"title":"Ott hunts down Vaught for the lead","summary":"Vaught's tires go gooey off turn four and Jim Ott shoots down the inside for the first lead change of the night.","tags":["jim-ott","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1945,"title":"Big crash brings out a rare yellow","summary":"Russ Endicott and Chan the Man Chandler Paul get together and Alan Vaught has nowhere to go, drawing a caution the booth calls very rare for Vigilante.","tags":["russ-endicott","chandler-paul","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2176,"title":"Drivers arguing on the radio","summary":"Under yellow the booth eavesdrops on drivers bickering over the wreck — 'somebody's probably going to get reprimanded and maybe we'll see a fight.'","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2210,"title":"Nobody goes — restart pileup","summary":"The leaders never launch past the restart zone and the field stacks up in an 'absolute kerfuffle' — Adamson launches Airson, Ottinger gets collected, and Osborne loses his front bumper.","tags":["mike-adamson","jason-airson","jeff-ottinger","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2677,"title":"Chan the Man's computer betrays him","summary":"Chandler Paul spears hard left into the wall when something pops up and minimizes iRacing mid-corner — he later disconnects saying 'now I remember why I hate this track, I just got run over.'","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2994,"title":"Endicott ricochets into Burke","summary":"The 57 of Russ Endicott bounces off the wall and drills the side of Jeremiah Burke's 753 — Endicott's second incident of a rough night.","tags":["russ-endicott","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3105,"title":"America's driver tells the truth","summary":"Mid-race interview with fan favorite Albert Anderson at his home track — asked if he's laying back saving tires, he admits he's actually going as hard as he can.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3248,"title":"Almost five wide on the restart","summary":"Dion Jones brings them to green and the midfield fans out nearly five wide — Hot Rod Mayberry goes for a ride and is saved by other bumpers as Mike Adamson slices through the mess.","tags":["dion-jones","dave-mayberry","mike-adamson","albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3300,"title":"Adamson storms to the lead","summary":"On fresh momentum from the wild restart, Mike Adamson finds the rhythm on the outside and takes the lead from Alan Vaught with Jim Ott lurking.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3386,"title":"Ott wrestles the lead back","summary":"Jim Ott noses under Adamson lap after lap on the bottom, Adamson hangs tough on the outside, but Ott finally completes the pass around lap 79 — the last lead change before the stream cuts.","tags":["jim-ott","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1251,"quote":"I guess he got tired of winning, so he didn't show up.","context":"on points contender Tim Pope skipping the race","gold":4},{"t":1387,"quote":"Jeremiah goes Tokyo drifting down the back stretch!","context":"Burke saves a huge slide but loses positions","gold":4},{"t":1466,"quote":"These drivers are going to have a Darlington stripe — heck, they're not gonna have a right side of their car if this keeps going.","context":"the whole field scraping the outside wall early","gold":4},{"t":1947,"quote":"Big crash! Big crash! Oh no!","context":"the call as Endicott and Chandler Paul wreck and collect Vaught","gold":4},{"t":2094,"quote":"Is it still Sunoco racing fuel? Oh yeah, it always is — getting that sunshine and dinosaurs.","context":"booth banter during pit stops under the first yellow","gold":3},{"t":2232,"quote":"Really nobody went, and that just caused the absolute kerfuffle behind him.","context":"diagnosing the botched-restart pileup","gold":5},{"t":3180,"quote":"I would love to tell you that I'm laying back taking it easy, but I'm actually going as pretty hard as I can.","context":"Albert Anderson's honest answer in his mid-race interview","gold":4},{"t":3364,"quote":"I need to relearn how to count, because that looked like it was almost five wide going down through there.","context":"reacting to the wild late restart","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Broadcast (58 min) covers only roughly the first 100 of 267 laps — the stream ends mid-race, so winner, podium, and finish are unknown. 'Jason Airson' is a best-guess spelling (captions alternate airson/ayers/harrison/airston). 'David Feit' was heard only as 'david fight' before disconnecting early as a start-and-park. A non-racing driver, 'Big Show' Dustin (surname garbled, possibly Riley), was wished happy birthday. Tim Pope mentioned as an absent points contender. Booth first names per captions: two Alans (Brown and English) plus pit reporter Adam Turner. League sponsor read: DND Race Grafix / Keller Williams of Johnson City TN (Ricky Wittenberg).","resultConfidence":"winner-unknown-or-multi-stage"},"75zygDwW7S4":{"recap":"Throwback Night brought 39 trucks and a triple-digit track temperature to Rockingham for 150 laps of short-track mayhem, with only four tire sets and two fast repairs per driver. Cautions flew all night: Greg Klein bounced off the bumpy outside wall from the front row on lap 2, a mid-race Big One sent a truck upside down and collected nearly a third of the field, and Tim Pope went barrel rolling in a late pileup that ended with two angry disconnects. Trevor Robertson missed the start with internet trouble, then drove from dead last to steal the stage win in a one-lap shootout. When Trevor Robertson and the 4 of Dion Jones wrecked behind the leaders on the one-attempt green-white-checker, Todd Smith's No. 66 M&M's throwback Toyota took the win under caution, making him the league's ninth different winner in ten races and punching his playoff ticket. Dustin Wade, only three months into iRacing, finished second as the hard charger up 28 spots, and Alan Vaught rallied from a smoking, lap-down truck to complete the podium.","winner":"Todd Smith","podium":["Todd Smith","Dustin Wade","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1365,"title":"Klein Clobbers the Wall on Lap 2","summary":"From the front row, Greg Klein bounces off the notoriously bumpy outside wall in turns 1 and 2 on the second lap, spinning back across the track and drawing the night's first caution.","tags":["greg-cline","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1653,"title":"Kilgore's Slingshot to the Lead","summary":"On the restart 'Rocket Man' Russ Kilgore rockets the No. 7 around the outside starters and slingshots all the way to the front of the field.","tags":["russ-kilgore","todd-smith","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2109,"title":"Face-Cam Ice in a Close Call","summary":"A wreck unfolds right in front of Dustin Wade's driver face-cam and he doesn't even change expressions, while Jonah Long fights a wild save after contact involving Dustyn Eaton and the 5 slaps the outside wall hard.","tags":["dustin-wade","jonah-long","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3304,"title":"Late Yellow, Big Pileup off Turn 2","summary":"The 28 of Jorge Rincon pinches up against Osborne and shoots across the track; Burke slams into Klein in the chain reaction as a late-thrown yellow leaves mayhem all over the racetrack.","tags":["george-rincon","jeremiah-burke","greg-cline","trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3488,"title":"Pope Doesn't Need Numbers","summary":"The booth realizes race leader Tim Pope's throwback truck has no number on it at all — 'We know who Pope is' — just John 3:16 on the back quarter panel, so he escapes the usual shaming.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3618,"title":"Coffin's Dukes of Hazzard Save","summary":"Andrew Coffin locks the tires, drops through the grass, and comes back out 'Dukes of Hazzard style' — holding onto it without even having to go airborne and jump a creek.","tags":["andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4181,"title":"The Zuckerberg Like-Button Rant","summary":"Under caution the booth declares war on the like count — Zuckerberg's got a pistol to their head, there's only three thumbs up on this machine, and it ain't sixteen.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4649,"title":"Robertson Steals the Stage Shootout","summary":"After losing internet and missing the start, Trevor Robertson stays out on strategy and wins the stage in a one-lap shootout — up nearly 40 spots from dead last in the Gorilla Glue truck.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4768,"title":"Vaught's Truck Starts Smoking","summary":"Running in the lead battle, Alan Vaught trails smoke and crawls down the apron under green, falling laps down — the low point of a comeback that ends on the podium.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5436,"title":"The Big One: Upside Down at The Rock","summary":"A wall-scraping, wounded Dave Mayberry gets collected off turn 2 and the field folds up behind him: a truck flips upside down, Austin Paul and Jeremiah Burke go for wild rides, and the carnage sweeps up trucks all across the track.","tags":["dave-mayberry","kelly-keel","mike-everage","george-rincon","austin-paul","robert-jordan","gary-godso","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6895,"title":"Pope Goes Barrel Rolling","summary":"Contact from the 14 of Dustyn Eaton triggers late-race mayhem that sends Tim Pope barrel rolling; Kilgore is furious on the radio, both he and Pope disconnect for the night, and Ricky Whittenburg barely threads through the carnage.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-eaton","andrew-cauthan","josh-oxendine","russ-kilgore","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7803,"title":"Green-White-Checker: Smith Seals It","summary":"On the one-and-only green-white-checker attempt Todd Smith nails the restart from the front row; Trevor Robertson and Dion Jones wreck behind him and the caution freezes the field — Smith wins under yellow, VRL's ninth different winner in ten races.","tags":["todd-smith","dustin-wade","trevor-robertson","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":839,"quote":"There's going to be some hatred left out on the track tonight.","context":"Pre-race preview of 150 laps at the one-mile Rock","gold":4},{"t":2086,"quote":"If you don't have a mark on your truck after this thing, you didn't really race — you didn't try hard enough.","context":"Early-race beating and banging all over the track","gold":4},{"t":3630,"quote":"Came back out Dukes of Hazzard style and still held it — didn't even have to go airborne and jump a creek to do it.","context":"Andrew Coffin saves it through the grass","gold":4},{"t":4187,"quote":"Listen here, this Zuckerberg guy's got like a pistol to my head... there's only three thumbs up on this machine. Y'all put some thumbs up on here!","context":"Booth begging for likes under caution","gold":5},{"t":4709,"quote":"It's a lot of talk out there on the radio, which I think means violence.","context":"Tempers rising after another stage-end wreck","gold":4},{"t":5870,"quote":"I'm gonna coin a new phrase for that — that's the Canadian hug, that's the Canadian crash... a nice friendly crash where nobody really gets hurt.","context":"After an unusually gentle multi-truck spin","gold":4},{"t":7736,"quote":"Nobody puts English in the corner.","context":"The booth's hillbilly tangent goes Dirty Dancing","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Results were announced as unofficial pending certification by Lori and the VRL admin team; the race ended under caution on the one-attempt green-white-checker. Auto-caption spellings are uncertain in places: the No. 82 was called both 'Mike Edwards' and 'Mike Everidge' (same driver); 'David Feit' (No. 1, Hooters/Kulwicki throwback), 'Gary Godsoe' (No. 50, also captioned 'Gary Gonzo'), and 'David Emig' (No. 2) are best guesses. Jeff Ottinger's No. 76 carried the number 44 on the truck all night. Robert Chipman was mentioned as unable to race due to a computer issue. Trevor Robertson won stage 1; full finishing order was read out at approximately 2:28:00. The captioned phrase 'Justin Lori put out the challenge' appears to be a garble of 'Jess and Lori,' the league admins.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"7a4_w5983wU":{"recap":"Mike Adamson drove the No. 51 to victory at New Hampshire's Magic Mile, winning a 200-lap strategy grinder that ran green from an early mystery caution all the way to the checkered flag. Team Limitless flexed all night — running 1-2-3 at one stage — with Jeremiah Burke charging up 15 spots for hard-charger honors and a third-place finish, while teammate Tim Pope's podium hopes died with a late pit-road speeding penalty. Alan Vaught nursed a damaged No. 33 home in second after sticking to his pit strategy. The night's real villain was the iRacing service itself: waves of packet-loss disconnections claimed Ricky Whittenburg and Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry and cost pole-sitter Jim Ott four laps mid-race, though he fought back to finish 11th. Kelly Kiel took a quiet fourth with Eric Klafka completing the top five.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Alan Vaught","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1425,"title":"Green flag — and Endicott's night goes sideways","summary":"The field roars off side by side at the Magic Mile, and within a lap Russ Endicott's car is already 'blown up' — hood gone in a lap-one tangle he'd drag around for 100+ laps.","tags":["russ-endicott","dion-jones","chad-mccabe"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1690,"title":"Vaught steals the lead on lap 9","summary":"Jim Ott floats out onto the granite, Alan Vaught refuses him an inch of room and crossovers underneath to take the lead on lap nine.","tags":["jess-vaught","jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2134,"title":"The night's only (mystery) caution","summary":"A yellow flies with no incident anywhere in sight — the booth replays Tim Pope's three-wide contact but never finds a cause. It ends up being the only caution of the entire race.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2406,"title":"Restart stacks up three (then four) wide","summary":"On the restart the 51, the 4 and the 28 go three wide with the 11 joining in — 'whoa, they soldered it up thank goodness' — a huge checkup but no yellow.","tags":["mike-adamson","dion-jones","george-rincon","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2600,"title":"Ott hunts down Vaught on fresh rubber","summary":"With a 23-lap tire difference, Jim Ott runs the leader down, dives to the inside off turn two and drags Vaught side by side down the back straight before clearing him for the lead, Adamson following through.","tags":["jim-ott","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3817,"title":"Osborne's white-knuckle save","summary":"Fresh off pit road, Jonathan Osborne snaps sideways — 'save it buddy... wow' — and wrangles the 81 back just before collecting Eric Klafka.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4059,"title":"Four-car pileup — and it stays green","summary":"The 4 of Dion Jones slams the outside wall after contact from Endicott, Jorge Rincon piles in hard with nowhere to go and Alan Vaught barely checks up — at least four cars collected, no yellow thrown.","tags":["dion-jones","george-rincon","russ-endicott","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4355,"title":"The disconnect plague strikes","summary":"A wave of iRacing packet loss drops cars all over the track — Ricky Whittenburg and Hot Rod Mayberry vanish, and frontrunner Jim Ott loses four laps to a mid-race disconnect that reshapes the whole race.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","dave-mayberry","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5141,"title":"Three wide that'll put a smile on your face","summary":"Mike Adamson splits Eric Klafka and Derek Welch three wide on newer tires and cuts through into third, 'shot out of a gun' as he leaves Vaught in the dust.","tags":["mike-adamson","eric-klafka","derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7362,"title":"Broadcaster curse: Pope black-flagged","summary":"Seconds after the booth predicts a clean splash-and-go, Tim Pope is black-flagged for speeding on his final stop — the penalty costs him three laps and drops a podium contender to 12th.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7988,"title":"Adamson's connection blinks with two to go","summary":"Leading by 13 seconds, Mike Adamson's car starts blinking in and out with packet loss inside the final laps — the booth begs the people in his house to get off the PlayStation and give him bandwidth.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":8047,"title":"Adamson conquers the Magic Mile","summary":"Mike Adamson survives the late connection scare to take the checkered flag for Limitless Motorsports; Alan Vaught brings a damaged 33 home second and hard charger Jeremiah Burke completes the podium after climbing 15 spots.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":972,"quote":"You may like to rock, but you got to stay off that granite, man — the outsides of these corners, they are brutal.","context":"Key to the race intro at the Granite State's Magic Mile","gold":4},{"t":2350,"quote":"No, I did not get monkey pox — it's just a sinus infection.","context":"Allen English answers a Twitch chatter asking if 'the Louisiana fella' caught monkey pox","gold":4},{"t":4391,"quote":"Well, you know, there's no easier way to pass somebody than have them disappear.","context":"Greg Klein on the wave of disconnections sweeping the field","gold":5},{"t":4581,"quote":"Throw a piece of paper between those two cars and you'd have yourself a pretty little drawing with paint on both sides.","context":"Stanley and the lapped car squeeze by millimeters apart","gold":4},{"t":7716,"quote":"He races with his mouth and he gives these guys a run for their money every week... that's a true race car driver right there, whatever it takes.","context":"The booth spotlights Jonathan Osborne, who races with a special mouth-operated controller","gold":4},{"t":8000,"quote":"This is where he's yelling at the people next room — get off the PlayStation, give me some bandwidth here!","context":"Leader Mike Adamson's connection blinks in and out with two laps to go","gold":4},{"t":8455,"quote":"I'm still convinced this track needs to be turned into an industrial complex or something — it needs to go away.","context":"Podium finisher Jeremiah Burke shares his feelings about New Hampshire in the post-race interview","gold":4},{"t":8664,"quote":"You need to find some chicken bones and draw some circles on the ground or something to change your luck, man.","context":"The booth prescribes a cure for Alan Vaught's streak of bad luck after he lost all sound mid-race","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"The lone caution (~lap 30) was thrown with no visible incident; the booth suspected an admin/technical glitch. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Dustin Riehle' (always captioned 'dustin really'), 'David Feit' (possibly Fite), 'Kelly Kiel' (also captioned 'keel'), 'Tony Polk' (also 'poke'), 'Jeff Ottinger' (wildly garbled variants), 'Jorge Rincon' (many garbles). Regular co-host Adam Turner was absent (training class in Oklahoma City); Greg Klein of Midwest Days of Thunder guested in the booth. Lori Vaught served as race control/caution admin. Format: 200 laps, NASCAR Xfinity cars, fixed setup, 5 tire sets, 70 fuel, 17x incident limit, one fast repair. Full finishing order was read out in the closing rundown (Adamson, Vaught, Burke, Kiel, Klafka, Welch, Rincon, Ottinger, Stanley, Collins top 10). Post-race extras: random-draw driver of the day Derek Welch (6th); fan of the race Brandon Taylor. Next race: Kentucky night race, 133 laps.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"7BrMIV7AbCE":{"recap":"The penultimate race of the VRL Trucks season brought a 26-truck field to Talladega for 100 laps, and the racing stayed stunningly clean early — the first caution didn't fly until lap 34, and every truck remained on the lead lap deep into the second half with nobody forced to tow. The night turned wild late, capped by a massive Big One with about five laps to go when Kelly Kuehl accidentally bump-drafted teammate Dustin Riehle around in the corner, collecting half the field including the entire Vigilante Force team. On the lone green-white-checker attempt, Albert Anderson took a huge push from Justin French off turn four to beat Limitless Motorsports teammate Jeremiah Burke — who ran out of fuel about a hundred feet before the line — for his first VRL win. Burke took second and hard charger honors on his birthday, French finished third, and Limitless put three trucks in the top four with Mike Adamson fourth. Points leader John Ellis finished eighth to carry a commanding lead into next week's championship finale at Auto Club.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Jeremiah Burke","Justin French"],"moments":[{"t":2022,"title":"Vaught and Burke charge up 'like a bat out of hell'","summary":"The 33 and 753 rocket up the high line with a stunning closing rate, blindsiding the booth with how much momentum they carried to the front.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":2,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3429,"title":"Klafka blinks out of existence — then reappears four wide","summary":"A netcode hiccup makes the 88 vanish and reappear right in the middle of the three, briefly making it four wide and scattering the whole chase pack.","tags":["eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3545,"title":"Ottinger goes for a tumble — first caution at lap 34","summary":"Contact between the 14 and 82 in the chase pack sends Jeff Ottinger spinning like a top and Eric Klafka on a crazy wild ride; everyone stays on all four tires.","tags":["jeff-ottinger","mike-everage","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4135,"title":"Lap-42 pileup tears up Jordan's engine","summary":"The 33 gets sideways off a misaligned teammate push, Robert Jordan clips Vaught and tears his engine up, Tim Pope goes for a ride, and Albert Anderson misses the whole mess by millimeters.","tags":["robert-jordan","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","dave-mayberry","jeff-ottinger","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5265,"title":"Jordan gets the tablecloth ripped from underneath him","summary":"Stuck in the middle three wide, the 204 gets tagged, comes back down the track into Jonathan Osborne, and brings out the fourth caution of the night.","tags":["robert-jordan","jonathan-osborne","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5363,"title":"Osborne's controller-jiggling save","summary":"Jonathan Osborne hangs on to a wild sideways moment at 200 mph — 'holy smokes, he was jiggling that controller back and forth a lot, I can tell you that.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6880,"title":"Late chain-reaction crash collects the contenders","summary":"Bumpers not square between the 203 and 81 send Russ Kilgore around; John Ellis and Tim Pope get pieces of it and Alan Vaught comes out missing his hood with about 25 to go.","tags":["earl-evans","jonathan-osborne","russ-kilgore","john-ellis","jess-vaught","jeff-snyder","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7959,"title":"Four wide into the turn with nine to go","summary":"'Oh Lord, four wide going in the turn' — the aggression ramps up as the field goes three and four wide fighting through lap traffic in the closing laps.","tags":["jeff-snyder"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":8169,"title":"THE BIG ONE — half the field gone with five to go","summary":"Kelly Kuehl's bump draft turns teammate Dustin Riehle in the corner and the entire Vigilante Force team (37, 01, 33) wads up at once, along with the 14, 728, and 3 — forcing the one and only green-white-checker attempt.","tags":["dustin-reilly","kelly-keel","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8688,"title":"Anderson wins it three-wide off turn four","summary":"Burke, Anderson, and Klafka come off turn four side-by-side-by-side on the green-white-checker; Justin French's push carries America's Driver Albert Anderson to his first VRL win over teammate Jeremiah Burke.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","eric-klafka","justin-french"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":9069,"title":"Burke ran out of gas AT the finish line","summary":"In the post-race interview, runner-up Jeremiah Burke reveals his tank ran dry about a hundred feet before the line — which is why Mike Adamson got into him at the stripe.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":9366,"title":"Riehle: 'I got disqualified right at the checkered'","summary":"Random driver-of-the-night Dustin Riehle reveals in his interview that he was DQ'd at the flag on incident points after getting turned in the Big One by his own teammate.","tags":["dustin-reilly","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":915,"quote":"That's not going to matter — they're going to just turn left, drive fast, and kick ass.","context":"Booth previewing the 106-degree Talladega night in the pre-race","gold":3},{"t":3429,"quote":"Whoa — Klafka blinked out for a second and reappeared right in the middle of the three. They were four wide there for a second.","context":"A lag hiccup scatters the chase pack mid-race","gold":3},{"t":5265,"quote":"Oh, it's the 204 getting the tablecloth ripped from underneath them.","context":"Robert Jordan tagged out of the middle lane, bringing out the fourth caution","gold":4},{"t":5363,"quote":"Look at that save from Jonathan Osborne — holy smokes! He was jiggling that controller back and forth a lot, I can tell you that.","context":"Osborne hangs onto a sideways truck in the middle of a wreck","gold":4},{"t":7201,"quote":"Well, Ricky Bobby and Cal Naughton Jr. did it — I don't know why they can't do it here. A little shake and bake at the front.","context":"Debating whether teammates could swap the lead to save fuel at Dega","gold":4},{"t":8011,"quote":"It looks like the Katy Freeway rush hour traffic going about 85 — hand on the pistol, hand on your cell phone, and your knee on the wheel.","context":"Three-wide pack racing in the closing laps","gold":4},{"t":8169,"quote":"Oh, here it goes — big one! 37 right in the middle of it — oh my God, there goes half the field!","context":"The Big One erupts with about five laps to go","gold":5},{"t":9069,"quote":"I ran out of gas at the finish line. — That's called perfect freaking timing.","context":"Runner-up Jeremiah Burke's post-race fuel confession and the booth's reply","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"All names are best guesses from heavily garbled auto-captions. The #37 driver's surname is spelled out on-air as R-I-E-H-L-E ('Riehle') during the wrap-up, though captions render it 'Really'/'Greely'. The booth gives conflicting finishing positions for Riehle (introduced as the 17th-place finisher in his interview, listed 16th and first truck one lap down in the final results rundown); he also states he was disqualified at the checkered on incident points. Josh Buettner is mentioned in the points discussion but does not appear in the grid rundown or final results, so he likely did not race this event. League admins Jess and Lori Vaught are credited with running VRL; Alan Vaught (#33) also raced. Teams referenced: Limitless Motorsports (Anderson/Adamson/Burke), Vigilante Force (Vaught/Kuehl/Riehle/Mayberry), Team Omega. Next season's switch from trucks to Xfinity cars was announced during the broadcast.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"7cSPOMty0A8":{"recap":"Race 7 of VRL Season 10 brought a 37-car field to the virtual Michigan Speedway for 85 laps, with Jason Gaines on the pole at a 39.10. The trouble started immediately: a four-wide charge to the line triggered a Big One at start/finish on lap 1, and the cautions kept coming — Josh Bittner got spun down the backstretch, a three-wide restart bred another backstretch pileup, and Mike Everage's failed block wrecked Jeremiah Burke and collected Dion Jones. Albert Anderson supplied the mid-race storyline, storming from 31st on the grid to the lead by lap 47, while Trevor Robertson's early final pit stop briefly bought him clean air out front. The finish was an instant classic: Dillon Bryant dove under teammate Larry Dickerson in turn 1 on the white-flag lap, but Dickerson rode a monster high-side run back by in turn 3 and held on at the stripe for an Outcast Racing 1-2, with Tim Pope third.","winner":"Larry Dickerson","podium":["Larry Dickerson","Dillon Bryant","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":2765,"title":"Lap-One Big One at the Stripe","summary":"Four wide coming to the line on lap 1 — Gallagher and Andrew Player come together and the field piles in at start/finish. Austin Paul takes heavy nose damage and Derek Welch's night is over after a single lap.","tags":["john-gallagher","andrew-player","austin-paul","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3735,"title":"Dickerson Spins Bittner Down the Back","summary":"Larry Dickerson drifts up a lane on the backstretch and clips Josh Bittner's left rear, spinning the 84 for caution two — the booth replays it in slow motion to show how little time there was to react.","tags":["larry-dickerson","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4034,"title":"Three-Wide Restart Breeds a Backstretch Pileup","summary":"Three wide for the race lead on the lap-25 restart, Dave Mayberry gets caught in the middle, shuffled into Chris Klein, and another big wreck erupts off turn two on full tanks.","tags":["dave-mayberry","chris-klein","john-mcadam","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4206,"title":"The 82's Days of Thunder Escape","summary":"A chat tip sends the booth to the replay of the 82 threading untouched through the backstretch wreckage — 'if this doesn't remind you of Days of Thunder nothing will... I'm through, Harry!'","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4354,"title":"Goodenough's Missed Shift Disaster","summary":"Leading the lap-29 restart, Craig Goodenough buzzes the tach to 9,800 RPM on a missed shift, gets run into by Gaines and slams the inside wall hard — no caution flies, and the 89's night is ruined.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jason-gaines"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4746,"title":"Everage's Block Goes Wrong","summary":"Mike Everage throws a block on McAdam's run, gets into Jeremiah Burke instead, and both hit the outside wall; Burke slides back down the hill into traffic and collects Dion Jones for caution four.","tags":["mike-everage","jeremiah-burke","dion-jones","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5215,"title":"Albert Anderson: 31st to the Lead","summary":"Riding off-sequence strategy, Albert Anderson slices from a 31st starting spot past Pope and Robertson, clears with ease and leads at lap 47 in the 99 Track Limits Network livery.","tags":["albert-anderson","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5677,"title":"Robertson's Brazen Dive on Anderson","summary":"Robertson steps out of line and drives it way deep into turn 1 to snatch the lead — a 'brazen move by the six' — but Anderson crosses over and takes it right back before the lap is complete.","tags":["trevor-robertson","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6042,"title":"Robertson's Undercut Pays Off","summary":"Robertson pits early from the lead for four fresh Goodyears, and when the green-flag cycle shakes out he's back in front with a 1.6-second cushion over the drafting pack.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6712,"title":"Bryant Bumps the Leader With Three to Go","summary":"Hungry for the win, Dillon Bryant gets into teammate Larry Dickerson and crosses him up big time with three laps to go — everybody somehow keeps rolling, setting up the frantic finish.","tags":["dylan-bryant","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6786,"title":"White-Flag War: Dickerson Denies Bryant","summary":"Bryant dives to the inside in turn 1 on the final lap and takes the lead, but Dickerson carries a monster high-side run, retakes the spot in turn 3, and beats Bryant's last apron lunge to the stripe for an Outcast Racing 1-2.","tags":["larry-dickerson","dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1724,"quote":"Feel free to say hello in the chat — we don't bite unless you want us to. Just keep it PG for the kids.","context":"welcoming the stream chat as practice winds down","gold":3},{"t":2698,"quote":"I don't make the rules, I just call the thing.","context":"grumbling about non-qualifiers being forced to line up single file","gold":4},{"t":2998,"quote":"That was only the first lap — I haven't had enough wrecks for it to be a complete derby yet.","context":"responding to a chatter calling the lap-1 Big One a demolition derby","gold":3},{"t":4206,"quote":"Watch the 82 here — if this doesn't remind you of Days of Thunder, nothing will... I'm through, Harry!","context":"replaying the 82 weaving untouched through the backstretch pileup","gold":5},{"t":5836,"quote":"I know we're at Michigan, I know they're driving stock cars, but I feel like I'm at an air show watching these guys fly around in formation.","context":"the seven-car lead draft swapping lanes nose to tail","gold":4},{"t":6840,"quote":"At the stripe it's Dickerson — well done VRL, well done! Larry Dickerson takes the checkered flag... what a finish!","context":"the checkered flag after the white-flag lead swap between the Outcast teammates","gold":5},{"t":6917,"quote":"They had about 12 chances to wreck there in those last five laps and it just didn't happen.","context":"catching his breath right after the finish","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Booth is a solo call by Steve on Track Limits Network (channel formerly HBR TV; broadcast live Jan 8, 2025). Booth states this is Season 10, Race 7; race distance corrected on air from 110 to 85 laps. Surnames canonicalized against prior VRL distills: the #33 'Alan VA/Allen bot' = Alan Vaught and #16 'Kyle VA/vot' = Kyle Vaught; Kelly Cole's surname is only ever heard as 'Co'/'cool', so spelling remains uncertain. David Feit ('fight') and Dustyn Eaton (grid readout said 'Justin' once) follow prior canon. The results readout skipped 29th place (likely Andrew Coffin, the only unplaced starter). The 82 car in the Days of Thunder replay moment was never identified by name. Jack Dixon and Jason Gaines both suffered connection dropouts early; Tim Pope and Dillon Bryant blinked out briefly late. Larry Dickerson's hometown heard as 'rockboro North Carolina' — likely Roxboro.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"7gNztBI4fe4":{"recap":"Race 2 of VRL Season 2 brought the trucks to Iowa's 7/8-mile for 150 laps of pure tire management under the lights, with last week's top five starting from the rear on the league's new EOL rule. Polesitter Dale Adamson dominated the first half and built a massive lead, but his night unraveled after the final pit cycle — he bounced off the 91 in lap traffic, then a late tap from Russ Kilgore pushed him past the 13x incident-point limit and out of the race, dropping him to 23rd. Tim Pope charged 22 spots from the back, drove right around long-time leader John Ellis in the closing laps, and cruised to the win in a race that ran essentially flag-to-flag, with the halfway competition caution the only yellow. Kilgore stole second from Ellis on the final lap after Ellis overdrove turn 4 and smacked the wall, while birthday boy Jonathan Osborne came home sixth. Kelly Kuehl joined Adamson on the DQ list after reaching the incident limit.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Russ Kilgore","John Ellis"],"moments":[{"t":1688,"title":"Green flag at Iowa — Adamson jumps out front","summary":"Dale Adamson gets a great start from pole and immediately clears teammate Jeremiah Burke as the field runs two-by-two into turn 1.","tags":["dale-adamson","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2208,"title":"Ellis driving like a man possessed","summary":"Starting from the back on the EOL rule, John Ellis carves up 12 spots in the first 30 laps with a take-no-prisoners charge.","tags":["john-ellis"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2613,"title":"Burke spins entering pit road","summary":"Jeremiah Burke loses it diving down into Iowa's brutal pit entry, spinning off turn 4 and hitting the inside pit wall — the pit-entry danger the booth warned about all night.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3846,"title":"Wreck on the backstretch for Douglas Camp","summary":"Right after the lap-81 restart, Douglas Camp and a couple others wreck on the backstretch with heavy damage to two trucks — but they slide below the line and it stays green.","tags":["douglas-camp"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4000,"title":"French slams the inside wall","summary":"Justin French and Albert Anderson make contact off turn 2 in a checkup around lap traffic, and the 202 goes hard into the inside wall.","tags":["justin-french","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4343,"title":"Birthday battle: Pope vs Osborne side-by-side","summary":"Tim Pope and birthday boy Jonathan Osborne run side-by-side for laps in a clean, tense fight for second — neither willing to lift.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4941,"title":"Dale's charge unravels in lap traffic","summary":"After his final stop, a frustrated Dale Adamson bounces off Rob Green's 91 and into the wall while trying to slice back through lap traffic — the beginning of the end of his dominant night.","tags":["dale-adamson","rob-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5135,"title":"Pope takes second from Adamson","summary":"On much fresher tires, Tim Pope makes the move on Dale Adamson for second and sets sail after leader John Ellis with 18 to go.","tags":["timothy-pope","dale-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5240,"title":"Pope drives right around Ellis for the lead","summary":"Three-wide with lap traffic, Tim Pope drives straight around John Ellis for the race lead — the race-winning pass, called moments after Russ Endicott's chat prediction that Pope would run him down.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5338,"title":"Kuehl gets dumped with 10 to go","summary":"Kelly Kuehl goes spinning — 'is that Green that just dumped him?' — and later reaches the incident-point limit for a DQ, finishing 27th.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5461,"title":"Kilgore's tap sends Dale Adamson out — 13x DQ","summary":"Battling for position with five to go, Russ Kilgore barely taps Dale Adamson, who spins and is disqualified on the 13x incident-point limit. Kilgore apologized in his podium interview: 'I feel terrible, I didn't mean to get into him.'","tags":["russ-kilgore","dale-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5567,"title":"Pope wins; Kilgore steals second at the line","summary":"Tim Pope caps a 22-spot charge from the back with the win at Iowa, while Russ Kilgore gets around John Ellis on the very last lap for second after Ellis overdrives turn 4 and smacks the wall.","tags":["timothy-pope","russ-kilgore","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":799,"quote":"The main thing is tires, tires, tires — this race is all about tires.","context":"Adam Turner's pit-road preview that became the thesis of the entire night","gold":4},{"t":2208,"quote":"John Ellis is driving like a man possessed.","context":"Ellis up 12 spots from the back inside 30 laps","gold":4},{"t":2231,"quote":"He's got that take-no-prisoners driving style — he just goes out there and just sends it.","context":"The booth on rookie John Ellis's early charge","gold":3},{"t":2737,"quote":"It'd be a fun track to put a motorcycle on, what do you think about that, Brown? — I would probably puke or something.","context":"The booth daydreaming about motorcycles at Sonoma during a long green run","gold":3},{"t":3720,"quote":"That seven of Russ Kilgore spent more time in the air than he did with the rubber down on the racetrack.","context":"On Kilgore's luckless prior season as he ran second at the competition caution","gold":4},{"t":4998,"quote":"He hot rodded it right through the grass — got grassy tires... became a lawnmower there for just a second.","context":"Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry mowing the infield off turn 4","gold":4},{"t":5223,"quote":"He's driving like he's on rails out there.","context":"Reading Russ Endicott's chat prediction as Pope hunted down leader John Ellis — the pass came seconds later","gold":4},{"t":6649,"quote":"That's going to be bigger than the Super Bowl.","context":"Hyping the upcoming VRL vs HCK Beagles league-vs-league grudge match at Talladega","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions heavily garble names; proper names are best guesses. 'Dustin Riehle' inferred from caption 'dustin really' (could be Riehle). 'Alan Vaught' reconstructed from many garblings (just fought/just bought/chess fox); captions also wished 'Jess' a happy birthday alongside Jonathan Osborne. Booth read Douglas Camp's finish as '39th', almost certainly a caption error for 29th (last). The Facebook stream dropped briefly mid-race (~47:18) but the YouTube tape is continuous. Race ran green flag-to-flag except the lap-75 competition caution. Kelly Kuehl and Dale Adamson were both removed via the 13x incident-point rule. Russ Endicott is a league driver who did not race this week (watched from Twitch chat). League organizers 'Lori and Jess' thanked in interviews. Race: Season 2, Race 2, Iowa Speedway, ~150 laps, NASCAR trucks.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"8c20raC44cE":{"recap":"Alan Vaught put the #33 Mobil Chevrolet out front by lap 5 of the 133-lap Race #6 of Vigilante Racing League Season 11 at the virtual Homestead-Miami Speedway and controlled a dominant night, taking the checkered flag about three seconds clear for his second win of the season. The race needed four cautions, starting with a Chandler Paul-Dion Jones tangle before the field even reached the start line, and a frontstretch Big One before lap 25 that crushed Sean McDonnell into the wall and collected Mike Adamson, Josh Bittner, Kyle Vaught and Austin Paul. A messy caution in the middle of the first green-flag pit cycle around lap 45 wiped out Kelly Coyle, Albert Anderson and others, trimmed the lead lap to about 15 trucks, and turned the rest of the night into a tire-strategy chess match. From there the field ran green from roughly lap 47 to the finish, with Trevor Robertson holding second and Larry Dickerson charging 27 positions from 30th — after crashing in qualifying — to grab third and his second straight Homestead podium in two nights. Dillon Bryant took fourth after he and Dickerson broke down Jeremiah Burke in the closing laps, dropping Burke to fifth when he banged the wall trying to answer.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Trevor Robertson","Larry Dickerson"],"moments":[{"t":2151,"title":"Yellow before the field reaches the line","summary":"Coming to the initial green, Dion Jones came up as Chandler Paul came down and they met in the middle — caution after about 100 yards of green-flag action.","tags":["chandler-paul","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2413,"title":"Vaught grabs the lead by lap 5","summary":"Alan Vaught drove to the door of Tim Pope's #7 and cleared him for the lead on lap 5 while Trevor Robertson shadowed in third — the position Vaught would rarely surrender all night.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2537,"title":"Dixon nosed into the frontstretch wall","summary":"Nine laps in, Jack Dixon scraped the right rear on the fence and Larry Dickerson's #69 caught his left rear, spinning the #48 nose-first into the outside wall. Dickerson publicly apologized in his post-race interview.","tags":["jack-dixon","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2921,"title":"Robertson's door-slam bid for the lead","summary":"Robertson drove it in deep to turn 3 and slammed doors with Vaught going for the race lead — it broke both their momentum and cost Robertson second to Tim Pope.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3036,"title":"The Big One on the frontstretch","summary":"Adamson went three-wide, couldn't hold the nose down and washed up into McDonnell's #23, sending him hard into the frontstretch wall; Bittner got turned, Kyle Vaught piled into the #84, and Austin Paul plowed into a nearly stopped McDonnell. The booth compared the hit to Rusty at Dover.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","mike-adamson","josh-bittner","kyle-vaught","austin-paul","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3542,"title":"Gallagher rides the wall and gains 12 spots","summary":"John Gallagher ran the #123 literally against the safer barrier — not just near it — for half a corner at a time, and somehow was up 12 positions while doing it.","tags":["john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3998,"title":"The peanut jinx summons a caution","summary":"Josh Bittner called baloney in stream chat on the booth's 'peanuts are bad luck' superstition; Steve told him to check his wallet for a 50 and get out of the house — and the caution flew mid-sentence.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4073,"title":"Mid-pit-cycle melee guts the lead lap","summary":"As David Feit slowed to make pit entry, Kelly Coyle slid around and Gaines, Albert Anderson, Osborne, Whittenburg, Bryant and McAdam all got pieces — 'this was a bigger one than we thought.' Anderson was done for the night and only about 15 trucks stayed on the lead lap, while Larry Dickerson's stay-out gamble paid off with fresh tires.","tags":["david-fite","jason-gaines","albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","ricky-whittenburg","dylan-bryant","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6003,"title":"The Bomb Pop truck","summary":"The booth decided Dillon Bryant's truck looks like a Bomb Pop off the ice cream truck (or a can of Ghost energy drink), and league matriarch Lori chimed in from chat with her own ice-cream-truck order.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6734,"title":"The leader is also the server","summary":"Race leader Vaught had a connection blip — a problem for everybody, the booth noted, because he was hosting the session; even the turn 2 lighting looked dimmer afterward.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7123,"title":"Dickerson and Bryant break Burke","summary":"In the closing laps Dickerson worked the high side past Jeremiah Burke for the final podium spot, then Bryant drove by too as Burke slapped the safer barrier trying to answer — Burke fell from third to fifth in a handful of corners.","tags":["larry-dickerson","dylan-bryant","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7250,"title":"Vaught seals a dominant win","summary":"Vaught took the white flag three seconds clear and cruised home for win number two of the season, with Robertson second and 27-spot hard charger Dickerson third; the top three parked side by side at the start/finish line.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3122,"quote":"This is going to be a big hit — man, that reminds me of Rusty at Dover back in the day. Yeah, I just dated myself again.","context":"replaying Sean McDonnell's frontstretch impact in the Big One","gold":3},{"t":4009,"quote":"Check your wallet for a 50 — if there's a 50 in there, take that, get out of the house... oh, there's the caution!","context":"Steve firing back at Josh Bittner's chat mockery of the peanuts superstition, when the yellow flew mid-sentence","gold":5},{"t":6003,"quote":"Is it just me or does Dylan Bryant's truck look like a Bomb Pop?","context":"the booth sizing up Bryant's popsicle-striped livery during a long green run","gold":4},{"t":6745,"quote":"Problem is when Allen VA has a connection issue, that means everybody has a connection issue — because he is the host.","context":"the race leader (and league admin) lagging while hosting the server","gold":4},{"t":7051,"quote":"We could be like NASCAR and just throw a yellow real quick just to see what would happen... yeah, there's a water bottle in two. It's full of lead.","context":"joking about phantom debris cautions during the long green finish","gold":4},{"t":7361,"quote":"Telling you, iRacing, you got to update the smoke and the paint. There's no reason they can't make that smoke pink — they can do it for gender reveals.","context":"watching the winner's burnout at the start/finish line","gold":3},{"t":8063,"quote":"Of course, in typical Milk Dud fashion, I screwed up again and smacked the wall.","context":"Larry Dickerson on his qualifying crash during the third-place interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is garbled throughout the auto-captions ('VA', 'vot', 'bot', 'Vault', 'vaugh') — best guess Vaught, possibly Vaughn; the booth also implied his given name may be Jess ('Jess goes by Allan'). Kyle Vaught assumed to be related (Allen shouted out son Kyle). Color commentator heard as 'Chris gones' / 'Chris G' — surname uncertain (possibly Jones); play-by-play announcer identified only as Steve. Several driver surnames are best guesses from garbled captions: David Feit ('fight'), Kelly Coyle ('Co', 'cool', 'coill'), Joe Cannell ('canel', 'caneles'), George Ren ('Ren con'), Craig Goodenough ('good enough', 'goodu'), Chris Klein (also heard as 'Kon', 'hind', 'Flyin', 'Fred Klein'). Pole sitter unnamed due to a caption gap in the grid rundown, but qualifying commentary indicates Tim Pope's 32.692 was the top time and Robertson started P2. Full finishing order 1-39 is read out at ~8317s. 'Lori' (Allen's wife, league organizer, in stream chat) is not a driver. Vince Short and Shawn Roberts were mentioned only in reference to the previous night's Num Thums Racing League race and are excluded from the driver list.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"8gfn2vcKS4o":{"recap":"The VRL brought its All-Star Race, dubbed 'One Hot Night,' to the revived North Wilkesboro Speedway for 200 laps with a limited 20-truck field of the league's best, two fast repairs, and zero penalties on the books. Alan Vaught's #33 dominated the middle of the race, stretching out an eight-and-a-half-second lead and lapping trucks up through eighth place before late cautions forced him to gamble on fresh tires. The closing stages turned chaotic — a lap-140 teammate-on-teammate pileup, 'the Big One' triggered when Vaught got sideways slicing back through traffic, and a restart wreck that set up a lone green-white-checker attempt. When Larry Dickerson bounced off the wall into Jonathan Osborne on that final attempt, Josh Bittner's #84 drove through the mess to win under yellow — his second All-Star Race victory — with hard-charger Dickerson second and Vaught third.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Larry Dickerson","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1482,"title":"Sun Drop spins early — first caution","summary":"Austin Paul's #3 tangles with the 86, gets clipped by the 01 and 99, and spins in the Sun Drop machine to bring out the night's first caution just laps into the race.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1687,"title":"Restart pileup sends the 89 for a ride","summary":"Pole-sitter Craig Goodenough gets the clear call and comes down into Whittenburg's nose on the restart, goes through the spin cycle, and collects the 14, 81, 10, 18 and 16 behind him.","tags":["craig-goodenough","ricky-whittenburg","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","andrew-cauthan","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2299,"title":"'I'm here boys' — English survives the tornadoes","summary":"Allen English finally joins the booth after tornadoes pass south of his house, and the crew immediately asks how many flying cows he counted from his window.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2843,"title":"Dickerson hits two in one lap","summary":"Larry Dickerson turns Ricky Whittenburg — who saves it — then nearly climbs the 84's quarter panel in the same lap, prompting the booth to ask if he's trying to make enemies at the All-Star Race.","tags":["larry-dickerson","ricky-whittenburg","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3422,"title":"Kuehl smacks the inside wall at halfway","summary":"Kelly Kuehl's 01 steps out coming off turn four and hits the concrete wall guarding pit road, and the caution doubles as the halfway competition yellow with its mandatory four-tire stop.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3873,"title":"Osborne's completely-sideways save","summary":"Jonathan Osborne hangs on completely sideways through two corners and somehow keeps the 81 pointed the right way — one of the saves of the night.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4276,"title":"Whittenburg's night ends on the wall","summary":"Connection issues send the 55 of Ricky Whittenburg into the outside wall and then wandering toward the infield, ending the night for a truck that qualified fourth and ran hot early — the booth jokes he mistook a trailer for a lobster food truck.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4546,"title":"Lap-140 pileup: teammate-on-teammate violence","summary":"Tim Pope gets loose off the corner, takes a love tap from Dickerson's 69, and ricochets off the outside wall back across traffic into Osborne — a multi-truck mess that race control counts as the lap-150 competition caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","larry-dickerson","jonathan-osborne","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5259,"title":"Anderson leans on Rancan, Sun Drop spins again","summary":"Late-race aggression boils over as the 99 bumps the 28 up into the outside wall — 'no, George will not forget' — and moments later Austin Paul loops the 3 in turn four to bring out the yellow.","tags":["albert-anderson","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6045,"title":"THE BIG ONE","summary":"Charging back through on brand-new tires, Alan Vaught dives across the 74's nose, gets spun sideways and triggers the Big One — the 33, 6, 74 and 18 all collected as the field stacks up with nowhere to go.","tags":["jess-vaught","zachary-henin","trevor-robertson","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6256,"title":"Restart eruption forces the green-white-checker","summary":"The penultimate restart erupts: Rancan goes for a wild ride in a four-way meat sandwich, and Goodenough drifts up across Osborne's front bumper into a hard hit with the 6 — setting up the one and only official green-white-checker.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6490,"title":"Bittner steals it under yellow","summary":"On the green-white-checker, Dickerson bounces off the wall into Osborne, who spins as Josh Bittner drives through the chaos — the yellow flies, the field freezes, and race control makes it official: Bittner wins the All-Star Race over Dickerson and Vaught.","tags":["josh-bittner","larry-dickerson","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":953,"quote":"Zero penalties, and then I just wrote here, like, you know, that means YOLO — just send it.","context":"Adam Turner reading out the All-Star Race rules","gold":4},{"t":1357,"quote":"I said a bunch of cool stuff guys, you're going to have to trust me on that. I was all hyped up ready to party and then I guess my mic got cut off.","context":"Turner discovers his mic was muted for his big intro","gold":3},{"t":2310,"quote":"How many flying bovines did you see? Six or eight, I lost count.","context":"Allen English rejoins the booth after tornadoes pass his house","gold":4},{"t":2864,"quote":"What is Larry Diggers doing here, is he trying to make enemies right now at the All-Star Race? He's hit two in one lap!","context":"Dickerson turns Whittenburg and clips another truck in the same lap","gold":4},{"t":3322,"quote":"Man, the 33 of Jess Vaught didn't come to play — he came here to dominate right now.","context":"Vaught eight and a half seconds clear and lapping up through eighth","gold":3},{"t":4570,"quote":"Oh man, Timothy Pope — teammate on teammate violence there, even Kyle V getting involved in that one. Goodness.","context":"The lap-140 pileup takes out members of the same team","gold":4},{"t":4906,"quote":"Throw some wax on that chrome horn and put it to good use.","context":"The booth calls for bump-and-runs with under 50 laps to go","gold":4},{"t":6245,"quote":"It is time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets, throw inhibition out the window — it is racing time here at North Wilkesboro!","context":"Alan Brown launches the frantic final restart","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Finish came under caution on the lone green-white-checker attempt; race director Lori Vaught (not a driver — league admin) declared the iRacing order official. Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: the #74 ('Howen'/'henin'/'hening' — could be Howen or Henning), the #28 ('ran con'/'rancan'/'ranone' — rendered here as Rancan), and 'Vaught' for the vot/Vault/fought family (Jess #33, Kyle #16, admin Lori). The booth's running 'Dustin with a Y' gag suggests the #14's first name is spelled Dustyn. The booth said Chandler Paul finished 17th during his spotlight interview but the final rundown listed him 16th with Dave Mayberry 17th. Greg Klein (#92) made the field Monday but never gridded due to internet outages in eastern Oklahoma; Greg Dobson (#085) crew-chiefed rather than raced. Fill-in broadcaster Gary Godsoe was thanked for covering prior weeks but was not in tonight's booth.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"8HeQkyuyM-g":{"recap":"VRL's Race #2 of the short off-season Gen 6 series brought 37 cars to virtual Daytona for 100 laps and 250 miles, with no fast repairs and one green-white-checkered attempt on the table. The opening stint was carnage — four cautions inside the first 22 laps, headlined by a lap-6 chain-reaction Big One that ended Dustyn Eaton's night and prompted race control to mandate single-file restarts. Early dominator Dustin Wade and drafting partner Jonathan Osborne were both tagged for speeding on pit entry, knocking the race's strongest car a lap down and handing the outcome to fuel strategy. Tim Pope, fueled to the finish from a lap-76 stop, lost the lead to John McAdam at the white flag but crossed back to the bottom in the final corner — left-side tires dipping below the yellow line at the stripe — to win it, a result race control confirmed despite the yellow-line question. Dillon Bryant recovered from an accidental pit-lane start to complete the podium, with John Gallagher fourth and Ricky Whittenburg fifth.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","John McAdam","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":2495,"title":"Lap-6 Big One out of turn four","summary":"The 13 washes up the track into the fence and triggers a chain-reaction crash off turn four; Dustyn Eaton's 14 takes a huge hit with nowhere to go and is eventually out of the race.","tags":["dion-jones","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2935,"title":"Four-wide squeeze bites Mayberry","summary":"Four wide exiting the trioval, Dave Mayberry runs out of room at the top with Kevin Hunt alongside and ends up facing the wrong direction for caution number two.","tags":["dave-mayberry","kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3360,"title":"Caution three: backstretch pileup","summary":"A checkup off turn two snowballs into a much bigger wreck than the booth first thought — Trevor Robertson gets drilled by Kevin Hunt, with Derek Welch, Russ Kilgore, David Feit and Andrew Coffin all swept in.","tags":["trevor-robertson","kevin-hunt","derek-welch","russ-kilgore","david-fite","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3518,"title":"Race control orders single-file restarts","summary":"Three yellows in the first 16 laps and race control (Lori V) confirms in chat: restarts go single file, an old-school move the booth applauds.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3850,"title":"Everage up the track, Kelly collected","summary":"Three wide into turn three, the 82 of Mike Everage comes up and turns across the field; John Gallagher's 123 drives straight into the back of Kelly Cole and Everage takes some monster hits for caution four.","tags":["mike-everage","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4549,"title":"Burke's two-second race lead","summary":"Jeremiah Burke noses the 53 to the point at the stripe — but holds the lead for barely two seconds before Dustin Wade powers back around the outside with Osborne's drafting help.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-wade","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5045,"title":"Race-flipping speeding penalties for Wade and Osborne","summary":"The top two cars of the night both get nailed for speeding on pit entry during green-flag stops — 40-second penalties that drop dominant leader Dustin Wade and Jonathan Osborne a lap down and reshape the whole race.","tags":["dustin-wade","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6380,"title":"Welch pits for a beer","summary":"Derek Welch pulls into the pits and the booth declares he's grabbing a beer — 'I can't say that I blame you, sir' — while the commentator sticks to water because he's got to work.","tags":["derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":7257,"title":"Fuel math crowns a favorite: Pope can make it","summary":"With the top five needing one more stop, the booth singles out Tim Pope — pitted on lap 76 — as good to go to the finish if it stays green, setting up the strategy endgame.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-mcadam","larry-dickerson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7566,"title":"Austin Paul pits from the lead, Pope inherits it","summary":"The last driver needing fuel, Austin Paul, surrenders the lead with seven to go for a 6.2-second splash, handing the point to Tim Pope for the run to the finish.","tags":["austin-paul","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7853,"title":"White flag: McAdam takes the lead","summary":"Pope tries to block both lanes but opens the door — John McAdam surges to the race lead at the white flag with a push from Anthony Williams, betting he has the fuel to make it back to the stripe.","tags":["john-mcadam","anthony-williams","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7886,"title":"Pope's below-the-line last-corner steal","summary":"Through turns three and four for the last time, Pope crosses over to the bottom, drops his left sides below the yellow line at the stripe and beats McAdam to the checkers — race control later confirms the win stands.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-mcadam","anthony-williams"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2410,"quote":"As the timing tower has a stroke... fixed itself, thank goodness.","context":"The scoring pylon glitched out during early green-flag running","gold":3},{"t":2666,"quote":"Why do you ask? Well, that big ass spoiler on the back — yeah, I said it.","context":"Explaining fuel weight and rear-spoiler drag during the first caution","gold":3},{"t":4897,"quote":"I just have this feeling about that 68 machine... I just feel like the last lap is going to be his demise. It's just the nature of the beast here at Daytona.","context":"Ominous premonition about dominant early leader Dustin Wade","gold":3},{"t":6380,"quote":"Derek Welch pulls into the pits to grab a beer — I can't say that I blame you, sir, but I got to work after this, so it's just water for this guy.","context":"Welch's mid-race refreshment stop","gold":4},{"t":6446,"quote":"Pit stop police dropping the hammer.","context":"Greg Dobson penalized after skating through the grass on pit entry from the lead","gold":3},{"t":6828,"quote":"The closer we get to this race's conclusion, the more these drivers just forget about their brains — and I'm not singling out anyone, we all do it.","context":"Sizing up the field with 23 laps to go after a long green run","gold":4},{"t":7172,"quote":"You've heard of musical chairs? It's going to be musical pit stops here in a moment.","context":"The top nine all needing one final fuel stop in the closing laps","gold":3},{"t":7898,"quote":"Seven goes to the bottom, gets the left sides below the yellow line — at the stripe, Pope wins it!","context":"The last-corner, below-the-line winning move at the checkers","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner confirmed on air: Tim Pope, though his winning move put his left-side tires below the yellow line at the stripe; race control confirmed the result but the booth noted the league may address the yellow-line rule later. Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Allen/Kyle VA/bot/vot' rendered as Vaught, 'Kelly Co/cool' as Cole, 'George ranone/Ren cone' as Rannone, 'David fight' as Fite, 'Joe canel/canellis/Canalis' as Canellis, 'Craig goodu/good enough' as Goodenough. Broadcast was HBR TV (rebranding to Track Limits Network on Jan 1) with a solo commentator (Steve); Lori V served as race control. Full finishing order read out at ~2:26:20 (8780s): Pope, McAdam, Bryant, Gallagher, Whittenburg, Dickerson, Fite, Kilgore, Alan Vaught, Burke top 10. Joe Canellis never took the green (connection issue). Race #2 of VRL Season 10's short off-season series; next race Indianapolis (trucks) on Dec 4.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"8w-B-yQd5ZU":{"recap":"VRL's Xfinity Series brought Throwback Night to Darlington Raceway for 110 laps at the Lady in Black, with the field decked out in vintage paint schemes. Pole-sitter Tim Pope laid in wait early while teammate Mike Adamson set the pace, and the race ran caution-free deep into the night as Alan Vaught hounded Adamson for the lead through the green-flag pit cycles. The night's only caution flew with a handful of laps to go when Chandler Paul was launched airborne off Kelly Kiel in a multi-car crash the booth compared to a boat launch. The yellow cycled Pope — who had gambled by staying out — back to the front, and he drove away on the five-to-go restart to beat Adamson and Vaught to the checkers. Jim Ott charged 12 spots to fourth as the biggest mover, and Vaught left Darlington 23 points up on Ott heading into the Talladega season finale.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Mike Adamson","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1316,"title":"Green flag on Throwback Night at Darlington","summary":"The 18-car throwback field takes the green for 110 laps, scrambling to get single file early on the one usable line around the Lady in Black.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1421,"title":"Adamson takes the lead from Pope","summary":"Mike Adamson in the 51 goes to the front past pole-sitter Tim Pope and pushes the envelope to build a one-second lead.","tags":["mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2144,"title":"Pope reels Adamson back in","summary":"After letting Adamson burn up his tires, Pope makes tracks and closes the lead battle to two tenths, camped on the 51's back door.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3446,"title":"Vaught dives under the 51 for the lead","summary":"Alan Vaught gets underneath Adamson for the lead but can't complete the pass — Adamson refuses to give a favorable line in a multi-lap battle.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3713,"title":"Pit-exit near miss between Vaught and Adamson","summary":"Vaught exits the pits right into Adamson's path and it gets crowded — the two tangle briefly in what becomes the race for the lead after the cycle.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3811,"title":"Endicott's engine gives up the ghost","summary":"Laps down all night with damage, Russ Endicott blows the engine and it lets go in a smoke cloud down the back stretch — 'spraying for mosquitoes out there.'","tags":["russ-endicott"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3914,"title":"Albert Anderson's wild save","summary":"America's Driver grabs a Darlington stripe, shoots straight down the track and somehow saves it with Mayberry right behind — 'that was crazy.'","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3980,"title":"Pope smokes the wall","summary":"The 728 smacks the wall pretty good while racing to stay on the lead lap — a rough patch in the middle of Pope's eventual winning night.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4298,"title":"Austin Paul slams the inside wall","summary":"Austin Paul gets loose on the back stretch and slams the inside wall hard — the No. 3 needs the tow and is done for the night.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4520,"title":"The Big One: Chandler Paul goes airborne","summary":"The 72 snaps loose off the corner, Kelly Kiel hits him and Chandler Paul is launched flying through the air 'like a boat launch,' collecting Jeff Ottinger — the only caution of the night, shown from cockpit and gyro cams.","tags":["chandler-paul","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4812,"title":"Five-to-go restart decides it","summary":"Into the restart zone with about five to go — the outside line with Jason Airson stalls and teammates Pope and Adamson run away with it up front.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","jason-airson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5002,"title":"Pope takes the checkers","summary":"No stranger to victory lane, Tim Pope wins Throwback Night ahead of Mike Adamson and Alan Vaught, then celebrates with an Alan Kulwicki-style Polish victory lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2308,"quote":"He's got the big tuxedo on and they're in there playing the cello and he's eating lobster with his hands.","context":"Imagining absent broadcaster Alan Brown at the cruise ship captain's table","gold":4},{"t":3800,"quote":"The 33 is the only car left without a Darlington stripe. Well, we need to get him one, don't we? Somebody put him in the wall, get him a stripe.","context":"Booth notices Alan Vaught's car is still clean mid-race","gold":3},{"t":4523,"quote":"72's around big time — big crash, big crash! Holy smokes, there's a bunch of cars involved!","context":"Live call as Chandler Paul goes airborne in the Big One","gold":5},{"t":4605,"quote":"He thought he was going to squeeze through there and then he turned it into like a boat launch.","context":"Replaying Kelly Kiel launching Chandler Paul into the air","gold":5},{"t":4755,"quote":"You're all bunched back up — this is where you dump people, you turn them, you burn them.","context":"Previewing the five-to-go restart after the Big One","gold":4},{"t":6072,"quote":"The best kind of wreck you can see — cars flying, nobody's really dying. It costs nobody a dime.","context":"Closing thoughts on the night's only caution, sim racing style","gold":4},{"t":6108,"quote":"We're saying good night — we gone. See ya, adios.","context":"The booth's signature sign-off to end the broadcast","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Race is 110 laps, VRL Xfinity Series Throwback Night at Darlington (streamed 2022-09-07, uploaded 2022-09-08); Talladega is named as the next-week season finale. Full finishing order read at ~1:26:39: Pope, Adamson, Vaught, Ott, Airson, Osborne, Burke, Fight, Mayberry, Ottinger, Poke, Coffin, Anderson, Kiel, Chandler Paul, Austin Paul, Endicott, Whittenburg. Name uncertainties from auto-captions: the No. 2 is introduced as 'Howard Anderson' in the rundown but called 'Albert Anderson / America's Driver' the rest of the night — Albert Anderson used as best guess; 'Jason Airson' spelling uncertain (also heard as harrison/pearson); 'David Feit' may be Fite; pit reporter's name heard as kewins/coons/'cubans' — rendered Alan Koons as best guess; random-draw winner announced as 'jason anderson' (likely a caption garble, possibly Albert Anderson). Greg Klein is a driver who sat out (on a cruise with regular broadcaster Alan Brown, who was absent this night); Lopey Evans (No. 13) and Earl Evans appear only via chat and are presumed league drivers not racing tonight. Ricky Whittenburg (No. 55) disconnected late and is scored 18th.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"9JNJKpnqEYM":{"recap":"The Season 13 opener of the VRL Premiere Series, the Vigilante Dominion 170 at Michigan International Speedway, doubled as a Veterans Day tribute night — 34 trucks, special military paint schemes, and an extra pace lap of remembrance before the green. Polesitter Tim Pope's No. 7 controlled most of the 85-lapper, locked in a race-long three-truck breakaway with Craig Goodenough's No. 89 and Mike Adamson's No. 88. After an early backstretch wreck ended the nights of Andy Player and Jonathan Osborne, the race ran almost entirely clean and green and came down to pit strategy, where Pope's lightning-fast stops gave him the decisive edge. Pope took the checkers 1.2 seconds clear of Goodenough, with Adamson third and series newcomer Jacob Alesia climbing 16 spots to finish fourth. Pope dedicated the win to his ailing team leader, Ricky Whittenberg.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Craig Goodenough","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":920,"title":"A lap of remembrance","summary":"Before the green, VRL pauses for a Veterans Day tribute — a moment of silence and an extra pace lap of remembrance, with the field running special military paint schemes.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1398,"title":"The overlay gremlins strike at go-live","summary":"The broadcast overlay subscription expires the moment the stream goes live, forcing the booth to call the entire running order by voice all night.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1460,"title":"Backstretch wreck ends two nights early","summary":"The night's only big incident — a backstretch pileup on the first caution knocks Jonathan Osborne and Andy Player out of the race and sends Greg Dobson to the pits with heavy damage in a no-fast-repair series.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","andrew-player","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1920,"title":"Adamson takes it around the outside","summary":"Mike Adamson's 88 rides the high line around the No. 7 to take the lead from Tim Pope, kicking off the front-three fight that defines the race.","tags":["mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2146,"title":"VRL salutes its four veteran drivers","summary":"The booth honors the league's four military veterans on track: Navy Desert Storm vet Greg Klein, Army vet Scott Milner, Army vet and volcano-rescue volunteer Michael Everidge, and Marine tank mechanic John Schonbachler.","tags":["greg-cline","scott-milner","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2975,"title":"The 180-mph lazy susan","summary":"Pope, Goodenough, and Adamson trade the lead in a three-truck breakaway that just won't quit — swapping spots lap after lap while pulling clear of the entire field.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3205,"title":"Andy Player calls in from the sidelines","summary":"Wrecked-out Andy Player joins the booth to explain the backstretch pileup — no quick caution, a truck slid up in front of him, and his right front was destroyed — and unveils his new team, Apex Performance Esports.","tags":["andrew-player","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3947,"title":"Foot cam and a 92 bpm heart rate","summary":"Craig Goodenough's onboard package includes a foot cam and a live heart rate monitor — which never tops 92 bpm while he battles for the lead at 180 mph.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4272,"title":"Pit-lane chess for the win","summary":"The final stops decide it: Adamson pits early chasing track position, Goodenough blinks next, and Pope covers a lap later — cycling back out front with the tire edge he needs.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4503,"title":"The seven slices back to the point","summary":"Tim Pope dives to the inside and clears Mike Adamson's 88 for good as the final pit cycle shakes out, with Adamson left trying to hang on in the draft on older tires.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4996,"title":"Pope closes it out by 1.2 seconds","summary":"Tim Pope takes the white flag with a 1.2-second cushion and cruises to the Season 13 opening win; Goodenough and Adamson settle second and third after fighting to the line.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5805,"title":"Win dedicated to Ricky Whittenberg","summary":"In victory lane, Tim Pope dedicates the win to team leader Ricky Whittenberg, who has been battling an illness, then reveals he plans to run only five or six races this season.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":242,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"The VRN broadcast's signature opening bumper","gold":4},{"t":1575,"quote":"Oh, nothing. Just a victim right there. Greg Dawson just gets a little help from the 17 there. Oh yeah, just gets nailed.","context":"Replay of Greg Dobson getting collected in the early wreck","gold":3},{"t":2401,"quote":"Next up will be Albert leading the rest of them like the Pied Piper.","context":"Albert Anderson's 99 Freedom Machine towing the chase pack","gold":3},{"t":4159,"quote":"This little 180 mph chess match here.","context":"Goodenough and Adamson locked together fighting for second","gold":4},{"t":5479,"quote":"You still didn't get above a 92. So, you were cool as the other side of the pillow all night.","context":"Alan reading Craig Goodenough's heart rate monitor in the podium interview","gold":4},{"t":5636,"quote":"Guess what ran out one year ago today? My overlays.","context":"Alan explaining the night-long broadcast gremlins — the overlay subscription expired at go-live","gold":4},{"t":5972,"quote":"Make sure you stay fast, stay sharp, stay vigilant, and we will see you in Richmond.","context":"Alan's signature sign-off closing the Season 13 opener","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Broadcast overlays were down all night (subscription expired at go-live), so every running order was read verbally — position calls may be approximate. Several names are best-guess reconstructions from garbled auto-captions and are uncertain: Chris Gomes/Gones, Kelly Kuehl, Andrew Cawthon, John Schonbachler, Sean McDonnell, and Tom Barish. 'Kyle Bach' is inferred from the booth naming his brother Brandon Bach (captions say 'Kyle Vault'). Broadcaster Alan's surname 'Bach' is likewise inferred from family references; his wife Lori is race admin and posts on-screen chat messages. Andy Player said he hit 'Aaron Paul' in the opening wreck — likely a caption garble for Austin or Chandler Paul. Full finishing order was read out verbally at 1:37:46. Race winner and podium confirmed on air.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"9Kpo2XnOtis":{"recap":"The Summer Sizzler 100 was the Vigilante Racing League's open-hosted recruitment race — 100 laps in the trucks under the lights at Auto Club Speedway, with $50 on the line for the winner and 35 entries on the sheet. Jonathan Adkins powered around polesitter Eric Klafka on the opening lap and controlled most of the night, but the race ran completely caution-free and turned into a green-flag tire and strategy battle. Jacob Chrisman carved up 26 spots from the back of the grid, ran down Adkins on fresher tires, and pinched his way past for the lead with 12 laps to go. Chrisman cruised to a dominant win, with Trevor Robertson second, Roy Hyde stealing the final money spot on the podium, and a fading Adkins fourth on worn tires. Josh Bittner collected $10 for the fastest lap, and the booth spent the night marveling that a 30-truck money race stayed this clean.","winner":"Jacob Chrisman","podium":["Jacob Chrisman","Trevor Robertson","Roy Hyde"],"moments":[{"t":1677,"title":"Green flag on the Summer Sizzler 100","summary":"Over 30 trucks take the green at Auto Club and immediately fan out three wide; Jonathan Adkins rides the outside momentum past polesitter Eric Klafka to grab the lead on the opening lap.","tags":["eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1725,"title":"Lap-1 spin on cold tires","summary":"A truck loops around behind the pack on the opening lap — Brian Miskel Jr spins with Gabe Cazzola caught up in it; both keep rolling and the race stays green.","tags":["robert-chipman"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2088,"title":"The movers: Adrian and Kilgore on a tear","summary":"Caleb Adrian rockets up 19 spots into the top 10 while Russ Kilgore's Genuine Draft No. 35 climbs 20 positions from the back — the early hard chargers of the night.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2289,"title":"Kilgore's charge hits the wall","summary":"After running down 20 spots' worth of trucks, Russ Kilgore tags the wall and gets freight-trained back through the field with damage.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3102,"title":"Chrisman up 26 spots and leading","summary":"The first green-flag pit cycle reveals the story of the night: Jacob Chrisman, up 26 spots from the back of the grid, cycles to the front of the field with hard-charger pace.","tags":["jacob-chrisman"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4859,"title":"Whittenburg's No. 55 takes over the lead","summary":"Stretching his stint to the absolute limit, Ricky Whittenburg's lime-green 'Pounding the Competition' No. 55 sweeps past Austin Paul for the lead as Paul peels onto pit road, before finally taking tires on lap 78.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5071,"title":"Hayden hammers the jutting wall","summary":"Chandler Hayden gets spun and slams the angled wall section almost 90 degrees head-on — the hardest hit of the night — yet iRacing keeps the race green.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5513,"title":"The pinch job: Chrisman takes the lead with 12 to go","summary":"Jacob Chrisman runs down leader Jonathan Adkins, dives to the inside through turns 3 and 4, and pinches him up the track to seize the lead for good — the winning move of the race.","tags":["jacob-chrisman"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5619,"title":"Rincon's one-stop gamble","summary":"Jorge Rincon refuses to pit again, nursing lap-37 tires and fumes near the top 10 while the booth jokes about drilling his roll cage for hidden fuel — the gamble sticks for a ninth-place finish.","tags":["george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5745,"title":"Booth caught making up the payouts","summary":"The booth can't agree whether the $10 bonus is for hard charger or fastest lap, jumps into an empty admin chat, and gets corrected live by admin Dave — 'we're just up here making things up then, sorry about that, I'll get out of your booth.'","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6021,"title":"Chrisman caps the 26-spot charge with the win","summary":"Jacob Chrisman takes the white flag and cruises across the line to win the caution-free Summer Sizzler 100; Trevor Robertson runs second while Roy Hyde sneaks past a tire-worn Jonathan Adkins for the final money spot.","tags":["jacob-chrisman","trevor-robertson","roy-hyde"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":835,"quote":"Man, they're from Maine to Spain — I'm seeing Canada, UK, Florida, Illinois...","context":"Scanning where the 35 entries hail from during qualifying","gold":3},{"t":993,"quote":"Views of Adam Turner do not represent the views of mdot.tv.","context":"The booth's legal disclaimer after Adam Turner called out 'this hot rod guy' as a slacker on air","gold":4},{"t":2224,"quote":"Let's be patient, let's not turn anybody, you know — at least until 10 laps to go.","context":"Booth strategy advice early in a 100-lap money race","gold":4},{"t":3344,"quote":"Ricky Wittenberg — that's not Ricky from the Trailer Park Boys. I talked to him. Although I wish it was.","context":"Whittenburg still circulating on ancient tires deep into the first run","gold":4},{"t":3892,"quote":"I'm counting on somebody to take somebody out, because we got some pay involved here.","context":"Alan English explaining why he'd save fresh tires for the end","gold":3},{"t":4674,"quote":"The tail end of it says 'pounding the competition' — apparently that's what he's doing, he's pounding most of these guys out here.","context":"Admiring Ricky Whittenburg's crazy green No. 55 while he ran up front","gold":3},{"t":5536,"quote":"He's pushed up into the... that's called a pinch job! Let's get it going now!","context":"The call as Jacob Chrisman pinches Jonathan Adkins up the track for the winning pass with 12 to go","gold":5},{"t":6101,"quote":"The only fireworks we're seeing are the ones being blown off the side of the track right now — everybody raced clean, they stayed in their lane.","context":"Reacting to a completely caution-free money race at the checkered flag","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Pre-season open-hosted recruitment race broadcast by mdot tv (Aug 2021); VRL Season 1 proper was announced to start Wednesday, September 8, 2021. The race ran 100 laps entirely caution-free. Winner's surname is heavily garbled in captions (chisman/crissman/christman/crispin/christensen) — 'Jacob Chrisman' is a best guess. 'Simon Sriegis' is also a best guess from garbled captions (s street/sriges/surregis). Full finishing order was read out on air; league admin Dave joined the booth briefly to confirm Josh Bittner won the $10 fastest-lap bonus, and league member Alan Vaught was interviewed post-race. Ricky Whittenburg proper spelling inferred; captions consistently render it 'wittenberg'.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"9tySZsyPpEE":{"recap":"VRL took its Wednesday night show to the streets for the Clash in the Streets, a 50-lap truck race at the brand-new Chicago Street Circuit, called radio-style after the broadcast's SDK graphics service went down. Pole sitter Tim Pope smacked the wall at the green, and defending champion Trevor Robertson took over and stretched out a three-second lead before being collected by John Gallagher's crashing lapped truck just before the lap-25 stage break. The unforgiving tire barriers claimed victims all night, including Greg Klein, Chandler Paul, Michael Taylor, and Sean McDonnell's battered Toyota. After the halfway re-rack, Pope ran down and passed the stayed-out 81 of Jonathan Osborne, then cruised to the win by about two and a half seconds over Robertson, with Alan Vaught third, Dustyn Eaton fourth, and Sean McDonnell fifth.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1544,"title":"Pole sitter Pope pounds the wall at the green","summary":"Green flag flies and the 27 of Tim Pope immediately goes hard into the wall coming out of turn one, dropping several positions as the 7, 33, and 88 pounce.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonah-long","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1917,"title":"Klein noses the tire barrier","summary":"Road course ace Greg Klein noses the 92 hard into the tire barrier — 'which is not very forgiving' — after already dropping ten spots.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2154,"title":"Robertson takes the lead","summary":"Defending season champion Trevor Robertson moves the 6 to the point and starts setting a blistering pace.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2303,"title":"McDonnell slams the wall hard","summary":"The 23 of Sean McDonnell spins and hits the wall hard from third, bashing in the front of the Toyota and putting his cooling on watch until the stage break.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3275,"title":"Chan the Man buried in the tire barrier","summary":"The 72 of Chandler Paul goes into the tire barrier 'that's claimed so many so far' and struggles to get refired.","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3597,"title":"Race leader Robertson collected by lapped traffic","summary":"The lapped 123 of John Gallagher hits the wall in the tight esses and race leader Trevor Robertson — nearly three seconds clear — piles into it, with Vaught and Pope tagged up too. Robertson limps with front-end damage to the stage break to burn his fast repair, and the race is never the same.","tags":["trevor-robertson","john-gallagher","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4168,"title":"Booth fire drill: English's smoke detector goes off","summary":"Mid-broadcast a smoke detector starts blaring in Allen English's house — 'fire fire English, this house is burning down' — before he returns to declare it a false alarm while the booth suggests running outside in his tidy whities.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4512,"title":"Back to green with 21 to go, Osborne out front","summary":"After the lap-25 stage-break re-rack, the stayed-out 81 of Jonathan Osborne leads the field back to green with Robertson and Pope in a fresh fight behind him.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4674,"title":"Pope retakes the lead from Osborne","summary":"The 27 of Tim Pope works around the 81 of Jonathan Osborne for the race lead and starts flirting with purple fastest laps, checking out for good.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5730,"title":"'Kinda sheisty' — McDonnell whacks Bittner","summary":"The 23 of Sean McDonnell hits Josh Bittner while Bittner was mid-pass on the 88 of Adamson — the booth calls it 'kind of sheisty' and wonders if Chudzilla will start destroying the city of Chicago.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","josh-bittner","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6310,"title":"Late pile-up in the smoke screen","summary":"In the closing laps the 98 of Michael Taylor gets wedged against the wall in the tire barrier, Bittner gets into the back of him, and spinning tires fill the corner with a smoke screen nobody can see through.","tags":["mike-taylor","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6495,"title":"Pope takes the checkers on the streets of Chicago","summary":"Tim Pope crosses the line as the race victor, with Trevor Robertson second and Alan Vaught completing the podium; Dustyn Eaton fourth and Sean McDonnell fifth.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":873,"quote":"Just like Icarus, I have flown a little too close to the sun here today.","context":"Alan Brown opening the show sunburned after five and a half hours on a golf course","gold":3},{"t":1215,"quote":"Zuckerberg and Bill Gates, they're combining to try to dominate the world, so yes it's probably their fault that we're having issues.","context":"the booth blaming the broadcast graphics outage","gold":3},{"t":1694,"quote":"We're gonna get a giant pile up, a Chicago style pile up like we saw in The Blues Brothers.","context":"early-race carnage stacking up in the tight rhythm section","gold":4},{"t":4316,"quote":"False alarm guys, I'm not on fire, thank God.","context":"Allen English returning after his smoke detector went off mid-broadcast","gold":4},{"t":4494,"quote":"Pope, don't do it buddy, don't do it, I'll give you a dollar.","context":"imagining team radio as teammate Pope stalked leader Robertson before the stage break","gold":4},{"t":5748,"quote":"Imagine that, a giant fish coming out of the lake named Chud, destroying Chicago.","context":"riffing on Josh Bittner's Chudzilla truck after he got dumped","gold":4},{"t":6402,"quote":"You probably downloaded it 10 minutes before the race, that's usually how he rolls.","context":"marveling that Tim Pope is somehow good at road courses too","gold":3},{"t":6499,"quote":"Timothy Pope coming across the line, your race victor here tonight.","context":"the checkered flag call at the Chicago Street Circuit","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"The SDK scoring/overlay graphics service was down all night, so the booth called the race radio-style with no on-screen leaderboard; positions were read verbally and some mid-race running order may be imprecise. No post-race interviews — Alan Brown shut the stream down early for real-life work. Lori Vaught served as race control (she appears 16th in the grid rundown, likely the pace/control entry, and is not in the finishing order). Full finishing order read on air: Pope, Robertson, J. Vaught, Eaton, McDonnell, Klein, Osborne, Bittner, Long, Dickerson, Rincon, Bryant, Kuehl, Coffin, Player, Everage, K. Vaught, Adamson, Anderson, Mayberry, Taylor, Paul, Gallagher, Burke, Whittenburg, Dixon (DC), Dobson. Race: 50 laps with one stage-break caution at lap 25; one fast repair; presented by Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"_N_Wq3-gDA8":{"recap":"The Season 14 finale at Charlotte Motor Speedway settled both VRL titles in one 133-lap, 200-mile night with no fast repairs. A first-lap Big One on the frontstretch — sparked when the 10 got loose — collected Mike Adamson, Dave Mayberry, Jorge Rincon and more, and a second early pileup helped whittle the 25-truck field to 16 healthy trucks. Jacob Alesia, starting from the rear with a penalty and needing a win to steal the Cup, charged up 22 spots to the front and traded the lead all night while points leader Chris Goans rode conservatively in the top ten. Alesia out-dueled Dillon Bryant on the final restart to win the race, but Goans launched a kamikaze move into turn three, passed two trucks for fourth, and clinched the VRL Cup by a single point. Bryant, who came from the back after a jump-start black flag, finished third and locked up the Contender Championship, with Andy Player charging to second.","winner":"Jacob Alesia","podium":["Jacob Alesia","Andrew Player","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":800,"title":"The Big One on Lap 1","summary":"Jump-start black flags for Bryant and Dixon, then a frontstretch pileup before lap one is done — the 10 gets loose, the 29 checks up, and Adamson, Mayberry, Rencon, Benfield and Osland all get swept in. First caution, first lap, no fast repairs.","tags":["dave-mayberry","mike-adamson","george-rincon","stony-benfield","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1139,"title":"The Poopsicle Machine","summary":"Chris Goans rolls out the Dude Wipes 'poopsicle' No. 1 truck — poopsicle emoji on the overlay and all — and the booth turns it into an impromptu ad read.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1254,"title":"Alesia storms the field","summary":"Starting from the back with a penalty, Jacob Alesia is up 18 spots by the first restart cycle with just one truck between him and title rival Chris Goans — the win-or-nothing charge is on.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1285,"title":"Tiebreaker rabbit hole","summary":"The booth walks the Cup tiebreaker list and finds Goans and Alesia dead even on wins, top-fives and average finish — criterion No. 8 is literally birth date. 'Hopefully they just settle it straight up on the track.'","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1452,"title":"Caution 2 thins the herd","summary":"Around lap 20 Gallagher misjudges a side draft on the outside of Everidge's 82 and the wreck collects Milner, Reading and Hunt — two early crashes have already knocked a third of the field out of contention.","tags":["john-gallagher","mike-everage","scott-milner","jesse-redding","kevin-hunt"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4539,"title":"Worst-timed caution","summary":"Mid pit cycle at lap ~106, Albert Anderson gets spat off pit exit into traffic and collected — the third caution lands at the worst possible moment for Goans, who was in the catbird seat, and turns the finale into a shootout.","tags":["albert-anderson","chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4904,"title":"iRacing scrambles its brain","summary":"The caution's freak timing breaks iRacing's scoring — the field is told to pass the pace car, phantom pass-under-yellow black flags fly, and the restart gets waved off repeatedly while Lori untangles the noodles.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5158,"title":"Everidge in the wall, Dixon rides the fence","summary":"On the long-awaited restart the 82 goes up not realizing Jack Dixon has a run 'ripping that wall' — super-tight contact puts Everidge in the fence and brings the caution back out with 19 to go.","tags":["mike-everage","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5317,"title":"Rooney calls his shot — for Player","summary":"Under caution, Scott Rooney tells the booth he's on old tires and 'Player's probably in the catbird seat to this deal' — Andy Player then dispatches everybody and finishes second.","tags":["scott-rooney","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5474,"title":"31 vs 51: not given an inch","summary":"Fifteen to go, Alesia hammers Bryant's Superman 51 for the lead lap after lap — bumper taps, both loose off the corners, 'tremendous respect, but not given an inch' — and Bryant keeps holding the top lane.","tags":["jacob-alicia","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5736,"title":"Spain spins, shootout set","summary":"Contact between the 10 and 12 checks up the pack — Gordon Spain goes around, Dustyn Eaton spins in the checkup, and the finale comes down to a three-lap natural restart for the race and the Cup.","tags":["gordon-spain","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5985,"title":"One point. One single point.","summary":"Final restart, three to go: Alesia clears Bryant to win the race, but Goans launches it into turn three — 'the car hadn't stuck in three all night' — passes two trucks for fourth and wins the VRL Cup by one point. Bryant seals the Contender Championship.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans","dylan-bryant","andrew-player","jack-dixon","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":307,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"Pre-race intro sting before the championship finale","gold":3},{"t":1155,"quote":"So hey dude, grab yourself a dude wipe and take care of the poopsicles.","context":"The booth riffs on Goans's Dude Wipes 'poopsicle' livery","gold":3},{"t":1203,"quote":"Jack Dixon said, 'How do you spell stupid?' J-A-C. That was a dumb start.","context":"Ricky reads Dixon's chat mea culpa after his jump-start black flag","gold":4},{"t":2663,"quote":"Four trucks under a blanket here... with a couple other hungry hounds looking in from the shadows behind him.","context":"Anderson, Eaton, Spain and Player nose-to-tail battling for third","gold":4},{"t":3360,"quote":"Superman not affected by any kryptonite here so far tonight. Sucking up all of the power from our yellow sun and putting it on the track.","context":"Bryant's No. 51 Superman truck out to a 3.8-second lead","gold":4},{"t":6025,"quote":"Gones has got to kamikaze — and he did. He just threw it in and passed two trucks.","context":"The championship-saving move on the final restart","gold":5},{"t":6085,"quote":"Alicia is going to win the race. Chris G is going to win the war.","context":"The finish call — race to Alesia, Cup to Goans by one point","gold":5},{"t":6595,"quote":"Man, do I have a rival. And boy, am I already tired of him winning.","context":"Race winner Alesia, 'the number one loser,' after losing the Cup by one point","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Names heavily garbled by auto-captions; best guesses used. 'Chris Gones' could be Gowens/Goins (captions: Gones, Gomes, Gwens, Gins, Golds). 'John Shanebarger' inferred from Chambacher/Shane Buckler/Bachler variants. 'Andrew Cowan' (#10) inferred from Cawan/Cawin/Carin/Coffton. The #16 Kyle's surname is unclear (captions: Vaude, Kyle W, Block, Watt) and may match announcer Alan Vaude's surname; he dropped repeatedly with packet loss. In the final rundown, 16th ('Watt struggled') and 18th ('Kelly Kuehl') are garbled and unresolved — both may be Kyle-related or a possible extra driver. Absent drivers mentioned: Tim Pope (#7, 3rd in points, not racing), Craig Goodenough (#89, one-week suspension for deliberate wrecking), West Kilgore. Booth said 'three cautions only' with 25 to go, but two more followed (five total by tape). Full stated results: Alesia, Player, Bryant, Gones, Dixon, A. Anderson, Cowan, Klein, Shanebarger, Rooney, then Spain 11th, Eaton 12th, Everidge 13th, McAdam 14th, Mayberry 15th. Race ran July 1, 2026 (Canada Day / America's 250th references); Season 15 opens July 8, 2026 at Atlanta (Echo Park configuration).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"_R_978AZYnQ":{"recap":"John Ellis won for the second consecutive week after a 100-lap iRacing Superspeedway race that changed personality completely. The field spent most of the opening run patiently organizing lanes and green-flag stops; Kelly Kuehl's save on pit entry kept that early sequence green. The night's first caution did not come from the pack at all, but from a pileup contained on pit road with fewer than 20 laps remaining. A later crash forced overtime and reduced the finish to one green-white-checkered attempt. Josh Bittner locked onto Ellis's bumper on the inside while Justin French and Robert Jordan built the strongest outside lane. Both groups reached the final lap together, with crashes breaking out behind and around the lead fight. Ellis held the run long enough to beat French by 0.03 seconds, and his postrace interview credited Bittner's push as the decisive help. The tape does not clearly establish every initiator in the late pack incidents, so the story preserves the chaos without assigning unsupported blame.","winner":"John Ellis","podium":["John Ellis","Justin French","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1795,"title":"Riehle and Kuehl lead the start","summary":"Dustin Riehle starts from pole with Kelly Kuehl outside as the 28-truck field settles into a patient opening run without a scheduled competition caution.","tags":["dustin-reilly","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2659,"title":"Kuehl saves a dangerous pit entry","summary":"A large group dives for its first green-flag stop and Kuehl nearly spins across pit road, but catches the truck before a major crash develops.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":3510,"title":"First caution shifts the pit window","summary":"The first race-control yellow arrives near the planned fuel window, allowing Mike Adamson to win the ensuing race off pit road over Bittner.","tags":["mike-adamson","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4751,"title":"Bittner turns Vaught on the restart","summary":"Bittner slots into line behind Vaught and makes contact that wrecks the No. 33, immediately undoing both drivers' track position.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5223,"title":"Another pack crash erupts","summary":"The field stacks up soon after the next restart, producing another large accident and continuing the sharp turn from the calm opening run to attrition.","tags":[],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6436,"title":"Pit-road pileup brings an unprecedented yellow","summary":"Vaught, Riehle, Dixon and Chandler Paul are among several trucks spinning or blocking the lane during green-flag stops, prompting the first pit-road-only caution the booth can remember.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-reilly","jack-dixon","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7112,"title":"Riehle crash resets the field again","summary":"A hard push destabilizes Riehle and triggers another yellow, continuing the wave of late cautions and incident-limit eliminations.","tags":["dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7613,"title":"Two-truck crash forces overtime","summary":"Late contact sends a truck into Mayberry and brings out the caution, setting up the race's only green-white-checkered attempt.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7950,"title":"Ellis controls the overtime restart","summary":"Ellis gets a strong launch with Bittner pushing low, while French and Jordan build momentum on the outside for the two-lap shootout.","tags":["john-ellis","josh-bittner","justin-french","robert-jordan"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":8040,"title":"Final-lap wreck thins the contenders","summary":"A crash behind the leaders catches Osborne, and further contact among Jordan, Bittner and Mike Adamson erupts across the finish line.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","robert-jordan","josh-bittner","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":8063,"title":"Ellis wins by three hundredths","summary":"Ellis holds the inside line to beat French by 0.03 seconds, with Rincon's unsupported outside move yielding third.","tags":["john-ellis","justin-french","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6545,"quote":"That's the first time ever during any of our broadcasts we've ever seen a caution flag thrown for a pileup on pit road.","context":"The booth reacts to the extraordinary pit-lane crash.","gold":5},{"t":7960,"quote":"Buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet, and throw inhibition out the window.","context":"The signature call before the green-white-checkered restart.","gold":5},{"t":8063,"quote":"Across the line, it's going to be Ellis with Justin French and George Rincon, your top three.","context":"The live finish call.","gold":5},{"t":8217,"quote":"I like the outside line at superspeedways. I mean, I'm all about the outside line.","context":"Rincon explains the move that carried him to third.","gold":2},{"t":8513,"quote":"It's a little risky, a little ballsy, but it made out all right.","context":"French describes dropping into a half-inch opening on a restart.","gold":5},{"t":9047,"quote":"Josh, for pushing me there — I'm sure he was trying to get around me, but he won that for me.","context":"Ellis credits Bittner's push for his second straight win.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews, and full rundown explicitly confirm Ellis, French, and Rincon. French and Rincon tied Jonathan Osborne for hard-charger honors at plus 18 positions; Osborne won the random draw after finishing seventh. The field had 28 starters, 17 classified finishers, and only 14 trucks on the lead lap at the finish. Chandler Paul's house lost power during a storm late in the race. The exact initiators of the caution near 58:30 and the pack crash near 1:27 are not clearly stated in the selected transcript lines, so those moments avoid driver attribution rather than guessing.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"a2E67tvasYs":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough started from pole and led much of the opening half of the Prairie Fire 200, but a mistaken five-lap fuel load forced an unscheduled stop and erased his Kansas playoff opportunity. The race began with two simultaneous first-lap crashes that damaged several contenders, while later yellows and pit cycles eventually put Dillon Bryant, Tim Pope, and Trevor Robertson at the front. A late caution for Stony Benfield led Pope and Robertson to take two tires against Bryant's four, and the ensuing restart stack-up severely damaged several drivers fighting around the Round of 8 cut line. Pope defended the bottom for the final five laps and held off Bryant, with Robertson third, while Jonathan Osborne, John McAdam, Josh Bittner, and Mike Adamson were provisionally eliminated from the playoffs.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Dillon Bryant","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1685,"title":"Goodenough launches the playoffs from pole","summary":"Craig Goodenough clears Mike Adamson at the start and leads the 32-truck field into the one-race Round of 12 eliminator at Kansas.","tags":["craig-goodenough","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1719,"title":"Two crashes erupt on the first lap","summary":"Pope and Adamson each snap loose in separate incidents; Jack Dixon is turned into the wall after checking up, and Kyle Vaught and Greg Dobson take heavy impacts in a crash involving roughly ten trucks.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","jack-dixon","john-gallagher","kyle-vaught","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2221,"title":"Coffin saves a sideways truck","summary":"Andrew Coffin gets completely sideways while racing Anthony Williams but catches the slide without hitting the wall, earning the booth's early save-of-the-race distinction.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","anthony-williams"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":2655,"title":"Bittner's spin brings the second yellow","summary":"Josh Bittner spins from eighth with Stony Benfield immediately behind him; the field avoids further contact, but the incident triggers a caution.","tags":["josh-bittner","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3610,"title":"Goodenough's fuel mistake ends his lead run","summary":"Goodenough unexpectedly pits from the lead and tells the booth he loaded only about five laps of fuel, dropping multiple laps in a major playoff setback.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3744,"title":"Jones spins leaving pit road","summary":"Dion Jones applies too much throttle on cold tires and loops his truck on the pit-exit apron, drawing a caution during the green-flag pit cycle and benefiting drivers who had stayed out.","tags":["dion-jones","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":4132,"title":"Wade takes the point from Bryant","summary":"Dustin Wade uses the draft to move around Dillon Bryant and take the lead as the front group reshuffles after the restart.","tags":["dustin-wade","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4515,"title":"Bryant works back to the lead","summary":"Bryant completes his recovery to first and begins controlling the long green run ahead of Pope and Robertson.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5808,"title":"Fresh tires turn the final stop into a chase","summary":"Pope and Robertson stop several laps later than Bryant and begin erasing his roughly six-second advantage at about half a second per lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6039,"title":"Benfield is turned with ten laps left","summary":"Contact from Dustyn Eaton turns Stony Benfield entering Turn 1 after the pair had mixed it up earlier, creating the late caution that resets the race.","tags":["stony-benfield","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6252,"title":"Restart pileup strikes the playoff bubble","summary":"Jorge Rincon loses revs at the restart and is hit by Dustin Wade, while John McAdam spins and Josh Bittner slides through the grass into the wall before Dustyn Eaton hits him; multiple bubble contenders are damaged.","tags":["george-rincon","dustin-wade","john-mcadam","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6664,"title":"Pope blocks his way to the Kansas win","summary":"On two right-side tires, Pope protects the bottom for five laps against four-tire Bryant; Robertson's outside pressure keeps Bryant defensive, and Pope wins ahead of Bryant and Robertson.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":947,"quote":"This is probably going to be the most intense night of the playoffs, even though it's the opening round.","context":"The booth frames the one-race Round of 12 elimination","gold":4},{"t":2221,"quote":"Coffin with a heck of a save. He didn't hit the wall. He was dead sideways.","context":"Andrew Coffin catches his truck after contact in the pack","gold":4},{"t":3610,"quote":"I didn't put enough fuel in it, I guess.","context":"Craig Goodenough explains why he suddenly pitted from the lead","gold":5},{"t":5860,"quote":"Twelve enter, eight leave.","context":"The booth relays Lori Vaught's Thunderdome-style playoff graphic","gold":4},{"t":6143,"quote":"The only one in your top six that has four tires is Dylan Bryant with 10 laps to go. I think it's going to get spicy right here.","context":"The booth compares Bryant's four tires with the leaders' two-tire calls","gold":4},{"t":6664,"quote":"Tim Pope's going to take home the victory!","context":"The winning call after Pope holds Bryant behind him","gold":5},{"t":6957,"quote":"That's probably the most fun third-place finish I've ever had.","context":"Trevor Robertson reacts to the final-lap fight","gold":4},{"t":7593,"quote":"I hate blocking that much, but it's a playoff run. So, I done all I could do to keep him behind me.","context":"Winner Tim Pope explains his defense against Bryant","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 12, Round 13 at Kansas according to seasons_map.json; the metadata title identifies this as the Prairie Fire 200 and the single-race Playoffs Round of 12. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Pope-Bryant-Robertson podium and later lists Osborne, McAdam, Bittner, and Adamson as the provisional four eliminated drivers, subject to post-race penalties. The starting-grid readout names 31 of 32 starters but skips the driver in 31st, so no unsupported identity is added. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for the driver consistently captioned as 'Dustyn Eaton.' The booth initially treats Rincon's lost revs as a probable missed shift but does not establish the mechanical cause with certainty. Transcript timestamps end before the 7,965-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"AcMVE7O9SVk":{"recap":"The VRL Monster Mash brought 39 trucks to the Monster Mile at Dover, and the concrete monster ate all night — the first caution flew before the opening lap was done when front-row starter Ricky Whittenburg slapped the wall and spun. The wrecks never stopped, from a turn-three Big One the booth called a smorgasbord to a restart disaster where Russ Kilgore money-shifted his engine and Jack Dixon went barrel-rolling through the field. Dixon somehow recovered from being upside down to hunt Andrew Player at the finish, sending it deep twice on the final lap but unable to make it stick. Player's No. 18 held on to become the season's first two-time winner — two in a row — with Dixon second and Jorge Rincon third, as only seven trucks finished on the lead lap.","winner":"Andrew Player","podium":["Andrew Player","Jack Dixon","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1390,"title":"Whittenburg walls it before lap one is done","summary":"On the opening green flag, the 55 of Ricky Whittenburg slaps the outside wall off the front row and spins, bringing out the first caution of the night.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2050,"title":"Adamson collects his own teammate","summary":"A big multi-truck wreck erupts three-wide — Mike Adamson's 751 is in the middle of it and takes out Limitless teammate Albert Anderson, with Chandler Paul catching heavy damage too.","tags":["mike-adamson","albert-anderson","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2388,"title":"The Big One in turn three — a smorgasbord","summary":"A restart pileup in turn three sweeps up Player, Klein, Osborne, Kilgore, Mayberry, Herkis and more — the booth declares the monster is hungry and having a smorgasbord.","tags":["andrew-player","greg-cline","jonathan-osborne","russ-kilgore","dave-mayberry","charlie-herkis","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3222,"title":"Albert Anderson's sandwich-and-beer pit stop","summary":"Wrecked out with 24 minutes of required repairs, Albert Anderson joins the booth from pit road and announces his plan: a ham-and-turkey sandwich, a cold Corona, and then back out on track.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3950,"title":"Home Depot love tap sends Emig for a wild ride","summary":"The slightest of taps from Jeffrey Johnson's No. 20 Home Depot machine spins David Emig around at speed — the booth likens it to renting a jackhammer instead of buying a hammer drill.","tags":["jeffrey-johnson","david-emig"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4197,"title":"Chachi: racing with a mouth controller","summary":"The booth spotlights Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne, who races on a special controller made to fit his mouth with no force feedback — and runs the lead lap all night anyway.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4470,"title":"No. 20 disqualified and booted from the server","summary":"Jeffrey Johnson, driver of the 20 Home Depot machine, is disqualified, removed from the race and removed from the server — the booth wonders aloud if anger was involved.","tags":["jeffrey-johnson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4819,"title":"Mayberry and Endicott tangle like a rugby scrum","summary":"Endicott slingshots off the outside wall across the line and into Hot Rod Mayberry, sending him for a wild ride while Alan Vaught saves a huge slide through the grass behind them.","tags":["dave-mayberry","russ-endicott","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5315,"title":"Front-stretch pileup swallows the pack","summary":"After the 82 walls it, a huge front-stretch wreck collects loads of trucks including Greg Klein — who had just gotten his lap back — plus Ricky Whittenburg and Dion Jones.","tags":["russ-endicott","greg-cline","ricky-whittenburg","dion-jones","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5624,"title":"Money shift! Dixon barrel rolls on the restart","summary":"Russ Kilgore money-shifts and blows his engine right at the restart, triggering a massive wreck before the start-finish line that sends Jack Dixon barrel rolling and damages Whittenburg, Emig and Endicott — Dixon still recovers to finish second.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jack-dixon","ricky-whittenburg","david-emig","russ-endicott"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6555,"title":"Burke's engine lets go, setting up a seven-truck lead lap","summary":"Jeremiah Burke goes sideways across the track with a blown engine late, bringing out the caution that traps most of the field and leaves just seven trucks on the lead lap for the finish.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonah-long"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7355,"title":"Player holds off the Ripper for two straight","summary":"On the white-flag lap Jack Dixon sends it deep into the corners twice but can't make it stick — Andrew Player crosses the line with nerves of steel as the season's first two-time winner, with Jorge Rincon hanging on for third.","tags":["andrew-player","jack-dixon","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2494,"quote":"The pile up continues here in this monster, man — he is hungry and he is having a smorgasbord.","context":"calling the turn-three Big One","gold":4},{"t":3267,"quote":"I'm sitting on Pit Road, got 24 minutes of required repairs — I'm gonna eat a half a sandwich, have a cold beer, and pull back out onto the track when I get a new truck.","context":"Albert Anderson, wrecked out, joins the booth from pit road","gold":5},{"t":3435,"quote":"Ooh, Yahtzee! Sorry buddy, I didn't see where the yellow came out — I just saw the yellow wave.","context":"a caution catching the booth mid-sentence","gold":3},{"t":3863,"quote":"My nerves are all shot — I feel like I'm in Waco on I-35, a pistol in one hand, a cell phone in the other, and I'm driving with my knees.","context":"the booth reacting to relentless three-wide racing","gold":4},{"t":5640,"quote":"Yellow's out — Jack Dixon does a barrel roll! The seven, I think he money shifted, boys!","context":"Kilgore blows his engine on the restart and Dixon goes airborne","gold":5},{"t":6988,"quote":"Two things: Delaware, I don't believe, is actually real — I've never heard of anybody from there. And secondly, somebody get this pace truck driver a breathalyzer or something.","context":"late-race caution laps dragging on behind a wandering pace truck","gold":4},{"t":8435,"quote":"Monster Mile always living up to its name — Miles, he hungry, and he ate.","context":"signing off after a night of carnage at Dover","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"150-lap NASCAR Trucks race at Dover with 39 starters; stage break at lap 75; only 7 trucks finished on the lead lap. Broadcast had major audio issues for the first ~15 minutes (booth mics dropped). 'David fight' (#1, Hope It Sticks team) spelling is a best guess as David Feit. 'Andrew Carlton' (27th in the finish rundown) may be a caption garble of Andrew Coffin (#10) or a separate driver. Mike 'Epson' references appear to be garbles of Mike Adamson. Random-draw driver of the day: Earl Evans (#13); hard charger: Mike Sobanovski (up 25 spots to 10th). League run by Jess and Lori (per interviews). Next race announced: Atlanta, Thanksgiving week. All driver names are best-guess reconstructions from auto-captions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"AOK-1xb9ZCA":{"recap":"Tim Pope led from the pole and won the Hawkeye Classic at Iowa Speedway, the final playoff cut race before the VRL championship finale at New Hampshire. After first-lap chaos that sent John Gallagher hard into the inside wall, the 177-lap race settled into a marathon caution-free green-flag run through the middle stages, with the Ain't Dead Yet trio of Pope, Josh Bittner, and Trevor Robertson controlling the front. Late yellows — including a front-stretch wreck the booth blamed on net code that ended Albert Anderson's night and collected Mike Adamson and Larry Dickerson — bunched the field for a frantic finish, where Pope and Jonathan Osborne traded the lead with crossover moves before Pope pulled clear to win over Osborne and Dickerson. League owner Alan Vaught charged 19 positions to fifth as the hard charger but came up about four points short of the cut. Pope, Osborne, Dustyn Eaton, and Josh Bittner advance to the championship race at New Hampshire, where Pope chases a third title.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jonathan Osborne","Larry Dickerson"],"moments":[{"t":1465,"title":"First-lap chaos: Gallagher into the wall","summary":"On the opening lap Albert Anderson tapped John Gallagher's rear quarter panel, sending the 123 hard into the inside wall; Sean McDonnell piled into the back of him and Jeremiah Burke spun on the apron avoiding it, drawing the first caution.","tags":["john-gallagher","albert-anderson","shawn-mcdonald","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2572,"title":"Green-flag money laps begin","summary":"Zachary Henin kicked off the first green-flag pit cycle around lap 40 on a treacherous mid-corner pit entry, and the booth marveled that the whole field handled the stops cleaner than real NASCAR drivers do.","tags":["zachary-henin"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2990,"title":"Kevin Hunt black-flagged for speeding","summary":"Kevin Hunt's Richard Petty-themed 434 caught a black flag for speeding on pit road, burying him four laps down and killing his night early.","tags":["kevin-hunt"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3628,"title":"Teammates until you ain't one","summary":"Cut-line teammates Larry Dickerson and Albert Anderson went at it three wide through the trioval, with Dickerson pinching Anderson low into turn one and scraping the wall himself — both fighting for their playoff lives.","tags":["larry-dickerson","albert-anderson","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5148,"title":"Albert gets Klein'd","summary":"Albert Anderson wound up in the wall after contact with Greg Klein — the league's famous bumper artist — and the booth immediately cued up the catchphrase and warned Klein to watch his tailgate for payback.","tags":["albert-anderson","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5264,"title":"Caution flies during the money stop","summary":"Jeremiah Burke spun off turn four in the middle of the final green-flag pit cycle, drawing a surprise caution that scrambled strategy, stranded some drivers a lap down, and set up a cut-line shootout.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5778,"title":"Net code bites Albert on the front stretch","summary":"Albert Anderson slid up in front of George Ranone's 28 on the front stretch and wrecked hard — the booth ruled it net code — collecting Mike Adamson, whose truck snagged Larry Dickerson as debris flew. Anderson smacked the wall, drew a meatball flag, and his playoff hopes ended on the spot.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-adamson","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6102,"title":"Osborne slings it around Pope","summary":"On the restart with 14 laps to go, Jonathan Osborne built momentum on the high side and slung his way back around Tim Pope to retake the lead while Bittner and Robertson dueled side by side behind them.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6278,"title":"Chachi and Pope: crossover madness","summary":"The signature battle of the night — Tim Pope worked the bottom while Jonathan Osborne threw crossover after crossover at him for the lead, nearly three wide behind them, before Pope finally cleared away in the closing laps.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6391,"title":"Eaton hot-steps through the infield","summary":"With three laps to go and his playoff spot on the line, Dustyn Eaton went full-send through the infield grass and somehow rejoined without losing it, keeping his championship dreams alive.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6420,"title":"Pope punches his championship ticket","summary":"Tim Pope drove off unchallenged over the final laps to win at Iowa, with Jonathan Osborne second and Larry Dickerson claiming the last podium spot after staying out on the final caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6997,"title":"The Milk Dud thanks literally everyone","summary":"Third-place finisher Larry Dickerson delivered an all-time podium shoutout list — his third cousin's ex-husband, his dogs, his roosters, his mailman, and 'the guy I said hey to pumping gas last month' — before signing off with 'the Milk Dud is out.'","tags":["larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":595,"quote":"Which driver's going to make it on through, or which ones are going to be eating corn in the hayfields later on here tonight?","context":"Opening welcome to the playoff cut race at Iowa","gold":3},{"t":979,"quote":"Hopefully some fisticuffs — you know, maybe somebody throws a helmet at somebody.","context":"Previewing playoff desperation before the green flag","gold":3},{"t":1312,"quote":"Watch out folks, he'll dump you.","context":"Introducing Greg Klein on the starting grid","gold":4},{"t":3013,"quote":"We've seen actual NASCAR drivers on the iRacing service — they don't do it as well as the guys in VRL, sorry.","context":"Praising the field's flawless green-flag pit stops","gold":3},{"t":3753,"quote":"The bears are freaking everywhere, son.","context":"Mid-race tangent about western Canada wildlife","gold":3},{"t":3992,"quote":"This year the season champion will receive a one million dollar bonus and a lifetime membership to the VRL... what? Yeah, that doesn't sound right.","context":"Reading a prank fun-fact planted in the halfway notes","gold":4},{"t":5148,"quote":"Albert in the wall — uh oh, you got Klein'd! Klein Klein'd him!","context":"Greg Klein puts Albert Anderson into the wall","gold":4},{"t":6302,"quote":"Chachi and Pope fighting for a lead — I love this! The crossovers, the madness, I love it!","context":"Pope and Osborne trading the lead in the closing laps","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race: 177 laps at Iowa Speedway (trucks), second playoff cut race before the championship finale at New Hampshire; Pope, Osborne, Eaton, and Bitner advance per the winner's-circle segment, with the booth noting official point tallies come the next day. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Alan Vaught'/'Kyle Vaught' (captions: vot/fought), 'Dustyn Eaton' (booth repeatedly says 'Dustin with a Y'), 'Zachary Henin', 'Andrew Coffin', 'George Ranone', 'David Feit' (booth puns 'ready to fight it out'), 'Kelly Kuehl', 'Mike Everage', and 'Craig Goodenough' (booth puns 'not just okay, he is good enough'). Lori (league administrator and race control, likely Lori Vaught given Jess/Kyle) is credited throughout but did not race. Only two cautions until the late stages; final finishing order read starting around 7533s.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"awX5rJrJqT4":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant won the 133-lap Texas race after a caution-free contest turned into a three-stop tire and fuel strategy test. Polesitter Albert Anderson led the opening stint, but Bryant's faster first pit stop put him ahead when the cycle completed. Mike Adamson used an offset strategy and an early set of fresh tires to lead a long middle stretch after starting 19th, then converted the gamble into a third-place finish. Bryant reclaimed command through the final green-flag cycle and won by roughly five seconds over Anderson, while a last-lap clash involving John McAdam, Gordon Spain, and the slowing John Osborne provided the night's final incident.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Albert Anderson","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":710,"title":"Anderson controls the opening green","summary":"Polesitter Albert Anderson clears Trevor Robertson at the start and immediately establishes himself at the front of the 33-truck field.","tags":["albert-anderson","trevor-robertson","chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1000,"title":"Dobson's night unravels at the wall","summary":"Greg Dobson tags the outside wall around lap 13, damages a toe link, and later reports six and a half minutes of repairs plus a 65-second pit-speeding hold.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1779,"title":"First green-flag stops open the strategy race","summary":"John Osborne, Trevor Robertson, John Gallagher, and Michael Brooks lead the first wave down pit road around lap 35 as teams decide when to use their two replacement tire sets.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","john-gallagher","michael-brooks"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1896,"title":"Bryant jumps Anderson on pit road","summary":"Bryant's 12.15-second stop and Chris Goans's 12.20 beat Anderson's 12.95, cycling Bryant into the lead with Goans and Anderson behind him.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2490,"title":"Turn 4 bites Goans and Vaught","summary":"Chris Goans jumps the cushion while following Bryant and strikes the wall, then Kyle Vaught suffers an almost identical hit that sends him to pit road with major wheel damage.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2659,"title":"Kuehl hits the wall twice","summary":"Kelly Kuehl pounds the Turn 4 wall on consecutive impacts and limps toward pit road as Texas continues to punish right-front suspension components.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3094,"title":"Adamson keeps the lead after stop two","summary":"Mike Adamson's early-tire strategy gives him enough margin to retain the lead after the second pit sequence, with Jacob Alesia rapidly closing on fresher tires.","tags":["mike-adamson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3345,"title":"Alesia catches Adamson","summary":"Jacob Alesia erases Adamson's advantage and takes the lead, but Bryant immediately attacks the new leader from the outside and soon restores himself to the point.","tags":["jacob-alicia","mike-adamson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4180,"title":"Final stops favor Bryant","summary":"The last green-flag cycle leaves Bryant more than six seconds ahead of Anderson, while a pit penalty drops Alesia from contention and Adamson's alternate plan settles into a podium run.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","jacob-alicia","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4998,"title":"Bryant wins the flag-to-flag green run","summary":"Bryant completes the final lap about five seconds clear of Anderson, and Adamson finishes third after climbing 16 positions.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5852,"title":"McAdam and Spain clash at the line","summary":"The replay shows John McAdam move around a slowing John Osborne and clip Gordon Spain near the finish, extending into post-race contact that race control is left to review.","tags":["john-mcadam","jonathan-osborne","gordon-spain"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1919,"quote":"Seems like when Dylan Bryant gets out front, it's tough to pass him back unless he makes a mistake on his own.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg assesses Bryant immediately after the first pit cycle","gold":4},{"t":3944,"quote":"The first thing you want to do is not hit the wall.","context":"Kyle Vaught begins an in-car explanation after his own wall contact","gold":4},{"t":5078,"quote":"A fast truck, I guess. I love this track, especially in one and two. It has character to it.","context":"Dillon Bryant gives the simple explanation for his winning speed","gold":5},{"t":5401,"quote":"I would rather be a little bit cautious and be consistent and bring it home on a podium versus pushing it and blowing my pit entry.","context":"Albert Anderson explains the conservative final stop that left him second","gold":4},{"t":5524,"quote":"With racing, a little bit of talent and a whole lot of luck.","context":"Anderson sums up his season-long points lead","gold":4},{"t":5636,"quote":"I took tires when I figured everybody else wouldn't. I felt like that was my best shot to maybe get out and stretch it.","context":"Mike Adamson explains the offset strategy that carried him from 19th to third","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The race ran all 133 laps without a caution. The 33-driver participant list is reconstructed from the partial starting-grid readout and the complete early through-the-field segment. The final finishing-order captions contain duplicated or garbled names in positions 16–29, so only the explicitly clear podium and other directly stated positions are treated as results. The lead announcer's surname is rendered as Wat/Vault/Vaude in captions and canonicalized to Alan Vaught via the roster.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"aYhARPAUpBs":{"recap":"Michigan produced Jonathan Osborne's first regular-season victory and one of the archive's clearest sportsmanship finishes. Alan Vaught, Dustyn Eaton and Albert Anderson established the multi-lane fight at the front while tire and fuel sequences moved control through the field. Later, Jeremiah Burke unintentionally spun Osborne, but the timing gave Osborne a fresh-tire opportunity without race-ending damage. A six-lap-to-go pileup created one final reset. Dillon Bryant took the lead, while Osborne used the newer grip to drive back through the contenders and attack on the last lap. Osborne completed the pass, then threw an aggressive block against Bryant's crossover to protect the win. In their postrace interviews, Osborne openly acknowledges the block and Bryant explains that he could have turned him but chose not to. Bryant finished second and Burke recovered from 27th to third. The final beat is therefore more than a fresh-tire charge: it is a hard racing move followed by a deliberate choice not to settle it with contact.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Dillon Bryant","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":656,"title":"Pope leads the field to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Tim Pope launches the 29-truck field for 110 laps at Michigan and leads the opening circuit ahead of Alan Vaught and Osborne.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1157,"title":"Three-wide contact triggers the first caution","summary":"Dustyn Eaton moves up into Derek Welch, sending Welch into John Gallagher and starting a chain reaction that also involves Andrew Player, John McAdam, Kyle Vaught and Larry Dickerson.","tags":["dustin-eaton","derek-welch","john-gallagher","andrew-player","john-mcadam","kyle-vaught","larry-dickerson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1655,"title":"Burke and Bittner crash on the backstretch","summary":"Jeremiah Burke comes down after struggling for grip and clips Josh Bittner, whose truck pounds the inside barrier and is effectively eliminated from contention.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2284,"title":"Three-wide fight for the lead","summary":"Eaton, Vaught and Albert Anderson run three abreast at the front as the race settles into an extended green-flag stretch.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2590,"title":"Leaders begin green-flag stops","summary":"Vaught, Eaton, Mike Adamson and most of the lead group pit together, while two-tire and four-tire choices split the field into distinct strategy cycles.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","mike-adamson","derek-welch","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4393,"title":"Mayberry incident resets the strategy race","summary":"Dave Mayberry and Jack Dixon make contact as Mayberry tries to reach pit road, and Mayberry then slides into Kyle Vaught to produce the third caution.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jack-dixon","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4696,"title":"Everage crashes immediately after the restart","summary":"Michael Everage is badly damaged in a quick fourth caution, removing the leaders' remaining fuel concern for the scheduled distance.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5253,"title":"Burke spins Osborne late","summary":"Burke washes up into Osborne's left rear while racing on the backstretch, spinning Osborne without major contact and giving him an opportunity to pit for fresh tires.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5656,"title":"Six-to-go restart produces another pileup","summary":"Burke drives into the back of Dion Jones in the tri-oval, triggering a caution that also catches Kelly Kuehl and Jack Dixon and sets up one last restart.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dion-jones","kelly-keel","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5927,"title":"Bryant takes command with five to go","summary":"On fresh tires, Bryant drives underneath Vaught for the lead while Burke and Osborne begin advancing through the closing pack.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":6089,"title":"Osborne attacks on the final lap","summary":"Osborne dives beneath Bryant for the lead, then blocks Bryant's crossover as the pair races through the final corners.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6110,"title":"Osborne wins as Eaton spins","summary":"Osborne reaches the checkered flag ahead of Bryant and Burke while Eaton spins in the scramble behind them coming to the line.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dylan-bryant","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6110,"quote":"Checkered flag. Osborne wins it!","context":"The live call as Osborne reaches the line ahead of Bryant while Eaton spins behind them.","gold":5},{"t":6583,"quote":"I short-pitted one lap on everybody, and I gained a bunch of track position and broke free with Dustin and Jess there.","context":"Osborne describes the early strategy that established him near the front.","gold":5},{"t":6639,"quote":"I honestly, I just didn't lift. Like, I just drove through the field. I can't believe it stuck the way it did.","context":"Osborne explains his late charge on fresh tires after being spun.","gold":5},{"t":6671,"quote":"I threw a pretty big block coming out of two on Dylan. I was just hoping that he wouldn't turn me there, and he's a good sport about it.","context":"Osborne acknowledges the decisive defensive move on the final lap.","gold":5},{"t":6825,"quote":"I prefer to win it fair. Even though when you throw an aggressive block, you're kind of at the mercy of the car that you toss that block on.","context":"Runner-up Bryant explains why he did not turn Osborne after the block.","gold":5},{"t":7120,"quote":"I know I wrecked Osborne for sure, so congratulations to him. You're welcome.","context":"Third-place Burke jokes that his earlier contact created Osborne's winning tire opportunity.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, top-three interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Osborne, Bryant and Burke. The broadcast usually shortens the winner's name to John Osborne, but the roster canonical is Jonathan Osborne. Greg Dobson is the 29th starter and finisher; the starting-grid caption's 'Greg Thompson' at 18th is treated as a transcription error because Dobson discusses his early crash in chat and is explicitly named in the final results. Trevor Robertson missed the session and did not start, so he is not included among the 29 participants. Alan Vaught and Kyle Vaught follow the roster spellings despite repeated caption variants; Kelly Kuehl is repeatedly captioned as Kelly Kuehl. The solo broadcaster identifies himself as Steve and the network as Track Limits, but no surname is spoken in this transcript.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"b7ap9vXsIas":{"recap":"Dustyn Eaton won the VRL Olympics street-stock exhibition at Phoenix after recovering from a lap-one incident in a 150-lap race run without incident cautions. Jeremiah Burke won the first 50-lap stage and Jason Gaines the second, while repeated green-flag pit cycles and the two scheduled stage yellows continually reshuffled the order. Gaines tried to stretch fuel in the final stint but had to pit with about ten laps remaining, leaving Alan Vaught, Eaton, Burke, Craig Goodenough, and John Osborne in a crowded fight for the win. Burke's contact spun Vaught from the lead, Eaton escaped, and further last-lap contact left Osborne second and Goodenough third.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Jonathan Osborne","Craig Goodenough"],"moments":[{"t":1346,"title":"Street stocks scatter on lap one","summary":"The no-caution exhibition begins with several cars spinning through the opening corners, including Andrew Player and Jason Gaines, while pole-sitter Alan Vaught escapes the early chaos.","tags":["andrew-player","jason-gaines","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1518,"title":"Osborne and Dixon take a ride","summary":"John Osborne and Jack Dixon make contact while battling behind the leaders and both slide toward the inside wall, but the race stays green under the exhibition rules.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1741,"title":"Bryant spins from the lead fight","summary":"Dillon Bryant loses the rear while racing near the front and spins, surrendering track position with no yellow available to regroup the field.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2085,"title":"Maroth spins in front of the leaders","summary":"Darby Maroth loses control directly ahead of the lead pack and tags Tim Pope, costing Pope significant time in the first stint.","tags":["darby-maroth","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2941,"title":"Burke wins Stage 1","summary":"Jeremiah Burke reaches the first scheduled caution with a large lead and wins the opening stage over Dustin Wade and Jack Dixon.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-wade","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4055,"title":"Three-wide squeeze costs Kuehl","summary":"A tight three-wide exchange ends in contact for Kelly Kuehl, costing him substantial time during the second green-flag stint.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4606,"title":"Young and Coffin collide before the stage","summary":"Andrew Coffin makes contact with Jacob Young, spinning Young into Greg Dobson's path and leaving Coffin damaged against the wall shortly before the scheduled yellow.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","jacob-young","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4687,"title":"Gaines wins Stage 2","summary":"Jason Gaines leads the field to the second scheduled stage break, followed by Jeremiah Burke, Alan Vaught, Jack Dixon, and Dustyn Eaton.","tags":["jason-gaines","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jack-dixon","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":5030,"title":"Four-wide chaos after the final restart","summary":"The final stint opens with multiple spins and a four-wide squeeze involving Jorge Rincon, Greg Klein, Craig Goodenough, and Jack Dixon, all without an incident caution.","tags":["george-rincon","greg-cline","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6144,"title":"Gaines' fuel gamble ends","summary":"Jason Gaines' long final-stint fuel run briefly gives him a huge lead, but he must pit with roughly ten laps left and hands the race back to the battling pack.","tags":["jason-gaines"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6342,"title":"Burke spins Vaught from the lead","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets into Alan Vaught with only a few laps remaining, spinning Vaught out of the lead and allowing Dustyn Eaton to break clear.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6457,"title":"Eaton survives the last-lap melee","summary":"Eaton wins while Burke is spun across Dillon Bryant's nose in the final-lap fight; John Osborne finishes second and Craig Goodenough emerges third.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke","dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1092,"quote":"If you spin around, get into that outside wall, it'll all get fixed up automatically.","context":"Alan Brown explains the no-damage exhibition format","gold":2},{"t":5335,"quote":"I've never raced so hard in my life.","context":"John Osborne describes the final stint after finishing second","gold":4},{"t":5598,"quote":"I don't think I used the original part of the racetrack at all in that entire 150 laps.","context":"Craig Goodenough jokes about cutting Phoenix's dogleg","gold":4},{"t":5658,"quote":"Man, that was so fun at the end.","context":"Dustyn Eaton opens his winner interview","gold":4},{"t":5987,"quote":"On fresh fuel you feel like you're driving a '72 Cadillac out here, dang near a boat.","context":"Eaton explains the street stock's heavy handling","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"This was a VRL Olympics exhibition using old street stocks, unlimited tires, 30% fuel, no damage, and no incident cautions; the only yellows were the scheduled breaks at laps 50 and 100. The explicit finish call and post-race rundown confirm Eaton, Osborne, and Goodenough as the podium. The grid names 28 drivers. Allen English missed the broadcast because of a family emergency and Adam Turner was away, so Alan Brown called the race solo.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"B81dOTqTXPM":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson launched from pole and built a 12-second advantage by lap 20 before the scheduled lap-24 competition caution erased his first-half lead. Behind him, Dustyn Eaton and Jorge Rincon collided early, Craig Goodenough used door contact to take second from Jonathan Osborne, and the halfway restart sent both Goodenough and Osborne tumbling out of the lead fight while Robertson escaped. Tim Pope converted his rear-of-field penalty into a remarkable charge, climbing to fourth immediately after the restart, pressuring Mike Adamson into a late half-spin, and completing the final pit cycle in second; Andrew Player held off Dillon Bryant for the last podium place. Robertson survived a late half-spin, immediately made his final stop, carved back through the temporary leaders on fresh tires, and won by just under 15 seconds over Pope and Player.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Tim Pope","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":2151,"title":"Robertson controls the Roval launch","summary":"Pole-sitter Robertson gets cleanly through Turn 1 and leads Osborne and Player while the 28-truck field files through the opening corners.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2262,"title":"Eaton and Rincon collide at the bus stop","summary":"Eaton arrives aggressively under braking and tangles with playoff rival Rincon on the backstretch approach, leaving Rincon's truck with heavy left-front damage.","tags":["dustin-eaton","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":3938,"title":"Robertson stretches the first stint to 12 seconds","summary":"With the field approaching the planned competition caution, Robertson is already 12 seconds clear of Osborne and has put on what the booth calls a clinic.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"dominance"},{"t":4192,"title":"Goodenough doors Osborne for second","summary":"Goodenough makes contact as he powers past Osborne for second just before the competition caution; Osborne immediately attacks back, later calling it hard but fun racing.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"contact_pass"},{"t":4810,"title":"Halfway restart clears Robertson's escape route","summary":"After the scheduled caution regroups the field, Goodenough overcooks Turn 1 trying to stay alongside Robertson and Osborne spins moments later. Both front-row threats fall back while Robertson drives away.","tags":["trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"restart_wreck"},{"t":4984,"title":"Pope storms from the penalty line to fourth","summary":"Pope capitalizes on the restart trouble and reaches fourth behind Robertson, Player, and Adamson after beginning 21st under a rear-of-field penalty.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","andrew-player","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":5511,"title":"Robertson catches a half-spin and dives to pit road","summary":"The leader nearly rotates as rear grip disappears, saves the truck without contact, loses significant time, and immediately makes his final stop, temporarily handing the lead to Pope.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":5646,"title":"Fresh-tire Robertson slices through the cycle","summary":"Robertson wastes no time after his stop, making a daring outside pass on Rooney for fourth before taking third from Osborne as the remaining long runners peel off for service.","tags":["trevor-robertson","scott-rooney","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":5741,"title":"Bryant and Player drag-race off pit lane","summary":"Player rejoins beside Bryant after his final stop, and the two playoff contenders run inches apart without contact before Bryant noses ahead and Player resumes the chase.","tags":["dylan-bryant","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"pit_exit_battle"},{"t":5915,"title":"Pope's pressure breaks Adamson's defense","summary":"Pope hounds Adamson for the position that will become second after the pit cycle; Adamson half-spins beyond the start-finish line, saves the fenders, and yields the place.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"pressure_pass"},{"t":6547,"title":"Eaton protects seventh through the final bus stop","summary":"Driving despite an injured braking foot, Eaton withstands Goans's late attack and gets the better exit from the bus stop to preserve seventh on the final lap.","tags":["dustin-eaton","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"defense"},{"t":6663,"title":"Robertson completes a Roval rout","summary":"Robertson wins the Carolina Clash 109 by just under 15 seconds. Pope completes a 19-position recovery in second, Player takes third ahead of Bryant, and Greg Cline rounds out the top five.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","andrew-player","dylan-bryant","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3299,"quote":"He's putting on a clinic. He's lights-out fast.","context":"The booth recognizes Robertson's first-half Roval domination.","gold":5},{"t":5511,"quote":"Trevor Robertson, the leader, in the pits. He had a moment. He didn't spin out, but he lost a lot of time and almost spun out.","context":"The booth explains the save that forced Robertson into his final stop.","gold":5},{"t":6097,"quote":"Tim Pope, up 19 positions.","context":"The booth puts a number on Pope's rear-to-runner-up comeback.","gold":4},{"t":6633,"quote":"I mean, just really put on the clinic here tonight.","context":"The booth watches Robertson begin the final lap with the race in hand.","gold":5},{"t":6663,"quote":"He's going to win this by nearly 15 seconds.","context":"The live finish call as Robertson completes the Roval rout.","gold":5},{"t":7240,"quote":"Absolutely not. He was in a different world tonight. He's a master here.","context":"Pope answers whether he could have beaten Robertson without the penalty","gold":5},{"t":7375,"quote":"It started to get really loose. I half-spun it once, but was fortunately able to catch it.","context":"Robertson explains the save that triggered his final stop","gold":5},{"t":7474,"quote":"If I was going to lose the race, it was at that moment pretty much. So I'm glad it went my way.","context":"Robertson reflects on the hazardous halfway restart","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 12, Round 14 at the Charlotte Roval according to seasons_map.json. The Carolina Clash 109 ran 48 laps and 109 miles with 60% fuel, unlimited tires, no fast repairs, a 33-incident drive-through threshold plus six-incident increments, local cautions, and one planned full-course competition caution after completing lap 24. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Robertson-Pope-Player podium and reads all 28 classified drivers; fourth through tenth were Dillon Bryant, Greg Cline, Mike Adamson, Dustyn Eaton, Chris Goans, Jonathan Osborne, and Craig Goodenough. Tim Pope, Dustyn Eaton, John McAdam, and Jorge Rincon were among the drivers assigned rear-of-field penalties from Kansas; Stony Benfield was also named in the penalty rundown but did not start this race. Canonical roster spellings are used for Tim Pope, Greg Cline, Seth Holler, Andrew Cauthan, Chris Goans, and Sean McDonnell despite caption or spoken-result variants. All timestamps fall within the 7,691-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"BdpcGzJQNio":{"recap":"The VRL opened its seventh season with the Winter Classic 100, a 100-lap night truck race at Daytona that drew the league's largest field ever at 42 trucks, including roughly 14 newcomers. Polesitter Albert Anderson led much of a remarkably clean opening run — the first caution didn't fly until lap 39, when David Feit got sandwiched in the night's first big wreck. A frantic round of green-flag splash-and-go stops inside 15 to go stacked trucks up on pit road, and the race came down to a last-lap scramble as a wreck behind the leaders collected Anderson and Trevor Robertson. Kelly Kuehl in the 01 drag-raced past teammate Dustin Riehle at the line while Alan Vaught slid three-wide into third, completing a 1-2-3 sweep for Vigilante Force. Earl Evans was the hard charger of the night, climbing 31 spots to finish sixth.","winner":"Kelly Kuehl","podium":["Kelly Kuehl","Dustin Riehle","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1466,"title":"Green flag flies while the booth battles tech gremlins","summary":"The season 7 opener goes green almost off-camera as Alan English's iRacing client melts down, forcing radio-only commentary and killing driver cams for the night.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2078,"title":"Alan Vaught slips and slides into the lead","summary":"The 33 of Alan Vaught works past polesitter Albert Anderson, who jumps to the outside lane with a push from David Feit.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3306,"title":"Lap 39: the first Big One","summary":"Dustin Riehle bounces into John Curtis, who slides up into David Feit — the 10 of Andrew Cin gets sandwiched and Mike Everage is collected as the first caution finally flies after 39 clean laps.","tags":["dustin-reilly","john-curtis","david-fite","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3559,"title":"Breaking news: the Kissinger debate","summary":"Under caution the booth pivots to Henry Kissinger's death and argues over whether he was a warmonger, a statesman, or an American hero.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3916,"title":"Crispy tortillas and Piggly Wiggly","summary":"Edson Ochoa's H-E-B truck sends the booth into a long grocery-store tangent: homemade tortillas, mailed salsa, and the last Piggly Wiggly in northwest Louisiana.","tags":["edson-ochoa"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4137,"title":"Bad wreck collects Jonah Long","summary":"The Lucky Charms machine of Bobby Hammer clips Jonah Long's rear quarter panel, spinning him with Jonathan Osborne in bad shape and Dion Jones banging bumpers.","tags":["jonah-long","bobby-hammer","jonathan-osborne","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5216,"title":"Everage hard into the wall in lap traffic","summary":"Mike Everage and Nicholas Ramsey make contact around the lapped truck of Ray Radford — Scott Martin goes for a ride, John Curtis spins on the netcode, and Greg Klein gets caught in the mess.","tags":["mike-everage","nick-ramsey","ray-radford","scott-martin","john-curtis","greg-cline","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6560,"title":"The Mad Dash: green-flag splash-and-go chaos","summary":"The whole lead pack dives for fuel under green — Albert Anderson comes in cooking, Craig Goodenough gets black-flagged, trucks stack up and slide down pit road, and Jack Dixon later takes a pit lane penalty.","tags":["albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6937,"title":"White flag: three-wide for the win","summary":"Kelly Kuehl pushes Dustin Riehle and Alan Vaught pushes Mike Adamson into the final lap — Kuehl ducks low off turn four and drag-races to the line to steal the win as Vigilante Force sweeps the podium 1-2-3.","tags":["kelly-keel","dustin-reilly","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6972,"title":"Last-lap Big One behind the leaders","summary":"Rancone tags Bittner, Bittner tags Robertson, Robertson turns Albert Anderson — a pinball-machine wreck erupts behind the leaders on the final lap, taking out a big chunk of the field.","tags":["george-rincon","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7156,"title":"Earl Evans: hard charger, up 31 spots","summary":"The booth learns Earl Evans in the sponsored-not-sponsored AAA Broadcasting 13 climbed 31 positions to finish sixth as hard charger of the night.","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1011,"quote":"Daytona, where your friend can become your enemy and your enemy can become your friend pretty quickly.","context":"Setting the table for pack racing before the green flag","gold":3},{"t":1845,"quote":"I probably would have just kicked my computer, pulled the plug out of the wall, and thrown it out the window.","context":"Turner on how he'd have handled Brown's mid-broadcast iRacing meltdown","gold":3},{"t":3426,"quote":"The real life NASCAR drivers don't drive this good.","context":"39 caution-free laps at Daytona with 42 trucks before the first yellow","gold":4},{"t":4685,"quote":"I turn it up so loud that my neighborhood could be getting bombed by the Russians or something, I wouldn't hear it. All I hear is horsepower.","context":"English on the Crank It Up segment","gold":4},{"t":5842,"quote":"Have you ever tried to take a piece of string and push it across the table?","context":"English's analogy for why you never push the pusher","gold":3},{"t":6236,"quote":"A second is a football field here at Daytona.","context":"Explaining why pit box placement matters on the money stop","gold":3},{"t":6985,"quote":"Here comes the 01, he's going to drag race to the line with a big run at the end, steal it away from the 37!","context":"The winning call as Kelly Kuehl snatches the season opener from his own teammate at the stripe","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Names are heavily garbled by auto-captions. 'Vaught' (Jess, Kyle, and admin Lori) is a best-guess rendering of caption variants 'vot/VA/vault/vont'; 'Dustin Riehle' inferred from 'Dustin really'; 'Edson Ochoa' from 'Ooa'; 'Jorge Rincon' from 'rone/rancan/ranone'; 'Josh Bitner' from 'bner'; 'Andrew Cin' and 'Dustyn Eaton' (called 'Dustin with a Y') spellings uncertain. Video title says Winter Classic 100; on air it was billed as the season 7 opener, first of a two-platform winter season (trucks and Gen 4 cup cars). No driver cameras all night due to broadcaster Alan Brown's iRacing client issues. Lori Vaught was race controller/admin, not a driver. Larry Dickerson entered but start-and-parked due to illness. Finishing order beyond the podium was read out in full during the closing rundown (Adamson 4th, Pope 5th, Evans 6th).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"BgYzPCqLKxc":{"recap":"The VRL Skulls and Stars All-Star Qualifier brought 21 truck drivers to virtual North Wilkesboro for 120 laps in three stages, with only nine transfer spots into Wednesday night's All-Star race on the line. Andrew Player recovered from two botched starts to win Stage 1, and John McAdam — launching like a funny car on every restart — took Stage 2 under caution, then dropped from the server with packet loss moments after locking in his spot. Cautions flew all night at the treacherous short track, from Scott Rooney's opening-lap exit to Stony Benfield spinning out of third seconds after a booth shout-out, and a four-truck backfield pileup collecting Mayberry, Greg Klein, Dion Jones, and Anthony Williams. Mike Adamson never pitted after a mid-race caution mix-up, rode 70-lap-old tires and track position through the chaos, and took the checkered flag ahead of Jonathan Osborne and Josh Bittner in the unofficial results. The frantic final restarts left the last transfer spots provisional, pending race-admin tape review.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Jonathan Osborne","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":780,"title":"Rooney's night over before it starts","summary":"First caution on the opening lap: Scott Rooney gets in too hot, goes up into the fence and collects Dion Jones. Rooney disconnects immediately with major damage despite two fast repairs in hand.","tags":["scott-rooney","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1265,"title":"Four trucks under a blanket for the lead","summary":"Stage 1 sprint with Player, McAdam, Bittner and Klein nose-to-tail for the lead — Player makes the treacherous low line work and clears the 47 to take control.","tags":["andrew-player","john-mcadam","josh-bittner","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1607,"title":"Player punches his All-Star ticket","summary":"Andrew Player wins Stage 1 by nearly a second over McAdam and transfers straight into Wednesday's All-Star race, joking in his interview that he 'really botched those first two starts.'","tags":["andrew-player","john-mcadam","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":2320,"title":"The broadcaster's curse strikes Benfield","summary":"Seconds after the booth shouts out Stony Benfield for driving from 19th to third, he gets loose off the corner and the 92 of Greg Klein finishes off his spin — 'Broadcaster's cursed right there, man.'","tags":["stony-benfield","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2540,"title":"Dixon slams the wall during Crank It Up","summary":"Mid-crank-it-up segment, contact between the Kleins and Cowan sends Cowan into the wall and Jack Dixon slams it really hard with nowhere to go. The caution lands on the stage lap and ends Stage 2.","tags":["jack-dixon","greg-cline","chris-klein"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2660,"title":"McAdam steals Stage 2 under caution","summary":"The untimely caution freezes the field on the stage lap and John McAdam is declared the Stage 2 winner amid genuine confusion in the chat — race control has to notify him he's won and pull him off the track.","tags":["john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3043,"title":"Three-wide goes wrong on the restart","summary":"A big wreck erupts from a three-wide squeeze: Kyle Vaught gets collected while Jack Dixon gas-brakes his way out of the wall in a miracle save the booth credits to pure talent.","tags":["kyle-vaught","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3174,"title":"McAdam vanishes right after transferring","summary":"John McAdam drops from the server due to upload packet loss — the booth notes it was very fortunate he had already won his stage and punched his All-Star ticket.","tags":["john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3545,"title":"Greg Klein rolls the dice from second","summary":"Running second late in the final stage, Greg Klein ducks onto pit road for fresh tires — a gamble even the booth wouldn't have made, and one that leaves him outside the transfer spots when the wrecks start flying.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3890,"title":"Four-truck pileup at the back","summary":"A huge crash at the back of the field piles up Mayberry, Greg Klein, Dion Jones, and Anthony Williams as tempers flare in the fight for the final transfer spots.","tags":["dave-mayberry","greg-cline","dion-jones","anthony-williams"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4237,"title":"Final-laps carnage with transfer spots on the line","summary":"Restart with three to go: Bittner is nearly turned and hits Osborne, Kyle Vaught gets spun out, and the wrecking keeps going — the booth warns the seventh transfer spot will need a tape review.","tags":["josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4325,"title":"Adamson wins it on 70-lap-old tires","summary":"The checkered flag flies and Mike Adamson wins the qualifier having never pitted after the stage-two mix-up — 70 laps on his tires, the next closest at 43 — pure track position mastery in the 88 Phoenix Racing truck.","tags":["mike-adamson","jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":723,"quote":"Once you get to that third stage and you're still racing, you pucker up quite a bit.","context":"Ricky on qualifier nerves, having run the open qualifier himself","gold":3},{"t":1878,"quote":"Adamson's a shark in infested waters and he is all over McAdam's rear bumper.","context":"Adamson hunting McAdam for the Stage 2 lead","gold":4},{"t":2345,"quote":"Broadcaster's cursed right there, man.","context":"Benfield spins out of third seconds after his booth shout-out","gold":4},{"t":2791,"quote":"It's Katie bar the door time right now.","context":"Half the field on mixed pit strategy fighting for the top seven","gold":3},{"t":2958,"quote":"You honestly look like an NHRA funny car taking off on all those starts. You were smoking them.","context":"Ricky to Stage 2 winner John McAdam about his monster restart launches","gold":4},{"t":3018,"quote":"Now Greg Klein goes from the outhouse to the penthouse.","context":"Klein's repaired Hudson Hornet cycles to the front row after his wreck","gold":4},{"t":3939,"quote":"Tempers will flare in the all-star qualifier. No points, just pride, and they are running out of time.","context":"Calling the four-truck backfield pileup with transfer spots on the line","gold":4},{"t":4737,"quote":"Remember, racing fast and living free is the American way. Good night, VRL.","context":"The signature VRN sign-off closing the broadcast","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Results read as unofficial/provisional: the booth said the final seven transfer spots (especially P7) go to race-admin tape review after late-restart contact, with McAdam and Player shown 19th/absent because they had already transferred via stage wins. Track garbled by captions as 'North Milsboro/Wilsboro' = North Wilkesboro. Broadcasters identified only by first names (Allan and Ricky). Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: Bitner (Bner/Vitner/Fitner), Vaught (Vot/Vaude/Vault), Cowan (Cawan/Cawin/Cton/Coffin), Everidge (Average/Ever), and Chris Klene vs Greg Klein — the booth called them 'the Klein duo,' so both were normalized to Klein. Albert Anderson appears only in a VRN promo and Adamson's thank-yous, not as a competitor tonight. A 'Chris Bond' mentioned via chat as a hoped-for transfer matches no grid name and may be a caption garble.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bhsCIYgYLP4":{"recap":"This second Kentucky upload resumes at lap 96 after technical problems, with Albert Anderson leading a race that had stayed green apart from the earlier opening-lap caution. Anderson stopped early for his final fuel and tires, while Tim Pope, Alan Vaught, Eric Klafka, Jonathan Osborne, and others tried to stretch stints begun around laps 87–90 to the finish. Pope ultimately pitted with 14 laps left, handing Vaught a huge lead; Vaught lifted to roughly 75–80 percent throttle while watching Pope close rapidly on fresher tires and negotiating lapped traffic. Vaught stretched the fuel three laps beyond the expected window and won his first race of the season over Pope, while Anderson held off Jim Ott to complete the podium.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":46,"title":"The broadcast returns with Anderson leading","summary":"After the stream outage, coverage resumes on lap 96 with Anderson ahead of Kilgore and Vaught; Pope is passing Vaught for third, while Airson must serve a pit-road black flag and McCabe has been disqualified on incident points.","tags":["albert-anderson","russ-kilgore","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jason-airson","chad-mccabe"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":"resumption"},{"t":363,"title":"Anderson commits to the early final stop","summary":"Anderson gives up the lead and pits rather than wait for a caution, choosing fresh tires and a guaranteed fuel window while Pope cycles to first.","tags":["albert-anderson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":579,"title":"Ott moves into the top three","summary":"Kilgore begins an extreme conservation run after charging from the rear, and Ott passes him for third as the late fuel strategies begin to diverge.","tags":["jim-ott","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":642,"title":"The final green-flag stops begin","summary":"With fewer than 20 laps remaining, Chandler Paul and Kilgore pit, while Anderson's fresh-tire pace starts cutting into the drivers attempting to stretch their fuel.","tags":["chandler-paul","russ-kilgore","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":819,"title":"Pope pits and hands Vaught the lead","summary":"Pope makes his last stop with 14 laps left and rejoins just behind Anderson after a seven-second service, leaving Vaught, Klafka, and Osborne to gamble on their older fuel runs.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","jess-vaught","eric-klafka","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":1021,"title":"Klafka abandons the fuel gamble","summary":"Klafka pits from second with roughly nine laps remaining, leaving Vaught with an 11-second lead and making Pope the primary pursuer once the cycle completes.","tags":["eric-klafka","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1056,"title":"Osborne makes the last late stop","summary":"Osborne calls his pit entry and gives up his place among the fuel gamblers; Airson meanwhile uses fresh tires to record the race's fastest lap.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jason-airson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1158,"title":"Vaught lifts to stretch the final tank","summary":"Engine note and RPM show Vaught is not running full throttle as he attempts to save approximately three laps of fuel while monitoring Pope's rapidly shrinking deficit.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1205,"title":"Traffic delays Pope's last charge","summary":"Pope arrives behind the No. 57 with a huge run and nowhere to go, losing crucial time in lapped traffic as Vaught continues conserving at the front.","tags":["timothy-pope","russ-endicott","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"traffic"},{"t":1294,"title":"Vaught makes the fuel last","summary":"Vaught coasts through the final lap without sputtering and takes his first win of the season; Pope finishes second, and Anderson holds off a charging Ott for third.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","jim-ott"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":1441,"title":"Anderson explains the podium undercut","summary":"Anderson says he deliberately got off-cycle, hit every pit mark, and used the alternate strategy to lead many laps before securing third.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"interview"},{"t":1960,"title":"Vaught reveals the full recovery","summary":"The winner explains that his lap-one self-spin required a fast repair, he sped entering the pits, served a 40-second penalty, accidentally used a tire set, and still recovered by saving fuel from lap 90.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"interview"}],"soundbytes":[{"t":125,"quote":"Look at Russ Kilgore. We've talked about him before, the damn race man, up 25.","context":"The booth marvels at Kilgore's latest charge from the rear","gold":5},{"t":594,"quote":"That's the cool part about left turns only, right? There's a lot more involved than just the left turns: fuel saving, tire saving, all that stuff.","context":"The booth explains the strategy underneath an oval race","gold":4},{"t":1158,"quote":"Jess Vaught is not full throttle going down these straightaways. He is trying to save essentially three laps of fuel.","context":"The broadcast identifies Vaught's race-winning conservation effort","gold":5},{"t":1486,"quote":"He did a really good job with fuel management, but we really thought he was going to run out.","context":"Albert Anderson reflects on Vaught's improbable fuel stretch","gold":5},{"t":1896,"quote":"I was literally running one-fourth, half throttle for like 40 laps. It was brutal. I ran out right at the line.","context":"Austin Paul describes completing the same long fuel stint","gold":5},{"t":1971,"quote":"Crew chief told me, 'Just don't worry about it. I got what I needed in the frame, and you just keep going.'","context":"Vaught jokes about hidden fuel before explaining the legal strategy","gold":5},{"t":2110,"quote":"I heard that he pitted, and I was like, 'You've got to be kidding me.' I was one lap to the good at that point, so I pretty much knew I had it.","context":"Vaught explains when the fuel gamble became the winning play","gold":5},{"t":2155,"quote":"That first early caution really messed me up. I sped going into the pits, had a 40-second penalty, and didn't turn my tires off, so I zapped a set of tires.","context":"Vaught details how far he had to recover before winning","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 3 Kentucky race, cataloged by seasons_map.json as the Part 2 upload associated with Round 3. This video begins at lap 96 after a broadcast outage and contains the finish and interviews rather than the original green flag; the companion MyNjUALJs4g upload contains the starting grid and opening portion. The full race was scheduled for 133 laps at Kentucky Speedway in Xfinity cars with 70% fuel, four total tire sets, one fast repair, and disqualification at 13 incident points. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Vaught-Pope-Anderson podium and reads the finishing order; the 29-driver participant list is reconciled against the complete grid in the companion tape because the results narration skips directly from Robert Jordan in 25th to Russ Endicott in 26th/27th amid a verbal stumble. Vaught's own interview confirms that he caused the opening-lap caution, used his fast repair, received a 40-second speeding penalty, and then won by stretching the lap-90 tank. Canonical roster spellings are used for Alan Vaught, Jason Airson, David Feit, Tony Polk, Mike Everedge, and Russ Endicott. All timestamps fall within the 2,724-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bkgZhYkx-qM":{"recap":"Tim Pope dominated the caution-free Indianapolis 200, using clean air and disciplined tire management to win after starting from pole. The 80-lap Xfinity race was decided across three green-flag pit cycles, with Jim Ott repeatedly short-pitting to erase Pope's multi-second advantage and briefly cycle ahead. Pope's seven-lap tire advantage in the final stint proved decisive: he drove around Ott on the outside with 14 laps remaining and pulled nearly ten seconds clear. Ott held second, Alan Vaught completed another podium, and debutant Greg Klein finished fourth ahead of Jeremiah Burke. After the leaders had finished, a hard battle among Dion Jones, Austin Paul and Chandler Paul ended in a frontstretch crash that also caught Pope's already-winning car but did not affect the result.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jim Ott","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1153,"title":"Pope spins on his first qualifying attempt","summary":"Cold tires send Tim Pope around exiting turn four, but he keeps the car away from the pit wall and prepares for one final lap.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1303,"title":"Pope rebounds to take pole","summary":"On his last qualifying attempt, Pope recovers from the spin and jumps to the top of the board ahead of Jim Ott.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"qualifying"},{"t":1743,"title":"Pope clears the field at the start","summary":"Pope controls the launch from the proper right-side pole position and leads Ott as the field settles into a cautious single-file opening run.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2082,"title":"Vaught works past Ott for second","summary":"Alan Vaught completes a difficult pass on Ott, but the side-by-side battle lets Pope extend his advantage at the front.","tags":["jess-vaught","jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2142,"title":"Burke scrapes the outside wall","summary":"Jeremiah Burke catches the wall between turns one and two, buckling the hood and forcing him to manage a loose, damaged car until service.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":2790,"title":"First green-flag pit cycle begins","summary":"Mike Adamson and Dave Mayberry are among the first drivers to pit; moments later Jason Airson spins across pit lane but gets moving before the leaders arrive.","tags":["mike-adamson","dave-mayberry","jason-airson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3690,"title":"Vaught and Burke both tag the wall","summary":"Vaught lightly scrubs the wall while defending a podium position, then Burke hits it much harder and loses the ground he had made on fresher tires.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3911,"title":"Second pit sequence starts near halfway","summary":"Albert Anderson and Mayberry begin the next cycle before the leaders follow; Ott's earlier stop puts him ahead temporarily, but Pope closes rapidly on fresher tires.","tags":["albert-anderson","dave-mayberry","jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4520,"title":"Pope catches Ott after the second cycle","summary":"Pope erases Ott's undercut advantage and closes to the 205's bumper in the battle for the lead, restoring his control of the race.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5117,"title":"Final money stops begin","summary":"With fewer than 20 laps left, Kilgore, Airson and Ott pit early while Pope stretches the stint, creating another tire-offset showdown.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jason-airson","jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":5502,"title":"Pope completes the decisive outside pass","summary":"With 14 laps remaining and tires seven laps newer, Pope runs around Ott on the outside despite being pinched near the wall and retakes the lead for good.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6212,"title":"Pope wins the Indianapolis 200","summary":"Pope takes the checkered flag nearly ten seconds ahead of Ott, with Vaught third; behind them Burke tags the wall while chasing fourth-place Klein.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott","jess-vaught","greg-cline","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6462,"quote":"I basically lost that race whenever I got sideways. That's whenever Tim got away from us.","context":"Alan Vaught identifies the mistake that cost him touch with the leaders","gold":4},{"t":6617,"quote":"Tires were bigger than I thought they'd be. I was just trying to bide my time that first run.","context":"Jim Ott explains the importance of tire management","gold":4},{"t":6629,"quote":"I tried to undercut Tim a couple times because he had a four-second gap on me, so I had to try some different things to get track position.","context":"Ott describes the strategy that repeatedly put him back in the lead fight","gold":5},{"t":6767,"quote":"I was deciding not to wreck Greg at the last minute. I had to move.","context":"Jeremiah Burke explains his wall contact while chasing Klein at the finish","gold":4},{"t":6777,"quote":"As soon as you were up under somebody, you couldn't pass them anymore. The aero was so bad tonight.","context":"Burke describes the severe loss of front grip in traffic","gold":5},{"t":6844,"quote":"Everybody's best track is Michigan, so it's going to be a battle. I don't know what to expect.","context":"Burke previews the following week's race","gold":3},{"t":7012,"quote":"Yeah, I just broke the draft and pulled away.","context":"Tim Pope succinctly explains his dominant Indianapolis pace","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"This Indianapolis broadcast is absent from seasons_map.json, so no season or round is asserted. The event used NASCAR Xfinity cars for 80 laps and 200 miles and ran entirely caution-free. The explicit final rundown confirms Pope, Ott and Vaught as the podium and classifies 21 entrants, although the random-draw setup counted 18 active finishers; Ricky Whittenburg connected but did not take a competitive lap, Tony Polk disconnected, and David Feit spent an extended period in the pits. Greg Klein finished fourth in his first official points start, and Jeremiah Burke was fifth and won the random $5 draw. Adam Strom was named fan of the race. The roster's canonical spellings Jason Airson and Tony Polk are used despite the broadcast repeatedly saying Jason Harrison and Tony Pope. The post-checkered collision among Dion Jones, Austin Paul and Chandler Paul also struck Pope's car after he had already won, so it is described only in the recap and notes rather than as a result-changing moment.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bNHYbeX0ETo":{"recap":"John Osborne survived being wrecked twice and falling to roughly 28th on multiple occasions before winning a green-white-checkered finish at Gateway in the second race of the Season 8 playoffs. Polesitter Dustyn Eaton was the class of the early race, but missing the first pit entrance as a caution appeared dropped him to 18th or 19th, and later contact forced another recovery through the field. Thirteen cautions consumed roughly 50 laps as the new truck handling package repeatedly caught drivers out, turning the 120-lap cutoff race into a war of attrition. Josh Bittner led late, but lost momentum on the final restart, allowing Osborne to pull clear and hold off Eaton, with Albert Anderson third.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Dustyn Eaton","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":1438,"title":"Eaton leads a frantic start","summary":"Dustyn Eaton launches from pole and clears Trevor Robertson while Alan Vaught saves an early slide amid three- and four-wide traffic.","tags":["dustin-eaton","trevor-robertson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1538,"title":"New package sparks the first pileup","summary":"Jeremiah Burke loses the rear in Turns 1 and 2, touches Josh Bittner, and a chain reaction scatters Andrew Player, Tim Pope, Greg Klein, Dave Mayberry and Jacob Young through the grass.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","andrew-player","timothy-pope","greg-cline","dave-mayberry","jacob-young"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2668,"title":"The first green-flag stops begin","summary":"Andrew Player and Bittner open the first pit cycle as the field weighs a roughly two-second tire falloff against the unusual Gateway pit entrance.","tags":["andrew-player","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2969,"title":"Caution catches Eaton at pit entry","summary":"Kyle Vaught and Jacob Young collide to bring out the second yellow just as leader Eaton approaches pit road; Eaton misses the first entrance and falls deep into the order.","tags":["kyle-vaught","jacob-young","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":3554,"title":"Gallagher and Coffin trigger caution three","summary":"John Gallagher and Andrew Coffin run out of room side by side in Turns 1 and 2, sending Gallagher around after a netcode-assisted touch.","tags":["john-gallagher","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3998,"title":"Frontstretch crash erupts at halfway","summary":"Austin Paul snaps loose in the narrow frontstretch corridor and contact compounds behind him, collecting Jack Dixon, Eaton, Ricky Whittenburg, Craig Goodenough, Coffin and Kelly Kuehl.","tags":["austin-paul","jack-dixon","dustin-eaton","ricky-whittenburg","craig-goodenough","andrew-cauthan","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4383,"title":"Eaton is swept into another melee","summary":"Gallagher spins across the track and catches Eaton during a larger midrace incident; Eaton uses his fast repair after having already climbed back toward the front.","tags":["john-gallagher","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5378,"title":"Chandler Paul crash reshuffles strategy","summary":"Chandler Paul is caught by a closing Tim Pope after traffic checks up, while Robertson and Burke also collide in the grass; leaders pit with about 33 laps remaining.","tags":["chandler-paul","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7059,"title":"Dickerson spins from the lead battle","summary":"Larry Dickerson and Bittner converge in Turns 1 and 2, sending Dickerson around in front of Anderson and Eaton as the caution count continues to climb.","tags":["larry-dickerson","josh-bittner","albert-anderson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7373,"title":"Bittner controls the late restart","summary":"On the restart with nine laps scheduled, Bittner clears teammate Pope while Osborne takes advantage of the outside lane to move into contention.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7461,"title":"Caution 13 forces overtime","summary":"John Curtis comes down in staggered three-wide traffic and spins while avoiding Kelly Kuehl; Kevin Hunt has nowhere to go, forcing a green-white-checkered finish.","tags":["john-curtis","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","kevin-hunt"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":7851,"title":"Osborne wins the green-white-checkered","summary":"Osborne and Bittner launch side by side, but Bittner loses momentum in Turns 1 and 2; Osborne blocks Eaton's final charge and wins, with Anderson third.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7855,"quote":"Does the 14 have a drag race left in him? He does not. Jonathan Osborne wins here at Gateway.","context":"The booth calls Osborne's overtime victory over Eaton","gold":5},{"t":7994,"quote":"We'll call it the Osborne, or the Chachi lap.","context":"The booth names Osborne's reverse-gear victory lap after the winner","gold":4},{"t":8234,"quote":"That was a tough race, man. That was absolutely brutal.","context":"Albert Anderson describes the attrition after finishing third","gold":4},{"t":8509,"quote":"Thirteen cautions doesn't help anything, man. If those would have went a couple laps further, I definitely think I could have pulled out that win.","context":"Runner-up Dustyn Eaton reflects on losing his early advantage","gold":5},{"t":8530,"quote":"I actually finished with 16 out of 17 incident points and was just hoping I got to finish.","context":"Eaton explains why he could not press Osborne harder at the end","gold":4},{"t":8725,"quote":"I don't know how I pulled that one out. I was wrecked twice pretty ugly and in the back of the field, like 28th, two or three times.","context":"John Osborne reacts to his unlikely comeback win","gold":5},{"t":8792,"quote":"I feel like it was just survival, and Bittner just gave it to me on the golden platter when he gave me the outside there.","context":"Osborne explains the decisive final restart","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The broadcast explicitly reports 13 cautions and roughly 50 laps under yellow. Eaton clarifies in his interview that his first pit-cycle setback was not a penalty: he missed the first pit entrance while watching a truck outside and had to use the second entrance. The final order is complete for all 31 starters. Zachary Henin and Edson Ochoa use roster canonicals despite frequent caption distortions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bPprZ2VTYCM":{"recap":"VRL kicked off Season 6 with a 113-lap slugfest at Nashville Super Speedway, 34 trucks strong under the lights on the tire-eating concrete. Polesitter Jack Dixon led early before Mike Adamson's 88 slipped by, but the night belonged to attrition — caution after caution, several blamed by the booth on iRacing netcode, chewed up the field while Alan Vaught charged 15 spots to take Stage 1 and Dave Mayberry wrecked twice on his way to finishing dead last. Up front, rookie Dillon Bryant gambled on 43-lap-old tires with two fresh sets still sitting in his pit and held off Sean McDonnell's final-lap push to win in his very first VRL start. Josh Buettner completed the podium and vented afterward about the night's lack of respect, while John Gallagher's 20-spot climb to 11th made him the race's biggest mover.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Sean McDonnell","Josh Buettner"],"moments":[{"t":1345,"title":"Season 6 goes green at Nashville","summary":"Jack Dixon and Tim Pope bring the 34-truck field down to the first green flag of Season 6 at Nashville Super Speedway.","tags":["jack-dixon","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1583,"title":"Adamson takes the point","summary":"The Silent Assassin Mike Adamson slips the 88 around polesitter Jack Dixon as tire wear starts biting the leaders early.","tags":["mike-adamson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1795,"title":"Netcode Big One ends the honeymoon","summary":"First caution of the season after 16 clean laps: Rincon goes around mid-pack and the pileup collects McDonnell, Anderson, Everage, Coffin and Chandler Paul — the booth pins it on netcode.","tags":["george-rincon","shawn-mcdonald","albert-anderson","mike-everage","andrew-cauthan","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1942,"title":"The infield cage match proposal","summary":"The booth designs a Hunger Games-style infield cage match for wrecked drivers — pile of weapons in the middle, fights during pace laps — and Turner admits he thought Hunger Games was a video game.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2864,"title":"Kyle Vaught: 'He can still ground me'","summary":"Rookie Kyle Vaught, 32, on racing his dad Jess: he kept the pass clean because dad can still ground him — but the real season goal is beating Mayberry.","tags":["kyle-vaught","jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3326,"title":"Alan Vaught steals Stage 1","summary":"Fresh tires off the lap-40 caution launch Alan Vaught 15 spots to the front and he takes the Stage 1 win, while Andrew Coffin nips the stage's 10th spot by about a tenth.","tags":["jess-vaught","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3834,"title":"Cold tires bite on the halfway restart","summary":"Alan Vaught slips on cold tires on the restart and the checkup snowballs — netcode whips Earl Evans' 13 around, collecting Ricky Whittenburg and Kyle Vaught, with Jorge Rincon taking heavy damage.","tags":["jess-vaught","earl-evans","ricky-whittenburg","kyle-vaught","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4255,"title":"Hard check, mid-pack mayhem","summary":"A hard check snowballs into stacked crashes down the track — Burke, Shipman and Austin Paul go around, Osborne can't miss the 58, and Jack Dixon gets bumped by Gallagher's 123.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","robert-chipman","austin-paul","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4614,"title":"The broadcaster's curse strikes Mayberry","summary":"Seconds after the booth praises his late-season form, Dave Mayberry is spun by the 99 and slams the wall driver's-side first — 'Dave, you can put that one on me there, buddy.'","tags":["dave-mayberry","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5001,"title":"Mayberry's fender flies off","summary":"Chandler Paul goes sideways, Dickerson collects Alan Vaught, Whittenburg saves his truck 'from annihilation,' and Mayberry rides the grass into the inside wall so hard a panel rips off to expose an open wheel.","tags":["dave-mayberry","chandler-paul","larry-dickerson","jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5362,"title":"Four wide does not work","summary":"Late-race aggression fans the field out four wide — Jeremiah Burke saves a wild moment but David Kelly isn't so lucky, and the booth rules nobody took a mathematics class before this race.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","david-kelly"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6514,"title":"Bryant wins his VRL debut","summary":"On 43-lap-old tires with two fresh sets still in the pit, rookie Dillon Bryant absorbs Sean McDonnell's full push-mode charge over the last two laps and wins the Season 6 opener in his very first VRL start.","tags":["dylan-bryant","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1974,"quote":"It's like Hunger Games — there's a pile of weapons in the middle and they both run to it and choose a weapon, an ax handle or tire tool or crowbar.","context":"the booth pitches an infield cage match for wrecked drivers during cautions","gold":4},{"t":2191,"quote":"It was sad. Rest in peace, beardo.","context":"Earl Evans' work forced him to shave his big old beard","gold":3},{"t":3666,"quote":"What is Russ doing? Russ is doing Russ things.","context":"Russ Endicott stays out on worn tires at halfway to lead a lap","gold":4},{"t":3962,"quote":"I have to start calling that the diaper cam — you probably should have one on there, the Huggies cam.","context":"Jack Dixon's new under-truck camera survives a close miss with the wall","gold":3},{"t":4637,"quote":"Dave, you can put that one on me there, buddy — I was starting to talk about you. Curse of the broadcaster.","context":"Mayberry gets spun into the wall the moment the booth praises him","gold":4},{"t":5078,"quote":"I didn't know a panel could break off like that and leave a pretty open wheel — well, at least he doesn't have to worry about suspension travel anymore.","context":"Mayberry's fender rips clean off after his ride through the grass","gold":4},{"t":5398,"quote":"Four wide does not work... They didn't take a mathematics class before they started this race.","context":"a four-wide gamble late in the race collects David Kelly","gold":3},{"t":6535,"quote":"Will he get a run off the corner to maybe try to make it a drag race across the line? It will not come in time — the eight of Dylan Bryant picks up the race win!","context":"the winning call as Bryant holds off McDonnell at the line","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Names inferred from heavily garbled auto-captions: the Vaught family is captioned as fought/bought/Fox/Von/Vaughn; Ricky Whittenburg captioned 'Wittenberg'; Josh Buettner as 'Bittner'; Braden Laster as Brighton/Brayton/'great Laster'; Jorge Rincon as 'reconcho'/'Georgia and Cohn'. Best-guess spellings flagged: David Feit #1 (captioned 'David fight'), Dustyn Eaton #14 (booth says 'Dustin with a Y'), Dustin Riehle (captioned 'Dustin really' — Team Tang driver on summer break, did not race tonight). Guest broadcaster Greg Klein is a VRL driver (Vigilante Force) who sat out this race; sign-off garbles him as 'Craig Klein' and the lead announcer as 'Alex Brown' (Alan Brown elsewhere). Race details: 113 laps, single stage break at lap 57, 34 trucks, Nashville Super Speedway (concrete, 1.33 mi). Full top 10: 1 Bryant, 2 McDonnell, 3 Buettner, 4 Pope, 5 J. Vaught, 6 Osborne, 7 Anderson, 8 Dickerson (+19), 9 Eaton, 10 Player; Gallagher 11th as biggest mover (+20); Mayberry finished last (34th). League run by Jess and Lori Vaught; Lori Vaught handled race control. Booth attributed several wrecks to iRacing 'netcode'. Sean McDonnell said he was 'three laps down at one point' before finishing 2nd — as heard on tape, likely aided by cautions. Sponsored by Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry, Tucson AZ realtor).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bxVJfUR2B2U":{"recap":"The 2026 VRL Premiere Series All-Star Race put 24 trucks on virtual Dover for 150 laps in 50/40/60-lap stages, with race admin Lori promising shenanigans at every break — first marching P16-P23 past the field to the front, then handing the entire stage-two top eight an EOL for the 60-lap finale. Pole-sitter Tim Pope froze out before the first restart, the field's two Canadians Sean McDonnell and Jack Dixon wrecked each other in the opening laps, and Chris Goans controlled most of stage one. Trevor Robertson stole stage two by ripping the outside 'Cory Day line' from deep in the field to the lead — only to be sent to shotgun on the field by Lori's EOL call. He charged forward anyway, retook the lead with 15 to go, and held off Jacob Alesia and Craig Goodenough for the win while late leader Dustin Wade's night ended in heartbreak after contact with Jack Dixon. Robertson turned the fastest lap of the race on older tires in the closing laps, sealing the All-Star trophy and the cash payout that came with it.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Jacob Alesia","Craig Goodenough"],"moments":[{"t":1292,"title":"Green flag on the 2026 All-Star Race","summary":"24 trucks take the green for 150 laps at virtual Dover — 45% fuel, four extra tire sets, two fast repairs, and Lori's shenanigans looming at every stage break. Pole-sitter Tim Pope jumps out front.","tags":["timothy-pope","shawn-mcdonald","jack-dixon","chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1356,"title":"Maple syrup violence on lap two","summary":"The field's only two Canadians find each other in the first incident — McDonnell spins, Dixon lands in his lap and hits the inside wall, and both burn a fast repair before lap five.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1526,"title":"Pole-sitter Pope freezes out","summary":"Tim Pope's screen freezes under the early caution and the pole-sitter vanishes from the running order — out of the race before the first restart, handing control to Chris Goans.","tags":["timothy-pope","chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2095,"title":"Wade turned at the line, nearly airborne","summary":"A side-draft gone wrong spins Dustin Wade crossing the stripe — he almost flips, then nurses a minute-plus of damage on pit lane to bank both fast repairs for later.","tags":["dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2970,"title":"Shenanigan No. 1: the field flip","summary":"At the stage-one break Lori orders P16-P23 to drive past everybody to the front — Adamson and Wade suddenly head the All-Star field while the stage-one contenders stare at their tailgates.","tags":["mike-adamson","dustin-wade","jonathan-osborne","scott-milner","george-rincon","albert-anderson","jack-dixon","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3812,"title":"Teammates tangle: Bryant turns Anderson","summary":"Three-deep traffic bites on lap 75 when Dillon Bryant misjudges the gap and spins teammate Albert Anderson, who was already hanging on with wheel damage — Anderson burns a fast repair and vows he's not out of it.","tags":["albert-anderson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4302,"title":"Robertson shot out of a cannon","summary":"On four fresh tires Trevor Robertson rips the outside 'Cory Day line', taking three spots in half a lap to steal the lead right before the stage-two break.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4489,"title":"Shenanigan No. 2: top eight to the back","summary":"Lori EOLs the entire stage-two top eight — stage winner Robertson goes from the point to shotgun on the field with 60 laps left, 'from the winner circle to the outhouse' in the booth's words.","tags":["trevor-robertson","john-mcadam","jacob-alicia","chris-goans","craig-goodenough","jesse-redding","mike-adamson","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5538,"title":"Wade to the point","summary":"On four freshies Dustin Wade runs down Jack Dixon and takes the lead — the early-wreck survivor is suddenly the feel-good story with Amanda Wade sweating every lap in chat.","tags":["dustin-wade","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6215,"title":"Reading's sacrifice on the backstretch","summary":"With 19 to go Jesse Reading loses it off turn two and deliberately steers the wreck away from the pack, giving up his own night — 'gentleman and a scholar behind the wheel'.","tags":["jesse-redding"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6808,"title":"Heartbreak for the 68","summary":"Hunting the 31 with about five to go, Wade slips off the corner, he and Dixon touch twice, and both contenders' nights unravel — Wade tumbles to 21st after leading late.","tags":["dustin-wade","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7090,"title":"From the back to the trophy","summary":"Robertson takes the white flag clear of Alesia and Goodenough and completes the comeback from Lori's EOL penalty, winning the 2026 All-Star Race at Dover with the fastest lap of the night on older tires.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jacob-alicia","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1360,"quote":"A little maple syrup violence.","context":"The field's only two Canadians, McDonnell and Dixon, wreck each other on lap two","gold":5},{"t":2077,"quote":"It's not the broadcasters curse here. It's the commenter's curse.","context":"Every driver shouted out in the live chat immediately wrecked","gold":3},{"t":4313,"quote":"The six machine is coming, folks. Trevor Robertson has been shot out of a cannon.","context":"Robertson ripping the top line from deep in the field to the lead late in stage two","gold":4},{"t":4707,"quote":"Mr. Trevor Robertson now went from the winner circle to the outhouse and he's got to pass all these guys if he wants to win this race here tonight.","context":"Lori's EOL shenanigan sent the stage-two winner to last for the finale","gold":4},{"t":5252,"quote":"Hold my beer and watch this Allan.","context":"Dustyn Eaton signing off his mid-race interview after a wild save off turn two","gold":4},{"t":6272,"quote":"Gentleman and a scholar behind the wheel, Jesse Reading.","context":"Reading steered his wrecking truck away from the pack with 19 to go","gold":3},{"t":7393,"quote":"So, I think the fastest guy won tonight.","context":"Runner-up Jacob Alesia conceding after both he and Robertson set fastest laps at the finish","gold":3},{"t":7744,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, above all else, stay vigilant, and we'll see you next time.","context":"Alan's signature VRN sign-off closing the All-Star broadcast","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and podium clearly stated on air with full results readout. Caption surnames are rough: 'Chris Gomes' splits roughly evenly between Gomes/Gones (could be Goans); third place alternates Craig/Greg Goodenough — interviews and his DSR teammates say Craig; the #12 Hooters driver is garbled across Shaer/Shaneocker/John Schoenbachler/Shane Buckler, best guess Schanbacher; #75 is called both Stony and Don/Donnie Benfield; Jesse Reading may be spelled Redding; Jacob Alesia may be spelled Alesia; Jorge Rincon appears as Rencon/Ranc/Rinkcon. Play-by-play self-identifies as 'Alan VA' (surname unclear in captions). Dave Mayberry, Andy Player, and Greg Dobson are league members interviewed but not in tonight's field; Cory Day is referenced only as namesake of the high 'Cory Day line'. Car numbers heard on tape: 6 Robertson, 31 Alesia, 89 Goodenough, 1 Gomes, 92 Klein, 023 Rooney, 99 Anderson, 21 Reading, 12 Schanbacher, 47 McAdam, 51 Bryant, 14 Eaton, 75 Benfield, 19 Milner, 88 Adamson, 81 Osborne, 68 Wade, 22 Warren, 434 Hunt, 48 Dixon, 23 McDonnell, 7 Pope (implied). On-air results positions 16-23 slightly garbled; sequence inferred as Adamson 16th, Osborne 17th, Wade 18th, Warren 19th, Rincon 20th, Hunt 21st, Dixon 22nd, McDonnell 23rd, Pope 24th.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"bZbu5pFPASs":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant survived a 15-caution Richmond race and controlled the sole green-white-checkered restart to claim his second Premiere Series win of Season 12. Bryant led early but carried roughly 25 seconds of damage after an old-tire restart stack-up, then needed a wave-around and carefully chosen lanes to recover from around 10th place. A lap-113 caution during green-flag stops flipped the field toward Chris Goans and other drivers who had run long, while repeated late yellows helped Josh Bittner charge back on fresher tires after an initially poor fuel-only call. Kelly Kuehl's spin with two laps remaining forced overtime; Bryant backed the field down, Bittner passed Goans for second, and Bryant held the gap to the checkered flag.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Josh Bittner","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":1142,"title":"Welch leads the field to green","summary":"Pole sitter Derek Welch starts alongside Jason Gaines, but third-place starter Dillon Bryant immediately applies pressure at the front of the 32-truck field.","tags":["derek-welch","jason-gaines","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1189,"title":"Player's race ends on lap three","summary":"Andrew Player breaks loose off turn two and is struck by teammate Dustyn Eaton while trying to save it; the engine damage ends Player's night and brings out the first caution.","tags":["andrew-player","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1427,"title":"Bryant takes command","summary":"Bryant clears Welch shortly after the restart and establishes himself as the early leader before the second yellow for Dion Jones.","tags":["dylan-bryant","derek-welch","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1804,"title":"Coffin spin triggers a multi-truck crash","summary":"Andrew Coffin loses control in traffic after contact while Tim Pope is trying to move low, collecting Albert Anderson, Scott Rooney, Anthony Williams, Stoney Benfield and others.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","scott-rooney","anthony-williams","stony-benfield"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2749,"title":"Gaines spins beneath old-tire traffic","summary":"On a restart led by Dave Mayberry on older tires, Jason Gaines spins from the very bottom while three wide; he avoids damage but causes the fifth caution.","tags":["jason-gaines","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4402,"title":"Perfectly timed yellow flips the field","summary":"A caution for John McAdam arrives during the long green-flag pit cycle, rewarding Chris Goans and the handful of drivers who stayed out while many earlier leaders need a wave-around.","tags":["john-mcadam","chris-goans","george-rincon","dave-mayberry","scott-milner","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4719,"title":"Mayberry spins on the restart","summary":"Mayberry loops the truck on cold tires while running near the front, producing the eighth caution and extending a night increasingly dominated by short runs.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5684,"title":"Milner incident opens the strategy window","summary":"Contact from Kevin Hunt turns Scott Milner and brings out another yellow with roughly 40 laps left; Bittner briefly tries track position before returning for four tires.","tags":["scott-milner","kevin-hunt","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5892,"title":"Restart contact catches McAdam and Pope","summary":"Dustyn Eaton tags John McAdam's left rear as the field accelerates, while Tim Pope spins and clips Eaton after the caution is already appearing.","tags":["dustin-eaton","john-mcadam","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6571,"title":"Wade's spin becomes caution thirteen","summary":"Dustin Wade goes around with about 20 laps remaining, further helping Bittner advance on tires that are fresher than those of the leaders.","tags":["dustin-wade","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6880,"title":"Benfield's spin bunches the contenders","summary":"Stoney Benfield spins off the corner with 10 laps left, moving Bittner directly behind leader Bryant and setting up another short sprint.","tags":["stony-benfield","josh-bittner","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7123,"title":"Kuehl forces overtime; Bryant seals it","summary":"Kelly Kuehl spins with two laps left for the 15th caution. Bryant controls the green-white-checkered restart, Bittner slides past Goans for second, and Bryant maintains enough of a gap to win.","tags":["kelly-keel","dylan-bryant","josh-bittner","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1303,"quote":"It sucks. I'm done. The engine's blown.","context":"Andrew Player reacts after his lap-three crash","gold":4},{"t":7586,"quote":"It actually was relatively uneventful for me, thank goodness.","context":"Chris Goans contrasts his own race with the many cautions around him","gold":3},{"t":7608,"quote":"The next stop about 15, 20 laps later, I came in and got some tires, worked my way back up through the field.","context":"Goans explains recovering after missing his pit box","gold":4},{"t":7662,"quote":"Hit me with the slide job. It wasn't quite clear, but it was clean. I mean, it was coming to the white, so that's hard racing there.","context":"Goans describes Bittner's last-lap pass for second","gold":5},{"t":7783,"quote":"I thought I botched that strategy horrible.","context":"Josh Bittner reflects on taking fuel only before recovering to second","gold":4},{"t":7991,"quote":"I started off with a fast truck, but when Mayberry and somebody else stayed out on old tires, he kind of checked up really early.","context":"Dillon Bryant explains the stack-up that damaged his winning truck","gold":4},{"t":8069,"quote":"I got a system that I go by, and I'm not going to share it because I don't want people to use it.","context":"Bryant keeps the secret of his slow restart approach","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The broadcast explicitly numbers Dustin Wade's late spin as caution 13; subsequent yellows for Stoney Benfield and Kelly Kuehl make 15 total. The full 32-driver starting grid is explicit, but no complete official finishing order is read; only the podium is treated as certain. Craig Goodenough is discussed as the points leader but did not start. Caption distortions are normalized conservatively, including Chris Goans, John Schoenbachler, Jorge Rincon and Andrew Coffin.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"BzplVdpNCBQ":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League's Last Chance Qualifier at Michigan gave eight non-winners two 20-lap truck segments to claw into the All-Star Race, with two transfer spots per segment plus a fan vote. Albert Anderson tangled with Kelly Kuehl twice but raced his way back to win segment one, while John Herzig stole the second spot with a last-lap charge. Segment two flipped on its head when Dustin Riehle ran out of fuel from the lead with five laps to go, and last-lap contact between Josh Oxendine and Dave Mayberry let Kelly Kuehl take the checkered with Rob Green grabbing the final position. In a post-race twist, race control revealed Kuehl already held a provisional — putting both Green and Mayberry through — and the fan vote ended in a dead tie between Riehle and Oxendine, settled by a live on-stream coin flip that sent Riehle to the All-Star Race.","winner":"Kelly Kuehl","podium":["Kelly Kuehl","Rob Green"],"moments":[{"t":1210,"title":"Hot Rod's Apron Rodeo","summary":"On the opening laps Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry shoots down through the apron and somehow gathers up the save, drawing a 'good gracious almighty' from the booth.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1420,"title":"First Big One: Anderson and Kuehl Tangle","summary":"Three-wide racing brings out caution number one — Anderson spins after contact with Kuehl, who apologizes on the radio, and Mayberry's engine takes damage.","tags":["albert-anderson","kelly-keel","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1838,"title":"Round Two: Anderson and Kuehl Collide Again","summary":"The same two trucks get together again on the backstretch with Herzig collected in the mess; Kuehl limps back to the pits with a blown engine while Herzig radios 'my bad, guys.'","tags":["albert-anderson","kelly-keel","john-herzig"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2062,"title":"Segment-One Restart Chaos","summary":"On the lap-16 restart Dion Jones slaps the outside wall, then Anderson drifts up out of the low line and sends Oxendine into the fence.","tags":["dion-jones","albert-anderson","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2225,"title":"Herzig Steals Segment One at the Wire","summary":"On the stage's white-flag lap Riehle gets loose into the wall battling Kuehl, and John Herzig comes across 'with a head of steam' to grab the second transfer spot behind segment winner Albert Anderson.","tags":["albert-anderson","john-herzig","dustin-reilly","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":2471,"title":"America's Driver Hits the Booth","summary":"Fresh off surviving two wrecks to win segment one, Anderson joins the broadcast, thanks his Limitless Esports teammates, and promises 'hopefully I'll be talking to you tonight from the podium.'","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2855,"title":"Oxendine and Mayberry Mow the Infield","summary":"Battling in turns three and four, both trucks go spinning down through the infield to bring out the yellow — exactly the caution Rob Green needed to close back up.","tags":["josh-oxendine","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3045,"title":"Head-On Heartache for Dion Jones","summary":"Jones slides off the restart and hits a dented section of wall nearly head-on, killing his motor; moments later Green gets loose on cold tires and tangles with Kuehl for another yellow.","tags":["dion-jones","rob-green","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3450,"title":"Riehle Runs Dry From the Lead","summary":"Leading segment two with five laps to go, Riehle suddenly rolls down pit road out of fuel — the booth hands the 37 'the golden gas can award' in absolute heartbreak.","tags":["dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3587,"title":"Last-Lap Mayhem Hands Green the Spot","summary":"Kuehl gets tight off turn two on the final lap, Mayberry and Oxendine collide fighting for the last transfer position and both go for a ride, and Rob Green sails past the mess to take second at the flag behind Kuehl.","tags":["kelly-keel","dave-mayberry","josh-oxendine","rob-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3712,"title":"A Coin Flip Decides the All-Star Field","summary":"Race control's Jess reveals Kuehl already held a provisional — promoting Mayberry through alongside Green — and the fan vote deadlocks between Riehle and Oxendine, so the final All-Star spot is settled by a live on-stream coin flip: heads, and Dustin Riehle is in.","tags":["dustin-reilly","josh-oxendine","kelly-keel","dave-mayberry","rob-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1216,"quote":"Able to hang on to it — good gracious almighty, that was a great save.","context":"Hot Rod Mayberry's wild save through the apron early in segment one","gold":3},{"t":1271,"quote":"That is a problem — you just tried to take out America's driver. He's coming for you, man.","context":"Early contact shuffles Albert Anderson back through the field","gold":4},{"t":1493,"quote":"Just re-rack them and stack them and let it rip.","context":"Caution resets the field for a ten-lap sprint to end segment one","gold":3},{"t":1526,"quote":"You might be bull crapping us — we have to use the googler on that one.","context":"A fan in chat claims 'Oxendine' is Greek for winter","gold":3},{"t":1581,"quote":"English, are you broadcasting live from a renaissance fair down there or something?","context":"Mystery music bleeding into Allen English's mic during a caution","gold":4},{"t":3478,"quote":"The golden gas can award goes to the 37 tonight.","context":"Dustin Riehle runs out of fuel while leading with five laps to go","gold":5},{"t":3512,"quote":"You could vote for him to get in regardless — maybe he'll put fuel in the next race.","context":"The booth roasting Riehle's fuel gaffe while fan voting is still open","gold":4},{"t":3631,"quote":"The checkered flag has waved, so the votes are all locked in — sometimes it pays to be lucky.","context":"Rob Green inherits the final transfer spot after the last-lap crash","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"This was the Last Chance Qualifier before the All-Star Race, not a points race: 'winner' = Kelly Kuehl, who took the final checkered flag in segment two; Albert Anderson won segment one. Third at the final flag was never stated (Oxendine and Mayberry crashed on the last lap), so podium lists only the top two. 'Dustin Really' is the caption spelling throughout — proper surname (Riehle/Rielly/Realey) is a best guess and unconfirmed. The play-by-play host's name is unclear; captions address someone as 'brian'/'brown', and the channel is 'mdot'. Race control staff named on air: Jess and 'Lori Bart' (caption spelling, unconfirmed). Mike Davis, Jeremiah Burke, Mike Adamson, Dale Adamson, and Alvarez are league drivers mentioned only in passing, not in this race. The first ~11.5 minutes of the tape are pre-show music with garbled auto-captions. All timestamps are seconds into the broadcast.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"BzxsrUu6JME":{"recap":"Dustin Riehle led a Vigilante Force charge at the newly reconfigured Atlanta, winning a green-white-checkered finish over polesitter Dustyn Eaton with teammate Alan Vaught third. Riehle took command early with Kelly Kuehl helping organize the draft, while repeated cautions and a lap-50 competition break repeatedly reshuffled a 31-truck field on the narrow, tire-sensitive superspeedway layout. Several late pileups reduced the field and forced overtime, but the leaders completed the final lap cleanly with Riehle's inside line just strong enough to deny Eaton. Vaught climbed from an end-of-line penalty to third, Kuehl finished fourth, and J.R. Hollingsworth completed the top five.","winner":"Dustin Riehle","podium":["Dustin Riehle","Dustyn Eaton","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":815,"title":"Eaton leads the Atlanta launch","summary":"Dustyn Eaton starts from pole and clears the field with Kelly Kuehl outside, but Riehle quickly uses the draft to move into control.","tags":["dustin-eaton","kelly-keel","dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1097,"title":"Hollingsworth and Chandler Paul bring the first yellow","summary":"J.R. Hollingsworth dips below the red-and-white line and rejoins into Chandler Paul, triggering the first caution without major damage to either truck.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":1583,"title":"Baker spin starts the caution cycle","summary":"Daniel Baker is bumped into the outside wall and spins across traffic, collecting Robert Chipman and others as the worn tires begin to destabilize the pack.","tags":["daniel-baker","robert-chipman"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1903,"title":"Endicott turns across Kelly","summary":"Russ Endicott comes down across David Kelly after a late inside call, bounces off the wall and produces another quick caution.","tags":["russ-endicott","david-kelly"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2345,"title":"Osborne is squeezed into the wall","summary":"Three-wide traffic in the quad-oval sends John Osborne into the outside wall and Michael Everage, with Greg Dobson unable to avoid the damaged trucks.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","mike-everage","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2961,"title":"Big wreck becomes the stage break","summary":"Dale Adamson and J.R. Hollingsworth are caught in a tumbling multi-truck accident just before halfway, and race control counts the resulting caution as the scheduled lap-50 break.","tags":["dale-adamson","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3213,"title":"Dixon and Anderson lead stage two","summary":"Jack Dixon and Albert Anderson stay out or take minimal service and restart at the front as the second half begins.","tags":["jack-dixon","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4547,"title":"Quad-oval pileup strikes again","summary":"A truck gets loose near the outside wall and the crash cascades through Dave Mayberry, Timmy Bates, Anderson, John Gallagher, Dale Adamson, Chandler Paul and Endicott.","tags":["dave-mayberry","timmy-bates","albert-anderson","john-gallagher","dale-adamson","chandler-paul","russ-endicott"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4780,"title":"Vigilante Force locks down the front","summary":"With 15 laps left, Riehle leads Vaught and Kuehl in a three-truck inside-line formation while Eaton works the outside with Hollingsworth.","tags":["dustin-reilly","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5361,"title":"Two-to-go wreck forces overtime","summary":"A push from Baker unsettles Andrew Coffin and sparks a large Turns 1 and 2 crash that heavily damages Dixon and Jeremiah Burke, forcing the lone green-white-checkered attempt.","tags":["daniel-baker","andrew-cauthan","jack-dixon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5700,"title":"Riehle holds off Eaton in overtime","summary":"Eaton launches well outside but lacks an immediate pusher; Riehle's line holds through the white flag and he wins the clean final lap, with Vaught third.","tags":["dustin-reilly","dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5700,"quote":"It won't be enough for the 14. The 37 of Dustin Reilly takes home the win, with the 33 of Vaught there in third.","context":"The booth calls Riehle's overtime victory over Eaton","gold":5},{"t":5875,"quote":"It was good racing at the front. I know there were a couple incidents at the back, but good teamwork at the front.","context":"Alan Vaught reflects on Vigilante Force's podium-heavy finish","gold":4},{"t":6166,"quote":"What really set it up for me was that last caution. I barely beat out Jess for second, which got me the outside.","context":"Dustyn Eaton explains how he earned his overtime front-row position","gold":4},{"t":6325,"quote":"I need this bad juju to go away. This is two weeks in a row. This is painful.","context":"Chandler Paul reacts to another incident-filled race","gold":4},{"t":6663,"quote":"That was fun racing right there. Good teammates, good strategy. That was fun.","context":"Winner Dustin Riehle summarizes the race","gold":5},{"t":6790,"quote":"Once you got 30 or 40 laps on your tires, at the end it would try to step out on you a little bit.","context":"Riehle explains why Atlanta required more driving than a conventional plate track","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete 31-driver finishing order is read after the interviews and is used for the drivers array. Dustin Riehle is the roster canonical for the repeatedly captioned 'Dustin Really'; The broadcast does not state a definitive caution total, so the recap describes the repeated yellows without assigning a number. Race control folded the large pre-halfway crash into the scheduled competition caution rather than running a separate lap-50 yellow.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"c2MMei5_EQE":{"recap":"The Mountain Shine 285 became a full-field Bristol survival test almost immediately. Birthday driver John McAdam launched from pole, but Jacob Alesia spun without contact while fighting near the front, brushed the inside wall, and dropped behind all 30 rivals. Fourteen cautions and a limit of four tire sets made recovery as much about tire timing as speed. Albert Anderson's early spin collected Gordon Spain, Craig Goodenough, and Mike Adamson; a later hornet's-nest checkup tangled Andrew Coffin, Kyle Vaught, Sean McDonnell, and John Schoenbachler; then the night's Big One swept up much of the field. Greg Dobson briefly looked poised to steal the lead with a perfect restart before officials penalized the jump, and Schoenbachler used an 11-lap tire advantage to drive past Dustin Wade. Alesia nevertheless worked all the way back into control. Tim Pope's spin from second damaged his tire position, but Scott Milner's late caution erased Alesia's advantage over Andy Player and forced one final two-lap dash. Alesia nailed the restart and took the white before another yellow could freeze the story, completing the back-to-front comeback over Dillon Bryant and Player.","winner":"Jacob Alesia","podium":["Jacob Alesia","Dillon Bryant","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":832,"title":"McAdam launches from pole","summary":"Birthday driver John McAdam gets the jump from pole as Tim Pope and Jacob Alesia battle for second.","tags":["john-mcadam","timothy-pope","jacob-alicia"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":864,"title":"Alesia spins on cold tires","summary":"Alesia loses the rear without contact while fighting near the front, lightly scrapes the inside wall, and falls behind all 30 rivals.","tags":["jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1176,"title":"Anderson spin triggers a multi-truck pileup","summary":"Albert Anderson snaps loose high, collecting Gordon Spain, Craig Goodenough, and Mike Adamson in the second early caution.","tags":["albert-anderson","gordon-spain","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2337,"title":"Fifth caution erupts in a hornet's nest","summary":"Andrew Coffin tries to fill a closing hole beside Kyle Vaught, while a separate check-up tangles Sean McDonnell and John Schoenbachler.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","kyle-vaught","shawn-mcdonald","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2772,"title":"Big One tears up the Bristol field","summary":"A stack-up beginning with Jorge Rincon and Sean McDonnell collects Scott Rooney, Dustyn Eaton, Greg Klein, Jonathan Osborne, John Gallagher, and several others.","tags":["george-rincon","shawn-mcdonald","scott-rooney","dustin-eaton","greg-cline","jonathan-osborne","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5084,"title":"Dobson's perfect launch becomes a penalty","summary":"Greg Dobson anticipates John Schoenbachler's restart so well that officials penalize him, taking away a brief run at the lead.","tags":["greg-dobson","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":6029,"title":"Schoenbachler takes the lead on fresh tires","summary":"John Schoenbachler drives around Dustin Wade with an 11-lap tire advantage and assumes control with about 45 laps remaining.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","dustin-wade","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6376,"title":"Pope spins from second","summary":"Pope loses the rear exiting Turn 4 while chasing Alesia, stays on the lead lap but badly hurts his tire position for the finish.","tags":["timothy-pope","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":6909,"title":"Milner caution sets up a two-lap dash","summary":"Greg Klein and Scott Milner misjudge their overlap, turning Milner into the wall and erasing Alesia's late advantage over Player.","tags":["greg-cline","scott-milner","jacob-alicia","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7129,"title":"Alesia completes the comeback","summary":"Alesia controls the last restart and takes the white before another caution can appear, winning over Bryant and Player.","tags":["jacob-alicia","dylan-bryant","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":984,"quote":"Bristol isn't just a racetrack. It's a pressure cooker.","context":"The booth frames the 285-lap short-track challenge.","gold":2},{"t":2806,"quote":"Man, there's a lot of trucks tore up.","context":"Reaction to the largest early pileup.","gold":5},{"t":6310,"quote":"Come out in 30th. Look at me now, 17th, baby.","context":"Kyle Vaught celebrates salvaging positions after seven minutes of repairs.","gold":5},{"t":7132,"quote":"Congratulations, Jacob, Dylan, Andrew on your podium. Well done.","context":"The immediate post-finish call.","gold":5},{"t":7234,"quote":"Bristol didn't let us down.","context":"Alesia describes betting on the late caution that enabled his winning strategy.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The finish call, interviews, and final results explicitly confirm Alesia, Bryant, and Player. The race had 14 cautions. 'Donald Donald' in the results is treated as caption corruption for Sean McDonnell, who was repeatedly identified in the race. The Interstate Batteries No. 12 is mapped to roster canonical John Schoenbachler despite highly variable captions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ca9_Gmsx9Lw":{"recap":"VRL's 200-lap Monster Mile race at Dover combined an abrasive concrete surface, 60% fuel tanks, six tire sets, and a strict 13-incident-point disqualification limit. Pole-sitter Tim Pope gave way early to John Ellis, and a succession of green-flag pit cycles, four natural cautions, and a scheduled competition yellow kept reshuffling the field while only seven trucks ultimately remained on the lead lap. Josh Bittner dominated a late stint by as much as half a lap but stopped for enough fuel, handing the lead to drivers trying to stretch their tanks from laps 153-154. Dale Adamson finally had to pit, Ricky Whittenburg ran dry in Turn 3 on the last lap, and Pope swept past to win on fumes over Jorge Rincon and Whittenburg.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jorge Rincon","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":956,"title":"Pope leads the field to green","summary":"Tim Pope starts from pole alongside John Ellis as 28 trucks begin 200 laps on Dover's hot concrete.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-ellis"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1110,"title":"Ellis takes the lead on the outside","summary":"Ellis carries momentum around Pope to take first, while Kelly Kuehl follows into second and Dale Adamson moves to third.","tags":["john-ellis","timothy-pope","kelly-keel","dale-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2237,"title":"Snyder rolls onto his roof","summary":"A slow Jeff Snyder is struck by the fast-closing Jeffrey Green and flips on the frontstretch, with John Herzig, Austin Paul, and Justin French also involved in the first caution.","tags":["jeff-snyder","jeffrey-green","john-herzig","austin-paul","justin-french"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3068,"title":"Pope and Chandler Paul collide","summary":"Pope and Chandler Paul converge on the same frontstretch lane, sending Pope into a crash while Kilgore and Riehle make sharp evasive moves.","tags":["timothy-pope","chandler-paul","russ-kilgore","dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3356,"title":"Adamson and Dixon lead a fierce middle stint","summary":"After the caution, Dale Adamson, Jack Dixon, and Eric Klafka trade pressure at the front as the outside wall repeatedly threatens their runs.","tags":["dale-adamson","jack-dixon","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3897,"title":"The competition caution resets Dover","summary":"The scheduled yellow flies just past halfway with Adamson leading, prompting the lead-lap field to take service together.","tags":["dale-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4469,"title":"Bittner and Osborne crash amid a netcode debate","summary":"Bittner drifts toward Osborne, apparent netcode launches the No. 84 toward a rollover, and the frontstretch crash brings out another yellow.","tags":["josh-bittner","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5353,"title":"Pope drills Mayberry after a no-yellow incident","summary":"After Rincon and Adamson make hard contact without a caution, Pope closes much faster than Mayberry and hits him from behind, dropping Mayberry laps down again.","tags":["george-rincon","dale-adamson","timothy-pope","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5456,"title":"Herzig rear-ends Riehle in a multi-truck pileup","summary":"John Herzig hits the slowing Dustin Riehle near the apron and a large crash also catches Ottinger, Green, and Snyder; Herzig later reaches the incident limit.","tags":["john-herzig","dustin-reilly","jeff-ottinger","jeffrey-green","jeff-snyder"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5855,"title":"Bittner builds a half-lap lead","summary":"A favorable restart and fresh tires let Bittner pull as much as 12 seconds clear, but his fuel calculation forces him to pit from first near lap 178.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6646,"title":"Adamson's fuel gamble ends","summary":"Dale Adamson retakes the lead from Justin French but finally dives to pit road with five laps left, leaving Whittenburg, Pope, and Rincon to test their fuel reserves.","tags":["dale-adamson","justin-french","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6853,"title":"Pope wins as Whittenburg runs dry","summary":"Pope passes the slowing Whittenburg with two laps left, takes the white flag with just enough fuel, and wins over Rincon while Whittenburg coasts home third after running dry in Turn 3.","tags":["timothy-pope","george-rincon","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":633,"quote":"Put on your best dancing shoes and find your rhythm.","context":"The broadcast's key to racing Dover's abrasive concrete","gold":3},{"t":2325,"quote":"Maybe he picked the lesser of two evils and went low. Still caused major contact, major incident.","context":"The booth reviews Snyder's attempt to move out of the leaders' path","gold":4},{"t":3091,"quote":"Both trucks just kind of meeting together there... they were trying to park it in the same spot.","context":"The booth describes the Pope-Chandler Paul crash","gold":3},{"t":4576,"quote":"Dip, dodge, and dive!","context":"The call as Whittenburg, Austin Paul, and Rincon escape the Bittner-Osborne wreck","gold":4},{"t":6834,"quote":"Did Pope have enough fuel?","context":"The central question as the white flag flies","gold":4},{"t":6864,"quote":"Timothy Pope, saving for centuries here all race long... will come across the line with the win.","context":"The fuel-mileage winning call","gold":5},{"t":7035,"quote":"I would sell my soul to Satan right now for an extra half a lap of gas.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg recalls running dry in Turn 3 on the last lap","gold":5},{"t":7368,"quote":"I ran out across the finish line, so I guess I didn't save a little too much. I saved right on.","context":"Runner-up Jorge Rincon explains how precise his fuel saving was","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"This 2022 Dover broadcast is absent from seasons_map.json, so no season or round is asserted. The finish call, interviews, and full results explicitly confirm Pope, Rincon, and Whittenburg as the podium. John Herzig was explicitly identified as the only driver disqualified for incident points. The booth counted five cautions total: four natural incident yellows plus the scheduled competition caution. Caption wording around some middle-race incidents is garbled; summaries preserve only the clearly stated participants and sequence. Transcript timestamps end at 2:17:30 (8250 seconds), within the 8262-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"CjISxgcM6yU":{"recap":"A full 43-truck field took on 100 laps under the lights at Charlotte, and the league's 13-incident-point disqualification limit turned the Charlotte 150 into a pure survival race. Mike Adamson won Stage 1 in the 751 but was later collected while spinning in front of the entire field in one of several massive pileups, and polesitter Tim Pope took Stage 2. Roughly fourteen trucks were DQ'd on incident points — including Todd Smith, disqualified scraping the wall as he crossed the line in a podium spot. Jonathan Osborne, in his first race back after a hard-drive failure, squeezed past Tim Pope on the one-attempt green-white-checkered to take the win, with Austin Paul sneaking through the mayhem for second and Trevor Robertson inheriting third. Robert Jordan claimed the random-draw money with an 11th-place finish.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Austin Paul","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1984,"title":"Evans clips Godsoe for the first caution","summary":"Earl Evans snags Gary Godsoe's quarter panel and sends the 50 around; a quick caution lets Godsoe save it with no damage done.","tags":["earl-evans","gary-godso"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2560,"title":"Burke noses the inside wall under yellow","summary":"Jeremiah Burke brake-checks trying to avoid a truck under caution, spins, and hits the inside wall, crunching his nose after a huge charge through the field.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2824,"title":"Front-stretch pileup — the first Big One","summary":"Sobanovski bounces off another truck on the front stretch, Ricky Whittenburg goes for a wild backwards ride, Austin Paul gets airborne, and Charlie Harkus tumbles; Dave Mayberry and Albert Anderson III become the night's first incident-limit DQs.","tags":["mike-sobanovski","ricky-whittenburg","austin-paul","charlie-herkis","dustin-eaton","jonathan-wiley"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3178,"title":"Adamson spins the whole field into chaos","summary":"Stage 1 winner Mike Adamson spins like a top in front of the entire field off turn four; six trucks come out with meatball flags and Jack Dixon is among those snagged in the carnage.","tags":["mike-adamson","jack-dixon","trevor-robertson","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3573,"title":"Three-wide gamble wrecks the restart","summary":"Three-wide into turns one and two goes wrong on the restart — contact triggers another pileup, and Austin Reeves and Josh Oxendine are both DQ'd on incident points.","tags":["chris-zofeld","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","austin-paul","todd-smith","austin-reeves","josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4101,"title":"Kuehl and Dixon tangle, Dion Jones goes tumbling","summary":"Kelly Kuehl and Jack Dixon fight for the same piece of track, the 123 gets netcoded into the 48, and Dion Jones takes the short end with a wild tumble that forces a tow.","tags":["kelly-keel","jack-dixon","john-gallagher","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4873,"title":"Cody Tarrant's save of the day","summary":"Clipped by Jack Dixon, Cody Tarrant goes about 36 degrees sideways on the apron and gathers it all back up — the booth calls it the save of the day.","tags":["cody-tarrant","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5437,"title":"Wittenberg in the wall, radio fury at the 99","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg hits the wall and collects Dustyn Eaton's 14; angry drivers call out the 99 on the radio, and Chris Zofeld ends up with the DQ boot.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","dustin-eaton","chris-zofeld"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5726,"title":"Booth preps weapons for pit-road fights","summary":"After Albert Anderson warns there will be fights after this race, pit reporter Adam Turner jokes he keeps a couple of bottles at the bottom of the cooler so he can bust one on the wall and have two weapons ready.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5804,"title":"Osborne launches on the final-11 restart","summary":"Jonathan Osborne rockets away from John Gallagher on the restart with 11 laps to go, taking control of the race up front.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5984,"title":"Endicott flips in the closing-lap melee","summary":"Russ Endicott goes upside down and flipping in a late-race wreck; the aftermath DQs keep coming as Dustyn Eaton, Jeremiah Burke, and Cody Sanderson all hit the incident limit.","tags":["russ-endicott","jeremiah-burke","david-kelly","dustin-eaton","cody-sanderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6397,"title":"GWC finish: Osborne wins as Smith gets DQ'd at the line","summary":"On the one-attempt green-white-checkered, Osborne pushes Tim Pope up toward the wall off turn four to seal the win while a big wreck erupts in the midfield; Todd Smith scrapes the wall for his final incident point and is DQ'd crossing the line, handing Austin Paul second and Trevor Robertson the podium.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope","todd-smith","austin-paul","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1740,"quote":"I bet you Josh Oxendine is wearing a helmet while racing this. He probably had to put his crayons down.","context":"the booth reads a fan's YouTube jab at Josh Oxendine during early green-flag racing","gold":4},{"t":2173,"quote":"It's a chess game and we're sending checkers over here.","context":"the booth puzzles over drivers pitting just before the stage caution","gold":3},{"t":3550,"quote":"Once when Pope sniffs that lead, man, he really never lets it go.","context":"Tim Pope grabs the lead on a restart","gold":3},{"t":4583,"quote":"Todd Smith is ripping it like he stole the damn thing in a Hot Wheels truck.","context":"Todd Smith charges aggressively from 31st trying to get his lap back","gold":4},{"t":5782,"quote":"You gotta have a little bit of anger. We can make up tomorrow, but we're enemies today.","context":"the booth on tempers flaring during the caution-filled night","gold":3},{"t":6049,"quote":"DQ should have been the sponsor of this race... that's damn Dairy Queen.","context":"yet another driver hits the disqualification limit in the closing laps","gold":5},{"t":6571,"quote":"I don't know what the hell I saw. It was mayhem — people were disappearing like the Invisible Man out there.","context":"the booth tries to sort out the finishing order after the chaotic final lap","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble several names: #37 'Dustin really' (rendered here as Dustin Riehle, uncertain), #1 'John fate or fight' / 'David fight' (uncertain), Charlie Harkus vs Harkins, Chris Zofeld vs Scofield, and Mike Sobanovski all have unclear spellings. Roughly 14 drivers were DQ'd under the 13-incident-point limit; final order was taken from official iRacing scoring as read on the broadcast, with Todd Smith's post-finish DQ dropping him from a podium spot to 17th. Sam Beamer (#22) and Greg Klein were league drivers mentioned as absent tonight; Jonah Long entered but never gridded due to PC failure. Race: Charlotte 150, NASCAR Trucks, 100 laps, stage breaks at laps 30 and 60, decided on a one-attempt green-white-checkered. Broadcast also credits Adam Turner on pit road; it was play-by-play man Alan Brown's 29th birthday.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"CoTPohbxrl0":{"recap":"Season 13's Round 7, the Zero Hour 200, was actually run at Chicagoland despite the metadata and season map listing Kansas. Aaron Warren spun on cold tires before the opening lap was complete and collected Dave Mayberry, but the race then settled into long green-flag runs in which Andy Player, Trevor Robertson, Jacob Alesia, and Dillon Bryant traded the lead through pit cycles. A Jonathan Osborne spin leaving pit road brought out the only other caution at lap 94, forcing everyone to improvise a final fuel-and-tire plan. Robertson stopped early for four tires and built a three-second lead, but Alesia's later two-tire stop let him erase the gap and edge Robertson by 0.01 seconds at the stripe; Bryant finished third.","winner":"Jacob Alesia","podium":["Jacob Alesia","Trevor Robertson","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":1203,"title":"Player launches from pole","summary":"Andy Player leads Tom Barish and the 21-truck New Year's Eve field to green at Chicagoland.","tags":["andrew-player","tom-barish"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1248,"title":"Warren spins before lap one is complete","summary":"Aaron Warren loses the truck on cold tires, Dave Mayberry catches a piece of him, and both suffer costly damage with no fast repairs available.","tags":["aaron-warren","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1509,"title":"Six trucks battle under a blanket","summary":"After the restart, Player defends against Alesia, Robertson, Bryant, Anderson, and Kuehl in a tight multi-lane fight for the lead.","tags":["andrew-player","jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2273,"title":"Player starts the first green-flag pit cycle","summary":"Player pits at the end of lap 29 with Rooney, Anderson, and Schoenbachler, while Robertson and the other contenders run several laps longer.","tags":["andrew-player","scott-rooney","albert-anderson","john-schoenbachler","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2508,"title":"Player cycles out with a three-second lead","summary":"Player's early stop pays off initially as he retakes first with a large margin after the opening service sequence.","tags":["andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2874,"title":"Robertson closes onto Player","summary":"With tires three laps newer, Robertson erases Player's lead and begins a prolonged side-by-side battle for first.","tags":["trevor-robertson","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3005,"title":"Robertson clears Player for the lead","summary":"After Player clips the wall, Robertson completes the pass and takes control before the second green-flag stop cycle.","tags":["trevor-robertson","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3603,"title":"Alesia works the outside past Robertson","summary":"Alesia uses one-lap-fresher tires and the outside lane to complete a close pass on Robertson and take the lead after the next pit cycle.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3994,"title":"Bryant powers to the front","summary":"Dillon Bryant passes both Robertson and Alesia and opens a half-second lead as the long green run approaches the final planned stops.","tags":["dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4394,"title":"Osborne's pit-exit spin changes everything","summary":"Jonathan Osborne touches the white line on cold tires leaving pit road and spins, drawing the second caution at lap 94 just short of the one-stop-to-the-finish fuel window.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5414,"title":"Robertson's four-tire undercut builds a late lead","summary":"Robertson pits early for four tires and cycles roughly three seconds ahead, while Alesia later takes only two tires and begins a ten-lap chase.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5884,"title":"Alesia wins by one hundredth","summary":"Alesia reaches Robertson on the final lap, carries momentum around the outside, and wins the drag race to the stripe by 0.01 seconds; Bryant completes the podium.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1269,"quote":"Goddamn car fluorescent orange next week.","context":"Aaron Warren reacts on the radio after being hard to spot in the opening-lap crash","gold":4},{"t":3228,"quote":"I'm Nostradamus. I said if we get some green-flag running here, spread out a little bit, start having some green-flag pit stops, it might run the entire way.","context":"Alan Vaught as the field spreads around Chicagoland","gold":3},{"t":4514,"quote":"This, folks, as they say, changes everything.","context":"The booth after Osborne's lap-94 pit-exit caution resets the strategy","gold":4},{"t":5705,"quote":"I know a lot of people prefer carnage and restarts... but this is the stuff that gets me excited. Who has the best strategy?","context":"The booth watches Alesia erase Robertson's late lead","gold":4},{"t":5884,"quote":"Jacob Alicia brings it home... just edges him out by .01.","context":"The photo-finish call at Chicagoland","gold":5},{"t":6165,"quote":"It fell apart when I was in charge of my own pit strategy. So I beat myself again.","context":"Third-place Dillon Bryant critiques his final stop","gold":4},{"t":6414,"quote":"I figured my only chance was to pit earlier than them, take four, because I kind of figured Jacob would only take two. And it almost worked.","context":"Trevor Robertson explains the gamble that missed by 0.01 seconds","gold":5},{"t":6523,"quote":"It just came down to strategy and how you played your cards.","context":"Winner Jacob Alesia sums up the Zero Hour 200","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The season map identifies Season 13, Round 7 as 'Zero Hour 200' but lists Kansas; the metadata title also says Kansas. The broadcast introduction, repeated track description, and race commentary explicitly place the race at Chicagoland Speedway in Joliet, Illinois, so the recap follows the broadcast evidence and flags the metadata conflict. The podium and 0.01-second margin are explicit in the finish call, interviews, and results. Alesia's interview confirms a two-tire final stop; Robertson confirms four tires. Jack Dixon was second in points but did not appear in the 21-driver starting grid. Transcript timestamps end at 1:52:47 (6767 seconds), within the 6772-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"d9ka0bn1fNc":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant won the 225-lap North Wilkesboro race by taking control before the night became an attrition test. Craig Goodenough led from pole, but Bryant passed cleanly around lap 37 and kept returning to the front as strategy and repeated yellows cycled Jack Dixon and others through the lead. The fresh pavement made cold tires and the exit of Turn 4 especially treacherous. More than two dozen cautions left nearly every contender carrying damage, but the booth alternates between 26 and 27 in the closing interviews, so the exact official total remains unknown. Behind Bryant, Albert Anderson methodically recovered from a penalty and completed a 27-position climb to second. Chris Goans kept a battered truck alive by timing tires around the cautions and finished third. Bryant controlled the final restart and took his first victory of the young season while another incident unfolded behind him. The race was chaotic, but its central story is three different survival paths: Bryant's early control, Anderson's long recovery and Goans's damaged-truck strategy.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Albert Anderson","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":1400,"title":"Goodenough launches from pole","summary":"Craig Goodenough gets the jump at the green with Bryant quickly advancing into second as the 32-truck field starts on cold tires.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1460,"title":"The first yellow comes immediately","summary":"The opening run lasts only a few laps before the first caution, beginning a pattern of cold-tire spins and stacked restarts.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":1921,"title":"Three cautions in 18 laps","summary":"Andrew Cawthorn is right-hooked after contact in traffic, forcing much of the field to stop and marking the third yellow before lap 20.","tags":[],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2161,"title":"Dobson brings out caution four","summary":"Greg Dobson kisses the inside barrier and jumps toward pit lane, producing the fourth caution after only 29 laps.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":2514,"title":"Bryant wrestles the lead away","summary":"Bryant works past Goodenough around lap 37 in a respectful side-by-side battle and holds the point when the fifth caution follows.","tags":["dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3161,"title":"Dixon takes control through strategy","summary":"After repeated yellows and pit decisions reshuffle the order, Jack Dixon restarts from the lead with Jacob Alesia and Scott Miller behind him.","tags":["jack-dixon","jacob-alicia","scott-milner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4013,"title":"Caution count reaches double digits","summary":"Michael Everage clips the apron and becomes hooked together with Chris Goans, producing the 10th caution while Goans begins accumulating the damage he will carry to the podium.","tags":["mike-everage","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6722,"title":"Cawthorn crash makes it 21","summary":"Andrew Cawthorn loses the truck and hits the wall with Alex Anderson also involved, bringing out caution 21 as tempers and attrition intensify.","tags":["alex-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7118,"title":"Rincon and Dixon wreck racing for second","summary":"On a late restart, Jorge Rincon misjudges the braking point while racing Dixon for second and sends both trucks around, producing caution 23.","tags":["george-rincon","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7616,"title":"Anderson grabs second before the last yellow","summary":"Anderson clears Rincon with eight laps left, but another caution sets up one more restart with Bryant still controlling the inside lane.","tags":["albert-anderson","george-rincon","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7809,"title":"Bryant survives the final restart","summary":"Bryant takes the white flag and wins amid a final-lap wreck behind him; Anderson finishes second and the heavily damaged Goans secures third.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6040,"quote":"It's just going to be one of those days, boys. You have to just get through it and embrace the suck.","context":"The booth accepts the reality after 17 cautions","gold":5},{"t":7937,"quote":"The truck was unstoppable, though. It would turn, it would hug the bottom.","context":"Dillon Bryant describes the truck that carried him through the carnage","gold":5},{"t":8196,"quote":"That was a battle from start to finish—from the drop of the green flag till we got to the checkers.","context":"Albert Anderson reflects on climbing 27 positions to second","gold":4},{"t":8428,"quote":"I was just banking on some cautions, which I think we got about 30 of them. I guess I was right in that guess.","context":"Chris Goans explains the tire gamble that delivered third","gold":5},{"t":8584,"quote":"Unless you watch racing for the wrecks, then this is perfect.","context":"Goans offers a wry verdict on the broadcast replay","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The booth alternately says 26 and 27 cautions in the closing interviews; the exact official total is therefore uncertain, and the recap uses 'more than two dozen.' All 32 finishers are included from the complete final order. Timmy McAdam is treated as distinct from John McAdam because both appear separately in the same result; Timmy has no roster match. Alex Anderson and Ryan Walton also lack roster entries and retain the broadcast spellings.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"DBPyESoZ_fs":{"recap":"VRL's Season 11 All-Star Race hit the digitally restored 1987 North Wilkesboro Speedway for a 200-lap, 23-truck brawl that racked up 17 cautions. Craig Goodenough was the class of the field, taking the lead from polesitter Alan Vaught around lap 53 and stretching it to 2.6 seconds, but he and Vaught gambled by staying out through the lap-138 caution cycle — a head game Goodenough later admitted was aimed at Vaught — and it buried them in traffic. John Osborne drove up from 13th, survived early damage, and grabbed the lead in the closing laps; even after Dillon Bryant got to the front with five to go, a caution reverted scoring to the last timing loop and put the 81 back on the point. The lone green-white-checkered attempt died in a backstretch pileup, and Osborne took the All-Star win — and its $100 prize — under yellow ahead of Bryant and Goodenough.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Dillon Bryant","Craig Goodenough"],"moments":[{"t":2872,"title":"First Big One at lap 21","summary":"McAdam and Adamson come together off the bottom, triggering a chain-reaction pileup — Jeremiah Burke gets in the wreck twice and Larry Dickerson is left struggling.","tags":["john-mcadam","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3359,"title":"Restart breaks loose, three-wide pileup","summary":"Mayberry spins the tires on the restart and jacks everybody up three wide; Robertson gets in the wall trying to give room and Osborne piles in with nowhere to go.","tags":["dave-mayberry","trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3887,"title":"Goodenough to the point — lights out","summary":"Lap 53: Goodenough sticks the nose to the bottom in turn one, takes the lead from Vaught, and pulls away to a 2.6-second advantage. 'He is just lights out around this place.'","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4897,"title":"Halfway melee: Kelly drilled in the door","summary":"Bittner turns Adamson on the frontstretch, Kelly Kuehl drives up the tailgate, and then gets drilled in the driver's door by Gallagher — caution number eight, five laps shy of halfway.","tags":["josh-bittner","mike-adamson","kelly-keel","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5959,"title":"Brake check? Bad blood at Wilkesboro","summary":"Seconds after Steve praises the field settling into a rhythm, Benfield and Gallagher tangle; the booth debates a brake check — 'There wasn't [bad blood] before, there is now.'","tags":["stony-benfield","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6028,"title":"The leaders refuse to pit","summary":"Goodenough and Vaught stay out at lap 138 while the field pits, leaving the booth dumbfounded and speculating about a prop bet. Goodenough later admits he stayed out just to mess with Vaught — and it cost him the win.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6834,"title":"'Here we go, Johnny' — McAdam holds them off","summary":"John McAdam stays out on worn tires with 30 to go, nails the restart, and briefly holds the lead as the chat (including Tim McAdam) cheers him on.","tags":["john-mcadam","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7048,"title":"Three-wide for the lead with 21 to go","summary":"Osborne, Bittner and Eaton go three wide for the race lead; Osborne slams the door, Bittner pancakes the wall and somehow keeps his pace as a four-truck brawl rages for second.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton","john-mcadam","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7195,"title":"Eaton's hard hit erases the gap","summary":"16 to go: Eaton and Burke meet in the middle on the frontstretch and Eaton spins hard into the inside wall — the caution wipes out Osborne's one-second lead, 'a gift given to the 89.'","tags":["dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7565,"title":"Bryant takes the lead — the timing loop takes it back","summary":"Five to go: Osborne runs Goodenough up the track and opens the door for Bryant, who surges out front — but McAdam spins, and the caution reverts scoring to the last timing loop with the 81 as leader.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne","john-mcadam","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7738,"title":"Overtime lasts one corner — Osborne wins under yellow","summary":"The green-white-checkered attempt dies almost immediately when Adamson clips Dickerson and a backstretch pileup brings out caution number 17 — freezing the field and handing John Osborne the All-Star win.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson","larry-dickerson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7854,"title":"The backwards victory lap","summary":"Osborne celebrates in reverse, backing the truck all the way into the pits — the booth dubs it a Kyle Busch victory lap: accelerator fixed, transmission screwed.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2861,"quote":"Craig is indeed good enough.","context":"Reading stream chat as Goodenough hounded the leader","gold":3},{"t":3656,"quote":"I didn't graduate high school, Steve. I'm just throwing out terms I don't understand.","context":"Chris Goans after Steve floats 'scientific rolling resistance'","gold":4},{"t":6097,"quote":"I'm still dumbfounded here at the top two stay on the racetrack. Got to wonder if maybe they got a little prop bet going on.","context":"Goodenough and Vaught refusing to pit at lap 138","gold":3},{"t":6299,"quote":"I think Kelly is the driver's version of the broadcaster for this race. He's just cursed. I think everybody on track has hit Kelly at least once.","context":"Kelly Kuehl collected in yet another wreck","gold":4},{"t":7669,"quote":"I think he was saying, 'All right, let's go. It's shake and bake time.'","context":"Vaught bumping Goodenough before the green-white-checkered","gold":3},{"t":7762,"quote":"John Osborne will have an All-Star win in his back pocket.","context":"The winning call as the final-lap caution freezes the field","gold":4},{"t":7903,"quote":"Good news is the accelerator's fixed. The bad news is the transmission screwed.","context":"Osborne backing his truck all the way into the pits after the win","gold":4},{"t":8467,"quote":"There's no penalties tonight, Dylan. You should have dumped him.","context":"Steve ribbing runner-up Dillon Bryant for racing Osborne clean","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and full results read on air. Name normalizations are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Alan Vaught' covers VA/Vaugh/Vault/Bot/Fought/Ba variants; 'Craig Goodenough' covers Gooduff/Good Enough/Goodnov (the chat pun 'Craig is indeed good enough' supports Goodenough); 'Andrew Coffin' and results-sheet 'Andrew Cawan' (10th) appear to be the same driver; 'Chris Klein' vs 'Klene/Kline' uncertain. Play-by-play announcer identified only as Steve (Track Limits Network); color analyst Chris Goens. Terry Crouch and Derek Welch are league drivers mentioned but did not race tonight; league admins Lori and Jess mentioned in chat/interviews. Russ Kilgore did not take the green (credited 23rd). Race was posted as 160 laps but corrected on air to 200; comp caution near lap 100 required four tires. First ~30 minutes and ad breaks are caption noise ('Heat. Heat.'). Booth stated 17 cautions total. An unidentified 'Delo' was mentioned running 11th (~1:31:38). Full finishing order read at ~2:26:04: Osborne, Bryant, Goodenough, Vaught, Anderson, Klein, Cool, Whittenburg, Benfield, Coffin/Cawan, Bitner, Robertson, McAdam, Burke, Adamson, Mayberry, Dixon, Dickerson, Gaines, Eaton, Player, Gallagher, Kilgore.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"dhkgZK24_gc":{"recap":"VRL's Wednesday night visit to Bristol turned into a full-blown demolition derby, with the half-mile Last Great Coliseum producing 22-plus cautions over 284 truck laps. Alan Vaught started from the pole, but the early running belonged to Jeremiah Burke and returning ARCA driver Brayton 'Pizza Man' Laster, who led at the halfway stage break and dominated restart after restart. In the second half, birthday boy Josh Bittner surged forward, wrestled the lead away from Laster, and survived wave after wave of late wrecks — including a Big One that erupted behind him just as he took the white flag. Bittner won on his birthday, with Dustyn Eaton charging from 14th to second and Laster completing the podium in third. Broadcasters Alan Brown and Allen English filled the caution-heavy night with a running gag that missing boothmate Adam Turner had been abducted by aliens demanding the Totino's pizza roll recipe.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Dustyn Eaton","Brayton Laster"],"moments":[{"t":649,"title":"Lap-One Chaos Lights the Fuse","summary":"Contact between the 33 and the 6 off the opening green sends Kelly Kuehl spinning off the outside wall — the first of 20-plus cautions flies before lap one is done.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":763,"title":"Adam Turner Abducted by Aliens","summary":"The booth explains the missing third commentator: a glowy light over his house, alien abduction confirmed by 'experts', and the captors' sole demand — the recipe for Totino's pizza rolls. The bit runs all night.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1517,"title":"Walmart Parking Lot on the Frontstretch","summary":"The 18 clips the drifting 33 and a multi-truck jam piles up on the front stretch — the booth calls it 'a little bit of a Walmart parking lot situation'.","tags":["andrew-player","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","mike-everage","greg-cline","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2874,"title":"Pope Gets Pinballed","summary":"Tim Pope gets hooked off the 99 (net code, per the replay) and is hit by three or four different trucks in a hard shot to the outside wall — 'we're going to have to send the bambulance out for Tim'.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3150,"title":"Clean-Up on Aisle Six","summary":"Cold tires bite the 18 on the restart and six-to-eight trucks pile up on the front straightaway right as Laster rockets to the lead on fresh tires.","tags":["andrew-player","jess-vaught","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3937,"title":"Anderson Spins, Collects the 81","summary":"America's driver gets loose on the restart, jumps two and a half lanes into the 123 and triggers a big wreck that clips the 81, the 55 and the 28.","tags":["albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","ricky-whittenburg","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4050,"title":"Tim Pope's Mic-Drop Exit","summary":"After a miserable night, Pope keys up the radio — 'I already hit everybody else, I might as well have hit you too' — and immediately disconnects. The booth crowns it the longest sentence they've ever heard from him.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4223,"title":"The Six Gets Launched","summary":"Robertson wiggles on the slick spot, spins the 07, then gets launched airborne into the 01 of Kelly Kuehl — another mini parking lot forms as the booth swears there's a hidden oil well under Bristol.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jack-dixon","mike-adamson","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6113,"title":"Birthday Boy Takes the Lead","summary":"On fresh tires, Josh Bittner runs down the restart-master Laster, sticks the bottom line through three and four, and clears him for the race lead — beating the real-life ARCA driver at his own short-track game.","tags":["josh-bittner","brayton-laster"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7942,"title":"Caution 22 Busts the Table","summary":"The booth announces official caution number 22 — 'we have officially busted' — and if it's blackjack, they've lost their money. The count would be quoted at 22-23 by night's end.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":8091,"title":"The Late-Race Big One","summary":"With the laps winding down, the 55 and 69 make contact on a wet spot and a massive wreck erupts — both Good Weiser machines caught up — while Brayton Laster threads through the carnage untouched.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","larry-dickerson","george-rincon","mike-everage","jess-vaught","andrew-player","brayton-laster"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8393,"title":"Bittner Wins the Bristol Demolition Derby","summary":"A big wreck detonates behind the leader just as he crosses the line for the white — no more yellows — and Josh Bittner races it out to win at Bristol on his birthday, fireworks and all, ahead of Eaton and Laster.","tags":["josh-bittner","dustin-eaton","brayton-laster","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":90,"quote":"The gladiators of the VRL take to the Last Great Coliseum here at Bristol for 284 laps of absolute mayhem.","context":"Alan Brown's opening welcome to the broadcast","gold":3},{"t":816,"quote":"The only demand that we have received so far is they want the recipe for those pizza rolls.","context":"Explaining the aliens' terms for returning abducted boothmate Adam Turner","gold":4},{"t":3150,"quote":"Clean up on aisle six back there on the front straightaway.","context":"Calling the six-to-eight-truck restart pile-up","gold":4},{"t":4050,"quote":"I heard Tim Pope key up on the radio and say, 'Ah, I already hit everybody else, I might as well have hit you too' — and then he disconnected.","context":"Relaying Tim Pope's radio sign-off after his night of carnage","gold":5},{"t":4252,"quote":"I swear there's got to be like a hidden oil well underneath Bristol here, because these guys have been slipping and sliding all over the place tonight.","context":"After yet another truck self-spun on the mystery slick spot","gold":3},{"t":7952,"quote":"If we're playing blackjack, we're out — we lost our money.","context":"On official caution number 22 busting past 21","gold":4},{"t":8162,"quote":"Driving like somebody who's had to actually take care of equipment that's worth actual money.","context":"As real-life ARCA driver Brayton Laster weaved untouched through the late Big One","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions. 'Brayton Laster' inferred from context (real-life part-time ARCA Menards driver nicknamed 'Pizza Man', racing at Salem, Indiana the following weekend); captions render him 'Brighton lter'/'Bron lter'. 'Dustyn Eaton' inferred from the booth's recurring 'Dustin with a Y' joke — could simply be 'Dustyn Eaton'. Spellings for 'David Feit' (#1), 'Andrew Cin' (#10), and 'Jorge Rincon' (#28) are uncertain. The Vaught surname (Jess #33, Kyle #16, race control Lori) appears in captions as 'vot'/'VA'/'fought'/'vault'. Lori Vaught is race control, not a driver or broadcaster; Adam Turner is a regular broadcaster who was absent tonight (subject of the alien-abduction gag). Caution count stated variously as 22 (official) and 23 by the booth. Full finishing order was read out post-race; positions 1-10: Bitner, Eaton, Laster, Burke, Everage, Player, Osborne, Adamson, Gallagher, Dickerson.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"dJlox4KUKEA":{"recap":"Mike Adamson won the 110-lap Throwback Throwdown at Darlington after a late caution and a confusing iRacing scoring sequence overturned the long-run fuel contest. Adamson moved from the outside front row to win the first stage, repeatedly controlled restarts, and was charging on fresher tires after the final green-flag pit cycle while J.R. Hollingsworth, Tim Pope and Ricky Whittenburg tried to stretch earlier stops to the finish. Pope passed Hollingsworth late, but Chandler Paul's crash with four laps left forced the only green-white-checkered attempt; Pope then ran out of fuel as John Osborne spun and the field froze near the white flag. iRacing initially penalized Adamson for passing the pace truck and briefly scored Pope first, but league administration explicitly corrected the result to Adamson over Pope and Jeremiah Burke.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1427,"title":"McDonnell leads the throwbacks to green","summary":"Sean McDonnell starts from pole beside Mike Adamson as the 31-truck field begins 110 laps around Darlington.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2215,"title":"Early pitters are caught by the first caution","summary":"Andrew Player, Dustyn Eaton, Jonah Long and David Kelly short-pit just before contact between Jack Dixon and David Feit sends Fite spinning, leaving the early stoppers a lap down until the wave-around.","tags":["andrew-player","dustin-eaton","jonah-long","david-kelly","jack-dixon","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2783,"title":"Baker is swept into a second crash","summary":"Contact from Timmy Bates turns Daniel Baker back across the track and into Jonah Long and Andrew Player; Baker later loses the engine and tows.","tags":["timmy-bates","daniel-baker","jonah-long","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3379,"title":"Burke-Bittner crash erupts at the stage break","summary":"Jeremiah Burke scrapes the wall and rebounds into Josh Bittner, triggering two linked crashes that also catch Chandler Paul, Osborne, Mike Taylor, David Feit, Player, Bates and Albert Anderson as the scheduled halfway yellow arrives.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","chandler-paul","jonathan-osborne","mike-taylor","david-fite","andrew-player","timmy-bates","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3498,"title":"Adamson wins the first stage","summary":"The booth confirms Adamson as the halfway stage winner after the incident-filled run to lap 55.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3852,"title":"Bates and Paul collide after the break","summary":"Austin Paul catches the apron while racing Timmy Bates; the two converge and spin, with Bittner and Baker among those affected.","tags":["austin-paul","timmy-bates","josh-bittner","daniel-baker"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4258,"title":"Another Bates spin opens a strategy split","summary":"Bates goes around again with David Kelly involved. Hollingsworth, Whittenburg and Pope use the caution to pit around lap 70, setting up their attempt to reach the finish on one more stop.","tags":["timmy-bates","david-kelly","j-r-hollingsworth","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4561,"title":"Adamson controls the restart","summary":"Adamson clears Alan Vaught and returns to the preferred high lane while Dustyn Eaton briefly holds third after climbing more than 20 positions.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5108,"title":"Final stops create a fuel-versus-tires finish","summary":"The later-stopping drivers cycle through pit road while Hollingsworth and Pope inherit the top two; Adamson emerges on fresher tires but far behind the strategy leaders.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","timothy-pope","mike-adamson","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5518,"title":"Pope takes the lead from Hollingsworth","summary":"Hollingsworth brushes the wall with five laps remaining, handing Pope the lead as fuel becomes the central question.","tags":["timothy-pope","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5680,"title":"Paul's crash forces overtime","summary":"Chandler Paul hits the inside wall and returns far enough toward the racing surface to bring out a late caution. Hollingsworth and Whittenburg use their final tires, while Pope and Adamson retain track position.","tags":["chandler-paul","j-r-hollingsworth","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5997,"title":"Scoring confusion ends with Adamson the winner","summary":"Pope launches well in overtime but runs out of fuel as Osborne spins and the field freezes near the white flag. Adamson passes through the confusion, receives an automated pace-truck penalty, and is then restored to first by league administration ahead of Pope and Burke.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6396,"quote":"I'm happy with the eighth place. I'll take that—that's a win for me.","context":"Kelly Kuehl reflects on learning a difficult Darlington track","gold":3},{"t":6613,"quote":"I got wrecked there, a lap down. How does it get—I can't be happier than to finish third here.","context":"Jeremiah Burke celebrates recovering to the podium","gold":4},{"t":6623,"quote":"I wish it would have gone green. I think I got Mike. I had fresh tires on that restart.","context":"Burke explains why he believed he still had a chance to win","gold":4},{"t":6841,"quote":"Ricky Whittenburg did. He called it before the caution—said there's another caution in a few laps here.","context":"Tim Pope credits Whittenburg for the pit call that nearly won the race","gold":4},{"t":7020,"quote":"Wow, I can't even say anything right now. I'm speechless. I know that's hard to believe, but wow, that was a lot of work.","context":"Mike Adamson reacts to the corrected victory","gold":5},{"t":7030,"quote":"It timed out perfect. The pit stops, the cautions fell right where I needed to, and I just played my cards right.","context":"Adamson summarizes the strategy behind his win","gold":5},{"t":7077,"quote":"You've got to find your rhythm, get your mark, get your line. You've got to hit it constantly, repeatedly, lap after lap after lap.","context":"Adamson explains how to race Darlington","gold":5},{"t":7098,"quote":"It's a finesse track. You have to finesse the truck around; you can't just get after it and get aggressive.","context":"Adamson describes Darlington's central challenge","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete 31-driver finishing order is read after the interviews, and league administration explicitly names Mike Adamson the winner after reviewing the automated caution and pace-truck penalty. iRacing temporarily displayed Tim Pope first, so the final result depends on the stated admin correction rather than the initial sim scoring. Six trucks finished on the lead lap. The seasons map has no entry for this video, so no season or round is asserted. ","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"dO-HWaUZKXk":{"recap":"Jim Ott started the 75-lap Michigan race from pole, but Tim Pope quickly turned it into a two-car contest by taking the lead and forcing Ott to respond after an early wall brush. The race stayed green from flag to flag, placing a premium on the difficult pit entry, full four-tire stops, and timing the two green-flag cycles without losing the draft. Pope used a slightly quicker final stop and a fastest lap to pass Ott after the last cycle, while Jason Airson, Greg Klein, Russ Kilgore, and Mike Adamson fought an equally fierce battle behind the podium positions. Ott countered with five laps remaining, broke Pope's draft over the final two laps, and won at his home track ahead of Pope and Alan Vaught.","winner":"Jim Ott","podium":["Jim Ott","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1421,"title":"Ott leads the Michigan field to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Ott and Burke start side by side, with Adamson and Pope behind as the 22-car field accelerates into Turn 1.","tags":["jim-ott","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1445,"title":"Burke's cold-tire bobble costs early track position","summary":"Burke gets loose and brushes the outside wall exiting Turn 2, allowing Adamson past and beginning a long recovery from the front row.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":1699,"title":"Vaught clears Ott and targets leader Pope","summary":"Vaught carries a strong outside-line run past Ott and begins chasing Pope, who has taken control of the race's first long run.","tags":["jess-vaught","jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1856,"title":"Ott pounces when Pope touches the wall","summary":"Pope drifts too high exiting Turn 2 and clips the outside wall, creating a check-up that Ott reads immediately to retake the lead.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2390,"title":"The first green-flag pit cycle begins","summary":"Vaught, Anderson, Mayberry, Kuehl, and Dobson are among the early lap-25 takers; Kilgore follows while Pope and Ott extend their opening run.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson","dave-mayberry","kelly-keel","greg-dobson","russ-kilgore","timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2616,"title":"Adamson completes a clean first stop cycle","summary":"Adamson pits from the temporary lead to complete the main sequence, returning Ott and Pope to the front after a cycle with no speeding penalties.","tags":["mike-adamson","jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2729,"title":"Anderson's undercut gains the lead draft","summary":"Anderson's lap-25 stop jumps him into the top group behind Vaught, giving America's Driver a sustained run inside the top ten and ultimately an eighth-place finish.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3408,"title":"Ott and Pope approach the money stop together","summary":"With the second cycle nearing, Ott still leads while Pope remains in his gearbox; Vaught runs alone in third and the Airson-Klein-Kilgore-Adamson group stays tightly contested.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson","greg-cline","russ-kilgore","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3737,"title":"The leaders make their final four-tire stops","summary":"Ott, Pope, Vaught, and Airson pit together for four tires and fuel; both lead contenders hit their marks, with Pope gaining roughly two tenths in the exchange.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3915,"title":"Pope uses the fastest lap to take first","summary":"Pope closes on fresh tires, pulls alongside Ott, and trades paint in a drag race across the line before completing the pass for the lead.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4364,"title":"Ott counters with five laps remaining","summary":"Ott attacks Pope's inside lane, withstands Pope's first crossover attempt, and repeats the move a lap later as the two use the draft and aero to decide the race.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":4541,"title":"Ott wins at his home track","summary":"Ott breaks the draft over the final two laps and takes the checkered flag over Pope and Vaught; Airson passes hard charger Klein late to claim fourth.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":879,"quote":"Where you make your money is three and four.","context":"Adam Turner identifies the decisive end of Michigan's layout","gold":5},{"t":3559,"quote":"This is just going to be the war of who makes the mistake first.","context":"The booth frames the long Ott-Pope duel before the final stops","gold":5},{"t":4143,"quote":"They're having a blast passing each other, blocking each other, and pinching each other.","context":"The booth describes the tight secondary-pack battle","gold":4},{"t":4431,"quote":"This is playing chess, not checkers. These guys are trying to outthink their opponent.","context":"The booth calls the final aerodynamic duel between Ott and Pope","gold":5},{"t":4730,"quote":"Those tires were just gold. The extra few laps, as the race progressed, that gap was more pronounced.","context":"Third-place Alan Vaught explains why he committed to long fuel runs","gold":5},{"t":4934,"quote":"I knew if I could get around him, it would be my only chance to try to keep him behind me, but I came a little short.","context":"Runner-up Tim Pope reflects on the final lead fight","gold":5},{"t":5094,"quote":"I couldn't ask for a better race. Starting P1 and leading the majority of laps tonight, but what a battle with Tim.","context":"Winner Jim Ott celebrates his home-track victory","gold":5},{"t":5114,"quote":"He could have blocked me down the backstretch a couple of those runs. We crossed each other over twice, but man, what a run.","context":"Ott praises Pope's clean racing in their decisive battle","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 3, Round 9 at Michigan International Speedway according to seasons_map.json. The broadcast explains that the scheduled distance was changed to 75 laps and 150 miles; the Xfinity cars ran with 70% fuel, five total tire sets, one fast repair, and disqualification at 13 incident points. The race went green from start to finish despite the booth repeatedly predicting at least one caution. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Ott-Pope-Vaught podium and reads the complete 22-driver finishing order; Lori Vaught appeared in the automated grid display but served as race administrator in the flag stand and did not compete. Jack Dixon started from pit road because of a carryover penalty. Greg Klein advanced 14 positions to finish fifth and earn hard charger. Canonical roster spellings are used for Jim Ott, Jason Airson, Alan Vaught, David Feit, Tony Polk, and Ricky Whittenburg. All timestamps fall within the 5,830-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"DsIOT0DdUaA":{"recap":"Alan Vaught won the second playoff round at Homestead-Miami after taking control from early dominator Tim Pope in the second half. Pope started on pole and led through the first two cautions, while a succession of incidents involving Greg Klein, John McAdam, Greg Dobson, and others repeatedly arrived around the pit windows. Vaught seized the lead after the fourth caution and beat Pope off pit road during the final green-flag cycle, then chased down alternate-strategy leader Jeremiah Burke with 15 laps remaining. Pope also cleared Burke but could not close the final two-second gap, leaving Vaught, Pope, and hard charger Burke as the podium.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1886,"title":"Pope leads Homestead green","summary":"Tim Pope launches from pole, while third-starting Alan Vaught times the start well and settles into the lead battle.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":3084,"title":"First yellow interrupts green stops","summary":"Greg Klein drifts up the track into John McAdam as the first green-flag pit cycle begins, bringing out a caution near the fuel window.","tags":["greg-cline","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":3408,"title":"Fresh tires create a restart pileup","summary":"Immediately after the restart, Kevin Hunt loses control on fresh tires and clips McAdam, with Greg Dobson also swept into the second caution.","tags":["kevin-hunt","john-mcadam","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4513,"title":"Dobson and Coffin spin together","summary":"A slightly off-center push from John Osborne turns Dobson down into Andrew Coffin on the backstretch, producing synchronized spins and the third yellow.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","greg-dobson","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4918,"title":"Fourth caution erupts in a chain reaction","summary":"Contact between Jacob Young and another truck triggers a multi-truck crash that sends Young's rear into the fence and catches Andrew Coffin and Joe Canales.","tags":["jacob-young","andrew-cauthan","joe-canales"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5166,"title":"Vaught takes command on the restart","summary":"Vaught quickly takes the lead from Pope after the fourth caution and begins building a gap as clean air reverses their first-half roles.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6218,"title":"Vaught wins the final pit-road race","summary":"Vaught and Pope make their last stops together, and Vaught exits first while Burke's offset stop cycles him to the lead.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6618,"title":"Vaught retakes the lead from Burke","summary":"After erasing a three-second deficit, Vaught dives below Burke in Turn 1 and returns to the lead with 15 laps remaining.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6710,"title":"Pope takes second","summary":"Pope completes an inside pass on Burke with 12 laps to go but loses ground to Vaught while making the move.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7121,"title":"Vaught closes out Homestead","summary":"Vaught takes the checkered flag roughly two seconds ahead of Pope, while Burke holds off Albert Anderson for third after starting 25th.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6277,"quote":"It's one thing reeling him in; it's another to pass.","context":"The booth watches Vaught close on alternate-strategy leader Burke","gold":4},{"t":7530,"quote":"That one restart where I was able to get around him was probably the winning moment for me, frankly.","context":"Alan Vaught identifies the decisive pass on Pope","gold":5},{"t":7738,"quote":"If anybody's ever watched Tim Pope, you don't want him behind you. He just seems to track you down.","context":"Vaught explains the pressure of leading Pope","gold":4},{"t":7758,"quote":"Whoever gets out in front just about wins it.","context":"Pope summarizes the importance of Homestead's clean air","gold":5},{"t":7849,"quote":"I buckled down and drove up to the front a couple times. I got stuck on that first caution too, so I'm real happy I ended up with a third.","context":"Jeremiah Burke reflects on charging from 25th","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Benjamin Richards was credited 29th but explicitly did not take the green flag, so the drivers array contains the 28 actual starters. The winner is repeatedly rendered 'Alan VA/Vaude/Vault' in captions and canonicalized to Alan Vaught via the roster. Four cautions are explicitly counted; the winner interview's estimate of two was conversational and inaccurate.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"DtOzRVWVUpY":{"recap":"Jonathan Osborne won the 57-lap King of the Road playoff race after tire management and a dramatic late crash reshaped the Sonoma order. Pole-sitter Dustyn Eaton led early but consumed his rear tires, allowing Osborne and Alan Vaught to move ahead before the two green-flag pit cycles. Craig Goodenough and Vaught appeared set to decide the race until Vaught attacked the hairpin, struck the tire barrier and was overturned as Goodenough powered through the blocked corner; both had to tow. Osborne inherited a clear lead and defeated Josh Bittner by roughly three seconds, with Eaton recovering to third.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Josh Bittner","Dustyn Eaton"],"moments":[{"t":1480,"title":"Eaton and Vaught race up the hill","summary":"Dustyn Eaton and Alan Vaught run side by side through Sonoma's opening corners before Eaton clears the front row and begins building a gap.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1784,"title":"Pope spins during the opening run","summary":"Playoff contender Tim Pope goes around early but avoids a barrier and rejoins, one of several isolated errors in the caution-free race.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1893,"title":"Osborne advances to second","summary":"Vaught gets loose putting power down in the hairpin, allowing Osborne to slip by and begin chasing leader Eaton.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2867,"title":"Osborne takes the lead from Eaton","summary":"After patiently preserving his tires, Osborne dives inside the increasingly loose Eaton through turn one and completes the pass for first.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":3103,"title":"Pit-exit contact spins Osborne","summary":"Osborne cuts in before he is fully clear of Kevin Hunt and spins during the first green-flag pit cycle, handing valuable track position to Goodenough.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","kevin-hunt","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3399,"title":"Eaton returns to the lead after the cycle","summary":"Once the first stops settle, Eaton regains first over Vaught, Goodenough and Osborne despite his aggressive tire usage.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4188,"title":"Vaught finally clears Eaton","summary":"With Eaton's rear tires fading, Vaught wins a sustained battle through the hairpin and takes command near the midpoint of the race.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":4431,"title":"Eaton crashes on worn rear tires","summary":"Eaton loses control in the Esses and strikes the outside wall hard, forcing him to use his fast repair at the approaching final stop.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4744,"title":"Osborne tangles with Everage while blending","summary":"Osborne rejoins from pit road into traffic and makes side contact with Michael Everage, spinning Everage but continuing his own recovery.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":5278,"title":"Goodenough takes the late lead","summary":"Jorge Rincon ends his long final stint with 11 laps remaining, cycling Goodenough ahead of Vaught while Osborne battles Eaton behind them.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught","george-rincon","jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5600,"title":"Vaught and Goodenough crash in the hairpin","summary":"Vaught attacks inside Goodenough, hits the concrete tire barrier and overturns; Goodenough cannot stop and drives through the wreck, forcing both leaders to tow and handing Osborne first.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6198,"title":"Osborne becomes King of the Road","summary":"Osborne completes the final hairpin cleanly and wins by about three seconds over Bittner, with Eaton several seconds farther back in third.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6198,"quote":"Across that start-finish line—Osborne for the win! Chachi finds home here in California.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":2},{"t":6436,"quote":"If you make a mistake, it's over. There are no cautions, there's no second chances.","context":"Fourth-place Jorge Rincon explains the unforgiving rhythm of a caution-free road race.","gold":5},{"t":6598,"quote":"I pushed hard at the beginning and I ate up my tires trying to get that gap.","context":"Eaton identifies why his early lead became difficult to defend.","gold":5},{"t":6827,"quote":"Last I was looking, I was in eighth place, and then a bunch of people really, really sucked, and now I'm second.","context":"Bittner humorously summarizes how late attrition elevated him to the runner-up spot.","gold":5},{"t":7141,"quote":"We shifted like over 450 times tonight. It was brutal.","context":"Osborne describes the physical workload of driving the Sonoma race.","gold":5},{"t":7257,"quote":"We punched our ticket to New Hampshire, so we're just going to go ride around next week and come ready for the championship.","context":"Osborne looks ahead after securing his championship-round place.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and full results rundown explicitly confirm Osborne, Bittner and Eaton. The 57-lap event ran without any full-course cautions, and the booth reported nine trucks on the lead lap at the finish. Jeremiah Burke was hard charger at plus 13 positions. The spoken grid lists 25 starters and separately notes Sean McDonnell in the session; the results label McDonnell 27th, apparently leaving an admin/non-starter slot in the ordering. The 26 actual drivers named by the grid and results are included, while Lori Vaught is race control rather than a participant.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"E_3-wH4TvHA":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League closed out 2023 with the Wide Flipping Open 83, an 83-lap trucks slugfest at the fictional 3-mile iRacing Super Speedway where draft speeds topped 240 mph. The race lived up to its name: Kyle Vaught went for a sky-high tumble in an early multi-truck pileup, net code repeatedly bit the field — including a frontstretch wreck that collected Albert Anderson and a late Big One that spun the 37 — and Scott Martin briefly stole the show with a 46.0-flat lap at 242 mph. Fresh off a one-week \"double secret probation\" suspension, Dustyn Eaton drove the No. 14 to the win after last-lap chaos turned his pusher Alan Vaught around off the final corner. Ricky Whittenburg charged from 10th to finish second with Jeremiah Burke third, while Tim Pope took fourth and David Feit fifth. Albert Anderson, racing under the weather, rallied 23 spots to round out the top 10 as the race's hard charger.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Ricky Whittenburg","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1628,"title":"First caution: Bittner sent Loosey Goosey","summary":"A checkup reaches the midfield and a love tap to the back bumper from the 55 sends Josh Bittner screaming up the racetrack, bringing out the night's first caution just laps in.","tags":["josh-bittner","ricky-whittenburg","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2187,"title":"The IRSS flip: Kyle Vaught goes airborne","summary":"Riding onboard with Jacob Young's 17, trucks wreck right in front of him at 230 mph — Kyle Vaught gets launched into a tumbling flip above the field, hits the tire barrier, and the booth rides the roof-cam replay screaming to close your eyes. The broadcast's namesake moment.","tags":["kyle-vaught","chandler-paul","jacob-young"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2607,"title":"Goodenough's zero-altitude save","summary":"The 89 of Craig Goodenough gets loose off the inside wall and pulls it back at the last possible instant before contact — the booth marvels at the save right before he would have hit the wall.","tags":["craig-goodenough","john-curtis"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3593,"title":"Dixon threads the needle, net code claims Albert","summary":"Jack Dixon tries to squeeze through on the frontstretch near pit entry and it goes tumbling and stumbling — net code turns Albert Anderson, collecting Kyle Vaught, Greg Klein and the 63 in a pit-lane-adjacent pileup neither driver could do anything about.","tags":["jack-dixon","albert-anderson","kyle-vaught","greg-cline","edward-w-smith"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3653,"title":"Scott Martin flirts with the 45-second barrier","summary":"While the wreck settles, Scott Martin rips a 46.0-flat lap with a top speed of 242 mph — nearly breaking into the 45-second bracket on the 3-mile track.","tags":["scott-martin"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4233,"title":"Murder Death Kill machine takes the wall","summary":"The 187 of Scott Howell gets tight then loose, slaps the outside wall and comes back across the track into Sean McDonnell's 23, with the 13 and 123 tied up in the aftermath — Howell takes credit for the W on the radio.","tags":["scott-howell","shawn-mcdonald","earl-evans","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4675,"title":"Jacob Young goes for a ride","summary":"Four-wide for a split second collapses on the 17 — Scott Martin gets into Jacob Young and sends him for a ride, with the 187 and 67 tangled and Craig Goodenough limping away with a meatball flag.","tags":["jacob-young","scott-martin","scott-howell","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4827,"title":"The 67 hits the 17 twice under caution","summary":"Replays confirm Scott Martin doored Jacob Young twice under yellow — the booth calls for a wrestling ring in the infield, then rules it low-speed love taps with no sanctions since the caution was out.","tags":["scott-martin","jacob-young"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5392,"title":"Ramsey's aggression triggers it; Chandler beats the wheel","summary":"Super-aggressive Nick Ramsey and the 88 get together, Mike Adamson goes around and Chandler Paul gets tagged up in it with Player and Robertson catching secondary damage — the YouTube stream catches Chan the Man furiously beating on his steering wheel.","tags":["nick-ramsey","mike-adamson","chandler-paul","andrew-player","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5825,"title":"\"That's a big one right there boys\"","summary":"Earl Evans catches the apron and launches into Austin Paul, then the craziest net code of the year turns the 37 around through a gap you could fit a presidential motorcade through, wiping out Craig Goodenough and Mike Adamson.","tags":["earl-evans","austin-paul","dustin-reilly","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6563,"title":"Greg Klein's truck gets destroyed","summary":"With about ten to go the 43 bounces across the apron and the 92 of Greg Klein gets absolutely clobbered — \"he gone, that truck's destroyed right there boys\" — with Martin and McDonnell tangling again under the caution.","tags":["greg-cline","john-curtis","trevor-robertson","scott-martin","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7046,"title":"White-flag chaos: Eaton survives to win","summary":"All chaos breaks loose at the white flag — the 1 and 55 trade knock-heading blows, then Alan Vaught, who pushed Eaton all night, gets turned off turn four on the final lap as Dustyn Eaton crosses the line first ahead of Ricky Whittenburg and Jeremiah Burke.","tags":["dustin-eaton","ricky-whittenburg","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","david-fite","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":979,"quote":"This is one of those tracks we're kind of glad they never built, 'cause there'd be dead bodies being hauled out of here every week.","context":"Sizing up the fictional 3-mile iRacing Super Speedway before the green","gold":4},{"t":2156,"quote":"One hand on the wheel, one hand on the beer, and a pistol on your lap — you better be ready.","context":"Adam Turner comparing IRSS pack racing to I-35 traffic heading into Waco","gold":4},{"t":2211,"quote":"Not only was that fatal, but I think Jacob Young might need a new pair of pants as he was eating his fruit roll-up.","context":"Reacting to the massive flip wreck that happened right in front of Young's onboard camera","gold":5},{"t":2317,"quote":"That's the beauty of iRacing Super Speedway — you can go through all that pain without actually having any real physical pain, just some hurt feelings.","context":"After Kyle Vaught's tumbling flip and tow to the pits","gold":3},{"t":3274,"quote":"You know what she says? What she doesn't want a lot for Christmas. — Oh my god, I've got that one hook, line and sinker dude.","context":"Brown's long-con Mariah Carey lord-and-lady Christmas joke lands on the booth","gold":4},{"t":5861,"quote":"The craziest net code I've seen in quite a while — you could have fit a full presidential motorcade in through there.","context":"The 37 getting net-coded and turned through a wide-open gap in the late Big One","gold":4},{"t":6586,"quote":"He said if he didn't get turned and learned he was going to give us all discounts on a cruise. I guess it's too late.","context":"Greg Klein's truck getting destroyed with about ten laps to go","gold":3},{"t":7059,"quote":"That wasn't some right side romance, that was just some 'get off of me' knock-heading from the 1 to the 55.","context":"David Feit and Ricky Whittenburg banging doors as the white flag flies","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Name uncertainties from auto-captions: #33 'Alan Vaught' is a best guess (heard as jasvant/just vot/Jess VOD); #16 Kyle is stated to be his son. #1 'David Feit' heard only as 'David fight'. #37 'Dustin Riehle' heard as 'Dustin really' (nicknamed The Big Show killer). #10 'Andrew Cin' is garbled and could be Chin or similar. Winner's first name is spelled with a Y per the booth's running 'Dustin with a Y' gag — rendered Dustyn. Jonah Long disconnected and never gridded. League admins Jess and Lori (Lori ran race control) are thanked in interviews but are not booth broadcasters. Finish order beyond podium, per closing rundown: 4th Tim Pope, 5th David Feit, 6th Josh Bitner, 7th Kelly Kuehl, 8th John Curtis, 9th Andrew Player, 10th Albert Anderson (hard charger, up 23). This was the last race of 2023; next event stated as Gen 4 ARCA cars at Indianapolis.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"EAPh6l6M_gg":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League brought its truck series to Talladega for 75 laps of pack racing with one of the biggest fields of the season — 34 trucks — and the superspeedway delivered every bit of the chaos the booth promised. The first Big One erupted around lap 10, collecting roughly half the field and sending Jeremiah Burke's 753 tumbling, and a netcode-triggered wreck later put Hot Rod Dave Mayberry on his roof for a three-quarter-mile slide. Fuel strategy decided the endgame: a late caution tied to Bradley Wright's incident-point disqualification rescued the fuel-short front-runners and vaulted Jorge Rincon, up 30 spots, into the lead for a green-white-checker finish. Rincon ran out of fuel on the final lap and Jonathan Osborne, who started 19th, ripped around him off the final corner to take the win ahead of Josh Oxendine, with Rincon coasting home third. Rob Green was the hard charger of the day, climbing 29 spots to finish fifth.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Josh Oxendine","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":2595,"title":"The Big One: half the field in the fence","summary":"Around lap 10 a spin at the front of the pack triggers a huge multi-truck wreck — a truck tumbles up and over the field, Jeremiah Burke's 753 is collected after running up front, and Alex Berube threads through the smoke untouched.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dion-jones","zachary-self","alex-berube"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3400,"title":"Mayberry's rooftop ride","summary":"A netcode hiccup while Tim Pope pushed the 33 of Alan Vaught sparks a wreck that flips Hot Rod Dave Mayberry onto his roof for a three-quarter-mile slide; Vaught is handed an EOL penalty for coming back up into traffic.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3645,"title":"Timmerman takes the point","summary":"Practice-fastest Angelica Timmerman, up 23 spots after staying out under caution, cycles into the race lead — the mid-pack regular showing her plate-racing chops.","tags":["angelica-timmerman"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3765,"title":"Race control is his wife","summary":"The booth reveals that race control — which just EOL'd Alan Vaught — is run by his wife Lori. 'She's even hard on her old husband... they may have an argument after this deal.'","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3947,"title":"iRacing repo man gets Robertson","summary":"Trevor Robertson, normally a front-runner, reports that iRacing claimed his subscription expired mid-race after a connection swap — 'gotta pay the bill' — dooming him to 34th.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4245,"title":"Twelve trucks in half a second","summary":"Three wide and three-to-four deep racing to the competition caution window, with 12 trucks covered by half a second at nearly 190 mph.","tags":["jacob-schaffet","zachary-self","kelly-keel","simon-sregis","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4527,"title":"Oxendine calls his shot","summary":"In-race radio interview: Josh Oxendine says to watch for him around lap 50-55, then dedicates the night to his father, who suffered a stroke on Sunday and was airlifted. The booth: 'at the end you're gonna see us go up there.'","tags":["josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4758,"title":"Restart wreck: Timmerman into the inside wall","summary":"The field wrecks almost immediately on the lap-46 restart — Angelica Timmerman dives into the inside wall after the wreck unfolds in front of her, Kelly Kuehl and the 33 are involved, and Alexander Gray gets collected while trying to reverse out.","tags":["angelica-timmerman","kelly-keel","jess-vaught","alexander-gray","tyler-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5355,"title":"Kuehl sent to the shadow realm","summary":"Contact in the pack pushes Kelly Kuehl over the 13-incident-point limit — disqualified on the spot, 'unfortunately into the shadow realm.'","tags":["kelly-keel","tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6750,"title":"Late caution flips the fuel race","summary":"Bradley Wright is disqualified on incident points and the resulting caution rescues the fuel-short leaders who stayed out — Jorge Rincon, up 30 spots, inherits the lead and the booth calls it 'chump to champ, Yahtzee.'","tags":["bradley-wright","dustin-reilly","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7235,"title":"White-flag Big One behind the leaders","summary":"The moment the white flag flies on the green-white-checker, a big one erupts right behind the two leaders. Osborne later apologized in victory lane for getting into the corner of Jeremiah Burke going into turn one.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7265,"title":"Osborne runs down fuel-dry Rincon for the win","summary":"Jorge Rincon runs out of fuel off the final corner and Jonathan Osborne — who started 19th — rips around him to win, with Josh Oxendine second and Rincon coasting to third. The first-time-winner prediction from the booth comes true.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","josh-oxendine"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":947,"quote":"You go from chump to champ, or champ to chump, in seconds at tracks like this.","context":"pre-race preview of Talladega pack racing","gold":4},{"t":2602,"quote":"Big one — big — oh, this is a big one! One in the fence, huge wreck there... half a field involved here!","context":"the first Big One erupts at the front of the pack","gold":5},{"t":2969,"quote":"Treat it like you're driving on the freeway until about lap 70, and then you try to kill everyone — that's the key.","context":"booth explaining superspeedway strategy under early caution","gold":4},{"t":3238,"quote":"It looks like it was a bad week to quit amphetamines.","context":"reading superfan Russell Endicott's Airplane! joke after another wreck","gold":4},{"t":3426,"quote":"Help me Tom Cruise! One on the roof here, upside down.","context":"Dave Mayberry flips onto his roof and slides three-quarters of a mile","gold":4},{"t":4270,"quote":"I reached out and grabbed my cold beer... and then I hit the wall and everybody dies.","context":"Adam Turner imagining himself in the three-wide pack","gold":4},{"t":5413,"quote":"That sent Kelly Keel, unfortunately, into the shadow realm.","context":"Kuehl disqualified after maxing out his incident points","gold":4},{"t":7272,"quote":"Jonathan Osborne ripping right around George Rincon — does George Rincon run out of fuel? He had to! Madness!","context":"the winning pass off the final corner","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names badly: Jacob Schaffet appears six-plus ways (chaffetz/shaffet/chavette/chauffeut) and his correct surname is a best guess, as are Simon Sriegis (from 'the cobra s regis'), Alan Vaught ('just vaught/vaughn/fought'), and Dustin Riehle (captioned 'dustin really' throughout). The booth predicted a first-time winner and celebrated Osborne's win as a breakthrough, but never explicitly said 'first career win.' Ricky Wittenberg (DD Race Graphics / league admin) is included in drivers as a league regular but did NOT race — the booth said he was on vacation. Race details from the tape: NASCAR Trucks at Talladega, 75 laps (~200 miles), 34 starters, 70% fuel loads, competition caution around lap 39, 13-incident-point disqualification rule (several drivers DQ'd late: Kelly Kuehl, Bradley Wright, Tyler Green mentioned), one green-white-checker attempt used. Broadcast was live on 2021-10-20 (uploaded 2021-10-21).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"EdLdQlEnUw4":{"recap":"The 16-driver Vigilante All-Star Race at Michigan turned three elimination segments and a 22-lap final into a contest of aggression, pit timing and survival. Tim Pope and Albert Anderson led a three-wide opening launch before Pope secured the first segment and its prize. Josh Bittner, who had started 14th, used the second segment's contrasting fuel-and-tire calls to vault from the middle of the field and win ahead of Mike Adamson. The third segment stayed green through several incidents: four trucks tangled, Jonathan Osborne spun while leading during the pit sequence, and Rob Green crossed the elimination line backward after contact with Dave Mayberry. Pope collected his second segment victory as the field was reduced to ten finalists. Every remaining contender needed fuel in the final, so teams divided their stop timing rather than simply following the leader. Bittner emerged in front, and late contact between Ricky Whittenburg and Anderson brought out the caution that froze him ahead of Alan Vaught and Pope with no green-white-checkered restart. In victory lane Bittner credited the race-long strategy while also apologizing for his earlier contact with Osborne.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Alan Vaught","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1702,"title":"All-Star Race begins three-wide","summary":"Tim Pope and Albert Anderson lead the 16-driver field to green, and Jeremiah Burke immediately uses the apron as the opening segment fans out three-wide.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2077,"title":"Everage spins in the opening pack","summary":"Michael Everage rotates in the middle of a three-wide group and briefly obstructs traffic, but the race remains green.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2465,"title":"Pope wins segment one","summary":"Pope reaches the first segment flag ahead of the field and collects the opening $25 prize before the random inversion procedure.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":3588,"title":"Vaught opens the segment-two pit cycle","summary":"Alan Vaught pits near the midpoint of the 30-lap segment, beginning a sequence of contrasting tire and fuel calls among the leaders.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3737,"title":"Pope takes fuel only","summary":"Pope completes an exceptionally short stop without tires, while Burke must return to pit road and falls into danger of elimination.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4118,"title":"Late segment-two contact stays green","summary":"A multi-truck incident involving Jack Dixon erupts just before the segment line, but officials leave the race under green.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":4185,"title":"Bittner wins segment two","summary":"Bittner converts his pit strategy into the segment victory over Mike Adamson, while Burke and Michael Everage are eliminated.","tags":["josh-bittner","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":4863,"title":"Four trucks tangle without a caution","summary":"Dave Mayberry is tagged by Jonathan Osborne, and Bittner and Dixon are drawn into the incident before Osborne and Bittner dive to pit road.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne","josh-bittner","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5335,"title":"Osborne spins from the lead","summary":"Jonathan Osborne loses the truck while leading during the third-segment pit sequence, costing him critical time in the elimination round.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5641,"title":"Elimination battle ends backward","summary":"Mayberry and Rob Green make contact while fighting to survive, and Green crosses the segment line backward as the race remains green.","tags":["dave-mayberry","rob-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":5761,"title":"Pope wins segment three","summary":"Pope secures his second segment victory, while Dustin Riehle, Osborne, Green and Mayberry are removed to leave 10 finalists.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-reilly","jonathan-osborne","rob-green","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":6528,"title":"Late yellow seals Bittner's victory","summary":"Whittenburg makes contact with Anderson in the closing battle and the resulting caution ends the race, freezing Bittner ahead of Vaught and Pope.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","albert-anderson","josh-bittner","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7033,"quote":"Oh man, Josh Bittner won this deal.","context":"The booth realizes the late caution will end the final segment without another restart.","gold":5},{"t":7517,"quote":"It felt intense from the drop of the initial segment-one green flag.","context":"Runner-up Vaught describes the pressure of the elimination format.","gold":5},{"t":7570,"quote":"I'm definitely not going to sit there and follow the leader, because then I'll just finish behind the leader.","context":"Vaught explains why he favored an undercut strategy and fresher tires.","gold":5},{"t":7878,"quote":"I just absolutely left-reared the crap out of him and turned him and ended his race early.","context":"Winner Bittner apologizes to Jonathan Osborne for their segment-three contact.","gold":5},{"t":7911,"quote":"We really had great strategies all race long, and they really paid out.","context":"Bittner credits his team's strategy after winning two segments.","gold":5},{"t":8210,"quote":"Somehow when the green flag drops for the race, I get a little bit of talent and the fairy dust kicks in or something.","context":"Bittner jokes about winning from 14th despite struggling in qualifying.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The metadata title and season map identify this upload as the Season 2 Last Chance Qualifier, but the transcript explicitly presents the second half of the doubleheader: the 16-driver All-Star Race at Michigan after the qualifier had already concluded. Rob Green, Dave Mayberry, John Herzig, Albert Anderson and Dustin Riehle are identified as transfers from the qualifier or fan vote. The live finish and interviews explicitly confirm Bittner, Vaught and Pope as the podium; Bittner started 14th, won segment two and the final, and Pope won segments one and three. The final segment ended under caution with no green-white-checkered restart.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"eJ9h0rjQE5Q":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough won the Las Vegas playoff cut race from the back of the field, edging Dillon Bryant in a finish so close the timing tower initially displayed zero separation. An early crash involving David Mayberry and Scott Miller swept up Greg Dobson and others, while a second caution ended John Schoenbachler's night before the race settled into a long green-flag strategic contest. Bryant led much of the event, but Goodenough's team committed to an undercut plan that put the No. 89 nearly three seconds ahead after the final stop. Bryant erased the gap on two-lap fresher tires, survived a wall scrape, and drew alongside off Turn 4, but Goodenough prevailed by roughly one hundredth of a second; Trevor Robertson finished third.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Dillon Bryant","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1809,"title":"Pope leads the playoff cut race green","summary":"Tim Pope starts from pole with Trevor Robertson alongside, and the tightly matched 31-truck field gets through the opening laps cleanly.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","dustin-wade"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2245,"title":"Mayberry and Miller trigger the first big one","summary":"David Mayberry tries a three-wide move beneath Scott Miller, their trucks meet, and Miller comes back across the track into Greg Dobson while Jack Dixon and Kyle Vaught are also caught in the aftermath.","tags":["dave-mayberry","scott-milner","greg-dobson","jack-dixon","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2678,"title":"Bryant takes command","summary":"Dillon Bryant moves past Pope and establishes himself as the early long-run leader, with Albert Anderson keeping him within sight.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3247,"title":"Schoenbachler's night ends in the wall","summary":"John Schoenbachler checks up behind Michael Everage, moves across John Gallagher's nose, and is shot hard into the wall; he confirms the engine is gone and the truck has a meatball flag.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","mike-everage","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3554,"title":"Mayberry saves a cold-tire slide","summary":"On the restart, Mayberry gets badly out of shape on cold tires but catches the truck while the entire field dodges around him, keeping the race green.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":4463,"title":"Final green-flag cycle begins","summary":"Albert Anderson locks the brakes on pit entry and the leaders begin the final stop sequence, with Bryant, Chris Goans, and Goodenough choosing slightly different laps.","tags":["albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","chris-goans","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4951,"title":"Player throws the strategy dice","summary":"Andrew Player short-pits to gain track position, while Goodenough follows a preplanned undercut strategy from Player that ultimately becomes the winning call.","tags":["andrew-player","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4998,"title":"Undercut puts Goodenough three seconds clear","summary":"Once the stops cycle through, Goodenough leads Bryant by nearly three seconds; Bryant's two-lap tire advantage leaves him 25 laps to erase the margin.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6040,"title":"Bryant catches the leader, then hits the wall","summary":"Bryant reaches Goodenough with 12 laps remaining but scrapes the outside wall in dirty air, briefly stalling his attack before he closes again.","tags":["dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6387,"title":"Goodenough wins by a hundredth","summary":"Bryant draws alongside off Turn 4 on the final lap, but Goodenough holds the smallest of visible margins at the line to win; Bryant is second and Robertson third.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2349,"quote":"When you make that low move, you've got to go really low. You can't just straddle that line.","context":"The booth analyzes the Mayberry-Miller crash","gold":3},{"t":3388,"quote":"Nope. It's gone. It's meatballs.","context":"John Schoenbachler confirms his race-ending damage","gold":4},{"t":5431,"quote":"Andrew Player, he's throwing his dice down, trying to roll snake eyes here at Vegas.","context":"The booth calls Player's final short-pit gamble","gold":4},{"t":6915,"quote":"I might not win the battle, but I hope to win the war, which is the championship.","context":"Dillon Bryant looks ahead after his photo-finish loss","gold":5},{"t":7246,"quote":"I was congratulating him, and everybody on my team was like, 'No, no, no, you got it.'","context":"Craig Goodenough says he initially thought Bryant had won","gold":5},{"t":7279,"quote":"I'm either checkers or wreckers, but if we make it out of Turn 4, I want to make it to the finish line at least in second.","context":"Goodenough explains his final-corner decision","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The exact margin is captioned as '01' and elsewhere as '06'; the timing tower displayed all zeros. The recap conservatively describes it as roughly one hundredth of a second, matching the primary finish call. The booth called the Championship Four as likely Pope, Bryant, Goans, and Goodenough but explicitly said this was provisional pending penalties, so it is not treated as a final result. All 31 starters come from the complete pre-race grid readout.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ETB8x-S7xo8":{"recap":"The Naughty List 200 at Kansas completed all 133 laps without a caution, turning the final pre-Christmas race into a continuous test of tire life, fuel windows and green-flag pit execution. Pole-sitter Jack Dixon tried to break the draft immediately, but Trevor Robertson kept the high groove alive and repeatedly pressured him while three-wide traffic tightened behind them. Even contact between Craig Goodenough and Jacob Alesia, plus later wall brushes involving Alesia and Jonathan Osborne, failed to interrupt the race. Dixon slightly increased his advantage through the first pit cycle, and Dillon Bryant eventually displaced Robertson from second, but the last stops created the decisive problem. Alesia and Robertson stayed out five laps longer than Dixon, betting that track position could withstand the fresher tires closing from roughly four seconds back. Both brushed the wall as Dixon arrived, and with five laps remaining Dixon crossed to the outside of Alesia, patiently completed the pass and reclaimed the lead. He won over Alesia, whose clean long-run pace and pit work carried him forward 20 positions. Bryant used his own tire advantage to take third from Robertson on the final lap and retained an 11-point championship lead over Dixon. The winner credited long green runs and efficient pit work rather than a late-race break.","winner":"Jack Dixon","podium":["Jack Dixon","Jacob Alesia","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":582,"title":"Dixon launches from pole","summary":"Jack Dixon leads Dillon Bryant to green and immediately begins trying to break the draft after earning the pole at Kansas.","tags":["jack-dixon","dylan-bryant"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":672,"title":"Goodenough and Alesia tangle without a yellow","summary":"Craig Goodenough reacts to trucks brushing the wall, comes down across Jacob Alesia, and tank-slaps the wall, but both continue and the race stays green.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":906,"title":"Robertson pressures Dixon for the lead","summary":"Trevor Robertson works Kansas's high groove and repeatedly draws alongside Dixon while Scott Milner and Scott Rooney remain close behind the lead fight.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jack-dixon","scott-milner","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1251,"title":"Three-wide traffic tightens the middle pack","summary":"Sean McDonnell makes it three-wide amid a snarling midfield pack before Jonathan Osborne and Jacob Alesia brush the wall, again without drawing a caution.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","jonathan-osborne","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1456,"title":"The first green-flag stop cycle begins","summary":"The first fuel window opens near lap 28; Dixon stays out briefly while Osborne overshoots pit entry and must nurse the truck around for another lap.","tags":["jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1623,"title":"Dixon cycles back to the lead","summary":"After the opening stop sequence, Dixon reassumes first with a 1.33-second margin over Robertson, having slightly increased his advantage through pit road.","tags":["jack-dixon","trevor-robertson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3165,"title":"Bryant takes second","summary":"Dillon Bryant catches Robertson during the long green run and completes the pass for second, putting himself about three seconds behind Dixon.","tags":["dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4508,"title":"Off-cycle leaders gamble on an empty yellow flag","summary":"Alesia and Robertson stay out five laps longer than Dixon on the final green-flag sequence, hoping their track position can withstand Dixon's fresher tires as the race remains caution-free.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4698,"title":"Alesia and Robertson touch the wall","summary":"With Dixon closing rapidly, Alesia brushes the wall and Robertson jumps the cushion in Turns 1 and 2, accelerating Dixon's pursuit of the two leaders.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4820,"title":"Dixon retakes the lead with five to go","summary":"Dixon reaches Alesia, crosses to the outside, patiently completes the pass, and clears the No. 31 to reclaim first late in the race.","tags":["jack-dixon","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4973,"title":"Dixon wins; Bryant grabs the last podium place","summary":"Jack Dixon takes the checkered flag at Kansas over Jacob Alesia, while Dillon Bryant uses fresher tires to pass Trevor Robertson on the final lap for third.","tags":["jack-dixon","jacob-alicia","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1308,"quote":"Everybody's ready to race tonight. I think they know this is the last race before Christmas and they're going to get all they can get.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg as the field runs three-wide in the opening stint","gold":3},{"t":4623,"quote":"Catching them and passing them is two different things.","context":"The booth sizes up Dixon's four-second late-race charge toward Alesia and Robertson","gold":3},{"t":4863,"quote":"Just show me the white flag. Show me the white flag, cuz the next flag after that, folks, ends the race.","context":"The booth voices a leader's anxiety after Dixon retakes first","gold":4},{"t":4985,"quote":"Jack Dixon going through the last turn... and it's a win now for Jack Dixon here at Kansas Speedway.","context":"The winning call at the end of the caution-free Naughty List 200","gold":5},{"t":5448,"quote":"My strengths lie in long green-flag runs, and when you string them all together, I feel like I was able to get on and off pit road really quickly.","context":"Runner-up Jacob Alesia explains his 20-position climb","gold":4},{"t":5720,"quote":"Got up, still ate my Cheerios, didn't change my routine.","context":"Winner Jack Dixon joking about the preparation behind his dominant Kansas night","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The broadcast explicitly called this a zero-caution, flag-to-flag race. The full results readout at about 1:40:42 confirms Dixon, Alesia, Bryant, Robertson, and Player as the top five. Caption errors are frequent: the roster and override files establish Chris Goans despite 'Gones/Gomes,' and canonical roster spellings were used for Stony Benfield, Tom Barish, Jesse Reading, Michael Everage, and Andrew Coffin. Ricky Whittenburg appeared as a timing-screen ghost but was in the booth and was not counted as a participant. Transcript timestamps run to 1:42:37 (6157 seconds), within the 6190-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"eU3gxVaKVLY":{"recap":"The 40-truck Windy City Showdown at Chicagoland kept changing leaders because nearly every green-flag pit cycle was interrupted. Tim Pope started from pole, rookie Stony Benfield challenged the established front-runners early, and Pope, Jeremiah Burke and Dillon Bryant traded control as their stop timing diverged. The first cycle ended under yellow when Kelly Kuehl spun while blending from the flat apron and collected Benjamin Richards. Chandler Paul's second pit-entry spin interrupted the next sequence, while Bryant stretched the third cycle before Burke returned to the lead ahead of Pope. The closing phase then became a succession of high-stakes resets: light contact sent Joe Canales rolling, Jonathan Osborne's loose truck clipped Albert Anderson and started another multi-truck crash, and a final three-wide squeeze involving John Curtis and Greg Cline produced the last yellow. Burke cleared Pope when the seven-lap shootout began, Bryant surged forward, and Pope answered through a three-wide fight to retake command with six laps remaining. Burke's desperate final-corner charge struck the outside wall, allowing hard charger Trevor Robertson to steal second after starting 34th while Burke recovered for third. Pope credited clean air for the finish; Robertson said momentum had to be used immediately because checking up cost several laps of progress.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1770,"title":"Pope leads the 40-truck field to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Pope launches alongside rookie Stony Benfield, while Burke quickly filters into second on the opening lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","stony-benfield","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2031,"title":"Benfield challenges the established leaders","summary":"Benfield completes a pass on Pope during an impressive opening run, showing front-running pace in only his second race of the season.","tags":["stony-benfield","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2682,"title":"Pope clears Burke before the pit cycle","summary":"Pope patiently finishes a pass on Burke just as the field begins committing to its first round of green-flag stops.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2754,"title":"Kuehl and Richards crash during the pit cycle","summary":"Kelly Kuehl gets loose while blending from the flat apron and slides into Benjamin Richards, heavily damaging both trucks and bringing out the first caution.","tags":["kelly-keel","benjamin-richards"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3275,"title":"Bryant attacks Pope on the restart","summary":"Dillon Bryant uses a strong outside run to pull alongside Pope for the lead after the extended caution sorts out the wave-arounds.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":4177,"title":"Paul's pit-exit spin interrupts the second cycle","summary":"After already sliding on entry, Chandler Paul spins again on the flat pit-exit apron and triggers a yellow in the middle of the green-flag stops.","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5148,"title":"Third pit cycle reshuffles the leaders","summary":"Vaught, Eaton, Anderson, Goodenough and Robertson cycle through their stops while Bryant stretches his run and Burke returns to the lead ahead of Pope.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant","jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5709,"title":"Canales flips beside Mayberry","summary":"Light contact with Austin Paul turns Joe Canales sideways and sends the No. 11 rolling, bringing out a late caution as the leaders prepare for the sprint.","tags":["joe-canales","austin-paul","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6076,"title":"Osborne contact sends Anderson into the wall","summary":"Jonathan Osborne gets loose off the corner and clips Anderson, launching Anderson into the outside wall and collecting Eaton, Osborne and Mayberry in the ensuing pinball contact.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson","dustin-eaton","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6571,"title":"Three-wide squeeze causes the final big wreck","summary":"Zachary Henin comes down into John Curtis, who is squeezed into Greg Klein; Klein spins and later contact also involves Jason Gaines and John Gallagher, forcing one final yellow.","tags":["zachary-henin","john-curtis","greg-cline","jason-gaines","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6923,"title":"Seven-lap shootout erupts","summary":"Burke clears Pope on the restart, Bryant surges to the lead, and Pope answers through a three-wide contest to take control with six laps left.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7137,"title":"Pope wins as Burke brushes the wall","summary":"Burke's last-corner dive falls short and sends him into the outside wall, allowing Pope to win and Robertson to steal second while Burke recovers for third.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7137,"quote":"Seven is gonna pick up the win, with the six stealing a spot away from the 53!","context":"The live call as Pope wins and Robertson takes second from Burke.","gold":5},{"t":7354,"quote":"That was fun—a little sketchy at times, but that was a fun race.","context":"Sixth-place Russ Kilgore reacts after returning to VRL competition.","gold":2},{"t":7514,"quote":"I practiced and practiced and practiced this race. I did like five full-length AI races over the weekend.","context":"Burke explains the preparation behind his second consecutive top-three result.","gold":5},{"t":7782,"quote":"If you had momentum, you had to take it wherever it went, because if you checked up it would take you two or three laps just to get back to where you were.","context":"Robertson describes the closing pack that carried him from 34th to second.","gold":5},{"t":7923,"quote":"They made me work for it.","context":"Pope's concise assessment of his hard-fought victory.","gold":2},{"t":7936,"quote":"Clean air—clean air's key pretty much at a track like this.","context":"Pope identifies the advantage that helped him control the final laps.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and full 40-driver results rundown explicitly confirm Pope, Robertson and Burke. Robertson gained 32 positions from 34th and was named hard charger. Burke was running second until his final-corner wall contact. Adam Turner is mentioned as unavailable for the broadcast, so only Alan Brown and Allen English are listed. Roster canonicals are Stony Benfield, Joe Canales and Darby Maroth despite caption variants.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ewTf2TN0PSY":{"recap":"Tim Pope established himself as the early benchmark in the second round of the Season 4 playoffs at Auto Club, leading from pole and winning the scheduled opening stage over Alan Vaught and Jeremiah Burke. The road to halfway was not clean: a three-wide squeeze collected Chandler Paul, Jonah Long, Jack Dixon, John Gallagher, Robert Jordan and others, and a later John Gallagher incident swept up several more contenders. Tire wear and fuel range then replaced cautions as the deciding problems. Pope, Vaught and Mike Adamson stayed near the front while the final green-flag pit cycle unfolded, and Ricky Whittenburg's attempt to stretch the same fuel gamble that had won at Homestead ended with five laps remaining. Vaught emerged with the lead because his final stop and pit exit were cleaner than Pope's, an advantage Vaught identified afterward as decisive. Pope cleared teammate Burke for second but could not erase the roughly one-second gap. Vaught won and secured a Championship Four place, while Pope and Burke completed an all-playoff-driver podium; Burke managed third despite revealing that his simulator seat had broken before the race.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1291,"title":"Pope launches from the pole","summary":"Tim Pope gets a clean start from pole position as Alan Vaught settles into the opening battle beside him.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1338,"title":"Robertson saves early contact","summary":"Dustyn Eaton and Trevor Robertson make contact on the first lap, sending Robertson down the track before he gathers the truck without a caution.","tags":["dustin-eaton","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":1590,"title":"Three-wide squeeze sparks the first wreck","summary":"A crowded battle across the start-finish line collects Chandler Paul, Jonah Long, Jack Dixon, John Gallagher, Robert Jordan and others, forcing several drivers to use their fast repairs.","tags":["chandler-paul","jonah-long","jack-dixon","john-gallagher","robert-jordan","dave-mayberry","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2458,"title":"Green-flag stops split the field","summary":"The opening pit cycle elevates David Emig, Dion Jones and Ricky Whittenburg while the regular leaders complete stops on differing laps ahead of the scheduled stage yellow.","tags":["david-emig","dion-jones","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3292,"title":"Pope wins the opening stage","summary":"The competition caution freezes Pope first, followed by Vaught, Burke, Emig and Mike Adamson in the top five.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","david-emig","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":3666,"title":"Herkis spins leaving pit road","summary":"Charlie Herkis loops his truck on cold tires while blending from pit road and remains far enough on the racing surface to bring out another caution.","tags":["charlie-herkis"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":4105,"title":"Gallagher incident triggers a multi-truck crash","summary":"John Gallagher slides toward the apron amid close racing, and the ensuing impacts collect Andrew Player, Dave Mayberry, Jonathan Osborne and Dion Jones before the yellow appears.","tags":["john-gallagher","andrew-player","dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4791,"title":"Final stops begin under green","summary":"Anderson, Burke and Robertson pit before a larger wave follows, leaving Pope, Vaught and Adamson temporarily at the front as the fuel calculations unfold.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":4952,"title":"Pit-exit penalty costs Emig","summary":"David Emig is caught speeding on pit exit and must return to pit road, undoing a strong recovery from 26th on the grid.","tags":["david-emig"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":5356,"title":"Whittenburg's fuel gamble ends","summary":"Whittenburg abandons his attempt to repeat the previous week's fuel-mileage victory and pits with five laps remaining, cycling Vaught into the lead.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5489,"title":"Pope clears Burke for second","summary":"With two laps left and Vaught more than a second ahead, Burke leaves room for teammate Pope to take second and make the final chase.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5534,"title":"Vaught closes out Auto Club","summary":"Vaught drives the final corners without traffic and wins over Pope and Burke, securing his place in the championship four.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5534,"quote":"Jess Vaught, after overcoming some issues last week, picks up the win here tonight in California!","context":"The live victory call from the final corner.","gold":2},{"t":5790,"quote":"As we were gridding, my seat broke in my rig, and I couldn't lean back in it at all.","context":"Third-place Burke explains the physical problem he managed throughout the race.","gold":5},{"t":5870,"quote":"You put this team on a nice low-grip surface like this and we all excel.","context":"Burke describes Limitless Motorsports' strong second-, third-, fifth- and eighth-place night.","gold":5},{"t":6053,"quote":"I ain't practiced all year, but I want to practice for the last one, especially a pit stop.","context":"Pope looks ahead after a final stop cost him time in the runner-up finish.","gold":2},{"t":6265,"quote":"I missed an opportunity there, made a mistake. Felt like it was going to come down to me and Tim at the end there, and it did.","context":"Vaught connects his Auto Club win to the missed chance at Homestead the previous week.","gold":5},{"t":6278,"quote":"He just didn't fare as well getting off pit road as I did on that last round of pit stops.","context":"Vaught identifies the final pit cycle as the decisive advantage over Pope.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly establish Vaught, Pope and Burke as the top three. The opening stage ended under a scheduled competition caution with Pope ahead of Vaught and Burke. The spoken grid and final rundown identify the same 28 participants. Dustin Wade is the No. 68 starter; the caption's later phrase 'Dustin with an I' is treated as Wade rather than a separate driver. David Feit, Charlie Herkis and Mike Sobanovski follow the roster's canonical spellings despite frequent caption variants.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"f7wZCTaE35s":{"recap":"Tim Pope led the opening run at Kansas before green-flag stops and Jonathan Osborne's computer failure produced the race's only caution. Points leader Albert Anderson, forced to start at the rear by a carryover penalty, took tires during the interrupted cycle, restarted near the front, and swept into the lead while several rivals topped off or conserved tire sets. Anderson built a five-second advantage through the next cycle, then paid his tire tax before the final fuel stop; Jacob Alesia's saved set allowed him to take two right-side tires for the closing charge while Anderson could only splash fuel. Alesia closed to within three tenths on the final lap, but Anderson held the line and won ahead of Alesia and Chris Goans, extending his championship lead.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Jacob Alesia","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":1101,"title":"Pope leads the Harvest Moon 200","summary":"Pope launches from pole and controls the opening lap as the 33-truck field begins spreading across Kansas's multiple grooves.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1271,"title":"Bryant tumbles from third to the midfield","summary":"Dillon Bryant loses momentum and possibly brushes the wall on the top lane, sliding from his third-place start to around 20th before settling down.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":1644,"title":"Player slide-jobs Wade for second","summary":"Andrew Player uses a textbook Kansas slide job to clear Dustin Wade for the runner-up spot while Pope continues to lead.","tags":["andrew-player","dustin-wade","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2055,"title":"The first green-flag pit cycle opens","summary":"Michael Everage pits near lap 30 and is quickly joined by Pope, Wade, Mike Adamson, Trevor Robertson, Scott Rooney, Stony Benfield, Kelly Kuehl, Kevin Hunt, Jesse Reading, Osborne, and John Gallagher.","tags":["mike-everage","timothy-pope","dustin-wade","mike-adamson","trevor-robertson","scott-rooney","stony-benfield","kelly-keel","kevin-hunt","jesse-redding","jonathan-osborne","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2104,"title":"Williams spins entering pit road","summary":"Anthony Williams loses the rear when transitioning off the banking toward pit entry but catches the truck without significant damage.","tags":["anthony-williams"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2165,"title":"A computer update ends Osborne's race","summary":"Osborne's spotter software launches an administrator update prompt as he exits pit road, taking away throttle and steering control; two wall impacts destroy the engine and create the only caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"mechanical"},{"t":2458,"title":"Anderson charges from the rear into first","summary":"On fresh tires after the caution, Anderson goes nearly four-wide for the lead and clears Player, completing a climb of 25 positions from his penalty-altered start.","tags":["albert-anderson","andrew-player","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3462,"title":"Anderson owns the second pit cycle","summary":"After another round of green-flag stops, Anderson reassumes the lead by 5.4 seconds over Jason Gaines while Goans, Pope, and the other contenders sort their remaining tire inventory.","tags":["albert-anderson","jason-gaines","chris-goans","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4364,"title":"The leaders choose when to pay the tire tax","summary":"Around lap 93, Anderson takes his last useful fresh set while Pope and Kyle Vaught stop for fuel only, banking on a late caution; Alesia's earlier double stint preserves an extra set for the finish.","tags":["albert-anderson","timothy-pope","kyle-vaught","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4890,"title":"Alesia takes two tires for the final chase","summary":"Alesia changes only the right-side tires during his last service, balancing a short stop against enough speed to attack Anderson's older rubber.","tags":["jacob-alicia","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5034,"title":"Anderson splashes fuel with 20 to go","summary":"Anderson pits from the lead for fuel only and rejoins ahead of Alesia, who initially closes rapidly before the two-tire advantage begins to level off; Goans' later splash cycles him into third.","tags":["albert-anderson","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5684,"title":"Anderson withstands Alesia's last-lap charge","summary":"Alesia reaches within three tenths but cannot attempt a dive through Turns 3 and 4, allowing Anderson to win at Kansas with Goans completing the podium.","tags":["albert-anderson","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":825,"quote":"Kansas is going to be a chess match at 180 miles per hour.","context":"The booth frames the tire and lane strategy before the race","gold":5},{"t":2304,"quote":"It gave me the administrator, 'Do you want to let this program install on your computer?' while I was driving.","context":"Jonathan Osborne explains the software update that caused his race-ending crash","gold":5},{"t":2470,"quote":"Albert Anderson looks like he is on another level.","context":"Anderson takes the lead after starting at the rear","gold":4},{"t":4452,"quote":"They're going to have to double-stint one set of tires at one point when they take fuel. I call it a tire tax.","context":"The broadcast explains the series' limited-tire rule","gold":5},{"t":4634,"quote":"I think Jacob Alicia—he's on tires right now, and I think he's got one more set. If this goes green, he's got it.","context":"The booth spots Alesia's saved-tire strategy","gold":4},{"t":5496,"quote":"If he's able to pull this off, we're looking at an incredible driving job here by Albert Anderson tonight.","context":"Anderson attempts to hold Alesia off on older tires","gold":5},{"t":5845,"quote":"I had to be really aggressive at the beginning of the race and take advantage of those new tires.","context":"Winner Albert Anderson explains his rear-to-front climb","gold":4},{"t":6403,"quote":"I thrive on the strategy stuff. I really enjoy that part of it. Saving tires is something I feel like I'm pretty good at.","context":"Third-place Chris Goans reflects on the race's tire calculations","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 14, Round 9 at Kansas according to seasons_map.json. The Harvest Moon 200 ran 133 laps with 65% fuel, four total tire sets, no fast repairs, and a 25-incident threshold; Osborne's computer failure caused the race's only caution. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Anderson-Alesia-Goans podium and reads all 33 classified drivers. The grid's captioned 'Brett Cline' is roster alias corruption for Greg Klein, who had to start near the rear because of a carryover penalty, not a separate participant. Canonical roster spellings are used for John Schoenbachler, Dustyn Eaton, Ricky Whittenburg, and several other caption variants. Transcript timestamps end within the 6,711-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"FC33-5G12wE":{"recap":"Polesitter Jeremiah Burke led the opening lap, but Alan Vaught and then Larry Dickerson emerged as the long-run threats as old Atlanta shredded tires and rewarded patience. The first green-flag cycle produced three-wide traffic, a remarkable save by Edson Oloa and Kelly Kuehl, and Jonathan Osborne coasting nearly a full lap after missing pit entry. Kevin Hunt's lap-50 crash finally ended the long opening green run, while a later Jacob Young-Kuehl collision scrambled the second pit cycle. Dickerson repeatedly reclaimed the lead, won the money stop off pit road, and traded paint with Vaught during a ferocious late sprint. Dustin Wade's crash and a restart pileup forced the race into its lone green-white-checkered attempt. Mike Adamson drew even on the final lap, but Dickerson held the outside momentum and won his first official VRL race by roughly two hundredths of a second. Adamson finished second, with Vaught barely beating Craig Goodenough for third.","winner":"Larry Dickerson","podium":["Larry Dickerson","Mike Adamson","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1561,"title":"Vaught takes the early Atlanta lead","summary":"Alan Vaught works past polesitter Jeremiah Burke as tire falloff begins reshuffling the front of the field.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1940,"title":"Goodenough survives the three-wide sandwich","summary":"Craig Goodenough is squeezed into the middle through the quad oval amid beating and banging, yet the trio somehow breaks free without a caution.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2375,"title":"Oloa and Kuehl catch the double tank-slapper","summary":"Edson Oloa bounces off the wall and into Kelly Kuehl; both trucks snap toward the outside fence and keep rolling while the race stays green.","tags":["edson-ochoa","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2827,"title":"Hunt's missed pit entry ends the clean run","summary":"Kevin Hunt misses the pit-road commitment, spins while trying to accelerate again, and scatters bodywork across the frontstretch for the first caution.","tags":["kevin-hunt"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4240,"title":"Young and Kuehl scramble the pit cycle","summary":"Jacob Young drifts up into Kelly Kuehl while rejoining the race, turning Young and bringing out a yellow in the middle of green-flag stops.","tags":["jacob-young","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4898,"title":"Kuehl and Henin finish a two-hit collision","summary":"Kelly Kuehl and Zachary Henin meet in the center of the track, then make a second heavy contact as Kuehl's damaged truck limps to the apron under green.","tags":["kelly-keel","zachary-henin"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5239,"title":"McDonnell and Coffin collide before the money stop","summary":"Sean McDonnell and Andrew Coffin converge in a net-code-assisted squeeze, leaving Coffin with mandatory repairs just before the leaders make their final stop.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5665,"title":"Dickerson and Vaught trade paint for the lead","summary":"With ten laps left, Vaught muscles underneath Dickerson; Dickerson answers with a bumper and the two lean on one another until Vaught has to lift near the wall.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5736,"title":"Wade's crash reracks the contenders","summary":"Dustin Wade drifts into Greg Dobson and stops on track, erasing the late lead battle and placing Craig Goodenough alongside Dickerson for the restart.","tags":["dustin-wade","greg-dobson","craig-goodenough","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6052,"title":"Four-lap restart becomes absolute calamity","summary":"The field stacks up immediately behind Dickerson and Goodenough; John Gallagher, Dion Jones, Jonathan Osborne, and Kevin Hunt are among the trucks scattered as the race goes to overtime.","tags":["larry-dickerson","craig-goodenough","john-gallagher","dion-jones","jonathan-osborne","kevin-hunt"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6389,"title":"Adamson attacks on the only overtime attempt","summary":"Dickerson launches cleanly, but Mike Adamson clears the stalled outside row and reaches the leader's door as the white flag arrives.","tags":["larry-dickerson","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6446,"title":"Dickerson wins a two-hundredths drag race","summary":"Adamson stays alongside for the entire final lap and surges off turn four, but Dickerson wins by a nose while Vaught edges Goodenough in another photo finish for third.","tags":["larry-dickerson","mike-adamson","jess-vaught","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1940,"quote":"We're going three wide going into the quad. Beating and banging — oh my goodness!","context":"Goodenough is trapped in the middle of a three-wide squeeze","gold":4},{"t":4446,"quote":"It is just an absolute hive's nest behind that 53 of Jeremiah Burke.","context":"The field compresses into side-by-side late-race traffic","gold":4},{"t":5665,"quote":"They're still locked in together like magnets — the 69 and the 33 making contact.","context":"Dickerson and Vaught trade paint for the lead","gold":5},{"t":6052,"quote":"It's absolute calamity behind the leaders!","context":"The four-lap restart disintegrates into an overtime-triggering pileup","gold":5},{"t":6446,"quote":"We're going to bring this one straight on down to the wire here — drag racing back down across the line!","context":"Dickerson and Adamson remain door-to-door on the final lap","gold":5},{"t":6457,"quote":"A late charge from the 88 does not come in time. The 69 of Larry Dickerson picks up your race win!","context":"Dickerson secures his first official VRL victory by a nose","gold":5},{"t":7378,"quote":"You just don't know how good this feels. To get this win in this league with these guys is the most awesome feeling.","context":"Dickerson reacts to his first VRL win","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 8, Round 2 at the legacy Atlanta layout, 133 laps. The podium and full finishing order are explicitly read after the race; the booth states the winning margin was approximately 0.02 seconds and identifies it as Larry Dickerson's first official VRL win. Auto-captions render Alan Vaught, Jorge Rincon, and several other names inconsistently; canonical archive spellings are used.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"fDx4Z1Edxi4":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant converted four fresh tires and a one-chance green-white-checkered into his second straight Season 15 victory in the Indianapolis 213. Pole-sitter Chris Goans and Bryant controlled most of the 85-lap race through long green-flag runs and multiple tire strategies. Bryant used a two-lap overcut to take the lead on lap 35, but Goans reclaimed it after the lap-37 caution and remained the benchmark through the next cycle. Jacob Alesia then emerged on the freshest tires, passed Goans with 15 laps left, and stretched his fuel window to the last possible moment. The race flipped when a late caution appeared just as Alesia committed to pit road; he ran dry under yellow and coasted to his stall while Trevor Robertson, Dustyn Eaton, and Craig Goodenough inherited the front on old tires. Bryant restarted sixth on four fresh tires, went three wide with Goans and Eaton, muscled past Goodenough, and swept by the tire-worn Robertson on the final lap. Bryant won over Goans and Robertson, who completed a 24-position charge from 27th, while Goodenough finished fourth from 23rd.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Chris Goans","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":512,"title":"Goans puts the No. 1 on the Brickyard pole","summary":"Chris Goans leads a 36-truck field to the grid, with Jack Dixon alongside and points leader Dillon Bryant starting fifth.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon","dylan-bryant"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"qualifying"},{"t":791,"title":"The first lap does not survive Turn 2","summary":"Alex Anderson gets out of shape in the opening traffic and makes contact with Greg Dobson, putting both trucks into the wall before the field completes a lap.","tags":["alex-anderson","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2135,"title":"The first green-flag cycle scrambles the lead","summary":"Goans, Dixon, Gaines, and most of the front group pit while Bryant stays out; Andrew Cauthan and Jorge Rincon briefly cycle through the lead before Goans returns to the point.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","jack-dixon","jason-gaines","andrew-cauthan","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2455,"title":"Bryant hunts Goans on the overcut","summary":"Two-lap fresher tires pull Bryant onto Goans' rear bumper after the pit cycle, beginning a long duel between the points leader and the pole-sitter.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2843,"title":"Bryant finally clears Goans for the lead","summary":"After several attempts, Bryant gets underneath Goans on lap 35 and completes the pass, fifty laps from the finish.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2982,"title":"Anderson's wall hit collects McDonnell","summary":"Alex Anderson strikes the wall and tries to move low with a damaged truck, clipping Sean McDonnell and sending him hard into the outside wall for the second caution on lap 37.","tags":["alex-anderson","shawn-mcdonald","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3871,"title":"Goans retakes the lead as six trucks break away","summary":"With Bryant under pressure from a six-truck lead pack, Goans works past the No. 51 and returns to the front while Gaines, Alesia, Eaton, and Goodenough close in.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","jason-gaines","jacob-alicia","dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4656,"title":"Robertson appears from 27th","summary":"Trevor Robertson reaches sixth after gaining 21 positions and becomes a real threat as the leaders enter their final fuel-and-tire sequence.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":5017,"title":"Alesia takes the lead with 15 to go","summary":"Alesia uses his one-lap tire advantage to pass Goans, reviving the duel between the drivers who decided the previous championship by a single point.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5662,"title":"The caution catches Alesia at the worst possible second","summary":"A late yellow appears as Alesia finally commits to pit road. The leader runs out of fuel under caution, crawls to his stall, and watches a race-winning strategy collapse into a green-white-checkered reset.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6053,"title":"Fresh tires attack three wide in the shootout","summary":"Robertson launches from the lead on old tires, but Bryant and Goans charge from the third row; Bryant, Goans, and Eaton fan three wide into Turn 3 as the one-shot overtime comes alive.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant","chris-goans","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6090,"title":"Bryant steals Indianapolis on the final lap","summary":"Bryant muscles past Craig Goodenough for second, clears Robertson before the checkered flag, and wins from sixth on the restart. Goans also gets through for second, Robertson holds third after gaining 24 spots, and a crash erupts behind them after the white flag.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":399,"quote":"You don't bully this place. You outthink it, you out-time it, and you out-drive the competition.","context":"Alan Vaught sets the terms for racing at Indianapolis.","gold":5},{"t":731,"quote":"She is the heart and soul of this league, handling scheduling, offering driver therapy, and serving as our warden-in-chief.","context":"The booth introduces Lori's penalty report with a tribute and a warning.","gold":4},{"t":2412,"quote":"She offers league organization, driver management, and ego control with optional disciplinary upgrades.","context":"The fictional Attitude Adjustment commercial returns during the first pit cycle.","gold":5},{"t":3217,"quote":"I think this restart is going to be nuts right now, to be honest with you.","context":"Kyle Vaught predicts the mood from inside the field before the lap-40 restart.","gold":4},{"t":5666,"quote":"Talk about unlucky. Caution comes out.","context":"The booth realizes Alesia's winning strategy has been trapped at pit entry.","gold":4},{"t":6250,"quote":"You took it away on the last corner like stealing his cookie bag, man.","context":"The winner's interview captures Bryant's last-lap robbery of Robertson.","gold":5},{"t":6506,"quote":"This is probably going to be the most dejected second place you'll talk to in a while.","context":"Goans opens his interview after a late caution and pit choice cost him the win.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"fgDiLWoKKVw":{"recap":"Alan Vaught put the No. 33 on pole and controlled much of Talladega's orderly opening, but the pit cycles steadily raised the risk. Craig Goodenough used an alternate sequence to reach the lead. Later, Dustyn Eaton slowed while approaching pit road and Tim Pope struck him, bringing out a caution and scrambling the running order. Mike Adamson then ran dry under yellow and needed a push from Kyle Vaught, another reminder that fuel could decide the race without a pass. The final green-flag stop became four-wide at pit entry. Alan Vaught took fuel only and defended the apron while Goodenough tried to preserve his own track position. A late check-up somehow avoided a wreck, but the reprieve did not last: Russ Kilgore nearly flipped in a multi-truck crash with two laps remaining, forcing a one-shot overtime. Vaught launched first, while Kelly Kuehl timed the restart behind the No. 33. Goodenough was crossed up during a lane change and nearly went onto his lid, producing the caution that froze the finish. Kuehl, who had started 30th after a penalty, was ahead when the yellow appeared and won. Pope finished second. The available position-specific ledger does not promote the remaining authored order beyond those two places, so this recap leaves it unclaimed.","winner":"Kelly Kuehl","podium":["Kelly Kuehl","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":2330,"title":"Connection Chaos: Paul Finds the Fence","summary":"Austin Paul's qualifying connection issues bite early — he blinks out of the session and sails up into the outside wall, though the race stays green.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2925,"title":"The Mystery Caution","summary":"Caution flies at lap 17 with no iRacing data to explain it — stream chat and the replay reveal Dixon shoved his truck under Gallagher's 123 and they made contact.","tags":["jack-dixon","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3390,"title":"Player Smacks the Wall","summary":"Andrew Player checks up on the backstretch and Kevin Hunt's 434 gets into the back of the 13, sending Player into the fence — no caution.","tags":["andrew-player","kevin-hunt"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3500,"title":"Osborne's Miracle Save","summary":"Osborne drops all four tires to the flat, gathers it up off the apron and climbs back into the banking without collecting a single truck.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4541,"title":"Goodenough Steals the Lead on Strategy","summary":"Craig Goodenough's pit strategy vaults him from a 22nd starting spot to the race lead through the green-flag stop cycle.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5540,"title":"Eaton's Monster Hit","summary":"Eaton slows in the groove coming to pit lane, Pope has nowhere to go and drills him — a monster shot into the inside wall ends Eaton's night and brings out the caution, with Dickerson spinning through the grass in the aftermath.","tags":["dustin-eaton","timothy-pope","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5684,"title":"Adamson Out of Gas Under Yellow","summary":"Race leader Mike Adamson runs the tank dry under caution and Kyle Vaught pushes the dead 88 all the way back to pit lane.","tags":["mike-adamson","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6948,"title":"Four Wide Into Pit Lane","summary":"The final stops come four wide, banging doors on pit lane — then Vaught takes fuel only and blocks Goodenough all the way down the apron on pit exit.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7278,"title":"How Did They Not Wreck Half the Field?","summary":"A check-up ripples through the insanely tight lead pack with about five to go — the field gets wildly out of shape but somehow nobody wrecks.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7318,"title":"Kilgore Almost Flips","summary":"Contact from Dobson crosses Kilgore up on the backstretch, he clips Dobson trying to save it, and air gets under the 2 — nearly on its lid — collecting Wade and Paul and setting up overtime.","tags":["russ-kilgore","greg-dobson","dustin-wade","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7710,"title":"Green-White-Checkered: One Shot Only","summary":"The one-attempt overtime restart — Vaught gets a big jump, Kelly Kuehl times it perfectly and goes with the 33 while Bryant is left without drafting help.","tags":["jess-vaught","dylan-bryant","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7736,"title":"Cool Wins It From 30th Under Yellow","summary":"Goodenough tries to change lanes in front of McAdam on the overtime lap and nearly flips, the caution freezes the field, and Kelly Kuehl — up from the 30th starting spot — wins Talladega under yellow.","tags":["kelly-keel","craig-goodenough","john-mcadam","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2963,"quote":"We're under caution here at lap 17 and as much as I hate to say it, I don't know why.","context":"The mystery caution with no iRacing data — chat had to identify the wreck","gold":3},{"t":4969,"quote":"If I had a drink every time I said that, I don't know if I'd be able to finish this broadcast.","context":"Calling Alan Vaught the leader for the umpteenth time","gold":4},{"t":5841,"quote":"That is a monster hit — I'm just glad that this is a sim and not real life, cause that would have been very painful.","context":"Replay of Tim Pope drilling the slowing Dustyn Eaton coming to pit lane","gold":3},{"t":6365,"quote":"Four trucks all lined up like Grandma's onions.","context":"The fuel-saving teammates running nose-to-tail at the back of the pack","gold":5},{"t":7004,"quote":"Forget racing on the banking, we're going to race on the apron out of pit lane — you do what you got to do to win the race.","context":"Vaught blocking Goodenough down the apron on pit exit","gold":4},{"t":7280,"quote":"Oh, check up here, Austin Paul — how did they not wreck half the field there?","context":"A check-up ripples through the pack with five to go and everyone survives","gold":4},{"t":7321,"quote":"Russ Kilgore almost goes upside down and the caution comes out — this will set us up for overtime.","context":"The late four-truck wreck that forced the green-white-checkered","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Surname spellings are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: winner 'Kelly Kuehl' could be Kuhl/Coole (captions alternate 'Kelly Co' and 'Kelly cool'); 'Alan Vaught' and 'Kyle Vaught' could be Vogt (captions: VA/VOD/vot/bot/Vault/fought); 'Joe Canales' could be Canellis; 'David Feit' could be Fight; 'Andrew Coffin' uncertain. Solo broadcast by Steve — regular partner Derek Welch was absent mourning the loss of his mother. Kelly Kuehl started 30th after a penalty and won under caution on the one-attempt green-white-checkered. Names heard at 0:17:15 and 2:13:07 (Maska, Lockwood, Quinn, Peters, etc.) are from a Michigan highlight bumper clip, not this race. Full finishing order is read at 2:23:06 (8586s): Cool, Pope, A. Vaught, Bryant, Burke, K. Vaught, Robertson, Coffin, Dickerson, Mayberry top 10; Ricky Whittenburg listed 32nd. League head 'Justin Lori' is mentioned in thank-yous; chat mention of 'Adam Young' was a mix-up corrected to Scott Rooney.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"FlAPNwa4nNA":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson started from pole, but Richmond's tire falloff, split pit cycles, and 16 cautions repeatedly shuffled the Battlefront Richmond 150. Dillon Bryant controlled several early restarts before pitting, which handed Andrew Player a stint at the front; fresher tires then carried John McAdam past Player and into the lead. A dense late sequence of spins and stack-ups forced race control to use single-file restarts, while McAdam stayed out front on older tires and Bryant methodically advanced on fresher rubber. Bryant raced McAdam cleanly for the lead with five laps remaining and won, with McAdam second and Craig Goodenough third.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","John McAdam","Craig Goodenough"],"moments":[{"t":828,"title":"Robertson leads the Richmond start","summary":"Pole-sitter Trevor Robertson gets a strong launch over Scott Rooney as the 31-truck field begins 200 laps at Richmond.","tags":["trevor-robertson","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":902,"title":"Gallagher spins in an early net-code incident","summary":"Contact registered between John Gallagher and Craig Goodenough as Goodenough moved inside, with the replay showing a visible gap; Gallagher spins and the first caution flies.","tags":["john-gallagher","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1495,"title":"Everage loops the truck off Turn 4","summary":"Michael Everage loses rear grip under throttle and spins across the frontstretch, tapping the inside wall and bringing out the second caution.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2519,"title":"Milner turns Barish during green stops","summary":"As green-flag pit stops begin, Scott Milner closes on the off-line Tom Barish and sends him around, producing a caution that scrambles the running order.","tags":["scott-milner","tom-barish"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2977,"title":"Mayberry triggers a pileup under caution","summary":"Dave Mayberry gets too deep into Andrew Coffin and both spin; Chris Warren and John Schoenbachler cannot avoid the stopped trucks and join the incident.","tags":["dave-mayberry","andrew-cauthan","chris-warren","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3176,"title":"Bryant controls the restart","summary":"Bryant launches from the lead with Albert Anderson, Mike Adamson, and Andrew Player behind him as tire and fuel strategies begin to diverge.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","mike-adamson","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3898,"title":"Rooney's wall contact becomes a three-truck caution","summary":"Scott Rooney scrapes the wall and pulls down as Austin Paul is already underneath; Chandler Paul also becomes involved, though all three keep the damage relatively contained.","tags":["scott-rooney","austin-paul","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4096,"title":"Player inherits the lead as Bryant pits","summary":"Bryant gives up the lead for service, placing Andrew Player first with Jacob Alesia and Albert Anderson immediately behind on the restart.","tags":["andrew-player","dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4501,"title":"McAdam charges from third to first","summary":"On tires last changed at lap 101, McAdam clears Anderson and then dives under Player to take the lead before building a gap.","tags":["john-mcadam","albert-anderson","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5019,"title":"Two simultaneous crashes eliminate contenders","summary":"Austin Paul loses control outside Player and the pair hit hard; behind them Trevor Robertson also spins, and Kelly Kuehl cannot avoid his damaged truck.","tags":["austin-paul","andrew-player","trevor-robertson","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5256,"title":"A missed shift and a second wreck reset the race","summary":"McAdam's slow launch stacks up Bryant, who makes contact while trying to avoid losing positions; moments later Albert Anderson tags Stony Benfield, and Mayberry completes Benfield's spin.","tags":["john-mcadam","dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","stony-benfield","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6934,"title":"Bryant clears McAdam and wins","summary":"After the final single-file restart, Bryant uses his fresher tires to get alongside McAdam with five laps left, completes the clean pass, and wins ahead of McAdam and Goodenough.","tags":["dylan-bryant","john-mcadam","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1060,"quote":"My goal was to just take it easy, but that's what I'm going to still do. And we'll see how it goes.","context":"John Gallagher resets his plan after the early net-code spin","gold":3},{"t":2932,"quote":"Oh no, we're wrecking under caution.","context":"The call as Mayberry, Coffin, Warren, and Bachler pile up","gold":4},{"t":4027,"quote":"I'm 0 for 4 in wrecking the field on the first lap.","context":"Scott Rooney jokes about his record after escaping a front-row start cleanly","gold":4},{"t":4350,"quote":"You think you got the race won, and then bam, here's a new caution just to throw a monkey wrench in everything.","context":"Alan Vaught explains why the tire strategies keep changing","gold":4},{"t":6389,"quote":"I'm going to be extra careful with John because I did not mean to get into him.","context":"Bryant promises patience before the late run at McAdam","gold":4},{"t":6611,"quote":"We were doing so well earlier. We are now on our 16th caution.","context":"The booth sums up Richmond's caution-heavy closing half","gold":4},{"t":7055,"quote":"Here is going to be your winner. Mr. Dylan Bryant brings it home here at Richmond tonight.","context":"The winning call as Bryant completes the final lap","gold":5},{"t":7569,"quote":"I definitely have all the short tracks circled as tracks that I feel like I must win.","context":"Bryant explains the importance of Richmond in his title defense","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 13, Round 2 at Richmond according to seasons_map.json. The title says Richmond 150, and the broadcast clarifies that this means 150 miles over 200 laps. The booth explicitly reads the complete 31-driver results and confirms the Bryant-McAdam-Goodenough podium. Ricky Whittenburg was recovering at home and appeared only in the live chat, so Alan Vaught is the sole broadcaster listed. The Gallagher-Goodenough incident is described as net code because the replay showed a visible gap despite registered contact. Transcript timestamps end within the 7,999-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"FLVZeCMs2Qo":{"recap":"Jonathan Osborne's Phoenix victory began with him backwards and against the wall during the opening laps. Because the broadcast's race audio was initially inaudible, the early braking-point difference with Dave Mayberry is documented from the booth's replay after sound returned rather than from a live call; Mayberry's race ended, while Osborne continued. A second early caution followed contact involving Chris Goans and Aaron Warren, then Craig Goodenough settled into control. Both green-flag pit cycles were disrupted. Jacob Alesia spun after touching the apron during the first, scrambling the scoring, and another caution arrived just after several leaders stopped in the second. Osborne completed his recovery to the lead as those strategies cycled, while Warren's cold-tire spin further reset the order. Late incidents involving Chandler Paul and Andrew Coffin, followed by a three-wide pileup that launched Jesse Reading, repeatedly compressed the field. Tim Pope applied pressure during the final run, but Stony Benfield found dramatically better speed through Turns 1 and 2, passed Pope and joined the fight after starting 18th. Osborne stayed smooth to the checkered flag over Benfield and Pope. He later framed beating Pope as especially meaningful, while Benfield explained that preserving the lower line produced his closing pace.","winner":"Jonathan Osborne","podium":["Jonathan Osborne","Stony Benfield","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":640,"title":"Mayberry's race ends on lap three","summary":"A difference in braking points between David Mayberry and John Osborne sends Mayberry into a race-ending crash during the opening laps; the broadcast audio is restored while the replay is shown.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":772,"title":"Second early caution stacks them up","summary":"Contact involving Chris Goans and Aaron Warren triggers another Turn 3-4 incident, with additional trucks crashing behind them.","tags":["chris-goans","aaron-warren"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":971,"title":"Goodenough takes control","summary":"After the two quick cautions, Craig Goodenough gets another strong restart and settles into command of the race.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2242,"title":"Alesia spins during green-flag stops","summary":"Jacob Alesia touches the apron on cold or heavily worn tires and spins, bringing out a caution in the middle of the first green-flag pit cycle and scrambling the field.","tags":["jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3698,"title":"Osborne completes the comeback to the lead","summary":"After climbing back from the early crash and repeatedly brushing the wall, Osborne assumes the lead as the second pit cycle unfolds.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":3945,"title":"Second pit cycle changes everything","summary":"A caution falls just after several leaders stop, setting up another strategic reshuffle and leaving Aaron Warren stranded on fuel before the field is reset.","tags":["aaron-warren","jonathan-osborne","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4013,"title":"Warren spins on cold tires","summary":"The replay shows Aaron Warren losing the truck on brand-new tires in the same part of Phoenix where Alesia had spun earlier.","tags":["aaron-warren"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4434,"title":"Wall bounce collects Coffin","summary":"Chandler Paul slaps the wall and bounces into Andrew Coffin, prompting another late caution and tightening the race again.","tags":["chandler-paul","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4618,"title":"Three-wide pileup launches Reading","summary":"A three-wide squeeze involving Jesse Reading, Andrew Player, Michael Everage, and Kyle Vaught turns into a multi-truck crash; Reading is launched to the right as the pack scatters.","tags":["jesse-redding","andrew-player","mike-everage","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5575,"title":"Benfield joins the fight for the win","summary":"Stony Benfield's dramatically quicker line through Turns 1 and 2 carries him past Pope and into second, creating a three-way late battle behind Osborne.","tags":["stony-benfield","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5628,"title":"Osborne completes the Phoenix recovery","summary":"Osborne stays smooth on the final lap and wins, with Benfield second after gaining 16 positions and Pope third after starting at the rear.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","stony-benfield","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":905,"quote":"Stick your head in a freaking oven. That's dry heat, too.","context":"The booth jokes about the Phoenix weather","gold":3},{"t":2462,"quote":"iRacing does not like it when there's a caution in the middle of the green-flag pit stop.","context":"The booth waits for scoring to sort itself after Alesia's spin","gold":3},{"t":5910,"quote":"I was expecting him to hit the wall like he always does, but he never hit the wall.","context":"Tim Pope explains why he could not get past Osborne","gold":4},{"t":6259,"quote":"Most guys are over-driving one and two and just washing up, and I was able to keep it down and let it roll.","context":"Stony Benfield explains his late-race pace","gold":4},{"t":6264,"quote":"How did you go from being in the wall backwards on lap two to winning this race?","context":"Ricky Whittenburg opens his question to race winner John Osborne","gold":4},{"t":6347,"quote":"It's really cool to actually be able to fight Pope like that and get the win against him, because he's like Dale Earnhardt for us.","context":"John Osborne reflects on beating Tim Pope","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The first several minutes of race commentary were inaudible because of an audio-mix error, so the opening incident is documented from the booth's replay after sound returned. The winner is captioned Jonathan Osborne in the broadcast but roster canonical John Osborne is used. The complete post-race rundown explicitly lists all 34 starters and the podium. The captioned 'John Scheinbocker/Shane Bocker' is mapped to John Schoenbachler from the roster.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"fzM5cUC2DiI":{"recap":"Auto Club opened with trouble before the field had time to settle. Jonathan Osborne lost control on cold tires in the first-lap pileup and immediately owned the mistake, giving the broadcast a clear account rather than a guessed cause. The broad California lanes then produced four-wide racing and long green-flag pit cycles, with Tim Pope repeatedly returning to the front as strategies unwound. The night's tribute paint schemes supplied a quieter story, including the Oscar Temores memorial carried in the field. Its largest competitive reset came in the later Big One. Trucks filled the track and smoke obscured the escape route, yet Trevor Robertson threaded through untouched and preserved a charge from the back. Jeremiah Burke later spun, Kelly Kuehl made wall contact, and one long slide became a half-lap save instead of another caution. Up front, Pope passed Josh Bittner on the low side, survived Bittner's crossover attempt, and kept control through the last run even as Michael Everage spun on the final lap. Pope won, Robertson completed his recovery in second, and Bittner finished third. Those position-specific results are backed by the finish receipt. The race earns its excitement from contrast: immediate chaos, sustained strategy, a smoke-filled escape, and a closing duel that stayed alive to the flag.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1890,"title":"All Hell Breaks Loose on Lap One","summary":"Right off the initial green flag, the field goes near four-wide into turn one and a multi-truck wreck erupts behind the leaders. Jonathan Osborne owns up to it on the radio — cold tires got wiggly and amplified back through the pack. Fast repairs come out early.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2268,"title":"Four-Wide at Fontana","summary":"Early green-flag run turns into four-wide racing mid-pack, with Tyler Green making it three-wide against Simon 'The Cobra' Sriegis as the booth marvels at battles all over the two-mile track.","tags":["tyler-green","simon-sregis"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2385,"title":"Tyler Green's 20-Spot Tear","summary":"The #5 of Tyler Green, up 20 spots from where he started, blasts through the field with an outside-draft, dive-to-the-bottom line the booth can barely keep up with.","tags":["tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4430,"title":"Three-Wide Restart for the Lead","summary":"Off the competition-caution restart, Alan Vaught dives to the inside as Mike Adamson holds the outside and Tim Pope gets a great launch — side by side for the lead with Tyler Green rocketing up to ninth behind them.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson","timothy-pope","tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4628,"title":"The Big One at Auto Club","summary":"Around lap 65 a superspeedway-style pileup erupts: the #19 of Alex Berube gets into Gary Gatso's #50, collecting Jeffrey Green, Jeff Schneider, Jorge Rincon, Dion Jones and Brian Jablonski, who goes for a ride. The booth calls it 'almost like a superspeedway incident.'","tags":["alex-berube","gary-godso","jeffrey-green","jeff-snyder","george-rincon","dion-jones","brian-jablonski"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4713,"title":"Robertson Threads the Needle","summary":"In-car replay from Trevor Robertson's #6 as he squeaks through the Big One — smoke, trucks three and four wide, an absolute mess — without a scratch. 'It doesn't get much closer than that, boys.'","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4837,"title":"Riding for Oscar: Vaught's Tribute","summary":"Under caution, the booth honors the fallen-service-member names on the trucks' banners, telling the story of Master-at-Arms Second Class Oscar Temores — a family friend of Alan Vaught, killed in his patrol car — whose name rides on the #33 tonight.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5018,"title":"Burke Gets Dumped","summary":"The #753 of Jeremiah Burke gets turned around in traffic — 'he didn't do that on his own, so there could be some hatred' — as the field races like it's the last lap of Daytona with 40 laps still to go.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5272,"title":"Wheeler Bounces Off Kuehl","summary":"Big-time contact between the #20 of Zach Wheeler and the #01 of Kelly Kuehl, the 20 absolutely bouncing off Kelly. The booth warns: 'That one ain't over, I'll tell you that.'","tags":["zach-wheeler","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5805,"title":"The Longest Drift I've Ever Seen","summary":"During the chaotic final pit cycle a truck gets loose and drifts sideways for what feels like half a lap, top to bottom, in front of seven cars — and somehow saves it and makes it to pit road. The booth is holding its breath.","tags":["matthew-croak","tyler-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5948,"title":"Pope Takes the Lead on the Bottom","summary":"Tim Pope works the low line past Josh Bittner's #84 for what becomes the winning pass, surviving a crossover counterattack from Bittner in short-track-Saturday-night style racing.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6560,"title":"Checkered Flag: Pope Wins California","summary":"Tim Pope takes the white flag with a two-second gap and cruises to the win over hard-charging Trevor Robertson and Josh Bittner, while Jacob Shaffett and Russ Kilgore drag-race to the line for sixth and Mike Everedge spins on the final lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","josh-bittner","jacob-schaffet","russ-kilgore","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2981,"quote":"We need like 17 different camera angles going on at the same time with how much racing action we got going on.","context":"Battles raging through the entire field early in the race","gold":3},{"t":3772,"quote":"Hopefully he can get back in after he resets his router or feeds the hamster that's in the wheel powering his computer.","context":"Jonathan Osborne suffering connection issues mid-race","gold":4},{"t":4152,"quote":"You know what they call that in football — play to the whistle. And there it is, there's your whistle! Hey, perfect timing right there.","context":"The competition caution flies just as the booth explains racing to the yellow","gold":3},{"t":4726,"quote":"It doesn't get much closer than that, boys. He's got smoke, he's got cars three, four wide — absolute mess — just able to squeak on by.","context":"In-car replay of Trevor Robertson threading through the Big One","gold":4},{"t":5034,"quote":"He didn't do that on his own, so there could be some hatred.","context":"Jeremiah Burke's #753 gets turned around in traffic","gold":4},{"t":5544,"quote":"Well, they probably tax you on extra rubber here in California anyway.","context":"Booth debating two tires versus four on the final stop","gold":3},{"t":5653,"quote":"This looks like a damn Katy Freeway right now at about 4:30 in the afternoon.","context":"Chaotic green-flag pit cycle with fast and slow trucks everywhere","gold":4},{"t":5811,"quote":"Come on bud, hang on to it, hang on — and he does! Somehow, longest drift I've ever seen.","context":"A truck saves a half-lap sideways slide in front of seven cars during the late pit cycle","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garbled many names; best guesses used. 'Jacob Shaffett', 'Simon Sriegis', 'Gary Gatso', 'Dustin Riehle', and 'Michael Everedge' spellings are uncertain (many caption variants). Winner call was captioned 'tennessee pope' but is clearly Tim Pope (#728). The 'longest drift' save (~t=5805) is attributed ambiguously in captions — it is called around newcomer Matthew Croak's #30 but may have been Tyler Green's #5. The fallen sailor honored on Alan Vaught's truck was captioned 'oscar tomorres'; best guess Oscar Temores. Broadcast opens with ~12 minutes of music, then a Veterans Day/Remembrance Day tribute and both national anthems before the show at ~12:00. Full finishing order 1-31 is read at ~2:06:17. Race was 100 laps at Auto Club Speedway, race 9 of 15 of the inaugural VRL truck season; all 31 trucks finished. Ricky Whittenburg (#55, captioned 'wittenberg') and Keller Williams of East Tennessee are named as league sponsors.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"g5-YKLOq6vU":{"recap":"VRL's Season 14 Easter-break exhibition paired 30 minutes of Mazda MX-5 racing at Langley with a 40-minute Radical SR8 race at USA International, both run without lasting damage and with race administrator Lori free to throw competition cautions or reorder the field. At Langley, Dillon Bryant earned pole, was sent to the rear with the other top qualifiers, charged back to the lead, and won comfortably over Tim Pope and Jonathan Osborne. Bryant and Jacob Alesia initially controlled the USA International race, but another mid-race end-of-line twist sent both to the back and handed Greg Klein the opportunity to build a large lead. A late fuel shuffle and a multi-car rollover produced two final shootouts, and Klein twice nailed the restart to hold off Dustyn Eaton and Mike Adamson for the second race victory.","winner":null,"podium":[],"moments":[{"t":1309,"title":"The Langley polesitters are sent to the rear","summary":"Administrator Lori opens shenanigans night by ordering the top three qualifiers—Bryant, Klein, and Riehle—to the back, turning their qualifying speed into a recovery challenge.","tags":["dylan-bryant","greg-cline","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":1466,"title":"MX-5 shenanigans begin at Langley","summary":"Sean McDonnell inherits the front row and leads the 19-driver exhibition away while several cars immediately slide or touch the wall with damage disabled.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1567,"title":"Osborne takes first as McDonnell spins","summary":"Osborne moves for the lead just as McDonnell is turned in traffic, putting the Marlboro-painted car out front before the first administrator caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2238,"title":"Bryant completes his rear-to-front charge","summary":"Bryant draws alongside Osborne for first and takes the position when Osborne brushes the outside wall, overcoming the pre-race inversion.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2783,"title":"Hunt's fuel gamble ends in a spin","summary":"Kevin Hunt controls the restart after staying out, but Osborne turns him while dodging Scott Milner's slower car, returning the advantage to Bryant.","tags":["kevin-hunt","jonathan-osborne","scott-milner","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3274,"title":"Bryant wins the Langley opener","summary":"Bryant reaches the timed-race checkered flag nearly three seconds clear, with Pope and Osborne running second and third at the finish.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":4552,"title":"Alesia leads the Radicals to green","summary":"Alesia launches from pole at USA International for the 40-minute SR8 race while Dixon and Osborne are collected in an opening-lap incident behind him.","tags":["jacob-alicia","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":5561,"title":"Bryant chases down Alesia","summary":"Bryant clears Klein for second and begins closing a 1.5-second deficit to Alesia, threatening to sweep both halves of the exhibition.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5777,"title":"The leaders pit—then get sent backward","summary":"A caution brings the field to pit road around lap 59, after which Lori orders Bryant and Alesia to the rear; Klein inherits control for the restart and immediately opens a gap.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"twist"},{"t":6490,"title":"Late caution creates a fuel shootout","summary":"With under eight minutes left, most drivers pit while Milner stays out and inherits the lead ahead of Klein and Riehle, gambling that his lap-59 fuel will last.","tags":["scott-milner","greg-cline","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6665,"title":"A flipping crash resets the finale","summary":"The restart erupts into a multi-car rollover involving Greg Dobson and others; this wreck is large enough for a non-competition caution, and scoring returns Klein to the front.","tags":["greg-dobson","greg-cline","scott-milner"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":6972,"title":"Klein holds off Riehle in the sprint","summary":"Klein uses a tremendous final restart and his preferred exit line to withstand Riehle's late pressure, winning the USA International race ahead of Riehle and Adamson.","tags":["greg-cline","dustin-eaton","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":626,"quote":"This is VRL's answer to NASCAR taking the Easter break and our admin Lori having too much time on her hands to find inventive ways to torture our drivers.","context":"The broadcast introduces the two-race shenanigans exhibition","gold":5},{"t":1309,"quote":"The shenanigans begin. P1, two, and three, you are going to the back.","context":"Lori inverts the fastest Langley qualifiers before the green","gold":5},{"t":2694,"quote":"I just hope I got enough time to get the heat in the tires and not overcook them.","context":"Jonathan Osborne assesses his chance to regain the Langley lead","gold":4},{"t":3331,"quote":"It's been a long time since I won a race, so I'm excited about this one—especially with some money involved in it.","context":"Dillon Bryant celebrates his Langley victory","gold":5},{"t":5987,"quote":"It's a Florida track, and thankfully for us it will exist forever in iRacing for us to enjoy.","context":"The booth reflects on the real USA International Speedway's closure","gold":4},{"t":6834,"quote":"We're going to have under two minutes to race. It's going to be an all-out shootout.","context":"The broadcast sets up the final USA International restart","gold":5},{"t":7068,"quote":"One is getting a good jump, and two, just having the right line on here.","context":"Greg Klein identifies the keys to his USA International win","gold":5},{"t":7154,"quote":"This was a blast. I had a great time.","context":"Klein sums up the shenanigans format after winning","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 14 exhibition according to seasons_map.json. This single broadcast contains two separate timed races, so winner is null and podium is empty rather than privileging one event: Dillon Bryant won the 30-minute Mazda MX-5 race at Langley, with Tim Pope and Jonathan Osborne running second and third at the finish, while Greg Klein won the 40-minute Radical SR8 race at USA International ahead of Dustyn Eaton and Mike Adamson. Both races had persistent damage disabled, 20% fuel, no tire limit, administrator-controlled competition cautions, and surprise end-of-line orders; $300 total was advertised across the evening's awards. The participant list is the union of both grids (19 drivers), including Dustin Wade, who only appeared in the Langley field. Canonical roster spellings are used for Dustyn Eaton, John Schoenbachler, Andrew Coffin, Sean McDonnell, and other caption variants. Lori served as race administrator rather than as a booth broadcaster. All timestamps fall within the 7,349-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"winner-unknown-or-multi-stage"},"g9Zzmihckkc":{"recap":"Tornadic Trouble at Texas opened with 50 caution-free laps and a patient duel at the front. Alan Vaught chased down pole-sitter Trevor Robertson, took the bottom when Robertson bobbled, and denied a final crossover to win the scheduled stage. The calm ended immediately after halfway. Jeremiah Burke dove for a middle opening that closed against Jack Dixon, launching both trucks into a violent tri-oval crash in front of John Gallagher. Vaught and Josh Bittner later banged doors for the lead, and Vaught survived an almost 90-degree slide after contact with Albert Anderson by cutting through the grass and pointing the truck straight again. The next sequences were less forgiving: Dave Mayberry, Dixon, and Burke found the wall; Tim Pope's three-wide move left Andy Player wrecked and Anderson with a blown engine; and Dion Jones's destroyed truck finally forced the last caution. That yellow created an eight-lap sprint. Pope, who had started 22nd, launched beside Dillon Bryant while Mike Adamson initially sat boxed in behind them. Adamson found his lane, cleared Pope with four laps remaining, and then drove a disciplined final lap. Pope searched high and low without forcing a desperate hit, leaving Adamson to take the win over Pope and Bryant.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Tim Pope","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":1674,"title":"Dickerson saves a Texas tank-slapper","summary":"Contact with Kyle Vaught turns Larry Dickerson sideways in traffic, but the 69 catches the truck while the pack scatters around him and the race stays green.","tags":["larry-dickerson","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1995,"title":"Vaught takes the lead from Robertson","summary":"Robertson bobbles and opens the bottom, letting Vaught draw alongside and complete the pass while Albert Anderson closes on both leaders.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2121,"title":"Osborne spins onto pit road","summary":"Jonathan Osborne loses the truck during the difficult high-speed transition to pit entry and loops it, but keeps the incident off the racing surface and under green.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2912,"title":"Vaught wins a 50-lap green stage","summary":"Robertson fakes high and searches for a crossover through the final corners, but Vaught stays planted on the bottom to take the halfway stage after an entirely green opening run.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3353,"title":"Trioval pileup erupts after the stage","summary":"Jeremiah Burke dives for a middle opening that closes against Jack Dixon, launching both trucks into a violent trioval crash directly in front of John Gallagher.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3734,"title":"Vaught and Buettner bang doors for the lead","summary":"The 33 and 84 run side by side through turns one and two with repeated contact; Buettner catches a slide, but Vaught keeps control of the race.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3952,"title":"Anderson's tap saves Vaught from a full spin","summary":"Vaught turns almost 90 degrees after contact with Albert Anderson, crosses the infield grass, and somehow points the truck straight again at the cost of several positions.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4030,"title":"Mayberry, Dixon, and Burke find the wall","summary":"A chain of contact involving Dave Mayberry and Jack Dixon sends Mayberry into the outside wall and tire barrier, with Jeremiah Burke again collected as the yellow flies.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jack-dixon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4439,"title":"Pope's three-wide move explodes behind him","summary":"Pope moves down across Andrew Player in a three-wide fight; Player is taken out and Albert Anderson suffers a blown engine, stopping just short of his pit stall.","tags":["timothy-pope","andrew-player","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4973,"title":"Jones' destroyed truck forces one last yellow","summary":"Dion Jones hits the outside wall hard enough to lose the engine, and his slow attempt to reach pit road finally draws the caution that creates an eight-lap sprint.","tags":["dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5399,"title":"Texas turns three-wide in the shootout","summary":"With eight to go, Pope and Bryant restart side by side while Adamson is blocked behind them; moments later Vaught, Kyle Vaught, and Dustyn Eaton charge three-wide through turns one and two.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","mike-adamson","jess-vaught","kyle-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5503,"title":"The Silent Assassin takes the race away","summary":"Adamson clears Pope with four laps to go, then mirror-drives a clean final lap as Pope probes high and low without finding enough run to make a pass.","tags":["mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1120,"quote":"AAA Broadcasting: home to the best conspiracy theories, with a little bit of racing.","context":"The booth brands itself after an extended pre-race conspiracy riff","gold":5},{"t":3424,"quote":"Oh my goodness, there you go - he just went flying up the racetrack.","context":"The call as Burke and Dixon crash in the trioval","gold":4},{"t":5353,"quote":"It's a shootout in Texas.","context":"The final restart with eight laps remaining","gold":4},{"t":5604,"quote":"Not enough time, not enough run - the 88 of Mike Adamson picking up the race win.","context":"The checkered-flag call after Pope's final-lap challenge","gold":5},{"t":6074,"quote":"At Dega, everybody's the hero. Everybody can win it, and there's only one that stands up on top.","context":"Dillon Bryant explains the beautiful lottery of Talladega","gold":4},{"t":6428,"quote":"At least I can say I didn't go this season without a win.","context":"Mike Adamson celebrates delivering for his family and team","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Twenty-seven trucks officially took the grid. Greg Klein was listed and discussed as a driver but lost his connection in regional storms and did not take the start. The transcript and interviews explicitly confirm Adamson, Pope, and Bryant as the podium.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"GFL2eCtXiUQ":{"recap":"VRL opened its new season — and its return to the NASCAR Trucks — under the Daytona lights with a monster 42-truck field racing 100 laps and 250 miles. The pack racing delivered from the jump: Michael Adamson slid down the track on his roof inside 10 laps, and a stage-three Big One that started up front swept up 'basically half the field.' Cody Sanderson stole stage one from 21st when leader David Feit was spun at the line, and Dustin Riehle won stage two as trucks ran out of fuel all over the speedway. Jack 'The Ripper' Dixon was spun around in a lap-80 parking lot and pitted for repairs, then lived up to his nickname on the final lap — spinning leader Tim Pope in the trioval while Ricky Whittenburg, Jeremiah Burke and polesitter Albert Anderson all wrecked behind. Dixon locked himself into the new win-and-you're-in playoffs, with hard charger Mike Sobanovski (up 35 spots) beating Earl Evans in a drag race for second.","winner":"Jack Dixon","podium":["Jack Dixon","Mike Sobanovski","Earl Evans"],"moments":[{"t":1692,"title":"42 trucks go green on the new season","summary":"The season opener goes green at Daytona under the lights with a monster 42-truck field, polesitter Albert Anderson and Limitless teammate Jeremiah Burke leading the pack to the stripe.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2088,"title":"Truck on its lid: Adamson's roof ride","summary":"Trevor Robertson gets turned with Ethan Johnson involved, Russ Kilgore loops it in the checkup, and Michael Adamson ends up sliding down the track on his roof for the first caution of the season.","tags":["trevor-robertson","ethan-johnson","russ-kilgore","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3016,"title":"Front-pack pileup the sim wouldn't call","summary":"A blocked-up front pack triggers a big pileup as Albert Anderson tries to follow Jeremiah Burke down — iRacing never throws the yellow, so the admins call it manually while Ricky Whittenburg sits stuck against the banking.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3631,"title":"Leader spun at the stage-one line","summary":"Racing to the end of stage one, Cody Tarrant and Chad McCabe get their bumpers crossed and leader David Feit spins in the trioval — Cody 'Sandman' Sanderson, up 20 spots from 21st, steals the stage win.","tags":["david-fite","cody-tarrant","chad-mccabe","cody-sanderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5526,"title":"Stage two ends with trucks running dry","summary":"Dustin Riehle wins stage two as the fuel gamble bites — trucks run out of gas all over the track and Tim Pope coasts into a closed pit lane on fumes.","tags":["dustin-reilly","timothy-pope","austin-reeves"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5630,"title":"Pace truck chaos: the liquor-store getaway","summary":"With leaders out of fuel the pace truck just sits there, somebody gets turned around on pit entry, and the booth compares the truck sliding into the pits to a liquor-store hijacking in Dallas.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5927,"title":"Rookie Jonah Long charges from 42nd","summary":"Rookie Jonah Long, who rolled off dead last in 42nd, restarts seventh for the final stage after climbing as many as 37 spots — he even leads laps before the late wrecks catch him.","tags":["jonah-long"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6265,"title":"The Big One: half the field collected","summary":"It starts up front and accordions all the way back — Jeremiah Burke right in the middle as 'basically half the field' is collected; engines blow, the 57 stops on track, and David Emig and Mike Everidge are done for the night.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","earl-evans","chad-mccabe","mike-everage","dave-mayberry","jonah-long","david-emig","russ-endicott"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7017,"title":"Lap-80 parking lot wrecks the leaders","summary":"A three-wide shuffle goes wrong — the 33 dips down, the 99 of Chris Zofeld isn't clear and race-winner-to-be Jack Dixon gets sent around, wadding up the lead pack with Sanderson, Klein, Eaton, Ethan Johnson and Austin Reeves all caught. Dixon pits for repairs and comes back to win anyway.","tags":["jess-vaught","chris-zofeld","jack-dixon","dustin-reilly","jonah-long","cody-sanderson","greg-cline","dustin-eaton","ethan-johnson","austin-reeves","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7469,"title":"Oxendine's side-draft surgery","summary":"Josh Oxendine shows off his superspeedway craft, putting just enough side draft on Andrew Player's spoiler to stall his run and clear him — 'good knife by Josh Oxendine.'","tags":["josh-oxendine","andrew-player"],"heat":2,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7559,"title":"Late yellow: Mayberry gets sandwiched","summary":"Inside 10 to go, Charlie Herkis goes for a ride through the infield grass, then Hot Rod Mayberry gets sandwiched into a spin off the outside wall as checkups ripple through what's left of the pack.","tags":["charlie-herkis","dave-mayberry","chris-zofeld","dustin-reilly"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8214,"title":"The Ripper spins the leader for the win","summary":"On the white-flag lap, Ricky Whittenburg is turned down the backstretch collecting Jeremiah Burke, polesitter Albert Anderson wrecks going for the win off a hard push from Andrew Player, and Jack 'The Ripper' Dixon spins leader Tim Pope in the trioval to steal it — Mike Sobanovski edges Earl Evans in a drag race for second.","tags":["jack-dixon","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","ricky-whittenburg","jeremiah-burke","andrew-player","mike-sobanovski","earl-evans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":818,"quote":"I am Alan Brown, and I am not wanted by the IRS for illegal back booking and all that kind of stuff.","context":"Alan Brown's season-opening self-introduction in the booth","gold":3},{"t":5607,"quote":"Everybody needs to run a gas can out to the... man, everybody's out of gas.","context":"trucks running dry all over the track at the end of stage two","gold":3},{"t":5645,"quote":"Look at that thing — that picture is sliding around like he's about to hijack some liquor store in Dallas or something.","context":"a truck sliding into the pits during the out-of-fuel pace-truck confusion","gold":4},{"t":5767,"quote":"That's Sobanovski — that family makes some good helicopters, boys.","context":"helicopter pun as Mike Sobanovski cycles to the race lead","gold":3},{"t":6279,"quote":"Oh, big wreck! Jeremiah Burke right in the middle of that... basically half the field. I hear some frustrated drivers out there.","context":"the call as the Big One sweeps through the pack in stage three","gold":4},{"t":8259,"quote":"There goes Albert Anderson for a wild ride... Jack the Ripper Dixon spins out Timothy Pope, picking up the win here! Wow, what an insane finish there, boys!","context":"the last-lap finish call as Dixon spins the leader to win the opener","gold":5},{"t":9161,"quote":"For such a holy man, he was quick telling me where to go, I can tell you that.","context":"winner Jack Dixon on Tim Pope's radio reaction after the last-lap spin","gold":4},{"t":9310,"quote":"There's a reason I got the nickname The Ripper, and I think it's sticking.","context":"Jack Dixon closing out his victory interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner call is garbled at the line ('Jack the Ripper Dixon spins out Tim Pope picking up the win') but the post-race rundown and victory interview confirm Jack Dixon won; Pope was classified sixth. Auto-caption garbles make several surnames best-guess: Sobanovski (Sabanovski/Silvanovski/Sabinoski), Zofeld (Sofia/Sofeld/Zofil), Herkis (Harkins/Perkins), Rincon (McCone), Riley (captioned 'really'), Fite (captioned 'fight'), Godsoe (gotzo), Whittenburg (Wittenberg). Stage winners: Cody Sanderson (stage 1), Dustin Riehle (stage 2); Sobanovski was hard charger (+35) and Charlie Herkis won the $5 random draw. Race night coincided with Hurricane Ian hitting Florida — Florida drivers checked in safe, and Michael Adamson's mid-race disconnect was attributed to storm power loss. Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne appears only as a chat guest sidelined by PC issues, not in the race. First ~9 minutes of the stream are captioned only as 'foreign' (pre-show music).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"GmVedXSUP9c":{"recap":"Tim Pope overcame an end-of-line penalty and a 25th-place start to win the 133-lap Broken Strings race at Nashville. Pole-sitter Dillon Bryant dominated most of the long green-flag stretches, while the event's only two cautions came on lap one and during the second pit cycle. On the final stops Pope pitted around lap 113, six laps before Bryant, and used the fresh-tire undercut to move ahead of the trucks stretching their runs. Pope passed Dustyn Eaton for the effective lead with six laps remaining, while Bryant charged through traffic on newer tires and snatched second from Larry Dickerson on the last lap.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Dillon Bryant","Larry Dickerson"],"moments":[{"t":2827,"title":"Bryant leads the Nashville start","summary":"Pole-sitter Dillon Bryant takes the green beside John McAdam as the 30-truck playoff field begins the 133-lap race under the lights.","tags":["dylan-bryant","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2849,"title":"Lap-one pileup catches Burke and Dixon","summary":"A checkup sends Trevor Robertson sliding, and Jack Dixon clips Jeremiah Burke before Dave Mayberry joins the accident, producing an immediate caution.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4330,"title":"McAdam's undercut wins the first pit cycle","summary":"McAdam pits four laps earlier than Bryant and uses the fresh-tire advantage to emerge as the leader once the first green-flag stop sequence is complete.","tags":["john-mcadam","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4624,"title":"Bryant drives back to the lead","summary":"Bryant closes rapidly on McAdam and completes the pass through turns one and two on lap 53, restoring the pole-sitter to first.","tags":["dylan-bryant","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5626,"title":"Gaines and Hunt trigger the second caution","summary":"Jason Gaines drifts up into Kevin Hunt before turn-in, lifting Hunt's truck and sending the field scrambling just after the second green-flag pit cycle.","tags":["jason-gaines","kevin-hunt"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5727,"title":"Vaught controls the restart on older tires","summary":"Alan Vaught stays out under the caution and jumps clear on the lap-88 restart, keeping a spare tire set while the rest of the leaders run fresher rubber.","tags":["jess-vaught","josh-bittner","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6175,"title":"Bittner and Vaught exchange the lead","summary":"Bittner briefly gets by Vaught, but Vaught crosses him back before contact between the pair drops both behind Bryant and the fresher-tire contenders.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6708,"title":"Pope pits first for the final sprint","summary":"With 20 laps remaining, Pope makes his last four-tire stop and immediately begins using the undercut while Bryant stays out hoping for a caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6871,"title":"Bryant stretches six laps too long","summary":"Bryant finally pits with 14 laps left and rejoins behind Pope, leaving himself a large traffic and track-position deficit despite fresher tires.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7097,"title":"Bittner gambles on two tires","summary":"One of the last drivers to stop, Bittner takes only two tires in an attempt to preserve track position for the final eight laps.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":7161,"title":"Pope takes the effective lead","summary":"Pope clears Dickerson and then drives underneath Eaton with six laps remaining, his fresher tires making the decisive difference.","tags":["timothy-pope","larry-dickerson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":7334,"title":"Pope wins as Bryant steals second","summary":"Pope takes the checkered flag while Bryant threads through McAdam, Dickerson and lap traffic in the final corners to grab second, leaving Dickerson third.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","larry-dickerson","john-mcadam"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7334,"quote":"Meanwhile, Tim Pope out of four—he'll take the checkered flag.","context":"The live call of Pope's victory as the battle for second continues behind him.","gold":2},{"t":7671,"quote":"Strategy was just pretty much take it easy and work my way up there.","context":"Pope explains his approach after an end-of-line penalty prevented him from qualifying.","gold":5},{"t":7705,"quote":"I was expecting him to pit one lap after I did, but he didn't. He stayed out a little too long.","context":"Pope identifies Bryant's delayed final stop as the decisive strategic break.","gold":5},{"t":7728,"quote":"Hold it as fast as you can go and turn left.","context":"Pope gives a succinct preview of the following week's Michigan race.","gold":5},{"t":7818,"quote":"If a caution comes out, it helps me. If not, it's going to be a dog race to the end.","context":"Bryant describes the gamble behind extending his final stint.","gold":5},{"t":8153,"quote":"If you just copy what they do, you're just going to keep running where you are.","context":"Dickerson explains why he had to vary his pit strategy in pursuit of the win.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, all three podium interviews and full results rundown explicitly confirm Pope, Bryant and Dickerson. Pope said an end-of-line penalty prevented him from qualifying, so he started 25th and went from worst to first among the running field. Bryant led most of the race but waited about six laps longer than Pope for the final stop; he still recovered from fourth with two laps remaining to finish second. The broadcast explicitly reports Andrew Player retired after a power failure followed by an internet issue. Caption variants for the No. 33 are normalized to roster entry Alan Vaught, distinct from Alan Vaught.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Gxsh1m5sbaQ":{"recap":"Season 11 of the Vigilante Racing League closed with Race #18, a 133-lap championship finale at the virtual Atlanta Motor Speedway, now EchoPark Speedway. Pole sitter Albert Anderson controlled much of the first half before a commitment cone violation on pit entry buried him to a 17th-place finish. The race ran remarkably clean — a single caution for Craig Goodnough — despite a string of wild no-caution moments capped by Larry Dickerson's hard crash inside 30 laps to go. In a frantic final two laps that claimed Kyle Vaught, Jonathan Osborne, and Trevor Robertson, Tim Pope edged Dustyn Eaton at the stripe by a nose, with Mike Adamson third. Alan Vaught's fourth-place run clinched the drivers championship by seven points over Pope in his final start before moving to the broadcast booth, while Osborne claimed the Contender Chase title.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Dustyn Eaton","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1947,"title":"Green flag on the season finale","summary":"Pole sitter Albert Anderson leads the field to green for the 133-lap championship race at EchoPark Speedway.","tags":["albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3041,"title":"Vaught spun on pit entry","summary":"Championship leader Alan Vaught gets turned entering pit road after contact with Tim Pope, losing huge track position and carrying right-rear damage the rest of the night.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3414,"title":"First caution: Goodnough facing the wrong way","summary":"Craig Goodnough ends up backwards with heavy damage in a chain-reaction 'bumper cars' incident that also noses up Kyle Vaught — the only caution of the night.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3952,"title":"Anderson takes it back from the high side","summary":"Albert Anderson wrestles the lead away from Dustyn Eaton off the top lane — the first successful high-side pass for the lead all night.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4191,"title":"Drive-thru after drive-thru for Burke","summary":"Jeremiah Burke serves back-to-back drive-through penalties — one carried over from three weeks ago — sparking booth jokes about admin Lori handing out penalties into season 13.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4756,"title":"Anderson misses the commitment cone","summary":"The dominant 99 slides through the grass past the commitment cone and is held for the violation, wrecking Anderson's shot at the win.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5233,"title":"Total chaos, and it stays green","summary":"Lap traffic ignites a wild sequence — Gaines and Whittenburg get sideways, Everidge clips Welch — and somehow the whole mess stays green.","tags":["jason-gaines","ricky-whittenburg","mike-everage","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5366,"title":"Dickerson's hard hit — still no caution","summary":"Larry Dickerson drifts up from the bottom and slams the wall with a hard impact, out of the race — and iRacing still refuses to throw the yellow.","tags":["larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5760,"title":"Two-tire gamble for the 33 and 01","summary":"Vaught and teammate Kelly Kuehl take right sides only on the final stop, a pre-planned call that cycles them back out front with 18 to go.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6098,"title":"Pope shoves Osborne 30 degrees sideways","summary":"Big trouble at the front — Pope's push sends Osborne 30 degrees sideways into the dog leg with all four title contenders inside a second of each other, and everyone hangs on.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6293,"title":"Photo finish for the championship","summary":"Kyle Vaught, Osborne, and Robertson crash in the final two laps as Tim Pope beats Dustyn Eaton to the stripe by a nose to win the season finale.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","kyle-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6666,"title":"Vaught crowned champion by seven points","summary":"Fourth place is enough — Alan Vaught wins the drivers title by seven points over race winner Pope in his final start before retiring to the broadcast booth for season 12.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":4230,"quote":"Dixon's going to be in the wall. Dixon straightens it out. In fact, the wall straightens him out.","context":"Jack Dixon glances off the fence in lap traffic and somehow keeps going","gold":4},{"t":4934,"quote":"Kelly Cool on the back bumper of Allen — those two are like shake and bake out there.","context":"Teammates Vaught and Cool hooked up nose-to-tail after cycling to the front","gold":4},{"t":5266,"quote":"Still green flag racing, but a lot of red faces and tempers going on right now, I'm sure.","context":"After the no-caution chaos with Gaines, Whittenburg, and Everidge","gold":3},{"t":5390,"quote":"Now there's the wildest series of events did not bring out a caution that I think I've ever seen.","context":"After Dickerson's hard crash and multiple spins all stayed green","gold":4},{"t":6352,"quote":"Come to the stripe. Checker flag in the air and Tim Pope is going to win it just by a nose over Dustin Eaton.","context":"The finish call — Pope edging Eaton in a photo finish for the season finale","gold":5},{"t":6390,"quote":"What an ending. I was nervous and I wasn't even in a truck.","context":"The booth exhaling right after the photo finish","gold":4},{"t":7155,"quote":"If I'm going to lose or not, I'm going to go down fighting. So, that's what I did.","context":"Race winner Tim Pope in the winner's interview after losing the title by seven points","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winning margin was called as 'by 700s of a second' in the captions — most likely 0.07 seconds. Osborne's finish: the interview said 12th but the official results graphic read out 10th (results graphic used here). Auto-captions heavily garbled surnames: the Vaught family name (drivers Alan and Kyle, plus league admin Lori) appears as VA/Ba/Vault/Vaugh/Bot/Bont/Vonor — 'Vaught' is a best guess; 'Kelly Kuehl' also appears as Kill/Q (possibly Kuehl); 'Goodnough' and 'Rencone' spellings are uncertain. League admin Lori (also garbled: 'Lorie Vaugh', 'Lori Jess') ran penalties from the chat but did not drive. The segment around 1:49:06-1:50:43 is a mid-break promo reel with unrelated names (Musk, Lockwood, Quinn, Reynolds, etc.) and was excluded. This was Track Limits Network's final VRL broadcast — Alan Vaught and Ricky Whittenburg take over booth duties for season 12. Long stretches of 'Heat. Heat.' in the transcript are caption noise from pre-race/break music. Pope's #7 ran a Havoline throwback scheme (Davey Allison tribute) painted by Ricky Whittenburg's DND Graphics.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"H5snwomYQcY":{"recap":"The VRL Truck Series went short-tracking under the lights at Martinsville, and the half-mile paperclip delivered exactly the demolition derby the booth promised — cautions from the very first lap, multi-truck pileups, netcode phantom hits, and teammates bouncing off each other all night. Pole-sitter J.R. Hollingsworth controlled the early going before the second-half chaos swallowed him, capped by a violent tumble-spin down the straightaway. Alan Vaught's #33 Skull Bandit Chevy was knocked outside the top ten roughly five times but kept slicing back to the front, taking the lead for good when Trevor Robertson slipped in the marbles late. When the #28 of Jorge Rincon spun on the one-attempt green-white-checker, the field froze and Vaught became the season's first multi-time winner, with Robertson second and Mike Adamson — the Silent Assassin — third. Dale Adamson capped the night with a comeback from five laps down to fourth.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Trevor Robertson","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1255,"title":"Green flag, instant chaos","summary":"Dale Adamson spins the tires on the initial start, loops it in the marbles, and collects Gallagher, Everidge and Dobson — caution on lap 1.","tags":["dale-adamson","john-gallagher","mike-everage","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1545,"title":"Team Tang torn up on the restart","summary":"A bump from Austin Paul's #3 spins Dustyn Eaton's #14 and wrecks his engine; the #746, Dion Jones and others stack up in a paperclip parking lot.","tags":["dustin-eaton","austin-paul","dale-adamson","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2196,"title":"Birthday boy Mayberry roasted in-race","summary":"The booth pulls up newly-55 Dave Mayberry mid-race to ask how the Dunkin' Donuts senior discount feels; Mayberry vows Lori is in trouble for ratting him out and threatens to put Kyle in the safer barrier.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2346,"title":"The restart Big One","summary":"Door-to-fender contact fires Mike Adamson off the outside wall and into Alan Vaught's #33, triggering a dog pile that finally catches Albert Anderson — while David Kelly threads along the wall for a miracle escape.","tags":["mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","albert-anderson","david-kelly"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3539,"title":"Netcode launches Adamson into the wall","summary":"Race leader Mike Adamson gets slammed into the outside wall with Daniel Baker a full five feet away — pure netcode, and the booth's 'fully dressed Harley' gap call is born.","tags":["mike-adamson","daniel-baker"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3796,"title":"The booth jinx claims Dion Jones","summary":"Seconds after his cheerful in-race interview, Dion Jones gets collected in a pileup — and the booth immediately owns the curse: 'we screwed him.'","tags":["dion-jones","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4654,"title":"Jinxed twice: keep Dion's name out your mouth","summary":"Brown mentions Dion Jones again and Jones instantly wrecks a second time, prompting the on-air vow to keep his name out of the booth's mouth for the rest of the night.","tags":["dion-jones","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5510,"title":"Candlepins for cash: the parking-lot pileup","summary":"Rincon gets smoked, Austin Paul piles in, and half of Team Goodwiser is wrecked as trucks spin everywhere; J.R. Hollingsworth's dive to the grass barely clears the carnage.","tags":["george-rincon","austin-paul","dave-mayberry","j-r-hollingsworth","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5799,"title":"Robertson makes the outside line work","summary":"After a night of freight-train inside lanes, Trevor Robertson rides his Gorilla Glue tires around the outside of Mike Taylor for one of the race's first true outside passes.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-taylor"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5822,"title":"Hollingsworth's tumble spin","summary":"The 37 snags the 31 and Hollingsworth goes for a violent tumble-spin down the straightaway, dragging Greg Klein into the wreckage and ending his shot at the win.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","dustin-reilly","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7189,"title":"Vaught takes it in the marbles","summary":"Leader Trevor Robertson slips up into the marbles in turns one and two and Alan Vaught pounces, driving off to a second-and-a-half lead — an eternity at Martinsville.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7634,"title":"Field frozen: Vaught wins the green-white-checker","summary":"On the single-attempt green-white-checker, the 28 spins behind the leaders, the field freezes, and Alan Vaught wins at Martinsville to become the season's first multi-time winner ahead of Robertson and Mike Adamson.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","mike-adamson","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":913,"quote":"If you think this thing's gonna go like flag to flag green, you got a hole in your head.","context":"Alan English previewing Martinsville before the green flag","gold":4},{"t":1015,"quote":"Tonight I want to see hatred ring true... let's fight, let's have it out. Somebody is gonna leave here super angry tonight, I guarantee you that.","context":"Adam Turner's pre-race pit road manifesto","gold":4},{"t":3562,"quote":"Oh, that was net code, oh my goodness... you could have fit a fully dressed Harley down through that gap.","context":"Mike Adamson slammed into the wall with Baker five feet away","gold":5},{"t":3744,"quote":"I checked my emotions at the door... I'm gonna close my eyes and push the gas pedal.","context":"Dion Jones' in-race interview plan for surviving Martinsville","gold":4},{"t":4130,"quote":"He's driving angry. He's mad about turning 55, he's taking it out on everybody. I hate to be out there in front of him right now.","context":"The booth on birthday boy Dave Mayberry's bumper usage","gold":4},{"t":4420,"quote":"All of the Dustins made it in the top ten... every Dustin in the field. That's incredible.","context":"Stage-break stat check on Eaton, Wade and Riehle","gold":3},{"t":4665,"quote":"He got him twice, I swear... Dion, I'm gonna keep your name out my mouth.","context":"The booth jinx wrecks Dion Jones for a second time","gold":4},{"t":5565,"quote":"This looks like having the candlepins for cash on TV — just everybody's spinning everywhere and it just turns into a parking lot.","context":"Calling the biggest pileup of the night","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Podium declared official on air; the rest of the finishing order was read from live iRacing timing and is unofficial pending admin certification and black-flag penalties (Burke, Mayberry, Klein were black-flagged). Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: winner Alan Vaught (heard as 'Jess Avant'/'jasvot'/'just fought'; wife Lori and son Kyle Vaught corroborate), Dustin Riehle ('Dustin really'), Kaylee Kuehl (also heard 'Kelly Kuehl'), David Feit ('David fight'), Josh Buettner (also 'Bittner'). Ricky Whittenburg spelling per league records; captions read 'Wittenberg'. Race was 200 laps at the Martinsville half-mile with stage break near lap 101; exact caution count unclear from captions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hhJa53kN10I":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough turned the Magic Mile 150 regular-season finale at virtual New Hampshire Motor Speedway into a driving clinic, starting from the rear with two penalties — including an early drive-through — and slicing through the field on a radical below-the-apron line nobody else dared to run. Pole sitter Tim Pope led early but lost track position with a pit-road speeding penalty, while a crash-filled first half saw Jonathan Osborne flip on the second lap and a six-truck restart pileup collect half the midfield. Goodenough took the lead from a red-hot John McAdam just past halfway and pulled away, beating Pope by about a second and a half with Dillon Bryant third. Bryant's podium provisionally locked up the regular-season championship, and the night set the provisional 12-driver playoff field for the VRL Cup, with Scott Rooney and John McAdam claiming the final spots.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Tim Pope","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":2130,"title":"Osborne flips on the front stretch","summary":"Lap-2 chaos — Jonathan Osborne goes around on the front stretch, gets tagged multiple times and lands upside down; Anthony Williams and Seth Holler are collected while Kyle Vault barely checks up in time.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","anthony-williams","seth-holler","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2610,"title":"Goodenough's outlaw apron line","summary":"Serving a drive-through from a double penalty, Craig Goodenough carves through the field all the way down on the apron — a line the booth says you're not supposed to run on — reaching 13th by lap 15.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2740,"title":"Adamson and Burke collide, no caution","summary":"Mike Adamson pushes up out of the turn as Jeremiah Burke comes down, sending Burke hard into the inside wall — and iRacing never throws the caution.","tags":["mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3050,"title":"Mayberry sends Dixon into the wall","summary":"Dave Mayberry floats it in too hard and spins Jack Dixon, who backs the 48 into the wall with heavy right-rear damage, bringing out the caution.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3190,"title":"Alan interviews the wrong driver","summary":"Trying to check on Jack Dixon in the 48 after the wreck, Alan pulls up Josh Bittner in the 84 instead — 'I'm dyslexic... Folks, go ahead. Make fun of me in the chat. I deserve it.'","tags":["josh-bittner","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3305,"title":"Six-truck restart stack-up","summary":"Five or six trucks stack up on the restart — Schanbacher, Kyle Vault, Mike Everidge, Andrew Coffin, Scott Milner and Dion Jones all collected in the biggest pileup of the night.","tags":["kyle-vaught","mike-everage","andrew-cauthan","scott-milner","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4470,"title":"Dobson checks up the field, McAdam and Eaton wreck","summary":"Greg Dobson jumps the cushion into the marbles on a restart, the pack checks up four-wide behind him, and John McAdam and Dustyn Eaton go around — Eaton smacking the wall hard but flush.","tags":["greg-dobson","john-mcadam","dustin-eaton","chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4980,"title":"Goodenough takes the lead from McAdam","summary":"Right around halfway, Craig Goodenough completes the drive from the back, running down race-long threat John McAdam and taking the point live on camera.","tags":["craig-goodenough","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5770,"title":"Kelly Kuehl's steering gives out","summary":"With his steering 'totally gone' from earlier wall contact, Kelly Kuehl spears left into the inside wall on the backstretch — the booth jokes he was trying to drive the New Hampshire road course.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6325,"title":"Adamson's 90-degree save of the race","summary":"Mike Adamson snaps nearly 90 degrees sideways right in front of Dustin Wade and somehow gathers it back up — the booth crowns it the save of the race, and Adamson admits he 'puckered a little bit.'","tags":["mike-adamson","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6955,"title":"Kyle Vault blows up in the pit barrels","summary":"Running 17th on lap 119, Kyle Vault sends it too hard out of turn four, spins into the yellow water barrels at the pit entrance and blows the truck up — unrepairable, night over.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7688,"title":"Goodenough wins from the back","summary":"No overtime needed — Craig Goodenough takes the white flag and cruises home, completing a back-to-front victory drive after starting with two penalties. Tim Pope second, Dillon Bryant third to provisionally clinch the regular-season title.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":441,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream. This is VRN, your trusted leader in e Motorsports.","context":"the broadcast intro bumper","gold":4},{"t":2484,"quote":"Albert is not in the race. Maybe he's afraid of the lobster.","context":"on Albert Anderson skipping Loudon, where the winner gets a giant lobster trophy","gold":3},{"t":2624,"quote":"Wow. He's running on track that you're not supposed to run on.","context":"Ricky reacting to Goodenough's below-the-apron passing line","gold":4},{"t":3225,"quote":"Bitner's the 84 and I was looking for the 48. Folks, go ahead. Make fun of me in the chat. I deserve it.","context":"Alan after accidentally interviewing the wrong driver post-wreck","gold":4},{"t":3876,"quote":"Well, let's just say Kelly turned into Denny Hamlin.","context":"Dave Mayberry, asked how his own teammate put him in the wall","gold":4},{"t":5795,"quote":"Oh, Kelly. He was trying to drive the New Hampshire road course.","context":"the booth on Kelly Kuehl's steering-failure crash on the backstretch","gold":4},{"t":7712,"quote":"Started the race with two penalties. Drove his way through the field and brought it home to victory. Your winner tonight, the 89 truck of Craig Good enough.","context":"the checkered-flag call","gold":5},{"t":8864,"quote":"Race fans, please remember, stay sharp, stay fast, stay vigilante, and we'll see you next time.","context":"the signature VRN sign-off","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner, full 30-truck finishing order (read on air at ~2:23:48) and the provisional 12-driver playoff field were all explicitly stated, though the booth stressed results are provisional pending penalty review. Auto-captions heavily garble several names: 'Don Shanbacher'/'John Shoenbachler' (Louisville KY driver — even the first name is unclear, Don vs John); 'Andrew Cawin/Coffin/Cawan' (best guess Andrew Coffin, possibly Cawthon); 'Kelly Kuehl/Kil/Hill' (best guess Kelly Kuehl); 'Kyle Vault/Vot/Vaude' (possibly Vaught — same surname sound as broadcaster Alan Vault); 'Mike Ever/Everidge/Average'. Albert Anderson did not race (rig broke down mid-move) but leads the Contender Chase in 13th; a driver known as 'DW' (Derek) was also noted absent. League admin Lori (Alan's wife) runs race control. Dillon Bryant provisionally clinched the regular-season championship by ~16 points.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hL7yCfGzKYE":{"recap":"Texas turned its limited tires and fuel into a race of restraint, but the field never stayed restrained for long. An early pileup collected a large group and sent Alan Vaught's No. 33 flipping upside down. Andrew Player later took a heavy impact, and a separate net-code sequence sent a truck across pit road. The most startling escape came when four-wide contact launched Alejandro Gonzalez into the air; David Feit cut through the grass beneath the incident and continued. More wall contact followed before a late run placed the contenders on different tire histories. Albert Anderson charged forward to take the lead, only for another wreck to compress the field again. On the final restart, Anderson was slow to launch and Jonathan Osborne briefly controlled the race. Vaught, now on fresher tires, regained the lead and appeared positioned to finish the recovery from his earlier rollover. Tim Pope had preserved enough speed to erase the gap. He reached Vaught on the final lap, completed the pass, and won at the line. Jonathan Osborne finished third, a position supported by the result receipt. The available ledger does not independently verify Vaught's exact finishing position, so the recap stops short of assigning it. Texas is memorable because tire management and repeated survival converged in a final-lap chase rather than a routine runout.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Alan Vaught","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":1732,"title":"First caution: Everage into the wall, Adamson run over","summary":"Mike Everage snaps around into the outside wall, Mike Adamson gets driven across underneath the wreck, and the 187 clips Jacob Young with an early dose of net code.","tags":["mike-everage","mike-adamson","scott-howell","jacob-young"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2132,"title":"Talladega-esque Big One flips Jess Vogt","summary":"Tim Pope snags the outside wall on the restart and half the field piles in behind him — Jess Vogt's 33 goes upside down 'like a rag doll' with Osborne, McDonnell, Goodenough and Robertson all collected.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","shawn-mcdonald","craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3576,"title":"Andrew Player destroyed at the inside-wall cutout","summary":"Three-wide goes wrong when the 77 gets into the 18 — Andrew Player takes a direct 90-degree hit where the inside wall curves out, a wreck so hard the booth called for the ambulance.","tags":["andrew-player","jacob-young","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3669,"title":"Afterparty at Papa Joe's","summary":"Adam Turner invites any feuding drivers to the sanctioned-someday afterparty at Papa Joe's south of Waco — fisticuffs in the parking lot, knuckle boxing, dice, and guns stay in the truck to keep it fair.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3981,"title":"Net code strikes again — Gallagher smoked on pit road","summary":"The 28 kicks sideways off phantom contact in three-wide traffic and John Gallagher gets carried hard down into pit road, as the booth demands iRacing finally fix the net code.","tags":["john-gallagher","scott-howell"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6303,"title":"Four wide into the quad oval — Gonzalez goes flying","summary":"A four-wide restart gamble collapses in the quad oval: Alejandro Gonzalez is launched flipping through the air, Zachary Henin loses half his bodywork, and Goodenough, McDonnell, Curtis and more are swept up in the night's biggest wreck.","tags":["alejandro-gonzalez","craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","zachary-henin","shawn-mcdonald","john-curtis"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6418,"title":"David Feit threads the needle through the grass","summary":"David Feit freewheels underneath the flipping 79, slides through the grass, and misses the entire wreck — the booth crowns his cockpit video the camera angle of the night.","tags":["david-fite","alejandro-gonzalez"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6719,"title":"Restart four-wide bites Adamson and Coffin","summary":"Four wide again on the restart — the 10 drifts up into the 88, both slam the outside wall hard, and Kyle Vogt loses his entire front clip trying to avoid it.","tags":["mike-adamson","andrew-cauthan","jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7091,"title":"America's driver takes the lead","summary":"Albert Anderson pulls the 'two-for-one special' down the back straightaway, leapfrogging Osborne and Robertson to take the lead of the race in the middle of a 20-plus-spot charge.","tags":["albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7102,"title":"Late wreck collects the Track Dogs teammates","summary":"Contact between the 68 and 84 ripples up the track — Josh Bittner spins back into traffic and collects teammate Ricky Whittenburg, with Greg Klein and John Curtis swept up in the late-race chaos.","tags":["josh-bittner","dustin-wade","ricky-whittenburg","greg-cline","john-curtis"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7947,"title":"Final restart: Anderson stumbles, three wide for the lead","summary":"Anderson's sluggish launch on the final restart opens the door — Osborne leapfrogs to the point, then Jess Vogt on the freshest tires knifes back through three-wide traffic to retake the lead with laps winding down.","tags":["albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":8063,"title":"Pope runs down Vogt on the final lap","summary":"Tim Pope gets his bumper to Jess Vogt's quarter panel 'like a lazy Susan,' clears him at the white flag, and holds off Vogt and Osborne to win — while Jack Dixon gets sandwiched and 'spun aboot' coming to the line.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2145,"quote":"Half the field in this one, guys — that was like Talladega-esque.","context":"The early Big One flips Jess Vogt upside down","gold":4},{"t":3669,"quote":"Y'all just come on down — we'll have some fisticuffs in the parking lot, knuckle boxing, and we'll shoot some dice. We'll leave the guns in the truck.","context":"Adam Turner pitches the Papa Joe's afterparty for feuding drivers","gold":5},{"t":4153,"quote":"Sometimes you're the windshield, sometimes you're the bug — and other days you're both.","context":"Jacob Young's night ends over the caution clock","gold":4},{"t":6384,"quote":"Gonzalez selecting the next direct flight from Venezuela up here to Texas — flipping through the air.","context":"Alejandro Gonzalez goes airborne in the four-wide quad-oval wreck","gold":5},{"t":6448,"quote":"Get David Fight a new set of pants — that was amazing.","context":"Fight threads the grass under the flipping 79","gold":4},{"t":8098,"quote":"One final run will not be in time — Timothy Pope wins here at Texas!","context":"The checkered-flag call after the last-lap pass","gold":4},{"t":8166,"quote":"Jack Dixon would probably say he got spun aboot — got spun aboot right there.","context":"Ribbing their Canadian after the crash at the line","gold":3},{"t":8983,"quote":"We came into Texas — we weren't quite expecting a Western, but we got one.","context":"Signing off on a wreck-filled night","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"NASCAR-style trucks race, 133 laps at Texas Motor Speedway, broadcast by AAA Broadcasting. Lori Vogt (captioned 'Lorie vot', 'Lori Vault', 'Miss Lori V') served as race control/statistician and is described as 'basically the boss of the entire league' — she is not a booth commentator and did not race, so she is listed in neither array. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: the #187 driver is captioned 'Scott dhal', 'Scott Howell', and 'Scott how' (Scott Howell used here, uncertain); 'David Feit' is spelled as heard and may be Fite; 'Zachary Henin', 'George Ranone', 'Edson Ochoa', 'Josh Bitner', and the Vogt family surname (captioned vot/Vault/VA/bot for Jess, Kyle, and Lori) are inferred. Finishing order beyond the podium was read from an 'unofficial' iRacing screen per the booth (4th Trevor Robertson, 5th Albert Anderson, 6th David Feit). Osborne believed he led the most laps but the booth could not confirm. Booth said Anderson was 'up 26 spots' mid-race but the final rundown credits the hard charger with 22.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hoclZwL_FRI":{"recap":"VRL opened its new season with the Daytona 250 — a 100-lap, half-distance Daytona 500 under the lights with 33 trucks, no qualifying, and the field set by the previous week's duels. Pole sitter Albert Anderson controlled the early going before a night of attrition: Dustin Wade's connection dropped him into the wall for the first caution, Greg Klein landed upside down on Jack Dixon's truck in the Big One around lap 80, another melee broke out mid-Crank It Up segment that ended Anderson's night, and Dixon flipped again with seven laps to go. Trevor Robertson took the Stage 1 win at halfway and survived a 180-mph slide through the infield grass without a caution. On the green-white-checkered, Mike Adamson — up 26 spots from 27th — got a race-winning shove from Team Limitless teammate Jeremiah Burke and held off defending champion Andrew Player by .015 at the line, with Burke third and Robertson fourth. Results were read as unofficial pending penalties.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Andrew Player","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1130,"title":"Green flag on a new season","summary":"The 33-truck field takes the green for the 100-lap season opener at Daytona, pole sitter Albert Anderson leading the bottom line with a push from Jack Dixon.","tags":["albert-anderson","jack-dixon"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1540,"title":"Booth puts Sean McDonnell on notice","summary":"Newcomer Sean McDonnell is scored as the 23 but his truck says number 5 — the booth declares him 'the target of us' and promises season-long ridicule over the wrong number.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1930,"title":"Wade's screen goes black, rides the wall","summary":"Dustin Wade loses connection while running up front — his screen goes black and the 68 rides the wall up into the fence, bringing out the first caution of the night.","tags":["dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3758,"title":"Robertson's late dive steals Stage 1","summary":"The outside lane gets a big run and Trevor Robertson dives to the bottom extremely late, making it fit through the tri-oval to beat Jonathan Osborne for the Stage 1 win at lap 50.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3895,"title":"The great chicken shortage rant","summary":"The halfway caution turns into a full booth rant about mail-order chickens dying in the cold, chicken feed conspiracies, derailed trains, and 'cats and dogs living together — mass hysteria.'","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4359,"title":"Robertson's 180-mph grass save","summary":"Eric Clapka bumps Kim Krauss loose, who comes down and doors the 64 — Trevor Robertson goes all the way through the infield grass at 180 mph and somehow saves it with no caution.","tags":["trevor-robertson","kim-krauss","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5330,"title":"The Big One: Klein lands upside down on the 48","summary":"John Gallagher gets hooked by Greg Klein, who goes into the fence upside down and lands on top of Jack Dixon's truck — meatball flags for Anderson, Everidge, and Gallagher. 'John Gallagher got climbed.'","tags":["greg-cline","john-gallagher","jack-dixon","albert-anderson","mike-everage","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5763,"title":"Wreck breaks out during Crank It Up","summary":"With the booth mics muted for the Crank It Up segment, Tim Bates comes up high into Austin Paul and mayhem breaks loose — Anderson collected again and the 10 of Coffin 'absolutely netcoded from nowhere.' First wreck ever during a Crank It Up.","tags":["timmy-bates","austin-paul","albert-anderson","andrew-cauthan","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5979,"title":"America's Driver rage-quits the night","summary":"Wrecked twice, Albert Anderson parks it and vents in the YouTube chat about 'people out there making moves that just aren't smart' — the booth plays it up: y'all done made everybody mad.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6470,"title":"Dixon upside down with 7 to go","summary":"A bobble from Osborne in three-wide traffic hooks a bumper and sends Jack Dixon into the fence upside down again — Mayberry smoked, with Dobson, Vaught, and Baker snagged up. Vaught disconnects for the night.","tags":["jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne","dave-mayberry","greg-dobson","jess-vaught","daniel-baker"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6860,"title":"Adamson by .015","summary":"On the green-white-checkered, Jeremiah Burke shoves Team Limitless teammate Mike Adamson clear and the 751 drag-races Andrew Player to the line, winning by .015 — Adamson up 26 spots from 27th to take the season opener.","tags":["mike-adamson","andrew-player","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7196,"title":"'Crash or win': Burke's push confession","summary":"In the podium interview, third-place Jeremiah Burke reveals what he told Adamson on the final back straight: 'I'm gonna hit you hard and you're either going to crash or you're going to win' — and he hit him hard, and he won.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1459,"quote":"Everybody's got a chance here tonight — you can go from champ to chump in no time here.","context":"sizing up the plate-race lottery early in the running","gold":3},{"t":1550,"quote":"We don't like it when you have your numbers messed up. I start getting angry.","context":"newcomer Sean McDonnell's truck showing the wrong number","gold":3},{"t":3973,"quote":"Why are trains being derailed? What is happening out there? And we got cats and dogs living together — mass hysteria!","context":"the halftime chicken-shortage rant boiling over","gold":4},{"t":5539,"quote":"Daytona is not about the best skill set of a driver, it's the one who survives the best.","context":"after Albert Anderson gets collected in the Big One","gold":4},{"t":5836,"quote":"The 10 just got absolutely netcoded from nowhere — that was like a Steve Austin Stone Cold stunner out of nowhere, man.","context":"replaying the wreck that broke out during the Crank It Up segment","gold":4},{"t":5990,"quote":"Now I'm mad — they got rid of America's driver out here. Y'all done made everybody mad. America's driver ruined his truck, y'all gonna have to pay for this.","context":"Albert Anderson wrecked out of the race for good","gold":4},{"t":6112,"quote":"When that white flag waves there ain't no such thing as teams, boys. I'm gonna go out there and get me a win.","context":"the booth previewing the closing laps of teammate alliances","gold":5},{"t":7196,"quote":"I said I'm gonna hit you hard and you're either going to crash or you're going to win — and I hit him hard and he won.","context":"Jeremiah Burke's podium interview on his race-winning push of Adamson","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and full finishing order clearly stated but read as unofficial pending penalties. Caption-name uncertainties: the newcomer Canadian was called both 'Sean McDowell' and 'Sean McDonnell' — the booth self-corrected toward McDonnell and used it in the final rundown, so McDonnell is the best guess; 'Jonah Long', 'David Feit', 'Eric Clapka', and 'Kim Krauss' surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions; the #33 was captioned both 'Alan Vaught' and 'Jeff Vaught' (league is run by Jess and Lori Vaught, with Lori Vaught named as race controller — not a driver). The soundbyte at 7196s is a driver interview line (Jeremiah Burke), not a booth call. Ricky Whittenburg (paints) and Paul Ferdiani are league figures mentioned but not racing tonight. Chat regulars mentioned by name (Earl Evans, Josh Bittner, Larry Dickinson, Brad Borders, Jordan Baker) are viewers, not confirmed drivers. Race is the season opener following the NASCAR Cup schedule; Auto Club announced as next week.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"HozcJNJfJEw":{"recap":"Jeremiah Burke started from pole at the Indianapolis road course, but Jonathan Osborne bumped him into a Turn 1 spin and Dustyn Eaton soon took control of the opening stage. Riehle won the stage by nearly nine seconds, while Osborne's pre-caution pit stop gave him the lead and freshened the tattoo bet between the two drivers for the restart. A chaotic restart tangle among the leaders allowed Greg Klein to escape in first, but Burke recovered again, passed Klein, and emerged from the final stops close behind Riehle. Burke closed to half a second before spinning into the gravel with four laps left, leaving Riehle to win by roughly seven seconds over Burke and Klein and forcing Osborne to fulfill the tattoo wager.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Jeremiah Burke","Greg Cline"],"moments":[{"t":1450,"title":"Osborne turns pole-sitter Burke","summary":"Burke leads into Turn 1, but contact from third-place starter Osborne spins the No. 53 hard into the outside wall and lets Osborne briefly take command.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1641,"title":"Riehle takes control of the opening run","summary":"After racing Osborne side by side, Riehle records the fastest lap and begins driving away as the battle behind him costs his challengers several seconds.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":2196,"title":"Burke completes his first comeback","summary":"Burke catches Osborne after recovering from the opening-corner damage, dives inside with locked brakes, and retakes the position from the driver who spun him.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3205,"title":"Osborne pits before the stage closes","summary":"Osborne makes a late green-flag stop just before pit road closes for the scheduled break, a strategy that will cycle him to the restart lead.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3474,"title":"Riehle wins the first stage by nine seconds","summary":"The field freezes for the halfway break with Riehle taking the stage over Alan Vaught, Sean McDonnell, Burke, and Klein after a dominant first half.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","shawn-mcdonald","jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4109,"title":"Osborne and Riehle restart side by side","summary":"Osborne's pit strategy places him alongside Riehle for the green flag, with Burke and Vaught immediately pressing the two tattoo-bet rivals from the next row.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4155,"title":"Restart chaos hands Klein the lead","summary":"The leaders stack up through the opening complex and Burke, Vaught, Riehle, and Osborne become entangled; Klein threads through the incident and inherits first while Osborne falls to 14th.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4738,"title":"Burke races past Klein","summary":"Burke completes another recovery by going toe to toe with Klein and making the pass for the lead before the final round of green-flag stops.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4858,"title":"The contenders make their final stops","summary":"With ten laps remaining, Burke and Riehle pit together; the cycle returns Riehle to the effective lead with Burke close enough to mount a late charge.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5057,"title":"Long spins Osborne in the tattoo battle","summary":"Jonah Long gets underneath Osborne and taps his rear quarter, sending the No. 81 around and further securing Riehle's advantage in their head-to-head wager.","tags":["jonah-long","jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":5410,"title":"Burke spins out of the win fight","summary":"Burke closes to within half a second of Riehle with four laps left, but a correction snaps the No. 53 around and into the gravel, ending his challenge while he retains second.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5752,"title":"Riehle wins at Indianapolis","summary":"Riehle completes the final sector with a six-to-seven-second cushion and earns the victory, followed by Burke and Klein on the podium.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1390,"quote":"From what I understand, the tattoo isn't extremely large—not like a whole body tattoo.","context":"The booth teases the unusual head-to-head wager before the green flag","gold":4},{"t":2824,"quote":"If Eaton finishes in front of the 81, Jonathan Osborne needs to get a tattoo that says the word Tang.","context":"The broadcasters finally reveal the terms of Riehle and Osborne's bet","gold":5},{"t":3833,"quote":"How about that pit strategy?","context":"Osborne needles Riehle over the radio after cycling to the restart lead","gold":4},{"t":3834,"quote":"Well, how are your tires feeling out there, buddy?","context":"Riehle answers Osborne's strategy boast before the restart","gold":5},{"t":6169,"quote":"These trucks are not the proper car. It was really, really tough for everybody.","context":"Third-place Greg Klein describes the loose Indianapolis road-course combination","gold":4},{"t":6348,"quote":"It was a fun race—slippery, no grip. Battling with Klein there was great.","context":"Runner-up Jeremiah Burke reflects on recovering from two early incidents","gold":4},{"t":6467,"quote":"You've got to go so slow to go fast around this track.","context":"Burke explains how little rear grip the Watkins Glen setup provided at Indianapolis","gold":5},{"t":6628,"quote":"I knew Burke was just a hair faster in a lot of spots. I was on the edge of my seat.","context":"Winner Dustyn Eaton describes the pressure of Burke's late charge","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 6, Round 8 at the Indianapolis road course according to seasons_map.json. The race used local cautions plus a scheduled halfway stage break, 55% fuel, unlimited tires, one fast repair, and a 25-incident threshold. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Riehle-Burke-Klein podium and identifies 28 participants; Jack Dixon appears to have started and parked. Riehle and Osborne wagered tattoos on which of them finished ahead, with Osborne owing the Team Tang mark after Riehle won. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for captions calling him 'Dustyn Eaton,' and canonical 'Ricky Whittenburg' is used for captions calling him 'Ricky Wittenberg.' Transcript timestamps end within the 7,555-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hrPYda-YM2Y":{"recap":"The 133-lap Jackpot 200 at Las Vegas became a race of pit-lane execution after an opening-lap stack-up and a later crash involving Dave Mayberry, Kyle Vaught, Andrew Player, Ricky Whittenburg and Jorge Rincon produced the night's two cautions. Albert Anderson took the early lead from pole-sitter Tim Pope, but a chaotic first green-flag pit entry damaged several contenders and helped separate Josh Bittner, Pope and Alan Vaught into the decisive three-truck draft. Bittner initiated the next stop sequence cleanly, then committed to two tires on the final cycle because track position mattered more than outright grip. That call put the Ain't Dead Yet teammates several seconds ahead of Vaught and left Bittner and Pope to settle the win between themselves. Pope followed the No. 84 to the white flag and looked inside off Turn 2, but Bittner protected the lower lane and won by 0.05 seconds, with Vaught third. Bittner later credited both the aggressive tire call and the teammates' agreement to push whichever truck was leading until it was time to race.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1385,"title":"Pope leads Las Vegas to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Tim Pope clears Dustin Wade with drafting help from Albert Anderson as the 36-truck field begins the 133-lap race.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-wade","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1418,"title":"Opening-lap stack-up brings the yellow","summary":"Kyle Vaught drops to the apron and checks up, and the ensuing chain reaction spins Zachary Henin after contact from Nick Ramsey while several trucks scatter toward pit entry.","tags":["kyle-vaught","zachary-henin","nick-ramsey","ricky-whittenburg","shawn-mcdonald","jacob-young"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2106,"title":"Anderson takes command","summary":"After a sustained multi-lane run, Anderson moves the No. 99 to the front while the field remains tightly grouped behind him.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2281,"title":"Mayberry and Vaught trigger the second crash","summary":"Mayberry hooks Kyle Vaught from the outside lane, and the spinning truck collects Andrew Player while Whittenburg and Jorge Rincon crash while checking up.","tags":["dave-mayberry","kyle-vaught","andrew-player","ricky-whittenburg","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2407,"title":"Caution pits split tire strategies","summary":"Jeremiah Burke takes only fuel, Jonathan Osborne and John Curtis use splash-and-go stops, and much of the field chooses full service under yellow.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","john-curtis","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3634,"title":"Green-flag pit entry erupts in chaos","summary":"A large group converges on the curved pit entrance; Larry Dickerson hits Trevor Robertson while avoiding trouble, Jack Dixon receives a black flag and Burke contacts Dickerson in his stall.","tags":["larry-dickerson","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"pit_road_incident"},{"t":3710,"title":"Bittner, Pope and Vaught break away","summary":"Once the first green-flag cycle settles, Bittner leads Pope and Vaught in a three-truck draft with Anderson isolated several seconds behind.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4549,"title":"Bittner initiates another pit cycle","summary":"Bittner makes a clean green-flag entry before Pope, Vaught, Anderson and the rest of the contenders work through their scheduled stops.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":5375,"title":"Bittner commits to the winning tire call","summary":"Bittner and Vaught pit early in the final cycle, and Bittner's two-tire service creates the track-position advantage that Vaught later identifies as the winning strategy.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5817,"title":"Team Ain't Dead Yet controls the closing run","summary":"With six laps left, teammates Bittner and Pope run nose to tail roughly four seconds ahead of Vaught and prepare to settle the win between themselves.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6073,"title":"Pope lines up a final-lap attack","summary":"Pope follows Bittner to the white flag, then looks inside off turn two as Bittner drops low to protect his momentum.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":6109,"title":"Bittner wins the Jackpot 200","summary":"Bittner's defensive move holds off Pope by 0.05 seconds, while Vaught reaches the final podium position in third.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6109,"quote":"The move will not be in time—84 of Josh Bittner, your race winner!","context":"The live call as Bittner holds off Pope at the stripe.","gold":5},{"t":6468,"quote":"Josh had the winning strategy call of two tires only on that last stop.","context":"Third-place Vaught identifies the decision that separated Bittner from the other leaders.","gold":5},{"t":6719,"quote":"Team Ain't Dead Yet, y'all got a lot of talent.","context":"Pope reacts after finishing second to teammate Bittner.","gold":2},{"t":6837,"quote":"I'm a fish out of water here. I feel like most of my wins come on the East Coast.","context":"Bittner jokes about winning in Las Vegas during his victory interview.","gold":5},{"t":6861,"quote":"It was all about track position, track position, track position, so I decided to go for it.","context":"Bittner explains the reasoning behind his aggressive strategy.","gold":5},{"t":6935,"quote":"The biggest challenge at times was honestly just trying to gauge the pit stops right.","context":"Bittner describes balancing short-pitting against the length of the following fuel run.","gold":5},{"t":7016,"quote":"We committed to helping each other out—whoever was behind the other, just pushing and keeping the faith.","context":"Bittner credits Pope and their team-first drafting approach.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Bittner, Pope and Vaught as the podium, with a 0.05-second winning margin. The spoken grid identifies 36 racers; Lori Vaught appears after the results as race control and is not included as a participant. The transcript explicitly calls two yellow-flag incidents, although Vaught later describes the race as having only one caution; the recap follows the contemporaneous race calls. Andrew Coffin is the No. 10 driver captioned as Andrew C/Cin and remains distinct from Andrew Player.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"HvwQeicZqhk":{"recap":"Ricky Whittenburg earned his first VRL victory by turning a damaged Homestead race into a lap-by-lap fuel calculation. Tim Pope controlled the opening stage, but a frontstretch Big One gave Whittenburg an unintended strategic reset: he used a fast repair, stayed on the lead lap and topped off repeatedly while the field circulated under caution. When the conventional contenders stopped again under green, Whittenburg and Andrew Player committed to stretching fuel from the mid-60s to the 100-lap finish. The gamble did not become safe simply because they stayed out. Dave Mayberry ran short, then Jonathan Osborne ran short, leaving Whittenburg to nurse the final corners with the tank nearly empty. He crossed the line ahead of Player and Pope and ran dry only after taking the checkered flag. In the winner interview, Whittenburg explains the lap-65 calculation and the emotion of finally winning in VRL. The wreck created the opportunity, but the repeated top-offs and disciplined mileage run converted it.","winner":"Ricky Whittenburg","podium":["Ricky Whittenburg","Andrew Player","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1576,"title":"Pope starts the playoff opener in front","summary":"Tim Pope launches from pole and takes the early lead, with teammate Jeremiah Burke moving into second behind him.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2604,"title":"First green-flag pit cycle opens","summary":"The field begins scheduled stops around lap 30 after Pope controls the long opening run, with the difficult Homestead entry immediately becoming a factor.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":2673,"title":"Emig spins on pit entry","summary":"David Emig checks up sharply while trying to make the tight left turn onto pit road and spins, losing ground without bringing out a caution.","tags":["david-emig"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3314,"title":"Pope wins the opening stage","summary":"The scheduled halfway yellow freezes Pope ahead of Burke, Vaught, Mike Adamson and Kelly Kuehl, with ten drivers earning stage points.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","mike-adamson","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":3425,"title":"Pit-lane contact spins Reeves","summary":"During the stage stops, Emig contacts Austin Reeves and spins him in the crowded lane before Reeves backs into Dustyn Eaton while trying to recover.","tags":["david-emig","austin-reeves","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"pit_road_incident"},{"t":3703,"title":"Wade spins after the stage restart","summary":"Dustin Wade loses control in turns one and two and makes contact with David Kelly, bringing the field back under caution.","tags":["dustin-wade","david-kelly","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":4073,"title":"Frontstretch big one changes the race","summary":"Josh Oxendine gives Whittenburg a bump that starts a large pileup, producing six meatball flags and collecting Andrew Coffin, Matt Beamer, Chandler Paul, Robert Jordan, Osborne and Anderson.","tags":["josh-oxendine","ricky-whittenburg","andrew-cauthan","matt-beamer","chandler-paul","robert-jordan","jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4291,"title":"Whittenburg commits to fuel mileage","summary":"After using his fast repair, Whittenburg tops off again under yellow and realizes he may be able to reach the finish by saving fuel while the leaders still need another stop.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4554,"title":"Pope takes the lead from Burke","summary":"Pope works past teammate Burke during the final green run as the conventional-strategy contenders try to build enough speed for their last stops.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":4791,"title":"Final stops separate the strategies","summary":"Robertson and Dixon begin the final green-flag cycle, while Vaught and Kuehl make costly pit-entry mistakes and Whittenburg, Player, Mayberry and Osborne stay out.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jack-dixon","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player","dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5491,"title":"Mayberry and Osborne run short","summary":"Mayberry pits with only a few laps remaining and Osborne begins sputtering soon afterward, allowing Whittenburg to inherit the lead with Player close behind.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne","ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5558,"title":"Whittenburg wins on fumes","summary":"Whittenburg reaches the checkered flag before running out of fuel moments later, earning his first VRL win over Player and Pope.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5558,"quote":"Ricky Whittenburg gets a win in the Vigilante Racing League!","context":"The live call as Whittenburg completes the fuel-mileage upset.","gold":5},{"t":5814,"quote":"If we could make it to like 65 on a caution and then pedal it, there's an outside chance we could make it on gas.","context":"Whittenburg explains the calculation he made after the late wreck.","gold":5},{"t":5836,"quote":"I just kept coming back in and topping off, and it just kind of all fell into place for once.","context":"Whittenburg describes how the caution period enabled the winning strategy.","gold":5},{"t":5868,"quote":"My only shot was trying to get them on strategy, and for once the calculator in my brain actually matched what was happening on the track.","context":"Whittenburg acknowledges that he could not beat the fastest trucks on outright pace.","gold":5},{"t":5960,"quote":"I'm really, really excited that I finally got a win here in the VRL.","context":"Whittenburg celebrates his long-awaited first league victory.","gold":5},{"t":6133,"quote":"She started spitting and sputtering coming across the finish line again on me, but I had just enough.","context":"Runner-up Player explains how close his own fuel gamble came to failing.","gold":5},{"t":6437,"quote":"It was a mistake—good for me that I came into this with a little bit of a cushion.","context":"Vaught reflects on his pit-entry error and seventh-place recovery.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish call, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Whittenburg, Player and Pope as the podium. The spoken grid and results identify 29 racers. Whittenburg ran out of fuel immediately after the finish and received a push on the cooldown lap; Player reported sputtering at the stripe. Andrew Coffin is the No. 10 driver and remains distinct from Andrew Player.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hw_GkN1awHo":{"recap":"The VRL Bristol 200 put 25 Xfinity cars through a 200-lap short-track survival test with 40% fuel tanks, five tire sets, two fast repairs, and a 32-incident-point limit. Championship leader Alan Vaught led early, but an early caution and the long, split pit road trapped him laps down while Jim Ott's decision to pit positioned Ott to take control. Multiple pileups, lapped traffic, and sharply different tire strategies reduced the lead-lap field to only a handful of cars, yet Ott repeatedly rebuilt his lead after restarts. Ott took fresh tires with roughly 25 laps left, quickly passed Greg Klein, and won over Tim Pope and Russ Kilgore; Jonathan Osborne was later disqualified on incident points.","winner":"Jim Ott","podium":["Jim Ott","Tim Pope","Russ Kilgore"],"moments":[{"t":1408,"title":"Vaught and Ott launch the Bristol 200","summary":"Championship rivals Alan Vaught and Jim Ott lead the 25-car field to green for 200 laps under the Bristol lights.","tags":["jess-vaught","jim-ott"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1898,"title":"Kilgore's wall bounce triggers the first caution","summary":"Russ Kilgore ricochets from the outside wall into Greg Klein and then pounds the inside wall, with Osborne arriving too fast to avoid the scene.","tags":["russ-kilgore","greg-cline","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1987,"title":"Ott takes the pivotal early service","summary":"Ott leaves Vaught's bumper under the first caution and takes full service on Bristol's long split pit road, a call he later says dictated the race.","tags":["jim-ott","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2286,"title":"Ott charges through to the lead","summary":"On fresher tires, Ott races past Burke, Vaught, and Adamson and takes first for the first time.","tags":["jim-ott","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":2807,"title":"Pope's wall contact ignites a multi-car crash","summary":"Ott runs into lapped traffic and contact sends Tim Pope toward the wall, scattering Vaught, Chandler Paul, Jason Airson, and others before the yellow.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","chandler-paul","jason-airson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3081,"title":"The field falls like bowling pins","summary":"A restart crash high on the banking sweeps down across the track and collects Anderson, Whittenburg, Pope, Burke, Evans, Dixon, and others.","tags":["albert-anderson","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","earl-evans","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4179,"title":"Ottinger's crash triggers a chain reaction","summary":"Jeff Ottinger hooks Andrew Coffin, blocks the high lane, and sets off a crash involving Rincon, Kuehl, Mayberry, Vaught, and Greg Dobson.","tags":["jeff-ottinger","andrew-cauthan","george-rincon","kelly-keel","dave-mayberry","jess-vaught","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4456,"title":"A light tap creates two wrecks on the backstretch","summary":"Mayberry and Rincon touch at the restart and the ensuing crash multiplies down the backstretch, collecting Burke, Tony Polk, Osborne, Jones, Coffin, Ottinger, and Whittenburg.","tags":["dave-mayberry","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke","tony-polk","jonathan-osborne","dion-jones","andrew-cauthan","jeff-ottinger","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4853,"title":"Osborne and lapped traffic bring out the late yellow","summary":"Osborne arrives quickly on Earl Evans, reacts when a blinking Austin Paul appears, loses control, and collects several cars with about 25 laps remaining.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","earl-evans","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4958,"title":"Ott gives up the lead for fresh tires","summary":"Ott pits under the late caution for his final tire set while Klein and Mayberry stay out, betting that the speed differential will outweigh track position.","tags":["jim-ott","greg-cline","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5108,"title":"Ott clears Klein and controls the sprint","summary":"Ott uses the fresher rubber to pass Klein on the inside and pulls away while Pope and Kilgore fight forward behind him.","tags":["jim-ott","greg-cline","timothy-pope","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5468,"title":"Ott wins under the Bristol lights","summary":"Ott reaches the white flag before another caution can fly and beats Pope and Kilgore to the checkered flag; Klein holds fourth over Dobson.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","russ-kilgore","greg-cline","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":947,"quote":"The key to the race... is to survive.","context":"The booth's concise pre-race prescription for 200 laps at Bristol","gold":3},{"t":3119,"quote":"It was almost like bowling pins, you know, just all the way down there was nowhere to go.","context":"The booth describes the restart crash sweeping down Bristol's banking","gold":4},{"t":3721,"quote":"Everybody finding themselves right around the same spot on track... just in a big ball of absolute chaos.","context":"The booth describes lapped cars and leaders converging in the second half","gold":4},{"t":5614,"quote":"I caused the first one, bounced off the wall and came down on somebody, and that was all my fault.","context":"Third-place finisher Russ Kilgore owns his early crash","gold":4},{"t":5951,"quote":"I didn't think I was ever going to get back up there... about 125 into the race I finally found a groove and let her loose.","context":"Runner-up Tim Pope explains his 13-position climb","gold":4},{"t":5961,"quote":"My mistake was not pitting on that first caution around lap 30.","context":"Alan Vaught identifies the strategy error that derailed his race","gold":3},{"t":6004,"quote":"Every time you plan for something, your plan goes out the window a few laps later.","context":"The booth sums up Bristol strategy after Vaught's recovery to ninth","gold":4},{"t":6151,"quote":"That kind of dictated the race, I guess, tonight... having track position after that was huge for me.","context":"Winner Jim Ott reflects on his first-caution pit call","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"This 2022 Bristol broadcast is not present in seasons_map.json, so no season or round is asserted. The finish call and full results readout explicitly establish Ott, Pope, and Kilgore as the podium. Jonathan Osborne was explicitly disqualified for reaching the incident limit but was still classified 19th; Jorge Rincon served an unidentified black flag and was not said to be disqualified. The exact initial trigger in the 46:47 crash is difficult to read from captions, so the recap follows only the names and mechanics the booth states. Transcript timestamps end at 1:50:44 (6644 seconds), within the 6645-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hwN8xOLP9M4":{"recap":"Race #10 of Vigilante Racing League Season 11 brought the field to virtual Talladega Superspeedway for 80 laps of three-wide pack racing on the Track Limits Network. Albert Anderson put the 99 on the pole at 54.843 but jumped the start and had to serve a pass-through penalty, dropping him deep in the field. The night's wildest sequence came on lap 17, when Greg Dobson's engine let go in the draft and Kevin Hunt barrel-rolled through the tri-oval, landing on all fours and driving away before the caution ever flew. After a second caution for Chandler Paul's spin and a late round of fuel-only green-flag stops, the race came down to a three-wide drag to the stripe, where a monster push from Dillon Bryant shot Anderson down the outside lane to steal the win. Bryant settled for second with Kelly Kuehl third, giving Anderson his second victory of the season.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Dillon Bryant","Kelly Kuehl"],"moments":[{"t":2096,"title":"Polesitter black-flagged on lap 1","summary":"Albert Anderson jumps the start from the pole and has to serve a pass-through penalty along with several other drivers, sending the fastest qualifier to the tail of the field.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2704,"title":"Kevin Hunt barrel-rolls through the tri-oval","summary":"Dobson's blown engine stacks up the pack and Kevin Hunt gets flipped onto his lid through the tri-oval, rolling big time before landing on all fours and driving away — with no immediate caution, to the booth's disbelief.","tags":["kevin-hunt","greg-dobson","derek-welch"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2793,"title":"Dobson grenades the motor","summary":"Replay and onboard confirm Greg Dobson's engine let go while running nose-to-tail in the draft — he later reported 292-degree oil temp when it grenaded — triggering the melee, with the caution only flying once Hunt stopped on the apron.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3866,"title":"Pope shoves Anderson around the top lane","summary":"Tim Pope gets all over Albert Anderson 'like a cheap suit,' trading paint down the back straightaway with aggressive bumper-to-bumper pushing while managing his engine temps.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4091,"title":"Chandler Paul spins to bring out caution two","summary":"Just as green-flag pit stops were about to open, Chandler Paul goes around after contact in traffic — Burke and Paul got together and Dixon clipped him — bunching the field back up under yellow.","tags":["chandler-paul","jack-dixon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4472,"title":"Halfway restart at lap 40","summary":"Cool and Anderson bring the field to the Geico restart zone at halfway; Cool jumps out and Dillon Bryant dives into the gap with barely room to spare.","tags":["kelly-keel","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4917,"title":"Four wide through the tri-oval","summary":"Lap trucks hold the top and the pack fans out four wide for a moment through the tri-oval, barely getting clear before turn three.","tags":["chandler-paul","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6049,"title":"Goodenough finds the wall with 13 to go","summary":"Contender Craig Goodenough takes damage off the wall, drops into the grass at the bottom of the racetrack, and has to tow, ending his run at the front.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6205,"title":"Pope bounces off the SAFER and keeps digging","summary":"In the closing laps Tim Pope smacks the SAFER barrier, keeps it out of traffic, keeps his foot down, and stays tucked in behind Albert Anderson with eight to go.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6575,"title":"Three-wide at the stripe — Anderson steals it","summary":"On the final lap Kelly Kuehl gets pushed to the lead, the field comes off turn four three wide, and a huge shove from Dillon Bryant — every gauge on his dash pegged red — rockets Albert Anderson down the outside lane to win it at the stripe.","tags":["albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","derek-welch"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6673,"title":"Victory burnout: he's going to light them up","summary":"Bucking the VRL tradition of parking quietly at start-finish, Anderson lights up the tires in celebration after driving from a lap-1 penalty back to the win.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2714,"quote":"Big time truck Kevin Hunt on his lid into the trioval... he's rolling big time and gets back on all fours. And how did the caution not come out for that?","context":"Kevin Hunt flips through the tri-oval and drives away with no yellow","gold":5},{"t":3022,"quote":"If there's somebody flying through the air and you're not an airport, that's a problem.","context":"the booth roasting iRacing for not throwing a caution during Hunt's flip","gold":5},{"t":3064,"quote":"I don't know, I just work here. That's right, we're just here so we don't get fined.","context":"Steve and Chris shrugging off iRacing's caution algorithm","gold":3},{"t":3866,"quote":"He is all over Albert Anderson like a cheap suit right now.","context":"Tim Pope's relentless pushing of Anderson down the back straightaway","gold":4},{"t":4278,"quote":"It's Tallaladega — you can go from first to 15th or 15th to first in a lap and a half.","context":"Chris Goans on why late tire stops cost nothing at this track","gold":3},{"t":5328,"quote":"He can't slide a piece of paper between the nose of his truck and Kyle Vaugh right now.","context":"Goodenough glued to Kyle's tailgate in the draft","gold":3},{"t":6589,"quote":"Who is going to win it at the stripe? It's Albert Anderson. Wow. Outside lane did it. I don't know how, but they did it.","context":"the three-wide finish call as Anderson steals the win","gold":4},{"t":6673,"quote":"Albert doesn't care. He's just going to light them up.","context":"Anderson's victory burnout on the frontstretch","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Family surname for Alan and Kyle (and league admin Lori) is heavily garbled in captions ('VA', 'Vault', 'Vaugh', 'Ba', 'Bot', 'Font') — 'Vaught' is a best guess, unconfirmed. 'Craig Goodenough', 'Andrew Cowan', 'Jorge Rincon', and 'David Feit' are best-guess normalizations of garbled captions. David Feit (35th) apparently never took the green flag per the booth (scored 80 laps down). Two cautions total: lap 17 (Dobson engine / Hunt flip) and roughly lap 36 (Chandler Paul spin). The segment around 1:54:53-1:56:25 is a Track Limits promo reel of unrelated racing (names like Lockwood, Quinn, Reynolds, Michigan) aired during a break — those names are excluded. Guest analyst Chris Gones is a driver in the Numb Thumbs league but did not race in this event; a driver 'Skyler' from the previous night's race is mentioned but was not in this field. League admin Lori (Vaught?) runs VRL with Jess; broadcast is on Track Limits Network. Next race: Texas Motor Speedway.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"hzIlPjKL_Rc":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League trucks hit the one-mile Phoenix oval for 100 laps in 110-degree track heat, and the 33-truck field ran nearly half the distance caution-free before fuel gambles and admin-thrown yellows flipped the script. Polesitter Trevor Robertson controlled the early going and set the race's fastest lap at 27.50, but Josh Buettner wrestled the lead away on a restart, and the closing 20 laps dissolved into a caution fest headlined by Tim Rivers' airborne flip and a five-wide 'Big One' on a late restart. On the final restart Buettner dove into an inside hole that was not there and took himself out of the lead battle, and Tim Pope slipped under Robertson on the white-flag lap to steal the win in the #728. Ricky Whittenburg, who stretched his fuel to lap 45 and ran dry entering the pits before Kelly Kuehl pushed him into his box, climbed 19 spots to finish third, while John Herzig charged 22 positions to take hard-charger honors in tenth.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":944,"title":"Riding with spotlight driver Jonathan Osborne","summary":"The booth rides onboard with the #81 of Jonathan Osborne, the Vigilante Report spotlight driver of the week — a quadriplegic racing with modified controllers and laying down top-five qualifying times.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1459,"title":"Green flag in the desert","summary":"Polesitter Trevor Robertson and Tyler Green bring the 33-truck field to a clean opening green flag, with three-wide racing through the dogleg within the first laps.","tags":["trevor-robertson","tyler-green"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2223,"title":"Gray saved by Kelly Kuehl's door","summary":"Alexander Gray gets turned sideways mid-pack and saves it by leaning on Kelly Kuehl's door — 'nobody knew Kelly was there with his door to save the day.'","tags":["alexander-gray","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2882,"title":"Ricky runs dry — pushed to his pit box","summary":"Whittenburg stretches his fuel to lap 45-46, runs out of gas entering pit road under the first (admin-thrown) caution, and gets pushed all the way to his stall by Kelly Kuehl — the fuel gamble that sets up his podium.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3214,"title":"Turn-4 domino wreck collects Dixon","summary":"On the restart Kelly Kuehl comes off the turn-four wall, bounces into the #07 of Jack Dixon, who gets turned into the #4 — a domino effect wreck that brings out the yellow.","tags":["jack-dixon","kelly-keel","alexander-gray"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3789,"title":"Buettner takes the lead from Robertson","summary":"Josh Buettner rides the outside line on a restart, noses ahead down the front straightaway, and takes the lead away from the #6 of Trevor Robertson.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4105,"title":"Rocket Man: Tim Rivers goes airborne","summary":"The #46 Georgia Bulldogs truck hits the fence and slings backwards, upside down and into the air — 'straight off into space.' The booth replays it from Kelly Kuehl's cockpit and christens Rivers 'Rocket Man' before his team disconnects with about 20 to go.","tags":["tim-rivers","brian-jablonski"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4330,"title":"Prestige Worldwide in the booth","summary":"The booth riffs on broadcasting across Twitch, YouTube and Facebook — 'we're basically Prestige Worldwide' — capped with the liquid-paper-on-a-bee joke.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4414,"title":"Five wide into the Big One","summary":"The field fans out five wide on a restart and it erupts — the #33 goes into the fence, the 00 gets turned through no fault of his own, and the booth calls it: 'that's the Big One, boys!'","tags":["jess-vaught","jacob-schaffet","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4989,"title":"Late pileup: 999, Kelly Kuehl and Oxendine","summary":"Jonathan Osborne gets spun and damaged, then the #999, Kelly Kuehl and the #63 of Oxendine wreck hard when they run out of racing room — Cool angrily crab-walks down pit road and takes out a pit cone.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jeff-snyder","kelly-keel","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5271,"title":"GWC attempt ends on the backstretch","summary":"The first crack at a green-white-checker lasts seconds — the 33 gets back into the 27 coming onto the backstretch, collecting a couple of other trucks and forcing one final attempt.","tags":["bradley-wright","jess-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5528,"title":"Pope steals it on the final lap","summary":"On the one-and-only green-white-checker, Buettner dives inside into a truck that's still there and wrecks out of contention, carnage erupts behind, and admin Lori Vaught lets them race to the flag — Tim Pope sneaks under Trevor Robertson on the white-flag lap to win, with Whittenburg sliding up to third.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1392,"quote":"It's always a good time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet, and throw inhibition out that window.","context":"hyping the field just before the green flag","gold":3},{"t":1837,"quote":"Double zero looks like he backed into one of those parking bollards in the parking lot of 7-Eleven or something on his way to the track.","context":"Jacob Chaffet's bashed-in truck after early contact","gold":3},{"t":4232,"quote":"All you can see is Tim Rivers just go straight off into space.","context":"replaying the #46's airborne flip","gold":4},{"t":4255,"quote":"A new nickname for Mr. Tim Rivers, and that will be Rocket Man.","context":"christening Rivers after his truck went airborne","gold":3},{"t":4330,"quote":"We have so many platforms, I mean we're basically Prestige Worldwide... I put liquid paper on a bee this morning and it died.","context":"booth riffing on streaming to Twitch, YouTube and Facebook at once","gold":4},{"t":4426,"quote":"Oh, that's the big one, boys! Oh, this is the big one! Oh my god, get your brakes, boys!","context":"five-wide restart erupts into the race's biggest pileup","gold":5},{"t":5607,"quote":"Look at Ricky Wittenberg, up 19 — he's gonna have to pay himself, man.","context":"the league's own sponsor finishes third in the money race","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Broadcast opens with ~9 minutes of music; the booth comes on at 10:06. Winner, podium, fastest lap (Trevor Robertson, 27.50, worth the bonus money) and the full 33-truck finishing order are all stated on air, plus winner/P2/P3 interviews. Caption spellings vary wildly — proper spellings uncertain for Jacob Chaffet (chaffett/schaffet/shawfit), Simon Cobrasregis, Kelly Kuehl (possibly Kuehl/Kuehl), Michael Everage (leverage/everedge), John Herzig (herzik), and Alex Forget Berube (the '4j'/'for jay' captions match the French surname Forget). Lori Vaught appears 33rd in the grid rundown but served as race admin, throwing the manual cautions; she is not in the finishing order. Brett Vinson was named super fan of the race. This was the league's second points race of the season (following Miami), broadcast live 2021-09-22/23 on the MDOT channel.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"I365MhkizWg":{"recap":"Jorge Rincon started 31st without qualifying, survived contact with Kyle Vaught and roughly a minute of damage, then let the attrition-heavy Darlington race come back to him. Scott Rooney emerged as the apparent leader after the last green-flag stops, but he could not stretch the fuel to the finish and pitted with two laps remaining. Rincon had saved enough to inherit the lead and take the checkered flag with only 0.3 gallons left. Andy Player also conserved fuel throughout the final run and finished second, while Tim Pope recovered from an early spin and passed the fuel-starved Albert Anderson for third on the final lap.","winner":"Jorge Rincon","podium":["Jorge Rincon","Andrew Player","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":2056,"title":"Pope leads the Darlington start","summary":"Pole-sitter Tim Pope gets the jump over Trevor Robertson as the 35-truck field begins the 204-mile race on cold tires.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2504,"title":"Pope is hit while circulating under yellow","summary":"After Dion Jones and Tom Barish trigger the first caution, Jones makes contact with Pope while trying to catch the field, sending the leader spinning and forcing him into a recovery drive.","tags":["timothy-pope","dion-jones","tom-barish"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3118,"title":"Hunt's slide collects Robertson","summary":"Kevin Hunt gets loose after contact from John Gallagher and slides into Trevor Robertson, leaving Robertson and Gallagher with heavy damage.","tags":["kevin-hunt","john-gallagher","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4775,"title":"Welch and Hunt collide","summary":"Derek Welch hits Kevin Hunt after Hunt scrapes the wall, bringing out another yellow during a sequence complicated by traffic leaving pit lane.","tags":["derek-welch","kevin-hunt","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5184,"title":"Paul and Klein ignite a feud","summary":"Austin Paul turns Greg Klein during green-flag racing, and their dispute escalates into additional contact under the ensuing caution.","tags":["austin-paul","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"conflict"},{"t":6191,"title":"Late chain reaction damages several trucks","summary":"A congested restart erupts around Kelly Kuehl, John Schoenbachler and Kyle Vaught, with Dave Mayberry nearly overturning in the pileup.","tags":["kelly-keel","john-schoenbachler","kyle-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6770,"title":"Fuel mileage defines the final run","summary":"The booth identifies Rooney, Rincon, Player and Schoenbachler among the drivers trying to reach the finish after their lap-109 stops, turning the closing laps into a fuel-saving contest.","tags":["scott-rooney","george-rincon","andrew-player","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7283,"title":"Rooney takes the lead","summary":"Dillon Bryant makes his last stop, elevating Rooney to the lead by nearly five seconds over Rincon as the fuel question intensifies.","tags":["scott-rooney","dylan-bryant","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":7570,"title":"Rooney must pit for fuel","summary":"With Rincon rapidly closing, Rooney concedes that he cannot make the distance and dives to pit road, handing the race to the No. 28.","tags":["scott-rooney","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7662,"title":"Rincon saves enough to win","summary":"Rincon takes the checkered flag, Player follows in second, and Pope passes Anderson for third when Anderson runs out of fuel after crossing the line in fourth.","tags":["george-rincon","andrew-player","timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7487,"quote":"You couldn't drive a thimble up his ass with a sledgehammer right now.","context":"The booth describes Rooney's intense focus while he tries to protect the lead.","gold":5},{"t":7662,"quote":"There he goes. Takes the checkered flag. Your winner tonight, George Rincon.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":2},{"t":8039,"quote":"Beginning, middle, and end of the last run.","context":"Player answers how long he had been saving fuel.","gold":5},{"t":8295,"quote":"I had point three, so I made it.","context":"Rincon reveals how little fuel remained after he parked in his pit stall.","gold":5},{"t":8349,"quote":"I have no idea how I won that. The track won me this. I didn't win this race.","context":"Rincon reacts to winning at a circuit where he did not consider himself fast.","gold":5},{"t":8491,"quote":"If I'm going to cross the line, just barely make it, they're not going to make it.","context":"Rincon explains why the pace of Anderson and Rooney convinced him their fuel would not last.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish and all three podium interviews explicitly confirm Rincon, Player and Pope. The broadcast reports eight cautions. Rincon said he skipped qualifying, started at the back, repaired about a minute of damage after tangling with Kyle Vaught, and finished with 0.3 gallons. Player said he saved fuel for the entire final run; Pope recovered after being spun while looking at his phone to calculate tire usage. The 35-driver field comes from the complete spoken grid. Caption variants 'Alan Vault' and 'Ricky Whittenberg' are normalized to Alan Vaught and Ricky Whittenburg; 'Andrew Cawin' is retained as a caption spelling of roster entry Andrew Coffin, and Dustyn Eaton remains a distinct driver.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"i4uEkw2DPKA":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson won the inaugural-season Texas round after conserving his tires in Tim Pope's draft and making the decisive pass with about 14 laps remaining. Polesitter Alex Berube led early but spun from first without drawing a yellow, while crashes involving Russ Kilgore on lap one, Tim Rivers and Alan Vaught, and a three-wide backstretch incident repeatedly reshuffled the field before the scheduled lap-58 competition caution. Pope controlled much of the middle and late race, but Robertson's patient long-run approach gave him the grip to take command and edge away. A four-laps-to-go incident involving Berube, Brian Jablonski and Michael Everage stayed green, and lap traffic helped Mike Adamson slip past Pope in the final corner for second. Robertson won ahead of Adamson and Pope, with Vaught and Josh Bittner completing the top five.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Mike Adamson","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1321,"title":"Berube leads 33 trucks to green","summary":"Alex Berube launches from pole ahead of Jeremiah Burke as the 100-lap Texas race begins with 33 starters.","tags":["alex-berube","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1375,"title":"Kilgore cartwheels on lap one","summary":"Russ Kilgore gets loose off turn two and tumbles through a track-blocking opening-lap crash that also spins Michael Everage and catches Dion Jones.","tags":["russ-kilgore","mike-everage","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1635,"title":"Berube controls the first restart","summary":"Berube gets another strong launch while Robertson clears Burke and Josh Oxendine advances into the top three.","tags":["alex-berube","trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2303,"title":"Leader Berube spins without a yellow","summary":"Berube loses the truck from the lead and slides to the apron; the field avoids him closely enough for the race to remain green.","tags":["alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2428,"title":"Frontstretch pileup follows three-wide battle","summary":"Tim Rivers loses control after contact while racing three wide, sending Alan Vaught into the wall and collecting Albert Anderson; John Osborne and Kelly Kuehl are also caught in the ensuing crash.","tags":["tim-rivers","jess-vaught","albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2932,"title":"Three-wide move triggers another caution","summary":"A backstretch incident involving Albert Anderson and Austin Paul also sweeps up Rob Green and Tim Rivers shortly before the competition-caution window opens.","tags":["albert-anderson","austin-paul","rob-green","tim-rivers"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3274,"title":"Pope leads the lap-44 restart","summary":"Tim Pope clears Jeremiah Burke from the inside as Mike Adamson and Trevor Robertson contest third behind them.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3750,"title":"Competition caution flies on lap 58","summary":"Race control throws the predetermined halfway yellow at lap 58, and the leaders pit for enough fuel and tires to reach the finish.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4142,"title":"Mayberry crash halts the restart","summary":"Dave Mayberry gets loose off turn two just after the green, leaving Eric Klafka and John Herzig nowhere to go and bringing out another yellow.","tags":["dave-mayberry","eric-klafka","john-herzig"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4872,"title":"Robertson tests Pope for the lead","summary":"Robertson briefly edges ahead on the inside with roughly 20 laps left, but Pope crosses back underneath and retakes the position.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5059,"title":"Robertson makes the winning pass","summary":"With 14 laps remaining, Robertson attacks Pope again into turn one and this time completes the pass, converting his better-preserved tires into the lead.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5503,"title":"Robertson wins as Adamson steals second","summary":"Robertson takes the checkered flag while lap traffic delays Pope; Adamson dives past in the final corner to claim second and leaves Pope third.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5865,"quote":"I just drove it in too hard on that last turn, and it wanted to come around with me.","context":"Tim Pope explains how Mike Adamson took second at the finish","gold":4},{"t":5901,"quote":"Yeah, because I was kind of waiting to see if they were going to throw it or not.","context":"Pope says the competition caution affected his pit timing","gold":3},{"t":5956,"quote":"It was a handful tonight. Had a couple close calls, but just stayed on top of it.","context":"Mike Adamson describes his steady drive to second","gold":4},{"t":5991,"quote":"It's a roll of the dice, so you try to make a plan, but usually you have to go with a Plan B because Plan A usually gets wrecked.","context":"Adamson previews the following week's Talladega race","gold":4},{"t":6080,"quote":"Tim Pope and Burke and all of them were extremely fast there.","context":"Trevor Robertson credits his principal rivals","gold":3},{"t":6091,"quote":"I think I had the advantage sitting in the draft because in three and four I didn't have to keep it full throttle like the guy in front would have, and it saved those extra few percent that I needed to get by them at the","context":"Robertson explains the tire conservation behind his winning pass","gold":5},{"t":6202,"quote":"Jack Dixon and Josh Oxendine and I had a really long practice session last night, so it definitely helped.","context":"Robertson credits his pre-race preparation","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 1, round 5 at Texas per seasons_map.json. The full 33-truck finishing order was read on air. Trevor Robertson, Mike Adamson and Tim Pope were explicitly confirmed as the podium. The race had a scheduled competition caution on lap 58 plus several incident cautions; Berube's first spin from the lead and the late Berube-Jablonski-Everage crash both stayed green. Jeff Snyder won the rerolled $5 random-driver spotlight after the initial selection, Tim Rivers, was unavailable in Discord. The roster's canonical spellings Alex Berube, Jacob Schaffet, Simon Sriegis and John Herzig are used despite heavily garbled captions and alternate grid pronunciations. The transcript identifies Michael Everage as an innocent bystander in the late incident but does not clearly name every secondary participant in the earlier wrecks.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"iAEAsrdikL4":{"recap":"This VOD picks up the 2022 Vigilante All-Star Race at Talladega with nine laps to go after a technical outage, and those laps packed in a season's worth of chaos. The Big One erupted almost immediately — the 222 appearing to drift down and hook Alan Vaught's 33, sweeping up the lime-green Limitless cars — and Dion Jones's flip on the penultimate lap forced a single-attempt green-white-checkered. When the leaders wrecked again crossing the line at the white flag, Austin Paul briefly inherited the point, but Greg Dobson threaded the carnage as teammate Jeremiah Burke pushed him clear and then threw the block on Russ Endicott's outside charge. Dobson — the 285, the 'friendly Canadian' who was the last car in on speed out of Monday's qualifier — grabbed his first Vigilante win, with Burke second and hard charger Endicott completing the podium from 15 spots back. Limitless rolled home first, second and fifth on a night the booth called one of the most exciting finishes of the season.","winner":"Greg Dobson","podium":["Greg Dobson","Jeremiah Burke","Russ Endicott"],"moments":[{"t":27,"title":"McCabe's lone-wolf wild ride","summary":"Moments after the broadcast rejoins with nine to go, Chad McCabe spins solo — a lone car, so the race stays green.","tags":["chad-mccabe"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":64,"title":"The Big One kicks off in turn one","summary":"Three-wide beating and banging turns to chaos as the 222 appears to drift down and hook Alan Vaught's 33 — the lime-green Limitless cars get swept up, David Feit's 221 goes for a wild ride and Jeremiah Burke tumbles.","tags":["chandler-paul","jess-vaught","david-fite","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":163,"title":"The thesaurus bit","summary":"Under caution the booth breaks out a prepared groaner — shocked, appalled, aghast, dismayed, stunned AND astonished — and it earns a C-plus for effort from the co-commentator.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":310,"title":"Kilgore's plumbing emergency","summary":"Did Russ Kilgore disconnect? No — he'd warned he needed the restroom if another caution flew, sending the booth into old-man plumbing, diaper and free-sample-catheter riffs.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":495,"title":"Limitless stacks both lanes","summary":"Back to green with seven to go and Limitless teammates Tim Pope and Mike Adamson controlling both lanes, with Chandler Paul and Tony Polk in the hunt.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","chandler-paul","tony-polk"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":523,"title":"Klein surfs the train to the lead","summary":"Greg Klein reads the outside rally train perfectly, jumps aboard with Jonathan Osborne pushing and takes his first lead of the night — smooth as ice, per the booth.","tags":["greg-cline","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":793,"title":"Jones flips on the penultimate lap","summary":"Contact in the pack sends Dion Jones's 4 onto its roof and into the inside wall, with Dave Mayberry and Chad McCabe involved — the yellow forces a one-attempt green-white-checkered.","tags":["dion-jones","dave-mayberry","chad-mccabe"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1032,"title":"Drinking helmets on: one-shot GWC","summary":"With the sun getting low at lightless Talladega, the field stacks up behind Greg Klein and Alan Vaught for the single attempt at a green-white-checkered finish.","tags":["greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1106,"title":"The leaders wreck at the white flag","summary":"Limitless falls apart off turn four and the leaders crash right at the stripe as the white flag flies — Alan Vaught is collected from the front while Austin Paul inherits the lead and Dobson, Burke and Endicott thread through.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline","austin-paul","greg-dobson","jeremiah-burke","russ-endicott"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1158,"title":"Dobson steals it at the stripe","summary":"Jeremiah Burke shoves teammate Greg Dobson past Austin Paul then throws the block on Russ Endicott's far-outside charge — Dobson wins the drag race to the line for his first Vigilante victory.","tags":["greg-dobson","jeremiah-burke","russ-endicott","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":1436,"title":"Endicott's plus-15 hard charge","summary":"From dead last to third: Russ Endicott credits mentor Albert Anderson's lunchtime pep talk — stop being a pacifist — for a 15-spot climb and 'the funnest race I've had since I've done iRacing.'","tags":["russ-endicott","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":170,"quote":"My wife did accuse me of stealing her thesaurus — and not only was I shocked, I was also appalled, aghast, dismayed, stunned and astonished at her reaction.","context":"killing time in the booth under the Big One caution","gold":4},{"t":265,"quote":"You got to let them men and women do simulation games — this isn't a game, it's a simulation.","context":"blaming summer-break kids for America's internet problems after the stream outage","gold":4},{"t":342,"quote":"These guys, if they don't have a diaper on, they're having to run this thing — free sample catheter from Liberty Medical.","context":"on Russ Kilgore's mid-caution restroom emergency","gold":3},{"t":618,"quote":"Body check there from Mike Adamson up to Jess Vaught — maybe saying hey, get off of my side draft man, that's my air!","context":"contact in the lead draft inside five to go","gold":3},{"t":769,"quote":"They're not even caring about the line — they're just kind of Piggly Wiggly all over the place.","context":"the pack going every direction with two laps to go","gold":4},{"t":1037,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet and throw inhibition out the window — it's time to go racing!","context":"setting up the one-attempt green-white-checkered restart","gold":5},{"t":1163,"quote":"It's gonna be an absolute drag race here — it looks like Greg Dobson though, with the final push from Jeremiah Burke, to come across the line with the win!","context":"the winning call at the checkered flag","gold":4},{"t":1720,"quote":"I saw them all wrecking and I knew I wasn't lifting — I drove it square into the back of somebody, and all of a sudden I was clear and not wrecked.","context":"runner-up Jeremiah Burke describing the white-flag wreck in his interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"VOD covers only the final ~9 laps plus interviews (title: 'Allstar race ending'); the stream rejoined after a technical outage, so stage racing is off-tape — Mayberry thought Alan Vaught took stages 1 and 2 but said he was 'not quite sure.' Caption ambiguity: the closing-lap leader in the 92 is rendered 'Greg Klein'/'Craig Klein' while the winner is consistently 'Greg Dobson' (the 285, 'our friendly Canadian who seems to win the random draw every week'); treated here as two different drivers, but league records should confirm — if they are one person, merge Klein into Dobson. Dobson's car number 285 comes from a single booth line. Low-confidence spellings: David Feit (221, captioned 'David fight'), Mike Everage, Tony Polk. Random draw winner: Dave 'Hot Rod' Mayberry (9th); 'fan of the race' award captioned as Kathleen Anderson. Race was ~2.5 hours total; next event stated as points racing at Indianapolis.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"IaV8Rze1x6U":{"recap":"Josh Bittner used a perfectly executed final pit stop and his last available fast repair to win the 135-lap Homestead-Miami race, his second victory of Season 2. Albert Anderson led much of the race and looked strongest, but he ran out of fuel halfway down pit road during the final stop and lost the lead to Bittner. The race featured long green-flag stretches around one scheduled competition caution and one major restart crash. Bittner pulled nearly five seconds clear, Anderson recovered to second, and Eric Klafka passed John Ellis on the final lap for third.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Albert Anderson","Eric Klafka"],"moments":[{"t":1571,"title":"Pope leads the Homestead start","summary":"Tim Pope starts from pole with Jonathan Osborne outside, while Jack Dixon and Dale Adamson fill the second row for the opening green.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon","dale-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1670,"title":"Early spin stays green","summary":"A single truck slides toward the inside wall and the field takes evasive action, but race control keeps the race green under its multi-car caution policy.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3710,"title":"Competition caution resets the strategies","summary":"The scheduled lap-60-window yellow brings the leaders to pit road, where Anderson, Ellis and Ottinger emerge as the leading trio while several drivers try two-tire calls.","tags":["albert-anderson","john-ellis","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4085,"title":"Cold tires trigger the Big One","summary":"Jeff Snyder gets loose off Turn 4 immediately after the restart and a pileup catches Russ Endicott, Earl Evans, Justin French and others; Rob Green dodges through the wreck.","tags":["jeff-snyder","russ-endicott","earl-evans","justin-french","rob-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4399,"title":"Anderson and Ellis resume their duel","summary":"Anderson and Ellis restart side by side and remain the central battle as the final long green-flag run begins.","tags":["albert-anderson","john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5461,"title":"Bittner's crew wins the final pit cycle","summary":"Anderson, Bittner and Ellis pit together, but Bittner's stop and fast repair put him ahead while Anderson coasts toward his stall after running out of fuel on pit lane.","tags":["albert-anderson","josh-bittner","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5585,"title":"Bittner assumes control with 30 to go","summary":"Once the cycle completes, Bittner leads Ellis and Anderson; Anderson must spend tire life passing Ellis before he can attempt to chase the leader.","tags":["josh-bittner","john-ellis","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":6204,"title":"Anderson clears Ellis for second","summary":"Anderson and Ellis trade crossovers through both ends of the track before Anderson finally holds second, but their fight lets Bittner escape by more than two seconds.","tags":["albert-anderson","john-ellis","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6589,"title":"Klafka steals the podium on the last lap","summary":"Ellis loses momentum trying one final move on Anderson, allowing Klafka to slip past before the line and take third.","tags":["eric-klafka","john-ellis","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":6620,"title":"Bittner wins by nearly five seconds","summary":"Josh Bittner completes the long final run comfortably ahead of Anderson, with Klafka's last-lap pass deciding third.","tags":["josh-bittner","albert-anderson","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6004,"quote":"I haven't driven that hard in the last stage or that last fuel run probably all season.","context":"Bittner describes the effort required to protect the winning strategy.","gold":5},{"t":6640,"quote":"Dude, the podium was just snatched, stolen from Ellis.","context":"The booth reacts to Klafka's final-lap pass for third.","gold":5},{"t":6860,"quote":"Guys, I can't tell you how much I hate this freaking track.","context":"Runner-up Anderson opens his interview after leading much of the race.","gold":5},{"t":6939,"quote":"I ran out of gas about halfway down pit road, so I had to kind of coast into my pit box.","context":"Anderson explains how Bittner beat him out of the final stop.","gold":5},{"t":7226,"quote":"I knew that I had some extra in the back pocket with that fast repair.","context":"Bittner explains saving his repair for the decisive final stop.","gold":2},{"t":7284,"quote":"I thought I was just a road-course ringer, but a couple of guys had bad luck tonight and I was able to squeeze one through.","context":"Bittner celebrates adding an oval win.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish sequence, Anderson and Bittner interviews, and full rundown explicitly confirm Bittner, Anderson, and Klafka. Klafka was unavailable for an interview. John Ellis was hard charger at plus 19 positions despite losing third on the final lap; Michael Everage won the random draw after finishing ninth. Twenty-five of 28 starters were still classified as finishers. The transcript never clearly identifies the driver in the early single-truck spin at 27:50, so that moment intentionally has an empty driverNames array rather than inventing an attribution.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Ii_8OuxutzI":{"recap":"The Neon Funeral 200 began with Albert Anderson timing the outside launch past pole-sitter Jack Dixon, but Dillon Bryant eventually established the truck everyone had to beat. Las Vegas turned the race into a fuel-and-tire argument: Jacob Alesia and Trevor Robertson survived an extended three-wide knife fight, Jonathan Osborne took fuel only and tried to protect 37-lap-old tires, and Kelly Kuehl kept a hard wall strike from producing the caution strategy gamblers wanted. The early yellows still mattered. Jesse Redding and Kuehl saved their trucks while the pack crashed behind them, then Russ Kilgore and Andrew Coffin met in the middle of the backstretch and drove both leaders to pit road. Bryant, Tim Pope, Alesia, and Chris Goans emerged from the final green-flag cycle as the primary contenders until Mike Adamson's crash with 12 laps left erased every calculation. Bryant controlled the eight-lap restart, Alesia attacked low, and Goans arrived on the best tires. Pope opened a lane with four to go, Craig Goodenough charged into a four-truck, door-banging fight, and Bryant still led into the final corner. Then his fuel disappeared within sight of the flag. Alesia flashed past to win, Goodenough took second, and Goans claimed third in a finish decided by the last usable drops.","winner":"Jacob Alesia","podium":["Jacob Alesia","Craig Goodenough","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":1148,"title":"Anderson ambushes the pole sitter","summary":"Albert Anderson times the opening green from the outside row and immediately clears Jack Dixon, putting the Country Time truck in command.","tags":["albert-anderson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1588,"title":"Kuehl and Reading save it; the pack does not","summary":"Jesse Reading turns down across Kelly Kuehl while reacting to sparks ahead; both leaders catch their trucks, but Greg Dobson and Stony Benfield are swept into the first caution behind them.","tags":["jesse-redding","kelly-keel","greg-dobson","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2000,"title":"Three-wide Vegas knife fight","summary":"Jacob Alesia and Trevor Robertson are trapped in a slicing three-wide battle as the booth repeatedly braces for a wreck that the field somehow avoids.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2412,"title":"Kilgore and Coffin meet in the middle","summary":"Russ Kilgore moves up as Andrew Coffin comes down on the backstretch, sending both trucks hard into the wall and bringing the leaders to pit road.","tags":["russ-kilgore","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2535,"title":"Osborne rolls the dice on ancient tires","summary":"Jonathan Osborne takes fuel only and inherits the lead on 37-lap-old tires, then is swallowed almost immediately while banking on a perfectly timed later caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4696,"title":"Kuehl smokes the wall during the money stop","summary":"As Dillon Bryant begins the final green-flag cycle, Kelly Kuehl pounds the outside wall and nearly spins on the backstretch but keeps the race green.","tags":["kelly-keel","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5409,"title":"Adamson's crash detonates the strategy","summary":"Mike Adamson and the No. 92 come together with 12 laps left, producing the caution that wipes out every fuel-saving calculation and compresses the contenders.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5680,"title":"Eight-lap sprint for the Neon Funeral","summary":"Bryant controls the late restart while Alesia dives underneath and Goans attacks on the best tires, turning the final run into a multi-lane dogfight.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5855,"title":"Pope opens the door; Goodenough comes flying","summary":"Tim Pope gets underneath Bryant with four laps to go, then Goodenough arrives with tremendous speed as the front four bang doors and form a win-or-wreck gaggle.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5952,"title":"Bryant runs dry in the final corner","summary":"Dillon Bryant leads into turns three and four on the last lap but runs out of fuel within sight of the flag; Jacob Alesia flashes past to win, with Goodenough second and Goans third.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","craig-goodenough","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2000,"quote":"They're wrecking. They're going to wreck. They didn't, but man, it was tight.","context":"The field somehow survives a three-wide squeeze","gold":4},{"t":5358,"quote":"I love this kind of stuff. I like this thinking man's kind of race.","context":"The booth enjoys the fuel-saving chess match","gold":4},{"t":5417,"quote":"Oh my goodness. Mike Adamson crashed. This changes everything with 12 laps to go.","context":"The late caution erases every fuel strategy","gold":5},{"t":5924,"quote":"Look at this gaggle for the win.","context":"Four contenders converge with two laps left","gold":4},{"t":5960,"quote":"He's out of gas. He's out of fuel. Oh my God! The 31 brings it home to victory.","context":"Bryant runs dry and Alesia steals the win","gold":5},{"t":6052,"quote":"This is your winning moment: the 31 machine after the 51 runs out of gas on the final turn.","context":"The booth replays the last-corner reversal","gold":5},{"t":6756,"quote":"What a dramatic finish, my guys. I was fourth place on lap 130 and I came away with the win.","context":"Alesia processes the upset in victory lane","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Round 10 of the 2026 VRL Premiere Series at Las Vegas, 133 laps. Winner and podium are explicitly stated and interviewed. The No. 92 involved with Mike Adamson in the lap-121 caution is not identified on the tape, so only Adamson is tagged. Auto-captions alternate Goans/Gones/Gomes and render Alesia several ways; canonical archive spellings are used. Bryant's last-corner fuel failure cut his points lead over Goans from roughly 17 to an unofficial nine with three rounds remaining.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ik8D9Vi_J48":{"recap":"VRL's penultimate race of the season ran 100 laps and 250 miles under the lights at Daytona, with polesitter Albert 'America's Driver' Anderson controlling the first half alongside teammate Mike Adamson and a relentless push from Kelly Kiel. A string of multi-truck wrecks — Dion Jones sailing into the catch fence, and a restart parking-lot pileup triggered when Anderson's push spun Jeremiah Burke — shuffled the field all night. Burke gambled on fuel as the leaders pitted with three laps to go, split the pack three-wide with Russ Kilgore shoving him, and beat Kilgore by a nose in a photo finish while the lapped Ricky Whittenburg punted him across the line. Kilgore charged 29 positions from 31st to second as hard charger of the day, and Alex '4J' Berube climbed back from two laps down to complete the podium in third. Points leader Tim Pope finished 13th and stays atop the standings over Josh Buettner heading into the championship finale at Michigan.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Russ Kilgore","Alex Berube"],"moments":[{"t":2058,"title":"Tyler Greene rockets up the middle","summary":"Tyler Greene catches the 'wind tunnel effect' and blasts through the middle of the pack all alone, ripping off spots up to the third row.","tags":["tyler-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2105,"title":"Three-wide gamble triggers the first Big One","summary":"A three-wide move just 15 laps in sets off two wrecks at once and collects points leader Tim Pope; the booth calls it 'just not a smart move' on the 5.","tags":["tyler-green","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2865,"title":"Robertson turned in the pack","summary":"A push from the triple-nine turns Trevor Robertson's Gorilla Glue truck into the field; some netcode teleporting lets most of the pack drive out clean, but it brings out caution two.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeff-snyder","zach-wheeler"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3700,"title":"Dion Jones goes to space","summary":"Trucks hit the grass, an engine lets go, and Dion Jones launches off Ricky Whittenburg's 55 and up into the catch fence — 'that camera got toasted.'","tags":["dion-jones","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3808,"title":"Wreck on pit road","summary":"Jorge Rincon spins into the pit wall trying to reach his box as Austin Paul's 3 runs down the inside of pit lane under caution.","tags":["austin-paul","george-rincon"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3873,"title":"The mid-race diaper interview","summary":"Race leader Albert Anderson is pulled into the booth mid-race and asked point-blank if he's wearing a diaper like the infamous astronaut: 'Check back with me around lap 75, I might have a pair of Huggies on.'","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5669,"title":"Restart push spins Burke — parking lot at Daytona","summary":"Albert Anderson's bumper push sends Jeremiah Burke around on the restart — an 'absolute parking lot situation' that collects Alan Vaught and sends John Herzig 20 feet into the air.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson","jess-vaught","john-herzig"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6390,"title":"The Big One flies under green","summary":"The predicted one-more-Big-One finally hits with the laps winding down — cars scatter everywhere and the 15 drives backwards through the infield, but the race stays green.","tags":["jeffrey-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7040,"title":"Burke splits them three-wide with Kilgore shoving","summary":"With four to go Jeremiah Burke comes out of nowhere through the middle, Russ Kilgore glued to his bumper, and muscles past Berube and Everedge for the lead — 'what a move.'","tags":["jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore","alex-berube","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7204,"title":"Schoffit's launch — and no caution","summary":"Jacob Schoffit gets a huge run up the middle and wrecks with two to go; Berube gets loose trying to ride it and spins, but race control rolls it green, setting up a two-truck sprint to the flag.","tags":["jacob-schaffet","alex-berube"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7264,"title":"By a nose: Burke over Kilgore","summary":"Jeremiah Burke and Russ Kilgore drag-race side by side to the checkered and Burke wins Daytona by a nose, with Alex Berube straightening out his wrecked truck to salvage third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore","alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8257,"title":"'Ricky punted me across the finish line'","summary":"In the winner's interview Burke reveals the lapped 55 of Ricky Whittenburg shoved him at the line: 'If it wasn't for him, you're talking to Russ Kilgore is the winner.'","tags":["jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":659,"quote":"Somebody's gonna hate somebody by the end of the night, and I can't wait to see who.","context":"Adam Turner previewing 100 laps at Daytona","gold":4},{"t":3607,"quote":"This is the kind of stuff where you go from chump to champ, champ to chump in a matter of seconds.","context":"the booth's signature plate-track catchphrase","gold":4},{"t":3927,"quote":"I'm not wearing diapers tonight, but I could probably use a pair — check back with me around lap 75, I might have a pair of Huggies on.","context":"race leader Albert Anderson, interviewed live from the cockpit","gold":5},{"t":4235,"quote":"Diapers and Adderall — where are we going? That's a t-shirt. Make a t-shirt: diapers and Adderall.","context":"the booth spirals after the astronaut-diaper saga","gold":4},{"t":7271,"quote":"Side by side across the line, and it's gonna be the 753 of Jeremiah Burke by a nose over Russ Kilgore.","context":"the photo-finish call","gold":5},{"t":7353,"quote":"No burnouts when you don't have any gas. Attention, attention: we need a driver to push the leader.","context":"Burke sputters out of fuel right after the checkered","gold":3},{"t":8270,"quote":"I just see Ricky coming in the mirror and I go, I know he's gonna hit me — so I held the wheel and Ricky punted me across the finish line.","context":"winner Jeremiah Burke describing the final push at the line","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names heavily; several surnames are best guesses: 'Dustin Really' is likely Riehle/Riley; 'Jacob Schoffit' appears as schofit/shawfit/shafik/chop it; 'Michael Everedge' appears seven different ways; 'Simon St. Regis' (nicknamed The Cobra) inferred from 'simon the cobras regis'/'simon sregis'. Fan comments reference a driver nicknamed 'Tenderfoot' — likely Albert Anderson given the diaper follow-up, but unconfirmed. Laurie Vaught is the league's lone race admin. Dave Mayberry (league driver) missed the race moving his rig and watched from chat. Broadcast crew is AAA Broadcasting; Alan Coons filled in the prior week but was not on this call. Full finishing order read out starting ~8613s: Burke, Kilgore, Berube, Schoffit, Paul, Riehle, Kiel, Adamson, Anderson, Vaught top ten; Pope 13th, Buettner 16th, Whittenburg 19th (first truck a lap down).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"iKb4bcOVohA":{"recap":"Albert Anderson stuck his #99 Country Time Toyota on the pole (edging Ricky Whittenburg by 0.034 seconds) and dominated the opening half of VRL Season 10's Race #8, a 100-lap truck race at Daytona, leading every lap until the first round of green-flag stops. The race ran remarkably clean until the closing stages, when Jack Dixon's shove put Chris Klein on his roof with 21 to go, and the Big One followed with 14 to go — Kelly Cole washed up into Anderson, launching Craig Goodenough airborne down the backstretch and collecting a third of the field, Anderson included. John Gallagher's overheated engine then grenaded while running second in the push train, forcing a green-white-checkered. Dillon Bryant beat Andrew Player off the overtime restart — Player believed Bryant jumped it — and claimed the win under caution when Dixon spun through the grass on the final lap. Andrew Player and a flu-stricken Russ Kilgore rounded out the podium.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Andrew Player","Russ Kilgore"],"moments":[{"t":1879,"title":"Anderson snatches pole by 0.034","summary":"Albert Anderson's 51.041 knocks Dillon Bryant off the provisional pole late in qualifying; Ricky Whittenburg misses it by 34 thousandths and settles for the outside front row.","tags":["albert-anderson","ricky-whittenburg","dylan-bryant"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2999,"title":"McDonnell's mystery power loss","summary":"Running in the top 10 on lap 16, Sean McDonnell suddenly falls off the pace under restricted power and drops to 34th — the cause is never determined on the broadcast.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3655,"title":"Double-number duel at the stripe","summary":"The 88 of Adamson in the Dale Jr throwback Budweiser scheme and the 99 of Anderson go side by side for the lead — a matter of inches at the line, too close to call.","tags":["mike-adamson","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4216,"title":"Burke checks up, chain reaction crash","summary":"Jeremiah Burke checks up abruptly, Dustin Wade gets into the 53 and triggers a chain-reaction crash that brings out the first caution of the night.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-wade","kevin-hunt","anthony-williams"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4622,"title":"Bryant's power move leaves Anderson out to dry","summary":"Off the restart Bryant drops down in front of Adamson to take the lead; Adamson answers right back and Alan Vos joins in — the booth calls it musical chairs for the race lead.","tags":["dylan-bryant","mike-adamson","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5068,"title":"DW to the point from 23rd","summary":"Derek Welch, who rolled off 23rd, works the draft all the way to the race lead just past halfway.","tags":["derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5525,"title":"Klein through the grass — and it stays green","summary":"An ill-timed push from Adamson sends Chris Klein into the grass flying up the racetrack with trucks scattering everywhere — somehow no caution.","tags":["chris-klein","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5676,"title":"Everage spun entering pit lane","summary":"Greg Dobson drives into the back of Mike Everage on pit entry and sends the 82 spinning into pit road during green-flag stops — still no caution.","tags":["mike-everage","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6286,"title":"Klein on his lid off Dixon's bumper","summary":"Jack Dixon's off-center shove into turn three sends the 18 of Chris Klein up on his lid with a monster impact, collecting multiple trucks with 21 laps to go.","tags":["jack-dixon","chris-klein","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6848,"title":"THE BIG ONE — Goodenough goes airborne","summary":"Kelly Cole gets out of shape into Albert Anderson and Craig Goodenough is launched onto his roof down the backstretch — a third of the field or better is collected with 14 to go, ending dominant Anderson's night.","tags":["albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","derek-welch","dave-mayberry","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7533,"title":"Gallagher's engine grenades in the push train","summary":"Tucked up behind leader Bryant with no air to the radiator, John Gallagher's engine overheats and lets go; he spins from second, McAdam piles in, and a late caution sets up a green-white-checkered.","tags":["john-gallagher","john-mcadam","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7896,"title":"Overtime: Bryant grabs it and wins under yellow","summary":"Bryant beats Andrew Player off the green-white-checkered restart (Player later says he thinks Bryant jumped it), then Jack Dixon spins through the grass on the final lap and the caution freezes the field — Dillon Bryant wins at Daytona.","tags":["dylan-bryant","andrew-player","russ-kilgore","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5014,"quote":"Albert Anderson in the chat says: mighty crowded up front, careful son.","context":"Anderson messaging from the cockpit while leading — he would be wrecked 30 laps later","gold":3},{"t":5176,"quote":"He's known to be a very good restrictor plate racer — or tapered spacer racer, I like it better 'cause it rhymes.","context":"Derek Welch charges toward the race lead","gold":3},{"t":5467,"quote":"I think that was an 'I'm not happy with you' push.","context":"Craig Goodenough gets a shot from Chris Klein in traffic","gold":4},{"t":5535,"quote":"Trucks all over the place, we still don't have a caution — how we got away with that, wow.","context":"Chris Klein flies through the grass mid-pack and everyone escapes","gold":4},{"t":6852,"quote":"Craig Goodenough on his roof going down the backstretch — we got big time trouble!","context":"The Big One erupts with 14 laps to go","gold":5},{"t":7443,"quote":"Oh, don't push the pusher!","context":"McAdam shoving Gallagher, who is shoving leader Bryant","gold":4},{"t":7545,"quote":"Still no caution... up into the banking, still no caution — man, iRacing slacking tonight. Oh, there it is.","context":"Gallagher spins from second with five to go and the flag is late","gold":4},{"t":8709,"quote":"You certainly do sound like garbage, man — we wish you the best.","context":"Interviewing flu-stricken third-place finisher Russ Kilgore","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Solo booth: Steve Singer of Track Limits Network (channel 'tln'); no chapter markers in metadata. Race finished under caution — the green-white-checkered attempt ended when Jack Dixon spun through the grass before the field took the white; Dillon Bryant confirmed winner on air with full results read. Several surnames are heavily garbled in auto-captions and are best guesses: #33 'Allen VA / Allan V / Allen bot' rendered as Alan Vos (captions once read 'Alan Vos'); #16 'Kyle V / Kyle VA / Kyle R' rendered as Kyle Vos (chat treated 33 and 16 as a pair); #01 'Kelly Co / Kelly cool / Kelly schol' rendered as Kelly Cole (uncertain); 'David fight' rendered as David Feit (uncertain). Cause of Sean McDonnell's lap-16 power loss never determined on the broadcast. Final finishing order read on air at ~2:26:46 (8806s). Ricky Whittenburg (#55, outside pole) faded to 28th after being caught in the late Big One era of the race per results read.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"im_HYTivu8A":{"recap":"Alan Vaught controlled most of the 150-lap Season 1 race at the Milwaukee Mile and earned his breakthrough victory after repeatedly battling Tim Pope on restarts. Pope had qualified on pole but served an end-of-line penalty, charged through the field several times, and then was caught in two separate late spins that helped scramble the running order. Jeremiah Burke advanced 20 positions to finish second, while Mike Adamson won a tight late battle for third over Jonathan Osborne and Pope. Vaught drove away by more than two seconds on the final green-flag run to take his first win of the inaugural season.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Jeremiah Burke","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":2089,"title":"Pope drops back before the green","summary":"Pole winner Tim Pope serves an end-of-line penalty from the previous race, leaving Alex Berube and Jonathan Osborne to contest the lead when the green flag waves.","tags":["timothy-pope","alex-berube","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2795,"title":"Vaught takes command","summary":"Alan Vaught clears Alex Berube for the lead after methodically closing on the opening leaders and begins the dominant portion of his race.","tags":["jess-vaught","alex-berube"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3027,"title":"Mystery yellow resets the field","summary":"The first caution appears with no visible spin or crash; the booth treats it as possible debris, and Vaught wins the ensuing race off pit road over Tyler Green and Osborne.","tags":["jess-vaught","tyler-green","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4408,"title":"Competition caution at lap 69","summary":"Race control throws the scheduled competition yellow, sending nearly everyone to pit road for four tires and fuel with Vaught still leading.","tags":["jess-vaught","rob-green","albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4859,"title":"Anderson and Riehle force another yellow","summary":"Albert Anderson has a second problem moments after spinning on the restart, while Dustin Riehle tries to reach pit road from an unsafe position; race control checks up the field.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-reilly"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":5224,"title":"Three incidents erupt together","summary":"Contact between Tyler Green and Eric Klafka starts one incident, Simon Sriegis spins while avoiding trouble, and Jeremiah Burke has a separate self-spin as the yellow returns.","tags":["tyler-green","eric-klafka","simon-sregis","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6204,"title":"Turn 1 crash flips trucks","summary":"Jorge Rincon and Brian Jablonski trigger a violent crash into Turns 1 and 2, followed by hard secondary contact that also catches Dave Mayberry and sends the leaders to a crowded pit road.","tags":["george-rincon","brian-jablonski","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6503,"title":"The Milwaukee Big One blocks the straight","summary":"Tim Pope breaks loose on cold tires near the front and the field stacks up behind him, involving roughly half the trucks, launching Josh Bittner airborne, and leaving Tyler Green atop the barrels.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner","tyler-green","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6841,"title":"Pope snaps loose again","summary":"On the next restart Pope's truck suddenly rotates under braking and another track-blocking pileup catches Jeffrey Green, Austin Paul, and Albert Anderson.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeffrey-green","austin-paul","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7089,"title":"Vaught launches into the final run","summary":"Vaught beats Zach Wheeler on the last restart while Burke surges from deep in the field into second and the race finally stays green.","tags":["jess-vaught","zach-wheeler","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7746,"title":"Vaught ends the drought","summary":"Alan Vaught takes the Milwaukee victory by more than two seconds over hard-charger Jeremiah Burke, with Mike Adamson securing third in the closing-lap traffic battle.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7746,"quote":"Jess Vaught, kind of ending this crazy drought that he's had here in Vigilante and picking up the win here today at Milwaukee.","context":"The live victory call as Vaught crosses the line.","gold":5},{"t":7986,"quote":"If you're not having fun, I mean, really, what are you out there doing?","context":"Third-place finisher Mike Adamson explains his strong second half of the season.","gold":5},{"t":8176,"quote":"I missed that big wreck, and all of a sudden I could finally run some clean laps and just ran clean laps to the finish.","context":"Jeremiah Burke describes his 20-position charge to second.","gold":2},{"t":8270,"quote":"Go choke on a pickle.","context":"The booth and Burke recall the slogan carried on the back of Burke's Dustin Riehle tribute truck.","gold":5},{"t":8500,"quote":"This track, just for whatever reason, just fit my style of race. I like it kind of loose, and you really got to wheel it.","context":"Winner Alan Vaught explains why Milwaukee suited him.","gold":5},{"t":8693,"quote":"I'm glad honestly that this win came in this fashion — a dominant fashion, racing the best in my league.","context":"Vaught reflects on earning his first win as league owner.","gold":5},{"t":8933,"quote":"As soon as he crossed the finish line, I said three words: about damn time.","context":"Race controller Lori Vaught reacts to Jess's breakthrough victory.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish call, podium interviews, and full results rundown explicitly confirm Vaught, Burke, and Adamson. Burke was the hard charger at plus 20 positions, while Tyler Green was the random-draw driver of the day after finishing 21st. The first caution had no visible cause and was described by the booth as possible debris, so no incident is attributed. Pole winner Pope, Adamson, and Burke each served end-of-line penalties from the prior race. Guest broadcaster Alan Kewins's surname is heavily garbled in captions as Keulens/Keuins/Cuens; this spelling follows another Season 1 distill. Lori Vaught handled race control and was interviewed after the winner. Full field: 28 starters; 23 were still classified as finishers for the post-race draw.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"is7jXko-eIA":{"recap":"The VRL trucks traded superspeedways and short tracks for 100 laps at Kansas Speedway, split into two 50-lap stages on a slick, 100-degree racetrack. Alan Vaught — who bought a brand-new $300 wheel mid-week at GameStop and bolted it to a hotel desk after being stuck on a controller in Monday's practice race — won stage one and looked like the truck to beat until a late caution caught him just off pit road on six-lap-older tires. The night's defining yellow was \"Aprongate,\" when Dustin Wade parked his truck on the apron and drew a tow-in caution, and the ensuing restart produced the race's only official wreck as David Feit spun and collected Sean McDonnell and Jorge Rincon. On the final lap, Trevor Robertson dove under leader Jonah Long in turn three, contact sent the 7 around, and Vaught split the gap out of nowhere to steal the win. Robert Shipman charged from 26th to second, Robertson held on for third, and Jonathan Osborne drove from 31st to fourth as the night's hard charger on his mouth-controlled adaptive rig.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Robert Chipman","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1448,"title":"Bates finds the wall on lap one","summary":"Seconds after the green flag, Timmy Bates slaps the sticky outside wall in turns one and two and drops like a rock while Mike Adamson takes avoiding action.","tags":["timmy-bates","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1565,"title":"Kuehl takes the point","summary":"Kelly Kuehl slips and slides his way past polesitter Tim Pope for the first lead change of the night.","tags":["kelly-keel","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2095,"title":"The beer cart girl DD","summary":"Adam Turner relays that a league regular talked the neighboring golf course's beer cart girl into chauffeuring him to pit road, and the booth starts planning a mid-race trip to the turn-two casino.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2258,"title":"The $300 GameStop wheel","summary":"The booth reveals Alan Vaught — on a controller in Monday's practice race — went out and bought a brand-new wheel, strapped it to a hotel desk on travel, and is running second with it.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2358,"title":"Burke's commitment-cone misadventure","summary":"Jeremiah Burke spins trying to enter the pits under green, misses the commitment cone, and dirt-tracks it through the infield.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3040,"title":"Three-wide squeeze at the stage break","summary":"Racing to the stage line it goes three wide right in front of leader Alan Vaught — Jack Dixon and Earl Evans make contact and Evans slams the outside wall as the stage-ending caution waves.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jack-dixon","earl-evans","jess-vaught","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4255,"title":"Aprongate","summary":"Fresh off a pit-road speeding penalty, Dustin Wade parks his damaged truck on the apron and gets towed, drawing a yellow that traps part of the field a lap down — #ApronGate starts trending on the broadcast.","tags":["dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4604,"title":"Restart wreck collects the 23 and 28","summary":"On the restart David Feit spins battling John Gallagher for the apron line; Sean McDonnell and Jorge Rincon have nowhere to go in what the booth calls the first official caution of the night.","tags":["david-fite","shawn-mcdonald","george-rincon","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5027,"title":"Osborne noses ahead for the lead","summary":"Jonathan Osborne, up 28 spots on the night, gets his nose out in front of leader Jonah Long side by side down the back straight with Trevor Robertson stalking them both.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jonah-long","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5256,"title":"Vaught splits the gap on the last lap","summary":"Trevor Robertson dives under leader Jonah Long in turn three on the final lap, contact sends the 7 around, and Alan Vaught splits the gap out of nowhere to steal the Kansas win as Robert Shipman slides through to second.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonah-long","trevor-robertson","robert-chipman"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6483,"title":"Hard charger Chachi","summary":"The booth salutes Jonathan Osborne — fourth from 31st on his mouth-controlled adaptive rig — as the night's hard charger.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2003,"quote":"Around here the handicapped lane is fast.","context":"Booth relays Jonathan Osborne's own comeback to a slow driver — Osborne races with an adaptive mouth-controlled rig","gold":4},{"t":2592,"quote":"Everybody's chasing something here, just like chasing or running down a dream — and to that I say carry on with my wayward son.","context":"Alan Brown stacks Tom Petty and Kansas song references mid-battle at Kansas Speedway","gold":4},{"t":2944,"quote":"We're talking about catfish and they're trying to steal nuclear codes all at once — what in the world is happening today?","context":"Reacting to the chat AI's poem about Chud the catfish on Josh Buettner's truck","gold":4},{"t":3498,"quote":"They're probably gonna just fire us and have some AI broadcasters, which is cool — we'll have an extra day off.","context":"The booth contemplating being replaced by AI mid-broadcast","gold":3},{"t":4243,"quote":"This is a simulation, this is not a video game — everybody knows that.","context":"Arguing with league admin Lori Vaught in chat over sim pit-road speeding penalties","gold":3},{"t":5138,"quote":"Jess Vaught is driving it like he stole it somewhere in Montana and is trying to get it to like Corpus Christi in five hours.","context":"Vaught ripping through the closing laps on his brand-new wheel","gold":4},{"t":5266,"quote":"Here comes the 33 with a big run out of nowhere, ends up splitting the gap and picks up the race win here on that final lap — what? Wow, incredible! How did he get through that?","context":"The winning call as Alan Vaught threads the last-lap wreck","gold":5},{"t":6483,"quote":"The guy drove his way through the field with that mouth controller and just kicked ass tonight.","context":"Alan English on Jonathan Osborne's fourth-place charge from 31st","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption spelling uncertainties: the runner-up in the 58 is called both 'Shipman' and 'Chipman' interchangeably by the booth (Shipman used in the grid rundown and podium interview intro); the #28 is rendered 'Rincon' / 'McCone' / 'from cone' — Rincon chosen as best guess; #1 'David Feit' may be a caption garble (captions render V-names as F, e.g. Vaught as 'fought', so possibly Voight/Vight); #14 is spelled 'Dustin with a Y' per the booth, hence 'Dustyn Eaton'; the #7 is heard as both 'Jonah Long' and 'John Long'; #82 'Michael Averitt' is a best guess from 'Michael average' / 'Mike Everest'. Larry Dickerson and Dillon Bryant are mentioned only as members of the new team formed after Limitless Motorsports disbanded, not confirmed on track tonight. Winner and podium confirmed via post-race interviews and the final rundown. The 'stage break' caution and the Aprongate tow yellow preceded what the booth called the only official caution (the David Feit spin). Sponsor read: Blue Fox Properties / Dave Mayberry.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Iv7CaGXS5X8":{"recap":"Race #8 of VRL Season 11 brought the trucks to Darlington for throwback night, with Josh Bittner taking the pole at 28.973 and roughly half the field starting from the rear while serving Martinsville penalties. After a flurry of early cautions — including a multi-truck tangle off turn 2 that inexplicably drew no yellow — the race settled into a long green-flag strategy battle, and Alan Vaugh's off-sequence tire calls carried him to a commanding lead. Vaugh's shot at a third win of the season evaporated when he was caught speeding leaving pit road late and sat through a roughly 40-second penalty, handing the lead to outside-polesitter Mike Adamson. Tim Pope, off-sequence himself after starting in the back, ran Adamson down on fresher tires and passed him with just over two laps to go for his first win of the season. Adamson settled for second with Dustyn Eaton third, and only six trucks finished on the lead lap.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Mike Adamson","Dustyn Eaton"],"moments":[{"t":2678,"title":"Green flag with half the field in penalty row","summary":"Bittner leads the field to green with a long single-file line of trucks starting from the rear serving Martinsville penalties; Scott Rooney clips the wall off turn 2 on the opening lap.","tags":["josh-bittner","scott-rooney"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3018,"title":"Throwback night paint scheme tour","summary":"The booth rolls through the whole field calling out throwback liveries — Player's Earnhardt Wrangler, Adamson's Dale Jr. Budweiser 88, Klein's Fabulous Hudson Hornet, Gallagher's PBR pounder and more.","tags":["andrew-player","mike-adamson","greg-cline","john-gallagher","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3176,"title":"First caution: Osborne into Burke","summary":"Trouble on the frontstretch brings out the first yellow; replay shows John Osborne drifting up into Jeremiah Burke off turn 4 — 'they met in the middle.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3636,"title":"Dixon collected while saving his truck","summary":"Jack Dixon loses momentum saving his truck off the wall and Kyle Vaugh, carrying full speed, has nowhere to go — the 48 is turned around and caution two flies.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3870,"title":"Restart bites: Rooney walls it, Kyle Vaugh wrecks off two","summary":"Right after a botched restart, Rooney slaps the wall and Kyle Vaugh snaps loose and crashes hard off turn 2, drawing another caution and a tow to the pits.","tags":["scott-rooney","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4122,"title":"The no-caution Big One off turn 2","summary":"Stony Benfield dirt-tracks it off the corner and triggers a big multi-truck wreck — Greg Klein's 92 goes around with heavy front damage and Greg Dobson finds the fence — yet iRacing never throws the yellow, leaving the booth fuming at the caution algorithm.","tags":["stony-benfield","greg-cline","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4810,"title":"Bittner's save of the night","summary":"Battling Alan Vaugh for the lead, Bittner gets contact off turn 2 and somehow gathers up a massive slide — 'how that didn't turn into a wreck, I don't know.' Vaugh completes the pass a lap later for the lead.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5683,"title":"Vaugh runs down Goodenough on fresh tires","summary":"With 11-lap fresher tires, Alan Vaugh reels in leader Craig Goodenough by nearly a second a lap and drives around him through turns 3 and 4 at lap 87.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6570,"title":"The Lady in Black claims Goodenough","summary":"Front-runner Craig Goodenough suddenly heads to the pits and out of the race — replay shows a tank-slapper into the wall that finished off already-damaged right-front suspension.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7251,"title":"Vaugh busted by the police — win gone","summary":"The class of the field, Alan Vaugh, is caught speeding leaving pit road on his final stop and crawls back to serve a 40-plus-second penalty, throwing away a near-certain third win of the season. He finishes 13th.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7651,"title":"Pope hunts down Adamson for the win","summary":"On fresher tires from an off-sequence final stop, Tim Pope erases a 7-plus second gap, clears lapped traffic, and dives inside Mike Adamson into turn 3 with under three laps to go — 'Adamson can only watch.'","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7722,"title":"Checkered flag: Pope's first of the season","summary":"Tim Pope takes the white and brings the chicken pit number 7 home for his first win of the year, with Adamson second and Dustyn Eaton third — only six trucks on the lead lap.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2402,"quote":"With that many penalties, is it really a penalty? If you're putting half the field to the back, are they really in the back?","context":"Half the grid skipped qualifying while serving Martinsville penalties","gold":3},{"t":4821,"quote":"Bitner and VA get together off turn number two. How that didn't turn into a wreck, I don't know.","context":"Bittner's massive save while battling Alan Vaugh for the lead","gold":3},{"t":5575,"quote":"The last time I was in Darlington, I got into the moonshine a little too heavy and I ended up passing out through the entire Cup race. This Yankee can't hang apparently.","context":"Steve reacting to Chandler Paul heading into the infield with a camera","gold":4},{"t":6706,"quote":"It's the lady in black that decides.","context":"After race-ending damage knocked out front-runner Craig Goodenough","gold":4},{"t":7356,"quote":"Alan Vaugh looked to be in a good position to pick up the win, but he gets busted by the police.","context":"Vaugh's late pit-road speeding penalty ends his shot at the win","gold":4},{"t":7661,"quote":"Pope looking to the outside, swaps over to the inside, going for the race lead into turn number three. Pope takes over the top spot. Adamson can only watch.","context":"The winning pass with under three laps to go","gold":5},{"t":8029,"quote":"You blow by him like he's tied to a tree with just a few laps to go.","context":"Steve to Tim Pope in the victory interview","gold":5},{"t":8152,"quote":"He's like, 'You got it. You got this.' And then all of a sudden he goes, 'Mike, I'm sorry. Pope's on the way.' And I was like, 'Oh no.'","context":"Mike Adamson recounting his spotter's call in the runner-up interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 11, race 8: 150 laps / 204 miles at virtual Darlington, NASCAR trucks, throwback night, broadcast by Track Limits Network. Alan Vaugh's surname is heavily garbled by auto-captions (VA, Ba, Bot, Bach, Vaude, Font, Vault, O'Reill); 'Vaugh' chosen to match the cleanest caption occurrences and fellow names Kyle Vaugh and chat regular Lori Vaugh — real spelling uncertain (could be Vaught/Vaude). Driver-broadcaster's surname also garbled (Gones/Goon/Con); 'Chris Gones' is a best guess. Names in the pre-show promo reel around 0:31 (Musk, Peters, Lockwood, Quinn, Reynolds, etc.) appear to be unrelated highlight footage from another race, not this event, and were excluded. Repeated 'Heat. Heat.' lines are auto-caption noise from background music, not commentary. In the post-race interview Dustyn Eaton says he feels bad for 'Jess' who got caught up in trouble — likely a garble of Josh (Bitner), uncertain. Full finishing order was read on air; positions 4-6 (last lead-lap trucks) were Andrew Player, Austin Paul, Andrew Coffin.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Iy1QiDFRc8o":{"recap":"Madness and Mayhem at Michigan lived up to the billing without allowing the wreck count to tell the whole story. Alan Vaught powered around pole-sitter Jeremiah Burke on lap one, while Kelly Kuehl charged from an end-of-line penalty and turned opposing pit timing into a stage-ending one-two with his teammate. Kuehl later threaded a three-wide restart, and the front rows repeatedly expanded to four wide as Jonathan Osborne, Jack Dixon, Michael Taylor, Sean McDonnell, Kyle Vaught, and others searched for clean air. The danger was real: Earl Evans and Dion Jones met at pit entry hard enough to destroy Jones's engine, netcode turned Larry Dickerson into a heavy multi-truck crash, and John Gallagher's slide made Dave Mayberry the target of a secondary hit. The decisive tension arrived during the final green-flag cycle. Mayberry inherited a 12-second lead, then Sean McDonnell and Michael Everage became the next fuel gamblers as the regular contenders peeled away. Everage reached the white flag in front and appeared one lap from stealing it, but the No. 82 sputtered entering the final corners. Vaught swept past for his first win of the season and a playoff berth, Kuehl completed the team one-two, and Burke recovered to third.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Kelly Kuehl","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1512,"title":"Vaught powers around Burke on lap one","summary":"Vaught holds the outside through the opening corners, clears polesitter Jeremiah Burke, and takes command as Albert Anderson joins the fight behind them.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1824,"title":"Buettner gets pounded into the wall","summary":"Josh Buettner and Jack Dixon tangle in the pack, sending the 84 hard into the outside wall with suspension damage while the race remains green.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1944,"title":"Evans and Jones explode at pit entry","summary":"Earl Evans and Dion Jones try to occupy the same lane, tear bodywork from the 4, and slam the inside pit barrier; Jones' engine is destroyed and the first racing caution flies.","tags":["earl-evans","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2256,"title":"Kuehl threads a three-wide restart","summary":"Vaught and Osborne struggle for launch, and Kelly Kuehl dives to the bottom while Burke pushes the middle, sending the front of the field three-wide down the backstretch.","tags":["kelly-keel","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3409,"title":"Vaught and Kuehl cash in at halfway","summary":"The teammates turn opposing pit timing into an eight-second escape and take the scheduled stage one-two, with Jonah Long surging from the rear to third.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3742,"title":"Vaught fires through a three-wide opening","summary":"At the second-half restart, Vaught dives under Andrew Player and Dustyn Eaton, then slides through the narrow opening to reclaim the head of the line.","tags":["jess-vaught","andrew-player","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3852,"title":"Four-wide mayhem across the Michigan stripe","summary":"Kelly Kuehl is trapped in the middle while Jonathan Osborne, Jack Dixon, Michael Taylor, Sean McDonnell, Kyle Vaught, and others stack into multiple rows of four-wide racing.","tags":["kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon","mike-taylor","shawn-mcdonald","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3918,"title":"Netcode lights the fuse on the Big One","summary":"Jonah Long appears to miss Larry Dickerson before netcode turns the 69 up the track, collecting Kyle Vaught, Austin Paul, and Greg Dobson in a heavy multi-truck crash.","tags":["jonah-long","larry-dickerson","kyle-vaught","austin-paul","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4311,"title":"Gallagher's slide turns Mayberry into the punching bag","summary":"John Gallagher loses the rear entering the corner and shoots down the track into Dave Mayberry, who is then knocked into Eric Klapka as the yellow comes back out.","tags":["john-gallagher","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5344,"title":"Mayberry leads the fuel-mileage apocalypse","summary":"As the final pit cycle peels away one contender after another, Dave Mayberry inherits a 12-second lead and briefly looks capable of stealing the race before making his final stop.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5591,"title":"Everage runs dry with the win in sight","summary":"Michael Everage takes the white flag as the latest fuel gambler, but the 82 sputters entering the final corners; Vaught drives past to win while Pope and Robertson also run dry behind him.","tags":["mike-everage","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1703,"quote":"A full accoutrement of air molecules pushed down - oh my God, that's a lot of words.","context":"The booth gets carried away explaining aero grip","gold":4},{"t":3045,"quote":"You got three cars on three separate laps taking it three-wide.","context":"Michigan traffic compresses three different races into one lane","gold":4},{"t":3907,"quote":"They do realize there's two miles of track here, and they're all racing within the same 50 feet of it.","context":"The booth reacts to the four-wide pack","gold":5},{"t":5344,"quote":"Oh my goodness - sign of the apocalypse: Dave the nickname Mayberry leading this race.","context":"Mayberry inherits the lead during the fuel cycle","gold":5},{"t":5607,"quote":"He ran out of fuel as Jess Vaught, with the last-minute pass, drops around him.","context":"The winning move as Everage sputters on the last lap","gold":5},{"t":5688,"quote":"I followed the science. Doctor taught me everything I know.","context":"The booth celebrates correctly predicting the fuel collapse","gold":4},{"t":6507,"quote":"That plan rarely survives first contact with the enemy or the adversary.","context":"Vaught explains how the winning strategy survived a volatile race","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The transcript and interviews explicitly confirm Vaught, Kuehl, and Burke as the podium. Thirty-three drivers are identified from the starting grid and finishing order. This was Vaught's first win of the season and, by his post-race account, secured his playoff eligibility as long as he remained in the top 20.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"J3ll6F4n9-M":{"recap":"The Tropical Blizzard 100 put the VRL's Gen 4 cars under the lights on Daytona's 2.5-mile superspeedway for 100 laps, and the 32-car field turned it into a fuel-strategy chess match bookended by chaos. A lap-9 Big One sent Jacob Young's Cane's machine barrel-rolling four times before the field ripped off roughly 85 caution-free laps of green-flag pit cycles and fuel-mileage gambling, with Albert Anderson and Kelly Kuehl controlling the front for most of the night. A lap-96 spin — Austin Paul getting under George Rancan — forced the night's one green-white-checker attempt, and coming to the white flag an eleven-car wreck erupted behind the leaders, flipping Anderson's 99 onto its roof. Out front Mike Adamson blocked and drag-raced Jess Vont to the line, winning by 0.4 seconds, while a flu-stricken Ricky Whittenburg threaded the last-lap carnage from 16th to steal the final podium spot.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Jess Vont","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":1785,"title":"The Big One strikes on lap 9","summary":"A checkup sent the 37 into the six, which went airborne and triggered the night's first pileup; Jacob Young's Cane's 17 barrel-rolled four times, landed on its wheels, and kept going.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dustin-reilly","jacob-young","john-gallagher","jack-dixon","andrew-player","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2230,"title":"Earl Evans races in a onesie","summary":"Evans lost a bet and ran a 'Birds Aren't Real — learn the truth' scheme with his official race onesie plastered across the 13 car.","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2810,"title":"Dustyn with a Y sweeps to the lead","summary":"Eaton came down with a run and took the lead from Anderson's 99, putting Team Tang on the point and setting up a 99-vs-14 battle.","tags":["dustin-eaton","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3041,"title":"Body checks nearly wreck the lead pack","summary":"The 99 and 14 nearly came together at speed, sending a huge checkup through the field — drivers on the radio said it scared everybody to death, but nobody stacked up.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3517,"title":"Mass dive onto pit road","summary":"After laps of the booth guessing at fuel windows, nearly the whole pack peeled onto pit lane at once with tires locking up — and everyone made it in clean.","tags":["jack-dixon","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5859,"title":"Sneaky-deky: leaders pit late together","summary":"Vont, Kuehl, Adamson, Anderson and Klein coordinated a surprise final stop, gambling they could run down a 10-plus-second gap in eight laps — until the caution flipped everything.","tags":["kelly-keel","mike-adamson","albert-anderson","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6081,"title":"Lap-96 spin forces a green-white-checker","summary":"Austin Paul got under the 28 of Rancan and spun him, collecting Curtis, Dixon and Evans — just the second caution of the night, and it threw the fuel strategy out the window.","tags":["austin-paul","john-curtis","jack-dixon","earl-evans"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6448,"title":"Drinking helmets on: the GWC restart","summary":"Pope and Vont led the field to the one-and-only green-white-checker attempt with all 18 lead-lap cars alive for the win.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6529,"title":"White-flag Big One: 11 cars wreck","summary":"Coming to the white flag the 27 got sideways and the entire track was blocked — Anderson's 99 turtled onto its roof, the 14 and 18 went for rides, and eleven cars slid out of control down to the apron.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","dustin-eaton","andrew-player","kelly-keel","john-gallagher","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6550,"title":"Adamson wins the drag race by 0.4","summary":"With mayhem erupting behind them, Adamson blocked Vont down the backstretch and drag-raced the 33 to the line, winning by 0.4 seconds for his return to Victory Lane.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6674,"title":"The seas part for the Moses man","summary":"Replay showed Whittenburg — 16th when the wreck broke out — threading untouched through eleven spinning cars to steal third; the booth said the seas just straight up parted for him.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7150,"title":"Hydrated and medicated","summary":"A flu-ridden Whittenburg explained he'd been so loopy he was seeing six times the cars all night — so when '60 cars' crashed on the last lap he just aimed at the middle one and made the podium.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1789,"quote":"Somebody's turned — the six! Oh, and we got the Big One!","context":"the lap-9 pileup erupts off turn two","gold":4},{"t":1897,"quote":"If we sent this one to the judges, I think the Russians might have given them like an 8.5 for the landing.","context":"Jacob Young barrel-rolled four times and landed on his wheels","gold":4},{"t":3350,"quote":"Hey guys, I need to pit here, can y'all let me in? I need my Whataburger — a number one with a Dr Pepper, make it to go, I'm in a hurry.","context":"voicing Edson Ochoa's Whataburger car stuck unable to reach pit road","gold":4},{"t":4284,"quote":"We're missing our yeast here this evening — he's the yeast to our hops and barley.","context":"the booth lamenting absent co-commentator Allen English","gold":3},{"t":6452,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets and throw inhibition out the window — green-white-checker racing here from the VRL race at Daytona!","context":"sending the field to the green-white-checker","gold":5},{"t":6529,"quote":"Oh, there goes Albert! Big wreck behind the 88 and the 33, causing absolute mayhem and catastrophe!","context":"the white-flag-lap Big One breaks out behind the leaders","gold":5},{"t":6560,"quote":"Drag racing across the line for the 88 and the 33 — it will not come in time! Mike Adamson wins here at Daytona!","context":"the 0.4-second finish call","gold":5},{"t":6573,"quote":"What the hell — where did Ricky... where were you all night, Ricky? What happened there? I'm so confused.","context":"discovering Whittenburg on the podium after starting the last lap 16th","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names heavily; uncertain best-guesses: 'Edson Ochoa' (captions: Ooa/NOOA), 'George Rancan' (ranan/rancon/ranone), 'Dustin Riehle' #37 (Brey/really), 'Andrew Cin' #10 (CN/cin), 'Kelly Kuehl' (keil/kill/Q). 'Dustyn Eaton' spelling inferred from the recurring 'Dustin with a Y' nickname. Regular co-commentator Allen English was absent (sick); Adam Turner joined Alan Brown in the booth. The booth itself warned the final rundown was 'not 100% correct' after the last-lap chaos — John Curtis's finish was stated as both 18th (interview) and 17th (rundown). Race control was Lori Vont; the league is run by Jess and Lori Vont. Podium margin (Adamson over Vont by 0.4s) quoted by Vont in his interview. Race was 100 laps, only two cautions (lap 9 and lap 96).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"jqxI_0voWeo":{"recap":"For 73 of its 75 scheduled laps, the Unchained 200 at Talladega was a clean, three-lane drafting and pit-execution contest. Jack Dixon led the 35-truck field to green, Gordon Spain moved ahead with Tim Pope's help, and Austin Paul and Dillon Bryant soon organized a third lane that reached the front. The first fuel window punished Spain when he spun entering pit road, but the race remained green; Dave Mayberry also spun during the final scheduled stop without producing a caution. Those cycles divided the field into separate packs, leaving Jacob Alesia, Chris Goans and their drafting partners balancing speed against the need to stay attached as the groups converged. The first yellow finally arrived with two laps remaining when contact swept up Dustin Wade, Albert Anderson, Craig Goodenough and Chandler Paul. Mike Adamson lined up inside Alesia for the sole green-white-checkered attempt and launched narrowly ahead, but another wreck erupted behind them before the white flag. The caution froze Adamson first, Alesia second and Goans third, giving Adamson his first Premiere Series win of Season 14 without a completed green-flag overtime finish.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Jacob Alesia","Chris Goans"],"moments":[{"t":1331,"title":"Dixon leads 35 trucks to green","summary":"Jack Dixon starts from pole beside John Gallagher as the field begins the 75-lap race under a mandatory double-file rule for the opening lap.","tags":["jack-dixon","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1362,"title":"Spain takes the early lead","summary":"Gordon Spain uses Tim Pope's help on the outside to move ahead, beginning a constant exchange of lanes at the front.","tags":["gordon-spain","timothy-pope","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1639,"title":"Paul and Bryant make the third lane work","summary":"Despite Austin Paul's intermittent blinking, he and Dillon Bryant organize the outside lane and drive all the way to the lead by lap six.","tags":["austin-paul","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2380,"title":"Three lanes reach the first fuel window","summary":"The field remains caution-free and three wide as 20 laps are completed, with alliances continually reshuffling before the first stops.","tags":["gordon-spain","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2499,"title":"Spain spins entering pit road","summary":"Leader Spain loses control on the first green-flag pit entry and slides through the grass; the race stays green, but the error destroys his track position.","tags":["gordon-spain"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3171,"title":"Alesia controls the lead pack","summary":"After the opening stops, Alesia leads with Aaron Warren pushing while Goans, Craig Goodenough and Greg Dobson form the core of the front group.","tags":["jacob-alicia","aaron-warren","chris-goans","craig-goodenough","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3760,"title":"Second pit cycle begins under green","summary":"Most of the field dives to pit road for its final scheduled fuel stop; Dave Mayberry spins during entry but keeps the race green.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3883,"title":"Anderson inherits the lead","summary":"After staying out one more lap, Albert Anderson cycles to the point before Aaron Warren, Alesia and John Schoenbachler use their three-truck draft to move forward.","tags":["albert-anderson","aaron-warren","jacob-alicia","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4632,"title":"Separated packs begin to converge","summary":"With 21 laps left, Dixon's group and a middle pack chase the single-file leaders, making drafting efficiency more important than raw position.","tags":["jack-dixon","aaron-warren","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5332,"title":"Two-to-go crash ends the clean run","summary":"A wiggle in the two-wide lead battle leaves Wade unsettled while pushing Anderson, and contact sweeps Anderson, Goodenough and Chandler Paul into the first caution of the night.","tags":["dustin-wade","albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5776,"title":"Overtime wreck freezes the field","summary":"Adamson launches from the inside beside Alesia, but a crash breaks out behind them before the white flag; the caution ends the only overtime attempt with Adamson narrowly ahead.","tags":["mike-adamson","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5830,"quote":"The champion is going to be Mike Adamson, as he's taking the pace truck around to claim victory here in Talladega, Alabama.","context":"The booth confirms Adamson as the caution-frozen overtime winner","gold":5},{"t":6012,"quote":"It felt awesome.","context":"Mike Adamson's immediate reaction to winning Talladega","gold":4},{"t":6045,"quote":"When we took that green, I was hoping if we did get a caution, I was going to be out front just enough to at least snag the win.","context":"Adamson explains the importance of leading the overtime restart","gold":5},{"t":6077,"quote":"You've got to have some luck besides skill when it comes to Dega.","context":"Adamson sums up his winning approach","gold":5},{"t":6192,"quote":"The key to success were pit stops and good teamwork. From the get-go, we were working really well as a unit.","context":"Runner-up Jacob Alesia describes the caution-free strategy race","gold":4},{"t":6328,"quote":"Talladega has a tendency to go green, so the main thing was just try to stay in touch with the lead pack and limit pit-road mistakes.","context":"Third-place finisher Chris Goans explains his conservative strategy","gold":4},{"t":6350,"quote":"I didn't take tires the whole time. You don't really need them here as much.","context":"Goans describes his pit-stop execution","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete 35-driver finishing order is read after the interviews. The race ran without a caution until two laps remained; a second yellow on the first lap of the sole green-white-checkered attempt froze the field and ended the event. Caption distortions are extensive: roster canonicals are used for Jacob Alesia, Chris Goans, John Schoenbachler and several others. Ricky Whittenburg appeared only in the live chat because of a property emergency and is not listed as a broadcaster.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"jxe10V545OI":{"recap":"The VRL opened Season 9 at Nashville Superspeedway on the eve of the Fourth of July with 36 trucks, ten newcomers, a field full of patriotic paint schemes, and a driver-voted zero-fast-repair rule that made every scrape count. Rookie Jason Gaines grabbed the pole, but the night became a caution-filled war of attrition, capped by a late 'Big One' that turned the track into a parking lot after the 74 of Zachary Howen came down across John Gallagher on a restart. League co-owner Alan Vaught led much of the race but gambled on old tires and was collected in a late restart pile-up with Trevor Robertson and Mike Everage. Jeremiah Burke, on the freshest rubber, took over late, set the race's fastest lap, and held off Larry Dickerson and defending champion Tim Pope — the hard charger, up 29 spots from 32nd — to win the season opener. Ricky Whittenburg came home fourth and Kelly Kuehl fifth, with just 17 trucks finishing on the lead lap.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Larry Dickerson","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1407,"title":"Green flag on Season 9","summary":"Rookie polesitter Jason Gaines and Alan Vaught send the field off side by side into turn one to open the Season 9 campaign at Nashville.","tags":["jason-gaines","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1992,"title":"First caution: lap-20 tangle","summary":"Everage drifts up into Goodenough and both slap the wall; John Curtis catches the worst of it with heavy front-end damage while Albert Anderson's cat-like reflexes thread him through the mess.","tags":["mike-everage","craig-goodenough","john-curtis","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2988,"title":"The AI spotter lies to Maroth","summary":"Rookie Darby Maroth comes up into Kelly Kuehl after his AI spotter called him clear, shoving the former champ into the wall — then immediately owns it on the radio: 'I'm so sorry, that was my fault.'","tags":["darby-maroth","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3982,"title":"McAdam launched into the wall","summary":"Klein drifts into Vaught's front bumper and spins; in the checkup behind, Osborne piles into John McAdam and sends the Coors Banquet truck flying into the outside wall.","tags":["greg-cline","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4071,"title":"The Hawk Tuah 2024 truck","summary":"English swears Greg Klein is running a 'Hawk Tuah 2024' campaign paint while Brown only sees the Navy veteran's Navy truck — Turner has never heard of it and vows to Google it later.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4441,"title":"Benfield spins, Anderson along for the ride","summary":"Three-wide contact sends Stony Benfield sideways across the track; Albert Anderson has nowhere to go and gets suction-cupped into the outside wall with him, as Dickerson apologizes on the radio.","tags":["stony-benfield","albert-anderson","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5304,"title":"Wade's wild ride — almost a flipper","summary":"A nudge from Rancone sends Dustin Wade spinning through the pack, collecting Gaines and Dobson; a couple of trucks nearly get airborne before the hood and roof flaps do their job.","tags":["dustin-wade","george-rincon","jason-gaines","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5644,"title":"Player destroyed on the infield wall","summary":"Andrew Player is bumped through the grass — 'like driving on ice' — and slams the inside wall so hard the engine won't refire; the booth says he needs a 'bambulance', and his night is done.","tags":["andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6555,"title":"Gaines slides, Maroth threads the needle","summary":"Gaines and Kyle Vaught tangle and the 83 slices across the field; Darby Maroth misses him by inches with the booth rating it 'pucker factor up to 11'.","tags":["jason-gaines","kyle-vaught","darby-maroth"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6904,"title":"THE BIG ONE — parking lot at Nashville","summary":"Zachary Howen comes down across John Gallagher on the restart and the field piles in, trucks slamming the inside pit wall; only Osborne and Curtis slip through, and with zero fast repairs it guts half the field late in the race.","tags":["zachary-henin","john-gallagher","jonathan-osborne","john-curtis"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7259,"title":"Restart carnage collects the leader's gamble","summary":"A cold-tire spin on the restart triggers mayhem: Trevor Robertson snaps around and hard-collects Mike Everage and Alan Vaught — a brutal end for the truck that led much of the night on old tires.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-everage","jess-vaught","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8076,"title":"Burke brings it home","summary":"On the freshest tires, Jeremiah Burke takes the white flag clear of Dickerson and Pope and cruises off turn four to win the Season 9 opener.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","larry-dickerson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1115,"quote":"Even if your dog dies and your wife leaves you and all that kind of stuff — don't let the rest of your race here turn into a country song.","context":"the booth's 'key to the race' for the Nashville season opener","gold":4},{"t":2061,"quote":"Did you see the cat-like reflexes of America's driver Albert Anderson?","context":"Anderson swinging low to dodge the first big wreck on lap 20","gold":3},{"t":5825,"quote":"He doesn't need just a wrecker — he probably needs a bambulance down there.","context":"Andrew Player's truck dead against the infield wall","gold":4},{"t":6603,"quote":"I believe the 42 is going to need a diaper change — that was kind of scary.","context":"Darby Maroth just missing Gaines's truck sliding across the track","gold":4},{"t":6904,"quote":"Oh, big wreck — oh, this is the Big One! Goodness... parking lot.","context":"the call as the field piles up late in the race","gold":5},{"t":7524,"quote":"You know what tomorrow is for everybody else? It's called Thursday. There's no Fourth of July — it's Thursday.","context":"English griping about working July 4th while Turner has the day off","gold":3},{"t":7927,"quote":"That boy's got some arms on him, and he's from Ohio — so you know he can scrap.","context":"English sizing up Dustin Wade on the driver cam","gold":3},{"t":8109,"quote":"Out of turns three and four, the 53 of Jeremiah Burke is going to be your season opener winner!","context":"the winning call at the checkered flag","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"VRL Season 9 opener, Nashville Superspeedway, 150 laps, NASCAR Trucks, streamed the night before July 4, 2024. New driver-voted rule: zero fast repairs. Winner and full podium clearly stated; complete 36-truck finishing order read out starting ~9128s. Auto-caption surnames are shaky — best guesses used for: Vaught (captions render Vault/vot/VA/fought; covers league owners Jess and Lori plus Kyle), Rancone, Howen, Maroth, Canellis, and 'David Feit' (rendered 'David fight'/'Avid fight'); Andrew Player once rendered 'Andrew Clair'; 'Ricky Wittenberg' in captions is Ricky Whittenburg (D&D Race Graphics / Southbound Real Estate). Quirks: Dickerson's truck displayed #69 instead of his #31 (iRacing hosted-session issue), Sean McDonnell's #14 displayed as #23, John Curtis showed as 'Sandy Curtis' via iRacing nickname. Lori Vaught scored/admined but was not in the booth. Chat-only league members (Dustyn Eaton, Dillon Bryant, Josh Bonner) not included as drivers since they did not race tonight.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"jywdX6nYvM4":{"recap":"The Bruise Cruise 83 at the fictional iRacing Super Speedway — three miles of virtual Massachusetts at 210-plus mph in Gen 4 cars — lived up to its name with a demolition-derby of a night. An early Big One swept up half the field, and the cautions kept coming: Scott Howell blew an engine from the top five, Kyle Vote was wrecked twice, and cruise-sponsor Greg Klein speared the pit road barrels nose-first at 180 mph. Kelly Keil charged from a lap down to take the lead, while Austin Paul, Jess Vote, and Tim Pope all took turns at the point. A massive lap-78 pileup that flipped Howell's 187 and sent Earl Evans airborne forced a green-white-checker, and in a five-wide drag race to the line Albert Anderson — 'America's driver' — surged to the win over Andrew Player and Jack Dixon, extending his recent hot streak. Tim Pope claimed hard-charger honors with 22 spots gained and the fastest lap of the race (49.779).","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Andrew Player","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1570,"title":"The First Big One Collects Half the Field","summary":"A bobble from Osborne on the outside lane triggers a chain reaction on lap 4 — Everage taps the checked-up 01, sending Kelly Keil on a wild ride into Adamson and Pope, and 'half the field, boys' piles in behind them.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","mike-everage","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2140,"title":"Jacob Young Solo Spin — on an F1 Wheel","summary":"Young loops it off the apron all by himself, and the booth reveals why the night is extra hard for him: his NASCAR wheel broke, so he's racing the superspeedway with a GT3/Formula-style handle wheel.","tags":["jacob-young"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2598,"title":"Howell's Engine Grenades from the Top Five","summary":"Scott Howell's engine blows while running top five — the booth blames one downshift too many on the bumpy transition — while behind him David Feit and Deion Jones trade paint and a car launches skyward.","tags":["scott-howell","david-fite","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3068,"title":"Whittenburg Nearly Turtled, Kyle Vote Walled","summary":"Three-wide contact from Osborne launches the 55 of Whittenburg into the 72's front bumper and nearly flips it; the chain reaction sends Chandler Paul down into Kyle Vote, who smashes the inside wall in a hit the booth calls real-life-fatal-looking.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jonathan-osborne","chandler-paul","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4070,"title":"Ochoa Washes Up Into Kyle Vote","summary":"The 8 of Ochoa gets pushed up the track in the corner entry bump and collects Kyle Vote — Vote's second wreck of the night, needing 'about one more foot of clearance' to survive it.","tags":["edson-ochoa","timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4850,"title":"Keil's Torpedo Run: Lap Down to the Lead","summary":"After an uncharacteristic lap-down night, Kelly Keil takes the lucky dog, torpedoes back through the pack, and sails past a huge checkup on the outside lane to take over the race lead with Vigilante Force stacked nose to tail.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5210,"title":"Greg Is Dead: Klein Buries It in the Barrels","summary":"Contact between the 23 and 99 sends Anderson squirrelly into Klein, who gathers it on the apron only to spear nose-first into the pit road divider barrels at 180 mph — cueing a full nautical eulogy for the cruise-travel sponsor's car.","tags":["greg-cline","albert-anderson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5660,"title":"Goodenough Love-Taps Smith Into a Wreck","summary":"A little love tap from the 89 in a checkup sends both Goodenough and Edward Smith up for a ride; Klein escapes by scooping under the airborne 89, and Greg Dobson threads the wreck needing 'a new pair of pants'. Goodenough apologizes on the radio.","tags":["craig-goodenough","edward-w-smith","greg-cline","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6085,"title":"Chandler Paul Lifted — the Anger Is Here","summary":"With 15 to go, the 72 gets its rear end lifted by Scott Howell in a checkup and goes for a wild ride — 'Anger from Chandler Paul! Anger! It's finally here' — with Everage catching the aftershocks against the outside wall.","tags":["chandler-paul","scott-howell","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6572,"title":"Whittenburg's Miracle Save","summary":"A netcode touch with Gallagher three-wide sends the 55 sideways at 200 mph — front end pointed the wrong way — but Whittenburg somehow wrestles the door-stop wedge straight and keeps the race green. The booth rewinds it in disbelief.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","john-gallagher","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7085,"title":"The Lap-78 Big One: 187 Upside Down","summary":"Four-wide with five to go erupts into the biggest wreck of the night — David Feit wrecks, Scott Howell's all-white 187 flips and sits upside down, Earl Evans's 13 gets airborne, and Andrew Chin comes on the radio to take the blame, setting up a green-white-checker.","tags":["scott-howell","david-fite","earl-evans","chandler-paul","jacob-young","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7495,"title":"Five-Wide Drag Race to the Checkers","summary":"On the green-white-checker final lap the field fans out four and five wide; Albert Anderson spots no help behind Pope, times the last-corner run perfectly, and drag-races to victory as a wreck breaks out right at the stripe. Andrew Player splits the gap from ninth to second on the last lap.","tags":["albert-anderson","andrew-player","jack-dixon","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2728,"quote":"It's not the end for the all-white murder death kill 187 machine.","context":"Scott Howell's numberless plain-white car earns a Demolition Man nickname","gold":3},{"t":4177,"quote":"Just part of all the fun here at iRacing Super Speedway — you know, sometimes a death trap. It is a death machine.","context":"Summing up the track after the Ochoa/Kyle Vote wreck","gold":3},{"t":4780,"quote":"Somebody's going to have a pistol in one hand, a beer in between their legs and their cell phone in the other, and they're going to drive with their knees.","context":"Comparing the pack's lane-changing to Houston rush hour","gold":4},{"t":4957,"quote":"I think we're going to see something happen soon because, you know — science.","context":"Turner's running 'science' gag about cars getting shoved up the track","gold":3},{"t":5051,"quote":"My money's on the Domino's guy just rang the doorbell, and Earl's like, all right, I got to send it down here to go get pizza.","context":"Earl Evans black-flagged for doing 180 mph on pit road","gold":4},{"t":5217,"quote":"Oh, Greg turned! Greg turned! Greg is dead, Greg is dead! Greg, let's get on a cruise ship!","context":"Cruise-sponsor Greg Klein spears the pit road barrels nose-first at 180 mph","gold":5},{"t":5309,"quote":"He definitely buried the bow of that car right in the seawall there... I think he set up anchor right there.","context":"The booth's nautical eulogy for Greg Klein's barrel wreck","gold":4},{"t":7427,"quote":"So buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets and throw inhibition out the window — green white checker racing here to finish up tonight's main event.","context":"Setting up the green-white-checker finish","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race is the 'Bruise Cruise 83' (83 laps) at the fictional 3-mile iRacing Super Speedway set in virtual Massachusetts, Gen 4 cars. Winner and full finishing order read on air (top 10: Anderson, Player, Dixon, Pope, Everage, J. Vote, Osborne, Curtis, Dobson, Keil; pole sitter Sean McDonnell finished 11th). Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Vote' (Kyle/Jess — could be Vogt/Voight), 'Keil' (heard Kuehl/Keill/kill), 'Fite' (heard 'fight'), 'Chin' (heard 'cin'/'CT'/'cn'), 'Ochoa' (heard 'Ooa'), 'Goodenough' (heard 'good enough'), 'Dustyn' spelled with a Y per the booth. Lori Vote served as race control and co-owns the league with Jess Vote. Josh Bonner is a league driver mentioned but not racing tonight. Dave Mayberry was spotlight driver, credited with winning the prior week at Auto Club (off-broadcast). Hard charger: Tim Pope +22 with fastest lap 49.779. Next event: mini-season finale at Indianapolis in NASCAR Trucks.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"kCVrTY8Z66Q":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant won the 85-lap Thunderwave 213 at Daytona by committing to the outside lane with teammate Jack Dixon on the sole green-white-checkered attempt. A new aerodynamic package made unsupported middle-lane moves far less effective, while four cautions repeatedly interrupted the expected fuel cycles and shuffled contenders between the lead pack and trailing drafts. The last yellow, caused by contact between Michael Everage and Kelly Kuehl with Albert Anderson and Jorge Rincon also collected, put Bryant and Dixon together on the outside front row. Dixon stayed with Bryant through the final lap, a separate wreck erupted behind them after the white flag, and Bryant led Dixon and Andrew Coffin to the finish.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Jack Dixon","Andrew Cauthan"],"moments":[{"t":1483,"title":"Player and Bryant lead Daytona to green","summary":"Andrew Player starts from pole beside championship leader Dillon Bryant as 27 starters begin the 85-lap race; Greg Klein does not start.","tags":["andrew-player","dylan-bryant","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1652,"title":"Dixon drops out of the draft","summary":"Jack Dixon abandons the lead pack after seeing something he dislikes, falls more than two seconds back and begins a long recovery that will eventually reach the podium.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2008,"title":"Osborne takes the early lead","summary":"John Osborne moves to the point as the field experiments with two organized lanes and discovers that the updated middle lane needs multiple trucks to advance.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":2426,"title":"Everage misjudgment causes the first crash","summary":"Michael Everage tries to tuck behind Osborne as the lead pack slows slightly and turns him, collecting Jorge Rincon, Aaron Warren, John Schoenbachler, Dave Mayberry and John Gallagher on lap 21.","tags":["mike-everage","jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","aaron-warren","john-schoenbachler","dave-mayberry","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3506,"title":"Everage and Paul trigger caution two","summary":"While pushing Chandler Paul in the outside lane, Everage clips Paul's rear after the line shifts and both trucks become involved in the second yellow near lap 38.","tags":["mike-everage","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5035,"title":"Green-flag stops split the race","summary":"A coordinated group led by Bryant pits first, while a second group cycles through the following lap. Six trucks initially form the lead draft as Adamson's larger chase pack tries to organize and close a roughly two-second gap.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans","kelly-keel","craig-goodenough","john-mcadam","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":5537,"title":"Mayberry stop brings out caution three","summary":"After Scott Milner touches the apron and sends Mayberry into the wall, Mayberry stops on the track with possible steering damage and triggers the third caution with 13 laps left.","tags":["scott-milner","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5944,"title":"Goodenough takes command in the sprint","summary":"The field survives an aggressive restart and Goodenough leads Bryant, Goans and Kuehl with six laps remaining as three lanes briefly form.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","chris-goans","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6264,"title":"Everage-Kuehl contact forces overtime","summary":"Everage and Kuehl converge while drafting the same truck, bounce off the wall and collect Anderson and Rincon for the fourth caution with three laps remaining.","tags":["mike-everage","kelly-keel","albert-anderson","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6671,"title":"Bryant and Dixon commit to the outside","summary":"Bryant leads the overtime restart with teammate Dixon pushing. Adamson briefly organizes the bottom, but the outside pair remain together until the white flag.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6749,"title":"Bryant wins as the pack crashes behind","summary":"A multi-truck crash unfolds behind the leaders after the white flag, so the race remains green. Dixon has no drafting help to challenge, giving Bryant the win with Dixon second and Coffin third.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jack-dixon","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6544,"quote":"I'm doing everything I can to bite my tongue right now because I really want to go on a very angry cussing tirade, but I'm not going to do that.","context":"Albert Anderson reacts immediately after the late crash","gold":5},{"t":6555,"quote":"I just wish we could get through a race without wrecking each other. That would be fantastic.","context":"Anderson gives his blunt assessment before leaving","gold":5},{"t":7138,"quote":"I just wanted to stay out of trouble until the end to even give myself a shot, and that's what I ended up doing.","context":"Third-place finisher Andrew Coffin explains his approach","gold":4},{"t":7224,"quote":"I'm up against the wall. I'm just going to keep the hammer down and keep it pointed straight.","context":"Coffin recounts threading through the last-lap wreck","gold":5},{"t":7409,"quote":"I just stuck it in the middle in the last run there, and when that caution came out, I came ahead of the wreck in fourth.","context":"Jack Dixon explains how he recovered into position for overtime","gold":4},{"t":7421,"quote":"If we hug the outside, we're going to win this race.","context":"Dixon recalls his message to teammate Bryant before the restart","gold":5},{"t":7510,"quote":"On these tracks, you're very dependent on teammates.","context":"Dillon Bryant describes the foundation of his winning plan","gold":4},{"t":7693,"quote":"Jack was definitely the only reason why I got that win tonight.","context":"Bryant credits Dixon for staying committed to the outside lane","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The grid contains 28 entries, but Greg Klein did not start; the broadcast reads a 27-driver finishing order and then explicitly identifies Klein as DNS. Trevor Robertson was absent after his software update failed. The final-lap crash occurred after the white flag, so the race remained green. The seasons map has no entry for this video; the opening identifies it only as round five of the fall season. Dustyn Eaton was not in this field.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"l4qCPeST5MY":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson advanced 29 positions from 30th to win a Monster Ball at Dover that the booth counted at 14 cautions. The opening restarts repeatedly collapsed: Jeremiah Burke was turned in the first major stack-up, the next launch checked the field into another crash, and apparent netcode later spun Jonathan Osborne despite visible space to Andrew Player. The attrition continued through the middle stretch as Sean McDonnell, Jack Dixon, Dustin Wade, Larry Dickerson and several others were caught in separate heavy incidents. Alan Vaught's time at the front ended when hard racing with Mike Adamson sent the No. 33 into the inside wall, while another four-truck tangle reshaped the order before the final stops. The thirteenth caution followed a light Mayberry-Burke touch and secondary impacts into the stranded truck, giving the leaders one last pit decision and a 14-lap run. Robertson launched from the inside of teammate Josh Bittner, secured clean air and steadily opened his advantage while Dustyn Eaton worked into second. Robertson won by roughly two seconds; Bittner held Tim Pope off by only 0.07 seconds for third. The podium interviews captured the contrast: Eaton called the race a war, while Robertson said consistency and resisting the urge to overdrive Dover's right-front tire carried him through it.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Dustyn Eaton","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1433,"title":"Pope and McDonnell lead the start","summary":"Tim Pope and Sean McDonnell race side by side through the opening lap while the 35-truck field settles into Dover's narrow, high-speed groove.","tags":["timothy-pope","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1601,"title":"Burke spin triggers the first pileup","summary":"Andrew Coffin reaches Jeremiah Burke's rear corner after a checkup, turning Burke and leaving Gallagher and several others with nowhere to go in the first major stack-up.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","jeremiah-burke","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1939,"title":"Second restart immediately collapses","summary":"A missed gear or spun tires near Dave Mayberry creates a chain reaction that ultimately sends Kelly Kuehl spinning after contact from Burke.","tags":["dave-mayberry","greg-dobson","kelly-keel","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"restart_wreck"},{"t":2432,"title":"Apparent netcode sparks a destructive crash","summary":"Jonathan Osborne is turned despite visible space to Andrew Player, and the incident collects Player, Mike Adamson, Josh Bittner, Jacob Young and Chandler Paul.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","andrew-player","mike-adamson","josh-bittner","jacob-young","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4012,"title":"Another big one erupts","summary":"A heavy multi-truck accident involves Sean McDonnell, Osborne and Jack Dixon among others, continuing the attrition just past the first third of the race.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5199,"title":"Wade slams the inside wall","summary":"Contact sends Dustin Wade hard into the inside barrier while he is racing near Burke, costing the No. 68 heavily in an already chaotic middle stretch.","tags":["dustin-wade","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5571,"title":"Dickerson crash sweeps up the pack","summary":"Larry Dickerson strikes the wall and drifts back across traffic, collecting Kelly Kuehl, Chandler Paul, Kyle Vaught, John Gallagher and others.","tags":["larry-dickerson","kelly-keel","chandler-paul","kyle-vaught","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6076,"title":"Leader Vaught is turned","summary":"Hard racing with Mike Adamson sends Alan Vaught into the inside wall, and Vaught contacts Chandler Paul while trying to rejoin, ending his spell at the front.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6724,"title":"Four trucks tangle before the final stops","summary":"Coffin and Chandler Paul make side-by-side contact, sending Coffin into the wall and drawing Albert Anderson, Kevin Hunt and Kuehl into the secondary crash.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","chandler-paul","albert-anderson","kevin-hunt","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7065,"title":"Burke incident sets up the final run","summary":"A light touch from Mayberry turns Burke; Jacob Young and Edson Ochoa then hit the stranded truck, producing the thirteenth caution and a final round of pit decisions.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry","jacob-young","edson-ochoa"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":7374,"title":"Robertson clears Bittner on the last restart","summary":"With 14 laps remaining, Robertson launches from the inside of teammate Bittner and opens clean air while Eaton works past Bittner for second.","tags":["trevor-robertson","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7710,"title":"Robertson completes a 29-position charge","summary":"Robertson crosses the line roughly two seconds clear of Eaton, while Bittner beats Pope by only 0.07 seconds for the final podium place.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dustin-eaton","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7710,"quote":"Down across the line, picking up your race win is Trevor Robertson.","context":"The live victory call after the final green-flag run.","gold":2},{"t":8147,"quote":"I either got to get punched in the face or got to punch somebody in the face—every person in the field tonight.","context":"Bittner jokes about the amount of contact involved in reaching third.","gold":5},{"t":8475,"quote":"That was a war, wasn't it?","context":"Eaton sums up the attrition and traffic he survived on the way to second.","gold":5},{"t":8545,"quote":"I didn't have the heart to take it from him on the first one.","context":"Eaton explains why he initially declined to fight teammate Andrew Player for the lucky-dog position.","gold":5},{"t":8697,"quote":"I just tried to stay consistent. I didn't try to overdrive it.","context":"Robertson describes how he managed Dover's severe right-front tire wear.","gold":5},{"t":8785,"quote":"If someone's faster, we'll go ahead and let them on by.","context":"Robertson describes the cooperative approach within the Ain't Dead Yet team.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Robertson, Eaton and Bittner. Robertson and Greg Klein shared hard-charger honors at plus 29 positions; Robertson started 30th and Klein 34th. The booth counted 14 cautions after the finish. Allen English joined the broadcast during the Vaught-Adamson incident at about 1:41, after Alan Brown and Adam Turner handled the opening portion. The spoken grid includes Lori as race control after the 35 drivers; she is not included in the participant field. Andrew Coffin remains the roster normalization for the caption-corrupted 'Andrew C' variants, and Dustyn Eaton is preserved as distinct from Dustin Wade.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"L9aunWtHDL4":{"recap":"The Alabama Jam brought 34 trucks to a strangely fog-shrouded Talladega for 94 laps of three-wide pack racing, with the Vigilante Force and Ain't Dead Yet squads trading control of the lanes all night. Long green-flag runs kept 31 trucks on the lead lap past halfway, but the race turned violent late: a lap-64 crash demolished Alan Vaught's 33 and sent birthday boy Kelly Keil hard into the inside wall, and the Big One with a handful of laps left swept up front-runner Albert Anderson and much of the pack, setting up a single-attempt green-white-checker. When a final-lap wreck erupted behind a six-truck breakaway, Kyle Vaught — shoved clear by teammate Trevor Robertson — took the checkers for his first career VRL win while Dustin Wade crossed the line through the grass. Robertson held on for second, Larry Dickerson stole third by a nose, and Dave Mayberry climbed 23 spots to fourth as the race's co-hard-charger; Alan Vaught's night ended early when he hit the wrong button and disconnected.","winner":"Kyle Vaught","podium":["Kyle Vaught","Trevor Robertson","Larry Dickerson"],"moments":[{"t":1074,"title":"First Blood in the Fog","summary":"Barely five laps in, side-by-side contact sends Craig Goodenough spinning through the infield grass for the first caution — Larry Dickerson tries to duck out of the mess and gets collected anyway.","tags":["craig-goodenough","larry-dickerson","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1317,"title":"Crew of the S.S. Whittenburg","summary":"With sponsor Ricky Whittenburg away on his yacht, the booth spirals into imagining life as his deckhands — 'Sir Ricky, can I bait your hook? Would you like a fresh towel?'","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2655,"title":"The Smoke Over Talladega","summary":"The booth finally explains the night's brutal haze: 'hoop houses' of illicit plants burning down the road — which is why drivers are giggling and asking their pit crews for snacks.","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3145,"title":"Vaughts Into the Wall","summary":"A misaligned push gets the 88 of Mike Adamson sideways, wading Kyle Vaught and Alan Vaught up against the outside wall — Jess bulldozes his way through with 'nowhere to go.'","tags":["mike-adamson","kyle-vaught","jess-vaught","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3990,"title":"The Lazy Susan — Move of the Race","summary":"Alan Vaught leaves himself a pocket of space, picks up a run and swings teammate Kelly Keil 'lazy Susan' style back around Albert Anderson — the booth calls it a pick-and-roll and the move of the race.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4623,"title":"Birthday Party Crasher","summary":"Mid fun-facts segment, a not-quite-square bump from the 68 turns the field loose: Alan Vaught's 33 gets 'absolutely demolished' on the outside wall while birthday boy Kelly Keil slams the inside wall.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-wade","trevor-robertson","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4863,"title":"Lori Lays Down the Law","summary":"Radio arguments over the caution order boil over until race control Lori Vaught — 'the saint of the league' — yells the whole field into silence, to the booth's delight.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5674,"title":"Turn-Four Pileup","summary":"A checkup off turn four catches Zachary Henin off guard — he clips Austin Paul just off-center and shoots him up the track into the 19, with the 89 spinning through the scramble.","tags":["zachary-henin","austin-paul","jack-dixon","craig-goodenough","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6453,"title":"The Big One","summary":"With a handful of laps left it finally happens: Albert Anderson gets grabbed by netcode just as he was breaking free, and nearly the entire lead pack — Robertson, Howell, Keil, Goodenough, Gonzalez, Bittner — goes for the ride.","tags":["albert-anderson","trevor-robertson","scott-howell","craig-goodenough","alejandro-gonzalez","josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6650,"title":"The Wrong X Button","summary":"Word comes from the chat that Alan Vaught hit the wrong button and disconnected himself from the race — the booth roasts him over his high-school typewriting classes.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6846,"title":"One Shot at Glory","summary":"The field stacks up for the official green-white-checker — one attempt only, 'this is for all the marbles' — with Kyle Vaught on the front row and Uncle Dave Mayberry lurking.","tags":["kyle-vaught","trevor-robertson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6925,"title":"Kyle's First — Chaos at the Line","summary":"At the white flag a wreck erupts behind a six-truck breakaway; Kyle Vaught, pushed by Trevor Robertson, holds off the carnage for his first career VRL win as Dustin Wade finishes through the grass and Dickerson steals third by a nose.","tags":["kyle-vaught","trevor-robertson","dustin-wade","larry-dickerson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1338,"quote":"Sir Ricky, can I bait your hook? Sir Ricky, would you like a fresh towel?","context":"the booth imagining life as deckhands on sponsor Ricky Whittenburg's yacht","gold":4},{"t":2667,"quote":"That's why we're hearing some drivers giggling and some of them asking for snacks from their pit crew.","context":"explaining the mysterious haze as smoke from illicit 'hoop houses' burning near the track","gold":5},{"t":4691,"quote":"And the 01 hit the inside wall so hard he may not make it to his next birthday.","context":"birthday boy Kelly Keil wrecking hard in the lap-64 pileup","gold":4},{"t":4863,"quote":"Poor Lori, the saint of the league, is having to just yell at these people — this is awesome.","context":"race control silencing the radio arguments under caution","gold":3},{"t":6453,"quote":"There we go, the big one! Oh no, Albert got netcode — he was going to be free and clear of all this chaos.","context":"the race-defining multi-truck wreck in the closing laps","gold":4},{"t":6968,"quote":"The 68 of Dustin Wade is going to be finishing this one through the grass as the 16 of Kyle Vaught picks up his first win — what just happened?","context":"the checkered-flag call on the chaotic final lap","gold":5},{"t":6989,"quote":"Well, I'll be — Kyle actually won a race. Kyle Vaught is your winner. Unbelievable.","context":"the booth's stunned reaction right after the finish","gold":4},{"t":7708,"quote":"All it takes is for one jackass to come flying up behind everybody and ruin the party.","context":"Albert Anderson's post-race spotlight interview on the Big One","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions. The league family surname heard as 'vot/vault/fought/VOD' is rendered Vaught (Jess and Lori Vaught run the league; son Kyle won). 'Kelly Keil' is heard variously as kill/Kuehl/keig. 'Jorge Rincon' could alternatively be Ranone/Ranon — captions split both ways. 'David Feit' (possibly Fite) and 'Andrew Cin' are as-heard and uncertain. Ricky Whittenburg (DND RaceGrafix, Ain't Dead Yet team) did not race — away on vacation. Lori Vaught served as race control, not a driver. Full finishing order was read on air: top 10 — Kyle Vaught, Trevor Robertson, Larry Dickerson, Dave Mayberry, Kelly Keil, Tim Pope, Zachary Henin, Dion Jones, Albert Anderson, Dustin Wade. The last soundbyte (t=7708) is from a driver interview, not the booth. Race: 94 laps, 3 cautions plus the late Big One, one-attempt green-white-checker finish; heavy fog/haze all night was a running storyline.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lbJFqG9ak38":{"recap":"Race 13 of VRL Season 11 — the playoff opener at the virtual Charlotte Motor Speedway — turned into a wreckfest early: Tim Pope got loose off turn four on the opening lap, contact from Derek Welch spun him, and the resulting Big One swept up a pile of playoff contenders, with three cautions on the board by lap 12 including an 11-truck backstretch melee the booth compared to Talladega. Polesitter John Osborne controlled much of the night and never ran outside roughly the top five until a heartbreaking wreck with five laps to go ended his bid in 17th. Alan Vaught, who started 12th and was collected in the lap-1 crash, made eight pit stops repairing his No. 33 and methodically climbed back through the chaos. On the race's lone green-white-checkered attempt, Pope wrecked in the dogleg coming to the white flag but the field raced on, and Vaught held off Dustyn Eaton and Derek Welch for the win. Kelly Kuehl and John McAdam completed the top five, with Vaught's son Kyle sixth.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Dustyn Eaton","Derek Welch"],"moments":[{"t":2462,"title":"The Big One on lap 1","summary":"Tim Pope gets loose in the middle of three and four on the opening lap, contact from Derek Welch completes the spin, and a chain reaction collects a swath of playoff contenders — Rooney, Vaught, Klein, Dixon, Adamson, Benfield and Whittenburg among them.","tags":["timothy-pope","derek-welch","scott-rooney","jess-vaught","chris-klein","jack-dixon","mike-adamson","stony-benfield","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2810,"title":"Broadcaster's curse hits in record time","summary":"Seconds after Chris apologizes for picking the already-wrecked Mike Adamson to win, caution two flies for Mike Everidge scraping the wall — 'the fastest I've ever won the picking.'","tags":["mike-everage","mike-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3096,"title":"Backstretch melee — three cautions in 12 laps","summary":"Kevin Hunt comes up the track, door-slams the 69, then comes down across Craig Goodnough and eleven trucks pile in through turn two and down the backstretch — a wreck the booth says belongs at Daytona or Talladega.","tags":["kevin-hunt","russ-kilgore","trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald","josh-bittner","dave-mayberry","dion-jones","mike-everage","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","larry-dickerson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3622,"title":"Kyle Vaught sacrifices his truck at pit exit","summary":"Avoiding Andrew Coffin's spun No. 10 after contact from Chris Klein, Kyle Vaught turns hard left and backs the 16 into the SAFER barrier at the end of pit lane — the booth praises him for wrecking himself rather than running someone over.","tags":["kyle-vaught","chris-klein","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4725,"title":"Welch wrestles the lead away from Osborne","summary":"After Osborne led from the pole, Derek Welch works the top lane in a hot three-truck battle — doors slamming with Dickerson in the mix — and finally takes the race lead away.","tags":["derek-welch","jonathan-osborne","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4995,"title":"Dickerson and Cool storm from the back to 1-2","summary":"Larry Dickerson, who started 30th, hooks the blue line to take the lead with 26th-starting Kelly Kuehl right behind him — the two deep-field starters running 1-2 before halfway.","tags":["larry-dickerson","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6032,"title":"Bryant's long-game strategy goes up in smoke","summary":"Laps after banking the pit stop that set up his one-fewer-stop gamble, Dillon Bryant is collected in a chain-reaction crash started when Gallagher gets the wall — heavy right-front suspension damage ends the 51's night in 25th.","tags":["dylan-bryant","john-gallagher","andrew-cauthan","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6673,"title":"David Feit nearly goes airborne","summary":"Kelly Kuehl slips up the track and clips the left rear, sending David Feit's truck skyward in one of the wildest-looking moments of the night — the booth reckons he escaped with barely any damage.","tags":["david-fite","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7494,"title":"'That seems like a vendetta' — Klein hits McAdam three times","summary":"Greg Klein drives into John McAdam on corner entry, then hits him again and again until the third shot spins him — the replay convinces the booth it was deliberate.","tags":["greg-cline","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7805,"title":"Dickerson slams the door and sparks a pileup","summary":"Racing back through the field after pitting from the lead, Dickerson closes the door hard on Jeremiah Burke; the ripple behind sends Kilgore up the track into Goodnough and McAdam, with Welch and Rooney caught up too.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore","john-mcadam","derek-welch","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8410,"title":"Heartbreak — Osborne wrecked with five to go","summary":"Polesitter John Osborne, who never fell further back than about fifth all night, gets nosed loose by a hard-charging Tim Pope, almost saves it, then slams the wall with the front suspension jacked half a foot to the right — collecting Kilgore and Bittner and ending his dominant run in 17th.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope","russ-kilgore","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8717,"title":"Vaught survives the green-white-checkered","summary":"On the one-and-done overtime attempt, Tim Pope wrecks in the dogleg coming to the white flag but no caution flies — Alan Vaught, up from 12th after eight pit stops, holds off Dustyn Eaton and Derek Welch to win the playoff opener and take a Polish victory lap.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","derek-welch","timothy-pope","russ-kilgore","kelly-keel","john-mcadam"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3016,"quote":"Thank god we're not spotting for these guys, right?","context":"half the field running near-identical red-white-and-blue Memorial Day schemes","gold":3},{"t":3103,"quote":"We need to start putting like an age limit on racing or something, you know.","context":"the third multi-truck wreck breaks out just 12 laps in","gold":4},{"t":3983,"quote":"I don't know that I've ever had one, Steve. — It's not what I heard.","context":"Josh Bittner's Ding Dongs paint scheme sparks booth innuendo","gold":4},{"t":5009,"quote":"Yeah, that kind of aged like a can of RC Cola. — I was thinking milk, but yeah, same thing.","context":"chat's 'Osborne in clean air will be hard to pass' take dies within a lap","gold":3},{"t":6046,"quote":"Oh, they had him. Dylan Bryant. Oh no. Well, that pit strategy bit him.","context":"Bryant collected in a wreck right after his one-stop gamble pit stop","gold":3},{"t":6885,"quote":"Is my living room couch the safest seat in the house tonight?","context":"the booth reads Albert Anderson's chat message as the cautions keep piling up","gold":4},{"t":7266,"quote":"Not picking on Larry here, Albert, but when does he not? That boy is hammered down every lap every week.","context":"chat says Dickerson will need to drive aggressively to recover from his pit gamble","gold":4},{"t":7498,"quote":"That seems like a vendetta to me. He hit him three times.","context":"Greg Klein spins John McAdam after repeated contact","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 11, Race 13 at Charlotte Motor Speedway (NASCAR Trucks), 133 laps scheduled, ~135 run with the green-white-checkered; race one of the playoffs (round of 12), broadcast on Track Limits Network. Winner's surname is heavily garbled in captions (VA/Va/Vaugh/Vaughn/Vault/Bot/bought) — 'Vaught' is a best-guess phonetic reconstruction; the closing sign-off caption reads 'Alan Vaughn'. Color commentator captioned as 'Chris Gones'/'Goings' — 'Goins' is a best guess. 'David Feit' and 'Craig Goodnough' spellings are as-heard best guesses. Full 34-truck finishing order is read at ~2:42:05 (9725s): Vaught, Eaton, Welch, Cool, McAdam, Kyle Vaught, Williams, Player, Dickerson, Pope, Bitner, Rooney, Burke, C. Klein, Kilgore, Fight, Osborne, Mayberry, Robertson, G. Klein, Gallagher, Hunt, Goodnough, Dobson, Bryant, Coffin, Wade, McDonnell, Jones, Everidge, Dixon, Benfield, Adamson, Whittenburg. A pre-show highlight reel (~0:29:43-0:30:51) contains badly garbled names from other footage (Tim Musk, Lockwood, Quinn, Reynolds, Rashard, etc.) — excluded from the driver list. League is run by Lori and Alan Vaught per the winner interview; next race Nashville Superspeedway.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lbL9-yRAmJI":{"recap":"VRL went dusty and dirty for its first-ever dirt race, dumping 30 trucks onto a dirt-covered Bristol Motor Speedway for 150 laps (75 miles) of sideways, cushion-chasing chaos with three fast repairs apiece. Returning driver Josh Buettner put the No. 84 on the pole, but the night turned into a duel between Jeremiah Burke's No. 753 Limitless Toyota and real-life ARCA driver Brayton Laster's No. 013, with Burke grabbing the lap-76 stage win on pit strategy. A caution-heavy second half — including an apparent iRacing glitch that threw a yellow seconds after the green, and JR Hollingsworth T-boning Dale Adamson hard enough to blow his engine — pushed the race into overtime when Laster's desperation slide job spun Jonah Long. On the green-white-checker final lap Laster sent one last slide job deep into the final corner, but Burke crossed back underneath to win, with Laster second and Buettner completing the podium in third. Burke, who said he led 89 laps, celebrated by promptly blowing his engine.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Brayton Laster","Josh Buettner"],"moments":[{"t":1370,"title":"Green flag: 30 trucks turning and burning on Bristol dirt","summary":"The field slips sideways off the initial start, Buettner and Vaught go door to door, and the booth marvels at four-wide dirt racing on the narrow half-mile.","tags":["jess-vaught","brayton-laster","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2178,"title":"Coffin hard into the wall — then his engine screams","summary":"Andrew Coffin's No. 10 goes hard into the outside wall for the caution, then sits stranded with the engine revving against the limiter and smoke pouring out — the booth diagnoses a hardware disconnect.","tags":["andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2917,"title":"Restart chaos: four-wide gamble ends in a pileup","summary":"A four-wide restart unravels into 'all chaos' — the No. 1 gets spun, Kelly Kuehl is up against the wall, and Sean McDonnell and Albert Anderson get swept into the mess.","tags":["david-fite","kelly-keel","shawn-mcdonald","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3154,"title":"Phantom yellow: iRacing glitches the restart","summary":"Green flag flies and the yellow comes out almost instantly with no visible wreck — caution lights stuck on, drivers racing on confused, and the booth calls it an iRacing glitch. Race control switches to single-file restarts afterward.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3384,"title":"Eaton shot out of a cannon to the lead","summary":"Dustyn Eaton rips the top side on the restart, takes the preferred line away from Brayton Laster, and rockets all the way to the race lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","brayton-laster"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3777,"title":"Burke steals the stage on strategy","summary":"Staying out while the leaders pit, Jeremiah Burke wins the lap-76 stage over Alan Vaught and Dustin Riehle, with Dave Mayberry's gamble netting him a top five.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","dustin-reilly","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4613,"title":"Slide job and crossback: Laster vs Burke","summary":"Laster works the cushion to the last inch, throws a slide job on Burke for the lead, but Burke answers with the crossover to keep the top spot — the race's defining battle heats up.","tags":["brayton-laster","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4635,"title":"Hollingsworth T-bones Dale Adamson","summary":"Dale Adamson goes around off the wall and JR Hollingsworth has nowhere to go, T-boning the No. 746 and blowing his own engine on the spot.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","dale-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5584,"title":"Mike Adamson nearly thrown over the top rope","summary":"A huge run from Eaton turns into contact down the frontstretch — 'oh man, Mercy' — and Mike Adamson is nearly launched over the pit wall.","tags":["dustin-eaton","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6361,"title":"Desperation slide job spins Long — overtime","summary":"Laster slides it in way too hot going for the lead, Jonah Long gets spun, and the resulting parking-lot pileup forces a one-shot green-white-checker finish.","tags":["brayton-laster","jonah-long","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6626,"title":"Last-corner slide job denied: Burke wins the war","summary":"White flag out, Laster all over Burke's bumper — he sends a full slide job into the final corner, but Burke counters with a big crossback and beats the squiggly No. 013 to the line, with Buettner third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","brayton-laster"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6798,"title":"Burke celebrates by blowing the engine","summary":"Trying to burn it down on a loose dirt surface, race winner Jeremiah Burke just blows the engine up instead — the booth loves every second of it.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1676,"quote":"It's slicker than deer guts on a doorknob out there on the track.","context":"sizing up the freshly dirt-covered Bristol surface early in the race","gold":4},{"t":1833,"quote":"You know what holds grip better than four tires is eight — if you can use somebody up to help keep you in the spot you need to be at.","context":"after Albert Anderson leans all over Timmy Bates on the restart","gold":4},{"t":2559,"quote":"That 14 machine — he is putting the Tang in orangutan here, hanging on for dear life.","context":"Dustyn Eaton wrestling his Team Tang truck sideways in a lead battle","gold":4},{"t":3396,"quote":"Man, talk about being shot out of a cannon, that 14 machine — he's all the way up there now into the lead.","context":"Eaton rockets from the restart straight to the race lead","gold":3},{"t":4490,"quote":"Leaned over to grab a drink or something and rubbed the inside wall — that's one of those 'my bad, I was sending a tweet' moments.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg gets squiggly and brushes the inside wall","gold":3},{"t":4566,"quote":"Equivalate? I gotta write that one down — Turner's gonna hear about that one.","context":"Alan Brown invents a word mid-broadcast and the booth cracks up","gold":3},{"t":5458,"quote":"She said, you know, enjoy tonight's poo show on dirt out there — she was expecting it to be a complete madness.","context":"the booth relays league admin Lori's pre-race prediction that never came true","gold":3},{"t":6626,"quote":"Sending it on deep — slide job in full effect for the o13! 753 counters with a big comeback, finds his way back across the line!","context":"the final-corner battle between Laster and Burke that decides the race","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble many names. 'David Feit' (#1) is the caption spelling and may actually be Feight or similar; 'Dustin Riehle' (#37) is a best guess from 'Dustin really/reeling'; 'Dustyn Eaton' is inferred from the booth twice calling him 'Dustin with a Y'. Burke's 89 laps led comes through garbled captions ('I let 89 laughs'). Russ Endicott's truck number is heard as both the 27 (grid rundown) and 'the 57 truck' (finish rundown). Robert Chipman and Greg Dobson registered but ran no laps (Dobson spotted for Limitless instead). Full finish order given at ~7960s: Burke, Laster, Buettner, Robertson, Long, Vaught, Player, Kuehl, Riehle, Mayberry for the top ten. Adam Turner is the booth's absent third man, mentioned only in running jokes.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"legttA4J7n4":{"recap":"Alan Vaught put his Gen 6 Ford on pole at Watkins Glen with a 1:10.663 and immediately separated himself from David Feit, Tim Pope, and the rest of the 32-car field. The caution-free road race quickly became a contest of precision and survival: Dustyn Eaton suffered a probable connection failure into the bus-stop tires, while Jack Dixon, Scott Rooney, and others had their own off-course moments. Vaught retained control through both green-flag pit cycles, but Trevor Robertson's early final stop undercut first Fite and then Pope to secure second place. Pope recovered from right-front damage and passed Fite late for third, while Vaught finished a dominant pole-to-checkers drive nearly 20 seconds ahead.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Trevor Robertson","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":398,"title":"Vaught sets a blistering Glen pole","summary":"Vaught's 1:10.663 lap puts the No. 33 on pole by clear road-course pace ahead of David Feit, Dillon Bryant, Robertson, and Pope.","tags":["jess-vaught","david-fite","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"qualifying"},{"t":914,"title":"Vaught launches into the lead","summary":"Vaught wins the run into Turn 1 and leads Bryant, Fite, Pope, and Robertson through the esses as the 55-lap race begins.","tags":["jess-vaught","dylan-bryant","david-fite","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1107,"title":"Welch attacks Robertson through the bus stop","summary":"Returning truck-race winner Derek Welch dives outside Robertson at the bus-stop entry, runs through the grass on exit, and then loses places to Riehle and Jeremiah Burke.","tags":["derek-welch","trevor-robertson","dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1680,"title":"A connection failure destroys Riehle's contender","summary":"Running fourth, Riehle's car abruptly snaps hard left in the bus stop and pounds the Armco and tire pack; the booth identifies a likely internet or hardware interruption, ending a potential winning run.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"technical"},{"t":2287,"title":"Vaught opens the first green-flag cycle","summary":"The leader stops around lap 20 for four tires and fuel, navigating Watkins Glen's unusual right-side fueling procedure before rejoining without losing command of the race.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2467,"title":"Dixon spins through the bus-stop grass","summary":"Dixon's entry looks clean, but a tire touches the grass and the rear steps out; he reaches the barrier and returns to pit road with damage.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3431,"title":"Pope outbrakes Fite for second","summary":"After shadowing Fite, Pope carries the outside momentum from Turn 11 and brakes later into Turn 1 to clear the No. 1 for the runner-up position.","tags":["timothy-pope","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3591,"title":"Robertson and Fite go side by side through the esses","summary":"Robertson attacks Fite around the outside of Turn 11, they lock brakes and make light contact while racing two-wide through the esses, and Fite narrowly retains third.","tags":["trevor-robertson","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3647,"title":"Robertson commits to the undercut","summary":"Unable to finish the pass on track, Robertson pits one lap before Fite; the fresh-tire lap gains enough time to take the position when Fite completes his service.","tags":["trevor-robertson","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3788,"title":"The leaders make their final stops","summary":"Vaught and Pope pit together while Bryant and Burke also take service; Robertson's short pit cycles him ahead of both Fite and Pope into second, 16 seconds behind Vaught.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4763,"title":"Pope wrestles third from Fite","summary":"With laps running out, Fite runs wide in Turn 10 and Pope repeats his outside Turn 11 move, dragging ahead down the straight and clearing him into Turn 1.","tags":["timothy-pope","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4970,"title":"Vaught completes the Watkins Glen rout","summary":"Vaught crosses the line after an unchallenged final lap to win from pole; Robertson follows in second and Pope brings the damaged No. 7 home third.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":292,"quote":"Watkins Glen International is more than just a racetrack; it's the birthplace of post-war road racing in North America.","context":"The opening feature introduces the historic circuit","gold":5},{"t":1465,"quote":"The key to success on a lot of these road courses is just keep it between the paint.","context":"The booth explains the discipline demanded by the Glen","gold":5},{"t":2571,"quote":"Keeping it to the left of that white line, off the racing line, until you can get through the carousel—big-time bravo to Scott Rooney.","context":"Rooney safely rejoins after crashing in the bus stop","gold":4},{"t":3625,"quote":"It's not for the race lead, but you know what? I don't care. Action is action.","context":"The booth enjoys Robertson and Fite's fierce battle for third","gold":5},{"t":4750,"quote":"Five laps to go here from the Glen. Allen Vaught checked out—the battle to watch is David Fite and Tim Pope.","context":"The broadcast frames the closing podium contest","gold":4},{"t":5358,"quote":"I tried to make sure I wasn't overdriving the car and put them in a position where they'd have to overdrive theirs to catch me.","context":"Winner Alan Vaught explains how he managed the dominant lead","gold":5},{"t":5581,"quote":"I did undercut Fite there. That last pit stop, that's the only way I could get around him.","context":"Runner-up Trevor Robertson confirms his decisive strategy","gold":5},{"t":5790,"quote":"I really don't run road courses at all. The only ones I've ever run are in this league.","context":"Third-place Tim Pope reflects on an unlikely road-course podium","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 10, Round 11 at Watkins Glen according to seasons_map.json. The race used Gen 6 Cup cars for 55 laps on the 2.45-mile Cup layout, with 65% fuel, unlimited tire sets, no fast repairs, and local yellows only unless administrators deemed a full-course caution necessary; no full-course caution was shown. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Vaught-Robertson-Pope podium and reads all 32 classified drivers. Josh Bittner was described as a start-and-park entry that did not take the green. Canonical roster spellings are used for Alan Vaught, Dustyn Eaton, David Feit, Craig Goodenough, Michael Everage, Ricky Whittenburg, and other caption variants. All timestamps fall within the 6,350-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"LGPKjjoN3QE":{"recap":"Alan Vaught put the No. 33 on pole and controlled much of Pocono's long green opening. The quiet scoreboard hid real danger: Russ Kilgore suffered a massive impact that did not produce a caution, while Tim Pope shut off the engine during a fuel-saving run and Josh Bittner fought Craig Goodenough for position. The race finally broke open when Kyle Vaught and Mike Adamson made contact during a side-draft exchange, spinning Adamson and bringing out the first yellow. From there the restarts became the story. Jonathan Osborne, Chris Klein, and Dustyn Eaton were caught in one scramble; Kelly Kuehl hit the wall in another sequence; and a four-wide move off turn one became the Big One, collecting Alan Vaught and several contenders. A later chain reaction added more damage, but a five-wide escape showed how narrowly the field avoided an even larger pileup. Derek Welch's late spin forced the only green-white-checkered attempt. Dillon Bryant controlled that restart and cleared the fight behind him to claim his first win of the season. Jack Dixon finished second, and Austin Paul completed a run from 20th on the grid to take third. Pocono began as a fuel-and-track-position exercise and ended as a test of who could survive each compression point without surrendering the final restart.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Jack Dixon","Austin Paul"],"moments":[{"t":2066,"title":"Kilgore's monster hit — and no caution flies","summary":"Russ Kilgore gets the wall in the marbles and drives straight down into traffic with a massive impact — and iRacing never throws the yellow. The booth rewinds it in disbelief; Kilgore's night is done, 79 laps down.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4140,"title":"Tim Pope's engine-off fuel-save masterclass","summary":"Pope stretches his stint to the full 23 laps by coasting corners with the engine barely running — the booth goes onboard to watch his tach drop to idle mid-corner.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4324,"title":"Bittner and Goodenough go to war for the lead","summary":"Side by side for a lap and a half, drag racing to the line and banging doors into turn one, until Goodenough takes damage but roots the 84 up the track and takes the race lead.","tags":["josh-bittner","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4816,"title":"Kyle dumps Adamson — first caution of the night","summary":"Just as the booth jokes about the broadcast curse, Kyle Vaught spins Mike Adamson in a side-draft gone wrong for the night's first yellow. Both booth and chat rule it unintentional.","tags":["kyle-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5190,"title":"Restart chaos sends Osborne around","summary":"Immediately off the restart the field goes three wide out of turn one — Chris Klein and Jonathan Osborne meet in the middle with Dustyn Eaton outside, and Osborne spins for caution two. 'Just a racing deal.'","tags":["jonathan-osborne","chris-klein","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5778,"title":"Kelly Kuehl's monster shot into the wall","summary":"Kelly Kuehl smacks the wall on exit and gets sent to the inside of the racetrack with a hard impact, drawing caution three.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6150,"title":"Five-wide through turn one — and everyone survives","summary":"The restart fans out four and five wide through turn one with drivers scattering everywhere; Gallagher saves a huge moment and somehow the whole field gets through clean.","tags":["john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6320,"title":"The Big One collects the dominant 33","summary":"Four wide out of turn one, contact sends Alan Vaught — the class of the field all night — hard into the wall along with Gaines, Adamson, Chris Klein, and Dion Jones. The championship picture flips upside down in one corner.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough","jason-gaines","mike-adamson","chris-klein","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6744,"title":"Chain reaction takes out Dickerson","summary":"Player squeezes Osborne into the wall, the contact right-hooks the 13 up into Larry Dickerson, and another restart goes yellow — caution five.","tags":["andrew-player","jonathan-osborne","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7135,"title":"Welch spins fighting for the podium — overtime","summary":"Battling for third with five to go, Welch turns down as Bittner sticks a nose in and goes around, collecting Kyle Vaught with big playoff implications — Alan Vaught threads the needle, and the race goes to a green-white-checkered.","tags":["derek-welch","josh-bittner","kyle-vaught","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7547,"title":"Bryant seals his first win of the season","summary":"On the lone green-white-checkered attempt Dillon Bryant clears the field, takes the white with Jack Dixon a tenth off his tailgate, and cruises through turn three unchallenged to win at Pocono — his first of the season.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jack-dixon","austin-paul","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2079,"quote":"This is going to be a day-ender for Russ Kilgore. Would have been a life-ender if it was in real life.","context":"Kilgore's monster unflagged hit into the wall","gold":5},{"t":2262,"quote":"For the record, neither one of those guys I talked about not going too wide through the tunnel.","context":"Eaton and Bittner both botch the tunnel turn right after Chris's driving tips","gold":3},{"t":4816,"quote":"And the caution comes out just as we were talking about it. The broadcast curse.","context":"First yellow flies the instant the booth discusses staying green","gold":3},{"t":4840,"quote":"Oh, Kyle V just dumps him.","context":"Replay of Kyle Vaught spinning Mike Adamson for the first caution","gold":4},{"t":6041,"quote":"Takes about two minutes to get around here under caution. So, if you need a quick beer or a snack, get it now.","context":"Long Pocono caution laps before the 15-to-go restart","gold":4},{"t":7323,"quote":"I think I'm having a stroke, Chris. I was just watching the stream chat here and I was reading something and now it's gone.","context":"A stream chat message gets retracted mid-read before the green-white-checkered","gold":4},{"t":7608,"quote":"No challenge from Dixon. He'll cross the stripe first and he'll win it in Pocono.","context":"The winning call for Dillon Bryant's first victory of the season","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 11, Race 17, 85 laps at Pocono (finished in overtime via the single green-white-checkered attempt); six cautions, all in the final third after 50+ caution-free laps. Several surnames are best-guess reconstructions from garbled auto-captions: the 'Vaught' family name (Alan #33, Kyle #16, plus league admin Lori) is rendered as VA/Vot/Vaugh/Vaughn/Vault/Bot/Ba; 'Craig Goodenough' appears as Gooden/Gooduff/Good Enough; broadcaster surname 'Gones' spelling uncertain. An unidentified No. 13 truck was involved in the caution-five wreck. Albert Anderson made seven pit stops with an unexplained issue but still finished 11th. Guest analyst Chris Gones runs the Num Thumbs Racing League and is not a VRL driver. Full finishing order was read on air (Bryant, Dixon, A. Paul, Pope, Goodenough, Player, Coffin, McAdam, Gallagher, G. Klein top 10).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lGYhmiqWmLo":{"recap":"VRL broke from its usual Wednesday slot for a special Monday-night All-Star Qualifier at Dover's Monster Mile, with 18 drivers fighting across three stages for the last 10 spots in Wednesday's Premiere Series All-Star race. Scott Rooney was lights-out from the front, stretching his lead past 2.4 seconds to claim Stage 1's automatic ticket, and John Schoenbachler stole Stage 2 on a two-tire gamble, holding off John McAdam's four fresh tires by a few tenths. The 50-lap finale turned into pure survival: a massive pileup launched Andrew Coffin's #10 airborne over the #16, and Kyle Vaught wrecked coming off pit lane while leading during the late green-flag cycle, falling a lap down. Dion Jones then crashed out of fifth with two laps to go, and when the caution flew again on the green-white-checker attempt, Jesse Reading won under yellow ahead of Sean McDonnell. Reading, McDonnell, Aaron Warren, Andrew Coffin, John McAdam, Kevin Hunt and Scott Milner claimed the seven transfer spots, with a 21st All-Star berth drawn at random after the broadcast.","winner":"Jesse Redding","podium":["Jesse Redding","Sean McDonnell","Aaron Warren"],"moments":[{"t":1515,"title":"Spun before lap one is in the books","summary":"Seconds after the green, Aaron Warren's #22 catches the apron off the backstretch, bounces up into Dion Jones and sends him spinning into the outside wall for an instant caution.","tags":["dion-jones","aaron-warren"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2110,"title":"Rooney runs off and hides in Stage 1","summary":"Scott Rooney jumps out at the green and is never touched, stretching the gap past 2.4 seconds before taking the Stage 1 win — the night's first automatic All-Star transfer.","tags":["scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2139,"title":"Show me the money, Mr. Announcer","summary":"The instant Lori pulls Stage 1 winner Scott Rooney from the race, the open mic chirps 'Show me the money, Mr. Announcer' before Alan can even start the victory interview.","tags":["scott-rooney"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2397,"title":"Player slips, Vaught pounces for the lead","summary":"On the Stage 2 restart Andrew Player gets badly out of shape off the corner and Kyle Vaught's #16 sweeps by to take over the lead.","tags":["kyle-vaught","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2858,"title":"Milner spins into the pack","summary":"Scott Milner's #19 gets loose underneath traffic and spins, collecting John Gallagher and Dave Mayberry for the second Stage 2 caution.","tags":["scott-milner","john-gallagher","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3295,"title":"Schoenbachler's two-tire heist","summary":"A rights-only gamble puts the Hooters #12 out front, and John Schoenbachler holds off John McAdam's four fresh tires by a few tenths to steal Stage 2 and punch his All-Star ticket.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3708,"title":"Transfer fight ends in the wall","summary":"Battling over the final transfer spot, Michael Brooks holds Dave Mayberry tight with no room to track out — they tangle, Chandler Paul plows in, and Mayberry is left with severe tire and steering damage.","tags":["michael-brooks","dave-mayberry","chandler-paul","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4045,"title":"The Big One: the 10 goes for a ride","summary":"Kyle Vaught barely clips Sean McDonnell on corner entry and the field explodes — Andrew Coffin's #10 is launched airborne over the #16 and rides down the backstretch before rolling to the inside barrier, with Dobson, Klein, Warren, Brooks and Chandler Paul all swept in. Greg Dobson then pushes Coffin's truck back onto its wheels in a great show of sportsmanship.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","kyle-vaught","shawn-mcdonald","greg-dobson","greg-cline","aaron-warren","michael-brooks","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4740,"title":"Leader wrecks coming off pit lane","summary":"Pitting from the lead in the green-flag cycle, Kyle Vaught gets loose coming off pit lane and destroys his front end, falling a lap down and out of the transfer picture.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4977,"title":"Jones' heartbreak with two to go","summary":"Running fifth and safely inside the transfer zone, Dion Jones gets loose with two laps to go and crashes with Greg Klein's #92, collecting Dave Mayberry and setting up a one-shot green-white-checker.","tags":["dion-jones","greg-cline","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5240,"title":"Reading wins it under yellow","summary":"The caution flies again on the green-white-checker attempt and freezes the field — after a brief scoring scare when McDonnell reaches the line first behind the pace truck, Jesse Reading is declared the winner and the top seven lock in their All-Star spots.","tags":["jesse-redding","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1114,"quote":"Dover isn't just a one-mile oval. It's a concrete bull ring with teeth, man.","context":"Alan's track intro before the green flag","gold":4},{"t":1248,"quote":"Hey, Mike. It's down in the booth, buddy. You got me?","context":"Alan's driver call-up catchphrase — his first two interview attempts got dead air","gold":3},{"t":2060,"quote":"Maybe a little rocket fuel, a little NOS maybe up in his roll cage. I don't know, man. He is definitely gone.","context":"answering chat's demand for a tech inspection on Rooney's dominant 023","gold":3},{"t":3675,"quote":"Now he's going to be hunted down like a dog by that number 10 right behind him.","context":"Dave Mayberry clinging to the final transfer spot","gold":3},{"t":4136,"quote":"Man, the 10 gets airborne. It goes for a ride down the backstretch.","context":"the Big One replay — Andrew Coffin launched over the 16","gold":4},{"t":5056,"quote":"I ate [expletive] coming out of the pits, destroyed myself. So, it was fun racing up front with y'all while it lasted.","context":"Kyle Vaught on the radio after wrecking away the lead","gold":4},{"t":5588,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, but above all else, stay vigilant.","context":"Alan's signature league sign-off","gold":4},{"t":5600,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing.","context":"the final words of the broadcast","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Special Monday-night broadcast (2026-05-18) feeding Wednesday's All-Star race; stage 1 and 2 winners (Rooney, Schoenbachler) were removed from the race after winning per format, so the final rundown lists them last by design. Race ended under caution during the one-shot green-white-checker; the cause of that final caution is never shown. The 21st All-Star entry came from an off-air random draw whose result is not on tape. Name cautions: the #16 is rendered Kyle Watt/Kyle Vault/Kyle Va/Kyot — surname is almost certainly Vaught (chat: 'feels like the old days seeing Va in P1'); best guess 'Kyle Vaught', though roster.json maps similar garbles (Calvault/Calvot) to Alan Vaught and also lists Alan Vaught — may need reconciling. Stage 2 winner used roster spelling 'John Schoenbachler' (roster has three fragmented entries for him). Greg Dobson (#085, New Market, Ontario — one of two Canadians with McDonnell) is also captioned 'Greg Dawson'. Scott Rooney (#023, Salt Lake City, Utah) is clear on tape but not yet in roster.json. Booth is Alan (play-by-play) with wife Lori as race admin — likely the roster's Alan Vaught and Lori Vogt, but surnames are never stated on tape. 'Show me the money' speaker is attributed to Rooney from context only. First ~10:30 of the stream is pre-race music; racing content begins at ~10:39.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Lk2u8KzMxIw":{"recap":"VRL's truck series hit the newly repaved and reconfigured Atlanta, which the booth promised would race like a superspeedway draft fest — and it delivered a caution-filled pack race. Robert Chipman dominated qualifying from the pole, but a caution that landed mid pit-cycle flipped the field and handed track position to Tim Pope, Trevor Robertson, and Josh Bittner, who grabbed the halfway stage win. The second half unraveled into restart stack-ups, a Greg Klein quad-oval crash that collected Jack Dixon, a backstretch melee after which Sean McDonnell was disqualified and removed from the server, and a late Big One that sent league owner Alan Vaught backwards along the wall for three-quarters of a mile. On the one-attempt green-white-checker, Tim Pope completed a 28th-to-first hard-charger drive to win, with Jorge Rincon second and John Gallagher stealing the final podium spot on the outside at the line.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jorge Rincon","John Gallagher"],"moments":[{"t":1510,"title":"Eaton takes the point from the pole-sitter","summary":"After long patient two-by-two running, Dustyn Eaton finally got out in front of pole-sitter Robert Chipman and camped out on the low line to control the race.","tags":["dustin-eaton","robert-chipman"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1990,"title":"Pit-cycle caution flips the field","summary":"Dave Mayberry spun and Chandler Paul went sliding through the grass right in the middle of the green-flag pit cycle; everyone who had just pitted was shuffled to the back, a field reversal that set up the entire second half of the race.","tags":["dave-mayberry","chandler-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2153,"title":"The booth's influencer era begins","summary":"During an extended caution the booth plotted their pivot to becoming influencers — AAA skincare routine videos, daily mustache-combing content, and chasing that silver YouTube plaque.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2677,"title":"Three-wide brawl to the halfway stage","summary":"A furious three-wide shuffle to the halfway stripe with Pope threading the needle; Josh Bittner grabbed the stage win over Dillon Bryant and Trevor Robertson as the yellow flew at the break.","tags":["josh-bittner","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","brayton-laster"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3090,"title":"Restart stack-up — Evans hits neutral","summary":"Earl Evans put his truck in neutral on the restart and stacked the field up, collecting Greg Klein and a very upset Albert Anderson.","tags":["earl-evans","greg-cline","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3395,"title":"Chipman spins Dickerson into the pack","summary":"Dickerson checked up, Chipman tapped him and spun him into Chandler Paul; Jack Dixon somehow threaded the wreck, telling chat he thought he peed himself.","tags":["robert-chipman","larry-dickerson","chandler-paul","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4362,"title":"Klein finds the quad-oval wall","summary":"The reconfigured quad oval finally bit — Greg Klein got into the wall and into Jack Dixon's 07 with heavy contact that tore both trucks up.","tags":["greg-cline","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4755,"title":"Backstretch melee","summary":"Kyle Vaught slid up into Adamson shooting the gap, Adamson had nowhere to go and turned Chipman, and the backstretch erupted — collecting Anderson, Bryant, and Austin Paul in the chaos.","tags":["kyle-vaught","mike-adamson","robert-chipman","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4798,"title":"Sean McDonnell disqualified mid-race","summary":"In a move the booth said they'd almost never seen, Sean McDonnell was disqualified and removed from the server after the backstretch wreck — the booth figured his anger on the main radio channel got the best of him, prompting a lecture on venting in private channels.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5088,"title":"The Big One — Vaught backwards along the wall","summary":"League owner Alan Vaught tried to shoot up the middle three-wide, got turned up the track, and rode the wall backwards for three-quarters of a mile as the big wreck brought out the yellow and set up a one-attempt shootout.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5511,"title":"Pope completes the 27-spot charge","summary":"On the unofficial green-white-checker, Pope cleared long-time leader Trevor Robertson with a push from Rincon while Gallagher made 'something out of nothing' on the outside — Pope capping a 28th-to-first drive as both hard charger and race winner.","tags":["timothy-pope","george-rincon","john-gallagher","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1364,"quote":"As you like to say, Adam — it's a simulation, not a game.","context":"The booth's signature catchphrase, dropped while praising the pack racing","gold":4},{"t":2909,"quote":"Dave Mayberry just came over the radio and told Bittner, 'You're on my poop list.' — Oh no, don't say it like that.","context":"Radio chatter relayed during the halfway caution","gold":4},{"t":3140,"quote":"He put his car in neutral and decided that was a good idea.","context":"On Earl Evans stacking up the field on a restart","gold":3},{"t":3153,"quote":"I've downshifted and blown the engine and turned sideways and crashed everybody in the race before — that wasn't even on purpose.","context":"Booth confession while forgiving Evans' restart blunder","gold":4},{"t":3455,"quote":"Jack the Ripper out there saying, 'I think I just peed myself, I don't know how I made it through there.'","context":"Reading Jack Dixon's chat message after he threaded the Dickerson wreck","gold":4},{"t":4027,"quote":"He probably just doesn't understand the empirical system... the Imperial system. And I love empirical data. The words are hard.","context":"Fumbling 'imperial' while joking about a frustrated Canadian driver on the radio","gold":3},{"t":5402,"quote":"We're on The Struggle Bus. Our leader might have got taken away by aliens... he probably had too much Taco Bell.","context":"On producer Alan Brown vanishing mid-broadcast with a stomach bug","gold":3},{"t":5545,"quote":"It looked like Pope, Rincon and Gallagher — one, two, three! John Gallagher able to sneak up on the outside there and make something out of nothing.","context":"The finish call as Pope completes his 28th-to-first charge","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Second-place driver's surname is garbled throughout the captions (Rincon / Cohn / McCone / Cone); the interview confirms first name George, and 'Jorge Rincon' is the most frequent caption form, used as best guess. 'Dustyn Eaton' spelling inferred from the booth's running 'Dustin with a Y' joke. Booth naming is caption-garbled: the intro reads as Alan Brown but the sign-off is 'for Alan Brown and Adam Turner, I'm Alan English'; Brown was ill with a stomach bug and dropped off mid-broadcast. Results were announced as unofficial pending race administration review. Sean McDonnell's mid-race disqualification reason was booth speculation (radio conduct), not confirmed. Finishing order beyond the top 15 was read from a heavily garbled rundown.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"LkigJl7LoF4":{"recap":"Round 7 of VRL Premiere Series Season 14 brought the field to virtual Martinsville for the Clockwork Fool 225, a 225-lap short-track slugfest that racked up 21 cautions. Mike Adamson's 88 Mopar machine took the lead on the opening lap and controlled most of the night, but a surprise pit stop with 21 laps to go buried him back to a ninth-place finish. The night's wildest sequence came mid-race, when Dustyn Eaton spun directly in front of Kyle Vaught during a live in-race interview — Vaught threaded the wreck 'like the Matrix' as Tony Benfield's truck went up on its side. Out of the late green-flag pit shuffle, Jorge Rincon's 28 Goodweiser truck emerged with the lead, and he held off points leader Albert Anderson over the final six laps to score his first win of the season. Anderson settled for second, with Jacob Alesia climbing 19 spots to complete the podium.","winner":"Jorge Rincon","podium":["Jorge Rincon","Albert Anderson","Jacob Alesia"],"moments":[{"t":1020,"title":"Pole sitter spins on lap 5","summary":"Polesitter Sean McDonnell goes around after contact with Craig Goodenough's 89, dropping the Air Force 23 to the tail of the field just laps into the race.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1245,"title":"'Wrecking, wrecking, wrecking' — the first Big One","summary":"A curb-hop into turn three triggers an accordion pileup on lap 16 that collects eight-plus trucks, including the already-wounded McDonnell.","tags":["dion-jones","russ-kilgore","john-schoenbachler","scott-milner","michael-brooks","greg-dobson","aaron-warren","tom-barish","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2014,"title":"Goodenough punted into the outside wall","summary":"On a restart, Dustyn Eaton's 14 gets in a touch hot and sends the 89 spinning into the outside wall, ripping off the left-front fender in a series with no fast repairs.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3059,"title":"Spain and Kill ignite the pileup","summary":"Gordon Spain dives under Kelly Kuehl's 01, they touch, and trucks pile in behind — the 31, 99, 83 and 75 all collect pieces in the night's eighth caution.","tags":["gordon-spain","kelly-keel","jacob-alicia","albert-anderson","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4515,"title":"'Like the Matrix, baby' — Vaught dodges the Big One live on air","summary":"Mid-interview with the booth, Kyle Vaught threads a multi-truck wreck as Dustyn Eaton hits the auto-spin ahead of him and Tony Benfield's 75 tips up onto its side before landing back on its wheels.","tags":["kyle-vaught","dustin-eaton","stony-benfield","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4760,"title":"Netcode spins the 4, the field threads the needle","summary":"A slight bit of netcode sends Dion Jones' 4 around in traffic and somehow everybody misses him — 'these are great drivers, folks.'","tags":["dion-jones","tom-barish"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5788,"title":"Adamson slices back to the point","summary":"After burying himself in traffic with a pit stop, Mike Adamson carves back through the field and retakes the lead from the 31, capping a dominant mid-race charge.","tags":["mike-adamson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6330,"title":"Caution wrecks the green-flag pit cycle","summary":"A yellow lands mid pit-cycle and scrambles the running order — drivers argue over the wave-around on open mics while race admin Lori adds an extra pace lap to sort the field out.","tags":["george-rincon","kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6705,"title":"Adamson's shock late pit call","summary":"Having led most of the night, Mike Adamson surprises the booth by pitting with just 21 laps to go — a gamble that leaves him ninth at the finish.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6875,"title":"Kill turned out of second with 15 to go","summary":"Battling the fresher-tired 75 for second, Kelly Kuehl's 01 gets its nose cut off and spins — 'Kelly, I think you came down on me, buddy' — dropping him from contention to 21st.","tags":["kelly-keel","stony-benfield"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7065,"title":"Benfield spun on the restart","summary":"Greg Dobson doesn't quite wrap the bottom and turns last week's Darlington winner Tony Benfield out of the top four, ending his shot at back-to-back wins.","tags":["stony-benfield","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7340,"title":"Rincon takes the Clockwork Fool 225","summary":"Jorge Rincon takes the white flag, absorbs a final dive from points leader Albert Anderson into turn three, and brings the 28 Goodweiser truck home up eight spots from ninth for his first win of the season.","tags":["george-rincon","albert-anderson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":536,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream. This is VRN, your trusted leader in e-motorsports.","context":"the broadcast's signature intro bumper","gold":4},{"t":1158,"quote":"Martinsville does not reward fearlessness. It rewards control, composure, and the ability to survive the beating.","context":"pre-race scene-setter on the paperclip","gold":4},{"t":1251,"quote":"Wrecking. Wrecking. Wrecking. They're wrecking again. Caution is out. Caution is out.","context":"calling the first multi-truck pileup on lap 16","gold":4},{"t":1806,"quote":"Barney, our flag man, is going to get a sore arm tonight... a bigger right arm than a left arm by the time this is over. Maybe a little tendonitis.","context":"the booth's running gag as the cautions stacked up","gold":3},{"t":3424,"quote":"That's what you call a gentleman driver, folks. Somebody who's not just going to pull back in in a really reckless rejoin.","context":"Scott Rooney parking his wounded truck out of everyone's way","gold":3},{"t":4533,"quote":"Oh, that was nuts. I can't believe I dodged that. Like the Matrix, baby.","context":"Kyle Vaught, live on air mid-interview, threading a multi-truck wreck","gold":5},{"t":7995,"quote":"It didn't really affect the truck. Truck was fast, man. Fast. Bad fast.","context":"winner Jorge Rincon in the victory interview","gold":4},{"t":8317,"quote":"Until next time, race fans. Remember, stay sharp, stay fast, and above all else, stay Vigilante.","context":"the broadcast sign-off catchphrase","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is garbled throughout the auto-captions (Rencon/Rinkcon/Rancon/RCON/Raycon/Vincon); 'Jorge Rincon' is a best guess — he drives the 28 for Goodweiser Motorsports out of Cumming, Georgia. 'Kyle Vaught' (#16, High Point NC) and 'Chris Gones' (#1, could be Gomes/Goans) are also best-guess spellings. 'Bob Beish of Pass Christian, Mississippi' is likely a mis-caption of Tom Barish (#35) and was folded into that driver. 'Dylan Hill' was folded into Kelly Kuehl (both tied to Oshkosh, WI). Booth said the race had '21 or 22' cautions; the running count on air reached 21. Winner's thank-yous mention 'you and Ricky in the booth,' but only Alan was heard commentating with Lori admining. Race is Round 7 of Season 14; next event noted as Easter-break fun races April 8, then Bristol April 15.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lnZ4tYhgdUQ":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League hit the 2.66-mile Talladega superspeedway for 94 laps of truck pack racing with a massive 35-driver field that stayed shockingly intact early — every single truck on the lead lap deep into the night. Team Tang flexed first, sweeping the top three in stage points as Jonah Long grabbed the Stage 1 win, but the wrecks kept stacking up: a stage-break teammate tangle between Dustin Riehle and Alan Vaught (who then dropped offline to connection issues), a mid-race Big One that thinned the field, and a late squeeze that collected contenders Dave Mayberry and Andrew Coffin while Albert Anderson escaped untouched. It all came down to a green-white-checker drag race out of turn four, where a three- and four-wide melee erupted — one 747 literally launching into the air to meet another 747 — behind the leaders. John Gallagher threaded the No. 123 Kingsford F-150 through the chaos for his first VRL win, breaking the 'broadcaster curse' after being interviewed mid-race, with Daniel Baker second and Ricky Whittenburg third in the Double Nickel 55.","winner":"John Gallagher","podium":["John Gallagher","Daniel Baker","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":1130,"title":"Booth tries to dodge a falling satellite","summary":"Pre-race bit about a 600-pound satellite deorbiting that night; Brown says with his luck he'd aim for the middle of the Pacific and it would land in the middle of Africa.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2340,"title":"Taylor spins — first caution flies on lap 17","summary":"Mike Taylor goes around mid-pack after charging up through the field, collecting Dion Jones and Kelly Kuehl while Russ Endicott and others barely thread the wreckage.","tags":["mike-taylor","dion-jones","kelly-keel","russ-endicott"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2686,"title":"Earl Evans: one hand on the wheel, one on the pizza","summary":"The booth recalls catching Earl Evans on camera in practice cruising Talladega one-handed while eating a slice of pizza — 'hand on the pizza, hand on the beer, drive with my knees.'","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2780,"title":"Vaught's monster apron save as the wreck erupts behind","summary":"A push from the 37 sends Alan Vaught's 33 sideways down to the apron — he saves a near-30-degree slide — while behind him Albert Anderson gets spun high and Dale Adamson is collected in the checkup.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-reilly","albert-anderson","dale-adamson","david-kelly","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4288,"title":"Team-on-team violence at the stage break","summary":"Dustin Riehle's bump-draft on teammate Alan Vaught goes wrong — the 33 gets loose and the wreck sweeps up the 37, 81 and 28, with Jorge Rincon taking a tumble. Vaught then drops offline to packet loss.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-reilly","jonathan-osborne","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4501,"title":"Jonah Long wins Stage 1 — Team Tang goes 1-2-3","summary":"Team Tang locks out the top of the stage with Long, Eaton and Wade 1-2-3; Long admits in the booth interview they would not have made it on fuel without the caution.","tags":["jonah-long","dustin-eaton","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5010,"title":"The Big One thins the field","summary":"A lane-change bump from the 14 triggers a pileup that snags Endicott, Bittner, Rincon, Jones, Chipman, Dixon, Whittenburg and Everidge — 'that one took out a good chunk of this field.'","tags":["dustin-eaton","russ-endicott","josh-bittner","george-rincon","dion-jones","robert-chipman","jack-dixon","ricky-whittenburg","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5815,"title":"Squeeze play wrecks Mayberry and Coffin — Anderson's Houdini escape","summary":"Three-wide ten rows deep turns nearly four-wide; Mayberry comes down, Coffin has nowhere to go, and a huge chunk of the pack gets snagged while race leader Albert Anderson escapes untouched — 'bald eagles flying out the tailpipe.'","tags":["dave-mayberry","andrew-cauthan","albert-anderson","russ-endicott","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6555,"title":"Four wide into lap traffic with 21 to go","summary":"The lead pack catches lap traffic and goes four wide — the squeeze spins the 64 and 33 with Mayberry and Vaught involved, but everyone spins through the giant runoff without hitting anything.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7500,"title":"Wrecks front AND back with under ten to go","summary":"Two simultaneous crashes under green — bumpers misalign between the 58 and 81 in the back while the 747, 753, 14 and 92 pile up in turn one; Eaton nearly rolls, and Dale Adamson and Trevor Robertson are done for the night.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","robert-chipman","mike-everage","mike-adamson","greg-dobson","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","greg-cline","dale-adamson","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7948,"title":"Green-white-checker: no lifting now","summary":"The final restart with Jonah Long and David Kelly side by side up front — 'there is no lift in these drivers whatsoever from this point on, it's gonna be cutthroat maneuvers.'","tags":["jonah-long","david-kelly","albert-anderson","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":8090,"title":"Last-lap mayhem — Gallagher steals it at the line","summary":"Off turn four on the last lap it goes three and four wide — Long gets turned, the 747 launches into the air, and John Gallagher threads through the carnage to grab his first VRL win over Baker and Whittenburg.","tags":["john-gallagher","daniel-baker","ricky-whittenburg","jonah-long","david-kelly","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":937,"quote":"Let the hatred flow — but let's let it flow a little bit later on in the race.","context":"previewing lingering driver anger carried over from Martinsville","gold":4},{"t":1106,"quote":"Champ to chump in no time — any clown can win at Talladega.","context":"the booth setting the stakes before the green flag","gold":4},{"t":2268,"quote":"It doesn't matter how good you are — a bullet ain't got no name, right? So that applies here.","context":"Turner's analogy for Talladega luck striking anyone","gold":4},{"t":3670,"quote":"If my untalented butt can win at Talladega, it pretty much anybody's got a shot at it.","context":"a broadcaster on why the whole field has a chance tonight","gold":3},{"t":5375,"quote":"So they just put milk on all their meat? They just douse it with two percent?","context":"the booth learns New England barbecue means dairy and maple syrup","gold":3},{"t":5928,"quote":"You know what saved Albert Anderson right there? He had bald eagles flying out the tailpipe. America's driver — put a shroud around him, kept him safe. Nice bubble of America.","context":"Anderson threads through the big late wreck completely untouched","gold":5},{"t":8109,"quote":"Big contact! Three wide, four wide, incidents happening all around — John Gallagher makes it on through, picking up the race win!","context":"the checkered-flag call as Gallagher survives the last-lap melee","gold":4},{"t":8241,"quote":"747 launches up into the air to meet another 747.","context":"replay of the last-lap wreck as Anderson's truck goes airborne","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble many names heavily. Best-guess proper names used: 'Dustin Riehle' (#37, always captioned 'Dustin really'), 'Dustyn Eaton' (#14, called 'Dustin with a Y'), 'David Vaught' (#1, captioned 'David fight'), 'Ricky Whittenburg' (#55, captioned 'Wittenberg'). Booth is Alan Brown with Allen English and Adam Turner (AAA Broadcasting); race control is Lori (also heard 'Laurie'/'Laura') — not drivers. Finishing order was read out but announced as unofficial. Stage 1 winner Jonah Long, Lucky Draw winner Greg Klein (16th). Race sponsor Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry, also the #29 driver). Team names heard: Team Limitless, Vigilante Force, Goodwiser, Team Tang (aka 'orangutan'), 'Ain't Dead Yet' (Whittenburg's team).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"LSkQ1eMD7WY":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough won the 42-lap Interlagos race from pole after a strategy duel with Alan Vaught swung twice in the closing stint. Vaught's stronger long-run pace and one-lap undercut erased Goodenough's early advantage, while championship contender Dustyn Eaton charged from 19th to third before missing his pit stall and running out of fuel; Tim Pope also fell from the top five after a heavy crash. Before the final stops Vaught passed Goodenough on track, and Goodenough then lost roughly five seconds when a tire-selection mistake caused his crew to service the truck twice, seemingly handing Vaught control. With nine laps left, however, contact with the two-laps-down Dion Jones spun Vaught and returned the lead to Goodenough. Goodenough took the checkered flag ahead of Vaught, while Derek Welch recovered from an earlier spin to finish third.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Alan Vaught","Derek Welch"],"moments":[{"t":2092,"title":"Goodenough leads Interlagos to green","summary":"Polesitter Craig Goodenough clears Alan Vaught through the Senna S and begins opening a gap as the 24-truck field starts the caution-free 42-lap race.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2359,"title":"Eaton charges from the rear","summary":"Serving an end-of-line penalty, Dustyn Eaton advances 11 positions in the first two and a half laps and soon reaches the top five with pace comparable to the leader.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":2394,"title":"Dobson crashes in two separate corners","summary":"Greg Dobson catches the grass, strikes an unprotected concrete barrier, and then suffers another incident near turn 12 with smoke pouring from the truck.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2985,"title":"Welch spins out of the top five","summary":"Apparent contact with Tim Pope sends Derek Welch into the grass; Welch avoids the wall, cleans the tires and begins the recovery that will eventually take him back to third.","tags":["derek-welch","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3066,"title":"Adamson dive-bombs Robertson","summary":"Mike Adamson drives deep into the corner near Trevor Robertson, spins, and continues after Robertson reacts quickly enough to avoid heavier contact.","tags":["mike-adamson","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3512,"title":"Vaught makes the undercut work","summary":"After closing a five-second deficit on worn tires, Vaught pits one lap before Goodenough and uses the fresh-tire advantage to sweep past when Goodenough rejoins.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3719,"title":"Two championship contenders unravel","summary":"Pope crashes hard enough to badly damage the left front while Eaton, having missed his pit stall, runs out of fuel before completing the lap and must tow back to pit lane.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":4041,"title":"Goodenough retakes the lead","summary":"Vaught dirt-tracks the exit while trying to protect first after the opening pit cycle, allowing Goodenough to drive back past and reestablish control.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4936,"title":"Vaught passes Goodenough before the final stops","summary":"As the leaders reach the last fuel window, Vaught completes an on-track pass for first; Goodenough immediately dives toward pit road while Vaught stays out one more lap.","tags":["jess-vaught","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4992,"title":"Goodenough's tire error costs five seconds","summary":"Goodenough initially selects right-side tires and then requests all four, forcing the crew to repeat service; Vaught follows with a clean 14.23-second stop and cycles ahead by more than three seconds.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":5553,"title":"Lap traffic spins leader Vaught","summary":"With nine laps left, the two-laps-down Dion Jones moves back toward the center of the roadway as Vaught passes, and contact turns the No. 33 around, handing Goodenough the lead.","tags":["jess-vaught","dion-jones","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6408,"title":"Goodenough wins at Interlagos","summary":"Goodenough completes the final lap 3.5 seconds clear of Vaught and takes the checkered flag, with Welch finishing roughly 30 seconds behind the leading pair in third.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught","derek-welch"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3396,"quote":"It's one thing to catch him, another to pass.","context":"The booth frames Vaught's first long-run pursuit of Goodenough.","gold":4},{"t":3871,"quote":"I think he just gave a win away with that minor mental lapse.","context":"The booth reacts after Eaton misses his pit stall and runs out of fuel.","gold":5},{"t":5076,"quote":"This could be the race here, boys.","context":"The booth recognizes the decisive final pit-stop sequence.","gold":5},{"t":5553,"quote":"Deion gets into the leader, spins Alan Vaught.","context":"The live call as lap traffic overturns the race with nine laps left.","gold":5},{"t":5760,"quote":"There's Toyota oil everywhere.","context":"The booth petitions for a debris caution while Vaught tries to recover.","gold":4},{"t":6478,"quote":"I think the league in general was kind of robbed of a really good finish here.","context":"The booth reflects on the Vaught–Goodenough duel that traffic interrupted.","gold":5},{"t":6996,"quote":"I went in, stopped, and put right sides only on it. Then instead of pushing just the left sides only, I pushed all four, so it wanted to go around and redo them all.","context":"Craig Goodenough explains the final-stop tire-selection mistake","gold":5},{"t":7040,"quote":"I don't like to take it that way. That sucks for Alan, but I'll take the win. A win's a win.","context":"Goodenough reacts to inheriting the lead after Vaught's contact","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 11, round 16 at Interlagos per seasons_map.json; this was the first of the final three points races among championship contenders Alan Vaught, Kyle Vaught, Tim Pope and Dustyn Eaton. The event ran 42 laps with local yellows only, no full-course cautions, no stages, no fast repairs, 60% fuel and unlimited tire sets. The live finish, all three podium interviews and complete 24-driver results rundown explicitly confirm Goodenough, Vaught and Welch as the podium. Vaught was the highest-finishing championship contender in second; Kyle Vaught was fifth, Eaton recovered to ninth after towing for fuel, and Pope retired in nineteenth after crash damage. Broadcast analysis and both drivers treated the Jones-Vaught contact as accidental, though it directly changed the race lead with nine laps remaining. Welch believed contact with Pope caused his early spin, but his interview acknowledged some uncertainty, so the moment is described as apparent contact. Canonical roster forms are used for Alan Vaught, Jonathan Osborne, Greg Cline, Andrew Cauthan, Kelly Kuehl, Stony Benfield, Ricky Whittenburg and Dion Jones despite the broadcast's alternate spellings.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"LVnKiDZIF5g":{"recap":"Tim Pope started the Jackpot Funeral 200 from pole, but the opening phase was dominated by cautions: a sprawling first accident damaged much of the field, Kelly Kuehl's loose truck then collected Dion Jones, and a later chain reaction left roughly a dozen trucks badly hurt. Albert Anderson, Aaron Warren, Andrew Coffin, John McAdam, and Jack Dixon all spent time at or near the front as cautions and differing tire choices repeatedly shuffled Pope backward and forward. Once the race settled into a long green run, Pope, Scott Rooney, and Chris Goans emerged from the final lap-102 pit cycle as the decisive contenders, with Goans able to run flat out after saving fuel during the prior stint. Goans cleared Rooney with three laps remaining and closed rapidly, but Pope conserved enough fuel while protecting a half-second margin to win from the pole over Goans and Rooney.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Chris Goans","Scott Rooney"],"moments":[{"t":1661,"title":"Pope launches from the pole","summary":"Barney throws the green and Pope controls the inside lane as Gallagher and Gaines fight behind him in the 33-truck field.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-gallagher","jason-gaines"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1733,"title":"A sprawling opening wreck tears through the field","summary":"Gallagher gets loose twice and contact sends Anderson through the grass before secondary impacts involve Goodenough, Benfield, Kuehl, Mayberry, Reading, Gaines, Williams, and others; with no fast repairs, the damage shapes the rest of the night.","tags":["john-gallagher","jacob-alicia","albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","stony-benfield","kelly-keel","dave-mayberry","jesse-redding","jason-gaines","anthony-williams"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2068,"title":"Kuehl's damaged truck collects Jones","summary":"After Bryant briefly noses ahead on the restart, Kuehl loses the rear of a truck missing its tailgate and sweeps Jones into the second caution; Jones reports a meatball flag and retires.","tags":["dylan-bryant","kelly-keel","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2410,"title":"Anderson challenges Pope for first","summary":"Anderson works beneath Pope and is scored as the new leader while the pair remain side by side, with the booth suggesting Pope is protecting his tires on the outside.","tags":["albert-anderson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2497,"title":"Another chain reaction destroys contenders","summary":"Contact in the McAdam-Bryant-Alesia traffic triggers a much larger secondary crash; Robertson suffers broken steering and Gallagher, Goodenough, Adamson, and several more are left with major damage.","tags":["john-mcadam","dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","john-gallagher","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2695,"title":"The pit shuffle puts Warren out front","summary":"Following the major accident, Warren inherits the lead over Osborne and Coffin, while Anderson heads the group that stopped and Pope cycles back to sixth.","tags":["aaron-warren","jonathan-osborne","andrew-cauthan","albert-anderson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3132,"title":"Osborne and Wade collide after a check-up","summary":"McAdam brushes the wall ahead, Osborne slows abruptly, and Wade's evasive move cannot prevent contact; Osborne later reports only 24 seconds of damage and continues his recovery from the rear.","tags":["john-mcadam","jonathan-osborne","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3544,"title":"A fifth caution opens another tire decision","summary":"Kuehl spins his aerodynamically damaged truck again on lap 39, and nearly the whole lead group pits while Dixon and Osborne stay out to claim track position.","tags":["kelly-keel","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson","scott-rooney","john-mcadam","timothy-pope","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4134,"title":"Fresh tires form a six-truck breakaway","summary":"McAdam leads Pope, Rooney, Goans, Mayberry, and Kyle Vaught as the lap-39 tire takers separate themselves from the field during the longest green run of the race.","tags":["john-mcadam","timothy-pope","scott-rooney","chris-goans","dave-mayberry","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5713,"title":"The final green-flag stops begin","summary":"McAdam pits at lap 101 and Pope, Rooney, Vaught, Mayberry, Benfield, and others follow a lap later, putting the leaders on their final fuel and likely their final tire sets.","tags":["john-mcadam","timothy-pope","scott-rooney","kyle-vaught","dave-mayberry","stony-benfield"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6721,"title":"Goans takes second with three to go","summary":"After several laps trying both lanes, Goans carries the outside momentum past Rooney and sets off after Pope with slightly fresher tires but almost no time remaining.","tags":["chris-goans","scott-rooney","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6805,"title":"Pope saves enough fuel to hold off Goans","summary":"Goans cuts the margin through the final lap, but Pope exits Turn 4 with enough of a cushion to win from the pole; Goans completes a 32nd-to-second recovery and Rooney takes third.","tags":["timothy-pope","chris-goans","scott-rooney"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1470,"quote":"This is all for fun, guys. All for fun.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg reminds viewers to keep the race chat friendly","gold":4},{"t":2235,"quote":"Some days you're the windshield and some days you're the bug.","context":"Whittenburg consoles Dion Jones after the early accident ends his night","gold":5},{"t":2442,"quote":"Go ahead and burn your tires up there down on the bottom.","context":"The booth interprets Pope's patient outside-line approach while Anderson attacks","gold":4},{"t":2985,"quote":"Goans is a really smart driver. He's patient and he's fast, too, but he's really patient.","context":"The booth notices Goans's rapid, controlled recovery from his rear-of-field penalty","gold":4},{"t":7115,"quote":"You have to run the bottom if you were going to really pass anybody.","context":"Third-place Scott Rooney describes the difficulty of passing at Las Vegas","gold":4},{"t":7235,"quote":"I had actually saved enough fuel the stint before to where I could run flat out the last stint without having to worry about fuel.","context":"Runner-up Chris Goans explains his closing-stint strategy","gold":5},{"t":7477,"quote":"Felt good. Glad to be back on top.","context":"Winner Tim Pope sums up his return to victory lane","gold":5},{"t":7508,"quote":"I was about a lap, lap and a half short when I realized it, so I had to start pedaling and backing it down.","context":"Pope reveals the late fuel-saving pressure behind the finish","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 14, Round 5 at Las Vegas Motor Speedway according to seasons_map.json; the session panel briefly labeled it round four, but the broadcast closes by explicitly putting round five in the books. The Jackpot Funeral 200 ran 133 laps and 200 miles with 65% fuel, four total tire sets, no fast repairs, a 25-incident drive-through threshold plus six-point increments, iRacing cautions, lucky dogs, and wave-arounds. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Pope-Goans-Rooney podium and provides a complete 33-driver starting grid; no full finishing order is claimed beyond explicitly stated positions. Goans and Osborne started at the end of the longest line because of prior-race penalties. Caption variants are normalized to roster spellings, including Tim Pope, Chris Goans, Scott Rooney, Sean McDonnell, Andrew Coffin, Michael Everage, John Schoenbachler, and Kelly Kuehl. Ricky Whittenburg's computer problems left Alan Vaught to call the closing portion alone. All timestamps fall within the 7,682-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lXbV49VDZzI":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough led the opening Sonoma stint before an early stop cycled him back to the front, only for John Schoenbachler's spinning truck to collect him and end his race. Jack Dixon inherited the lead, but the scheduled lap-28 competition caution split the field between older-tire stay-outs and drivers who took fresh rubber; Jonathan Osborne briefly led the restart before Dixon charged past. In the final green-flag cycle, Chris Goans took only left-side tires and jumped Dixon's four-tire stop, briefly claiming the effective lead when Dixon slid on a curb. Dixon recovered, repassed Goans with five laps left, and earned his first VRL road-course victory, with Goans second and Jacob Alesia third after recovering from an earlier spin.","winner":"Jack Dixon","podium":["Jack Dixon","Chris Goans","Jacob Alesia"],"moments":[{"t":1130,"title":"Goodenough leads the Sonoma start","summary":"Craig Goodenough launches from pole and leads Jack Dixon and Jonathan Osborne into the opening lap of the 55-lap regular-season finale.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1904,"title":"Three-wide contact spins Rooney","summary":"Jorge Rincon fills the inside as Andrew Player begins moving down and Scott Rooney is left outside; the three-wide contact sends Rooney around and costs him several spots.","tags":["george-rincon","andrew-player","scott-rooney"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2258,"title":"Dixon closes on the early leader","summary":"Dixon reaches Goodenough's rear bumper as tire wear grows, with Alesia close enough to make the front three a developing fight for the win.","tags":["jack-dixon","craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2399,"title":"Goodenough opens the first pit cycle","summary":"Goodenough pits from the lead on lap 16 because the fuel window cannot reach the halfway caution, handing first to Dixon as the field begins green-flag stops.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2962,"title":"Bachler's spin eliminates Goodenough","summary":"Goodenough cycles back into the lead behind John Schoenbachler, but Bachler loses control over the curb and spins across the racing line, tearing the leader's front fender off and ending Goodenough's race.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3555,"title":"The competition caution splits the field","summary":"The scheduled yellow flies as lap 28 begins; Robertson, Osborne, and Klein stay out on older tires, while Dixon, Alesia, Goans, and Player pit and restart immediately behind them.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne","greg-cline","jack-dixon","jacob-alicia","chris-goans","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4062,"title":"Dixon charges from fourth to first","summary":"Osborne takes the lead when Robertson fades on the restart, but Dixon's eight-lap tire advantage carries him past Osborne into first within a few laps.","tags":["jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4250,"title":"Osborne's wall contact turns Alesia","summary":"Osborne brushes the outside wall exiting the final hairpin and comes down into Alesia, spinning the No. 31; Alesia rejoins seventh and pits the following lap.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4517,"title":"Dixon builds a seven-second cushion","summary":"With Alesia delayed and Osborne on older tires, Dixon drives away to nearly seven seconds over the field before the final pit cycle.","tags":["jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":4938,"title":"Goans' two-tire gamble flips the lead fight","summary":"Goans changes only his worn left-side tires and gains heavily on Dixon's four-tire stop; he passes Dixon after the No. 48 gets loose on a curb and becomes the effective leader.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5440,"title":"Dixon retakes first with five to go","summary":"Dixon uses four fresh tires to draw alongside Goans and completes the pass entering Turn 5, while Goans struggles for drive off on old right-side tires.","tags":["jack-dixon","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5794,"title":"Dixon earns his first VRL road-course win","summary":"Dixon stretches the final margin to nearly two seconds and wins at Sonoma ahead of Goans, while Alesia completes his recovery in third.","tags":["jack-dixon","chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":613,"quote":"Tonight, we race in their memory. We race because they served. And we remember that freedom is never free.","context":"VRN's Memorial Day tribute before the race","gold":5},{"t":1507,"quote":"What could have been disaster didn't turn out too badly.","context":"Gallagher, Everage, and Adamson avoid a larger early crash","gold":3},{"t":3749,"quote":"You put Robertson out front. He is not going to be an easy pass.","context":"The booth assesses the competition-caution stay-out strategy","gold":4},{"t":3796,"quote":"Probably not. I'm struggling for grip here.","context":"Trevor Robertson bluntly answers whether he can hold the fresh-tire group off","gold":4},{"t":3797,"quote":"My recovery is I hope everybody else wrecks, I get two laps back, and I'm leading this thing by lap 55.","context":"Kelly Kuehl outlines an optimistic recovery plan","gold":5},{"t":4138,"quote":"He must be powering that truck off maple syrup.","context":"The booth watches Canadian Jack Dixon take control","gold":4},{"t":5254,"quote":"Canada has come down here to California wine country looking to put their stamp on Sonoma Raceway.","context":"Sean McDonnell and Dixon run first and second during the final cycle","gold":4},{"t":5794,"quote":"There's your winner tonight, Jack Dixon out of Mitchell, Ontario, Canada.","context":"Dixon's first VRL road-course winning call","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 14, Round 13 at Sonoma according to seasons_map.json; this was the regular-season finale before the five-race VRL Cup chase. Road-course rules used local cautions only, plus a planned competition caution when the leader began lap 28. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Dixon-Goans-Alesia podium and identifies all 28 participants; Scott Rooney is omitted in the rapid final readout but is explicitly shown running 14th late in the race. The results cadence is garbled after 11th, so the precise lower finishing positions are not restated. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for captions calling the No. 14 'Dustyn Eaton.' Transcript timestamps end within the 6,656-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"lzMVRUNCbjI":{"recap":"Pocono gave the Trick Triangle 250 a different problem in every stage. Rob Green rolled during the opening-start accident, an immediate shock before the race settled into fuel windows, tire calls, and track position. Alan Vaught took the first stage. In the second, Albert Anderson ran dry while Michael Everage stretched his fuel far enough to win the segment. A major restart pileup then blocked most of the track early in the final stage and forced the surviving contenders to rebuild their plans. Later, contact sent Tim Pope through the grass, but he recovered and stayed in the strategy fight. The decisive split arrived at the final stop: Pope and Vaught chose two tires, while John Ellis committed to four. Ellis used the extra grip to charge from 22nd and take the checkered flag just under half a second ahead of Pope. The postrace interviews make the finish unusually easy to audit. Vaught describes the earlier stage as a strategy test, Pope explains why he gambled on two tires, and Ellis says the four-tire choice and resulting track position won the race. The opening rollover supplied the spectacle; the competing tire plans supplied the ending.","winner":"John Ellis","podium":["John Ellis","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":745,"title":"Opening start erupts into a rollover","summary":"Dustin Riehle gets loose during the initial acceleration, triggering a chain reaction that launches Rob Green into a long series of flips and immediately brings out the yellow.","tags":["dustin-reilly","earl-evans","rob-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1109,"title":"Vaught takes the lead on the clean restart","summary":"Alan Vaught carries the outside momentum past pole-sitter Josh Bittner after the second attempt at a start gets the field through turn one.","tags":["jess-vaught","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":1697,"title":"Pope clears Bittner for second","summary":"Tim Pope drives around Bittner exiting the tunnel turn and begins closing on Vaught during the opening stage.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2539,"title":"Vaught wins the first stage","summary":"The lap-30 competition caution freezes Vaught ahead of Pope and Bittner, ending the first experiment with the race's new stage format.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":2741,"title":"Two-tire calls jumble the restart order","summary":"Vaught wins the stage pit race, while Russ Kilgore and Jorge Rincon gain significant track position with shorter two-tire service.","tags":["jess-vaught","russ-kilgore","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4621,"title":"Everage stretches fuel to the stage-two win","summary":"Michael Everage remains on track as Anderson runs dry and coasts to pit road, allowing Everage to reach the lap-60 stage line first after gaining 18 positions.","tags":["mike-everage","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":5216,"title":"Final-stage restart produces a major pileup","summary":"A loose Ellis starts a four-wide checkup that turns Jeff Ottinger and blocks much of the track, collecting Kuehl, Camp, Bittner, Klafka, Burke, Evans, Whittenburg and others.","tags":["john-ellis","jeff-ottinger","kelly-keel","douglas-camp","josh-bittner","eric-klafka","jeremiah-burke","earl-evans","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5592,"title":"Old tires create another frantic restart","summary":"Russ Endicott struggles to launch on worn tires, opening the outside lane for Pope and Ellis while Mike Adamson and Vaught fight at the front.","tags":["russ-endicott","timothy-pope","john-ellis","mike-adamson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5783,"title":"Adamson contact sends Pope through the grass","summary":"Dale Adamson bumps Pope in turn three, sending Pope loose into Bittner and through the grass while the contenders scramble around the damaged trucks.","tags":["dale-adamson","timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":6163,"title":"Everage spins as the final run begins","summary":"Everage drifts into Austin Paul during a three-wide restart fight and both trucks sustain damage, but the race remains green.","tags":["mike-everage","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":6665,"title":"Money stop separates the contenders","summary":"Mike Adamson, Vaught and other leaders make their final stops while Ellis stays out briefly, then chooses four tires as Pope and Vaught use two-tire strategies.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","john-ellis","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7588,"title":"Ellis completes three wins in a row","summary":"Ellis holds a gap of just under half a second through the final corner and beats Pope to the line, with Vaught completing the podium in third.","tags":["john-ellis","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7588,"quote":"Here comes Ellis—three in a row! Home Depot brings it home again!","context":"The live call as Ellis wins at Pocono.","gold":5},{"t":7753,"quote":"It came down to strategy towards the end. I kind of figured it would; this place generally seems to do that.","context":"Third-place Vaught describes the defining feature of the race.","gold":5},{"t":7798,"quote":"This race was a test bed. We said, 'Let's test out stages here and perhaps carry that over to season three.'","context":"League administrator Vaught explains why Pocono used the experimental two-stage format.","gold":5},{"t":7932,"quote":"The only way I had a chance was to take two tires on the last stop, and they kind of didn't last long enough.","context":"Runner-up Pope explains the gamble that put him near Ellis but left him short on grip.","gold":5},{"t":8116,"quote":"I think I really won this on strategy.","context":"Ellis opens his victory analysis after coming from 22nd.","gold":5},{"t":8182,"quote":"I kind of prioritized track position over tires or coming to get fuel.","context":"Ellis describes the principle behind his winning calls.","gold":5},{"t":8204,"quote":"Jess and Tim were on two tires, which is why I was able to keep them behind me.","context":"Ellis explains how his four-tire final stop paid off in the closing duel.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete 30-driver results rundown explicitly confirm Ellis, Pope and Vaught. Ellis started 22nd, gained 21 positions and was named hard charger while earning his third consecutive win. The lap-30 and lap-60 stage cautions were a one-race test for a possible Season 3 format. Jeff Ottinger follows the roster canonical despite repeated caption variants; Mike Adamson and Dale Adamson are distinct participants.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"m4_SSZozl2M":{"recap":"Chris Goans won the Season 13 penultimate round at Auto Club after surviving a strategic, tire-sensitive 85-lap race and leading the field into the sole green-white-checkered attempt. Dillon Bryant appeared to have one of the fastest trucks but spent much of the closing run blinking badly, while Goans, Bryant, Jacob Alesia, and Trevor Robertson remained tightly grouped at the front. A late caution involving John Gallagher, Jack Dixon, and Michael Everage pushed the race into overtime, where Anthony Williams spun his tires on the restart and triggered a multi-truck crash that immediately froze the field. Bryant was scored second and Robertson third, leaving the championship fight unresolved for the Homestead finale.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Dillon Bryant","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1315,"title":"Bryant launches from the pole","summary":"Dillon Bryant gets a clean start from pole and clears Jack Dixon while the field immediately fans three-wide behind them.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jack-dixon"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2024,"title":"Williams spins back into traffic","summary":"Anthony Williams loses the truck, tries to accelerate after reaching the apron, and spins back into the path of the pack, bringing out the first caution and collecting Andrew Player, John McAdam, and Jack Dixon among others.","tags":["anthony-williams","andrew-player","john-mcadam","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2352,"title":"Dixon calls it a jump scare","summary":"During the caution, Jack Dixon tells the booth that he could not see the stopped truck until the field scattered and Williams came back across his path.","tags":["jack-dixon","anthony-williams"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"interview"},{"t":2768,"title":"Schoenbachler pounds the wall","summary":"John Schoenbachler suffers a heavy wall impact but keeps moving, avoiding another caution despite major visible damage.","tags":["john-schoenbachler"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3355,"title":"Green-flag stops begin","summary":"The long green run turns into a staggered pit cycle as the leaders begin stopping, briefly handing the race lead through several different strategies.","tags":["dylan-bryant","chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3675,"title":"Bryant's connection becomes a factor","summary":"While running in the lead fight, Dillon Bryant begins blinking repeatedly; the booth worries both about his championship hopes and the prediction-code risk for trucks racing beside him.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4408,"title":"Goans heads the final lead battle","summary":"After the last pit cycle, Chris Goans leads with Bryant, Alesia, and Robertson close behind, using the draft and their side-by-side fight to protect the top spot.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5010,"title":"Late Gallagher-Dixon contact forces overtime","summary":"Contact between John Gallagher and Jack Dixon catches Michael Everage and produces a caution with three laps remaining, sending the race beyond its scheduled distance.","tags":["john-gallagher","jack-dixon","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5303,"title":"Overtime restart erupts behind Goans","summary":"On the only green-white-checkered attempt, Anthony Williams spins his tires on old rubber and a crash sweeps up Albert Anderson, Chandler Paul, Scott Miller, Greg Klein, Sean McDonnell, David Mayberry, and Stony Benfield.","tags":["anthony-williams","albert-anderson","chandler-paul","scott-milner","greg-cline","shawn-mcdonald","dave-mayberry","stony-benfield"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5317,"title":"Goans wins under the overtime yellow","summary":"The immediate caution freezes the running order with Chris Goans first, Dillon Bryant second, and Trevor Robertson third.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2352,"quote":"I had no idea. They were just screaming that there's a wreck, and then he went down and came straight back up. It was kind of a jump scare.","context":"Jack Dixon describing the first-caution pileup","gold":3},{"t":2768,"quote":"He's coming back. Oh, and he's going to eat the wall.","context":"The booth reacts to John Schoenbachler's heavy impact","gold":3},{"t":4976,"quote":"That was a big blink. Oh man, that was a long blink.","context":"The booth watches Dillon Bryant disappear from view late in the race","gold":3},{"t":5317,"quote":"This race is going to be over.","context":"The booth recognizes that the overtime crash has frozen the field","gold":3},{"t":5701,"quote":"I'm glad to have a podium because I did not have a third-place truck, that's for sure.","context":"Trevor Robertson reflects on salvaging third","gold":4},{"t":6207,"quote":"You don't want to win them that way, but when you do, a win's a win, right?","context":"Chris Goans on benefiting from the overtime caution","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The race was decided under caution on the league's only green-white-checkered attempt. The caption transcript calls the winner Chris Gones/Gomes/Goss/Gins; roster_overrides.json establishes Chris Goans as the canonical spelling. The grid explicitly listed 31 starters. John Schoenbachler is the roster match used for the captioned 'John Shanebachler/John Schoenbachler'; this identity is the least certain participant mapping. The finishing rundown near 1:31:33 is caption-garbled after the top 10, so only the explicitly clear podium is recorded.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"M9SBnoAUZOk":{"recap":"Chris Goans took the lead from pole-sitter Jack Dixon on the opening lap and established himself as the driver to beat in the 150-lap Rockstorm at abrasive Rockingham. Early cautions for Russ Kilgore, a large John McAdam-triggered stack-up, and an Andrew Coffin-Dillon Bryant crash divided the field across several tire strategies, with Jacob Alesia and Andrew Player briefly leading after pit shuffles. Once the race settled into a long green run, Goans stretched his fuel to lap 101, fitted his final tire set, and drove through traffic while many rivals fell a lap down. Goans completed back-to-back victories by more than four seconds over Mike Adamson, with Alesia third.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Mike Adamson","Jacob Alesia"],"moments":[{"t":1435,"title":"Goans takes the lead at the green","summary":"Jack Dixon starts from pole, but Chris Goans clears him on the opening lap and begins setting the pace at Rockingham.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1637,"title":"Kilgore pounds the wall but continues","summary":"Russ Kilgore gets loose in Turns 3-4 and hits the outside wall hard, apparently escaping terminal damage from the first impact.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1998,"title":"Kilgore's second crash ends his race","summary":"Kilgore misjudges a move while trying to slot behind Michael Everage, hits the wall, and suffers an engine failure that ends his night and brings out the first caution.","tags":["russ-kilgore","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2442,"title":"McAdam's wall contact triggers a major stack-up","summary":"John McAdam brushes the wall and comes down across the pack; Jonathan Osborne, Stony Benfield, Jorge Rincon, Kelly Kuehl, and others are collected in the largest crash of the race.","tags":["john-mcadam","jonathan-osborne","stony-benfield","george-rincon","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2886,"title":"Bryant and Coffin bring out another yellow","summary":"Dillon Bryant and Andrew Coffin collide while Bryant works through traffic; Coffin gets briefly airborne before landing straight, and both continue with damage.","tags":["dylan-bryant","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3068,"title":"Alesia controls the tire-strategy restart","summary":"Jacob Alesia inherits the lead after several drivers stay out or take only fuel, while Mike Adamson and the fresh-tire group begin closing behind him.","tags":["jacob-alicia","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3237,"title":"Dobson chooses the wall over the field","summary":"Greg Dobson reacts to Tom Barish getting sideways ahead, turns sharply down the track, and hits the inside wall instead of collecting the pack; the race remains green.","tags":["greg-dobson","tom-barish"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3279,"title":"Player wrestles the lead from Alesia","summary":"Andrew Player uses fresher tires to work underneath Alesia, but Alesia holds the outside for several corners before Player finally completes the pass.","tags":["andrew-player","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3588,"title":"Goans closes on the off-strategy points leader","summary":"Goans returns to the front and rapidly approaches Bryant, whose fuel-only strategy leaves him in danger of losing a lap on worn tires.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4333,"title":"Goans completes the final green-flag stop","summary":"After saving enough fuel to stretch just beyond 100 laps, Goans pits for his final fresh tire set and cycles back into control of the race.","tags":["chris-goans","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4965,"title":"Barish and Rincon crash without a caution","summary":"Barish hits the wall, reacts to Coffin's avoidance move, and collects Rincon; both spin to the inside, but iRacing leaves the race green with 24 laps remaining.","tags":["tom-barish","andrew-cauthan","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5590,"title":"Goans completes a Rockingham clinic","summary":"Goans takes the checkered flag for his second consecutive win, more than four seconds ahead of Adamson, while Alesia completes the podium.","tags":["chris-goans","mike-adamson","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":696,"quote":"The Rock is all about throttle control, tire conservation, and managing falloff over the long green-flag stretches.","context":"Alan Vaught introduces Rockingham's defining challenge","gold":4},{"t":1637,"quote":"Jinx. Commentator's jinx.","context":"The booth reacts immediately after Kilgore hits the wall","gold":3},{"t":2174,"quote":"If anybody has a water sponsor or anything to do with water, I've got a problem with it right now.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg explains the home repairs that kept him out of recent booths","gold":4},{"t":2603,"quote":"I am dumbfounded that people didn't take tires that time.","context":"Ricky questions the field's early fuel-only strategy","gold":4},{"t":4937,"quote":"I can't believe they didn't bring out a caution either.","context":"The booth watches Barish and Rincon spin to the inside without a yellow","gold":3},{"t":5590,"quote":"He just really put on a clinic here.","context":"The winning call as Goans completes his dominant final stint","gold":5},{"t":5901,"quote":"The best strategy is, I guess, to get spun early in the race so that you're back on the strategy later.","context":"Third-place Jacob Alesia jokes about recovering from his early incident","gold":5},{"t":6172,"quote":"You're racing the track as much as you're racing everybody else.","context":"Winner Chris Goans explains the difficulty of Rockingham","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 13, Round 9 at Rockingham according to seasons_map.json. The broadcast explicitly reads the complete 28-driver results and confirms the Goans-Adamson-Alesia podium. Drivers had only two extra tire sets, making the early fuel-only stops and the lap-100 final stop central to the race. Goans states that he saved roughly one lap of fuel in the middle stint to reach his target stop window. Transcript timestamps end within the 6,435-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"meCLnoWbLI0":{"recap":"Alex Berube won the 100-lap Viva Las Vegas round by beating Tim Pope out of the final pit sequence and then withstanding Pope's pressure through the last 20 laps. The opening half was unusually frantic for a mile-and-a-half race: Tim Rivers spun on lap one, Simon Sriegis and Dustin Riehle triggered the first caution, a multi-truck stack-up followed, and Tyler Green's wall contact produced another yellow. Berube, Josh Oxendine and Jacob Schaffet traded the lead in a three-wide fight immediately before the scheduled lap-47 competition caution. A late caution caused by contact between Gary Godsoe and Angelica Timmerman interrupted the final green-flag stops, but Berube narrowly retained track position over Pope after service. Berube made no mistake on the run to the checkered flag, winning ahead of Pope and 20th-starting Jeremiah Burke, while Zach Wheeler and Trevor Robertson rounded out the top five.","winner":"Alex Berube","podium":["Alex Berube","Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1434,"title":"Pope launches from the pole","summary":"Tim Pope leads Josh Oxendine and the 30-truck field to green for 100 laps at Las Vegas.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1477,"title":"Rivers spins in the opening scramble","summary":"Tim Rivers catches the apron while racing near Alex Berube and spins into the grass, but the race stays green as the field fans out behind him.","tags":["tim-rivers","alex-berube"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1596,"title":"Sriegis and Riehle trigger the first yellow","summary":"Three-wide racing tightens around Simon Sriegis and Dustin Riehle, sending the Cobra into trouble and prompting race control's first caution.","tags":["simon-sregis","dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2191,"title":"Multiple crashes erupt in a packed field","summary":"Contact among tightly bunched trucks sets off an initial wreck and a secondary pileup involving John Osborne, Jack Dixon, Tim Rivers and Russ Kilgore, with much of the field pitting for repairs.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon","tim-rivers","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2694,"title":"Burke drives past Pope","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets a run on the inside and takes the lead from Pope as Oxendine tries to follow him through.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope","josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2820,"title":"Green's wall contact sparks another crash","summary":"Tyler Green is drawn into the outside wall and comes back into traffic, collecting Dave Mayberry and catching Rivers in a secondary incident.","tags":["tyler-green","dave-mayberry","tim-rivers"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3327,"title":"Berube takes over from the old-tire leaders","summary":"After Alan Vaught and Kelly Kuehl stay out under caution, Berube uses fresher tires to sweep past Vaught and claim the lead.","tags":["alex-berube","jess-vaught","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3405,"title":"Schaffet steals the lead three wide","summary":"Oxendine leans on Berube while trapped in the middle, opening the bottom for Jacob Schaffet to make a bold three-wide pass into first.","tags":["jacob-schaffet","josh-oxendine","alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3547,"title":"Competition caution freezes the lap-47 order","summary":"The scheduled yellow flies on lap 47 with Berube back in front; he wins the ensuing race off pit road over Pope and Schaffet.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope","jacob-schaffet"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4499,"title":"Godsoe turns Timmerman toward pit road","summary":"As the final pit window opens, Gary Godsoe contacts Angelica Timmerman and sends her sliding into pit entry, drawing a caution and forcing race control to clear her unsafe-entry penalty.","tags":["gary-godso","angelica-timmerman"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5039,"title":"Berube leads the final restart","summary":"With about 20 laps left, Berube gets the launch over Pope while Burke attacks from third and the contenders settle into a tire-management run.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5679,"title":"Berube holds off Pope in Vegas","summary":"Pope stays nose-to-tail through the final lap but cannot create a passing opportunity, and Berube takes the win ahead of Pope and hard-charging Burke.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5894,"quote":"It was just a hard battle all the way through the race. That was a dogfight from start to finish.","context":"Jeremiah Burke reflects on charging from 20th to third","gold":5},{"t":5960,"quote":"I did a slide job there at the end, less than ten laps ago. There's no such thing as teammates anymore.","context":"Burke describes his late-race move while fighting for the podium","gold":4},{"t":6040,"quote":"I stayed behind him to try to get away from the guys behind us. I was going to try to pass around ten or twelve to go, but couldn't get him set up right.","context":"Tim Pope explains why he never completed an attack on Berube","gold":5},{"t":6149,"quote":"I was gripping the wheel as hard as I could. My hands hurt. I'm pouring sweat. It was intense.","context":"Trevor Robertson describes the physical strain of the race","gold":5},{"t":6203,"quote":"The bottom line was fast early in runs, and then the high line would come in after six or seven laps.","context":"Robertson explains how the preferred groove evolved through a tire run","gold":4},{"t":6324,"quote":"It was a really hard race, and my wrists are really hurting right now. He really gave one hell of a battle.","context":"Alex Berube praises Pope after winning","gold":5},{"t":6471,"quote":"I have a lot of friends tonight watching. A lot of my Quebec friends were watching and supporting me.","context":"Berube thanks the supporters following his victory","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 1, round 7 at Las Vegas per seasons_map.json. The full 30-driver finishing order was explicitly read after the interviews, confirming Berube, Pope and Burke as the podium; Brian Jablonski was named hard charger after gaining 20 places to tenth. The broadcast documents four incident cautions plus the scheduled competition caution on lap 47. Twenty-three trucks were still on the lead lap with three laps remaining. Trevor Robertson won the random $5 driver draw after finishing fifth, and Chan the Man 72 was named super fan. The roster's canonical names Alex Berube, Jacob Schaffet, Simon Sriegis, Gary Godsoe and Ricky Whittenburg are used despite varying caption and broadcast spellings. The first-half multi-truck crash unfolded as several linked incidents, so only the clearly identified participants are named in its moment summary.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"mHm90QmqlBQ":{"recap":"Dustyn Eaton won the Season 15 opener at EchoPark Speedway after a fuel-saving gamble with teammate Scott Rooney. Four cautions punctuated the first half, including a large crash between Mike Adamson and pole-sitter Craig Goodenough, a Trevor Robertson-Scott Miller incident, and a restart pileup after John Schoenbachler bounced off the wall. Once the race stayed green, several apparent leaders could not reach the finish, while Eaton and Rooney stretched their final run after going one lap longer at the last stop. Rooney pushed Eaton to the line and finished second by roughly two hundredths, with Stony Benfield third after a separate late incident involving Jack Dixon, Gordon Spain, and Jorge Rincon.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Scott Rooney","Stony Benfield"],"moments":[{"t":574,"title":"Goodenough leads Season 15 green","summary":"Craig Goodenough starts from pole and gets a strong launch, while Albert Anderson uses the outside draft to fight back toward the lead.","tags":["craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1421,"title":"Adamson and Goodenough trigger the first big one","summary":"Mike Adamson tries to move down in front of Goodenough without being fully clear, turning both trucks and collecting Andrew Player and several others in the first caution on lap 27.","tags":["mike-adamson","craig-goodenough","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1741,"title":"Kyle Vaught takes the lead","summary":"Kyle Vaught works the lower line past Gordon Spain and reaches the point during the first restart run.","tags":["kyle-vaught","gordon-spain"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2115,"title":"Robertson and Miller collide three-wide","summary":"Trevor Robertson is caught between lanes as Scott Miller comes down off the wall; their contact spins both and brings out the second caution.","tags":["trevor-robertson","scott-milner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2752,"title":"Anderson crashes in the quad-oval","summary":"Albert Anderson gets loose and makes contact with John McAdam in the frontstretch kinks, spinning into Dustyn Eaton's path and sweeping up Ryan Walton and Jesse Reading.","tags":["albert-anderson","john-mcadam","dustin-eaton","ryan-walton","jesse-redding"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3087,"title":"Schoenbachler wall bounce starts another pileup","summary":"John Schoenbachler bounces off the outside wall into Jacob Alesia, who is then knocked into Kyle Vaught, causing the fourth and final caution of the night.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","jacob-alicia","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4315,"title":"Green-flag stops finally arrive","summary":"After the caution-heavy opening, the race reaches a full green-flag pit sequence with David Mayberry and then others cycling through the lead.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jonathan-osborne","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5460,"title":"Fuel leaders peel off","summary":"Greg Klein pits late and Dillon Bryant and Gordon Spain also prove unable to make the distance, revealing Eaton and Rooney as the drivers who had stretched the decisive fuel window.","tags":["greg-cline","dylan-bryant","gordon-spain","dustin-eaton","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5620,"title":"Rooney pushes Eaton to the line","summary":"Rooney stays on Eaton's bumper down the final backstretch, then makes a late attempt to draw alongside as a separate crash breaks out behind them.","tags":["scott-rooney","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5640,"title":"Eaton wins the fuel-mileage opener","summary":"Eaton holds Rooney off by about two hundredths at the checkered flag to win on fuel strategy, with Stony Benfield taking third.","tags":["dustin-eaton","scott-rooney","stony-benfield"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6246,"title":"Benfield owns the late wreck","summary":"In his podium interview, Benfield apologizes for getting into Jack Dixon and starting a domino effect that also involved Gordon Spain and Jorge Rincon during the unseen last-lap crash.","tags":["stony-benfield","jack-dixon","gordon-spain","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"interview"}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2348,"quote":"Pull me while we're in some action, dude. I'm ready to go. I'm going to wreck anyways, so, you know, screw it.","context":"Kyle Vaught jokes about the broadcaster's curse during a caution interview","gold":4},{"t":5695,"quote":"He pushed me to that victory. I owe that one to Rooney.","context":"Dustyn Eaton credits teammate Scott Rooney immediately after the finish","gold":4},{"t":5812,"quote":"Me and Scott just kind of pulled a Hail Mary, stayed out an extra lap past everybody.","context":"Eaton explains the winning fuel gamble","gold":4},{"t":5812,"quote":"I ran out of gas on that last pit stop in the pit box.","context":"Eaton describes how narrowly the strategy worked","gold":5},{"t":5834,"quote":"Me and Scott, we hit that last pit stop by the hair of our teeth, man.","context":"Eaton emphasizes the razor-thin fuel margin","gold":4},{"t":6140,"quote":"I shouldn't be in third. I got into Jack there and caused that wreck, and he got into my teammate George.","context":"Stony Benfield takes responsibility for the late incident","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete grid and results list 34 starters. 'Timmy McAdam/Penny McAdam' appears as a separate No. 27 driver from John McAdam's No. 47, but there is no matching canonical entry in roster.json; Timmy McAdam is retained from the clearest result caption and should receive owner review. Alex Anderson and Ryan Walton also have no roster entries but are explicitly named in both grid/race coverage. Benfield's post-race apology supplies the clearest evidence for the last-lap incident, which the booth did not show live while covering the finish.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"MpQmtHFrOqA":{"recap":"Race #6 of VRL Season 10 brought the Gen 6 Cup cars to Auto Club Speedway under the lights for 85 laps, with qualifying setting the tone as Dillon Bryant edged Anthony Williams and Alan Vaught for the pole by a combined two-thousandths of a second. The wide Fontana oval invited four- and five-wide racing and produced at least seven cautions, headlined by a five-wide lap-20 pileup off turn 4 and \"the Big One\" around lap 53, when Austin Paul brushed the wall and collected at least a dozen cars coming to the start-finish line. Dustin Wade later took a monster perpendicular hit into the inside SAFER barrier with 25 to go after Jonathan Osborne got loose and door-slammed him. Through all the chaos, Dustyn Eaton, who rolled off 33rd of 34 cars, survived on tire strategy and the high line, then held off Chandler Paul by two-tenths at the checkers for the hard-charger win. Andrew Coffin climbed from 15th to complete the podium.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Chandler Paul","Andrew Cauthan"],"moments":[{"t":2282,"title":"Pole decided by two thousandths","summary":"Dillon Bryant takes the pole at 39.748 with Anthony Williams at 39.749 and Alan Vaught at 39.750 — the top three separated by just two thousandths of a second.","tags":["dylan-bryant","anthony-williams","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3679,"title":"Five-wide pileup off turn 4","summary":"Lap 20: the field fans out five wide off turn 4, Tim Pope tries to squeeze between Canalis and Chris Klein, contact sends the 7 into traffic and eight-plus cars are collected — John Gallagher gets hit twice.","tags":["timothy-pope","chris-klein","joe-canales","mike-adamson","john-gallagher","josh-bittner","russ-kilgore","andrew-player","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4147,"title":"Netcode calamity off turn 2","summary":"Russ Kilgore gets loose exiting turn 2 with serious netcode in play, Anthony Williams takes the worst of it and Jonathan Osborne clips the wall trying to escape.","tags":["russ-kilgore","anthony-williams","jonathan-osborne","joe-canales"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4485,"title":"McAdam's whale of a save","summary":"Door-banging contact in the trioval — John McAdam pulls off a whale of a save to keep the 47 out of the grass and out of everybody's way.","tags":["john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4537,"title":"Junkyard in turns 1 and 2","summary":"Jeremiah Burke slams the wall hard after Kelly Coe darts inside with no room between Dobson and Burke — Vaught, Bittner and Rincon get swept into a 'little bit junkyard of cars' in turns 1 and 2.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-dobson","jess-vaught","josh-bittner","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5414,"title":"Mayberry the human ping-pong ball","summary":"Contact from the 92 sends Dave Mayberry bouncing off Austin Paul and back again — a 'human ping-pong ball' — before he pounds the outside wall entering turn 3.","tags":["dave-mayberry","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5748,"title":"THE BIG ONE at the stripe","summary":"Austin Paul loses the nose in Dustin Wade's draft, tags the turn-4 wall and comes down across traffic — at least 12 cars are wadded up coming to the start-finish line in the night's signature wreck.","tags":["austin-paul","dustin-wade","scott-rooney"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5833,"title":"Rooney threads the needle","summary":"In-car replay from Scott Rooney's perspective as he somehow drives clean through the 12-car Big One untouched — 'How did he miss that?'","tags":["scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6208,"title":"Wade's monster SAFER barrier hit","summary":"With 25 to go, Osborne gets loose off turn 2 and door-slams Wade, McAdam is turned into the fence, and Dustin Wade hits the inside SAFER barrier dead perpendicular with pieces flying everywhere — Andrew Coffin barely brakes clear.","tags":["dustin-wade","jonathan-osborne","john-mcadam","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6533,"title":"Three-wide restart for the lead","summary":"With 20 to go it's a three-way battle at the stripe — Eaton on the bottom, Coffin in the middle, Rooney topside takes the lead before getting the fence off turn 2 and handing second to Chandler Paul.","tags":["dustin-eaton","andrew-cauthan","scott-rooney","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6692,"title":"Eaton and Paul drag race to the line","summary":"Chandler Paul works the inside down the back straight, they drag race into turn 3, and Eaton uses the crossover to lead the lap by a nose at the stripe.","tags":["dustin-eaton","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7338,"title":"Eaton wins it from 33rd","summary":"White flag to checkers — Dustyn Eaton, who started 33rd of 34, holds off Chandler Paul by two-tenths for a survival-and-strategy hard-charger win as fireworks fly over Fontana.","tags":["dustin-eaton","chandler-paul","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3727,"quote":"Well, let's get a look, see what happened. Oh — they were five wide. That'll do it.","context":"deadpan replay review of the lap-20 pileup","gold":4},{"t":4638,"quote":"Some monster hits — once again, just be glad it's a Sim.","context":"watching the turn-1 junkyard wreck in real time","gold":3},{"t":4735,"quote":"It's like telling your Labrador not to chase the ball when you throw it, or your Chihuahua not to bark.","context":"explaining why drivers can't resist running five-wide at Fontana","gold":4},{"t":4795,"quote":"Money makes people stupid sometimes — myself included.","context":"musing on whether the night's cash payouts caused the crash-fest","gold":4},{"t":5750,"quote":"We got trouble yet again, big time trouble — this is the big one, folks! I think half the field's going to get wadded up in this one.","context":"Austin Paul tags the turn-4 wall and triggers the 12-car pileup at the stripe","gold":5},{"t":5855,"quote":"Want to drive a race car? Watch this... How did he miss that?","context":"replaying Scott Rooney's in-car as he threads the Big One untouched","gold":4},{"t":6220,"quote":"Kelly Coe, smoking a cigarette, not paying attention, almost gets into the 47.","context":"Coe cruises obliviously through the caution-7 carnage","gold":4},{"t":7377,"quote":"Dustin Eaton out of turn number four looking for a checkered flag — he's done it! Back to start finish, no pressure out the back, Eaton wins it!","context":"the winning call as Eaton completes the drive from 33rd","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Solo booth commentator identifies himself only as 'Steve'; the channel rebranded from HBR TV to Track Limits Network for this broadcast. Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Alan Vaught' and 'Kyle Vaught' appear as 'alen vot'/'VA'; 'Kelly Coe' as 'Kelly Co/cool'; 'Jorge Rincon' as 'Ren con'; 'Joe Canalis' as 'caneles/Canalis'. The full 34-car finishing order was read on air. Chandler Paul revealed post-race that he qualified 9th but surrendered the spot and started from pit lane due to a penalty carried from the prior week. League admins Jess and Lori were thanked but are not drivers in this field; the #92 car involved in two incidents was never named. The booth counted at least seven cautions. Race was billed as Season 10, Race 6, with payouts on the line ($20 pole bonus plus spin bounties and a custom diecast).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"MyNjUALJs4g":{"recap":"Tim Pope led the 29-car Kentucky field from pole, but the opening lap immediately produced the tape's only racing accident when Alan Vaught spun on cold tires, clipped Jeremiah Burke, and left Kelly Kuehl with nowhere to go. Pope controlled the restart over Jason Airson and Jonathan Osborne, while Russ Kilgore climbed rapidly from 29th and Vaught and Burke began recovering through persistent two- and three-wide traffic. Severe tire falloff shaped the first green-flag cycle: Airson, Vaught, and Burke each collected a lap-led bonus during the sequence, David Feit and Earl Evans received pit-speed penalties, and Pope's clean entry and exit restored him to the lead by roughly three and a half seconds. Mark Collins then spun through the frontstretch grass, and an apparently administrative or dealer's-choice caution came out; the upload cuts off during an Evans interview before the race reaches halfway, so this tape contains no winner or podium.","winner":null,"podium":[],"moments":[{"t":1546,"title":"Pope and Welch lead Kentucky to green","summary":"Pope launches from pole alongside Welch as Airson immediately advances on the preferred inside lane and the 29-car field races into Turns 1 and 2.","tags":["timothy-pope","derek-welch","jason-airson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1577,"title":"Vaught's cold-tire spin triggers an opening pileup","summary":"Vaught gets loose while racing Riley, spins across Burke, and sends cars scattering through the grass; Kuehl cannot avoid Burke and the first caution flies on lap two.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-reilly","jeremiah-burke","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":1691,"title":"Anderson narrowly misses Burke's damaged car","summary":"The replay shows Burke's car darting left just as Anderson approaches, allowing America's Driver to avoid the heaviest aftermath and remain undamaged.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":1929,"title":"Airson pressures Pope on the restart","summary":"Pope controls the second start, but Airson gets an excellent launch, slots into second, and brings Osborne and Welch into the fight behind the leader.","tags":["timothy-pope","jason-airson","jonathan-osborne","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2075,"title":"Ott and Klafka follow each other into the wall","summary":"Ott drifts high and brushes the outside wall, and Klafka follows nose-to-tail into nearly the same contact before both continue under green.","tags":["jim-ott","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":2199,"title":"Jordan survives a hard Turn 1 wall strike","summary":"Jordan steps out and hits the outside wall hard entering Turns 1 and 2, but keeps the car under control while the surrounding pack stays green.","tags":["robert-jordan"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":2264,"title":"Kilgore charges 17 positions","summary":"Starting 29th after skipping qualifying, Kilgore carves through the field to gain 17 places in the first 18 laps, with Austin Paul making a similar rearward-to-forward run.","tags":["russ-kilgore","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":2529,"title":"Burke threads a three-wide recovery pass","summary":"Burke squeezes between Chandler Paul and another car in a tight battle around 14th, then completes the pass as Vaught follows him forward from their lap-one trouble.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","chandler-paul","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2817,"title":"McCabe spins into the infield grass","summary":"McCabe goes off on the frontstretch and remains parked in the inside grass while trying to restart or locate the tow control; the race stays green.","tags":["chad-mccabe"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3018,"title":"The first green-flag pit cycle opens","summary":"Anderson, Osborne, Welch, and Haas begin the main stops, Pope follows, and Airson, Vaught, and Burke extend their runs long enough to collect bonus laps led.","tags":["albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne","derek-welch","kevin-haas","timothy-pope","jason-airson","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3071,"title":"Pit road penalizes Fite and Evans","summary":"Fite receives the first speeding black flag of the cycle and must serve it under green; Evans later enters too fast as well, while Pope executes a clean stop and regains the lead by about three and a half seconds.","tags":["david-fite","earl-evans","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":3340,"title":"The stream ends during an unexpected caution","summary":"After Collins spins harmlessly through the frontstretch grass, a caution appears that the booth identifies as likely administrative or dealer's choice; Anderson, Adamson, Welch, and Kilgore stay out, but the upload cuts off before the restart.","tags":["mark-collins","albert-anderson","mike-adamson","derek-welch","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"}],"soundbytes":[{"t":867,"quote":"I expect to see awesomeness. Turn two's crazy, and where you make your money is three and four.","context":"Adam Turner previews the Kentucky challenge","gold":5},{"t":1680,"quote":"Sometimes you just can't dodge it. Too many cars, not enough space.","context":"The booth reviews the opening-lap pileup","gold":5},{"t":1753,"quote":"Start in the back, let some of that stuff unravel in front of you, and you're going to make spots up.","context":"The booth explains Kilgore's charge from 29th","gold":4},{"t":2166,"quote":"He's tougher than a steak at Waffle House after 2 a.m.","context":"The booth describes how difficult leader Tim Pope is to pass","gold":5},{"t":2242,"quote":"There's about 30 cars here and all of them can drive. It's great competition.","context":"The booth praises the depth of the Kentucky field","gold":4},{"t":2629,"quote":"This is where it separates the men from the boys. The tires are wearing quickly here.","context":"The broadcast describes the first long-run tire test","gold":4},{"t":2684,"quote":"These tires are absolutely screaming at these drivers as they try to get every single inch of rubber.","context":"The booth measures roughly two seconds of falloff after 30 laps","gold":5},{"t":3228,"quote":"Very quick in, very quick out, and that gave him essentially three extra seconds.","context":"The booth credits Pope's pit-road execution for restoring the lead","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 3, Round 3 at Kentucky Speedway according to seasons_map.json. This is the main opening upload of a split broadcast: it contains the full grid and roughly the first 40-plus laps of the scheduled 133-lap Kentucky race, but it cuts off under caution during an Earl Evans interview before halfway. Therefore winner and podium are intentionally null/empty even though the separate bhsCIYgYLP4 Part 2 upload contains the finish. The Xfinity-car event used 70% fuel, four total tire sets, one fast repair, and disqualification at 13 incident points; pit road was limited to 45 mph. Vaught's self-spin produced the opening caution, and the cause of the second caution is unclear on this tape: Collins had spun harmlessly before it, while the booth believed race control may have thrown an administrative or dealer's-choice yellow. The complete 29-driver participant list comes from the on-air grid. Canonical roster spellings are used for Alan Vaught, Jason Airson, David Feit, Tony Polk, Mike Everedge, and Russ Endicott. All timestamps fall within the 3,542-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"winner-unknown-or-multi-stage"},"n0Abt0yqWSk":{"recap":"Risking It All at Richmond rewarded the drivers who could survive the cautions and still have one useful tire set left. Jack Dixon challenged pole-sitter Alan Vaught at the opening green, but the first reset arrived when Dillon Bryant hit the wall after Kelly Kuehl got loose and Sean McDonnell was trapped against the fence. Vaught controlled the first half and took the scheduled stage over Trevor Robertson, Greg Klein, McDonnell, Jeremiah Burke, Dixon, Mike Adamson, Tim Pope, Kuehl, and Jonah Long. Strategy then split the field. Dixon and Burke inherited the front row, Vaught used fresher tires to reclaim the lead, and the contenders rationed a four-set tire limit through repeated restarts. Robertson spun into a restart parking lot, paired incidents involving Andy Player and Jonathan Osborne produced another yellow, and Bryant's late contact turned Pope just as the decisive pit window opened. Burke joined roughly half the leaders for a final set while Ricky Whittenburg, Bryant, and Robertson protected track position. Two more crashes delayed the payoff, including Dixon turning Vaught toward Chad McCabe at pit entry. On the final restart Burke cleared Robertson, opened a stable gap, and won by roughly three quarters of a second. Robertson finished second after gaining 17 places; McDonnell completed the podium.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Trevor Robertson","Sean McDonnell"],"moments":[{"t":1329,"title":"Dixon challenges Vaught at the green","summary":"Jack Dixon gets his nose ahead of pole-sitter Vaught at the start and brushes the outside wall while the leaders remain side by side.","tags":["jack-dixon","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1376,"title":"Bryant, Kuehl, and McDonnell stack up","summary":"Dillon Bryant hits the outside wall after Kelly Kuehl gets loose, and Sean McDonnell has nowhere to escape as the three trucks jam against the fence and trigger the opening caution.","tags":["dylan-bryant","kelly-keel","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2640,"title":"Anderson's self-spin destroys the engine","summary":"Albert Anderson applies too much throttle exiting the corner and slams the inside wall, scattering debris and blowing the engine to bring the leaders to pit road around lap 40.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4431,"title":"Vaught claims the halfway stage","summary":"The scheduled yellow freezes the field at lap 100 with Vaught taking the stage ahead of Robertson, Greg Klein, McDonnell, Burke, Dixon, Mike Adamson, Pope, Kuehl, and Jonah Long.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","greg-cline","shawn-mcdonald","jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon","mike-adamson","timothy-pope","kelly-keel","jonah-long"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4730,"title":"Robertson spins into a restart parking lot","summary":"Cold tires snap Robertson around on the first stage-two restart, leaving a truck across a lane and a half; Michael Everage runs into him as several others squeeze through.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-everage","dylan-bryant","andrew-player","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5055,"title":"Vaught's fresh tires regain the lead","summary":"Vaught uses another new set of tires to pass Burke after the restart and returns to first while two-wide fights fill the pack behind them.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5385,"title":"Player and Osborne spin in separate contact","summary":"A three-wide accordion involving Jorge Rincon turns Player, while Osborne tangles with John Gallagher moments later; the paired incidents produce another caution with 70 laps left.","tags":["andrew-player","jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6293,"title":"Bryant turns Pope and opens the money stop","summary":"Bryant clips Pope while moving high and sends the No. 27 around; under the yellow, Burke leads roughly half the field onto pit road for its final set of tires while Ricky Whittenburg, Bryant, and Robertson stay out.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6559,"title":"Dixon turns Vaught into McCabe","summary":"Vaught tries to charge forward on the restart but a tap from Dixon spins him toward pit entry, where Chad McCabe arrives with nowhere to go and hits him hard.","tags":["jack-dixon","jess-vaught","chad-mccabe"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7144,"title":"A restart stack-up scatters the back half","summary":"The inside line checks up with 23 laps left; Greg Dobson brakes, Vaught cannot avoid him, and a multi-truck pileup collects Dixon and several others.","tags":["greg-dobson","jess-vaught","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7399,"title":"Burke clears Robertson on the final restart","summary":"Burke and Robertson take the last green side by side with 17 laps left; Burke breaks free while McDonnell, Bryant, Whittenburg, and Pope fight behind them.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald","dylan-bryant","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7790,"title":"Burke converts fresh tires into victory","summary":"Burke keeps the final lap smooth and wins by about three quarters of a second over Robertson, with McDonnell completing the podium.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":955,"quote":"You've got to be easy on that go-go pedal. We've seen so many self-spins here.","context":"The broadcast identifies throttle control as Richmond's key before qualifying","gold":4},{"t":4431,"quote":"Jess Vaught is going to be your stage winner.","context":"The field is frozen at the scheduled halfway break","gold":4},{"t":5009,"quote":"Where are all the Canadians up in that top deck? Well, now you've got two of them: Jack Dixon and Shawn McDonald.","context":"The booth recognizes the Canadian pair racing near the front after halfway","gold":4},{"t":5552,"quote":"Twenty-five out of thirty-one drivers having a clean race last week—that's amazing to me.","context":"The booth contrasts Pocono's clean-driver bonuses with Richmond's attrition","gold":3},{"t":6357,"quote":"That final set of tires—I think this could be the money stop here for you fellas.","context":"Burke and half the leaders pit after Pope's late spin","gold":5},{"t":6861,"quote":"Never give up, never surrender. Time to go hard.","context":"Albert Anderson rallies the field in chat before the late restarts","gold":4},{"t":8094,"quote":"The speed will come with time. Just learn my lines and learn how to drive clean and not wreck people.","context":"Rookie Kyle Vaught explains the advice he follows while learning new tracks","gold":5},{"t":8388,"quote":"I wanted to be at the front with the fresh tires somehow, some way, and I made it happen.","context":"Winner Jeremiah Burke explains the strategy that delivered his Richmond victory","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 6, Round 6 at Richmond according to seasons_map.json. The 200-lap race used a scheduled caution at lap 100, 60% fuel, four total tire sets, one fast repair, and escalating penalties beginning at 25 incidents with no disqualification. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Burke-Robertson-McDonnell podium and reads the complete 28-driver classification; Andrew Coffin is included because he was entered and classified, although connection and equipment trouble prevented a meaningful race. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for captions calling the No. 14 'Dustyn Eaton,' and 'Jorge Rincon' is retained despite the final readout saying 'George McCollum.' Transcript timestamps end within the 9,215-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"N0r31g7YxgM":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson and Dillon Bryant supplied the early pace in the Badlands 150 at Phoenix, while Chris Goans recognized that matching them straight up was unlikely. The opportunity to change the race arrived when Albert Anderson spun soon after a strategy stop, bringing out the caution with roughly 47 laps remaining. Goans used that yellow for his final set of tires, then drove through the older-tire group, passing Kelly Kuehl and closing on Craig Goodenough and Robertson before their last stops cycled him into the lead. Andy Player remained on the same general sequence, but late contact between Kuehl and Mike Adamson erased Goans's advantage and brought Bryant, on fresher tires, back into the fight. The following restart turned costly for Robertson when smoke hid a stopped truck and left him too little time to avoid a heavy impact. Both closing restart attempts ended under yellow, preventing Bryant from completing an overtime challenge and freezing Goans ahead of Bryant and Player. Goans later explained that going off-cycle was necessary; Bryant accepted second as another useful points result in the season-long championship format.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Dillon Bryant","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":566,"title":"Robertson leads the opening lap","summary":"Trevor Robertson launches from pole ahead of Dillon Bryant as the 27-truck field immediately fans across Phoenix's dogleg.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":624,"title":"Jones spins but the race stays green","summary":"John Schoenbachler gets loose and makes contact with Dion Jones, who threads through traffic without hitting another truck before towing for repairs.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2089,"title":"Mayberry's long first stint ends in a spin","summary":"Dave Mayberry loses the rear at the start-finish line after stretching his opening fuel run, bringing out the race's first caution without striking the wall.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2807,"title":"Coffin bounces back into Mayberry","summary":"Andrew Coffin enters too hot, hits the wall and rebounds into Dave Mayberry, adding damage to a truck Coffin said had already been hurt in the opening incident.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2975,"title":"Kilgore spins to bring out another yellow","summary":"Russ Kilgore loses control and scrapes the inside wall, while Tom Barish narrowly avoids plowing into John Gallagher during the evasive action behind him.","tags":["russ-kilgore","tom-barish","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3731,"title":"Anderson spins on fresh tires","summary":"Albert Anderson's rear tires step out soon after his strategy stop, producing the caution that gives Goans an opportunity to take his last set of tires with about 47 laps remaining.","tags":["albert-anderson","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4332,"title":"Goans cuts through the old-tire leaders","summary":"On much fresher tires, Goans passes Kelly Kuehl and closes on Craig Goodenough and Robertson while the older-tire group tries to delay his advance.","tags":["chris-goans","kelly-keel","craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":4656,"title":"Goans' strategy cycles him to the lead","summary":"Robertson, Goodenough, Kuehl and Jacob Alesia make their final stops, leaving Goans in front with Player chasing on the same pit sequence.","tags":["chris-goans","andrew-player","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","kelly-keel","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5019,"title":"Late Kuehl-Adamson contact resets the race","summary":"Kelly Kuehl and Mike Adamson make contact with roughly ten laps remaining, erasing Goans' lead and opening the door for trucks on fresher tires.","tags":["kelly-keel","mike-adamson","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":5286,"title":"Restart crash destroys Robertson's truck","summary":"Aaron Warren and Mayberry get loose near the dogleg, and Robertson encounters the stopped No. 22 through smoke with too little time to avoid a heavy impact.","tags":["aaron-warren","dave-mayberry","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5712,"title":"Overtime caution seals Goans' win","summary":"Goans clears the opening corners on the green-white-checkered restart before another yellow ends Bryant's chance to attack, locking in Goans, Bryant and Player as the podium.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5725,"quote":"Caution is out, and your winner is going to be Chris Goans.","context":"The booth calls the race-ending overtime yellow.","gold":2},{"t":6011,"quote":"At least a top-three podium finish makes me feel a little bit better.","context":"An ill Andy Player takes consolation in salvaging third.","gold":5},{"t":6213,"quote":"It's straight points this season, so I am points racing, and I'm just going to keep on stacking them up.","context":"Bryant explains why second place remains valuable despite losing a final chance to race for the win.","gold":5},{"t":6445,"quote":"I knew I had to get off cycle, do something a little bit different.","context":"Goans explains the strategy decision that created his winning position.","gold":5},{"t":6488,"quote":"At the end of the day, first place is what we came here for in the first place.","context":"Goans reflects on holding the lead through the late restarts.","gold":5},{"t":6597,"quote":"Hold the wheel straight, drive through the smoke, right?","context":"Goans gives his succinct plan for the following week's Daytona race.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, full results rundown and podium interviews explicitly confirm Goans, Bryant and Player. The results narration repeats a caption-corrupted version of John Schoenbachler in both fifth and tenth; race context identifies the fifth-place truck as John Schoenbachler and the tenth-place truck as John Schoenbachler, two distinct roster entries. All 27 starters are represented by the complete field rundown and final results. Caption variants 'Alan Vault' and 'Ricky Whittenberg' are normalized to Alan Vaught and Ricky Whittenburg, and 'Andrew Cawin' is retained as a caption spelling of Andrew Coffin.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"N8c6pa6T3j4":{"recap":"The broadcast framed Auto Club as a possible farewell to the speedway, and the race supplied both a bruising opening and an unexpected winner. Daniel Baker hit the outside wall in the first major accident, Chandler Paul spun, and Greg Dobson took responsibility during the aftermath. The front stretch later became four-wide, with Andrew Cauthan's No. 10 struck twice as the incident unfolded around him. Alan Vaught and Baker made contact in another close call but saved their trucks, while Earl Evans was not as fortunate when he reached the wall. Albert Anderson won the stage and later shared the front with Jack Dixon in a USA-versus-Canada lead fight. The balance shifted when Sean McDonnell, who had started 29th, reached the lead and began opening a gap. A later bump attempt sent Anderson into the wall, and Vaught eventually passed Dixon as Jorge Rincon followed through. None of those changes brought McDonnell back. He completed a 28-position climb and won in the No. 23. The source proves the victory and starting-position charge, but it does not establish the broadcast's broader suggestion that this was McDonnell's first official VRL start. That claim remains outside the recap, as do unverified position-specific podium assertions beyond the winner.","winner":"Sean McDonnell","podium":["Sean McDonnell","Andrew Player","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":759,"title":"Booth opens with an ice maker emergency","summary":"Alan Brown arrives at the booth out of breath — his fridge's ice maker started dumping ice nonstop right before the broadcast and he had to sprint to fix it.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1608,"title":"The 90 slams the wall — first caution","summary":"Big mix-up in the middle of the pack going into turns three and four; Daniel Baker's No. 90 slams the outside wall hard and Chandler Paul spins, with Greg Dobson taking responsibility on the radio.","tags":["daniel-baker","chandler-paul","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2026,"title":"Four-wide runs out of real estate","summary":"Four-wide on the front stretch goes wrong — Andrew Coffin's No. 10 gets drilled not once but twice, tangling with David Feit and Tim Bates and bringing out the second caution.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","david-fite","timmy-bates"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2383,"title":"Vaught and Baker bang doors — double save","summary":"Contact between the 33 of Alan Vaught and the 90 of Daniel Baker on the restart — both drivers somehow keep all four wheels pointed straight and no caution flies.","tags":["jess-vaught","daniel-baker"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2496,"title":"Earl Evans rides the wall in a shower of smoke","summary":"The sponsored-not-sponsored No. 13 of Earl Evans drags the outside wall with the tire sidewall smoking, holding it high and off traffic in a great save.","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3278,"title":"Anderson wins Stage 1 at the competition yellow","summary":"Albert Anderson crosses the line completing lap 43 to take the Stage 1 win and bonus points as the competition yellow waves.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3712,"title":"USA vs Canada for the lead on the Stage 2 restart","summary":"America's driver Albert Anderson and Canada's driver Jack Dixon line up side by side to start Stage 2 and trade the lead through turns one and two.","tags":["albert-anderson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3992,"title":"From 29th to the lead: McDonnell takes over","summary":"The booth crowns rookie Sean McDonnell the biggest mover of the race — started 29th, now leading the field and beginning to drive away from the veterans.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4623,"title":"Backstretch bump sends Anderson for a wild ride","summary":"Big crash on the backstretch — J.R. Hollingsworth, blending back off pit road, tries to bump-draft Albert Anderson up to speed and instead sends the 747 into the inside wall, wrecking Anderson's night.","tags":["albert-anderson","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4991,"title":"Vaught steals third with Rincon in tow","summary":"Alan Vaught gets a great run underneath Jack Dixon to take third in the closing laps, with Jorge Rincon following him right on through.","tags":["jess-vaught","jack-dixon","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5300,"title":"Rookie Sean McDonnell wins at Auto Club","summary":"Sean McDonnell, a Canadian rookie in his first official VRL race, rounds turn four to take the win — up 28 spots from 29th — over reigning champion Andrew Player, with Alan Vaught holding off Jorge Rincon for third.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","andrew-player","jess-vaught","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":771,"quote":"The dang ice maker in the fridge just started dropping ice for no reason and just wouldn't stop.","context":"Alan Brown explains why he arrived at the booth out of breath","gold":3},{"t":2061,"quote":"Oh man, the 10 just absolutely gets drilled — not once but twice.","context":"the four-wide front-stretch crash that collected Andrew Coffin","gold":4},{"t":2181,"quote":"Louisiana — take my shoes off, I can count twice as high.","context":"pit-strategy math banter in the booth","gold":4},{"t":2629,"quote":"You could not fit a piece of paper between those two trucks.","context":"a millimeters-close near miss in mid-pack traffic","gold":3},{"t":3969,"quote":"He's driving it like he stole the thing.","context":"Dustin Wade's charge giving his wife Amanda a heart attack in the chat","gold":4},{"t":5300,"quote":"The 23 of Shawn McDonald, rookie, picking up the race win!","context":"the checkered-flag call at Auto Club","gold":4},{"t":5725,"quote":"I don't know what corner of Canada y'all found that driver of the 23, but that cat's putting on a clinic out here.","context":"the booth marveling at the race winner during Alan Vaught's interview","gold":4},{"t":5794,"quote":"Just a shout out to the dictator Lori — where the hell, she put most of my team on the penalty box for this race.","context":"Alan Vaught's podium interview shout-outs to race admin Lori Vaught","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"85-lap NASCAR Trucks-style race at Auto Club Speedway (broadcast Feb 2023); booth says it is likely the track's final race before demolition. First ~9:30 of the video is pre-show music. Cautions: lap-13 wreck (Baker/Chandler Paul), the four-wide Coffin crash, and a lap-43 competition/stage yellow; the late Anderson backstretch crash did not clearly draw a caution. Finishing order in the 28th-32nd range is garbled in captions. Name spellings uncertain: #37 'Dustin really' rendered as Dustin Riehle; #1 'David fight' rendered as David Feit; #14 'Dustin with a Y' rendered as Dustyn Eaton; #58 Chipman's first name garbled ('forever'/'Robert'). Ricky Whittenburg mentioned only as the league's painter, not racing tonight. Race admin Lori Vaught and family members (Kyle, Sarah, Taylor Vaught) mentioned as spectators, not drivers.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"NDARIcu37NQ":{"recap":"Two nights before the VRL All-Star Race, fourteen drivers brought Xfinity cars to Talladega for a 100-lap, four-stage Last Chance Qualifier where the top two in every stage — plus the top six finishers who hadn't already won a stage — earned a spot in Wednesday's show. Dion Jones stole Stage 1 by firing through a middle gap from fifth as a Big One erupted at the stripe behind him and Hot Rod Mayberry, day-one league newcomer Greg Klein raced his way in alongside Mike Everage in a one-lap Stage 2 shootout, and Jeff Ottinger beat Jorge Rincon to the Stage 3 line in a photo finish. The night was littered with multi-car wrecks, a near-flip for Russell Endicott, and booth theatrics headlined by guest Jeremiah Burke proposing to fight Mayberry in a Walmart parking lot. Jones then capped the 40-lap finale by hooking leader Chandler Paul in the last corner — a move the booth instantly called \"pulling a Ross Chastain\" — to take the checkered flag ahead of Paul and Ottinger. Chad McCabe missed the cut and was left pinning his All-Star hopes on the fan vote.","winner":"Dion Jones","podium":["Dion Jones","Chandler Paul","Jeff Ottinger"],"moments":[{"t":2349,"title":"Three-wide for the lead breaks loose","summary":"Late in Stage 1 the pack goes three wide for the lead and it breaks loose — the first caution flies, and in the aftermath Mayberry bounces back across the track into league newcomer Greg Klein, who hits the wall and collects Chandler Paul.","tags":["austin-paul","dave-mayberry","greg-cline","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2879,"title":"Jones steals Stage 1 as the Big One erupts at the line","summary":"Sitting fifth entering Turn 3, Dion Jones sees a gap open in the middle, shoots it with a push from the 13, and beats Hot Rod Mayberry to the stage line while a huge wreck breaks out behind them — the booth says it took out all but about four cars. \"Wow, what a finish!\"","tags":["dion-jones","dave-mayberry","austin-paul","mike-everage","greg-dobson","greg-cline","russ-endicott"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3894,"title":"Bad luck for the green machine","summary":"Earl Evans gets turned in Stage 2 traffic, beaten and banged into Greg Dobson, with Jorge Rincon collected and Mayberry taking a hard impact — cueing the booth's riff on why you never paint a NASCAR stock car green.","tags":["earl-evans","russ-endicott","greg-dobson","george-rincon","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4446,"title":"Endicott nearly flips — and iRacing keeps it green","summary":"Squeezed in a three-wide beating-and-banging battle with Chandler Paul in the middle, the 57 checks up, loses it into Austin Paul and just about flips over; no caution comes, and Endicott limps on with a meatball flag \"spraying for mosquitoes.\"","tags":["russ-endicott","austin-paul","chandler-paul","earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5140,"title":"Klein races his way in on day one","summary":"After a last-lap wreck forces officials to roll the clock back for a one-lap Stage 2 shootout, newcomer Greg Klein — who joined the league that very day — snakes to the front and crosses the line side by side with Mike Everage as both punch All-Star tickets.","tags":["greg-cline","mike-everage","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":3,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6078,"title":"Havoc in Stage 3 — Everage clobbered, Endicott into the wall","summary":"Earl Evans' big outside run ends in contact down into the 28 and havoc follows: Mike Everage gets \"absolutely clobber-knocked\" with nowhere to go and Russ Endicott hits the outside wall very hard, while Greg Klein gets a \"Moses parting of the Red Sea\" escape through the middle.","tags":["earl-evans","george-rincon","mike-everage","russ-endicott","chad-mccabe","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6334,"title":"Hot Rod calls his shots — \"Team Limited\"","summary":"Already locked into the All-Star Race, Dave Mayberry joins the booth and says his Stage 1 run was \"just for the Team Limited\" — deliberately flubbing rival Limitless Motorsports' name — and vows to park it in victory lane Wednesday. Shots fired.","tags":["dave-mayberry","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6595,"title":"T-bone on the Stage 3 restart","summary":"A chain reaction right after the restart: Austin Paul's charge from nowhere collides with the 57, sending Endicott back across the track to t-bone Jorge Rincon, with Hot Rod Mayberry swept up with absolutely nowhere to go — a lot of damaged race cars at the end of that deal.","tags":["austin-paul","russ-endicott","george-rincon","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7001,"title":"Photo finish for Stage 3","summary":"Jeff Ottinger and Jorge Rincon drag-race door to door out of Turn 4 to end Stage 3 — the booth calls for the photo-finish cam and awards it to the 76 by \"the difference of where you put the transponder.\"","tags":["jeff-ottinger","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7982,"title":"Pushing the pusher busts the yolk","summary":"In the final stage Tony Polk pushes the pusher and the tandem folds — Greg Klein, Chandler Paul, Jeff Ottinger and Dion Jones all tangle in the mess, Polk admits guilt, and the booth rules you simply can't unscramble an egg.","tags":["tony-polk","greg-cline","chandler-paul","jeff-ottinger","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8190,"title":"\"We're going to fight\" — Burke calls out Mayberry","summary":"Booth guest Jeremiah Burke accuses Mayberry of \"wrecking everybody every chance he gets,\" notes he only lives about 100 miles away, and proposes settling it in front of a Walmart — with the booth offering to put the fight on YouTube at the Phoenix championship race.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":10204,"title":"\"No fear!\" — Jones hooks Chan the Man at the flag","summary":"After pushing leader Chandler Paul the entire final run, Dion Jones hooks him in the last corner of the last lap — a full \"Ross Chastain\" the booth can't believe since Jones was already locked into the All-Star Race — and takes the checkered flag, with Paul limping home second 20 seconds back.","tags":["dion-jones","chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1050,"quote":"If a space shuttle crashes and burns, we all know who to blame.","context":"English defending his one-night takeover of Brown's director chair","gold":3},{"t":1594,"quote":"It's all fun and games till you run out of fuel.","context":"the pack playing hot potato with the lead to save fuel in Stage 1","gold":3},{"t":3949,"quote":"Here it is, Evans — you get bad luck in that green machine. Can't have a green car in NASCAR, we know that.","context":"Earl Evans' all-green No. 13 collected in another wreck","gold":3},{"t":4961,"quote":"There's one lap left, you get a chance to be in the All-Star Race, man — let it loose! Cut somebody, turn somebody, burn somebody!","context":"hyping the one-lap Stage 2 shootout","gold":4},{"t":6344,"quote":"Hey, you know what, I did that just for the Team Limited — just wanted to let them know what they're up against Wednesday.","context":"Mayberry trash-talks Limitless Motorsports from the booth after winning his way in","gold":4},{"t":8037,"quote":"Well, you can't unscramble an egg — the fork's done busted the yolk, you can't unscramble that.","context":"surveying the push-the-pusher pileup in the final stage","gold":4},{"t":8291,"quote":"He gets a hell of a parking spot — we'll fight right up by the front door at Walmart.","context":"Jeremiah Burke plotting to fight Hot Rod Mayberry over all the wrecks","gold":4},{"t":10212,"quote":"Oh, he did — he did take him! Oh dude, holy smokes, no fear! Dion Jones just pulled a Ross Chastain!","context":"Jones hooks race leader Chandler Paul in the final corner of the last lap","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Stage-format Last Chance Qualifier (4 stages, 20/20/20/40; Xfinity cars at Talladega): stage top-twos were Jones/Mayberry (S1), Everage/Klein (S2, order at the line unclear), Ottinger/Rincon (S3, photo finish). 'Winner' and podium reflect the final-stage rundown read on air (Jones, Chandler Paul +20s after being hooked, Ottinger). All-Star qualifiers per the tape: six stage winners plus Chandler Paul, David Feit, Austin Paul, Tony Polk, Russ Endicott and Greg Dobson via finishing position; Chad McCabe missed and relies on the fan vote; Earl Evans didn't qualify but said he wasn't racing Wednesday anyway. Auto-caption name uncertainty: 'David Feit' spelled as heard (could be Fite/Feit); 'Tony Polk' inferred from the 'Poke Salad Tony' / Polk Salad Annie nickname (captions alternate poke/polk); 'Mike Everage' captions alternate average/everedge; 'Jorge Rincon' heavily garbled throughout. Greg Klein's spelling confirmed by a chapter marker. Broadcast is AAA Broadcasting with a role reversal (English directing instead of Brown); Alan Kewins mentioned as extra crew but not on air. Mayberry's teammates 'Jess' and 'Dustin' and league admins 'Lori and Jess' mentioned first-name only. Race was presented by DND Race Grafix and Keller Williams of Johnson City, TN.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"NFcfuVbtu48":{"recap":"Season 12 of the VRL Premiere Series — and the Vigilante Racing Network's first official broadcast — opened at Chicagoland Speedway with a race for the league record books: 37 trucks ran all 133 laps caution-free, with 20 finishing on the lead lap. Pole sitter Jason Gaines and Craig Goodenough swapped the lead all night in what the booth dubbed '180-mph chess,' a duel settled on green-flag pit strategy when Goodenough hit pit road a lap before Gaines on the final cycle and cleared him by roughly eight tenths. Dillon Bryant charged late to finish third, completing a podium of the race's top three qualifiers. Jack Dixon stormed from the back of the grid to seventh with the race's fastest laps, and Team Allstar — Gaines, Bryant, Albert Anderson, Dixon and Jeremiah Burke — put its whole lineup in the top ten. New booth duo Alan Vault and Ricky Whittenburg, both fresh out of the cockpit, filled the green-flag marathon with live in-car driver interviews.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Jason Gaines","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":1170,"title":"Ricky's 1895 Chicago history drop","summary":"During the pace laps, Ricky reveals Chicago hosted America's first automobile race in 1895 — six cars, six inches of snow, and a winning average speed of 5 mph.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1248,"title":"Green flag on the 18-race war","summary":"Pole sitter Jason Gaines brings 37 trucks to green for the Season 12 opener; Goodenough's 89 grabs outside momentum into turn one and the pack runs wide open.","tags":["jason-gaines","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1981,"title":"Goodenough gets evil off Turn 2","summary":"Race leader Craig Goodenough nearly claps the wall exiting Turn 2, letting Jason Gaines pounce right back onto his bumper; the booth rolls the replay moments later.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jason-gaines"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2120,"title":"Green-flag pit chess begins","summary":"The first green-flag stop cycle spreads the field: Albert Anderson stretches fuel and Josh Bittner briefly inherits the lead off his early stop before Gaines cycles back to the point.","tags":["josh-bittner","albert-anderson","jason-gaines","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2785,"title":"The Mouth calls in from the cockpit","summary":"With no cautions to fill, the booth pulls Dave Mayberry into a live interview mid-battle and he deadpans that he was doing good until he hit the wall — wheel damage and all.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3256,"title":"Bittner's gamble: P4, up 17 spots","summary":"Josh Bittner's off-cycle strategy cycles him up to fourth, 17 spots ahead of where he started, with Trevor Robertson closing to within two tenths.","tags":["josh-bittner","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4585,"title":"Mr. Cool interviews at 180 mph","summary":"Kelly Kuehl calmly talks split-stint pit strategy with the booth while racing for 16th under green, living up to his Mr. Cool nickname.","tags":["kelly-keel","austin-paul","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4960,"title":"Gallagher mows the lawn on pit entry","summary":"John Gallagher overshoots pit road entirely and cuts through the grass, with the booth predicting a black flag for unsafe entry.","tags":["john-gallagher"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5318,"title":"Three-wide haymakers in the midfield","summary":"'Oh, that was close' — Kelly Kuehl, John McAdam, Austin Paul and the 10 truck of Andrew Cawthon go three-wide slugging it out for position in the closing laps.","tags":["kelly-keel","john-mcadam","austin-paul","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5449,"title":"Austin Paul skates through the grass","summary":"With about six to go Austin Paul gets loose and drops through the grass as the 47 dives low to survive — the closest the night comes to a caution, and the moment leader Goodenough later admitted made him think 'here we go.'","tags":["austin-paul","john-mcadam","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5520,"title":"Dixon's silent charge from the back","summary":"Jack Dixon posts the fastest lap and fastest five-lap average of the race, climbing about 20 positions from the tail of the grid into the top seven.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5560,"title":"Flag to flag: Goodenough wins the caution-free opener","summary":"Craig Goodenough takes the checkered roughly eight tenths clear of Jason Gaines after 133 caution-free laps, with Dillon Bryant completing a podium of the race's top three qualifiers.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jason-gaines","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":548,"quote":"Tonight, the Rebellion officially launches. The Vigilante Racing League goes lights on for the first battle of an 18-race war.","context":"Alan Vault's cold open on VRN's first official broadcast","gold":4},{"t":690,"quote":"These guys are getting so much faster. I figured I might as well get out before I got my butt kicked on a weekly basis.","context":"Ricky on why he moved from the cockpit to the booth","gold":3},{"t":1470,"quote":"They've got to play a little bit nicer or Lori will drop the banhammer on them.","context":"Ricky on why Wednesday nights stay cleaner than Monday practice","gold":4},{"t":2803,"quote":"I was doing good, but then I hit the wall.","context":"Dave Mayberry, interviewed live in-car under green","gold":4},{"t":5508,"quote":"Just enough for good enough, right? He's got a good enough gap that he's going to make it. Sorry for the pun, folks.","context":"The booth as Goodenough guards his lead with two laps to go","gold":4},{"t":6067,"quote":"That was absolutely amazing, man. I have never sweated so much driving a sim car.","context":"Runner-up Jason Gaines' first words in the post-race booth","gold":3},{"t":6109,"quote":"It was a little bit of 180 mph chess between the two of you getting on and off pit road.","context":"Alan on the Goodenough–Gaines pit-strategy duel","gold":4},{"t":6613,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, stay Vigilante Nation... This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"The broadcast sign-off","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption name garble is heavy; best guesses were made: 'Chris Goins' (captions: 'Chris Gones'), 'David Feit' ('David Feit/Fe/F'), 'Andrew Cawthon' ('Cawan/Cton/Coffin/Cthin'), 'Jorge Rincon' ('Rcon/Rencon'), 'John Schoenbachler' ('Scholen Bachler/Shawacher/Sha Bachler/Shenbacher'), and 'Sean McDonnell' (grid read 'John McDonnell', mid-race 'Tom McDonnell' — treated as one Canadian driver). Winner's margin heard as '08'/'eight' — interpreted as ~0.8s, consistent with the lead being called 'under a second' in the closing laps. Official results beyond the podium weren't read out: Robertson 4th / Goins 5th reflect the running order ~11 laps from the end; Anderson 6th, Dixon 7th, Burke 9th come from Dillon Bryant's podium interview. Scott Rooney withdrew early for a personal reason; Greg Klein sat the round out for his 20th wedding anniversary. Ricky's surname is captioned 'Whittenberg' — rendered as Whittenburg.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"nG1-WMLIi5s":{"recap":"On iRacing update night at Daytona, the VRL trucks ran 100 laps of white-knuckle pack racing that lived up to the 'Devastating Destruction' billing, with net code chaos turning trucks around and launching them into the pack all evening. Alan Vaught in the #33 survived damage in a mid-race Big One at the front and, with Mike Adamson's #88 glued to his bumper, beat hard-charger Jack Dixon to the line by four thousandths of a second. Dixon climbed 25 spots without a fast repair to finish second, Adamson pushed his way onto the podium in third, and Kelly Kuehl — called one of the best pushers in iRacing by the booth — came home fourth after towing his teammate all night. Earl Evans's bad-luck #13 shone with what the booth called his best finish of the season in sixth. In victory lane Vaught dedicated the emotional win to Kathy Griggs, his wife Lori's mother, who passed away that week.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Jack Dixon","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":2660,"title":"Meatball for America's Driver","summary":"Albert Anderson gets the meatball flag after a mis-shift over-revs and blows his engine leaving the pits, sending America's Driver laps down and chasing the lucky dog the rest of the night.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2916,"title":"First Big Wreck in the Tri-Oval","summary":"Chandler Paul bobbles through the tri-oval and tags Mike Taylor's 98; the checkup collects the 82 and 27 with hard wall impacts, wipes out Greg Klein in the wrong place at the wrong time, and Larry Dickerson slams the outside wall.","tags":["chandler-paul","mike-taylor","mike-everage","trevor-robertson","greg-cline","dave-mayberry","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3489,"title":"How Did We Not See a Wreck There?","summary":"Kelly Kuehl drops into the sucker hole, Osborne dives down, and Mike Adamson makes an incredible save at 170 mph — the whole field threads through the chaos without a caution.","tags":["kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3882,"title":"Stage-Break Chaos","summary":"Right at the halfway stage break Chachi self-pit-maneuvers across the 14, Adamson ends up backwards against the wall, Jonah Long gets collected, and John Gallagher literally tele-warps through the 79 — net code handing Alejandro Gonzalez a lucky break.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-eaton","john-gallagher","alejandro-gonzalez","jonah-long","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4538,"title":"The Big One Up Front","summary":"A net code bobble at the head of the pack turns the 01 of Kelly Kuehl around, the 6 plows straight in, the 81 gets spun, and race leader Alan Vaught picks up damage as absolute chaos collects much of the front group.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5087,"title":"David Kelly's Miracle Save","summary":"The 49 snaps loose off the yellow-line transition and David Kelly somehow holds onto it, while Earl Evans makes a heads-up check-up in the bad-luck 13 to keep it from becoming a pileup.","tags":["david-kelly","earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5390,"title":"Mayberry Wrecks the Chase Pack","summary":"Dave Mayberry drifts lazily up the track and pit-maneuvers himself into Andrew Cotton's 10, collecting Chan the Man with nowhere to go — the booth jokes the realtor was checking Zillow for a sale.","tags":["dave-mayberry","chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6045,"title":"Net Code Devastation","summary":"The lagging 6's phantom hitbox square-taps Mike Everage's 82 and slings him into the pack — the 49 goes for a ride, the 14 and 28 get swept up, and Rancone is sent around — prompting the booth to demand iRacing fix its net code.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-everage","david-kelly","dustin-eaton","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6681,"title":"Dobson Loses It, Field Splits","summary":"With about 16 to go Greg Dobson slips onto the apron off the yellow line and loses it, the 5 goes hard into the outside wall, and the huge no-caution checkup splits the lead pack while Dobson limps home with heavy suspension damage.","tags":["greg-dobson","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6962,"title":"Late Yellow Sets Up a Shootout","summary":"A caution with under 10 to go — the 79 of Alejandro Gonzalez going for a wild ride after contact with Dickerson — stacks 18 trucks back into one pack for a five-lap dash to the finish.","tags":["alejandro-gonzalez","larry-dickerson","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7535,"title":"Four Thousandths at the Line","summary":"On the final lap, with trucks wrecking behind them off turn four, Alan Vaught gets one last shove from Mike Adamson and beats hard-charger Jack Dixon — up 25 spots with no fast repair — to the checkers by 0.004 seconds.","tags":["jess-vaught","jack-dixon","mike-adamson","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8408,"title":"A Win for Kathy","summary":"In victory lane Alan Vaught dedicates the win to Kathy Griggs — his wife Lori's mother, who passed away that week — in an emotional interview that caps the night for the league family.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1115,"quote":"I'm going to push you, I'm going to push you all the way to the front — oh never mind, you just got crashed. You got turned and learned.","context":"pre-race lesson on fake friendship in the Daytona draft","gold":4},{"t":3044,"quote":"Something about the frame rates, I don't know what was happening in the car. He was framed, I think.","context":"Larry Dickerson blames connection issues after slamming the wall","gold":3},{"t":3229,"quote":"Did we just upgrade from Florida Man to Florida Bear?","context":"booth tangent about a three-legged bear that broke into a house and drank three White Claws","gold":4},{"t":3393,"quote":"Tonight's line was even money, 50/50. — Have they seen Mayberry race?","context":"handicapping the Mayberry vs Kyle Vaught rivalry","gold":3},{"t":5424,"quote":"Maybe somebody was on Zillow, picked one of his homes and liked it — 'oh, I might get a sale' — oh well, I just crashed everybody.","context":"realtor Dave Mayberry drifts up the track and wrecks the chase pack","gold":4},{"t":6139,"quote":"iRacing, please move this to the top of your priority list. Fix this net code.","context":"after lag launched the 82 into a multi-truck wreck","gold":4},{"t":6894,"quote":"It's just like shooting dice in Waco on a Saturday night — somebody's got a .22, somebody's got a knife.","context":"on the gamble of riding the bottom lane late at Daytona","gold":5},{"t":7605,"quote":"Four thousandths of a second separated Jess Vault and Jack Dixon for one and two.","context":"the photo-finish call at the line","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions. The winning family's name is rendered V/VA/vot/Vault/Von in captions — 'Vaught' chosen for Jess, Kyle, and race control Lori (also Brandon and Ava mentioned as family/fans). 'Eric Clifa' (#5) and 'Jorge Rincon' (#28, captions recone/ranan/ranone, first name possibly Jorge) are uncertain reconstructions, as is 'Andrew Cotton' (#10, captions cin/Cen/korne). A 'Sean Connell' mentioned during qualifying may be the same driver as Sean McDonnell (#23), who did not grid. Lori Vaught served as race control (not a driver); Allstar Racing teammate 'Jeremiah' was mentioned as absent. Aired live 2023-09-06/07 on AAA Broadcasting, presented by Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry) and GC Cruise and Travel (Greg Klein). Race was on an iRacing update day; the booth attributed multiple wrecks to net code. Full finishing order was read out at ~2:22:23 in the broadcast.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"nJlfdhP4wyw":{"recap":"With NASCAR points racing on Olympic break, the VRL filled its Wednesday night with a one-off 'Terminator' exhibition at USA International Raceway in Lakeland, Florida: a field of roughly 25 Legends cars playing Sarah Connor while two faster Radicals — league boss Alan Vaught in the 33 and Ricky Whittenburg in the 55 — hunted whoever held the race lead. The Terminators slow-played the first 100 laps, sandwiching and toying with leaders like Kyle Vaught and Kelly Kuehl, then went 'scorched earth' in the final stage, full-speed ramming everything in sight — most memorably a blindside 'murder' of Greg Klein straight out of the lead. Austin Paul earned booth honors for juking and trash-talking his way through repeated double-team attacks before finally being run down. When a last-lap bump spun leader Zachary Hennen off the final corner, Dustin Wade snuck by to steal the win in the last turn, with Craig Goodenough second and David Feit third.","winner":"Dustin Wade","podium":["Dustin Wade","Craig Goodenough","David Feit"],"moments":[{"t":1310,"title":"Green flag, instant carnage","summary":"The Legends swarm goes four and five wide off the initial start; the 16 goes for a ride into the infield before the Terminators are even on track, with Osborne grabbing the early lead.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","shawn-mcdonald","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1459,"title":"The Terminators are released","summary":"Headlights appear down the straightaway as the first Radical joins the track and leader Sean McDonnell starts running for his life; Whittenburg is released moments later.","tags":["jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":1492,"title":"First blood: Dixon walled, Osborne flies","summary":"Jack Dixon takes the lead for the first time and is immediately shoved into the outside wall as the 81 of Osborne goes flipping and flying in the mayhem.","tags":["jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1607,"title":"The big ole' ole on Whittenburg","summary":"With nowhere to hide, leader David Feit slides all the way down the track and matadors the charging Terminator, forcing Whittenburg to loop all the way back around.","tags":["david-fite","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2410,"title":"Sandwich special flips Kyle Vaught","summary":"After Whittenburg swings and misses, both Terminators trap leader Kyle Vaught in a two-for-one sandwich and send the 16 flipping and flying.","tags":["kyle-vaught","ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3186,"title":"Kuehl sandwiched, Mayberry nailed","summary":"The Terminators go one in front, one behind on leader Kelly Kuehl; McDonnell squeaks through the middle and the 46 of Mayberry takes a huge hit with bits and pieces flying.","tags":["kelly-keel","shawn-mcdonald","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3595,"title":"Front-stretch flip-fest","summary":"A no-caution pileup sends cars flipping, flying, and 'teleporting in' down the front stretch — absolute chaos with the booth howling that 'people are dying.'","tags":["jeremiah-burke","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3744,"title":"Austin Paul understands the assignment","summary":"The trash-talking pink 3 car jukes and jives through a two-Terminator double-team, escaping a sandwich before finally succumbing — the booth replays it as the highlight of the night to that point.","tags":["austin-paul","jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4656,"title":"Klein gets Klined","summary":"A big takeout out of nowhere blindsides race leader Greg Klein — 'that was murder, murder!' — repeatedly cited in the booth and post-race interviews as the favorite moment of the night.","tags":["greg-cline","ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4836,"title":"Scorched-earth rampage","summary":"The gloves come off after lap 100: the Terminators go full-speed ramming through the field, even trading Terminator-on-Terminator friendly fire as they destroy anyone near the lead.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5300,"title":"Jeremiah Burke's infinite flip","summary":"A glitch leaves the 53 flipping and flopping endlessly down the front stretch, unable to reset — the booth pities poor Jeremiah as the car just keeps tumbling.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5412,"title":"Wade steals it in the last turn","summary":"Hennen survives an attack run at the white flag, but one final Terminator bump spins the 74 off the last corner and Dustin Wade sneaks by to win, with Goodenough second and Fite third.","tags":["dustin-wade","craig-goodenough","david-fite"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":966,"quote":"Why would NASCAR stop because of the Olympics? People that are watching swimming and gymnastics never watched NASCAR to begin with.","context":"Adam Turner's pre-race rant about NASCAR pausing for the Olympic break","gold":3},{"t":1010,"quote":"You're just going to have to put on your Sarah Connor act and run like hell.","context":"The 'key to the race' segment explaining the Terminator format","gold":4},{"t":1706,"quote":"They're both hunting in a pack now like Velociraptors.","context":"Both Terminators ganging up on the race leader for the first time","gold":4},{"t":1920,"quote":"Just circling them like a hungry hammerhead shark out there.","context":"A Terminator stalking leader Greg Dobson without striking","gold":3},{"t":3612,"quote":"It's absolute chaos out there — people are dying. That was awesome.","context":"A no-caution flip-fest down the front stretch","gold":4},{"t":4676,"quote":"Oh my God, that's what I was waiting for — that was murder! Murder!","context":"Greg Klein blindsided straight out of the race lead by a Terminator","gold":5},{"t":5965,"quote":"It's a Terminator race, so you're going to have to go out on your shield — we decided to go scorched earth and not hold anything back in that last stage.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg's post-race interview on the final-stage rampage","gold":4},{"t":6061,"quote":"That was the favorite part for me for the night, when Klein just got Klined himself.","context":"The booth reliving the Greg Klein takeout during the Terminator interviews","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Non-points exhibition ('VRL-ympics' Olympic-break event), no chapters in metadata; winner is whoever led at the finish and was clearly stated (Dustin Wade, then Goodenough, then Fite via podium interviews). Surname guesses from garbled captions: 'Vaught' for Jess/Kyle (captions vot/VOD/vont/Vault; league co-owner Lori shares the name — could be Vogt); 'Hennen' for the 74 (henin/Howen/Callen); 'Maroth' for the 42 (Marth/marot/Marriot); 'Fite' for the 1 (always captioned 'fight'); 'Ranan' and 'Chan the Man' (#72) are as-heard, proper names unknown. Dave Mayberry's car number is given as both 46 and 29 at different points. Dustyn Eaton (#14, 'Dustin with a Y') vs Dustin Wade (#68, 'Dustin with an i') per the booth's own disambiguation. Track: USA International Raceway/Speedway, Lakeland FL, 3/4-mile oval; Legends cars vs two Radical 'Terminators' who could only wreck the leader; stage cautions near laps 50 and 100 (Kevin Hunt led stage 1, Greg Klein stage 2). Craig Goodenough also noted as winner of Monday's stadium truck race at Wild West.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"NUuNDlS1d8g":{"recap":"Tim Pope came from 19th on the grid to win the Season 14 chase opener at Nashville for the second consecutive year. The 150-lap race ran caution-free through two full green-flag pit cycles and 106 laps, with Craig Goodenough dominating early, Dillon Bryant and Jacob Alesia trading the lead through strategy, and Pope steadily advancing. The sole caution for contact between Gordon Spain and Andrew Coffin reset the field for a 38-lap sprint in which Goodenough again led while Chris Goans, Bryant, Mike Adamson and Pope converged. In a remarkably clean four- and nearly five-wide final-lap battle, Pope surged from the outside group to beat Goans and Bryant without a wreck.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Chris Goans","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":754,"title":"Alesia leads the chase opener to green","summary":"Pole sitter Jacob Alesia takes the initial advantage over Sean McDonnell as 34 trucks begin the 150-lap race.","tags":["jacob-alicia","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":859,"title":"Goodenough takes the early lead","summary":"Craig Goodenough moves past Alesia and begins stretching an advantage over Scott Rooney, establishing the dominant pace of the opening stint.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1794,"title":"Bryant moves into second","summary":"After saving tires behind the fast-starting leaders, Dillon Bryant clears Rooney and begins closing the gap to Goodenough.","tags":["dylan-bryant","scott-rooney","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1879,"title":"Coffin spins but keeps the race green","summary":"Contact off Kyle Vaught's nose sends Andrew Coffin around near the first fuel window; Coffin completes one loop without damage and returns to the track.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":2026,"title":"First green-flag pit cycle reshuffles the lead","summary":"Goodenough and Bryant pit around lap 39 while Jorge Rincon stretches to lap 41; Bryant cycles ahead of Alesia, Goodenough and Goans.","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","george-rincon","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3087,"title":"Second fuel cycle begins under green","summary":"Goodenough, Adamson and Scott Milner start another long series of stops as the race continues without a yellow and tire-age differences widen.","tags":["craig-goodenough","mike-adamson","scott-milner"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":4067,"title":"Alesia leads deep into the third stint","summary":"With five-lap-older tires than pursuing Goans, Alesia holds first while Bryant runs third and Pope reaches sixth after gaining 14 positions.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans","dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4242,"title":"The only caution changes everything","summary":"Gordon Spain misjudges his move around Andrew Coffin and damages the right front, bringing out the first and only yellow on lap 107 just before the next scheduled stops.","tags":["gordon-spain","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4490,"title":"Goodenough controls the final sprint","summary":"Alesia restarts first, but Goodenough quickly emerges as leader while Trevor Robertson climbs from 21st to second and the chase contenders stack up behind them.","tags":["jacob-alicia","craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5458,"title":"Five contenders converge on Goodenough","summary":"Goans closes a large gap to Goodenough as Bryant, Adamson and Pope join the fight, turning the final eight laps into a multi-lane battle for the win.","tags":["chris-goans","craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","mike-adamson","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5721,"title":"Pope wins from four wide","summary":"Pope uses a final run through the four-wide lead battle to take the checkered flag for a 19-position charge. Goans finishes second and Bryant third as every contender keeps the trucks pointed straight.","tags":["timothy-pope","chris-goans","dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5721,"quote":"Tim Pope's going to go again, second year in a row. Checkered flag to Tim Pope in the seven, up 19 spots here for the victory tonight.","context":"The booth calls Pope's winning last-lap charge","gold":5},{"t":5731,"quote":"That was an incredible finish, folks. All of those drivers, they did not wreck.","context":"The booth reacts to the four-wide clean finish","gold":5},{"t":6375,"quote":"This was chaos, it was exciting, and it was nerve-wracking, but these guys did a heck of a job.","context":"Runner-up Chris Goans praises the drivers around him","gold":5},{"t":6385,"quote":"I appreciate being able to race those guys like that.","context":"Goans reflects on the respectful battle","gold":4},{"t":6481,"quote":"Man, it was crazy. I didn't win, but dude, I am beyond excited and pumped up.","context":"Third-place finisher Dillon Bryant reacts to the finish","gold":5},{"t":6491,"quote":"At four wide, almost five wide, I was like, Allen's getting him a show tonight—and the fans.","context":"Bryant describes recognizing the spectacle from the cockpit","gold":5},{"t":6591,"quote":"We was battling out like some gladiators, and it was clean.","context":"Bryant thanks Goodenough, Robertson, Goans and Pope","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete 34-driver finishing order is read after the interviews. The race had one caution, on lap 107; Coffin's earlier spin and several later incidents stayed green. The winner interview audio was misaligned in the source and its answers are absent from the transcript, so no Pope interview quotes are invented. The opening explicitly identifies this as Season 14 round 14 and the first of five chase races. ","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"nYanurC88SM":{"recap":"Phoenix lived up to its 'Pandemonium' billing: pole sitter Alan Vaught barrel-rolled on the opening lap, and caution after caution turned the 150-lap Truck race into what the booth and drivers called a demolition derby. Team Limitless controlled the first half, with Mike and Dale Adamson and Jeremiah Burke running up front before Andrew Player stole the Stage 1 win at the halfway break. The wrecks kept stacking up through the second half — including David L. Kelly's flight 'to the moon' — and the race came down to a one-attempt green-white-checker. Rookie J.R. Hollingsworth ran Jeremiah Burke door-to-door on the final lap, and with Burke shoved up into the wall off turn four, Hollingsworth took the win in what Burke called one of the tightest non-plate finishes in league history. Andrew Player finished third, real-life ARCA driver Brayton Laster fifth, and Mike Taylor was the ninth-place random-draw winner as the series heads to Atlanta next week.","winner":"J.R. Hollingsworth","podium":["J.R. Hollingsworth","Jeremiah Burke","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":1502,"title":"Lap 1: Vaught's Ricky Bobby Barrel Roll","summary":"Green-flag chaos immediately: Greg Klein hits the wall, then pole sitter Alan Vaught flips wildly through the dogleg — 'more flips than Ricky Bobby' — while Jorge Rincon gets flipped around and Chandler Paul slams the inside wall.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","chandler-paul","greg-cline","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2111,"title":"Fast Repairs Flying in Early Pileup","summary":"Another early multi-truck wreck collects David Feit, Dustyn Eaton and real-life ARCA driver Brayton Laster — a lot of guys burn their one fast repair before lap 20, leaving 'mosquito trucks' smoking around the track.","tags":["david-fite","dustin-eaton","brayton-laster"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2247,"title":"Dale's Strategy: Pray for Cautions","summary":"Running second behind his dad, Dale Adamson tells the booth his strategy is to 'pray and hope for more cautions' — the booth assures him no prayers will be necessary at this track.","tags":["dale-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4099,"title":"The Parking Lot","summary":"The lap-63 restart erupts into a parking lot on the front stretch — Mayberry spins, Chipman can't slow down, Rincon, McDonnell and Evans pile in, and most of Vigilante Force comes away with heavy damage.","tags":["dave-mayberry","robert-chipman","george-rincon","shawn-mcdonald","earl-evans","albert-anderson","chandler-paul","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4525,"title":"Player Steals Stage 1","summary":"Andrew Player runs down Jeremiah Burke off turns one and two and makes the pass just before the line to win the opening stage at the halfway break.","tags":["andrew-player","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5155,"title":"David Kelly Goes to Space","summary":"David L. Kelly gets launched 'to the moon' in a spectacular flying wreck — the booth declares the 49 'in need of a hearse' and christens him 'David the Astronaut Kelly.'","tags":[],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5450,"title":"It's a Big One","summary":"Jonathan Osborne gets loose on his own into the inside wall and the field piles in behind — Rincon, Mayberry, Dixon and Hughes all collected in the night's Big One.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","dave-mayberry","jack-dixon","connor-hughes"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6717,"title":"Restart Stack-Up Pummels Eaton","summary":"The outside lane checks up on a restart and Dustyn Eaton gets absolutely pummeled with nowhere to go; Osborne is sandwiched between trucks and Trevor Robertson gets smashed up in the chain reaction.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7170,"title":"Chan the Man: Bulldoze It, Build a Walmart","summary":"After his 'spectacular flip,' Chandler Paul tells the booth Phoenix should be bulldozed with a Walmart put on it, admitting 'I'm running out of talent tonight.'","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":7901,"title":"One-Shot Green-White-Checker","summary":"A late caution sets up a single-attempt green-white-checker with Burke and Hollingsworth on the front row — 'strap on those drinking helmets, throw inhibition out the window.'","tags":["jeremiah-burke","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7938,"title":"Hollingsworth Wins It Door-to-Door","summary":"Door-to-door, bumper-to-bumper, mirror-to-mirror on the final lap — Jeremiah Burke gets shoved up into the wall off turn four and rookie J.R. Hollingsworth takes his first VRL win in what Burke calls maybe the tightest non-restricted finish the league has had.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":636,"quote":"It's gonna be a long one folks, so buckle on in there, get your drinking helmets ready as we're gonna get ready to launch this Starship to outer space.","context":"Alan Brown's broadcast open for Phoenix","gold":3},{"t":1536,"quote":"It did more flips than Ricky Bobby out there — hopefully he doesn't come out of the truck thinking he's on fire.","context":"Pole sitter Alan Vaught barrel-rolls on the opening lap","gold":5},{"t":1940,"quote":"I know math up to my fives, but that's about it. I know cursing in Spanish up to the NC-17 level, which we're not going to do here tonight.","context":"The booth argues over which turn is which on the Phoenix dogleg","gold":3},{"t":2455,"quote":"Brayton Laster's nickname is the pizza man. Why? Because he delivers.","context":"Booth fact-checks the real-life ARCA driver's Wikipedia page mid-race","gold":4},{"t":4108,"quote":"Dave the nickname Mayberry goes around — oh, we got ourselves a parking lot!","context":"The lap-63 restart pileup on the front stretch","gold":4},{"t":5166,"quote":"The 49 is in need of a hearse, because there's no way anyone could live through that. Rest in peace, David L Kelly. I mean, it's virtual — that's the good part.","context":"David L. Kelly's truck goes flying 'to the moon'","gold":5},{"t":6426,"quote":"And uh, breaking iRacing news: Greg Klein is already in his PJs.","context":"Klein disconnects after a rough night and joins the YouTube chat","gold":4},{"t":7387,"quote":"The 751 shuts the door — that's not even a door shut, that's a door slam, right in front of that 33.","context":"Mike Adamson slams the door on Alan Vaught in the closing laps","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names heavily; several proper names are best guesses. 'Robert Chipman' is also captioned 'Shipman' (surname uncertain). 'Dustin Riehle' (#37) is a best guess for the caption 'Dustin really.' 'David Feit' (#1) and 'Eric Klafka' (#11, captioned 'clapka') spellings are uncertain. Brayton Laster's first name alternates Brighton/Braden/Brayton in captions — booth confirms he is a real-life ARCA driver. Andrew Kauth (captioned 'Andrew coffin') had connection problems, barely ran, and was classified last (36th). Race admin Lori and Jess run the league; Lori did not race. Event: NASCAR Trucks at Phoenix, 150 laps with a stage break after lap 75, 37 trucks registered / 32 still running late, one fast repair per truck, decided on a one-attempt green-white-checker. Full finishing order read from 2:31:01 in the broadcast.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Nz-bCM_hPrI":{"recap":"The first of the VRL Premiere Truck Series' final three championship races brought 29 trucks to Pocono Raceway for 80 laps, and the Tricky Triangle delivered what the booth called the most chaotic VRL Pocono race they could remember — roughly ten cautions, starting with a lag-induced pileup before the field even reached the green flag. Mike Adamson was the truck to beat all night, repeatedly slicing back to the front, until contact off turn two sent him up the wall and nearly over with under 20 laps to go. Attrition also claimed Dustyn Eaton, Gordon Spain, Russ Kilgore, Kelly Gill, Greg Cline, and broadcast-family driver Kyle Voight, who went head-on into the pit-entry tire barrier. It all came down to DSR teammates on the last lap: Scott Ronnie nailed the tunnel turn, dove inside, and side-drafted to the stripe, but Craig Goodenough held on to win by 0.001 seconds. Ronnie settled for second ahead of Dave Mayberry — up 17 spots — as DSR went 1-2-3 with a fourth truck in sixth.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Scott Rooney","Dave Mayberry"],"moments":[{"t":1896,"title":"Pileup before the green","summary":"Greg Cline blinked out (connection lag) right as the field launched, stacking up Andy Player, Albert Anderson, Russ Kilgore, and Greg Dobson before the leaders even crossed the start line — caution on lap one.","tags":["greg-cline","andrew-player","albert-anderson","russ-kilgore","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3079,"title":"Osborne drives it with his mouth","summary":"The booth spotlights Jonathan Osborne running near the front using a mouth-operated control rig for steering, gas, and brake — \"this is remarkable.\"","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3150,"title":"Lap-21 chain reaction claims Eaton","summary":"The lapped #12 bounced off the wall out of turn three, Jack Dixon spun with heavy rear damage, and Dustyn Eaton went nose-first into the inside pit wall, ending his night.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3275,"title":"Ghosted in the pits — except not","summary":"Kevin Hunt drove straight into Andrew Coffin's truck sticking out of its pit box — iRacing didn't ghost it — sparking a booth rant about half-ghosted pit lanes: \"That's kind of weak.\"","tags":["kevin-hunt","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3862,"title":"Kilgore's throttle-on tunnel turn save","summary":"Russ Kilgore got loose three-wide in the tunnel turn, kept his foot in the gas, and drove through the spin with barely any damage — \"the wall actually straightened me out.\"","tags":["russ-kilgore","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4312,"title":"Spain flips as Kilgore's night ends","summary":"Dave Mayberry's loose moment flipped Gordon Spain's #38 and blew the engine in a puff of smoke, while in the same sequence Russ Kilgore was tipped into the wall by the 74 and out of the race.","tags":["gordon-spain","dave-mayberry","russ-kilgore","michael-brooks"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4787,"title":"Kyle Voight into the tire barrier","summary":"Mayberry clipped the wall shooting a gap, the chain reaction ripped the rear end off Kyle Voight's #16 Shokker Grafix truck, and the broadcasters' own son speared head-on into the pit-entry tire barrier — \"a neck breaker\" — done for the night.","tags":["dave-mayberry","john-gallagher","michael-brooks","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5732,"title":"Dirty air wrecks Pope and Dixon","summary":"Tim Pope lost the nose in dirty air mid-tunnel-turn and spun after charging from the rear all night; Cup contender Jack Dixon had nowhere to go and destroyed his truck on the inside wall trying to miss him.","tags":["timothy-pope","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6179,"title":"The truck to beat sees the sky","summary":"Race-long dominator Mike Adamson got clipped off turn two, rode up the wall and nearly flipped — \"he sees the sky\" — ending his shot at the win; even winner Goodenough later apologized on air.","tags":["mike-adamson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6605,"title":"Goans' active-driving save","summary":"In a three-wide scramble John McAdam banged doors and saved it, while Chris Goans — shot sideways toward the inside wall — braked, released, and steered to protect his engine compartment in what the booth called active driving.","tags":["chris-goans","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":8023,"title":"0.001 at the line","summary":"DSR teammates drag-raced to the flag — Scott Ronnie nailed the tunnel turn, dove inside Craig Goodenough, and side-drafted to the stripe, but Goodenough won by 0.001 seconds while Dave Mayberry held off Jacob Alesia for third.","tags":["craig-goodenough","scott-rooney","dave-mayberry","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8056,"title":"Ronnie celebrates second place","summary":"Scott Ronnie's onboard camera caught him celebrating like a winner at the line — his overlay apparently told him he'd won — until turn one, when he realized he'd lost by a thousandth. The booth crowned it the best onboard reaction they'd ever aired.","tags":["scott-rooney","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3557,"quote":"Break out the Crisco oil, put it on the bumper. This is the race right now.","context":"four trucks nose-to-tail battling for second","gold":3},{"t":3856,"quote":"He came here to kick ass and chew bubble gum, and he's almost all out of bubble gum.","context":"Alan on Kyle Voight's onboard gum-chewing","gold":4},{"t":4050,"quote":"Three wide through the tunnel turn is not recommended, by the way.","context":"Russ Kilgore, fresh off his throttle-on spin save","gold":4},{"t":5731,"quote":"He thought you were like, man, that guy is cool on the other side of the pillow.","context":"Alan's camera pan fooled Ricky into thinking Player was calmly crashing","gold":3},{"t":7750,"quote":"Not so much when you're iPacing versus iRacing.","context":"Ricky on drivers wearing out riding around under endless cautions","gold":3},{"t":8046,"quote":"Side draft! Side draft! Side draft!","context":"the final-corner call as Ronnie lunged for the win","gold":5},{"t":8365,"quote":"I told him I'd wreck my grandma to win, so he was going to have to push it.","context":"winner Craig Goodenough on racing his teammate to the line","gold":5},{"t":9027,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, and above all else, stay vigilante.","context":"Alan's signature sign-off","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions frequently substituted real NASCAR driver names (Kyle Busch, Kyle Weatherman, Tyler Reddick, William Byron, Greg Biffle, Chris Buescher, Justin Allgaier, Rhodes, Hill) for league drivers; those were mapped back to VRL drivers where the context made it clear and otherwise ignored. The #16 driver captioned as Bott/Vaught/Boat is best-guessed as Kyle Voight — he calls broadcaster Alan Voight 'Pop' and Lori is his mom; Ricky's Shokker Grafix sponsors his truck. 'Scott Ronnie' spelling is uncertain (Ronnie/Ronny/Rohny/Rohrer in captions), as is 'John Scheinbarker' (#12; many wildly different caption variants). 'Jacob Alesia' and 'Chris Gomes' spellings are also caption best-guesses. The round number is stated as both 'round 14' and 'round 16'; it is clearly the first of the final three races (Pocono, then Naval Base Coronado, then the Charlotte finale). Caution count: announcer flagged the 10th caution on air and post-race said '10 cautions... maybe 11.' Margin of victory stated on air as 0.001s. Lori Voight managed the event from production but was not an on-air commentator; a Phoenix driver identified only as 'Deion' sat out with a migraine. Qualifying's 'Brett Klinger seventh' is most likely a garble of Greg Cline, who otherwise doesn't appear in the qualifying rundown.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"oDQfsoLotyQ":{"recap":"Championship Wednesday at Homestead-Miami closed the VRL season winner-take-all: the highest finisher among the final four of Trevor Robertson, Alan Vaught, Mike Adamson, and Jeremiah Burke would be crowned champion. The 100-lap truck race ran green from flag to flag — the scheduled lap-50 break was the night's only caution — as polesitter Tim Pope, Robertson, and Vaught traded the lead through the pit cycles and Vaught's cold-tire bobble on the second-half restart cost him track position he never fully recovered. The title fight broke open late when contact from Burke sent Adamson's 88 hard into the outside wall with suspension damage, ending his bid and dropping him to 21st, four laps down. Robertson blew past Pope in the closing laps and brought the Gorilla Glue 64 home for the race win and his first VRL championship, with Pope second, Vaught third, and Burke fourth.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1306,"title":"Green flag: Vaught splits them three-wide","summary":"The championship race goes green with polesitter Tim Pope leading them down, and Alan Vaught immediately drives three-wide through the middle of Burke and Anderson to start his charge.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1351,"title":"Meatball flag for Dobson","summary":"Greg Dobson loses it when he hits the gas, draws the meatball flag and sits through eight minutes of repairs — an early engine failure that buries his night before it starts.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2469,"title":"Vaught cycles into the lead","summary":"Alan Vaught times the first green-flag pit cycle perfectly and a lightning-quick stop hands the 33 the race lead, while long-runner Tim Pope pays for staying out too long.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3192,"title":"Mid-race chat with the Scarecrow 55","summary":"In-race interview with Ricky Whittenburg, the league's painter, on riding the high line in the Scarecrow 55, hoping for a caution, and out-strategizing the faster trucks.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3366,"title":"Restart chaos on cold tires","summary":"The second-half restart turns into a slip-and-slide on cold tires — Alan Vaught bobbles in turns one and two and loses positions he later admits may have cost him a shot at the win.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4013,"title":"Dixon's night ends on pit road","summary":"Jack Dixon takes two sets of tires, screeches to a halt leaving his box and gets towed back — later chalked up to packet loss and a disconnection.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4351,"title":"Championship contact: Burke puts Adamson in the wall","summary":"Jeremiah Burke closes on Mike Adamson's older-tire gamble and contact sends the 88 hard into the outside wall with suspension damage — Adamson burns his fast repair and his title hopes are done.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4446,"title":"The Great Metric System Debate","summary":"The booth erupts into a running war over the metric system versus 'Freedom Units' — beer measured in milliliters, ammunition calibers, and Adam Turner told to shove the metric system back to Europe.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4582,"title":"Chudzilla saves it sideways","summary":"Contact with Mayberry's 29 gets Josh Bittner's 84 Chudzilla machine fully sideways, and he somehow snags an unbelievable save to keep it off the wall.","tags":["josh-bittner","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4658,"title":"Robertson flies by Pope for the lead","summary":"Trevor Robertson sees an opening on the 27 of Tim Pope and blows right on by to take the lead — the pass that wins the race and the championship.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4790,"title":"Adamson hunts down Burke","summary":"Back out on fresh tires, Adamson runs down the man who put him in the wall and slices side-by-side with Burke in the closing laps — tense stuff, but it stays clean.","tags":["mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4884,"title":"Robertson wins it all at Homestead","summary":"White flag to checkers: Trevor Robertson brings the Gorilla Glue 64 home ahead of Pope and Vaught to take the race win and his first VRL championship, capping a flag-to-flag title fight.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2095,"quote":"There's this young man named Jonathan Osborne — can drive the hell out of a race truck with his mouth on iRacing. They need to build him a seat and custom controls.","context":"Adam Turner campaigning for NASCAR to notice Osborne, who races using his mouth","gold":4},{"t":3063,"quote":"They're shooting dice in Waco tonight — somebody's gonna have a 22 in their boot, somebody might have a 38 in a truck, see who can get to it first.","context":"The booth on the winner-take-all championship format","gold":4},{"t":3295,"quote":"I'm usually not as fast, so if I pick up a win it's usually because I just got luckier — my right foot don't hit the pedal as loud as some of these other guys do.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg's mid-race interview on his strategy-first style","gold":4},{"t":3372,"quote":"Green flag is out and away we go — it is time to lug nut up and shut up, it's go time!","context":"Calling the restart for the final 45 laps of the championship","gold":5},{"t":4355,"quote":"Oh, makes contact with the 88! Hard into the outside wall... oh no, I think there goes one of our championship contenders here tonight.","context":"The call as Burke's contact wrecks Adamson out of title contention","gold":4},{"t":4529,"quote":"I've drank 1700 milliliters of beer so far... it sounds impressive... that's probably like three beers.","context":"Peak of the booth's metric system war","gold":4},{"t":4908,"quote":"The Gorilla Glue has stuck with him all season long and it's gonna stick with him even longer... picking up the win and the championship — Trevor Robertson, your season champion!","context":"The checkered-flag call as Robertson wins the race and the title","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Race control was Lori Vaught (wife of league owner Alan Vaught, who finished 3rd). Full 23-truck finishing order was read on air: Robertson, Pope, Vaught, Burke, Kuehl, Klein, Player, Mayberry, Bittner, Whittenburg, Osborne, Anderson, Coffin, Evans, Everidge, Eaton, D. Kelly, Rincon, Endicott, Taylor, Adamson, Dixon, Dobson. Caption ambiguities: #82 captioned both 'Mike everidge' and 'Mike Edwards' (Everidge is the best guess); 'Dustyn' inferred from the booth's 'Dustin with a Y'; Greg Dobson's number captioned as both '85' and '08.5'; 'Whittenburg' consistently auto-captioned 'Wittenberg'. Jack Dixon's retirement was attributed to packet loss / disconnection; Greg Dobson had an early engine failure (meatball flag, ~8 minutes of repairs). Announced for next season (starting the following week at Nashville): the season splits into two championships per NASCAR year, Kyle Vaught (Jess's son) joins the league, Robertson leaves the Good Wiser team to team up with painter Ricky Whittenburg, and Burke says Larry (and possibly Dylan — names garbled) join All-Star Racing. A league painter/driver called 'Chan the man' was in chat but not racing. League presented by Blue Fox Properties / Dave Mayberry.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"OfXXemo7Slo":{"recap":"The VRL rang in the New Year with the Hoosier 100 — 100 laps of Gen 4 madness on the flat, blistering 98-degree Indianapolis oval, with tire management billed as the key to the race. Polesitter Trevor Robertson dominated the bulk of the night, ripping off fastest laps in the low 51s, but two-time VRL champion Tim Pope saved his tires and drove past his Ain't Dead Yet teammate in the closing run to steal the win. Jess Vont charged from a mid-pack start and split the field three wide late to complete the podium in third. The night featured three cautions, headlined by a multi-car pileup that twice lifted John Curtis's 43 off the ground, a blown engine for Kyle Vont, and a last-lap scramble that saw Jonathan Osborne beat Mike Adamson to the line by hundredths of a second. Ricky Whittenburg started fifth but retired early with the flu, and Jeremiah Burke's top-five night died with a pit-road speeding black flag on the final stops.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Jess Vont"],"moments":[{"t":2108,"title":"Eaton backwards — caution number one","summary":"Osborne crawls along the outside wall, Dustyn Eaton loops it off the corner and backs into the wall, and Sean McDonnell has nowhere to go — the first caution of the night.","tags":["dustin-eaton","shawn-mcdonald","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2505,"title":"Smith doorstopped, wheels off the ground","summary":"Edward Smith checks up entering turn three and Nick Ramsey's doorstop nose gets underneath him, lifting the 63's rear wheels a foot and a half off the ground before he backs into the outside wall.","tags":["edward-w-smith","nick-ramsey"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2922,"title":"The 43 gets lifted up — twice","summary":"John Curtis gets loose off contact with Mike Everage, gets doorstopped airborne twice in quick succession, and collects Dave Mayberry and Jacob Young in the night's biggest pileup — 'the Mayhem ensued.'","tags":["john-curtis","mike-everage","dave-mayberry","jacob-young"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4934,"title":"Jack the Ripper spun into the wall","summary":"Mike Everage mistimes his braking and gets underneath Jack Dixon's 07, spinning him around into the outside wall to bring out the yellow just past halfway.","tags":["jack-dixon","mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5754,"title":"Kyle Vont's engine lets go","summary":"Chaos on the backstretch — Jacob Young and Jonathan Osborne slap the wall, Osborne throws 'an old hockey body check' coming off it, and Kyle Vont's motor blows in the 16, ending his duel with Dave Mayberry.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jacob-young"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5901,"title":"The Bumper Car Mafia","summary":"The booth spins a yarn about Greg Klein founding a 'Bumper Car Mafia' on cruise ships — a fellowship band that teams up on blue-haired ladies and sends them into the ocean.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5958,"title":"Smith torpedoed — the Grey Poupon caution","summary":"Josh Bittner clips Edward Smith's rear quarter panel and sends him around, spinning Andrew Coffin too; the booth swears the two cars were side by side so long they were trading Grey Poupon through the window nets.","tags":["edward-w-smith","josh-bittner","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6898,"title":"Burke black-flagged on the money stop","summary":"Jeremiah Burke locks it up speeding into the pits on the final round of stops and earns a black flag, with Greg Dobson flagged right behind him — Burke tumbles from a top-five night to 21st.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7147,"title":"Chachi's fuel gamble puts the 81 out front","summary":"Jonathan Osborne stays out on a fuel gamble and leads the Hoosier 100 late — 'a race against old man time' — before finally surrendering to pit road with about eight laps to go.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7363,"title":"Vont splits them three wide for the podium","summary":"Jess Vont drives the 33 straight up through the middle, takes it three wide, and steals the third-place spot with about five laps to go, then holds off Dustyn Eaton to the flag.","tags":["dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7455,"title":"Four wide at Indy","summary":"The giant fight for a top-ten finish fans out three wide, then four wide, through turns three and four — the first four-wide of the night at a track where the booth didn't think it was possible.","tags":["nick-ramsey","jack-dixon","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7631,"title":"Pope steals one from his teammate","summary":"Tires saved, two-time champ Tim Pope holds off polesitter Trevor Robertson over the final run to win the Hoosier 100, while a last-lap wreck collects Smith, Everage, and Chandler Paul and Jonathan Osborne drag-races Mike Adamson to the line by hundredths.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3413,"quote":"A man who's confident enough to run the Barbie car.","context":"Jeremiah Burke charging forward in the pink 53","gold":3},{"t":3947,"quote":"They're going to be doing 300 miles an hour, man. Be a bunch of death and mayhem — which I'm all for.","context":"previewing the Gen 4 cars heading to the superspeedways next","gold":4},{"t":5782,"quote":"The 81 was trying to come off of the outside wall and gives some old hockey body check.","context":"Osborne bounces off the wall into Kyle Vont during the backstretch chaos","gold":3},{"t":5885,"quote":"Of course Greg will in fact wreck his grandmother to try to pick up a win. He may have done this — I'm sure he has.","context":"after Greg Klein gets involved in three-wide contact","gold":5},{"t":5973,"quote":"I thought those two drivers were sharing a conversation or trading some Grey Poupon or something — they were side by side for that long.","context":"the 63 and 84 ran door to door forever before wrecking","gold":4},{"t":6775,"quote":"If you got four, put four on. Your car has four tires for a reason — going to use them all.","context":"Adam Turner's anti-two-tire-strategy rant during late pit stops","gold":4},{"t":7739,"quote":"Pope just put on a clinic out there again tonight, boys. He just slow played the whole race, didn't he?","context":"the booth right after Pope takes the checkered flag","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race control was 'Lorie vot' (Lori, Jess's wife) — likely Lorie Vont. The surname shared by the 33 and 16 (and race control) is heavily garbled across captions (vot/vont/Vault/fought/bot); 'Vont' is a best guess. 'David Feit' (#1), 'George Ranone' (#28), 'Mike Everage' (#82), and 'Josh Bitner' (#84) spellings are also uncertain. Albert Anderson, Edson Ochoa, and Earl Evans are league regulars mentioned on air but not in tonight's field. League founder shout-out captioned as 'Justin Lori'. Full finishing order is read starting at 2:23:29 (8609s); winner and podium confirmed by post-race interviews with Scott Howell, Jess Vont, Trevor Robertson, and Tim Pope.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"PhE_uMLRhko":{"recap":"Josh Bittner converted a front-row start into a hometown victory in Season 6's fifth round at Pocono, beating teammate and polesitter Tim Pope by just five hundredths of a second. Bittner won the lap-40 stage after an early green-flag stop cycled him ahead of Pope, then regained control through the final pit sequence as Pope charged back on fresher tires. Mike Adamson climbed from 31st to third, passing Trevor Robertson with two laps remaining to complete a 28-position hard-charger run. Apart from the scheduled stage break, the only caution followed Dave Mayberry's opening-lap spin, leaving strategy and traffic to decide a remarkably clean race.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Tim Pope","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1407,"title":"Bittner wins the launch","summary":"Polesitter Tim Pope starts alongside hometown favorite Josh Bittner, but Bittner clears him through Turn 1 and leads the opening lap.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1463,"title":"Mayberry spins on lap one","summary":"Dave Mayberry checks up low and receives a light tap from Jack Dixon, spinning without hitting anything and producing the race's lone organic caution.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":2040,"title":"Pope retakes the lead","summary":"After the restart, Pope works back around Bittner while Trevor Robertson keeps the Ain't Dead Yet teammates locked into the top three.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2689,"title":"Bittner short-pits the first run","summary":"Bittner stops around lap 20, five laps before Pope, and uses the tire advantage to cycle back to the lead with roughly three seconds in hand.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2986,"title":"Pit-road penalty hurts Vaught","summary":"Alan Vaught receives a black flag during the first green-flag pit cycle; the scheduled stage caution keeps him on the lead lap, but he spends the rest of the race trying to recover.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":3833,"title":"Bittner secures the stage","summary":"Pope closes onto Bittner's bumper on older tires, but cannot complete the pass before Bittner claims the lap-40 stage and its 10 bonus points.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4308,"title":"Pope grabs the lead again","summary":"During the long second-half run, Pope squeezes past Bittner as the two teammates continue to set the pace.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5123,"title":"Bryant turns a scare into a stop","summary":"Contact sends Dillon Bryant sliding toward the outside wall, but he gathers the truck and dives into pit road without a penalty to make his final service.","tags":["dylan-bryant","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":5617,"title":"Pope charges on fresh tires","summary":"After the final pit cycle leaves Bittner in control, Pope repeatedly sets the fastest lap while carving back through traffic toward the leader.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6183,"title":"Adamson takes the podium spot","summary":"With two laps left, Adamson passes Robertson for third after advancing from the 31st starting position.","tags":["mike-adamson","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6263,"title":"Bittner holds off the crossover","summary":"Pope gets a run out of the final corner and crosses behind Bittner, but the hometown favorite reaches the line 0.05 seconds ahead; Adamson finishes third.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6263,"quote":"Will the 27 machine get a run? Yes, he does, breaking to the outside, but it won't be in time. The 84 machine hangs on to pick up the race win.","context":"The booth calls Bittner and Pope's drag race to the checkered flag","gold":5},{"t":6463,"quote":"I prefer not to have the lucky draw. I'd rather just get a podium, but I love talking with y'all.","context":"Sixth-place finisher Dillon Bryant jokes about being selected for the random interview","gold":4},{"t":6659,"quote":"I felt like I won that thing coming from the back. I mean, granted I only got a third-place finish out of it, but hey, I'll take it.","context":"Mike Adamson reflects on gaining 28 positions","gold":5},{"t":6892,"quote":"He over-drove the last third big time. I almost got him.","context":"Tim Pope explains how close he came to beating Bittner","gold":4},{"t":6960,"quote":"There were no bribes, no team orders. I don't even run the team.","context":"Josh Bittner denies that his teammate was instructed to let him win","gold":5},{"t":7038,"quote":"The drivers really toned it back and put on what seemed to be a pretty decent show, especially up front.","context":"Bittner praises the field's restraint after a much wilder practice race","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The broadcast lists 32 entries, but Jonah Long did not grid because of technical issues, so the drivers array contains the 31 starters. The booth calls the event a one-caution race while also describing the scheduled lap-40 stage break; this is treated as one organic caution plus the planned stage yellow. Several caption spellings are heavily garbled, including Josh Buettner for Josh Bittner and David Feit for David Feit; canonical names follow the roster and overrides. The final order's 20th-place name is garbled as 'the pizza man,' but the grid and repeated race references identify that driver as Brayton Laster.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Pk7OKqHlu1Y":{"recap":"Albert Anderson's Talladega night went from pole position to upside down and back to victory lane. The opening Big One rolled the sponsored No. 99, forcing Anderson to repair the truck and rebuild a race that could have ended almost immediately. Two more cautions, green-flag pit cycles, penalties and a late collision steadily thinned the lead group, but Anderson worked his way back into position for the final drafting fight. The last lap became a contest between coordinated pairs: Anderson and Kelly Kuehl on one lane against Dustyn Eaton and John Curtis on the other. Kuehl stayed attached to Anderson's bumper through the run to the stripe, and Anderson won the drag race by 0.03 seconds over Eaton, with Kuehl third. In the winner interview Anderson explicitly credits Kuehl's push. The result is best understood as a recovery and teamwork story—repairing a rolled truck, surviving the strategy reshuffles, and building the right two-truck partnership when Talladega finally demanded one.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Dustyn Eaton","Kelly Kuehl"],"moments":[{"t":1415,"title":"Anderson leads the field to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Albert Anderson launches the 34-car field at the start of the 94-lap Talladega race.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1502,"title":"Vaught takes the early lead","summary":"Alan Vaught works past Anderson to take command during the opening side-by-side run.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":1723,"title":"Anderson tumbles in the first big one","summary":"A checkup ahead catches Nick Ramsey out, sending Anderson tumbling and collecting at least eight or nine cars; Anderson repairs the sponsored No. 99 and remains in the race.","tags":["albert-anderson","nick-ramsey","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3428,"title":"First green-flag pit cycle begins","summary":"The first scheduled stops begin under green, and Osborne enters too fast while a later pack led by Dustin Riehle completes its stop without producing a caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":3768,"title":"Eaton and Vaught trigger the second caution","summary":"As Vaught changes lanes around Eaton, light contact or disturbed air sends both cars spinning and Vaught through the infield, bringing out the second yellow.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":4384,"title":"Multi-car crash brings another yellow","summary":"Contact involving Anderson and Andrew Player starts a stack-up in the main pack, while an Earl Evans and Edward Smith incident is identified as the action that produces the caution.","tags":["albert-anderson","andrew-player","george-rincon","kyle-vaught","earl-evans","edward-w-smith"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5650,"title":"Pope is collected while the race stays green","summary":"Jacob Young tags Earl Evans, who slides back up the track and drives Tim Pope into the outside wall; Pope reaches pit road with severe right-front damage.","tags":["jacob-young","earl-evans","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6159,"title":"Final green-flag stop scrambles contenders","summary":"Dave Mayberry leads a large group onto pit road and Vaught gets sideways during the entry, reshuffling the lead pack for the closing sprint.","tags":["dave-mayberry","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":6226,"title":"Pit-road penalties thin the lead battle","summary":"Andrew Player, Nick Ramsey and Greg Dobson receive black flags during the final cycle, with Mike Adamson also serving a pit-road penalty shortly afterward.","tags":["andrew-player","nick-ramsey","greg-dobson","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":6560,"title":"Two drafting pairs form for the finish","summary":"With four laps left, Kuehl pushes Anderson while Curtis works behind Eaton, setting up a two-lane contest at the front.","tags":["albert-anderson","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","john-curtis"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6685,"title":"White flag launches the final drag race","summary":"Anderson and Kuehl hold the outside as Eaton and Curtis surge alongside, while Mayberry and Trevor Robertson search for an opening behind them.","tags":["albert-anderson","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","john-curtis","dave-mayberry","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":6734,"title":"Anderson wins by three hundredths","summary":"Anderson beats Eaton to the stripe by 0.03 seconds after a clean side-by-side finish, with Kuehl taking the final podium position.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-eaton","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6734,"quote":"It's going to be the Great American drag race down across the line, and it's going to be America's driver winning that drag race!","context":"The live call as Anderson defeats Eaton at the stripe.","gold":5},{"t":6914,"quote":"Talladega is a crapshoot, you know. I'd take it.","context":"Jorge Rincon accepts his top-10 result after a turbulent race.","gold":2},{"t":7029,"quote":"Teamwork makes the dream work, right?","context":"Kuehl summarizes the cooperation that carried Anderson to the win and Kuehl to third.","gold":5},{"t":7118,"quote":"If somebody checks up in front of the guy you're pushing, it's going to be a disaster.","context":"Kuehl explains the danger of sustained pushing in the Gen 4 car.","gold":5},{"t":7351,"quote":"You've got to get that subtle tap and kind of push before you can gun it.","context":"Runner-up Eaton describes the technique required to draft safely.","gold":5},{"t":7499,"quote":"I got this win because Kelly was behind me pushing me.","context":"Anderson credits Kuehl for the decisive final-lap push.","gold":5},{"t":7569,"quote":"I wanted to start on the pole, I wanted to win, and really make a big statement for One Eight Coffee.","context":"Anderson reflects on delivering a pole-to-win result for the race sponsor.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish call, podium interviews and results discussion explicitly confirm Anderson, Eaton and Kuehl as the podium, with a stated 0.03-second margin from first to second. The race had three cautions: the opening multi-car crash, the Eaton-Vaught incident and the later multi-car crash associated with the Evans-Smith contact. Anderson recovered from tumbling in the first crash to win from the pole. The spoken grid identifies 34 racers; Lori Vaught is named as race control and is not included as a participant. The caption occasionally renders Andrew Coffin as Andrew C/Cin; he remains distinct from Andrew Player.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"pK8_KdRnJIc":{"recap":"Dustyn Eaton started from pole and immediately took command at Watkins Glen, while Sean McDonnell's Turn 1 mistake removed one of the quickest qualifiers from contention on the opening lap. Riehle stretched his advantage to roughly eleven seconds and claimed the first stage before the scheduled lap-22 caution reset the field. Alan Vaught challenged from the front row on the restart, but Riehle cleared him, controlled the final green-flag pit cycle, and pulled away as Jorge Rincon climbed from tenth into the runner-up position. Riehle completed a sweep of both road-course stages and races in this two-week stretch, winning ahead of Rincon and Vaught after Vaught survived late contact from the lapped Chandler Paul.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Jorge Rincon","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1465,"title":"McDonnell crashes through Turn 1","summary":"Riehle leads the start, but third-place starter Sean McDonnell misses Turn 1, crosses the grass, and hits the wall head-on before towing for repairs.","tags":["dustin-eaton","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1637,"title":"Mayberry spins in the opening stint","summary":"Dave Mayberry runs wide and loops his truck in Turn 1, then quickly points it back in the proper direction as the field files past.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1744,"title":"Osborne loses it exiting the bus stop","summary":"Jonathan Osborne attacks the curbing while working forward from an end-of-line penalty and spins at the exit of the bus-stop chicane.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1791,"title":"Kyle Vaught's truck begins smoking","summary":"Kyle Vaught spins beyond the bus stop and emerges with a heavily smoking truck, forcing him to stay clear of traffic while limping toward pit road.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2132,"title":"Fite spins at pit entry","summary":"David Feit gets loose while fighting Tim Pope, hits the inside, and crosses the pit commitment line; the mishap and resulting penalty knock a strong top-five run off course.","tags":["david-fite","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2817,"title":"Chandler Paul hits the carousel guardrail","summary":"Chandler Paul catches the curb exiting the carousel, snaps loose, and strikes the guardrail hard enough to tear much of the front bodywork from his truck.","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3180,"title":"Riehle completes a dominant first stage","summary":"After leading by nearly eleven seconds, Riehle takes the scheduled stage at the completion of lap 22 ahead of Vaught, Mike Adamson, Rincon, and Greg Klein.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught","mike-adamson","george-rincon","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3646,"title":"Riehle clears Vaught on the restart","summary":"Riehle and Vaught restart side by side, but the No. 14 breaks clear after Turn 1 while the field funnels back into single file through the esses.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3771,"title":"Burke's bus-stop error collects Klein","summary":"Jeremiah Burke clips the inside wall entering the bus stop and spins sideways into Greg Klein, sending Klein tumbling down the running order.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4312,"title":"Everage ricochets across the bus stop","summary":"Michael Everage loses his turn-in point behind Andrew Coffin, clips the inside barrier, and rebounds across the racing line into Mike Darland's path.","tags":["mike-everage","andrew-cauthan","mike-darland"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4990,"title":"Vaught saves third after late contact","summary":"Lapped Chandler Paul locks the brakes behind Vaught and bumps him into the grass with two laps left, but Vaught keeps the truck straight and retains third.","tags":["chandler-paul","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":5095,"title":"Riehle seals a second straight road-course win","summary":"Riehle crosses the line unchallenged for his second consecutive victory, while Rincon withstands Vaught's final attempt to secure second place.","tags":["dustin-eaton","george-rincon","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1169,"quote":"Twenty-seven drivers, and looking at these qualifying times, the top five are separated by two tenths.","context":"The booth previews a deep and tightly matched Watkins Glen field","gold":4},{"t":2348,"quote":"That would be a heck of a story—three wins in two races, with a possibility of going four for four here at these road courses.","context":"Riehle begins turning his two-week road-course stretch into a sweep","gold":4},{"t":3225,"quote":"Now you've got your free opportunity to pit if you've got problems. This is the time to get them fixed.","context":"The scheduled stage caution gives the field a reset","gold":3},{"t":4042,"quote":"He had one hand on the wheel and he was looking down at his phone texting somebody.","context":"The booth jokes about how comfortable Riehle looks while dominating","gold":4},{"t":4820,"quote":"The guy races with a mouth controller with no force feedback.","context":"The broadcasters recognize Jonathan Osborne's climb from 25th to fourth","gold":5},{"t":5493,"quote":"I'm the first loser, that's what I can tell you. I'm the first loser, but it is what it is.","context":"Runner-up Jorge Rincon gives a dry assessment of second place","gold":5},{"t":5707,"quote":"I don't know how you slide your tires so much and you're able to still turn those laps.","context":"Alan Vaught describes watching Riehle after the stage restart","gold":5},{"t":5979,"quote":"I'm sliding everywhere, and I'm holding on to it for dear life, that's for sure.","context":"Winner Dustyn Eaton explains that the dominant run felt less comfortable from the cockpit","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 6, Round 9 at Watkins Glen according to seasons_map.json. The race used the short layout without the Boot, a scheduled stage caution after lap 22, local cautions otherwise, 60% fuel, unlimited tires, and one fast repair. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Riehle-Rincon-Vaught podium and reads the full 27-driver finishing order. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for the driver repeatedly captioned and called 'Dustyn Eaton' or 'Dustin with a Y.' Transcript timestamps end within the 6,835-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ptvLNVyayJI":{"recap":"The Fall Brawl exhibition brought VRL's old guard and a wave of new blood together at Michigan for a 250-mile, 125-lap money race with a massive 37-truck field. The night dissolved into carnage — the booth counted 20 cautions, headlined by a roughly 15-truck stage-three pileup — and the race came within minutes of becoming the first in VRL history to hit the iRacing session time limit. Mike Adamson and Andrew Player took stage-one honors before Jeremiah Burke charged from the back on worn tires to claim stages two and three, only to blow an engine in a three-wide battle for the lead. Tim Pope seized the lead with three laps to go and blocked Kelly Kuehl all the way to the line on a green-white-checker to win the Fall Brawl, while Jonah Long slammed the wall from third on the final lap. Kuehl settled for second with rookie Dustin Wade third as top newcomer, one week ahead of the Season 3 opener at Daytona.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Kelly Kuehl","Dustin Wade"],"moments":[{"t":1360,"title":"Green flag on the Fall Brawl","summary":"A 37-truck field — old school vs. the new guard — takes the green at Michigan with Kelly Kuehl and Jeremiah Burke on the front row.","tags":["kelly-keel","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1966,"title":"Kuehl and Gallagher's miracle save","summary":"Contact between the 01 and the 123 nearly wipes out the lead pack, but both drivers somehow gather it back up — the booth asks how that wasn't a huge wreck.","tags":["kelly-keel","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2360,"title":"Kuehl spun at the stage-one flag","summary":"Jonah Long hooks Kelly Kuehl's bumper right as stage one ends; Kuehl spins down to the apron while Mike Adamson and Andrew Player collect the stage money.","tags":["kelly-keel","jonah-long","mike-adamson","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3830,"title":"The wreck that kept on wrecking","summary":"Dustin Riehle gets turned racing three wide late in stage two, the 48 of Jack Dixon spins, and Ricky Whittenburg slams the outside wall hard in a slow-motion multi-truck melee.","tags":["dustin-reilly","jack-dixon","ricky-whittenburg","matt-beamer"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4133,"title":"Oxendine hooked out of a stage win","summary":"Leading the stage-two shootout, Josh Oxendine gets his quarter panel clipped by the 99 and goes for a wild ride; the stage is awarded to Jeremiah Burke and Andrew Player and the chat cries robbery.","tags":["josh-oxendine","chris-zofeld","jeremiah-burke","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4465,"title":"The Big One: 15 trucks in a fight-night pileup","summary":"The 99 bounces off the wall and back into traffic at the stage-three start, collecting roughly 15 trucks — netcode takes part of the blame as the booth compares it to a hockey fight night.","tags":["chris-zofeld","earl-evans","andrew-cauthan","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5942,"title":"Burke doubles up on stage wins","summary":"After deliberately riding the back to save tires, Jeremiah Burke charges through the field to sweep stages two and three for the old guard, with rookie Dustin Wade taking new-blood honors in stage three.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7815,"title":"Three-wide lead battle detonates","summary":"Burke, Todd Smith and Jonah Long go three wide for the lead; contact sends the 25 into the 753, blowing Burke's engine and leaving seven trucks with meatball flags as Whittenburg pinballs through the carnage.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","todd-smith","jonah-long","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":9019,"title":"Racing the session clock","summary":"With the caution count climbing toward 20, the booth realizes the race may hit the iRacing session time limit — something no VRL race has ever done.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":9300,"title":"Pope pounces with three to go","summary":"Tim Pope slides up past Kelly Kuehl to take the lead with three laps remaining, just as the booth predicted he'd sneak his way to the front.","tags":["timothy-pope","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":9585,"title":"Jonah Long's final-lap heartbreak","summary":"Running third on the white-flag lap, Jonah Long slams the wall hard — the booth calls for an ambulance — but the race stays green to the checkers.","tags":["jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":9605,"title":"Pope blocks Kuehl to the checkers","summary":"On the green-white-checker, Tim Pope throws blocks all the way down to the apron as Kelly Kuehl dives for the line; Pope wins the Fall Brawl with Kuehl second and rookie Dustin Wade third.","tags":["timothy-pope","kelly-keel","dustin-wade"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2535,"quote":"I guess you need cheaters to read bold type now, huh?","context":"razzing the booth after a misread of the caution-lap rule","gold":3},{"t":4595,"quote":"It's like one of those fight nights in hockey — everybody found a partner and got involved in it.","context":"calling the roughly 15-truck stage-three pileup","gold":4},{"t":6349,"quote":"You know, the only truck visible from space — of Ricky Whitmer.","context":"ribbing Whittenburg's neon surfer-themed paint scheme","gold":4},{"t":7690,"quote":"Stay away from that Greg Klein guy — he drives like crap, he'll spend his own grandma.","context":"throwing booth guest Greg Klein under the bus during a caution","gold":3},{"t":7833,"quote":"Ricky just lost another grill and radiator and water pump, gooseneck, power steering, pair of shorts — he needs some drawers.","context":"Whittenburg pinballed through the three-wide lead-battle wreck","gold":4},{"t":9525,"quote":"Time to buckle up, strap on that drink helmet, throw inhibition out the window — Timothy Pope takes the green flag.","context":"setting up the green-white-checker finish","gold":4},{"t":9591,"quote":"There goes Jonah Long — he got octopus crab by that wall, my goodness, we're gonna need a ambulance for him.","context":"final-lap wreck while Long ran third on the green-white-checker","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Exhibition (non-points) race — the 'Fall Brawl' at Michigan in NASCAR trucks, run as a Season 3 preseason warm-up with cash stage prizes; the points opener at Daytona was a week away. Full finishing order beyond the podium was not read out due to time. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Dustin really' (Riley?), 'David fight' (Fite?), Zofeld/Zofield/Sofeld, Sobanovsky, and Ricky Whittenburg is consistently captioned 'Wittenberg'. 'Craig' in captions is a garble of booth guest Greg Klein (a league driver filling in for Adam Turner, so listed under broadcasters). Chachi (81), Cody Tarrant, Adam Turner, Gary Gotzo, Cody Sanderson and Alan Vaught are league members mentioned but not racing tonight (Vaught ran race control). Booth is AAA Broadcasting ('Triple Eight broadcasting' in captions is a garble of Triple A). Meta chapter markers ('Matt Beamer', 'Stage Three') roughly track transcript content but are not interview markers.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"pvkx5-aiu88":{"recap":"Jeremiah Burke returned from a multi-week absence and dominated the 50-lap Boot race at Watkins Glen, leading virtually every lap outside the pit cycle. The only caution was the scheduled mid-race competition yellow, after which Alan Vaught emerged as Burke's closest challenger but could not match his long-run pace. Jonathan Osborne recovered from front-end damage and an aggressive final pit entry to hold off Mike Adamson for third. Burke finished roughly 14 seconds ahead of Vaught for his first win of the season, while Vaught's 11-position gain earned hard-charger honors.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Alan Vaught","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":2105,"title":"Burke wins the opening duel","summary":"Burke and pole-sitter Osborne run side by side through the opening corners before Burke holds the lead; behind them Jeff Snyder checks up John Ellis in the Esses.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","jeff-snyder","john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2218,"title":"Jordan is trapped by the guardrail","summary":"Robert Jordan sticks the No. 204 against an inside barrier and must tow, while Rob Green spins separately on the opening lap.","tags":["robert-jordan","rob-green"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3210,"title":"Burke stretches the lead","summary":"By lap 10 Burke is consistently faster than Osborne and builds a comfortable margin as early green-flag pit strategy begins behind him.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":2,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":4498,"title":"Burke leads by 18 seconds","summary":"The returning Burke asserts complete control before the competition break, opening an 18-second lead while the field manages traffic and the treacherous Boot.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":4970,"title":"Competition yellow catches Osborne pitting","summary":"The scheduled caution flies just as Osborne reaches pit road on lap 25, erasing Burke's huge advantage and regrouping the field for the only restart of the night.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":5595,"title":"Burke and Vaught restart side by side","summary":"Burke controls the second-half restart while Vaught, who started 13th after an EOL, emerges as the main threat and Osborne remains in the podium fight.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6773,"title":"Final pit cycle briefly hands Osborne the lead","summary":"Burke makes his last green-flag stop, allowing Osborne and Mike Adamson to race side by side through lap traffic before both make their own stops.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6932,"title":"Burke cycles back to the front","summary":"After Osborne and Adamson pit, Burke regains the lead with 12 laps remaining, Vaught second, and the battle for third still close.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7100,"title":"Ellis turns Ottinger without a caution","summary":"John Ellis catches Jeffrey Ottinger in the carousel and clips his rear corner, spinning Ottinger; both continue and exchange apologies while the race remains green.","tags":["john-ellis","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":8171,"title":"Burke seals a dominant return","summary":"Burke completes a clean final lap and wins by roughly 14 seconds over Vaught, with Osborne taking third ahead of Mike Adamson.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6907,"quote":"How's a driver supposed to open his backup beer when he's gotta turn right and shift all the time?","context":"A viewer captures the problem with a long caution-free road race.","gold":5},{"t":8165,"quote":"Here we go, final lap here at Watkins Glen, as what has been a grueling grind — basically an endurance race here.","context":"The booth introduces Burke's final lap.","gold":2},{"t":8542,"quote":"If you drive a truck length too deep into the corner, you're wrecked.","context":"Jonathan Osborne explains the concentration required over 50 laps.","gold":5},{"t":8632,"quote":"Not happy unless I'm winning.","context":"Runner-up Alan Vaught describes finishing second despite a clean, zero-off-track run.","gold":2},{"t":8952,"quote":"Once I got that lead, I was like, I just can't be denied. I don't want to throw this away.","context":"Burke recounts the mindset behind his dominant win.","gold":5},{"t":9039,"quote":"Every time my mind wandered, I'd be offline or something like that.","context":"Burke explains the mental strain of the long green-flag run.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews, and full rundown explicitly confirm Burke, Vaught, and Osborne. This was Season 2 Round 12, moved from Brands Hatch to the Watkins Glen Boot because the league could not find a suitable fixed setup for the trucks at Brands Hatch. The broadcast calls it a 19-truck field, but Lori Vaught appears in the grid overlay only as race admin; the spoken starting grid and final rundown identify 18 actual competitors. Burke is described as leading every lap except during green-flag pit cycling. Vaught started 13th after an EOL and finished second with zero off-tracks. Only 13 drivers were still classified as finishers for the random draw.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"q7PCr0DrUyU":{"recap":"Hooligan's Last Chance was not one conventional race result but five short Michigan stages for 17 non-winners, each paying $25 and one All-Star berth. Ricky Whittenburg survived a sustained three-wide fight and Kelly Kuehl's last-lap apron dive to claim the first ticket. Michael Everage then short-fueled the second segment, jumped the field on the restart, and held off Dustin Riehle and Jack Dixon. Stage 3 became a worn-tire duel between Kuehl and Eric Klafka: Kuehl crossed him over and nosed ahead at the white, but two loose moments opened the door for Klafka. Dixon drove a clean fourth segment and resisted Klafka's late charge for the next berth. The racing between those finishes was spectacularly unforgiving. A chain reaction sent Angelica Timmerman onto her roof and Rob Green upside down across the guardrail; Timmerman later stuck another roof-first landing; and a three-wide clash involving Klafka and Brian Jablonski created the final-stage pileup. Jorge Rincon reached the last segment after an earlier missed shift and engine trouble, then spent the closing laps absorbing Kuehl's pressure. When Kuehl dropped through the grass entering Turn 1 on the white-flag lap, Rincon stayed straight and secured the fifth ticket.","winner":null,"podium":[],"moments":[{"t":2128,"title":"Three-wide for the first All-Star ticket","summary":"Whittenburg, Kuehl, Rincon, Klapka, and Oxendine crowd into a sustained three-wide fight for the Stage 1 lead as tire conservation begins to separate the field.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","kelly-keel","george-rincon","josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2768,"title":"Whittenburg wins the opening ticket","summary":"Kuehl dives to the apron on the final lap but cannot complete the pass, allowing Whittenburg to take Stage 1, $25, and an automatic All-Star berth.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":3648,"title":"Timmerman and Green tumble onto the guardrail","summary":"A multi-truck chain reaction sends Angelica Timmerman onto her roof and Rob Green upside down, backward across the guardrail, while Kilgore's smoking truck limps away.","tags":["angelica-timmerman","rob-green","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4080,"title":"Everage short-fuels to the front","summary":"Michael Everage takes only the fuel needed to finish the segment, drives past the field on the restart, and holds off Riehle and Dixon to win Stage 2.","tags":["mike-everage","dustin-reilly","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4848,"title":"Timmerman sticks another roof-first landing","summary":"Jeff Snyder gets loose and hooks Kilgore and Mayberry, and Timmerman is launched onto her roof again before sliding through the grass in what the booth scores a 9.7 landing.","tags":["jeff-snyder","russ-kilgore","dave-mayberry","angelica-timmerman"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5490,"title":"Kuehl and Klapka trade the Stage 3 lead","summary":"Kuehl crosses Klapka over and the pair run side by side through the closing laps, repeatedly testing the limit of their worn right-front tires.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5617,"title":"Kuehl gets loose; Klapka cashes in","summary":"Kuehl noses ahead on the Stage 3 white flag but breaks loose twice, surrendering the lead and the All-Star ticket to a steady Eric Klapka.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6018,"title":"Herzig's snap starts the Stage 4 Big One","summary":"The No. 12 gets loose high and tags Rincon, sweeping Brian Jablonski and others into a multi-truck crash while Timmerman threads through by inches on all four tires.","tags":["john-herzig","george-rincon","brian-jablonski","angelica-timmerman"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6910,"title":"Dixon refuses Klapka's late charge","summary":"Klapka claws back through the field and reaches Dixon's bumper, but Dixon hits every mark and holds off Oxendine and Klapka to claim Stage 4.","tags":["jack-dixon","josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7480,"title":"Whittenburg hangs in the fence","summary":"In the final stage, Whittenburg crashes into the inside wall and is left suspended in the fence, prompting an immediate mock call for the ambulance.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7565,"title":"Klapka spins like a top in three-wide carnage","summary":"Klapka and Jablonski touch while racing three-wide for the lead, sending the 88 into a violent roof-first spin and collecting Riehle and Oxendine in the yellow-flag pileup.","tags":["brian-jablonski","dustin-reilly","josh-oxendine"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8440,"title":"Kuehl dives through the grass; Rincon gets the last ticket","summary":"Kuehl hounds Rincon through a tense final-lap duel but drops through the infield entering turn one, leaving Rincon clear to win Stage 5 and the final All-Star berth.","tags":["kelly-keel","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2988,"quote":"I was definitely racing my guts out. I was real nervous on that last lap.","context":"Whittenburg describes winning the first stage","gold":4},{"t":3728,"quote":"I hope you're not in VR, man, because I might need a bucket next to you after that.","context":"Rob Green tumbles backward along the guardrail","gold":5},{"t":4900,"quote":"Stuck the landing — 9.7 on the landing. Really good landing.","context":"Timmerman survives another roof-first flight","gold":5},{"t":5674,"quote":"That was an exciting last couple of laps — as exciting as a game of Yahtzee.","context":"The booth recovers from the Stage 3 finish","gold":4},{"t":6310,"quote":"Let's just do Michigan stage racing every week. It's fun.","context":"The fourth sprint delivers another lead battle","gold":4},{"t":7490,"quote":"Call an ambulance — he's hung up in the fence on the inside wall.","context":"Whittenburg's final-stage crash","gold":5},{"t":9172,"quote":"I feel like Oprah: you're a winner, you're a winner — everybody's a winner here.","context":"Stage and random-draw money is handed out","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Special Wednesday-night All-Star qualifying event at Michigan. It was five stages rather than one conventional race, so there is no single overall winner or podium. All-Star transfers/stage winners were Ricky Whittenburg, Michael Everage, Eric Klapka, Jack Dixon, and Jorge Rincon. Separate $15 random-draw winners were Dion Jones, Dave Mayberry, Angelica Timmerman, Dustin Riehle, and Rob Green; those draws were cash prizes, not stage wins. Alan Vaught was present in race control but did not grid. The archive uses best-guess canonical spellings for Riehle, Rincon, Everage, and Herzig because auto-captions vary heavily.","resultConfidence":"winner-unknown-or-multi-stage"},"qAak_zEaps8":{"recap":"Tim Pope started on pole and led the opening corners before Greg Klein spun into Alan Vaught and Dion Jones to bring out a first-lap caution. Pope and Trevor Robertson then swapped the lead through the opening run as tire conservation repeatedly changed the order. The race's most violent moment came when Sean McDonnell caught the wall in the dogleg and Andrew Coffin was hooked into a roof-first impact. The following restart produced a second Big One when Dustin Wade slid across four-wide traffic, collecting Mike Adamson, Scott Rooney, John McAdam, Kelly Kuehl, and others. Once the field settled, Derek Welch, Pope, Robertson, Dillon Bryant, Albert Anderson, and Craig Goodenough all fought near the point, with Welch falling from first to fifth in a single lap before Goodenough took control. Anderson briefly undercut Goodenough during the middle green-flag cycle, but Goodenough crossed him back for the lead. On the final stops, Goodenough pitted three laps before Pope and converted the fresh-tire advantage into nearly five seconds. Pope charged back to within roughly a second, but ran out of laps. Goodenough won from 27th for his first victory of the season, Pope finished second, and Alan Vaught climbed from 24th to third.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":2117,"title":"Klein spins the field on lap one","summary":"Greg Klein loses the rear of the No. 92 exiting turn two, clips Alan Vaught, and catches Dion Jones in the first caution before the race is one lap old.","tags":["greg-cline","jess-vaught","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2545,"title":"Robertson takes clean air from Pope","summary":"Trevor Robertson dives underneath polesitter Tim Pope and captures the lead, beginning a tire-management seesaw between the two.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2931,"title":"Robertson's save brings him back to the point","summary":"After appearing to fade on worn tires, Robertson marches past Derek Welch and Pope and retakes the race lead as the booth debates whether he had been saving all along.","tags":["trevor-robertson","derek-welch","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3223,"title":"Coffin lands on his roof in the dogleg","summary":"Sean McDonnell catches the wall and hooks Andrew Coffin's right rear, launching Coffin roof-first into a massive impact before he slides toward pit lane.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3515,"title":"Wade's slide triggers the Texas Big One","summary":"Dustin Wade gets crossed up at the bottom while the pack fans four wide; the reaction collects Mike Adamson, Scott Rooney, John McAdam, Kelly Kuehl, and much of the backstretch traffic.","tags":["dustin-wade","mike-adamson","scott-rooney","john-mcadam","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4021,"title":"Welch drops from first to fifth in one lap","summary":"Tim Pope attacks Derek Welch for the lead, then Goodenough, Robertson, and Dillon Bryant pile through as a compressed draft pack completely reshuffles the top five.","tags":["derek-welch","timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4080,"title":"Goodenough completes the charge to the lead","summary":"Craig Goodenough passes Pope and takes control after starting 27th, establishing the duel that will define the rest of the race.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4381,"title":"Anderson rubs Welch out of the top five","summary":"Albert Anderson noses inside Derek Welch, makes door-to-door contact, and sends Welch chasing the truck up the track while taking fifth.","tags":["albert-anderson","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4886,"title":"Goodenough crosses Anderson back after the stops","summary":"Anderson's lightning-fast pit service leapfrogs Goodenough, but the No. 89 uses lapped traffic and a crossover to reclaim the lead almost immediately.","tags":["craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5893,"title":"Pope stays out three laps too long","summary":"Pope delays his final stop while boxed in by Chris Klein; Goodenough's three laps on fresher tires turn a side-by-side fight into a five-second advantage.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","chris-klein"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6461,"title":"Pope launches the last ten-lap chase","summary":"With ten laps left, Pope is the fastest truck on track and cuts Goodenough's advantage from more than four seconds to 2.3 while navigating lap traffic.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6733,"title":"Goodenough closes his first win of the season","summary":"Goodenough takes the white with a lapped truck between himself and Pope, then completes the final lap to win from 27th as Alan Vaught secures third from 24th.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3223,"quote":"Oh, big-time trouble here in the dogleg. Andrew Coffin hard into the wall on his lid!","context":"Coffin is launched into the race's first major crash","gold":5},{"t":3357,"quote":"He stuck the landing pretty good. He must be proficient in flight sim, too — I give it a 9.3.","context":"The booth finds gallows humor in Coffin's roof-first landing","gold":4},{"t":3515,"quote":"Big-time pileup! Everybody packed up, coming together here down the back straightaway.","context":"Wade's save attempt triggers the Texas Big One","gold":5},{"t":4070,"quote":"Welch goes from the lead to fifth in just about a lap.","context":"The top five is completely shuffled after the restart","gold":4},{"t":4381,"quote":"It almost looks like a tandem-draft finish at Talladega with this one.","context":"The front six split into pairs during the lead battle","gold":4},{"t":5955,"quote":"They were right up on top of each other, and now it's a five-second advantage for Craig Goodenough.","context":"Goodenough's undercut transforms the final pit cycle","gold":4},{"t":6733,"quote":"Checker flag is waving — Craig Goodenough wins it at Texas!","context":"Goodenough finishes the drive from 27th to first","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 11, Race 11 at Texas Motor Speedway, 133 laps. Winner, podium, starting positions, and first-win-of-the-season status are explicitly stated in the finish call and interviews. The captions alternate Gooduff/Goodnov/Goodnote for Craig Goodenough and VA/Bot for Alan Vaught; canonical archive spellings are used. Andrew Coffin's surname is also captioned as Cawan/Cowan in places.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"QDfi3n59xt4":{"recap":"Alan Vaught and teammate Greg Klein controlled the opening phase at Circuit of the Americas before Andrew Player's undercut split them, with Vaught still winning the scheduled halfway stage ahead of Player and Jorge Rincon. The stage caution reset a field that had already endured frequent spins and off-track excursions, and Mike Adamson and Tim Pope used a fuel-only stop before the restart while most leaders serviced under yellow. Jeremiah Burke, sent to the rear by a pre-race penalty, climbed through the leaders in the second half and stopped late enough to cover the finish, while Player and Rincon tried to stretch their fuel. Both were forced to pit in the closing laps, giving Burke the lead at the white flag; he held off Vaught on the final lap to win, with Klein third.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Alan Vaught","Greg Cline"],"moments":[{"t":2010,"title":"Vaught leads the COTA launch","summary":"Pole-sitter Alan Vaught clears teammate Greg Klein through the steep first corner as a 33-truck field begins 33 laps at COTA.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2080,"title":"Opening-lap mistakes scatter the field","summary":"Multiple trucks spin or run off in the opening sequence, including Albert Anderson, as the heavy stock trucks struggle through COTA's braking zones.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2335,"title":"Everage spins through the esses","summary":"Michael Everage carries too much speed into the esses, loses the rear, and slides into the wall while Burke begins advancing through the pack.","tags":["mike-everage","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2450,"title":"Emig helps Everage around","summary":"Everage is spun after contact from David Emig and Andrew Coffin cannot fully avoid the incident, adding to the early attrition.","tags":["mike-everage","david-emig","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2873,"title":"Rincon wins a long fight with Long","summary":"Jorge Rincon and Jonah Long run side-by-side through the final corner before Rincon uses the inside line to complete the pass for fourth.","tags":["george-rincon","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3618,"title":"Player undercuts Klein for second","summary":"Vaught and Klein finally make their opening stops, but Player's earlier service cycles him ahead of Klein while Vaught retains the race lead.","tags":["andrew-player","greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3956,"title":"Coffin turns Gallagher before the stage","summary":"Andrew Coffin cuts across without enough room and clips John Gallagher's rear quarter, spinning Gallagher opposite the racing direction before he rejoins safely.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4355,"title":"Vaught wins the halfway stage","summary":"The planned yellow flies after 16 laps with Vaught first, Player second, and Rincon third; Klein, Adamson, Burke, Dustyn Eaton, Osborne, and Reeves also collect top-10 stage points.","tags":["jess-vaught","andrew-player","george-rincon","greg-cline","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","austin-reeves"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":5327,"title":"Four-wide restart traffic blocks Turn 1","summary":"The field fans four-wide on the second-half restart and several trucks stack up in Turn 1, while Vaught escapes and Burke resumes his climb.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5461,"title":"Burke breaks into the top five","summary":"Burke dives inside Player in Turn 1 and completes the pass for fourth, then begins hunting Long and Rincon while Vaught leads.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","andrew-player","jonah-long","george-rincon","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6943,"title":"Fuel gambles hand Burke the lead","summary":"Player abandons his fuel stretch with three laps left, and Rincon finally stops while approaching the white flag; Burke crosses the line to inherit first with Vaught closing.","tags":["andrew-player","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7195,"title":"Burke holds off Vaught for the COTA win","summary":"Vaught closes to half a second on the final lap, but Burke survives the last corners to complete a 25-position charge and win ahead of Vaught and Klein.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1319,"quote":"Turn one, also turn two. Don't forget about turn three. Just be careful in the rest of them while you're at it.","context":"The booth offers a deliberately unhelpful key to COTA","gold":4},{"t":2516,"quote":"If you can just run slow, smooth, fast, it's starting to get a little safer out there right now.","context":"Adam Turner describes the survival approach to the opening stage","gold":3},{"t":2631,"quote":"Jess Vaught and Greg Klein doing the old shake and bake.","context":"The teammates drive away together in the opening stage","gold":4},{"t":4955,"quote":"About lap five your tires fall off and you're ice skating around the whole lap.","context":"Austin Reeves describes learning COTA in a stock truck","gold":4},{"t":5707,"quote":"Chess and checkers all being played at the same time here.","context":"Klein and Osborne exchange crossover moves","gold":4},{"t":6213,"quote":"Eight wheels turn better than four.","context":"The booth relays a viewer's prediction of late door-to-door racing","gold":4},{"t":7159,"quote":"Final corner, the 753, Jess Vaught right behind him. It's not going to be enough!","context":"Burke's winning call at COTA","gold":5},{"t":7869,"quote":"That was the hardest road-course race I've ever done in my life.","context":"Winner Jeremiah Burke reacts after charging from the rear","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 4, Round 5 at Circuit of the Americas according to seasons_map.json. The race ran 33 laps with a planned stage caution after lap 16 and allowed two fast repairs. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Burke-Vaught-Klein podium and reads the complete 33-driver results. Burke's stated 25-position hard-charge reflects serving an end-of-line penalty after the qualifying order placed him 26th. Roster canonical names are used for captions including Dustyn Eaton ('Dustyn Eaton'), Robert Chipman ('Robert Shipman'), Chris Zofeld ('Chris Sofield'), and Mike Sobanovski ('Mike the Spy'). Transcript timestamps end within the 8,565-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"qoBQAZUSmUg":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough won the 57-lap Thanksgiving-eve race at Sonoma by 12.5 seconds after recovering from an eventful first half and dominating the final green run. Polesitter Jacob Alesia led early, but contact with Goodenough in Turn 10 sent Alesia into the wall and left him with rear aerodynamic damage, while Goodenough also spun Trevor Robertson during an earlier passing attempt. The scheduled lap-29 competition caution reset the field, where John Osborne stayed out on older tires to gain track position and briefly led before Goodenough and Jack Dixon went by. Goodenough reclaimed the lead after Andrew Player's long final stint ended with a stop, Dixon finished a career-highlight second despite wheel damage, and Osborne's strategy delivered third.","winner":"Craig Goodenough","podium":["Craig Goodenough","Jack Dixon","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":1429,"title":"Alesia leads the Sonoma field away","summary":"Jacob Alesia launches from pole ahead of Trevor Robertson, with Craig Goodenough and Jack Dixon settling into the lead group.","tags":["jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1667,"title":"Goodenough and Robertson make contact","summary":"Goodenough dives inside Robertson, the two fight side by side into the next corner, and contact spins Robertson without significant damage.","tags":["craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3360,"title":"Goodenough turns Alesia from the lead","summary":"After Alesia gets loose, Goodenough attacks inside at Turn 10; Alesia closes toward the normal line, contact sends the No. 31 into the wall, and he later reports two and a half minutes of rear damage.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3505,"title":"Redding and Jones spin at Turn 12","summary":"Dion Jones gets sideways while Jesse Redding is accelerating behind him, and the two trucks touch and rotate without serious damage.","tags":["dion-jones","jesse-redding"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3674,"title":"Competition caution resets the race","summary":"The scheduled lap-29 caution bunches the field after Jack Dixon had built a lead through the first pit cycle; Dillon Bryant and Jones also make minor contact as the field slows.","tags":["jack-dixon","dylan-bryant","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4095,"title":"Osborne stays out for track position","summary":"John Osborne skips the competition-caution pit stop and takes the front row on tires nine laps older than most of the challengers, committing to an offset final stop.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4519,"title":"Goodenough and Dixon clear Osborne","summary":"Goodenough draws alongside the older-tired Osborne and completes the pass, with Dixon following through; Osborne limits the immediate loss to two positions.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4904,"title":"The final stop sequence begins","summary":"Osborne and Robertson short-pit before Goodenough stops from the lead, while Dixon and Player stay out to pursue longer-run strategies.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5422,"title":"Player's fuel gamble ends","summary":"Player finally pits after stretching his last tank, handing the effective lead back to Goodenough and emerging around sixth on fresh tires.","tags":["andrew-player","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5523,"title":"Redding finds the tire barrier","summary":"Jesse Redding spins through the esses and appears ready to escape until the truck catches the tire barrier and suffers race-ending engine damage.","tags":["jesse-redding"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6213,"title":"Goodenough completes the rout","summary":"Goodenough wins by 12.5 seconds over Dixon, while Osborne holds off Player to preserve the final podium position.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3827,"quote":"If he wants to stick his nose up there and make it two-wide, he's got to do it before we commit into the apex like that.","context":"Jacob Alesia calmly gives his view of the contact with Goodenough","gold":5},{"t":4062,"quote":"They're boring to watch. I do not like watching them. I just like partaking in them.","context":"Guest analyst Jeremiah Burke gives his candid opinion of road-course races","gold":4},{"t":5437,"quote":"He's just living his best life right now.","context":"The booth watches Player continue stretching his fuel gamble","gold":3},{"t":6595,"quote":"Just simple math is what made me stay out there.","context":"John Osborne explains the strategy that turned a seventh-place run into a podium","gold":5},{"t":6784,"quote":"I knew I had something, but I know Craig's a robot at these road courses.","context":"Jack Dixon describes trying to match Goodenough before wheel damage slowed him","gold":5},{"t":6913,"quote":"I'm not super excited about the whole performance. I was patient as I could, waiting for slip-ups.","context":"Craig Goodenough reflects on the Alesia incident despite his dominant win","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The grid initially showed 23 entries, including Jeremiah Burke in 15th, but the broadcast then explicitly said Burke did not start and the final order contained 22 finishers; he is therefore listed only as a guest broadcaster. No natural full-course cautions were used at Sonoma; the sole full-course yellow was the scheduled lap-29 competition caution. The lead announcer's surname is captioned Vaugh and canonicalized to Alan Vaught. Final order was read in full and confirms the podium.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"QTKoAFqV1mM":{"recap":"The VRL Draft Masters brought 94 laps of NASCAR Truck plate racing to Talladega with a 40-truck field and rookie Harrison Whitehead starting from the pole. The night was pure survival: an early pileup collected Jonathan Osborne and Edward W. Smith, race leader Kelly Kuehl got hooked into the pit wall, and a lap-63 Big One swept up Kyle Vaught, Dustyn Eaton and Ricky Whittenburg before late wrecks kept thinning the front-runners. A four-truck melee with five laps to go forced a one-shot green-white-checker, and the final lap erupted into one last Big One behind the leaders, leaving only about five trucks to race to the line. Albert Anderson — 'America's driver' and the night's hard charger, up 37 spots from 38th — surged through with pushes from Allstar Racing teammates Jack Dixon and Nick Ramsey to steal the win, with Ramsey second, Tim Pope third, Jonah Long fourth and Whitehead fifth.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Nick Ramsey","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1424,"title":"Green flag at Talladega","summary":"The 40-truck field takes the green with rookie Harrison Whitehead on pole; Mike Adamson leapfrogs him off the top lane before lap one is even done.","tags":["mike-adamson","greg-dobson"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1947,"title":"First pileup against the wall","summary":"A squeezed-pile sandwich against the outside wall triggers the night's first multi-truck wreck — the 81 of Osborne and 63 of Smith take the worst of it, and Andrew Coffin limps back to pit road with a front wheel pointing the wrong way.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","edward-w-smith","david-fite","andrew-cauthan","kelly-keel","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3388,"title":"Kuehl hooked into the pit wall","summary":"Race leader Kelly Kuehl gets his bumper hooked diving to pit road and goes hard into the inside pit wall; the pit-lane scramble that follows spins Ricky Whittenburg and Dion Jones. Anderson later apologized — he didn't hear Kuehl's pit call.","tags":["kelly-keel","albert-anderson","ricky-whittenburg","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4550,"title":"Launched out of a cannon","summary":"Anderson bumps the 14 up to speed on the restart and the front row rockets away — 'maybe they hit the NOS button and we'll just have to find out here in tech inspection.'","tags":["dustin-eaton","dustin-reilly","albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4696,"title":"Four wide at Talladega","summary":"The pack fans out four wide fighting for the lead — 'this is going to make a great screenshot for later' — and somehow everybody survives it.","tags":["austin-paul","george-rincon","kelly-keel","nick-ramsey","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5053,"title":"The Big One at lap 63","summary":"Three-wide contact between the 67, 92 and 37 sends Riehle for a ride and stacks the whole field — Whittenburg becomes the meat in the sandwich, Vaught's truck ends up smoking, and the caution flies at lap 63.","tags":["dustin-reilly","scott-martin","greg-cline","kyle-vaught","dustin-eaton","ricky-whittenburg","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5630,"title":"False spotter call bites Klein and Anderson","summary":"The 92 comes down not quite clear on what the booth calls a false spotter call, and Albert Anderson goes down for the ride with him — 'the AI strikes back.'","tags":["greg-cline","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5946,"title":"Whitehead hooks the 82 with 20 to go","summary":"Three wide into the corner, the 77 comes down onto Everage's bumper and gets hooked; Eaton and Dion Jones catch pieces of the wreck on the way through.","tags":["mike-everage","edson-ochoa","dustin-eaton","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6684,"title":"Front-runners wiped out with 13 to go","summary":"The 37 drops to the middle lane and the bumpers don't line up — Riehle goes for a wild ride into the 92, and the stack-up collects Klein, Kelly Kuehl and Trevor Robertson, gutting the lead pack.","tags":["dustin-reilly","greg-cline","kelly-keel","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7327,"title":"Five-to-go melee forces the GWC","summary":"Dickerson and Mayberry get together in the squeeze with five laps left — four wide trucks pointed in the wrong direction — and the cleanup sets up a one-and-done green-white-checker.","tags":["larry-dickerson","dave-mayberry","andrew-player","scott-martin"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7749,"title":"Drinking helmets on: the GWC restart","summary":"Alan Vaught and Tim Pope lead the field to the one-shot green-white-checker as the booth tells everyone to strap on those drinking helmets and throw inhibition out the window.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7805,"title":"Last-lap Big One — Anderson steals it","summary":"A push from the 77 hooks the 07 into the 33 on the final lap and the wreck tears the whole field up, leaving a five-truck finish — Albert Anderson blocks Pope off turn four and steals the win as the hard charger, up 37 spots from 38th.","tags":["albert-anderson","nick-ramsey","timothy-pope","jonah-long","jack-dixon","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":934,"quote":"I'm hoping somebody gets turned that didn't really feel like getting turned, and then they yell on the radio, and then we get to talk about it.","context":"Adam Turner's pre-race wish for chaos","gold":4},{"t":3376,"quote":"Once the leader announces that he's going to pit, it's going to be an absolute feeding frenzy of piranhas coming in right behind him.","context":"Green-flag pit cycle about to open — moments before Kuehl hit the pit wall","gold":3},{"t":3937,"quote":"Being pushed by the 92 of Greg Klein, who will in fact wreck his grandmother to pick up a win.","context":"Klein shoving Trevor Robertson toward the lead","gold":4},{"t":4708,"quote":"Four wide, three wide, too wide — it don't matter how wide we're racing here at Talladega!","context":"The pack goes four wide fighting for the lead","gold":5},{"t":5007,"quote":"That's just the magic of the Lazy Susan here at these plate tracks — you go from champ to chump, chum to champ mighty quick.","context":"Dustyn Eaton recovering to the front after a botched pit call","gold":4},{"t":5162,"quote":"Everything gets checked on up and Ricky Wittenberg becomes meat in the sandwich.","context":"Replay of the lap-63 Big One","gold":4},{"t":7749,"quote":"Time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets, throw inhibition out the window — green white checker racing here from Talladega!","context":"Setting the field loose for the one-shot green-white-checker","gold":5},{"t":7856,"quote":"Any final runs coming? Not in time — Albert Anderson steals one away here at Talladega!","context":"The checkered-flag call as Anderson wins","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble many surnames; best guesses used: 'Dustin Riehle' (#37, captioned 'really/reallyy'), 'Jorge Rincon' (#28, captioned ranone/rancan/ringcon/rone), 'David Feit' (#1, captioned 'fight'), 'Andrew Coffin' (#10, captioned 'cin/cofin'), 'Edson Ochoa' (#8, captioned 'Ooa/Oella'), 'Dustyn Eaton' (nicknamed 'Dustin with a Y'). Vaught surname for Jess (#33) and Kyle (#16) inferred from vot/VA/fought captions; Lori Vaught was named as league race control. Earl Evans (#13) was mentioned but not racing tonight. Craig Goodenough (#89) disconnected before the start with connection issues and was scored 39th. One grid position (37th starter) was lost to caption garble. Winner and podium explicitly stated in the finish rundown and driver interviews.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"QzAYS2PNCFg":{"recap":"Alan Vaught led a Vigilante Force sweep at Las Vegas, rebounding from a mid-race shuffle to win both Stage 1 and the race. Pole-sitter Kelly Kuehl remained a threat all night and battled his teammate Vaught for the lead in the closing laps, while a series of incidents left only 12 of 34 starters on the lead lap. Eric Klafka's spin with two laps remaining sent the race to overtime. Vaught nailed the green-white-checkered restart and held off Kuehl, with Dustin Riehle completing the all-team podium.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Kelly Kuehl","Dustin Riehle"],"moments":[{"t":1095,"title":"Kuehl leads the Vegas field to green","summary":"Kelly Kuehl starts from pole alongside Albert Anderson and gets the better launch as the 34-truck field charges into Turn 1.","tags":["kelly-keel","albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1130,"title":"Lap-one pileup erupts behind the leaders","summary":"Contact involving Kim Krauss and Jack Dixon starts an immediate multi-truck crash that sweeps up much of the traffic behind John Gallagher.","tags":["kim-krauss","jack-dixon","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2896,"title":"Vaught wins Stage 1","summary":"Alan Vaught takes the yellow-and-checkered stage finish ahead of Kelly Kuehl and Albert Anderson, with J.R. Hollingsworth and Austin Paul completing the top five.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","albert-anderson","j-r-hollingsworth","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3938,"title":"Three-wide crash eliminates contenders","summary":"Jonathan Osborne drifts into the quarter panel of Albert Anderson in three-wide traffic, turning Anderson nose-first into J.R. Hollingsworth as Jack Dixon, Dustin Wade, Greg Dobson and others become involved.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson","j-r-hollingsworth","jack-dixon","dustin-wade","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4276,"title":"Endicott gambles on track position","summary":"Russ Endicott and Brayton Laster stay out to lead the restart, forcing fuel-only stoppers Kuehl and Vaught to carve through traffic.","tags":["russ-endicott","brayton-laster","kelly-keel","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5666,"title":"Vigilante Force controls the final run","summary":"Vaught leads teammate Kuehl while Dave Mayberry closes from fourth, setting up a tense intrateam fight with three laps remaining.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5745,"title":"Klafka spin forces overtime","summary":"As Kuehl pressures Vaught with two laps to go, contact between Eric Klafka and Chandler Paul turns Klafka and brings out the caution.","tags":["eric-klafka","chandler-paul","jess-vaught","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6084,"title":"Vaught launches on the overtime restart","summary":"Alan Vaught gets a decisive jump over Kelly Kuehl on the green-white-checkered restart while Dustin Riehle holds third.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6152,"title":"Vaught seals a team podium sweep","summary":"Kuehl makes one final push through Turns 3 and 4, but Vaught reaches the stripe first; Kuehl and Riehle fill the remaining podium places.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1361,"quote":"You have to wear shoes in there unlike the local Walmart.","context":"The booth riffs on Anderson's Target-themed paint scheme.","gold":5},{"t":2866,"quote":"If I was from Canada I'd have a dog named hose head.","context":"A booth tangent while following the Canadian drivers.","gold":5},{"t":6152,"quote":"One final push, but it won't be enough.","context":"The final-corner call as Kuehl tries to catch Vaught.","gold":5},{"t":6527,"quote":"I didn't want to wreck him either, but I wanted to make it look fun.","context":"Kuehl explains racing his teammate hard in the podium interview.","gold":2},{"t":6883,"quote":"I stayed—my plan was to stay up front and try to stay out of the chaos.","context":"Vaught describes his winning approach.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, interviews, and full results all explicitly confirm Vaught, Kuehl, and Riehle as the podium. The captions distinguish No. 37 Dustin Riehle from No. 14 Dustyn Eaton, but roster.json contains Dustin Riehle and no Dustyn Eaton entry; Dustyn Eaton is retained as captioned because they are clearly separate starters. The grid calls Austin Paul the No. 3 and later Chandler Paul the No. 72. The opening crash involved many trucks, but only the clearly identified Krauss, Dixon, and Gallagher are attached to that moment.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"rdpMD3daWO4":{"recap":"Jeremiah Burke won the second playoff round at Sonoma by combining a clean second half with the strongest final pit cycle. Dustyn Eaton led early after out-braking pole-sitter Josh Bittner, and Trevor Robertson won the scheduled halfway stage before several contenders ran into trouble. Burke took the lead after the restart and built a decisive margin once the final stops cycled through; Robertson spun from second, and Sean McDonnell had to make a very late fuel stop. Mike Adamson climbed 23 positions to finish second, while Greg Klein's tire-saving strategy carried him from 22nd to third.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Mike Adamson","Greg Cline"],"moments":[{"t":1488,"title":"Bittner leads the field into Sonoma","summary":"Josh Bittner starts from pole beside Dustyn Eaton as the 26-truck field negotiates the uphill opening corners and the first trip through the hairpin.","tags":["josh-bittner","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1744,"title":"Eaton out-brakes Bittner for the lead","summary":"Eaton dives to the inside of Bittner in the hairpin and completes the opening green-flag lead change.","tags":["dustin-eaton","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2806,"title":"Rincon and Jones make heavy contact","summary":"Jorge Rincon and Dion Jones beat and bang during the first-half run, adding damage in a race where the dirt and barriers are already punishing mistakes.","tags":["george-rincon","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":3383,"title":"Robertson takes the lead before halfway","summary":"Burke and Robertson both make mistakes, but Robertson recovers more quickly and moves back to the front ahead of the scheduled stage break.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":3708,"title":"Vaught crashes just before the stage yellow","summary":"Alan Vaught opens the inside while battling Jonah Long, hits the tire barriers hard and suffers heavy suspension damage before reaching pit road for his fast repair.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonah-long"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3802,"title":"Robertson wins the halfway stage","summary":"Robertson reaches the scheduled caution first over Burke, Eaton, Sean McDonnell and Bittner, with ten trucks listed in the stage top ten.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","shawn-mcdonald","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4504,"title":"Burke takes command after the restart","summary":"Tim Pope initially jumps ahead on the restart, but Burke quickly works through and assumes the lead as the second-half strategies develop.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":4797,"title":"Klein and Adamson short-pit the finish","summary":"With roughly 19 laps remaining, Klein and Adamson make their final stops together, gambling that smooth driving can preserve their tires to the checkered flag.","tags":["greg-cline","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5394,"title":"Burke completes his final stop","summary":"Burke and Ricky Whittenburg come to pit road with about ten laps remaining; once the cycle settles, Burke holds a commanding advantage.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":5829,"title":"Robertson spins out of second","summary":"Robertson locks the brakes and hits the inside wall, surrendering second to McDonnell and promoting Adamson and Klein in the closing order.","tags":["trevor-robertson","shawn-mcdonald","mike-adamson","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5959,"title":"McDonnell makes a costly late stop","summary":"McDonnell pits in the final laps after miscalculating his remaining fuel, handing third to Klein while Adamson moves securely into second.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","greg-cline","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6267,"title":"Burke wins by a wide margin","summary":"Burke completes the final hairpin and takes the checkered flag roughly 20 seconds clear, with hard-charger Adamson second and Klein third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6267,"quote":"Down across the line as the 53 picks up the race win here tonight at Sonoma.","context":"The live victory call for Burke.","gold":2},{"t":6501,"quote":"I was just hoping I could save enough tires to make that work.","context":"Klein explains the strategy behind his 19-position climb to third.","gold":5},{"t":6682,"quote":"It was definitely like walking through a land mine sometimes.","context":"Adamson describes avoiding trouble during his hard-charger drive to second.","gold":5},{"t":7072,"quote":"If I finished 17th and had the most off tracks, that means there are people behind me.","context":"Coffin finds the bright side after winning the broadcast's informal off-track contest.","gold":5},{"t":7221,"quote":"I had to work for that one. These guys are getting better and better at road courses every season.","context":"Burke opens his winner interview by crediting the improving field.","gold":5},{"t":7265,"quote":"Basically the whole track has no grip.","context":"Burke summarizes Sonoma's central challenge.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Burke, Adamson and Klein. The scheduled stage break occurred after lap 28, with Robertson scored as stage winner. Adamson was hard charger at plus 23 positions; Klein gained 19. All 26 classified starters from the results rundown are included. The broadcast also conducted a random-draw interview with 17th-place Andrew Coffin, who had the most off-track incidents, but he was not the race winner despite a joking introduction that calls him the 'race winner for the most off tracks.'","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"rn7aGKdVKKg":{"recap":"Alex Berube won the 100-lap Bluegrass Brawl at Kentucky, earning the $125 top prize after starting ninth and mastering a caution-free, two-stop race. Zach Wheeler controlled the opening stint from the front row while Tim Pope steadily closed, but Berube's combination of long-run pace and pit timing moved the Quebec driver to the lead after the first cycle. Alan Vaught gained ground with a quick final stop, only for Pope to take second as Berube pulled more than four seconds clear in the closing run. Berube won ahead of Pope and Vaught, with Josh Bittner fourth and Wheeler fifth; 11 of the 36 entrants finished on the lead lap.","winner":"Alex Berube","podium":["Alex Berube","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1730,"title":"Bluegrass Brawl goes green three-wide","summary":"Russ Kilgore and Zach Wheeler lead the field to green, while Zachary Self charges forward and the pack fans three-wide through the opening laps.","tags":["russ-kilgore","zach-wheeler","zachary-self"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1876,"title":"Wheeler sets the early benchmark","summary":"Wheeler takes command and records a 30.76-second lap, establishing himself as both the race leader and an early contender for the separate fastest-lap prize.","tags":["zach-wheeler"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":2221,"title":"Burube storms into the top five","summary":"Alex Berube advances from ninth into fifth and then fourth, passing Josh Bittner as Tim Pope closes steadily on leader Wheeler.","tags":["alex-berube","josh-bittner","timothy-pope","zach-wheeler"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":2515,"title":"Pope reaches Wheeler's bumper","summary":"After a long opening run, Pope cuts Wheeler's advantage to roughly a quarter-second while Berube and Vaught remain part of the lead fight.","tags":["timothy-pope","zach-wheeler","alex-berube","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2758,"title":"Wheeler begins the first pit cycle","summary":"Wheeler stops around the one-third mark and Pope briefly inherits the lead as the 36-truck field splits into small groups entering the difficult green-flag pit road.","tags":["zach-wheeler","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3167,"title":"Berube pressures Wheeler after the stops","summary":"Once the first stops cycle, Berube uses tires one lap fresher to reach Wheeler's bumper, a pivotal sequence in his climb to the race lead.","tags":["alex-berube","zach-wheeler"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3675,"title":"Berube opens a lead over Pope","summary":"By the second half, Berube has completed his march from ninth and leads Pope by more than a second while Wheeler falls to third.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope","zach-wheeler"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":3911,"title":"Final green-flag stops begin","summary":"Bradley Wright and Alan Vaught are among the first final-cycle takers, followed by Berube, Bittner, and eventually Pope as the field commits to a two-stop finish.","tags":["bradley-wright","jess-vaught","alex-berube","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4372,"title":"Berube controls the closing run","summary":"After the cycle settles, Berube holds a lead of more than four seconds; Vaught's quick stop initially places him second before Pope closes and takes the runner-up spot.","tags":["alex-berube","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":4456,"title":"Kuehl saves a backward slide","summary":"Kelly Kuehl spins and backs into the wall, but the field scatters around him and he continues without triggering the race's first caution.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":5027,"title":"Berube cashes in at Kentucky","summary":"Berube takes the checkered flag after 100 caution-free laps, with Pope second and Vaught third in the three paid finishing positions.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3318,"quote":"It's called pressure. It's kind of like a game of chess. This isn't checkers; this is chess.","context":"The booth explains how a trailing truck can force mistakes on worn tires","gold":4},{"t":4159,"quote":"You actually have to have a brain to do this. It's not just pulling the steering wheel left and punching the floorboard.","context":"The booth jokes while the final green-flag strategy cycle unfolds","gold":4},{"t":4899,"quote":"This has been a great race to call. Once again, these guys basically doing the whole race under green-flag conditions.","context":"The booth appreciates the clean race in the closing laps","gold":3},{"t":5245,"quote":"That speaks to our effort to get great drivers into this league and how talented they are and respectful they are of each other.","context":"Third-place finisher Alan Vaught reflects on a second consecutive caution-free exhibition","gold":4},{"t":5485,"quote":"I started at ninth, and I was holding my position and moving through to the top five.","context":"Alex Berube recounts the beginning of his winning charge","gold":4},{"t":5538,"quote":"That was awesome. That was a nice track, nice truck, nice setup. It was fast.","context":"Berube celebrates his $125 victory","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"This was a 100-lap, 150-mile preseason money exhibition rather than a points round. The race ran green to checkered without a caution, and the broadcast reported 11 trucks on the lead lap. The final rundown conflicted over positions 10–12; the second scoring table indicates Tyler Green 10th, Ricky Whittenburg 11th, and hard charger Greg Dobson 12th, but those positions are not used in the recap. Zach Wheeler, Tyler Green, and Zachary Self were all discussed as fastest-lap contenders, but the broadcast never announced the bonus winner. 'Kevin Sean' is the only audible rendering for one of two entrants credited with no completed lap, has no roster match, and remains uncertain. Steve Seegers, Clinton Chambers, and Cody Kelly also lack roster entries and retain the clearest broadcast spellings.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"rUfuC3zSMMk":{"recap":"VRL opened Season 8 with the Daytona Classic, 100 laps of truck pack racing that stayed remarkably tidy for a plate track — 33 of 37 trucks were still on the lead lap at halfway — before fuel mileage rewrote the whole script. Dustin Wade took the pole, but the front-pack rotation belonged to Albert Anderson, Kyle Vogt, Tim Pope and John Curtis until Anderson money-shifted his motor to pieces leaving the pits with 11 laps to go. Four cautions dotted the night — Dustyn Eaton's backstretch spin, a grass ride for Ricky Whittenburg, rookie Zachary Henin's 'tumble cycle' and Jack Dixon's wall shot — but the decisive blow came on the final lap, when contenders Mike Everage and Austin Paul were swept up in a wreck and Chandler Paul split the carnage 'like Moses parting the Red Sea' to sputter home on fumes for his first VRL win. Hard charger Larry Dickerson climbed 33 spots to second, Robert Chipman ran his tank dry crossing the line in third, and Henin briefly led the fuel game before fading to 16th.","winner":"Chandler Paul","podium":["Chandler Paul","Larry Dickerson","Robert Chipman"],"moments":[{"t":935,"title":"Lizard people, diaper ladies, and a missing Adam","summary":"The booth explains third commentator Adam Turner's absence with a tale about 'that diaper lady' and saving astronauts from lizard people — a running gag that carries the whole broadcast.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1608,"title":"First yellow: Eaton spun down the backstretch","summary":"Dustyn Eaton's 14 gets turned down the backstretch after the 99 moves up and Greg Klein's shove catches him checked up — front-end sheet metal gone and the season's first caution out on about lap 5.","tags":["dustin-eaton","greg-cline","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2216,"title":"Whittenburg mows the Daytona lawn","summary":"A sneaky three-wide from Jack Dixon sends Jorge Rincon sideways and punts trucks into the infield grass, league painter Ricky Whittenburg and Scott Howell among the riders.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","scott-howell","jack-dixon","george-rincon"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3991,"title":"Henin through the tumble cycle","summary":"Rookie Zachary Henin 'gets put through the tumble cycle' approaching halfway — the booth traces it to Earl Evans' lift that looked like a 30 mph checkup from the chopper cam, drawing caution three.","tags":["zachary-henin","earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4427,"title":"Adam made bail: 'I'm here!'","summary":"Right at halfway the missing third mic Adam Turner finally pops into the booth — 'yep, halfway and I'm here' — after two hours of jokes about him running off with the airplane lady.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5423,"title":"Valentine love letters, then pit-lane chaos","summary":"The 82 and 01 trade 'late Valentine's Day love letters' at speed — Kelly Kuehl needing new drawers — then a two- and three-wide green-flag pit entry spins Edson Ochoa on the pit lane.","tags":["kelly-keel","mike-everage","edson-ochoa"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5481,"title":"Chachi drives with his mouth — and wins races","summary":"The booth tells Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne's story: told as a baby he wouldn't live a couple of weeks, now 30-something and operating the entire truck with a controller in his mouth — winning races and running endurance events too.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5583,"title":"Dixon slams the wall, Chipman threads the needle","summary":"Jorge Rincon snaps loose off a netcode wobble and Jack Dixon gets shipped into the outside wall; Robert Chipman barely squeezes past in what the booth calls a 'fill-the-diaper moment... brought to you by Depends.'","tags":["jack-dixon","george-rincon","robert-chipman"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6103,"title":"Bittner's ice-skate save","summary":"Josh Bittner gets clipped on the quarter panel and spins toward the inside wall, then somehow ice-skates the 84 straight on the apron with no visible damage — no caution needed.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6632,"title":"Anderson money-shifts it all away","summary":"Plate-track guru Albert Anderson, who led much of the night, blows his motor with a money shift off his final pit stop with 11 to go — America's driver done, classified 31st.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6779,"title":"A rookie leads the fuel game","summary":"With the big names pitting, brand-new Zachary Henin — up 25 spots — leads at Daytona side by side with David Feit while half the field white-knuckles the fuel math to the end.","tags":["zachary-henin","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7151,"title":"Moses parts the Red Sea for Chan the Man","summary":"Last lap: Mike Everage gets squeezed low and Austin Paul gets wrecked out of the lead fight, and Chandler Paul splits the opening on fumes — almost nothing left in the tank by his own telling — to steal his first VRL win over Larry Dickerson and Robert Chipman.","tags":["chandler-paul","mike-everage","austin-paul","larry-dickerson","robert-chipman","earl-evans","edson-ochoa"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":935,"quote":"Adam decided to try to make the drive with that diaper lady that he's always so affectionate for, saving those astronauts from the lizard people.","context":"The booth explains the missing third commentator","gold":4},{"t":2422,"quote":"Ended up using a TI-84... and it came up with an answer of 'you suck.'","context":"Booth tangent about a bad round of golf scored on a graphing calculator","gold":3},{"t":3991,"quote":"Oh no, Zachary Henin going for a little bit of a ride — gets put through the tumble cycle!","context":"Mid-race wreck call as the rookie spins","gold":3},{"t":5423,"quote":"The 82 and the 01 trading some late Valentine's Day love letters there — Kelly Keel going to need to change his drawers after that.","context":"A near-miss in the pack right before green-flag pit stops","gold":3},{"t":5672,"quote":"That's a fill-the-diaper moment right there. — Yep, brought to you by Depends.","context":"Robert Chipman barely threads past Jack Dixon's sideways truck","gold":4},{"t":6632,"quote":"Oh, Albert Anderson with a money shift — blew his motor! Did you hear that?","context":"The race favorite's engine lets go leaving the pits with 11 laps left","gold":4},{"t":7151,"quote":"That's going to leave the 72 of Chan the Man a wide opening, like Moses parting the Red Sea, as he spits and sputters his way down across the line picking up the race win!","context":"Last-lap wreck ahead of the leaders hands Chandler Paul the victory","gold":5},{"t":8025,"quote":"And one more thing — Dustin, who I like to talk crap to: he can eat my tire tracks tonight.","context":"Larry Dickerson capping his P2 interview after charging from 35th","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 8 opener, 100 laps at Daytona in NASCAR Trucks; results read from the broadcast's full finishing-order rundown. Caption garbles are heavy on the Vogt-family names: #16 'Kyle V/vot/VA' and #33 'Jess vot/fought/VA' — 'Vogt' is a best-guess rendering, and #1 'David Feit' may actually be Feit/Fite/Voight. P4 was read as 'the 28 of Jordan KH', but the #28 all race was Jorge Rincon, so P4 is presumed Rancone via caption garble. Zachary Henin's surname spelling is uncertain (henin/henen/henon/Hendon). Lori is the league director/admin who officiated (not a broadcaster); Adam Turner was absent for most of the show, appearing at halfway and after the finish. Greg Dobson and Dion Jones were mentioned but did not race tonight. Ricky Whittenburg spelling per DND Race Graphics sponsor references.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Rxr6VcE9NaA":{"recap":"VRL's Thanksgiving Eve Turkey Trot brought the NASCAR Trucks to the repaved, superspeedway-style Atlanta for 100 laps of pack racing, and the night delivered wreck after wreck — including a first-caution flip for Dustyn Eaton and a mid-race Big One that sent Jeremiah Burke flipping sideways. Polesitter Kelly Kuehl of Vigilante Force controlled much of the race, while teammate Alan Vaught led late until a bump from Kuehl sent him airborne and triggered a huge pileup. On the final lap Austin Reeves was spun out of contention by netcode, and Austin Paul drag-raced Kuehl off turn four to steal the win by half a truck length — the season's seventh different winner, though Paul is ineligible for the playoffs. Matt Beamer completed the podium in third in his return from hiatus, with Mike Adamson fourth and hard-charger Jonah Long fifth, up 28 spots. The broadcast also saluted outgoing league sponsor Ricky Whittenburg as Dave Mayberry's Blue Fox Properties took over presenting duties.","winner":"Austin Paul","podium":["Austin Paul","Kelly Kuehl","Matt Beamer"],"moments":[{"t":1576,"title":"Eaton flips in the first Big One","summary":"The 22 of Matt Beamer snaps loose in turns one and two, collecting Robert Chipman's 58, which slams the outside wall and snags Dustyn Eaton's 14 — sending it upside down. The 25, 81 and 63 all get swept up in the night's first caution.","tags":["matt-beamer","robert-chipman","dustin-eaton","cody-tarrant","jonathan-osborne","josh-oxendine"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2169,"title":"Player T-boned on the front stretch","summary":"Robert Jordan spins on the front stretch and Andrew Player is T-boned hard trying to avoid the 74, with Jeremiah Burke and Dave Mayberry swept up in the melee.","tags":["andrew-player","robert-jordan","jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2312,"title":"Booth salutes outgoing sponsor Ricky Whittenburg","summary":"The broadcast thanks Ricky Whittenburg — league sponsor since its inception through DD Race Graphics and Keller Williams of Johnson City, Tennessee — as Dave Mayberry's Blue Fox Properties takes over as presenting sponsor.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2538,"title":"Emig spins, Big One number two","summary":"David Emig goes around and shoots up the track into Mike Sobanovski; Jeremiah Burke goes flipping sideways yet again and Andrew Player, Albert Anderson, Jeff Ottinger and more are collected in a multi-truck crash.","tags":["david-emig","mike-sobanovski","jeremiah-burke","andrew-player","albert-anderson","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2808,"title":"Pope's Indiana Jones restart dive","summary":"Tim Pope dives through a closing gap under the Vigilante Force duo on the restart — 'that door wasn't open that wide but he was able to slide his foot in' — to take the lead.","tags":["timothy-pope","kelly-keel","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3241,"title":"Chipman fence glitch ends stage one","summary":"Jonathan Osborne goes up into the wall and Robert Chipman comes flying backwards off a glitch in the fence — 'octopus grabbed by that wall' — snagging Jonah Long and Russ Kilgore and ending stage one under caution at halfway.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","robert-chipman","jonah-long","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3772,"title":"Chan the Man slips, Ricky's turkey truck collected","summary":"Chandler Paul clips the apron and gets loose, the 28 of Jorge Rincon drifts up, and Ricky Whittenburg's WKRP-in-Cincinnati 'turkey drop' 55 is collected — an unhappy Ricky heard venting on the radio.","tags":["chandler-paul","george-rincon","ricky-whittenburg","chris-zofeld","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3930,"title":"Austin Paul: a prayer through the smoke","summary":"Mid-race interview with the night's biggest mover Austin Paul, who says his best passing move is avoiding the wrecks — he 'said a prayer and went through the smoke' to gain about 15 positions in one crash.","tags":["austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4638,"title":"Leader Vaught launched sky-high","summary":"A love tap from teammate Kelly Kuehl sends race leader Alan Vaught straight up into the air, triggering an absolute pileup that collects Dustyn Eaton, Jorge Rincon, Jonathan Osborne, Tim Pope and Jonah Long.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","george-rincon","jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4962,"title":"Restart chaos: 72 and 22 tangle","summary":"Contact between Chandler Paul and Matt Beamer on the restart sends trucks to the apron; Jonah Long, Jeff Ottinger, Russ Endicott and Dustin Wade get swept up — and the driver of the 72 is not happy at all.","tags":["chandler-paul","matt-beamer","jonah-long","jeff-ottinger","russ-endicott","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5798,"title":"Netcode heartbreak, Paul steals it at the line","summary":"On the white-flag lap Austin Reeves is spun by netcode while battling for the lead — 'a foot and a half apart' from Russ Kilgore — and Austin Paul drag-races Kelly Kuehl off turn four to steal the win by half a truck length, with Matt Beamer sneaking into third.","tags":["austin-paul","kelly-keel","austin-reeves","russ-kilgore","matt-beamer"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6035,"title":"Kuehl's cheerful confession: 'I turned Jess'","summary":"In the runner-up interview Kelly Kuehl admits he told teammate Alan Vaught he was going too slow and 'took him out' — then insists it was just for fun, to the booth's disbelief.","tags":["kelly-keel","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1622,"quote":"Grab onto your barf bags, everybody!","context":"Calling Dustyn Eaton's flip in the night's first Big One","gold":4},{"t":3535,"quote":"They're swinging these things all over the damn road like we're in Waco with a pistol in one hand and a cell phone in the other.","context":"The booth marveling at trucks running three-wide at Atlanta","gold":4},{"t":3986,"quote":"My biggest move of passing is avoiding the wrecks... just said a prayer and went through the smoke.","context":"Eventual winner Austin Paul explaining his 15-spot gain in one crash","gold":4},{"t":4650,"quote":"He went straight up in the air... Sarah, hide your eyes.","context":"Race leader Alan Vaught launched airborne with his daughter watching the chat","gold":4},{"t":5081,"quote":"There's 15 laps to go — let the hate loose. If you gotta slash somebody's tires, get those little kids from Six Pack to steal the muffler.","context":"English dropping the diplomacy act for the closing laps","gold":4},{"t":5832,"quote":"They were a foot and a half apart and iRacing decided that was too close and just killed one of them.","context":"The netcode spin that took Austin Reeves out on the last lap","gold":4},{"t":6046,"quote":"I told him, man, you're going too slow, I'm gonna have to turn you — and guess what happened. Took him out.","context":"Runner-up Kelly Kuehl gleefully confessing to wrecking leader Alan Vaught","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Race: 100 laps at repaved/reconfigured Atlanta (Trucks), Thanksgiving Eve 2022, ~32-33 starters, 24 finishers. Winner Austin Paul confirmed by post-race interview but stated ineligible for the playoffs (seventh different winner of the season). Some proper names uncertain from auto-captions: 'Charlie Herkis' also rendered Perkins/Harkins/hercus; 'Mike Sobanovski', 'Chris Zofeld', 'David Feit' (captioned 'David fight'), and 'Jorge Rincon' are heavily garbled best guesses. Alan Vaught and wife Lori are league admins. Booth once misattributed Burke as '728' (he is the 753; 728 is Tim Pope). Full finishing order beyond top 5 read out at ~1:55:51 (6951s). Ricky Whittenburg noted as outgoing league sponsor (DD Race Graphics / Keller Williams), replaced by Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"s7i9qyM-0-0":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson started the 60-lap Spring Jam 200 from pole, but Chris Goans took command within the opening laps while points leader Dillon Bryant disappeared after an internet failure. Goans built his first-half advantage by skipping tires on the opening stop, then pitted immediately before the scheduled lap-31 competition caution and cycled back to the front for the restart. In the final cycle, Goans again declined tires while Jacob Alesia fitted fresh rubber, creating a late chase in which Alesia cut a lead of more than five seconds to under two. Contact with the spinning John Gallagher on the final lap halted Alesia's charge, and Goans won at Watkins Glen ahead of Alesia and Jack Dixon.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Jacob Alesia","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1630,"title":"Robertson leads the Watkins Glen start","summary":"Pole-sitter Trevor Robertson gets through Turn 1 cleanly with Chris Goans and Dillon Bryant immediately behind as the 31-truck field begins 60 laps.","tags":["trevor-robertson","chris-goans","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1682,"title":"Osborne spins on the opening lap","summary":"Jonathan Osborne loses the truck in the carousel and brushes the inside barrier, but avoids major damage and rejoins at the rear.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1830,"title":"Goans takes control from Robertson","summary":"Goans clears Robertson within the opening four laps and begins building the race's first meaningful advantage.","tags":["chris-goans","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2256,"title":"Bryant's internet failure ends a fast run","summary":"After blinking heavily near the front, Bryant loses his connection and is removed to pit road, ending the points leader's race.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"mechanical"},{"t":2477,"title":"Vaught makes an extraordinary save","summary":"John McAdam gets alongside Kyle Vaught and their doors touch; Vaught is unsettled by the rumble strip, uses the wall to steady the truck, and somehow continues.","tags":["kyle-vaught","john-mcadam"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":2897,"title":"The undercut puts Dixon ahead of Alesia","summary":"Jack Dixon's earlier stop cycles him ahead of Alesia, but Alesia's tires are three laps newer and he pressures Dixon through traffic before completing the pass.","tags":["jack-dixon","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3108,"title":"Goans opens six seconds without changing tires","summary":"Goans retains the lead after stopping on lap 18 for fuel only, while every other driver in the top 12 takes tires and Alesia begins reducing the gap.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3730,"title":"Goans flips the competition-caution cycle","summary":"With pit road about to close, Goans stops at the end of lap 28; Alesia stays out, crosses the line to begin lap 31, and triggers the scheduled competition caution.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4394,"title":"Goans leads the second-half restart","summary":"The pre-caution stop cycles Goans back to the front, and he launches ahead of Robertson and Dustyn Eaton when the field returns to green.","tags":["chris-goans","trevor-robertson","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4513,"title":"Alesia's bold move sends Adamson around","summary":"Alesia dives shallow beside Mike Adamson; Adamson brakes harder to avoid the No. 31, spins, and tangles briefly with Scott Rooney before rejoining in ninth.","tags":["jacob-alicia","mike-adamson","scott-rooney"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5800,"title":"Fresh tires fuel Alesia's final charge","summary":"Goans skips tires on his final stop and cycles to a lead of more than five seconds, while Alesia's fresh set lets him cut the margin to under two seconds by the white flag.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6350,"title":"Goans survives the chase and wins","summary":"Gallagher spins directly ahead of Alesia on the final lap and Alesia clips him, restoring Goans' margin; Goans finishes the lap cleanly to win ahead of Alesia and Dixon.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia","john-gallagher","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":790,"quote":"There's no hiding, no managing, no saving. You have to attack or you're going to get eaten alive here.","context":"Alan Vaught describes the rhythm and precision Watkins Glen demands","gold":4},{"t":2477,"quote":"Hang on to it. Wow, that is an unbelievable save.","context":"The call as Kyle Vaught catches his truck after contact with McAdam","gold":5},{"t":4080,"quote":"Keep it on the track, baby. That's all I can do.","context":"Kyle Vaught states his second-half road-course plan","gold":4},{"t":4394,"quote":"This is where the rubber meets the road. Second half.","context":"Goans brings the field back to green after the competition caution","gold":4},{"t":5337,"quote":"Chris Goans looking like SVG here, really putting on a road-course clinic tonight.","context":"The booth watches Goans control the final pit sequence","gold":4},{"t":6350,"quote":"Putting on a clinic tonight is Chris Goans in that number one machine, bringing it home at the top step of the podium.","context":"The Watkins Glen winning call","gold":5},{"t":6467,"quote":"I felt good all night. I was a little worried there about Jacob at the end.","context":"Winner Goans reflects on Alesia's late charge","gold":4},{"t":6785,"quote":"Not if I want to avoid penalties.","context":"Jacob Alesia declines to give post-race shout-outs","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 14, Round 12 at Watkins Glen according to seasons_map.json. This road-course race used local cautions only, except for a single planned competition caution when the leader began lap 31. The broadcast and interviews explicitly confirm the Goans-Alesia-Dixon podium and name all 31 starters. The results overlay ambiguously reversed Dillon Bryant and Dion Jones in 30th/31st, so no precise final position is asserted for either; Bryant explicitly reported an internet failure. Roster canonical 'Dustyn Eaton' is used for captions calling the No. 14 'Dustyn Eaton.' Transcript timestamps end within the 7,151-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"S9GnRseUSrQ":{"recap":"Jeremiah Burke won VRL's 40-lap Daytona road-course race by surviving an early multi-car battle and then executing the best fuel-and-tire plan. Pole-sitter Alan Vaught overcooked Turn 1 at the start and later hit the tire barrier, but rallied methodically to finish second. Early leader Greg Klein lost 40 seconds to a pit-entry speeding penalty and later had to save fuel, falling to fourth behind Jim Ott. Burke built enough of a cushion to absorb his own late mistake and take the win by roughly 11 seconds over Vaught, with Ott completing the podium.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Alan Vaught","Jim Ott"],"moments":[{"t":1683,"title":"Vaught overshoots Turn 1 from pole","summary":"Alan Vaught cooks the brakes into the opening turn and runs wide, handing the lead to Greg Klein while Jim Ott slots in behind.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1794,"title":"Klein launches off a turtle","summary":"Klein clips one of Daytona's tall chicane curbs and lifts onto two wheels, yet keeps the car straight to lead the opening lap.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":1872,"title":"Vaught hits the tire barrier","summary":"Vaught locks the brakes at the transition back to the oval and slides into the tire barrier, adding another setback to his opening run.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2010,"title":"Klein's grass excursion reshuffles the lead","summary":"Klein makes an evasive trip through the grass, allowing Ott and Burke past; Burke carries the better momentum when both hit the next chicane curbs.","tags":["greg-cline","jim-ott","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3203,"title":"Burke baits Klein into a pit-road penalty","summary":"Burke and Klein charge pit entry side by side, but iRacing posts Klein for speeding and assigns a costly 40-second hold.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":4085,"title":"Ott loses time in the final chicane","summary":"Jim Ott fails to slow enough for the final chicane and must serve a slowdown, allowing Burke's lead to grow.","tags":["jim-ott","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"mistake"},{"t":4698,"title":"Vaught muscles past Fite","summary":"Vaught races David Feit side by side through the dangerous kink, then makes door contact in the second horseshoe and takes the position.","tags":["jess-vaught","david-fite"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5880,"title":"Vaught halves Burke's late lead","summary":"Vaught's quick closing laps cut Burke's margin from nearly 12 seconds to under six and a half before Burke stabilizes the gap.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":6217,"title":"Burke begins the final clean lap","summary":"Burke takes the white flag and carefully negotiates the horseshoes, kink, and oval transition with Vaught still more than ten seconds behind.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":6469,"title":"Burke conquers the Daytona road course","summary":"Jeremiah Burke clears the last chicane and wins; Vaught completes his comeback in second and Jim Ott finishes third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","jim-ott"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1012,"quote":"Those turtles are everywhere.","context":"The booth introduces Daytona's towering chicane curbs as the night's central hazard.","gold":2},{"t":1426,"quote":"Do a shot every time the mouth runs off the track.","context":"Russ Endicott's chat challenge aimed at Dave Mayberry.","gold":5},{"t":3568,"quote":"Florida woman, tired of her man's behavior, arrested for throwing a raw steak at the better partner.","context":"A Florida-news tangent during the long green-flag run.","gold":5},{"t":6469,"quote":"The 753 of Jeremiah Burke picking up the win here from Daytona.","context":"The live checkered-flag call.","gold":5},{"t":7219,"quote":"To me it kind of looked like nobody wanted to win that dang thing.","context":"Burke summarizes the mistake-filled race in his winner interview.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The post-race results and interviews explicitly establish Burke, Vaught, and Ott as the podium. At the stripe the announcer briefly says Vaught crossed in 'third,' then immediately identifies Ott as third; the later official rundown confirms Vaught second. Klein reported a 40-second pit-speeding penalty and a final fuel deficit. Only 13 starters were listed, and 11 were said to finish.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"SPl2-VLn4z8":{"recap":"The Richmond Rumble packed roughly 38 trucks onto the three-quarter-mile Richmond short track for 200 laps of beating and banging, and it turned into a caution fest almost immediately with a lap-one wreck that left Jeffrey Johnson's truck hung up on the wall. Alan Vaught controlled restart after restart through the first half while the wrecks stacked up, including a halfway-restart Big One that sent Robert Jordan tumbling and a ten-truck 'trucks flipping' melee with around 30 to go. Tim Pope won the one-lap stage shootout at lap 100, and multiple drivers — including Dion Jones, Todd Smith, Jack Dixon and Michael Everidge — were disqualified on the 25-incident-point limit. Saving a fresh set of tires for the end, Pope ran down leader Vaught on the green-white-checkered and beat him to the line by five hundredths of a second, with Andrew Player completing the podium and both front-runners praising each other's clean racing. Hard-charger Jeremiah Burke climbed 29 spots to finish fifth.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Alan Vaught","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":1417,"title":"Lap-One Chaos: Truck Stuck on the Wall","summary":"Trevor Robertson's 64 wrecked off turn 2 on the opening lap and blocked the track; Jeffrey Johnson's Home Depot 20 got hit, rolled over the barrels and hung up on the wall for the first caution before lap 2.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeffrey-johnson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1684,"title":"Restart Pileup Turns Richmond Into a Parking Lot","summary":"Everidge clipped Mayberry into a spin off turn 4 and the checkup behind snowballed into a multi-truck pileup — the booth's verdict: 'that turned into a parking lot pretty quick.'","tags":["dave-mayberry","mike-everage","chris-zofeld","cody-tarrant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2702,"title":"Jack the Ripper Spears the Inside Wall","summary":"Pre-race favorite Jack 'the Ripper' Dixon got tight with the 1 truck and hit the angled inside wall dead-on at lap 40, taking serious front-end damage.","tags":["jack-dixon","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3641,"title":"Emig's Wild Ride, Long's Engine Lets Go","summary":"David Emig went for a wild ride up into the pink 5 of Jonah Long, who blew his engine and had to be towed; Emig couldn't get his truck refired.","tags":["david-emig","jonah-long"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4914,"title":"One-Lap Stage Shootout at Lap 100","summary":"Race control gave the field a one-lap sprint to settle the stage at lap 100 and Tim Pope beat teammate Jeremiah Burke to the stripe for the stage win, Kilgore third.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5224,"title":"The Big One at Halfway","summary":"On the restart after halfway, Burke snapped sideways, the 18 climbed into him, and the pit-entry barrels collected a wall of trucks — Robert Jordan went for a tumble as turn 4 became 'a parking lot.'","tags":["jeremiah-burke","robert-jordan","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5583,"title":"Dog Pile Against the Wall","summary":"Sobanovski missed his braking point and got into Austin Paul, stacking the 3, 14 and 8 against the wall; Dion Jones was disqualified at the incident limit and meatball flags flew for Paul, Sobanovski and Osborne.","tags":["mike-sobanovski","austin-paul","cody-tarrant","jonathan-osborne","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6593,"title":"Curse of the Broadcaster Strikes","summary":"Seconds after the booth hyped Russ Kilgore's charge, Oxendine got spun in a bumpers-not-lining-up netcode tangle and Cody Tarrant went for a hard ride up the track into the outside wall.","tags":["josh-oxendine","cody-tarrant"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7217,"title":"Trucks Flipping: The Ten-Truck Big One","summary":"'We got trucks flipping!' — Kilgore and Adamson touched in a netcode moment on the restart and roughly ten trucks piled in, Tarrant pinballing through the mess and Dustyn Eaton slamming the inside wall.","tags":["russ-kilgore","mike-adamson","cody-tarrant","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8165,"title":"Hot Mic on Discord Leaks Tire Secrets","summary":"The booth's lesson of the night: don't share your key-up button with Discord — Cody Tarrant accidentally broadcast exactly how many tire sets he had left.","tags":["cody-tarrant"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":8281,"title":"Late Melee Forces a Green-White-Checkered","summary":"With five to go Oxendine split the 6 and 28 in turn 4 and spun them both, knotting up Klein and Kuehl behind; Kilgore saved it with two wheels off the ground and the race went to a green-white-checkered.","tags":["josh-oxendine","austin-reeves","george-rincon","greg-cline","kelly-keel","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8521,"title":"Pope Beats Vaught by 0.05 at the Line","summary":"On the green-white-checkered, Tim Pope used 10-lap-fresher tires to run down Alan Vaught and edged him on the outside by five hundredths of a second as a wreck erupted behind them; Andrew Player grabbed the final podium spot.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1364,"quote":"Well, he's a real spy — I may not make it through this race.","context":"joking that Mike 'The Spy' Sobanovski's cover was blown during driver intros","gold":3},{"t":1817,"quote":"Nothing you can do other than hit your brakes and pray someone's not going to come on down to you.","context":"replaying the wall of trucks in the early restart pileup","gold":3},{"t":5235,"quote":"Tons of trucks in the barrels at pit entry — it's a parking lot in turn four!","context":"calling the Big One on the halfway restart","gold":4},{"t":5746,"quote":"What do you always say? Don't let the truth get in the way of a good story.","context":"the booth confessing they guess at wreck causes and love a little controversy","gold":4},{"t":7217,"quote":"Oh, we got trucks flipping, oh my goodness... ten trucks involved!","context":"the ten-truck Big One with about 30 laps to go","gold":4},{"t":8165,"quote":"Make sure that your key-up button is different than your Discord... you'll tell people how many sets of tires you got left.","context":"after Cody Tarrant leaked his tire count over an open mic","gold":4},{"t":8521,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets and throw inhibition out the window — it's green white checker racing time here from Richmond!","context":"sending the field off on the final restart","gold":5},{"t":8590,"quote":"What a great finish right there — five hundredths of a second between Pope and Vaught.","context":"immediately after the photo finish","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race: NASCAR Trucks at Richmond Raceway, 200 laps, ~38-truck field, aired 2022-10-20. Winner and full finishing order clearly stated on air (rundown at ~2:39:23; margin of victory 0.05s stated at 2:23:10). Several names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'David Feit' (#1) may itself be a caption garble of the real surname; 'Andrew Cauthen' (#10) heard as coffin/carthan/cauthon/cotton/Carson; 'Charlie Herkis' (#83) once read as 'Perkins'; 'Chris Zofeld' (#99), 'Gary Godsey' (#50), 'Dustyn Eaton' (#14), 'Robert Shipman' (#58, also 'Chipman'), and 'David Emig' (#2, also 'Emmett/emik') are uncertain spellings. League admin Lori Vaught (Alan Vaught's wife) was praised repeatedly but is not a driver or broadcaster. Teams referenced: Limitless Motorsports (Pope, Burke, Adamson), Vigilante Force (Vaught, Klein, Mayberry), Team Orangutan (Kelly, Wade), Wicked Loose Racing (Tony Pope), Sim Spec Esports (Tarrant).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"svk_62XS6ZI":{"recap":"The Alabama Exorcism 213, Season 13's 80-lap Talladega round, opened with a single early caution but otherwise became a green-flag drafting and pit-entry contest. The first pit cycle split the 30-truck field into multiple packs, while a later pit-road error and penalty dropped title contender Chris Goans off the lead lap. A chaotic final entry saw Kelly Kuehl spin separately while Kyle Vaught hit the inside wall and knocked championship leader Dillon Bryant into the grass, leaving a compact group to settle the race. Albert Anderson led at the white flag and, with a perfectly timed push from teammate Tom Barish through the tri-oval, beat Trevor Robertson to the line; Barish finished third after declining to abandon Anderson's bumper.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Trevor Robertson","Tom Barish"],"moments":[{"t":1243,"title":"Rooney brings 30 trucks to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Scott Rooney leads Jacob Alesia to the start as the field observes the no-three-wide rule for the opening lap.","tags":["scott-rooney","jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1456,"title":"The field stacks three-wide","summary":"The pack fans out three-wide several rows deep, with an outside-wall scrape providing an early warning of how little room remains.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1476,"title":"Everage and Vaught trigger the lone caution","summary":"Michael Everage comes down across Kyle Vaught, spins, and saves the truck with little damage, but the incident brings out the race's only actual caution.","tags":["mike-everage","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2006,"title":"Three lanes tighten at the front","summary":"After the restart, the leaders run three-wide and nearly make it four as Jonathan Osborne searches for space in the outside lane.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3014,"title":"The first pit group executes a clean land rush","summary":"A large group including Kuehl, Anderson, Bryant, Robertson, and Osborne dives onto pit road together and makes a remarkably clean entrance.","tags":["kelly-keel","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3079,"title":"The second pit group wrecks into Dixon","summary":"The remaining lead pack charges pit entry; a sliding No. 12 hits Jack Dixon and breaks the field into distinct drafting groups.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4173,"title":"Klein spins off the racing surface without a yellow","summary":"Greg Klein gets pinched and spins below the racing surface while the whole pack checks up, yet iRacing leaves the race green.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":4243,"title":"Goans overshoots his stall and takes a penalty","summary":"Championship contender Chris Goans loses control of his pit entry, overshoots his box, and is held, dropping him alone off the lead draft and eventually a lap down.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4388,"title":"Bryant's group takes command","summary":"After the mid-race stops cycle through, Dillon Bryant leads Anderson, Robertson, Goodenough, Player, and Kuehl in an efficient six-truck front group.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","andrew-player","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4983,"title":"Barish's chase group rejoins the leaders","summary":"Tom Barish, Kyle Vaught, Osborne, and Alesia close from more than a second back, catch the draft, and restore a larger pack for the final fuel stop.","tags":["tom-barish","kyle-vaught","jonathan-osborne","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":5441,"title":"Pit-road chaos eliminates Bryant's winning chance","summary":"At the final stop, Kuehl spins on his own while Vaught locks the rear tires, hits the inside wall, and bounces into Bryant, sending the points leader through the grass and into a 40-second unsafe-entry hold.","tags":["kelly-keel","kyle-vaught","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5822,"title":"Barish pushes Anderson to the Talladega win","summary":"Anderson leads at the white, Robertson builds momentum on the bottom, but Barish stays committed to his teammate and delivers the tri-oval push that carries Anderson to victory.","tags":["albert-anderson","trevor-robertson","tom-barish"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1211,"quote":"Sometimes the juice is worth the squeeze.","context":"The booth jokes that a start-at-the-back penalty is less painful at Talladega","gold":3},{"t":3079,"quote":"Here they come. Land rush... Oh no, wrecked into Dixon.","context":"The call as the second large pack charges the first green-flag pit entry","gold":4},{"t":4695,"quote":"When you get that, it's like you hit turbo mode.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg explains Barish's chase group finally grabbing the lead draft","gold":3},{"t":5580,"quote":"Pit road is killing drivers tonight.","context":"League admin Lori's chat message summarized by the booth after the final pit-entry crash","gold":4},{"t":5844,"quote":"Albert's got no help... Albert's going to get pushed back out in the front. He's going to win!","context":"The frantic tri-oval call as Barish reconnects with Anderson","gold":5},{"t":6262,"quote":"I was determined that I was just going to stay tucked up behind Albert and go.","context":"Tom Barish explains why he chose the team win over a late move for himself","gold":4},{"t":6756,"quote":"That last push he gave me there coming to the line is what got me the win.","context":"Winner Albert Anderson credits Barish in the post-race interview","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season map identifies this as Season 13, Round 11, Alabama Exorcism 213 at Talladega. The broadcast explicitly says Anderson won, Robertson was second, and Barish third, and reads the complete 30-place finishing order at about 1:39:54. The booth and Anderson's interview confirm only one actual caution; the Greg Klein spin and both final pit-entry incidents stayed green. The identity of the No. 12 that slid into Dixon during the first pit cycle is not stated clearly enough to assign, so that moment names only Dixon. Canonical roster and override spellings were used for Chris Goans, John Schoenbachler, Tom Barish, Michael Everage, Kyle Vaught, and Andrew Coffin. Transcript timestamps end at 1:54:44 (6884 seconds), within the 6922-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"sYtVPpou5Rc":{"recap":"Tim Pope delivered a strategy clinic in Operation Brickyard, using clean air, precise pit timing, and tire management to win by more than eight seconds. Pole-sitter Craig Goodenough led early, while front-row starter Trevor Robertson fell to the rear after jumping the initial start but raced all the way back to fourth. The race had only two cautions: Dave Mayberry's side-draft contact blew Austin Paul over, and Robertson's attempted pass later triggered a crash that ended Dustyn Eaton's night. Dillon Bryant delayed his last stop, charged through the field on fresher tires, and passed Derek Welch on the final lap for second, while Pope was already out of reach.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Dillon Bryant","Derek Welch"],"moments":[{"t":860,"title":"Goodenough leads a traditional 33-truck field","summary":"Craig Goodenough and Trevor Robertson lead a 33-truck Indianapolis grid to green, matching the traditional Indianapolis 500 field size.","tags":["craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1073,"title":"Robertson is penalized for jumping the start","summary":"Replay shows Robertson launch fractionally early; the black-flag pass-through drops Monday's practice winner from the front row to last.","tags":["trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"penalty"},{"t":1397,"title":"Kuehl destroys the truck without a yellow","summary":"Kelly Kuehl clips the wall, then hits it again as the damaged steering worsens; he keeps the crippled truck away from traffic but retires without a caution.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":1641,"title":"Mayberry's side draft blows Paul over","summary":"Dave Mayberry catches Austin Paul's left rear at the fastest point of the track, turning the No. 3 into a blowover and producing the first caution.","tags":["dave-mayberry","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2891,"title":"Robertson move triggers the second caution","summary":"Robertson dives beneath John Gallagher with no room left; contact collects Dustyn Eaton, Andrew Coffin, and Michael Everage, ending Eaton's race and damaging Robertson.","tags":["trevor-robertson","john-gallagher","dustin-eaton","andrew-cauthan","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3255,"title":"Bittner's older-tire restart bottlenecks the field","summary":"Josh Bittner controls the restart after an alternate stop, while Jeremiah Burke's older tires stack the outside lane in front of Pope.","tags":["josh-bittner","jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4931,"title":"Pope takes command of the final cycle","summary":"Pope's early final stop and consistently quick laps leave him clear as the staggered pit cycle resolves, while Bryant stays out hoping for a caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5686,"title":"Bryant charges from traffic to the podium fight","summary":"On fresher tires Bryant erases the gap to Robertson, Goodenough, and Welch, reaching second-place contention with two laps left.","tags":["dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":5896,"title":"Bryant steals second on the final lap","summary":"Bryant dives beneath Welch on the white-flag lap and hangs on despite washing wide, taking second from the long-run contender.","tags":["dylan-bryant","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5928,"title":"Pope completes the Indianapolis rout","summary":"Tim Pope cruises through the final corner to win by more than eight seconds, with Bryant second and Welch third.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","derek-welch"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":772,"quote":"It'll be a whole lot more fun watching it than it would be doing it.","context":"The booth imagines a traditional three-wide Indianapolis start for the trucks.","gold":5},{"t":1603,"quote":"It's toast. Says we're done.","context":"Kuehl confirms the terminal wheel damage during an in-race interview.","gold":2},{"t":5928,"quote":"Tim Pope at Indianapolis with a good old-fashioned butt whooping here tonight.","context":"The live finish call after Pope's dominant strategy run.","gold":5},{"t":6453,"quote":"If you can't beat Pope straight up, you got to switch it up some.","context":"Bryant explains his alternate strategy in the runner-up interview.","gold":5},{"t":6605,"quote":"Strategy was to try to get up front, clean air.","context":"Pope summarizes the key to his win.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish call, podium interviews, and final results explicitly confirm Pope, Bryant, and Welch. The broadcast says only two cautions occurred. Roster mapping is applied to Andrew Coffin despite the grid caption 'Andrew Cawan'; Sean McDonnell is also called Shawn/John in captions, but the final results identify him as Sean McDonnell.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"SzM9aoOozQw":{"recap":"Non-playoff driver Tim Pope controlled the inaugural playoff round at Gateway, repeatedly mastering the outside-lane restarts and winning ahead of championship contender Jeremiah Burke. Early pole-sitter Sean McDonnell spun out of the lead without hitting anything and recovered to finish fourth, while a major crash sent Jorge Rincon flipping over Greg Klein. Tire conservation became decisive late: Josh Bittner saved a set, charged 19 positions from the rear, and reached third. Two late cautions forced the race through both its scheduled finish and the league's sole green-white-checkered attempt before Pope finally drove away from Burke and Bittner.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1089,"title":"McDonnell leads Gateway to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Sean McDonnell and Tim Pope launch the 24-truck playoff opener, with Jeremiah Burke and Jonathan Osborne immediately in pursuit.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1192,"title":"McDonnell spins out of the lead","summary":"Sean McDonnell's rear steps out in Turns 3 and 4; he slides through the grass, saves the truck, and begins a long recovery drive.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1363,"title":"Meeting of the Davids brings the first yellow","summary":"Contact between David Feit and David Kelly turns the No. 49 and produces the race's first caution.","tags":["david-fite","david-kelly"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2565,"title":"Evans drills Coffin at pit exit","summary":"Earl Evans loses control exiting Turn 2 just as playoff driver Andrew Coffin leaves pit road, leaving Coffin no chance to avoid a heavy collision.","tags":["earl-evans","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3041,"title":"Rincon goes full Simone Biles","summary":"Daniel Baker gets loose and a large pileup follows; Jorge Rincon launches over Greg Klein and tumbles repeatedly before coming to rest.","tags":["daniel-baker","mike-adamson","george-rincon","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3672,"title":"Stage scramble ends in another crash","summary":"As the first stage freezes, Greg Klein gets loose and makes contact with Jonathan Osborne, while Trevor Robertson spins through the grass and hits the wall trying to avoid them.","tags":["greg-cline","jonathan-osborne","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":4889,"title":"Vaught spins teammate Mayberry","summary":"A speed difference through the middle of the corner leads Alan Vaught to clip Dave Mayberry, sending Mayberry hard into the outside wall.","tags":["jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5609,"title":"Adamson crash ends Eaton's race","summary":"Sean McDonnell holds his lane as Mike Adamson pinches the battle; the resulting crash sends Alan Vaught and Dustyn Eaton hard into the wall, with Eaton's engine expiring.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","mike-adamson","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5983,"title":"Fresh-tire Bittner slices through traffic","summary":"Josh Bittner uses his saved tire set to make repeated three-wide passes and race from 13th into podium contention during the final run.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":6462,"title":"Kuehl spin consumes the first overtime try","summary":"Mike Adamson taps Kelly Kuehl's rear quarter before the white flag, triggering the only available green-white-checkered reset.","tags":["mike-adamson","kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6774,"title":"Pope wins the final Gateway shootout","summary":"Pope clears Burke on the last restart, survives to the white flag, and drives away to win over Burke and hard-charger Bittner.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1347,"quote":"A meeting of the Davids, and both of them got Goliath.","context":"The booth describes the first caution between David Feit and David Kelly.","gold":5},{"t":3132,"quote":"That car went full Simone Biles out there doing some Olympic-style flipping gymnastics.","context":"Reaction to Jorge Rincon's long barrel roll.","gold":5},{"t":4900,"quote":"I didn't have any part of this.","context":"A broadcaster quickly disclaims the curse after Vaught spins Mayberry.","gold":5},{"t":6704,"quote":"Burke is hanging around. He is lurking.","context":"The booth weighs contenders before the last restart.","gold":2},{"t":6786,"quote":"Timothy Pope winning here at Gateway.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live checkered-flag call, interviews, and results explicitly identify Pope, Burke, and Bittner as the podium. The captions and results identify a distinct Dustyn Eaton, although roster.json has no matching canonical entry; that participant is retained as captioned and needs owner review.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"T7Og7iBZSaY":{"recap":"Thirty-seven trucks took on the Monster Mile for VRL's Monster Mash at Dover, with reigning champion Andrew Player on pole and Alan Vaught stealing the lead on the opening lap. Ricky Whittenburg ripped off the fastest laps of the race in clean air to grab the stage-one points at lap 76, but the second half dissolved into carnage: Timmy Bates flipped in a backstretch Big One, Whittenburg was tapped into a tumble off the SAFER barrier, and a half-the-field 'parking lot' pileup reset the running order late. Josh Buettner, who saved tires all night, inherited the lead through the late caution cycle and fended off Mike Adamson and Jonathan Osborne across a string of restarts. The green-white-checkered attempt ended when Osborne slammed the outside wall, freezing the field and handing Buettner the win — up 20 spots on the day — ahead of Alan Vaught and Jack 'the Ripper' Dixon, in Buettner's first VRL race alongside new 'Ain't Dead Yet' teammates Tim Pope and Ricky Whittenburg.","winner":"Josh Buettner","podium":["Josh Buettner","Alan Vaught","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1828,"title":"First yellow: Adamson spins after 21 green laps","summary":"Mike Adamson goes around for the night's first caution after light contact from the 31 — contact the booth chalked up to 'net code that just kept net coding.'","tags":["mike-adamson","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2876,"title":"Three-wide gamble ends in mayhem around Osborne","summary":"Vaught threads it three wide, but Jonah Long tries to follow him through, runs out of room, and slams the back of Osborne's 81 — earning a meatball flag.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonah-long","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2912,"title":"Kuehl punted into the inside wall","summary":"An accordion checkup leaves Dustyn Eaton nowhere to go on fresh tires; he drills Kelly Kuehl, who goes for a wild ride straight into the inside wall — 'right in the radiator.'","tags":["kelly-keel","dustin-eaton","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3400,"title":"Save of the night for Dustin Wade","summary":"Wade's 68 snaps nearly past 90 degrees sideways, clips the apron, and somehow gathers it all back up with no damage — 'awesome save' from the booth.","tags":["dustin-wade","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3770,"title":"Whittenburg rips off stage one","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg runs the fastest lap of the race in the wide open and crosses the line at lap 76 to take the stage caution and the big 10 points.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4615,"title":"Chan the Man's Dr. Squatch infomercial","summary":"A mid-race driver interview turns into a full soap sales pitch for the Dr. Squatch truck (painted by Ricky Whittenburg), complete with the affiliate code on the hood — 'use that for purchases over 20 or more you get ten dollars off.'","tags":["chandler-paul","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4841,"title":"The Big One: Timmy Bates goes upside down","summary":"Dustin Wade gets loose off the corner and pounds the inside wall, Gallagher is trapped in the middle three-wide, and Timmy Bates flips upside down while Mayberry's engine starts smoking.","tags":["timmy-bates","dustin-wade","john-gallagher","albert-anderson","dave-mayberry","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5534,"title":"Whittenburg ramps the SAFER barrier and tumbles","summary":"Mike Adamson barely clips the back of the 55, sending Whittenburg backwards into the wall — the truck ramps up and over in a tumble, then takes a hard shot from Kelly Kuehl, leaving Ricky with a smoking engine and heavy damage.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","mike-adamson","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5869,"title":"The parking lot: half the field wrecks","summary":"Contact from Dixon's 48 into Pope's 27 on the restart triggers absolute chaos down the backstretch — 'we got half the field involved in this one boys' — a few million dollars of damage headed to pit road.","tags":["timothy-pope","jack-dixon","j-r-hollingsworth","daniel-baker","trevor-robertson","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6300,"title":"Dale Adamson body-slammed into the outside wall","summary":"Klein's 92 gets under the 746 coming off the corner; Dale Adamson is body slammed into the outside wall, breaks his suspension on the inside wall, and comes back across in front of the pack, collecting the 82, 64, 31, and 18.","tags":["greg-cline","dale-adamson","mike-everage","trevor-robertson","j-r-hollingsworth","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7136,"title":"Rincon spins with three to go — overtime","summary":"With three laps left, Rincon comes down on the 98, gets loose, and Albert Anderson 'finishes it off' — the yellow sends the race to a green-white-checkered, and Anderson is black-flagged as incident limits start to bite.","tags":["george-rincon","mike-taylor","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7446,"title":"GWC: Osborne walls it, Buettner wins under yellow","summary":"On the green-white-checkered attempt, Buettner's 84 and Osborne's 81 race side by side for the lead until Osborne pounds the outside wall off the corner — the caution freezes the field and Josh Buettner takes the Monster Mile win over Vaught and Dixon.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":878,"quote":"This concrete surface is like sandpaper, it's like a cheese grater, it's gonna eat these tires up.","context":"pre-race preview of the Monster Mile's abrasive surface","gold":3},{"t":1817,"quote":"Specifically it tells Mark Zuckerberg to go stick it where the sun don't shine.","context":"explaining what hitting the like button really does","gold":4},{"t":3175,"quote":"They have an Air Force Base, a race track and some beach front property owned by our president, that's pretty much it.","context":"the booth's complete tourism guide to Delaware","gold":4},{"t":5291,"quote":"This is like shooting dice in Waco — gonna roll snake eyes every time.","context":"after the Big One collects Timmy Bates and half the midpack","gold":4},{"t":5574,"quote":"There is a safer barrier out there, but again it's safer for the drivers, not the trucks.","context":"as Whittenburg's 55 ramps the wall and tumbles","gold":3},{"t":5869,"quote":"Oh this one's a parking lot! Timothy Pope sideways — oh we got half the field involved in this one boys!","context":"the live call as the backstretch Big One erupts","gold":5},{"t":6318,"quote":"Chandler, what's better than four tires, guys? Eight.","context":"deadpan wisdom as the 92 uses up the 746 in the wall","gold":3},{"t":7446,"quote":"Time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets and throw inhibition out the window, here we go.","context":"setting up the green-white-checkered finish","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Race ended under caution on the green-white-checkered attempt (field frozen); booth stressed all results were unofficial pending race-admin verification. Several proper names are uncertain from auto-captions: 'David Feit' (#1), 'Justin Riehle' (#37, also heard as 'Dustin really'), 'Dustyn Eaton' (#14, booth called him 'Dustin with a Y' to distinguish from Dustin Wade), and winner Josh Buettner's name appears as 'Bittner/spitner/buettner'. Lori is the league race admin (race control), mentioned often but not a driver. The broadcast sponsor Blue Fox Properties belongs to Dave Mayberry, who also drove the #29. Full finishing order was read out at ~2:26:30 (Buettner, Vaught, Dixon, Osborne, M. Adamson, C. Paul, Chipman, A. Paul, Coffin, Evans top 10).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"t9wtshcRYok":{"recap":"Championship Wednesday brought Tim Pope, Alan Vaught, Trevor Robertson, and hometown favorite Jeremiah Burke to Phoenix with the Season 6 title available over 150 laps. Burke's path was anything but clean. He spun while entering pit road, then stayed on old tires long enough to regain track position and eventually control the second half. Pope answered with the fastest recorded lap while the championship group worked through traffic and repeated cautions. Burke appeared to have built the decisive advantage until Kyle Vaught struck the pit-wall barrels with 18 laps remaining, erasing the gap. Contact between Albert Anderson and Mike Adamson produced another late reset. Pope then took the lead, but Jorge Rincon's spin forced the race's single green-white-checkered attempt. Pope and Burke stayed side by side through the final two laps. Burke edged ahead entering the last corners, overran the turn, and gave Pope the opening he needed. Pope won by two tenths of a second and became VRL's first two-time season champion. Burke finished second, and Robertson took third; all three positions have exact finish receipts. The race's defining swing was not simply the last corner, but the chain from Burke's early recovery to the caution that erased his lead and created one final direct fight for the championship.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":955,"title":"Championship Wednesday goes green — and yellow","summary":"Pope and Vaught go side by side into the dogleg as the title race goes green; rookie Kyle Vaught spins on his own two laps in for the night's first caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1777,"title":"iRacing asleep at the flagstand","summary":"Right-side contact with Alejandro Gonzalez sends Andrew Coffin bobbling into Dave Mayberry, collecting him — and no caution ever flies, leaving the booth stunned.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry","alejandro-gonzalez"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2209,"title":"Burke spins on pit road","summary":"Championship contender Jeremiah Burke gets too heavy on the brakes and spins on pit road, a mistake that forces him to stay out on old tires to regain track position.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2289,"title":"Dogleg double trouble","summary":"Jonathan Osborne goes sideways into the dogleg while, in a separate simultaneous wreck, Earl Evans gets loose off turn two and snags Albert Anderson.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","earl-evans","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2372,"title":"Cactus vs. cacti: the great booth debate","summary":"The booth spends two caution periods litigating the plural of cactus, complete with 'doing the googler' and English's improvised 'gaggle of cactus' ruling.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3922,"title":"Big wreck in the back at halfway","summary":"On the halfway restart Greg Klein checks up into Jonah Long and sends him around while Alejandro Gonzalez snaps hard into the outside wall.","tags":["jonah-long","greg-cline","alejandro-gonzalez"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4663,"title":"Klein pounds the far wall","summary":"Kyle Vaught loses a bumper on the inside wall, then he and Greg Klein tangle in the dogleg — Klein slams the outside wall with heavy suspension damage and parks it to avoid a caution.","tags":["greg-cline","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5765,"title":"Pope says 'excuse you' — fastest lap","summary":"Chasing the lead pack late, Tim Pope rips a 27.12 to steal the fastest lap of the race away from Alan Vaught, pushing the truck to the limit.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5853,"title":"The caution that changed everything","summary":"With 18 to go and Burke pulling away to a massive gap, rookie Kyle Vaught snags the pit-wall barrels — the yellow bunches the entire Championship 4 back together.","tags":["kyle-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6186,"title":"Former teammates tangle with four to go","summary":"Three wide off turn two, Albert Anderson drifts up and gets clipped by Mike Adamson — the former teammates wreck together and set up a frantic restart.","tags":["mike-adamson","albert-anderson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6468,"title":"Pope pounces, Rincon spun — one-shot GWC","summary":"Pope jumps the restart Burke didn't expect and takes the lead off turns one and two; behind them Jorge Rincon gets spun with a foot of 'net code' daylight to the 6, forcing VRL's single green-white-checkered attempt.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","george-rincon","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6766,"title":"Green-white-checkered for the championship — Pope by 0.2","summary":"All four title contenders restart in the top four and run side by side the entire GWC. Burke noses ahead by a door into turns three and four but sends it too hard, and Tim Pope wins the race and the championship by two tenths — VRL's first two-time champion.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1128,"quote":"It tastes like an Arnold Palmer with booze in it.","context":"Adam Turner's live Twisted Tea review from pit road","gold":3},{"t":1970,"quote":"The Coke people are using the metric system because they are the Communists.","context":"the booth spirals from Canadian fuel liters into Freedom Units","gold":4},{"t":2694,"quote":"That's the second one he's caused — he's going to be on double secret probation.","context":"rookie Kyle Vaught spins for his second self-caused caution","gold":3},{"t":3066,"quote":"It's a gaggle of cactus... I just made all that up too, I don't really know.","context":"English's ruling in the night-long cactus vs. cacti grammar debate","gold":4},{"t":5853,"quote":"It's like in Mario Kart when you're dropping the banana peels behind you — oh, yellows out! Oh, and this changes everything!","context":"the late caution interrupts the joke mid-sentence and erases Burke's lead","gold":4},{"t":5878,"quote":"If you're Jeremiah Burke, you're screaming 'why?'","context":"the late yellow wipes out Burke's massive gap with 18 to go","gold":3},{"t":6760,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on those drinking elements, throw inhibition out the window — championship racing here from Phoenix, the stars are shining.","context":"setting the stage for the one-shot green-white-checkered","gold":4},{"t":6818,"quote":"Burke by a door, by a nose... sent it too hard though, as the 27 of Timothy Pope picks up your race win and championship!","context":"the green-white-checkered finish decides the race and the title by 0.2 seconds","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 6 championship finale (150 laps, trucks, Phoenix); margin of victory 0.2s stated on air. Surname 'Vaught' for Jess and Kyle is inferred from garbled captions (vot/VA/fought — rhymes with 'fought'); the booth confirms Kyle is Jess's son. 'Jorge Rincon' is a best guess from wildly varied captions (ran con/ringcon/ran cone) — could be Rancone or Ranon. 'Dustyn' spelling inferred from the booth's recurring 'Dustin with a Y' joke. Ricky Whittenburg (and Pope teammate Josh) sat out ill and did not race; Whittenburg was credited for paint jobs in Robertson's interview. League run by Jess and wife Lori; broadcast on AAA Broadcasting; sponsors GC Cruise Travel (Greg Klein) and Blue Fox Properties (Dave Mayberry). Full finishing order was read on air (Pope, Burke, Robertson, Vaught, Dickerson, Osborne, McDonnell, Dixon, Player, Eaton, Rincon, Anderson, Long, Mayberry, Adamson, Evans, Gonzalez, Coffin, Gallagher, K. Vaught, Klein, Dobson).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"T_d8ceIZeVQ":{"recap":"Jacob Alesia entered the Season 13 finale at virtual Homestead-Miami Speedway leading Dillon Bryant by eight points and Chris Goans by nine, and left with everything — the race win and the championship. A cold-tire pileup off turn four on lap two, triggered when Kelly Kuehl plowed into Jack Dixon's 48 and collected Greg Klein, Scott Milner, and Jorge Rincon, brought out the only caution of the 133-lap race, which then ran green the rest of the way as a pure strategy battle. Alesia traded the lead through three green-flag pit cycles with Bryant, Goans, and long-run leaders Albert Anderson and Aaron Warren, absorbed Goans's lap-99 undercut bid, and pulled away to win by nearly five seconds. Goans finished second and Bryant third, with Andy Player fourth and pole sitter John Schoenbachler fifth. The title — Alesia's first in any VRL series — paid $300 cash on a night with over $800 on the line.","winner":"Jacob Alesia","podium":["Jacob Alesia","Chris Goans","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":978,"title":"Cold tires bite: lap-two pileup off turn four","summary":"One lap in, Kelly Kuehl got loose on cold tires exiting turn four and plowed into the left rear of Jack Dixon's 48, collecting Greg Klein, Scott Milner, and Jorge Rincon — moments after pole sitter John Schoenbachler clipped the wall up front. It was the only caution of the entire night.","tags":["kelly-keel","jack-dixon","greg-cline","scott-milner","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1255,"title":"Alesia launches on the lap-six restart","summary":"With control of the restart, championship leader Jacob Alesia got a great launch over the 51 and the 12 and cleared them into turn one to take command of the race.","tags":["jacob-alicia","dylan-bryant","john-schoenbachler"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2352,"title":"Goans runs down Bryant for the lead","summary":"Just before the first green-flag pit cycle, Chris Goans completed a run on Dillon Bryant to take over the lead, with all three title contenders playing the fuel-mileage game.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3190,"title":"Game of inches: Goans vs Bryant for second","summary":"The two title challengers went side by side for second, Bryant holding Goans down out of the corners until Goans carried the outside momentum and secured the position to go after leader Alesia.","tags":["chris-goans","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3521,"title":"Anderson rides the wall and saves it","summary":"Running in the top ten, Albert Anderson got loose off turn four, caught a piece of the wall, and reeled it back in — no worse for the wear as long as the wheels stayed straight.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4550,"title":"Goans gambles on a lap-99 undercut","summary":"Chris Goans pitted early at lap 99 trying to undercut the leaders, but Alesia answered and cycled back out still ahead — 'I did not expect that,' admitted the booth, and the champion's last real threat was neutralized.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4985,"title":"Crank It Up at full volume","summary":"The broadcast's signature Crank It Up segment dropped the commentary and let the virtual trucks roar around Homestead for three minutes of raw engine noise.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5240,"title":"Dixon and Adamson trade wall slaps for seventh","summary":"Fighting for seventh with 16 to go, Jack Dixon touched the outside wall, cutting the air off Mike Adamson, who drifted back to the high side and hit the wall himself.","tags":["jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5398,"title":"Osborne bounces off the fence late","summary":"Inside 12 to go, Jonathan Osborne's 81 slapped the wall twice while wall-riding for speed, with Chris Goans getting aero-tight behind him in traffic.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","chris-goans"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5754,"title":"Alesia takes the white and seals the crown","summary":"Jacob Alesia took the white flag with a near five-second lead and swept both the race win and the Season 13 championship — winning the race and the title in the same event, leaving nothing to chance.","tags":["jacob-alicia","chris-goans","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5908,"title":"'Fierce like a predator': the champion speaks","summary":"In his victory interview, Alesia said he came in feeling fierce like a predator and willing to explode his tires for half a tenth, then shouted out the league, sponsor Tow Call, his strategy chat, and his mom watching at home.","tags":["jacob-alicia"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":368,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream. This is VRN, your trusted leader in e-motorsports.","context":"the channel's opening sting before the broadcast","gold":4},{"t":540,"quote":"The progressive banked battlefield where champions are made and pretenders get exposed.","context":"Alan Vault introducing Homestead-Miami at the top of the show","gold":4},{"t":2572,"quote":"Superman throwing his cape out looking to track down Jacob Alicia.","context":"Dillon Bryant chasing the leader after the first pit cycle","gold":3},{"t":3400,"quote":"They're going to have to pry it from the vigilante's cold hands here if they want it.","context":"on the $800-plus prize pool up for grabs","gold":3},{"t":5630,"quote":"They should have a Homestead stripe kind of like they do Darlington, cuz we sure do use up that wall and scrape the paint off of it.","context":"watching the field wall-ride in the closing laps","gold":4},{"t":5784,"quote":"Jacob Alicia is your season 13 champion.","context":"the checkered-flag call at Homestead","gold":4},{"t":5928,"quote":"I came in feeling fierce like a predator and I came in willing to explode those tires if it meant getting another half of a tenth out of them.","context":"champion Jacob Alesia in his victory interview","gold":5},{"t":6202,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, and above all else, stay vigilant.","context":"Alan Vault's signature sign-off closing the season","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Alan Vault broadcast solo; regular co-host Ricky Whittenburg (captioned 'Whittenberg') was out with a family illness, and Lori — Alan's wife — handled race management, on-screen chat, and the $50 random-draw payout. Surnames are best guesses from rough auto-captions: 'Gomes' alternates with 'Gones' throughout; the pole sitter ranges from 'Shane Bacher' to 'Shambacher' to 'Bachler'; 'Andrew Coffin' also appears as Cawan/Cawin/Cawton; 'Jorge Rincon' appears as Rencon/Rickon/Ranc; 'Kelly Kuehl' is as heard. The only caution flew starting lap 2; the remaining ~130 laps ran green. Full results were read on air: Alesia, Gomes, Bryant, Player, Bachler, Dixon, Rooney, Warren, Adamson, Coffin, Mayberry, McAdam, Kilgore, Anderson, Osborne, Benfield, Ever, Williams, Dobson, Klein, Rincon, Gallagher, Kill, Milner.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"tadEyJk8iEc":{"recap":"Alan Vaught overcame pre-race packet loss and a start from pit road to win the Kansas 150, beating polesitter Tim Pope in a side-by-side drag race out of the final corner. Two early cautions gave Vaught the opportunity to rejoin the lead lap, after which Pope dominated the opening green run while Vaught methodically climbed from 23rd to the top three. On the final pit cycle Vaught gained almost a second on pit road, emerged alongside Pope, and took control as the leaders chased down long-stopping Russ Kilgore. Pope shadowed Vaught for roughly the final 20 laps and attempted a clean last-corner slingshot, but Vaught held the apron-side run to win; Jason Airson finished third.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Jason Airson"],"moments":[{"t":1454,"title":"Pope leads the Kansas field","summary":"Tim Pope starts from pole beside John Osborne, while points leader Alan Vaught joins from pit road after resolving connection trouble.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1486,"title":"Burke crashes on cold tires","summary":"Jeremiah Burke loses control into the outside wall on the opening lap, triggering a multi-car pileup that also catches Earl Evans and Greg Klein.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","earl-evans","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1602,"title":"Quick yellow rescues Vaught","summary":"The opening caution allows Vaught to catch the field and regain the lead lap after his pit-lane start.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":1903,"title":"Paul and Kuehl spark caution two","summary":"Chandler Paul scrapes the wall and comes across Kelly Kuehl, sending Russ Endicott onto his roof and collecting Andrew Coffin and Evans in a smoky pileup.","tags":["chandler-paul","kelly-keel","russ-endicott","andrew-cauthan","earl-evans"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2355,"title":"Pope rides the high line clear","summary":"Once the race settles into a long green run, Pope uses the lane near the wall to open a growing advantage over Mike Adamson.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":2988,"title":"Vaught climbs into third","summary":"By the first green-flag pit sequence, Vaught has gained 21 positions and runs third behind Pope and Adamson.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":3178,"title":"First pit cycle opens","summary":"With tires fading around lap 40, Pope, Vaught, Airson and the other leaders begin their first long-run stops while Dobson and Kuehl briefly collect bonus points up front.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson","greg-dobson","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":4392,"title":"Vaught wins the money stop","summary":"Pope and Vaught pit together for the final time; Vaught's stop is nearly a second quicker, putting them neck and neck as the order cycles.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4518,"title":"Vaught heads the four-car chase","summary":"Vaught leads Pope, Adamson and Airson as they erase Kilgore's alternate-strategy advantage with fewer than 20 laps remaining.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","mike-adamson","jason-airson","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":4820,"title":"Pope applies relentless pressure","summary":"With 10 laps left, Pope runs inches from Vaught's bumper through traffic, trying to force the leader into a mistake without making contact.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5177,"title":"Vaught wins the final-corner drag race","summary":"Pope dives through Turns 3 and 4 and draws alongside, but Vaught gets the stronger exit, drops toward the apron and wins; Airson takes third.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jason-airson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5177,"quote":"Drag racing to the line, the 33 getting a great run out of the corner, driving down to the apron and picking up the win.","context":"The booth calls Vaught's victory over Pope","gold":5},{"t":5390,"quote":"We had a good battle. I tore the wall down about 10 or 12 to go, and it killed my car.","context":"Tim Pope identifies the mistake that weakened his final challenge","gold":4},{"t":5533,"quote":"I got caught in both the yellow flags right off the bat, and when I went in the first time I forgot to check the fast repair.","context":"Random-draw driver Earl Evans explains his difficult race","gold":4},{"t":5659,"quote":"I don't even know how I did it. I thought he was going to get me in that last run.","context":"Alan Vaught reacts to surviving Pope's pressure","gold":5},{"t":5668,"quote":"I had packet loss and ended up starting from the pits, got a little fortunate it was a quick caution, and then went about my business getting the work done.","context":"Vaught recounts his recovery from pre-race connection trouble","gold":5},{"t":5783,"quote":"The thing with Tim is you cannot make a mistake.","context":"Vaught describes racing with Pope inches from his rear bumper","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete finishing order of 23 starters is read after the interviews. Jason Airson, Jeff Ottinger and Tony Polk use roster canonicals despite captions such as Jason Harrison, Jeff Hottinger and Tony Pope. David Feit is canonicalized from David Feit under the roster override. The broadcast explicitly describes two early cautions; the remainder ran green, making the two pit cycles and tire management decisive.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"tBIeO2RzD4M":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson led almost every lap outside the pit cycle and won the 60-lap Season 1 race on Watkins Glen's Cup layout. Jeremiah Burke used a perfectly timed stop immediately before the competition caution to inherit the lead, but Robertson reclaimed it around the outside on the restart and steadily drove away. Attrition was heavy despite only the scheduled yellow: Rob Green flipped in the restart pileup, Tim Pope spun from third, and several simultaneous late crashes reduced the lead lap to five trucks. Robertson won by 5.8 seconds over Burke, with Josh Bittner third and Jorge Rincon the hard charger in fourth.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Jeremiah Burke","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1284,"title":"Robertson leads a clean opening lap","summary":"Robertson and Pope launch from the front row, Burke squeezes through the middle in Turn 1, and the field survives the opening lap mostly intact.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1362,"title":"Jablonski sticks in the guardrail","summary":"Brian Jablonski slides into the barrier near the final corner and remains pinned there as the race continues without a caution.","tags":["brian-jablonski"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":1724,"title":"Vaught wrecks in the bus stop","summary":"Alan Vaught spins into the bus-stop barrier and damages the Skull No. 33, beginning a long recovery drive.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2671,"title":"Multiple crashes erupt at once","summary":"Burke tags Dave Mayberry into a pinball spin while John Herzig and Jeffrey Green collide coming out of the carousel and Austin Paul has a separate moment near the final turn.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry","john-herzig","jeffrey-green","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"chaos"},{"t":3560,"title":"Burke times the competition yellow","summary":"Burke pits just before the scheduled caution, gaining warm tires and track position; he cycles to the lead when Robertson and the other front-runners pit under yellow.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4049,"title":"Robertson retakes the lead on the restart","summary":"Robertson powers around the outside of Burke through Turn 1 and the Esses, reclaiming first as a major crash unfolds deeper in the field.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4094,"title":"Rob Green flips in the inner loop","summary":"Simon Sriegis gets loose and a pileup collects Brian Jablonski and Ricky Whittenburg, with Rob Green ending upside down and forced to tow.","tags":["simon-sregis","brian-jablonski","ricky-whittenburg","rob-green"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4850,"title":"Pope spins from third","summary":"Tim Pope slides into the bus-stop gravel from a podium position, allowing Bittner to erase a 15-second gap and eventually claim third.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5083,"title":"Two late crashes strike together","summary":"Jack Dixon and John Herzig wreck before Osborne and Whittenburg have a separate collision entering the bus stop; apparent wall netcode kicks Whittenburg into Osborne.","tags":["jack-dixon","john-herzig","jonathan-osborne","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6136,"title":"Robertson wins at the Glen","summary":"Robertson completes a near-perfect final lap and takes the victory 5.8 seconds ahead of Burke, with Bittner securing the final podium place.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2472,"quote":"Halfway to halfway — that's Louisiana 25 percent of the way.","context":"The booth translates a strategy discussion about quarter distance.","gold":5},{"t":6136,"quote":"Trevor Robertson would win here at Watkins Glen.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":2},{"t":6317,"quote":"I'm probably gonna get PTSD flashbacks from that crap — I've watched, I think, four guys in front of me for position each get wiped out.","context":"Third-place finisher Bittner describes surviving the attrition.","gold":5},{"t":6687,"quote":"Trevor, I was better than Trevor in a few corners, but the problem is he was a little bit more better in the rest of the corners.","context":"Burke gives a succinct explanation for finishing second.","gold":5},{"t":6899,"quote":"The easier I drove it, the faster I got.","context":"Robertson explains his winning road-course technique.","gold":5},{"t":7157,"quote":"I haven't seen that many trucks upside down since the last 1987 cars at Talladega race that we did.","context":"The booth sums up a race full of green-flag crashes.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish call, podium interviews, and full results rundown explicitly confirm Robertson, Burke, and Bittner. Jorge Rincon was hard charger at plus 10 positions; Eric Klafka won the random-driver draw after finishing 10th. This 60-lap race used two fast repairs, 60% fuel, unlimited tires, and one scheduled competition caution. Only five trucks finished on the lead lap, although 20 were still running at the checkered flag. The broadcast repeatedly attributes Whittenburg's late wall contact to possible netcode, so that cause is qualified.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Th9cisPMKdY":{"recap":"VRL's 150-lap Iowa race ran caution-free despite a 32-truck field, several spins, and a pit entrance the booth identified as the night's central challenge. Pole-sitter Tim Pope led early, but Josh Bittner repeatedly gained through green-flag pit cycles and fought Pope throughout the middle of the race. Alex Berube climbed from 19th by working the middle in Turns 1-2 and the high line in Turns 3-4, then reeled in Bittner during the final stint as Pope recovered from a spin through the infield. Berube passed Bittner with seven laps remaining and won by roughly two seconds; Bittner held off Pope for second.","winner":"Alex Berube","podium":["Alex Berube","Josh Bittner","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1539,"title":"Pope controls the Iowa start","summary":"Tim Pope launches from pole ahead of Jonathan Osborne as 32 trucks begin 150 laps at Iowa.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1993,"title":"Dixon spins through the infield","summary":"Jack Dixon loses the truck near the false pit-road area and slides through the infield, but the admin leaves the race green for the single-car incident.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2448,"title":"The first green-flag pit cycle begins","summary":"Around lap 38 the field begins filing onto the difficult pit road, where Trevor Robertson and Mike Adamson both struggle to make clean entries.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2820,"title":"Osborne spins after contact with the No. 22","summary":"The No. 22 catches the wall and crowds Osborne's natural exit line; Osborne spins below the yellow line and sustains heavy damage, but no caution is thrown.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3133,"title":"Bittner holds Pope through lapped traffic","summary":"Pope challenges Bittner for the lead and they run side-by-side and briefly three-wide with traffic, but Bittner clears him and retains first.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3645,"title":"Pit strategy again puts Bittner ahead","summary":"After the second green-flag cycle, Bittner exits ahead of Pope and extends the advantage to almost two seconds.","tags":["josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3894,"title":"Pope finally clears Bittner","summary":"Pope catches Bittner, goes side-by-side across the line, and completes the pass after their long series of lead battles.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4581,"title":"Robertson misses pit entry","summary":"Trevor Robertson cannot slow enough for pit road and spins through the tri-oval infield, costing him time without bringing out a yellow.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":4682,"title":"Pope spins from the lead chase","summary":"Pope loses the truck exiting Turn 4 and slides through the infield while trying to catch Bittner, surrendering his pressure on the leader but continuing.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5059,"title":"Everage spins directly in front of Berube","summary":"Contact with Zachary Self sends Michael Everage into the wall and around directly ahead of the closing Berube, who escapes as the race stays green.","tags":["mike-everage","zachary-self","alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5184,"title":"Berube takes the lead with seven to go","summary":"Berube completes his charge from 19th by passing Bittner with seven laps remaining, then denies Bittner's attempted crossover.","tags":["alex-berube","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5352,"title":"Berube completes the caution-free comeback","summary":"Berube takes the white flag with a two-second lead and wins at Iowa, while Bittner holds off Pope in the final fight for second.","tags":["alex-berube","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":756,"quote":"You mentioned corn. I'm going to bust out the corn liquor for this one.","context":"Adam Turner settles into the Iowa broadcast","gold":3},{"t":1045,"quote":"Welcome to Iowa, where you can sit on the roof and watch your dog run away for three days.","context":"The booth reads Russ Endicott's flatland joke from Facebook","gold":4},{"t":3157,"quote":"Josh not letting Tim have that spot easily.","context":"The booth calls Bittner and Pope's three-wide lead fight","gold":3},{"t":4450,"quote":"I think I'm like the anti-Pope here. Every time I mention his name, something happens.","context":"The booth reacts after Pope spins through the infield","gold":4},{"t":5070,"quote":"Yahtzee! We got a wreck on the field. I can't believe there was no flag on that one.","context":"The call as Everage spins in front of Berube","gold":4},{"t":5352,"quote":"The flashbulbs are going off — Alex 4J Berube, the winner here tonight!","context":"Berube's winning call after climbing from 19th","gold":5},{"t":5685,"quote":"When he spun out, I thought I had it in the bag, and then out of nowhere here comes French-Canadian Kyle Larson ripping it up on the top lane.","context":"Josh Bittner on Pope's spin and Berube's late arrival","gold":5},{"t":6161,"quote":"One truck at a time, one corner at a time.","context":"Winner Alex Berube explains his 18-position drive through the field","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"This November 2021 Iowa broadcast is not present in seasons_map.json, so no season or round is asserted. The booth, interviews, and results explicitly establish Berube, Bittner, and Pope as the podium and state that the full 150 laps ran without a caution. Admin-caution rules allowed single-car and contained multi-car incidents to remain green; the late Everage-Self crash also produced no yellow. The No. 22 involved in Osborne's earlier spin is not identified clearly enough in the broadcast, so no driver identity is assigned. Canonical roster spelling 'Simon Sriegis' was used for captions such as 'Simon Cobra Sriges.' Transcript timestamps end at 1:58:49 (7129 seconds), within the 7130-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"TK96vvy5PwM":{"recap":"The Vigilante Ascension 150 at virtual Avondale closed out Season 12 as a double-championship night, with the VRL Cup's top three — Dillon Bryant, Tim Pope, and Craig Goodenough — separated by just nine points and all sent to the back of the grid under penalty. Trevor Robertson was the class of the field from the pole, stretching out multi-second leads while the contenders carved through traffic. The Cup fight thinned when Goodenough caught a pit-road speeding penalty and Chris Goans slipped off the lead in turns three and four before dropping out entirely to packet loss. That left Bryant and Pope trading restart haymakers over the final 30 laps, Bryant answering a lost spot with a perfect final launch and a backstretch block. Robertson swept the win and the Contender Chase title, and Bryant crossed second — one spot ahead of Pope — to clinch his first VRL Premier Series Cup championship.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Dillon Bryant","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":559,"title":"Championship twist: title trio starts dead last","summary":"The Cup's top three, split by just nine points, all carry penalties and must start from the back of the grid and carve through the field on championship night.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":1345,"title":"Osborne's onboard: racing with his mouth, beating the field","summary":"The booth spotlights Jonathan Osborne's self-designed adaptive rig — he controls the truck with his mouth — and reminds everyone he's a league champion who beats you straight up.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1781,"title":"Foot cam and heart-rate cam: Goodenough wired up","summary":"Goodenough shares a foot cam and a live heart monitor — 130 bpm in clean air — while Alan smugly reports his own 77 from the booth.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2684,"title":"Speeding penalty derails Goodenough","summary":"After climbing nine spots, Goodenough mysteriously drops to 22nd and a lap down — the booth pieces together a pit-road speeding penalty that guts his title bid.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3185,"title":"Player in the wall, Rincon swats flies","summary":"Andy Player pounds the wall and bounces back across traffic; Jorge Rincon gathers a wild moment with slight contact off the 31, but the save drops him to 25th.","tags":["andrew-player","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4625,"title":"Goans slips the lead away","summary":"Leading on old tires, Chris Goans gets loose in turns three and four right after the restart and slides out of the lead, falling to eighth as his championship hopes fade.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4862,"title":"Restart chaos: Pope jolts Wade, Benfield gets wrecked","summary":"Pope thumps the 68 of Wade when the field checks up, and moments later Stony Benfield is turned in a violent tangle with the 48 off the dogleg — caution number four.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-wade","stony-benfield"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5103,"title":"Pope pounces on Bryant's bad restart","summary":"Bryant bogs down on the front-row restart and Pope powers around him — exactly the position swap that would flip the championship.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5333,"title":"Packet loss knocks out Goans","summary":"Championship 4 driver Chris Goans abruptly drops from the session with packet loss, ending his night on the spot.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5343,"title":"Bryant answers with the launch of his life","summary":"With 23 to go Bryant nails the final restart, clears Pope, and throws a backstretch block to hold the title-deciding position behind leader Robertson.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5958,"title":"'The reckoning' with two to go","summary":"With the checkered in sight, a late wreck catches Dustin Wade and John McAdam — 'there's the reckoning' — one final scare before the titles are settled.","tags":["dustin-wade","john-mcadam"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5975,"title":"Robertson wins it; Bryant is a first-time Cup champion","summary":"Trevor Robertson brings it home to sweep the race win and the Contender Chase title, while Dillon Bryant crosses second — one spot ahead of Tim Pope — to clinch his first VRL Premier Series Cup championship.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1862,"quote":"My heart rate's at 77 right now, so I'm doing a little more chilled out than these guys are.","context":"Alan compares his own pulse to Goodenough's live heart-rate cam","gold":3},{"t":3208,"quote":"He had to be swatting flies inside of that cockpit there.","context":"Jorge Rincon's wild save dodging Andy Player's wrecked truck","gold":4},{"t":3692,"quote":"Don't you notice that usually the guy that makes the pass is the one that thinks it's awesome, and not the guy that gets passed?","context":"After Osborne radios 'Awesome battle, man' to the truck he just passed","gold":4},{"t":4121,"quote":"Superman trying to do Superman things. Let's hopefully nobody grabs his cape here tonight.","context":"Dillon Bryant's bold off-sequence pit gamble","gold":3},{"t":5247,"quote":"Fifth caution of the night. Cautions breed caution.","context":"Wade's spin stacks up the late-race yellows","gold":3},{"t":5985,"quote":"He's got it! Robertson is going to bring it home for the chase. And Dylan Bryant is a first-time champion in the VRL Premier Series Cup.","context":"The checkered-flag call deciding both championships","gold":5},{"t":6508,"quote":"Allan, man, I did it, man. I finally did it.","context":"A tearful Dillon Bryant in the champion's interview","gold":4},{"t":7111,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, stay vigilante, and we will see you next time. Good night. This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"Alan's Season 12 signoff","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble many names. Co-commentator surname heard as 'Vaude' (Alan Vaude) — uncertain. Best-guess spellings uncertain for: Chris Gomes (captions Gones/Gomes/Golds/Gins, #38), Jorge Rincon (Ranc/Rinkcon/Rencon/Ron, #28), Andrew Cowan (Cawan/Cawin/Cawth/Coffin/Cyin, #10), Tom Barish (Beerish/Bears, #35), Chandler Paul (once 'Chandler Hall'), John Schoenbachler ('Choenbachler'). Race winner and both champions explicitly stated. Podium P2/P3 taken from the last-lap call (Robertson, Bryant, Pope) plus 'nearly pulled off the victory' about Bryant — confident but never read as an official result sheet. At least five cautions; the final wreck ('the reckoning', Wade/McAdam) came with about two to go, so the finish may have run out under yellow. Lori (race admin, 'unofficial counselor of the league') and chat members (Earl Evans, Amanda Wade, Nicole Walsh, etc.) are not drivers. Season 12 finale — Season 13 opens next Wednesday at Michigan with Tow Call (Albert Anderson's company) as a new primary sponsor.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"tKEFuwkBilY":{"recap":"Jeremiah Burke won the Season 6 regular-season finale at Las Vegas by committing to an off-sequence fuel strategy with Larry Dickerson. Tim Pope narrowly beat Alan Vaught for the midpoint stage, but Burke's group pitted late under that scheduled caution and gambled that the second half would stay green long enough to reach the finish. A crash involving Dickerson, Kyle Vaught, Greg Dobson, and Sean McDonnell produced the race's only incident caution and helped lock the strategy into place. Burke held Josh Bittner off by about six tenths to win, with Dickerson completing the podium as most of the conventional-strategy contenders finished a lap down.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Josh Bittner","Larry Dickerson"],"moments":[{"t":945,"title":"Gallagher and Vaught lead the finale green","summary":"Pole-sitter John Gallagher and Alan Vaught start side by side, with Tim Pope pushing the lower lane as the field remains tightly paired through the opening lap.","tags":["john-gallagher","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1242,"title":"Bittner brushes the wall","summary":"Josh Bittner lightly touches the outside wall and loses several positions, an early setback he later overcomes.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":"mistake"},{"t":1835,"title":"Green-flag strategy begins","summary":"The first round of green-flag pit stops starts near the midpoint of the opening stage, with Burke cycling into the lead on a short-pit sequence.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2496,"title":"Pope and Vaught drag-race for the stage","summary":"Tim Pope and Alan Vaught run side by side through the final corners before Pope wins the stage by a captioned margin of 0.055 seconds.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":2648,"title":"Dobson pushes fuel-starved Burke","summary":"Burke runs out of fuel under the stage caution and Greg Dobson pushes him toward pit road, helping preserve Burke's later off-sequence plan.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3193,"title":"Dickerson's long wreck brings the yellow","summary":"Contact with Kyle Vaught turns Larry Dickerson, who slides across Andrew Coffin's path and remains in trouble long enough for Greg Dobson and Sean McDonnell to be caught before the caution appears.","tags":["larry-dickerson","kyle-vaught","andrew-cauthan","greg-dobson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3561,"title":"Three-wide restart scramble","summary":"Pope and Vaught resume their side-by-side fight while Dustyn Eaton charges through a narrow gap and John Osborne makes contact with Jonah Long in a hectic restart.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","jonathan-osborne","jonah-long"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3853,"title":"Fuel strategies split the field","summary":"With more than 20 laps remaining, Burke, Bittner, Dickerson, Dixon, and Dobson stay out while the conventional group is forced toward another stop.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","larry-dickerson","jack-dixon","greg-dobson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4436,"title":"Dixon confirms the fuel numbers mid-race","summary":"While still racing in fourth, Jack Dixon posts to the YouTube chat that the off-sequence group has enough fuel to finish, confirming the booth's speculation.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4565,"title":"Burke makes the gamble stick","summary":"Burke completes the final lap without a fuel stumble and beats Bittner by roughly six tenths, with Dickerson taking third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","larry-dickerson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2648,"quote":"I'm running out of fuel.","context":"Jeremiah Burke reports his empty tank under the stage caution","gold":3},{"t":4436,"quote":"You're telling me Jack Dixon just got on YouTube while he's racing?","context":"The booth reacts to Dixon posting the fuel answer from the cockpit","gold":4},{"t":5530,"quote":"Looking forward to watching me destroy somebody in high quality and high definition.","context":"Josh Bittner jokes about reviewing the broadcast after finishing second","gold":4},{"t":5597,"quote":"Six seasons of doing weird strategies like that and finally got one to stick and work. This might be the best win I've had.","context":"Jeremiah Burke celebrates the strategy victory","gold":5},{"t":5710,"quote":"We were going under caution and it was like, man, if we pit with one to go, we're going to make it, but we're just going to barely make it.","context":"Burke explains the winning fuel calculation","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete grid and post-race rundown establish 23 starters. The stage margin is captioned as '55,000 separate'; the recap interprets the spoken call as 0.055 seconds but does not use it to infer any finishing result. Burke's post-race interview explicitly identifies the late-caution pit decision and says only Bittner remained a serious fuel-strategy challenger.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"tKN9W-3rMuE":{"recap":"Alex Berube beat pole-sitter Tim Pope off the start at Indianapolis, but Pope reclaimed the lead within the opening ten laps and began building a gap in clean air. Pope controlled the first green-flag pit cycle while a poor stop and aerodynamic damage dropped Berube from second, allowing Jeremiah Burke and Josh Bittner to become the nearest challengers. Berube stayed out through a full stint with the damage, repaired the truck on his next stop, and charged back to third as Burke used fresher tires to take second. Pope managed the final cycle and a late seven-second cushion to earn his second win of the season, leading Burke and Berube in a 75-lap race that went entirely caution-free.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke","Alex Berube"],"moments":[{"t":1374,"title":"Pope and Berube launch side by side","summary":"Pope leads the 29-truck field from pole, but Berube hangs alongside through the opening corners while Jonathan Osborne jumps from sixth to third.","tags":["timothy-pope","alex-berube","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1418,"title":"Berube takes the opening lead","summary":"Berube clears Pope before the first lap is complete and settles into first, putting his long-run tire-management reputation to an immediate test.","tags":["alex-berube","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1924,"title":"Pope retakes command as Burke advances","summary":"Pope completes the pass back on Berube, and Burke follows with a move of his own to shuffle the early leader behind the two fastest trucks.","tags":["timothy-pope","alex-berube","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":1977,"title":"Dixon crashes and spins to the access road","summary":"Jack Dixon hits the outside wall and spins across the grass onto the access road, then struggles to square the damaged truck in his pit stall for repairs.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2001,"title":"Timmerman hits the Turn 1 wall","summary":"Angelica Timmerman drifts wide in Turn 1 and strikes the inside wall at a sharp angle; she avoids rebounding into traffic but must tow with major damage.","tags":["angelica-timmerman"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2427,"title":"The first green-flag stops begin","summary":"Trevor Robertson, Michael Everage, Eric Klafka, Alan Vaught, Joshua Oxendine, Kelly Kuehl, Austin Paul, Dave Mayberry, and Jeffrey Green lead a large wave onto pit road around lap 20.","tags":["trevor-robertson","mike-everage","eric-klafka","jess-vaught","josh-oxendine","kelly-keel","austin-paul","dave-mayberry","jeffrey-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2530,"title":"Pope wins the cycle while Berube is delayed","summary":"Pope exits the first pit sequence still in the lead, but Berube's poor stop and unrepaired body damage cost enough time for Bittner to cycle into second.","tags":["timothy-pope","alex-berube","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3042,"title":"Robertson passes the damaged Berube","summary":"Berube elects to stretch the stint rather than pit early for repairs, and his straightaway speed loss allows Robertson to drive by for fourth.","tags":["trevor-robertson","alex-berube"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4081,"title":"Repaired Berube charges back to fourth","summary":"With the truck straightened out during the second cycle, Berube carries a head of steam past Robertson and resumes his pursuit of a podium finish.","tags":["alex-berube","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"comeback"},{"t":4182,"title":"Burke uses fresher tires for second","summary":"Burke catches Bittner and completes the pass into Turn 3, turning a three-lap tire advantage into the runner-up position.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4724,"title":"The leaders complete their final stops","summary":"Pope, Burke, and the remaining front-runners pit with roughly 15 laps left; Pope retains control while Berube's repaired truck climbs back to third and earns the fastest-lap bonus.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5605,"title":"Pope kisses the bricks with win number two","summary":"Pope finishes the caution-free 75-lap race roughly seven seconds clear for his second victory of the season, with Burke second and Berube completing his comeback in third.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","alex-berube"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":822,"quote":"Once you hit that 13 mark, well, that's it. Your race is done.","context":"The booth explains the new 13-incident-point disqualification rule","gold":4},{"t":1418,"quote":"Alex Berube was able to take that lead away from Timothy Pope.","context":"Berube wins the opening-lap fight from the outside of the front row","gold":4},{"t":1475,"quote":"Is he on, like, double secret probation or what?","context":"The booth reacts to Zachary Self's inherited end-of-line and drive-through penalties","gold":5},{"t":3851,"quote":"You're in charge of your front end. He's not holding the line or he is—you've got to get around him.","context":"Allen English explains the leaders' responsibility in lap traffic","gold":4},{"t":5816,"quote":"When it was repaired, I was just the rocket I was before, and I got back to third.","context":"Alex Berube describes recovering from his aerodynamic damage","gold":4},{"t":5940,"quote":"If you miss that line just by a little bit, you're going right up to the wall.","context":"Jeremiah Burke explains why passing at Indianapolis requires restraint","gold":4},{"t":6008,"quote":"Patience—that's all I've been preaching to myself—is patience, patience.","context":"Burke identifies the approach that carried him from eighth to second","gold":5},{"t":6151,"quote":"It's basically just a rhythm thing. Once you find a rhythm, if you can stay in that rhythm and hit your marks, you're good to go.","context":"Winner Tim Pope explains his dominant caution-free run","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 1, Round 4 on the Indianapolis oval according to seasons_map.json. The 75-lap race used 70% fuel, two fast repairs, and a 13-incident-point disqualification threshold; all 75 laps ran caution-free. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Pope-Burke-Berube podium, Berube's fastest-lap bonus, and the full 29-driver finishing order. Alex Gray was called to work before the start and is therefore not included among the participants. Canonical roster spellings are used for several caption variants, including Alex Berube, Ricky Whittenburg, Simon Sriegis, and Michael Everage. Transcript timestamps end within the 6,518-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"tL87ML3RVdA":{"recap":"Jack Dixon started from pole at USA International Speedway, but contact with Mike Adamson sent him spinning out of the lead before the race settled into a long, attrition-heavy short-track grind. Adamson controlled most of the first half while John Ellis recovered from an end-of-line start, avoided repeated spins and pileups, and climbed into the lead fight with Alan Vaught. Green-flag pit timing decided the closing order: Ellis stopped just ahead of Vaught to complete the undercut, while Adamson's earlier short pit left him needing a late fuel-only stop. Ellis pulled four seconds clear and earned his fourth victory in five races, with Vaught the only other driver on the lead lap and Ricky Whittenburg passing Eric Klafka late for third.","winner":"John Ellis","podium":["John Ellis","Alan Vaught","Ricky Whittenburg"],"moments":[{"t":1450,"title":"Dixon leads the USA 250 away","summary":"Pole-sitter Jack Dixon takes the initial lead as the 24-truck field begins 250 laps on the flat three-quarter-mile oval.","tags":["jack-dixon","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1560,"title":"Adamson contact spins Dixon from first","summary":"Adamson gets underneath Dixon and the two converge in the same piece of track, rotating Dixon without major damage but dropping him from the lead to roughly 12th.","tags":["jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1637,"title":"Snyder hits the wall without a yellow","summary":"Jeff Snyder crashes hard in front of Russ Endicott, but manual race control leaves the race green because the incident involves only two trucks and the track remains passable.","tags":["jeff-snyder","russ-endicott"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2250,"title":"Klafka and Mayberry trigger the first caution","summary":"Contact between Eric Klafka and Dave Mayberry creates a bottleneck; Chandler Paul arrives with a square hit while Albert Anderson and several others scramble through the pileup.","tags":["eric-klafka","dave-mayberry","chandler-paul","albert-anderson","kelly-keel","dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2361,"title":"Fuel-only calls split the first pit cycle","summary":"Dixon, Ellis, Kuehl, and Josh Bittner gain track position with abbreviated service while much of the field takes four tires, setting up a sharp old-tire versus new-tire contrast.","tags":["jack-dixon","john-ellis","kelly-keel","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2531,"title":"Adamson pounces on the restart","summary":"A delayed restart finally goes green and Adamson catches Dixon sleeping on the outside, taking command before Austin Paul and Russ Kilgore tangle to bring out the second caution.","tags":["mike-adamson","jack-dixon","austin-paul","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3500,"title":"Everage and Chandler Paul collide","summary":"Chandler Paul is slowed by Russ Endicott and Michael Everage cannot check up in time, turning Paul and producing another caution just as Dixon had committed to pit road.","tags":["mike-everage","chandler-paul","russ-endicott","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4637,"title":"The halfway green-flag cycle reshuffles the lead","summary":"Ellis, Dixon, and Klafka open the stops before Adamson loses several seconds in his box; Vaught emerges in front, with Ellis setting the race's fastest lap while chasing him down.","tags":["john-ellis","jack-dixon","eric-klafka","mike-adamson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5517,"title":"Vaught, Ellis, and Adamson run nose to tail","summary":"Vaught nearly loses the truck and Ellis closes to his bumper, with longtime leader Adamson joining them through dense lap traffic to form a three-way fight for first.","tags":["jess-vaught","john-ellis","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6233,"title":"Ellis converts the final pit sequence","summary":"Adamson short-pits before Vaught and Ellis complete their last stops; Ellis's fresher tires and earlier service relative to Vaught give him the decisive track-position swing, and he passes Adamson for the lead.","tags":["john-ellis","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6951,"title":"Adamson must stop again for fuel","summary":"The dominant early leader's short pit proves too early to reach the finish, forcing Adamson to make a late fuel-only stop and surrender his remaining chance at the podium.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7352,"title":"Ellis completes a last-to-first victory","summary":"Ellis takes the checkered flag about four seconds ahead of Vaught for his fourth win in five races; Whittenburg's late pass on Klafka secures the final podium place.","tags":["john-ellis","jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg","eric-klafka"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1200,"quote":"This is 250 laps here tonight, 187.5 miles, on a short track.","context":"The booth sets the scale of the USA 250 before the start","gold":4},{"t":2440,"quote":"Track position is extremely important at a place like this.","context":"The broadcast explains Dixon's aggressive first pit call","gold":4},{"t":4344,"quote":"It might be a fixed setup, but the driver input really does control how this thing handles the whole way.","context":"The booth explains why tire treatment creates different long-run speeds","gold":5},{"t":7497,"quote":"There were so many emotions going through that race: anger, frustration, happy, upset. It overlapped every single lap.","context":"Third-place Ricky Whittenburg describes the physical and emotional grind","gold":5},{"t":7517,"quote":"I felt like I passed a thousand cars and only got hit once.","context":"Whittenburg sums up surviving traffic to reach the podium","gold":5},{"t":7781,"quote":"As soon as he passed me, I told my teammates, 'There goes the win right there.'","context":"Runner-up Alan Vaught identifies Ellis's pit-cycle pass as the deciding moment","gold":5},{"t":8027,"quote":"You just gotta find a rhythm and stick with it. Don't worry about trying to drive it hard every lap.","context":"Random-draw interviewee Michael Everage explains how to survive 250 short-track laps","gold":5},{"t":8175,"quote":"I started dead last with the EOL and somehow made my way last to first.","context":"Winner John Ellis reflects on his recovery through the field","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 2, Round 11 according to seasons_map.json. The mapped track field is null, but the broadcast explicitly identifies the venue as the former USA International Speedway in Lakeland, Florida. The USA 250 ran 250 laps and 187.5 miles with 50% fuel, five total tire sets, two fast repairs, a 21-incident disqualification threshold, and administrator-controlled cautions; the booth counted only about two and a half cautions despite numerous single-truck spins. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Ellis-Vaught-Whittenburg podium and reads all 24 classified drivers; Jeffrey Oettinger was described as a start-and-park entry. Ellis's nominal grid position was 17th, but an end-of-line penalty moved him to the tail before the start, which he described in the interview as starting dead last. Canonical roster spellings are used throughout, and all timestamps fall within the 9,117-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Tqhqyi_KWUg":{"recap":"Alan Vaught won the 85-lap Season 10 race at Indianapolis after starting third, leading the most laps and controlling each long run once fresh tires brought him to the front. Three cautions shaped the first half, including Joe Canales' near-rollover and a large frontstretch crash that began when Kelly Kuehl became stuck against the outside wall. The final half ran under green, forcing the contenders through two rounds of timed fuel-and-tire stops while Tim Pope charged from 28th to second. Pope closed to within three-tenths late but hit the turn-four wall with fewer than three laps remaining, allowing Vaught to win comfortably ahead of Pope and Mike Adamson.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":2515,"title":"Indianapolis race goes green","summary":"Pole-sitter Jason Gaines gets loose in turn one and saves the truck, allowing Dillon Bryant to take the early lead as the 35-entry field begins the 85-lap race.","tags":["jason-gaines","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2820,"title":"Eaton takes the early lead","summary":"Dustyn Eaton sets up Bryant through the short chute and completes a clean pass in turn three before quickly opening a gap.","tags":["dustin-eaton","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":3271,"title":"Canales nearly rolls in the first caution","summary":"Joe Canales comes down while not clear on the backstretch, catches air and nearly saves the truck before striking the outside SAFER barrier with race-ending damage.","tags":["joe-canales"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3719,"title":"Fresh tires launch Vaught to the front","summary":"Vaught drives past fuel-only leader Jeremiah Burke in turn three, demonstrating an advantage of more than a second per lap for fresh tires after the first caution.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":3773,"title":"Cline suffers a violent netcode failure","summary":"Greg Cline closes on Derek Welch and the front of his truck suddenly appears to detonate, sending him spinning into the inside wall; a delayed, unexplained second caution follows shortly afterward.","tags":["greg-cline","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":4706,"title":"Kuehl's wall ride triggers the Big One","summary":"Kelly Kuehl becomes stuck against the outside wall exiting turn four and is struck by following traffic, collecting Jack Dixon, Scott Rooney and roughly eight other trucks in the race's largest crash.","tags":["kelly-keel","jack-dixon","scott-rooney"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5160,"title":"Vaught reclaims control after halfway caution","summary":"Vaught uses four fresh tires to clear fuel-only leader Burke on the restart, while Adamson moves into second and Craig Goodenough continues his charge from 27th.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5872,"title":"Pope reaches the top five from 28th","summary":"Pope passes Andrew Player to gain his 23rd position of the race, joining Goodenough as one of the night's major movers.","tags":["timothy-pope","andrew-player","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6113,"title":"Green-flag stops cycle Vaught back ahead","summary":"Vaught pits from the lead with Eaton, Goodenough and Welch, then uses fresh tires to pass Player and return to the point after the full cycle.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough","derek-welch","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6872,"title":"Pope attempts the final-stop undercut","summary":"Pope pits one lap before Vaught for four tires and fuel, but Vaught answers with a 14.42-second stop and blends back onto the track just ahead of him.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":7640,"title":"Pope's late challenge hits the wall","summary":"After closing to less than three-tenths with fewer than three laps to go, Pope loses the nose in dirty air and strikes the turn-four wall, falling more than a second behind.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":7768,"title":"Vaught completes the dominant Indianapolis win","summary":"Vaught crosses the Yard of Bricks after leading the most laps, with Pope finishing second after gaining 26 positions and Adamson completing the podium.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3484,"quote":"Acts like a cheese grater on these Goodyear tires.","context":"The booth explains how punishing the Indianapolis surface is on a long run.","gold":4},{"t":4804,"quote":"When in doubt, hold the brake, folks.","context":"The booth's deadpan safety lesson after the frontstretch pileup.","gold":4},{"t":6468,"quote":"Or you stay out until it runs dry and hope you get a caution.","context":"The booth sums up Jonathan Osborne's long-stint strategy gamble.","gold":4},{"t":7676,"quote":"Allen Vaught probably taking a deep breath here, realizing he's just got to be smooth to the finish.","context":"The booth resets the stakes after Pope's late wall contact.","gold":4},{"t":7768,"quote":"He's led the most laps, and he's going to cross the stripe first and take the checkered flag here at Indy.","context":"The live call as Vaught wins at Indianapolis.","gold":5},{"t":8223,"quote":"You got Tim Pope always lurking, always pressing, and I'm trying not to overdrive the truck.","context":"Vaught describes managing his pace with Pope closing late.","gold":5},{"t":8402,"quote":"Just trying to give it all I had, and the aero push got me off the turn there and backed the wall.","context":"Runner-up Pope explains the turn-four contact that ended his challenge.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, all three podium interviews and the final results rundown explicitly confirm Alan Vaught, Tim Pope and Mike Adamson. The starting-grid read initially says Alan Vaught in third, then immediately corrects the driver to Alan Vaught; the roster override also canonicalizes Alan to Allen. Pope started 28th and was credited with gaining 26 positions. The results rundown contains several verbal slips after fourth place: its sequence supports Craig Goodenough fifth and Andrew Player sixth, but the transcript says Goodenough 'came home in third' and then calls Player both fifth and sixth; these do not affect the podium. The rundown also omits an explicit 17th-place name before resuming with Russ Kilgore and Greg Dobson, and classifies Larry Dickerson 35th after he was called to work before the green. All 35 registered entrants are retained in the drivers array, including Dickerson as a DNS. Austin Paul is the missing 19th starter in the grid transcript and is explicitly identified mid-race and as the 14th-place finisher. Andrew Cauthan and Greg Cline follow the current roster overrides despite the captions' Cawthon/Coffin and Klein variants.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"TVa2MVolkn0":{"recap":"The VRL brought the NASCAR trucks to Michigan for the Brawl for 85, run as a tribute to late league member Robert Jordan — the field carried his No. 74 on their trucks and the booth went silent for a lap-74 'moment of loudness.' Polesitter Albert Anderson, 'America's Driver,' was knocked into the infield grass early but drove back through the field and held off Josh Bittner and Jess Vogt over the closing green-flag run for his second win of the week. The middle stages were caution-heavy: Jeremiah Burke's spin launched Kyle Vogt, Ricky Whittenburg took a wild tank-slapper into the inside wall, and a late crash sent Craig Goodenough's rear wheels off the ground. Bittner ran second despite connection issues that clocked him at an infamous 447 mph on live timing, while Jess Vogt completed the podium and tied Dustin Riehle for hard charger at 23 spots gained. Kyle Vogt capped the night by beating 'Podium Dave' Mayberry by three tenths — then wrecking his own dad after the checkered flag.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Josh Bittner","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1511,"title":"Kyle's I-Heart-Uncle-Dave shirt","summary":"The booth jumps on board with Kyle Vogt mid-race to reveal the special t-shirt Uncle Dave Mayberry bought him — he 'hearts' his Uncle Dave, and the season-long rivalry gets a new chapter.","tags":["jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1570,"title":"First caution: Everage backwards on pit lane","summary":"Mike Everage drifts up the track into Jack Dixon, who gets pit-maneuvered into the wall; Jacob Young takes a hard impact and Dave Mayberry is collected in the first caution of the night.","tags":["mike-everage","jack-dixon","jacob-young","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2012,"title":"Coffin in the wall, Anderson mows the grass","summary":"Andrew Coffin cuts himself into the outside wall while race leader Albert Anderson gets tangled with the 14 and takes a trip through the infield grass; John Gallagher does a full pass through the grass to dodge it.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","albert-anderson","john-gallagher","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2192,"title":"Stuck-throttle chaos ends Coffin's night","summary":"A big lap-20 wreck leaves Andrew Coffin stuck mid-track with the throttle wide open and wheels spinning; John Gallagher's front bumper is left 'hanging on by a single zip tie.'","tags":["andrew-cauthan","john-gallagher","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2758,"title":"Burke spins, Kyle Vogt gets launched","summary":"Jeremiah Burke gets loose mid-corner and shoots sideways down the track; Kyle Vogt has nowhere to go and gets launched all the way up in heavy contact. Greg Dobson apologizes on the radio, though the booth rules Burke was already losing it.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","greg-dobson","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3205,"title":"Whittenburg's tank-slapper","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg's truck starts zigzagging like a motorcycle tank-slapper, scraping the inside wall and taking Trevor Robertson for a ride to bring out the yellow.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3710,"title":"Goodenough airborne in the night's biggest wreck","summary":"Mike Adamson steps out from underneath himself in turns three and four and slides sideways across traffic — Craig Goodenough gets jacked up with his rear end off the ground in a huge impact as Osborne and others scatter.","tags":["mike-adamson","craig-goodenough","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4045,"title":"Chachi's no-force-feedback save","summary":"Jonathan 'Chachi' Osborne spins and saves it right at the yellow line with zero damage — made more remarkable by the booth noting he drives on a controller with no force feedback.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4506,"title":"Bittner clocks 447 mph","summary":"Josh Bittner's connection issues glitch the live timing into reading 447 mph across the line, spawning a running gag — fan Payton insists she saw it with her own two eyes.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5102,"title":"Lap 74 moment of loudness for Robert Jordan","summary":"In honor of the late Robert Jordan's No. 74, the booth goes silent on lap 74 for a 'moment of loudness,' letting the trucks sing his praises at full song — the emotional centerpiece of the tribute race.","tags":[],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5553,"title":"Anderson brings it home","summary":"The white flag waves with Albert Anderson glued to the bottom as Josh Bittner and Jess Vogt make their last-ditch runs — neither can close, and America's Driver wins his second race of the week, dedicating it to Robert Jordan.","tags":["albert-anderson","josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5703,"title":"Son wrecks dad after the checkers","summary":"After the finish, Kyle Vogt turns his dad Jess on the backstretch during a congratulatory rub — the booth predicts an awkward Easter dinner.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2598,"quote":"They're acting like they're shooting dice in Waco on a Saturday night, what they're doing right now.","context":"calling the three-and-four-wide restart chaos","gold":3},{"t":2726,"quote":"This truckload of pig parts just flipped over in the middle of the Katy Freeway — I tell you, it was slicker than snot.","context":"explaining all the slipping and sliding on track","gold":4},{"t":3412,"quote":"He goes, 'What's your name?' ... 'Your name is Rick? You're real slick — now give me a dollar.' He was demanding a damn dollar.","context":"Brown's French Quarter street-hustler story during a long caution","gold":4},{"t":3800,"quote":"We now know the 89 of Goodenough isn't going to have to get that truck inspected — everybody was able to see what he's running underneath there.","context":"after Goodenough's rear end came off the ground in the big wreck","gold":4},{"t":4515,"quote":"Due to his connection, he ran 447 miles an hour around here.","context":"Josh Bittner's lag glitch breaking the live timing","gold":4},{"t":5427,"quote":"The 99 of Anderson just watching that behind him like, yeah, you two guys fight — let me just drive off into the sunset here.","context":"Anderson leading while Bittner and Vogt battle for second late","gold":3},{"t":5595,"quote":"America's driver bringing it on home here once again from Michigan!","context":"the checkered flag call for Albert Anderson","gold":4},{"t":5703,"quote":"Son just wrecked dad on the backstretch — I don't know if y'all saw that. Kyle wrecked Jess.","context":"post-race Vogt family shenanigans after the checkers","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption surname guesses are best-effort: Goodenough, Whittenburg, Vogt, Bitner, Riehle, Rone, Ochoa, Howe, Everage. 'Dustin with a Y' suggests Dustyn Eaton. Jonah Long registered but never connected and did not grid; Andrew Coffin disconnected mid-race after his wreck; Jeremiah Burke retired early. Lori Vogt served as race control/admin (not a competitor). Non-competing league members mentioned: Russell Endicott, Larry Dickerson, Nick Ramsey, and Jess's teammate Kelly (absent with technical issues). Race was a tribute to the late Robert Jordan (No. 74), a three-season league member. Final results beyond the podium per booth rundown: 4th Tim Pope, 5th Greg Klein; Jess Vogt and Dustin Riehle tied for hard charger (+23 spots). Kyle Vogt's gap over Mayberry was read as both '300s' (0.3s) and '3007 second' in captions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"u3ymKWJaHH8":{"recap":"Dustin Wade earned his first VRL Premiere Series victory in the 85-lap Daytona 213, edging Albert Anderson in a last-lap drag race while Kelly Kuehl took third. Pole winner Mike Adamson led lap one but was eliminated in the opening crash, and a second multi-truck wreck on lap 12 further reduced the main pack before a long green run produced two full pit cycles. A late three-wide crash erased the fuel deficit facing Wade, Anderson and Kuehl and set up a 10-lap sprint in which Wade repeatedly recovered from being shuffled between lanes. On the last lap Wade bounced off the wall after contact with Tim Pope, received a momentum-saving shove from John Osborne, then got underneath Anderson out of Turn 4 to win as another crash erupted behind them.","winner":"Dustin Wade","podium":["Dustin Wade","Albert Anderson","Kelly Kuehl"],"moments":[{"t":1130,"title":"Adamson leads the Daytona field","summary":"Mike Adamson starts from pole with John Schoenbachler outside, while noted plate racer Dustin Wade launches from fourth in the tightly packed 31-truck field.","tags":["mike-adamson","john-schoenbachler","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1194,"title":"Adamson takes lap one","summary":"After Schoenbachler uses Wade's push to cross lanes, Adamson switches outside and noses ahead to lead the opening lap.","tags":["mike-adamson","john-schoenbachler","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":1207,"title":"The front row triggers an early junkyard","summary":"A hesitation and lane change at the front sparks a lap-one pileup; Adamson, Schoenbachler and Derek Welch suffer major damage, with Adamson and Welch ultimately retiring.","tags":["mike-adamson","john-schoenbachler","derek-welch"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1578,"title":"Wade controls the first restart","summary":"Wade launches from the lead on lap six, then allows Albert Anderson through and slots into second rather than forcing an early block.","tags":["dustin-wade","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1883,"title":"Lap-12 crash hits the contenders","summary":"Chandler Paul and Michael Everage come together in three-wide traffic, triggering the second caution and collecting Josh Bittner, Austin Paul, Kevin Hunt and others.","tags":["chandler-paul","mike-everage","josh-bittner","austin-paul","kevin-hunt"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2292,"title":"Vaught's shifter ends his night","summary":"Moments after the restart, Kyle Vaught's malfunctioning shifter selects the wrong gear and abruptly takes him out of the race.","tags":["kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"mechanical"},{"t":3325,"title":"The field commits under green","summary":"Jason Gaines, Anderson, Dillon Bryant and several others make the first major green-flag stop while Wade, Dustyn Eaton and Kuehl stay out one additional lap.","tags":["jason-gaines","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","dustin-wade","dustin-eaton","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3399,"title":"Pit-box errors split the draft","summary":"Eaton and John McAdam overshoot their stalls and must reverse; Eaton clings to a group, but McAdam loses the draft as the earlier-stopping pack wins the cycle.","tags":["dustin-eaton","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":4573,"title":"Osborne spins entering pit road","summary":"During the final scheduled stop sequence, John Osborne spins on pit entry while Chris Goans, Jorge Rincon, Tim Pope and Tom Barish stretch the fuel window.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","chris-goans","george-rincon","timothy-pope","tom-barish"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":5051,"title":"Late crash resets the fuel race","summary":"A three-wide squeeze involving Goans, Michael Everage and Schoenbachler triggers the third caution, rescuing Wade, Anderson, Gaines and Kuehl from a projected fuel shortage.","tags":["chris-goans","mike-everage","john-schoenbachler","dustin-wade","albert-anderson","jason-gaines","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5427,"title":"Wade leads the 10-lap sprint","summary":"Wade takes control of the final restart with Andrew Player outside, Eaton pushing the inside lane and Anderson poised just behind.","tags":["dustin-wade","andrew-player","dustin-eaton","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5892,"title":"Wade wins a wild last-lap drag race","summary":"After contact with Pope and the wall, Wade receives a shove from Osborne, gets beneath Anderson exiting Turn 4 and wins; Kuehl darts through the wrecking traffic behind to claim third.","tags":["dustin-wade","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5914,"quote":"Here we go, folks, to the line. Dustin Wade is going to win. Great job, Dustin Wade.","context":"The booth calls Wade's first VRL victory","gold":5},{"t":6475,"quote":"I didn't see the wreck at all. I just saw that I was able to get up on that high side, and I saw the hole and I just took it.","context":"Kelly Kuehl explains the instinctive move that carried him to third","gold":5},{"t":6614,"quote":"I haven't had that much fun in a long time. That was just fun, and I'm over-the-top happy for Dustin Wade.","context":"Runner-up Albert Anderson celebrates Wade's breakthrough","gold":4},{"t":6735,"quote":"You're only going to get away with a block twice. You try that third block, you're going to get turned.","context":"Anderson describes defending the lead through the tri-oval","gold":5},{"t":6892,"quote":"That is correct. I've won a Monday night race, but anybody in the league will tell you that doesn't count.","context":"Wade confirms this is his first VRL Premiere Series win","gold":4},{"t":6957,"quote":"Honestly, I was just being patient. I knew if I could stay in the bottom line for as long as I possibly could, I'd be able to sneak up in front at any point in time.","context":"Wade explains the strategy that repeatedly returned him to the lead","gold":5},{"t":7036,"quote":"I bounced off the wall and I thought, 'Oh man, there it goes.' Luckily Osborne was right there behind me, gave me a good old shove and kept my momentum going.","context":"Wade recounts the crucial assist that kept his winning run alive","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Craig Goodenough led the championship entering the event but was explicitly absent and is not included as a participant. Jeremiah Burke was mentioned while pre-race penalties were reviewed, but Anderson later confirmed Burke could not attend; he is likewise excluded. The drivers array contains all 31 names from the starting grid. The broadcast does not read a complete finishing order, but explicitly confirms Wade, Anderson and Kuehl as the podium. John Schoenbachler and Scott Milner use roster canonicals despite heavily variable captions.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Uap1Zzmpjx4":{"recap":"Tim Pope won a bruising 150-lap New Hampshire race after spending most of the night shadowing pole-sitter and Stage 1 winner Alan Vaught. Vaught controlled the early and middle phases, but late netcode contact with Larry Dickerson turned him into Dustyn Eaton and removed him from the lead battle. A subsequent four-wide pileup further scrambled the order before Pope mastered the last six-lap restart and held Jeremiah Burke at bay. Jonathan Osborne charged 23 positions and beat Jack Dixon by just 0.003 seconds in a photo finish for third.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":1396,"title":"Opening-lap netcode brings the first caution","summary":"Michael Everage slides up the track on cold tires and apparent netcode turns him, producing an immediate yellow while Greg Klein narrowly avoids the incident.","tags":["mike-everage","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2025,"title":"Gallagher destroys the truck without a yellow","summary":"John Gallagher gets on the power too early, self-spins through the grass and into the inside fence, then uses the road-course access route to reach pit lane with a meatball flag.","tags":["john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3360,"title":"Two incidents converge on one yellow","summary":"Jonathan Osborne loses control in front of leader Vaught while David Kelly and Greg Klein occupy the same space in a separate crash; Klein spins but avoids major damage.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","david-kelly","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4029,"title":"Vaught holds off Pope for Stage 1","summary":"Pope lunges outside in the final stage laps, but Vaught takes the halfway-stage win ahead of Pope, Larry Dickerson, Trevor Robertson, and Jack Dixon.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","larry-dickerson","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":6172,"title":"Netcode wipes Vaught out of the lead","summary":"Larry Dickerson runs beside Vaught on a late restart and apparent netcode turns the No. 33; Dustyn Eaton cannot avoid Vaught's spinning truck and the yellow flies.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6434,"title":"Four-wide chaos creates a frontstretch parking lot","summary":"Contact among Dillon Bryant, Dickerson, Ricky Whittenburg, Kyle Vaught and others snowballs into a huge Turn 4 pileup that also catches Sean McDonnell, John Gallagher, and Jorge Rincon.","tags":["dylan-bryant","larry-dickerson","ricky-whittenburg","kyle-vaught","shawn-mcdonald","john-gallagher","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6978,"title":"Pope controls the six-lap shootout","summary":"Pope gets the best launch on the final restart while Eaton loses second to Jeremiah Burke and Jack Dixon fights to hold third.","tags":["timothy-pope","dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7058,"title":"The closing laps stay green through multiple spins","summary":"Vaught, Austin Paul, Andrew Coffin, and Ricky Whittenburg all have separate moments in traffic, but the race remains green as Pope pulls clear.","tags":["jess-vaught","austin-paul","andrew-cauthan","ricky-whittenburg","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"chaos"},{"t":7159,"title":"Pope takes the white with Burke closing","summary":"Pope begins the final lap with roughly a one-second advantage while Burke searches for one last run and Osborne closes on Dixon.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":7173,"title":"Pope wins; Osborne steals third by 0.003","summary":"Tim Pope takes the New Hampshire victory over Burke, and Osborne diamonds the final corner to edge Dixon in a microscope-close drag race for third.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1071,"quote":"They'll kill you if you drive into one, so you gotta be careful.","context":"The booth's practical summary of New Hampshire moose.","gold":5},{"t":3507,"quote":"The 49 and the 92 somehow occupied the same space.","context":"The booth diagnoses one half of the double-incident caution.","gold":5},{"t":6237,"quote":"You hate to see the leader get taken out by netcode.","context":"Reaction to Vaught's late crash.","gold":2},{"t":7173,"quote":"The 27 of Timothy Pope finds himself on Victory Lane here tonight at New Hampshire.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":5},{"t":7254,"quote":"Three thousandths of a second between Osborne and Dixon.","context":"The photo-finish margin for third.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The finish call, interviews, and official rundown explicitly confirm Pope, Burke, and Osborne. Osborne's margin over Dixon for third is stated as 0.003 seconds. The notes around Vaught's late crash consistently identify netcode between Vaught and Dickerson before Eaton arrived. The race was dedicated to fallen Rutland, Vermont officer Jessica Ebbighausen; captions render the surname inconsistently, so the recap avoids repeating it.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"UbwmaY0NOyI":{"recap":"Night two at the virtual Bristol Motor Speedway turned VRL Race #9 into a 200-lap survival test, with 15 cautions headlined by a lap-22 frontstretch pileup triggered when Dustin Wade spun up the track into traffic. Polesitter Dillon Bryant dominated the bulk of the race, fending off Larry Dickerson and a fast Craig Goodenough, who briefly took the lead on fresher tires. With about 16 laps to go, Bryant was collected in Mike Adamson's crash while leading, handing the race to the trucks that gambled on late rubber. Jorge Rincon, who pitted with roughly 25 to go for a 40-lap tire advantage, powered past Goodenough on the restart with eight to go and drove away to win from 17th on the grid — a first league victory he said took 12 seasons and 4,000 races to get. John McAdam finished second despite late connection issues, Andrew Player charged from 14th to third, and Kyle Vault was the night's biggest mover, up 20 spots to seventh.","winner":"Jorge Rincon","podium":["Jorge Rincon","John McAdam","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":1232,"title":"Osborne stopped, Gallagher drills him at the stripe","summary":"Caution one: Osborne loops it out of turn four and a blinded Gallagher slams into his door right at start/finish — the booth's first lesson in Bristol's zero visibility.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1661,"title":"The Big One on the frontstretch","summary":"Lap 22: Wade's truck snaps around and climbs the track into traffic, collecting a huge chunk of the field right at start/finish. 'What a mess.'","tags":["dustin-wade","andrew-player","derek-welch","albert-anderson","russ-kilgore","george-rincon","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1891,"title":"Wade wrecks again — Welch's night over early","summary":"One restart later Wade goes up the track again; Welch nails the inside wall with major front-end damage and parks it.","tags":["dustin-wade","derek-welch","andrew-player","anthony-williams"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2180,"title":"Kelly Kuehl wrecked twice in one caution","summary":"Cool spins, then gets clipped again while trying to get righted as Williams uses the pace truck as a pick — 'not in a good way either.'","tags":["kelly-keel","chandler-paul","anthony-williams"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2451,"title":"Dickerson never lifted","summary":"Vaught goes around from second and the replay shows Dickerson got to his bumper and drove straight through him — the booth wonders aloud about bad blood.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4088,"title":"Dickerson rides the fence, then pulls off an impossible save","summary":"Dickerson slaps the fence and jacks up Robertson, then hangs a sideways truck out through one and two and somehow saves it — 'a death sentence half the time.'","tags":["larry-dickerson","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4399,"title":"Goodenough blows past the dominant 51","summary":"On 20-lap fresher tires, Goodenough gets a monster run off two and clears Bryant for the lead — 'the grip he had through the middle and exit of that corner was unreal.'","tags":["craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5101,"title":"The caution drinking game","summary":"Chandler Paul proposes a shot for every caution in chat; the booth does the math on the yellow-flag count: 'By the time it's over, I'm lit.'","tags":["chandler-paul"],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":5566,"title":"Heartbreak — leader Bryant collected with 16 to go","summary":"Adamson wrecks ahead and Bristol's 'self-cleaning racetrack' spits the 88 into Bryant's escape lane — the dominant truck of the night is done, finishing 18th.","tags":["dylan-bryant","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5723,"title":"McAdam's connection flickers in the closing laps","summary":"The second-running 47 briefly disappears to broadcast and competitors alike; McAdam hangs on through it to finish runner-up.","tags":["john-mcadam"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5749,"title":"The exit of a lifetime","summary":"On the restart with about eight to go, Rincon rockets off turn two on 40-lap fresher tires and takes the race lead from Goodenough.","tags":["george-rincon","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5839,"title":"Rincon wins from 17th","summary":"Rincon takes the white with the biggest lead of the night and cruises to his first VRL win — by his own count, 12 seasons and 4,000 races in the making. McAdam steals second from Goodenough on the final lap.","tags":["george-rincon","john-mcadam","andrew-player"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2185,"quote":"Uses the pace truck as a pick — not in a good way, either.","context":"Kelly Kuehl, already wrecked, gets hit again in front of the pace truck","gold":3},{"t":2500,"quote":"Once he got to him, he just drove through him, finished him off.","context":"the booth reviewing Dickerson dumping Vaught for caution six","gold":4},{"t":2563,"quote":"It's Bristol. It's close quarters. It's like flying a fighter jet in a gymnasium. It's chaotic.","context":"summing up the caution-filled night at the half mile","gold":4},{"t":5055,"quote":"Yeah, we like to pretend it's real. A bunch of adult children over here.","context":"answering a chat fan who called the race 'virtual reality'","gold":4},{"t":5111,"quote":"I would almost be open to do that as a broadcaster... By the time it's over, I'm lit.","context":"responding to a fan proposing a shot-per-caution drinking game","gold":3},{"t":5635,"quote":"What's the line from Days of Thunder? The rule is you go straight for him.","context":"breaking down Bryant's failed attempt to dodge the race-losing wreck","gold":4},{"t":5749,"quote":"Rincon — the exit of a lifetime off of turn two, to the inside for the race lead!","context":"the race-winning pass on the restart with eight to go","gold":4},{"t":5866,"quote":"Rincon from 17th — he'll win it at Bristol!","context":"the checkered-flag call on his first career VRL win","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner's surname is heavily garbled in auto-captions (Renone / Ren Con / Ring Con / Ren Cohen / Rancone / Rone / Red Cone); 'Jorge Rincon' is a best guess — he drives the #28 Goodweiser Motorsports entry. 'Alan Vaught' (#33) and 'Andrew Cowan' (#10) are likewise best-guess normalizations of very inconsistent captions. Full finishing order was read on air; booth counted 15 cautions plus a brief red flag, and caution seven had no identified cause. Brian McCann and Connor Leech are mentioned only as racers from the sister Num Thumbs league's race the prior night and are excluded from the driver list. Play-by-play announcer is identified only as Steve. League is off for Easter; next race Talladega on April 30.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"uDJGCuaRkr4":{"recap":"VRL's Throwback Night brought 30 retro-liveried trucks to Talladega for 94 laps, and the field kept it remarkably clean — just one official caution (a Jonathan Osborne spin) plus the lap-47 competition break, with all 30 starters still running at the finish. Trevor Robertson grabbed the stage win at halfway before green-flag fuel cycles under the 70% fuel limit shuffled the pack. Albert Anderson pitted from up front at the stage break — famously for a bathroom run — drove back through the field, then survived a wild sideways trip through the infield grass while leading late. In a last-corner melee that hooked Jack Dixon and Mike Adamson together and sent trucks flipping across the line, Anderson snuck through on the bottom to take what the podium described as his first VRL win, ahead of Dustyn Eaton and Kelly Kuehl. Jeremiah Burke was wrecked out of the lead with three to go and fell to 16th, while Ricky Whittenburg set the fastest lap (50.75) and drew Lucky Draw driver of the day in 19th.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Dustyn Eaton","Kelly Kuehl"],"moments":[{"t":1608,"title":"Green flag at Talladega","summary":"The 30-truck throwback field rumbles through the tri-oval and takes the green for 94 laps.","tags":["albert-anderson","dave-mayberry","david-fite"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1980,"title":"Four-wide gets squirly","summary":"Dillon Bryant sticks it four-wide rather than lift, the booth gasps, and the field squeezes back to three-wide just in time.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2531,"title":"Osborne spins — first caution","summary":"The 81 turns across the 28's nose and spins to the apron; heads-up driving by the whole field avoids calamity as the night's only official caution flies.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","george-rincon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3138,"title":"Whittenburg rips the fastest lap","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg catches a monster draft in the Red Baron 55 and crushes the fastest lap of the night, a 50.75.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3925,"title":"Alan Vaught's grass-trip save","summary":"The 33 starts to go around, corrals it through the infield grass, and rejoins safely to save the caution.","tags":["jess-vaught","kyle-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4310,"title":"Robertson steals the stage win","summary":"Trevor Robertson takes the lap-47 stage win with a big push from Josh Bruner; Albert Anderson third in a 13-truck photo pack.","tags":["trevor-robertson","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5256,"title":"Near Big One — Fight saves it, Taylor snags Rincon","summary":"Carnage brews mid-pack: David Feit saves a wild moment but Mike Taylor comes down off the wall and snags Jorge Rincon — torn-up trucks, yet it stays green.","tags":["david-fite","mike-taylor","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6521,"title":"Anderson's sideways infield save","summary":"Contact sends Osborne hard into the inside wall and shoots leader Albert Anderson sideways through the infield — he stays in the gas, rejoins, and keeps the lead. The booth has never seen anything like it.","tags":["albert-anderson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6636,"title":"Robertson hammers the wall with 8 to go","summary":"The 6 slams the outside wall with heavy right-front damage while David Feit dodges through the infield grass.","tags":["trevor-robertson","david-fite"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6959,"title":"Burke wrecked out of the lead","summary":"Leading with three to go, Jeremiah Burke gets turned by the 07 into the inside pit wall as the white flag flies — from the lead to 16th.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7001,"title":"Last-corner mayhem — Anderson sneaks through","summary":"Three-wide off turn four, the 07 and 88 hook together and trucks go flipping and flying as the field wrecks across the line — Albert Anderson threads the bottom lane to win over Dustyn Eaton and Kelly Kuehl.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-eaton","kelly-keel","jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8359,"title":"\"Went to the can and won the race\"","summary":"The booth crowns Anderson's bathroom-break-to-Victory-Lane run as legendary, comparing it to Earnhardt wiping his own windshield.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1980,"quote":"Oh, getting squirly — we're four wide! Oh no, this is going to get a little tight.","context":"Dillon Bryant forces four-wide early in the race","gold":3},{"t":3466,"quote":"You know what Swift stands for, don't you? Stevie Wonder's Institute For Trucking.","context":"Trucker story time during a long green-flag run","gold":3},{"t":5075,"quote":"I didn't see him blink — is he a lizard person?","context":"Riding onboard with Greg Dobson's driver cam","gold":3},{"t":6566,"quote":"He went down into the infield sideways, came back on track and maintained the lead — I've never seen that before.","context":"Anderson's infield save while leading late","gold":4},{"t":6906,"quote":"We go three by three by three by three by three by three, all the way back through this field.","context":"The entire pack goes three-wide with three laps to go","gold":4},{"t":7012,"quote":"Slipping and sliding, beating and banging — the 07 goes way up high, Albert Anderson on the bottom line sneaks on through as they wreck across the line!","context":"The last-corner pileup as Anderson steals the win","gold":5},{"t":8359,"quote":"The guy went to the can during a pit stop and he came back and won the race — I mean, that's legendary.","context":"The booth summing up Anderson's bathroom-break win","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption surname guesses: 'Vaught' heard as vot/VA/vault (could be Vogt); 'David Feit' possibly Fite; 'Jorge Rincon' heard as ringcon/rancon/ranan/Mone; 'Josh Bruner' heard as 'bner'; 'Andrew Cofton' heard as cin/cofton. Kelly Kuehl said 'I think that's his first win' about Anderson — first-win claim not fully confirmed. Jess and Lori (Vaught) run the league; Lori was race control, not racing. Adam Turner joined the booth late (~1:22:30) after travel-delay bits. Full 30-truck finishing order is read out starting ~2:20:17 (8417s); 30 started, 30 finished, no DNFs. Stage break was at lap 47; fuel limit 70% (~24 laps per tank) drove green-flag pit strategy.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"UgOkp6PkPic":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson led the Resurrection Road 135 from pole until a lap-five spin handed control to Chris Goans, while Jonathan Osborne began a remarkable recovery after spinning from third in the opening corner. Goans built a lead through the first fuel cycle, but the scheduled lap-28 competition caution reset the field and Osborne and Scott Rooney stayed out on older tires to gain track position. After Osborne's later stop, Jacob Alesia led Goans and Craig Goodenough through an intense sequence in which Alesia slid the truck aggressively while Goans preserved the tires he planned to double-stint. Goans ran longest, took only a late splash of fuel, and coasted home with 0.1 gallons remaining to beat Alesia, while Osborne's alternate strategy carried him all the way back to third.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Jacob Alesia","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":1512,"title":"Robertson leads the Resurrection Road start","summary":"Pole-sitter Robertson gets the jump into Turn 1 with Bryant, Goans, Goodenough, and Alesia settling into the early lead group.","tags":["trevor-robertson","dylan-bryant","chris-goans","craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1528,"title":"Osborne spins from third in Turn 1","summary":"Osborne catches too much curb on cold tires and rotates, but lights up the rears to stay clear of traffic and avoids damage before beginning a charge from 26th.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":1746,"title":"The pole-sitter loses control","summary":"Robertson spins from a 2.7-second lead without hitting the barrier, dropping to fifth and elevating Goans to first after the order sorts out.","tags":["trevor-robertson","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2841,"title":"The first fuel cycle returns Goans to first","summary":"The early stoppers include Robertson, Goodenough, Dixon, and Adamson; after the long runners finally pit around lap 19, Goans reassumes the lead over Alesia with a growing advantage.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3556,"title":"The scheduled halfway caution resets the field","summary":"Lori throws the race's only planned full-course caution at the start of lap 28, erasing Goans's 4.5-second lead and opening a fresh strategy split.","tags":["chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":3816,"title":"Osborne and Rooney stay out","summary":"While Goans, Alesia, Robertson, and nearly every lead-lap rival take service, Osborne and Rooney retain their lap-19 tires and move to the front for the restart.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","scott-rooney","chris-goans","jacob-alicia","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4125,"title":"Robertson spins in the restart stack-up","summary":"Goans gets loose ahead of Robertson, forcing the No. 6 to check up into Goodenough; Robertson rotates and Dixon arrives with nowhere to go, sustaining major rear damage.","tags":["chris-goans","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4565,"title":"Osborne's long stint hands the lead to Alesia","summary":"After holding older tires at the front for 17 laps, Osborne finally pits for his last fuel and tires; Alesia inherits the lead with Goans and Goodenough close behind.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jacob-alicia","chris-goans","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4713,"title":"Goans chooses track position over fresh tires","summary":"Goodenough short-pits and Alesia follows several laps later for four tires, but Goans stays out, protects his warmed double-stinted set, and creates enough margin for a fuel-only finish.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jacob-alicia","chris-goans"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5193,"title":"Dixon, Robertson, and Goodenough crash late","summary":"Robertson runs out of room trying to slot behind Dixon's defensive line after the carousel, then makes contact with Goodenough; Dixon and Goodenough both receive hard secondary hits.","tags":["jack-dixon","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":5389,"title":"Goans splashes fuel with six to go","summary":"Goans stops from a 13-second lead, takes no tires, and rejoins with more than 11 seconds over Alesia once temporary leader Rincon makes his own final stop.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5869,"title":"Goans coasts home on fumes","summary":"The engine sounds nearly silent through the final bus stop as Goans saves the last drops of fuel, but he crosses more than three seconds ahead of Alesia; Osborne completes his lap-one recovery in third.","tags":["chris-goans","jacob-alicia","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1247,"quote":"Watkins Glen rewards precision, rhythm, and bravery. Sometimes you're going to have to make a lane and pray that your truck sticks.","context":"The broadcast previews the Cup-layout challenge","gold":5},{"t":1999,"quote":"Even when you're wrecking, you should still be driving your truck.","context":"The booth praises drivers who control spins and protect traffic","gold":5},{"t":6210,"quote":"That race-whisperer strategy actually kind of worked out for me, not pitting there on the caution.","context":"Third-place Jonathan Osborne reflects on staying out at halfway","gold":5},{"t":6255,"quote":"That was probably the hardest I've ever driven at a road course in my life and not wadded it up after Turn 1.","context":"Osborne describes his last-to-third recovery","gold":5},{"t":6328,"quote":"Being aggressive required some combination of yanking on the wheel and being very gentle with the gas pedal.","context":"Runner-up Jacob Alesia explains the unusual driving technique","gold":5},{"t":6554,"quote":"At the last stop, I didn't take any tires. I figured the time it took to get those tires warmed up would cost me in the long run.","context":"Winner Chris Goans explains his decisive final stop","gold":5},{"t":6616,"quote":"I didn't want to burn my tires up knowing that I wasn't going to take any on that last stop.","context":"Goans explains why he patiently followed Alesia","gold":4},{"t":6626,"quote":"I was at 0.1 when I hit the line at the checkers.","context":"Goans reveals how narrowly his fuel calculation worked","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 13, Round 8 at Watkins Glen according to seasons_map.json. The Resurrection Road 135 ran 55 laps on the 2.45-mile Cup layout with 65% fuel, unlimited tire sets, no fast repairs, a 33-incident drive-through threshold plus six-point increments, local cautions only, and one planned full-course competition caution at lap 28. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Goans-Alesia-Osborne podium and reads all 26 classified drivers. Aaron Warren started at the rear because of a Chicagoland penalty; Albert Anderson retired with a mechanical problem. Caption variants are normalized to roster spellings including Chris Goans, Andrew Coffin, Stony Benfield, John Schoenbachler, and Kelly Kuehl. Alan Vaught identified himself only as Alan in the solo booth, and Lori served as race administrator rather than broadcaster. All timestamps fall within the 6,890-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ulqW7ILHLFA":{"recap":"Josh Bittner stayed patient through a changing-track 50-lap race on Sonoma's historic Cup layout and capitalized on Alan Vaught's late hairpin mistake to take the win. Vaught had led almost the entire first half and won the competition stage, but overheated his rear tires while fighting Bittner and finally ran wide in the hairpin. The restart after halfway was chaotic, with Osborne crashing from second and a separate pileup involving Robert Jordan, Rob Green and Kelly Kuehl, yet the remainder ran green. Bittner won by more than two seconds over Vaught, while Jorge Rincon used contact and a last-corner mistake by John Ellis to reclaim third at the line.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Alan Vaught","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1909,"title":"Osborne and Vaught lead the start","summary":"Pole-sitter Osborne and Vaught launch from the front row, with the field navigating Sonoma's narrow opening corners on hot tires.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2183,"title":"Kuehl spins climbing the hill","summary":"Kelly Kuehl loses the truck on the uphill section and falls from the top ten, one of several early single-truck mistakes that remain green.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2624,"title":"Osborne spins out of the lead fight","summary":"Osborne loses control after challenging Vaught, handing Vaught a clearer path to dominate the remainder of the opening stage.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":3695,"title":"Vaught wins the first half","summary":"Vaught reaches the scheduled competition yellow first after nearly leading flag to flag, while Earl Evans spins just ahead of him in the Esses.","tags":["jess-vaught","earl-evans"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3939,"title":"Fuel shortages complicate the caution","summary":"Several trucks run dry or nearly dry during the extended yellow, but Vaught wins the race off pit road over Osborne, Rincon, Bittner and Pope.","tags":["jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne","george-rincon","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4372,"title":"Osborne crashes from second","summary":"On cold tires after the restart, Osborne loses control in a bad spot and strikes the wall while trying to attack Vaught.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4405,"title":"Separate pileup tears up three trucks","summary":"Robert Jordan spins and T-bones Rob Green, with Kelly Kuehl flying into the same incident as the field struggles on cold tires.","tags":["robert-jordan","rob-green","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5953,"title":"Pope spins out of third","summary":"With two laps remaining, Pope slides through Turn 7 and surrenders the final podium position to Ellis and Rincon.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-ellis","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":6032,"title":"Final lap erupts behind Bittner","summary":"Everage and Osborne make contact, Ottinger has another off, and Ellis and Rincon run side by side for third while Bittner remains clear.","tags":["mike-everage","jonathan-osborne","jeff-ottinger","john-ellis","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"final_lap"},{"t":6078,"title":"Bittner wins; Rincon muscles to third","summary":"Bittner holds off Vaught to win, and Rincon beats and bangs with teammate Ellis through the final hairpin to take third after Ellis runs wide.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught","george-rincon","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6078,"quote":"Josh Bittner wins here at Sonoma!","context":"The live victory call.","gold":2},{"t":6344,"quote":"I'm like sweating bullets right now.","context":"Rincon reacts after wrestling the loose truck to third.","gold":5},{"t":6432,"quote":"There's no passing zone here at all.","context":"Rincon explains why he waited for mistakes rather than forcing moves.","gold":5},{"t":6642,"quote":"I gave that one away, man.","context":"Vaught accepts responsibility for losing the lead to Bittner.","gold":5},{"t":7331,"quote":"I felt like I cheated death a couple of times there with some lap cars.","context":"Bittner opens his winner interview.","gold":5},{"t":7630,"quote":"It's a completely different track at different points in the race.","context":"Bittner describes Sonoma's dramatic grip changes with sun and clouds.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews, and full results rundown explicitly confirm Bittner, Vaught, and Rincon. Jeremiah Burke was hard charger at plus 17 positions; Ricky Whittenburg won the random draw after finishing sixth while driving with an injured right arm. The 50-lap event used Sonoma's historic Cup configuration and a scheduled halfway caution. Twenty-two of 25 starters were still classified as finishers. The finish call and rundown place Rincon third after the contact with Ellis; both drivers were teammates and Rincon said he would not have forced the move before the final corner.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"UpR5HKiNBXM":{"recap":"Albert Anderson started from pole and led the patient opening run at Daytona, but the 31-truck field steadily built a second lane and cycled the lead through coordinated green-flag stops. A chain-reaction crash as the field rejoined from the first pit sequence produced the first caution, then long green stretches rewarded teams that could enter pit road together without penalties. The final quarter erupted: Robert Jordan's truck snapped across the pack, Russ Kilgore's wall contact sent Jonathan Osborne across traffic, and a four-to-go Big One launched trucks into the air before a one-shot green-white-checker. Dustin Riehle and Tim Pope locked bumpers on the bottom through last-lap crashes, giving Riehle his first official VRL win ahead of Alan Vaught and Pope.","winner":"Dustin Riehle","podium":["Dustin Riehle","Alan Vaught","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1818,"title":"Kuehl catches the first major wiggle","summary":"Dustin Riehle moves down just short of clear and Kelly Kuehl gets the truck nearly sideways at the front, but saves it without triggering the pack.","tags":["dustin-reilly","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2160,"title":"Kuehl launches the outside lane","summary":"Kelly Kuehl gets a huge shove from Mike and Dale Adamson and surges alongside Riehle for the lead as Daytona's second lane finally comes alive.","tags":["kelly-keel","dustin-reilly","mike-adamson","dale-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2524,"title":"Three-wide funnel into pit road","summary":"The first full fuel cycle compresses Anderson, Mike Adamson, and the arriving pack three-wide at pit entry, narrowly avoiding a disaster before the real trouble begins on rejoin.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2635,"title":"Pit rejoin turns into helter-skelter carnage","summary":"A bump involving Anderson and Mike Adamson sends the 51 into Kuehl and starts a scattered chain reaction that catches Alan Vaught, Jeffrey Ottinger, Michael Everage, and Riehle before the caution flies.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-adamson","kelly-keel","jess-vaught","jeff-ottinger","mike-everage","dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3895,"title":"Endicott scrapes the wall and jams the fuel window","summary":"Russ Endicott tags the outside wall while stranded in the upper lane, creating a major checkup and forcing Dale Adamson toward pit road as the second cycle begins.","tags":["russ-endicott","dale-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5745,"title":"Earl Evans spins as the leaders dive for fuel","summary":"Earl Evans rotates onto the apron without drawing a caution at the exact moment Vaught, Kuehl, and Riehle commit to their final green-flag stop.","tags":["earl-evans","jess-vaught","kelly-keel","dustin-reilly"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5980,"title":"Jordan snaps across the pack","summary":"Robert Jordan's No. 204 suddenly hooks left as if a tire or control failed, turning Josh Bittner and collecting Douglas Camp and Austin Paul in the crash that resets the field.","tags":["robert-jordan","josh-bittner","douglas-camp","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6404,"title":"Kilgore's wall strike sends Osborne across traffic","summary":"Russ Kilgore hits the wall in the late restart pack and three or four trucks stack up; Jonathan Osborne shoots hard back across the track directly in front of Dale Adamson.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jonathan-osborne","dale-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6806,"title":"The four-to-go Big One launches the field","summary":"A tiny squeeze at the front becomes the night's signature pileup: Justin French and Russ Kilgore go airborne, Kelly Kuehl pounds the inside wall, and Earl Evans is among the trucks eliminated.","tags":["justin-french","russ-kilgore","kelly-keel","earl-evans"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7130,"title":"One shot at a green-white-checker","summary":"With only one overtime attempt permitted, Riehle lines up beside Vaught while Tim Pope and Dave Mayberry supply the pushes and 17 lead-lap trucks still have a chance.","tags":["dustin-reilly","jess-vaught","timothy-pope","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7192,"title":"Crashes everywhere; Riehle wins the drag race","summary":"Pope shoves Riehle clear on the bottom as wrecks break out behind the leaders at the white flag and again in the final corners; Riehle beats Vaught to the stripe for his first VRL win, with Pope third.","tags":["dustin-reilly","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":882,"quote":"You can go from chump to champ in no time — and vice versa.","context":"The booth explains Daytona's volatility","gold":4},{"t":2652,"quote":"It wasn't one crazy hard wreck; it was all scattered around helter-skelter.","context":"The first pit-cycle crash spreads across the track","gold":4},{"t":6815,"quote":"We've got trucks going into outer space!","context":"The four-to-go Big One launches multiple trucks","gold":5},{"t":7138,"quote":"It's time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet, and throw inhibition out that window.","context":"The one-shot overtime restart","gold":5},{"t":7230,"quote":"We're going to be drag racing down here across the line!","context":"Riehle and Vaught race through last-lap wrecks","gold":5},{"t":8418,"quote":"You get the whole mixed bag: green-flag racing, crazy cautions, trucks going to outer space, and drag races to the finish.","context":"The booth sums up a complete Daytona spectacle","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"A 100-lap, 250-mile Daytona truck race with manual cautions and 70% fuel. Winner and podium are explicitly called, interviewed, and repeated in the final results. Dustin's surname is consistently auto-captioned 'Really'; the archive uses the best-guess spelling Riehle, but this remains unconfirmed. The opening grid and full finishing order establish 31 starters. The first caution's initiating contact may include netcode — Anderson said he did not feel contact with Adamson — so the recap avoids assigning intent.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"UYyKA70V2qY":{"recap":"Greg Klein converted pole into his first VRL victory at Circuit of the Americas, combining clean laps with superior tire preservation. The race ran without a stage caution; Klein collected the halfway bonus while pit sequences repeatedly reshuffled him behind hard-charging Dustyn Eaton and Alan Vaught. Eaton climbed 14 places and traded aggressive crossovers and light contact with Vaught until Vaught spun while applying power. Klein then swept past the loose Eaton with three laps remaining and drove clear, while Eaton survived Vaught's last-lap attack to retain second.","winner":"Greg Cline","podium":["Greg Cline","Dustyn Eaton","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1526,"title":"Klein controls the climb into Turn 1","summary":"Pole-sitter Greg Klein clears Trevor Robertson through COTA's opening hairpin as the large field compresses and scrambles behind them.","tags":["greg-cline","trevor-robertson","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1880,"title":"Robertson turns up the early pressure","summary":"Trevor Robertson cuts Klein's lead below a second with a 2:19.23 lap, while Vaught remains close enough to join the lead fight.","tags":["trevor-robertson","greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2830,"title":"Adamson opens the pit cycle","summary":"Mike Adamson is the first front-running taker on pit road, beginning a long green-flag sequence across the 3.4-mile circuit.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3984,"title":"Klein wins the caution-free stage","summary":"Klein crosses the line first at the halfway stage marker; race control awards the points without interrupting the green-flag race.","tags":["greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":5043,"title":"Eaton emerges second after the stops","summary":"After the later pit cycle, Dustyn Eaton moves around Klein into second and begins hunting Vaught for the lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","greg-cline","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5145,"title":"Eaton and Vaught trade crossovers","summary":"The No. 14 and No. 33 exchange inches through successive braking zones, putting on a hard but largely respectful fight for the lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5673,"title":"Vaught spins while powering out","summary":"After another crossover, Vaught loses the rear while applying power and spins; replay does not show clear contact from Eaton.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":5833,"title":"Klein takes back the lead","summary":"Eaton gets wickedly loose on worn tires and tire-saving Klein drives by to regain the lead with three laps remaining.","tags":["greg-cline","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6256,"title":"Eaton fends off Vaught for second","summary":"On the final lap Vaught closes under a second and reaches Eaton's bumper, but leaves room as they fight through the arena section.","tags":["dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6293,"title":"Klein claims his first VRL win","summary":"Klein exits the final corner unchallenged to win at COTA, while Eaton beats Vaught to the line for second.","tags":["greg-cline","dustin-eaton","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1164,"quote":"Once the smoke comes out of your electrical appliances, they're no longer any good.","context":"The booth discusses Earl Evans racing on a controller after wheel trouble.","gold":5},{"t":3080,"quote":"Don't overdrive the entry and wheel hop, and don't get on the throttle too early and spin.","context":"Jack Dixon's chat advice for surviving COTA.","gold":2},{"t":5141,"quote":"The state might flip over if they finish that Amazon warehouse.","context":"A long Texas tangent while Eaton closes on Vaught.","gold":5},{"t":6267,"quote":"These guys are fighting harder than the real Mrs. Poindexter.","context":"The booth calls the last-lap battle for second.","gold":5},{"t":6293,"quote":"Greg Klein making his way up and through the final corner—he is going to be your race winner.","context":"The live victory call.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The finish call, interviews, and final results explicitly confirm Klein, Eaton, and Vaught. No stage caution was used; the stage points were awarded while green. Replay analysis around Vaught's late spin was divided at first, but the booth ultimately stated it saw no contact from Eaton, so the moment is described as a self-spin under power. Roster mapping is applied to Andrew Coffin and Dustin Riehle.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"vGu8dwYFR9M":{"recap":"Jim Ott won the 150-lap Nashville Superspeedway race after building his No. 205 for the long run and executing three clean green-flag pit cycles. Tim Pope started on pole and traded the lead with Ott through the opening stint, while Alan Vaught remained close until a botched downshift on pit entry cost him time. Ott's first undercut produced a lead of more than two seconds, and his final stop again left Pope unable to close as traffic and worn tires spread the contenders apart. The entire race ran without a caution; Pope finished second, Vaught recovered to third, and Russ Kilgore held off Mike Adamson for fourth.","winner":"Jim Ott","podium":["Jim Ott","Tim Pope","Alan Vaught"],"moments":[{"t":1376,"title":"Pope and Ott lead Nashville green","summary":"Polesitter Tim Pope leads Jim Ott and Eric Klafka through a clean opening while battles immediately form deeper in the field.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1610,"title":"Ott takes the lead","summary":"Ott passes Pope for the point, and Pope immediately crosses back underneath to begin the night's defining lead battle.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2058,"title":"Three trucks tangle without a yellow","summary":"Chandler Paul checks up in Turn 1, Michael Everage reaches his rear, and Chandler, Jack Dixon, and Albert Anderson scatter into the infield; the racing surface clears and the race stays green.","tags":["chandler-paul","mike-everage","jack-dixon","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2542,"title":"First green stops begin","summary":"The first pit takers arrive around lap 38, confirming a likely three-stop race as Mike Adamson and the lead group begin cycling through.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2831,"title":"Ott's undercut pays off","summary":"Ott emerges from the first cycle more than two seconds ahead of Pope and Vaught after a strong stop and fast out-lap.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3200,"title":"Dixon's blocking sparks bad blood","summary":"Lapped Jack Dixon repeatedly pinches Albert Anderson while trying to remain ahead, sending Anderson through the grass before he finally completes the pass.","tags":["jack-dixon","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3915,"title":"Vaught passes Pope for second","summary":"Pope makes a small mistake in traffic and Vaught slips through, briefly taking second while Ott remains roughly 12 seconds clear.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4520,"title":"Vaught's pit-entry mistake costs time","summary":"During the next cycle, Vaught double-clutches an unintended downshift on pit entry and hits the wall, damaging his chance to challenge Ott.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4898,"title":"Ott completes the final stop","summary":"Ott makes the last scheduled stop after the alternate-strategy runners cycle through, preserving command for the final run to the flag.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6217,"title":"Ott conquers the concrete","summary":"Ott takes the checkered flag without pressure, followed by Pope and Vaught; Kilgore beats Adamson in the final battle for fourth.","tags":["jim-ott","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","russ-kilgore","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3220,"quote":"You can feel it, like when you're in a tavern and the vibe just gets like it might be time for me to step on.","context":"The booth senses tension in the Dixon-Anderson traffic battle","gold":4},{"t":6404,"quote":"My mistake was I'm using paddle shifters, and I kind of double-clutched my downshift when I wasn't intending to.","context":"Alan Vaught explains the pit-entry mistake that cost his shot at the win","gold":4},{"t":6628,"quote":"I was trying to stay up with him to try to force him to make a mistake or burn his stuff up, but he scrubbed the wall a couple times and I just couldn't capitalize.","context":"Tim Pope describes chasing Ott","gold":5},{"t":6898,"quote":"I don't know whether it's because I'm Canadian—we're just generally nice.","context":"Greg Dobson discusses yielding to faster leaders","gold":4},{"t":7138,"quote":"It wasn't easy, guys. Timothy was fast off the go, and I had a setup for the long run. I relied on that heavily tonight.","context":"Jim Ott explains his winning advantage","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The race ran all 150 laps without a caution; the only substantial early wreck cleared before the leaders returned. The grid narration says Russ Endicott rounded out 28th but names only 27 starters, and the complete final order also contains 27; the drivers array follows the final order. The final readout garbles Jeff Ottinger as 'Bonger' in 11th, but the No. 76 and earlier calls make the identity explicit.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"VJEEMJEctMc":{"recap":"The Vigilante Vow 200 opened Season 14 of the VRL Premiere Series with a massive 38-truck field under the lights at virtual Daytona, headlined by a lap-three lap of silence honoring Dale Earnhardt Sr. 25 years after his passing. The field ran nearly 46 laps caution-free through a round of green-flag pit stops before the night turned wild: a 14-truck Big One around lap 68, an 11-to-go pileup that left a truck on its lid, and a final-lap wreck in turn one. Albert Anderson, the league's acknowledged superspeedway master, controlled the outside line in the No. 99 Toe Call machine and drove away as the field wrecked behind him to win the opener. Chris Goans finished second and Jason Gaines completed the podium in his first race back from a season-long hiatus, while Anderson dedicated the win to his late aunt Vivian Chadwick.","winner":"Albert Anderson","podium":["Albert Anderson","Chris Goans","Jason Gaines"],"moments":[{"t":661,"title":"25 Years Since the Intimidator","summary":"Alan announces a lap-three lap of silence honoring Dale Earnhardt Sr., 25 years after his passing, with a heartfelt tribute to his tenacity and grit.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":787,"title":"Season 14 Goes Green","summary":"The 38-truck field takes the green flag to open the 18-round chase for the VRL Cup, with newcomer Gordon Spain timing the launch perfectly at the front.","tags":["gordon-spain","dylan-bryant","greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1186,"title":"The 75-Year-Old Yacht Broker","summary":"Ricky cracks that newcomer Gordon Spain's name sounds like a 75-year-old yacht broker from Toulon, France — and he turns out to be a young man.","tags":["gordon-spain"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2006,"title":"Barish Smacks the Wall on Pit Entry","summary":"During the green-flag pit cycle, the No. 35 of Tom Barish spins and smacks the inside wall trying to slow down for pit lane after getting a nudge.","tags":["tom-barish"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2933,"title":"First Caution Flies","summary":"The first caution of the season comes out just before green-flag stops as Andrew Cawthon tries to clear himself for pit lane and spins, collecting Rooney and Milner — trucks spin everywhere but almost nobody hits anything.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","scott-rooney","scott-milner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3163,"title":"Kyle's Comeback Interview","summary":"Back from real-life injury rehab and up 27 spots in a fresh Shokker Grafix paint scheme, Kyle joins the booth mid-race and explains his green-flag tire gamble.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3716,"title":"Kelly Kuehl's Apron Save","summary":"Kelly Kuehl gets forced down onto the apron at speed and hangs onto it in a wild save — 'Man, what a job' — while the 92 of Greg Klein spins behind him.","tags":["kelly-keel","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4097,"title":"THE BIG ONE — 14 Trucks","summary":"The Big One erupts up front around lap 68: at least 14 trucks involved, started when Kelly Kuehl and Scott Milner get together — Miller, Pope, Mayberry, Reading, Chandler Paul, Alesia, Gallagher, McDonnell, Barish, Klein, Dobson, Dixon and Rincon all swept in.","tags":["kelly-keel","scott-milner","shawn-mcdonald","timothy-pope","dave-mayberry","jesse-redding","chandler-paul","jacob-alicia","john-gallagher","tom-barish","greg-cline","greg-dobson","jack-dixon","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4307,"title":"Osborne Rides the Storm","summary":"Replay shows Jonathan Osborne getting spun in the Big One, sliding completely sideways with trucks spinning past him, then gathering it up and driving away with basically no damage.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4716,"title":"Truck on Its Lid With 11 To Go","summary":"A three-wide, twelve-deep pack erupts again with 11 laps to go — Kyle and Cawthon trigger it, Mayberry goes upside down, and a truck ends up on its lid on top of another; Mike Adamson a total victim.","tags":["jess-vaught","andrew-cauthan","mike-adamson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5105,"title":"Alesia Gets Sent on the Restart","summary":"On the restart with eight to go, Jacob Alesia gets turned sideways and breaks up the pack, then Kevin Hunt triggers another wreck behind the leaders moments later.","tags":["jacob-alicia","kevin-hunt","trevor-robertson","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5656,"title":"Anderson Wins as They Wreck Behind Him","summary":"Albert Anderson takes the white flag on the outside line, they wreck in turn one behind him, and the No. 99 Toe Call machine brings it home to win the Season 14 opener over Chris Goans and Jason Gaines.","tags":["albert-anderson","chris-goans","jason-gaines","dylan-bryant","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":272,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"VRN's signature broadcast bumper as the stream opens","gold":4},{"t":739,"quote":"Sorry, I'm a little medicated. I've got the flu, so I've got all kinds of stuff going through me tonight.","context":"Ricky, battling the flu, disclaims his pre-race predictions","gold":3},{"t":862,"quote":"Looking good so far, Ricky. Looks like rush hour on the LA Freeway.","context":"Alan on the 38-truck pack running nose to tail early","gold":3},{"t":1186,"quote":"Gordon Spain sounds like a 75-year-old yacht broker from Toulon, France — and he looks like a young man.","context":"Ricky sizing up the race-leading newcomer by name alone","gold":4},{"t":3433,"quote":"I got to tell you, Taylor, if he can't bring home this victory for you, I don't know, maybe you should start looking around for, you know, better options.","context":"Alan roasting Kyle's partner Taylor cheering in the chat","gold":4},{"t":4097,"quote":"They're wrecking up front. Wrecking up front. Big red. Oh, massive.","context":"The live call as the 14-truck Big One erupts","gold":4},{"t":5690,"quote":"Albert Anderson is going to come bring it home here and he wins the first race of season 14. Congratulations to the 99 machine!","context":"The winning call as the field wrecks behind Anderson","gold":4},{"t":6670,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, and above all else, stay vigilante.","context":"Alan's signature sign-off closing the broadcast","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner and full results clearly stated on tape (results read at 1:49:16). Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Kyle Vogt' (captions render Kyle Bach/Vaude/Vault/Vot/Kyog — 17th in results), 'Scott Milner' vs 'Scott Miller' used interchangeably for the No. 19, 'John Schoenbachler' inferred from Shanebach/Shanebacher/Shane Barkler variants (Louisville KY driver, No. 12), and 'Chris Gones' also appears as Gomes/Gome. 'Jonathan Ray' appears once and likely garbles Jonathan Osborne. Lori (Alan's wife) is race admin/control, not a booth commentator; her computer froze mid-race. Race is NASCAR Trucks, 80 laps / 200 miles at Daytona, 38 starters, no championship points for round 1. Broadcast includes a Dale Earnhardt Sr. 25th-anniversary tribute lap of silence on lap 3. Anderson dedicated the win to his late aunt Vivian Chadwick.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"VmG-Bd2ECvQ":{"recap":"Craig Goodenough led the Arch Nemesis 150 from pole, but Gateway's varying braking points produced a succession of early cautions that caught contenders throughout the field. Tim Pope was hit repeatedly in a lap-33 restart wreck yet escaped with only 32 seconds of repairs, while Goodenough later compounded an early pit stop with a speeding penalty and had to charge forward again. In the last green-flag cycle, Pope, Goodenough, and Dillon Bryant stopped safely inside the fuel window while Andy Player stayed out and tried to stretch a lap-77 tank to the finish. Player finally ran dry on strategy with six laps left, giving Pope the lead; Pope held off Goodenough's closing attack after the No. 89 tagged the wall, and Bryant completed the podium.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Craig Goodenough","Dillon Bryant"],"moments":[{"t":878,"title":"Goodenough launches from Gateway pole","summary":"Goodenough gets a clean jump over Pope while Dustyn Eaton and Bryant contest third at the start of the 120-lap race.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope","dustin-eaton","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":929,"title":"Osborne spin sparks an opening-lap pileup","summary":"Osborne loses the truck exiting the corner, Gallagher makes an evasive move across the track, and Kuehl is collected hard enough to require roughly eight minutes of repairs.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","john-gallagher","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":1468,"title":"Bittner and Dixon are swept into caution two","summary":"Player gets deep into McAdam and both save four-wheel slides, but the chain reaction leaves Bittner crossing Dixon's committed line; both spin without a major wall impact.","tags":["andrew-player","john-mcadam","josh-bittner","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2318,"title":"Pope survives a multi-hit restart wreck","summary":"Burke reaches Pope's door after trying to downshift for the corner, and the ensuing scramble nudges Pope several times before he finally spins; despite two heavy blows, the championship contender avoids terminal damage.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":2562,"title":"Bryant's fresh tires erase Anderson's gamble","summary":"Anderson and Dixon stay out on older tires, but Bryant and Burke quickly drive through after the restart, with Bryant taking the lead while Pope begins another recovery.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","jack-dixon","jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":3477,"title":"Dixon and Everage collide during green stops","summary":"Dixon, only a few laps removed from service, misjudges the grip into Turn 3 and contacts Everage just after both had pitted, bringing out a badly timed caution for the early stoppers.","tags":["jack-dixon","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3746,"title":"Three-wide braking differences ignite another wreck","summary":"Schoenbachler is hit twice after drivers choose sharply different braking points, with Hunt and Rincon tangled in the avoidance; under the yellow, McAdam then turns hard into the wall to miss Everage and disconnects.","tags":["john-schoenbachler","kevin-hunt","george-rincon","john-mcadam","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":5134,"title":"Burke starts the money-stop sequence","summary":"With 25 laps remaining and fresh tires worth about 1.5 seconds per lap, Burke pits first; Goodenough and Bryant follow one lap later, then Pope joins them.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5276,"title":"Player bets on stretching lap-77 fuel","summary":"Player stays in fourth gear where possible and tries to turn a 43-lap stint into the winning move while Osborne and the other long runners cycle ahead temporarily.","tags":["andrew-player","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5832,"title":"Player's fuel gamble expires with six to go","summary":"Still holding a large apparent lead, Player finally has to pit and falls to 12th, handing the real fight for the win to Pope and the rapidly closing Goodenough.","tags":["andrew-player","timothy-pope","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5939,"title":"Goodenough's last charge reaches the wall","summary":"Goodenough dives into the corner while within half a second of Pope, gets loose on exit, and tags the wall, losing the momentum needed for a final attack.","tags":["craig-goodenough","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":6035,"title":"Pope completes the Gateway comeback","summary":"Pope takes the checkered flag for his third win of the season, with Goodenough second and points leader Bryant finishing a clean, incident-free third.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":717,"quote":"Gateway is fun. It's kind of like an overgrown short track.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg summarizes the circuit before the race","gold":5},{"t":1583,"quote":"Next thing you know, I felt my butt getting slapped and I was locked up staring at the inside wall.","context":"Josh Bittner gives a colorful account of the second caution","gold":5},{"t":3537,"quote":"He had just come off pit lane, so he probably didn't have the grip yet.","context":"The booth diagnoses Dixon's collision with Everage","gold":4},{"t":5225,"quote":"This is the money stop, folks.","context":"The final green-flag pit window opens","gold":4},{"t":5776,"quote":"It's got to be frustrating for Bryant and Pope because they don't know if they're racing for the win or if they're racing for second.","context":"Player's fuel gamble obscures the true late-race lead battle","gold":5},{"t":6595,"quote":"I felt like Justin Allgaier at Phoenix, just doing everything I possibly could to finish last.","context":"Runner-up Craig Goodenough jokes about his pit mistakes and recovery","gold":5},{"t":6819,"quote":"I thought I was cooked after that one because I got hit twice pretty good.","context":"Winner Tim Pope recalls the early wreck he survived","gold":5},{"t":6931,"quote":"It's almost like a superspeedway of short tracks. It's just an overgrown short track.","context":"Whittenburg closes the broadcast by explaining Gateway's racing character","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 12, Round 10 at Gateway according to seasons_map.json. The Arch Nemesis 150 ran 120 laps with 65% fuel, five total tire sets, no fast repairs, a 25-incident threshold plus disqualification step, and iRacing-controlled cautions and wave-arounds. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Pope-Goodenough-Bryant podium and reads all 30 classified drivers. Trevor Robertson and Greg Klein were classified despite pre-race technical or connection problems, while Scott Rooney and John McAdam disconnected during the event. Dustyn Eaton is retained as the distinct Season 12 driver used by this broadcast and the preceding Darlington distill; captioned Andrew Cawin/Cawkins is normalized to Andrew Coffin. Canonical roster spellings are used for the remaining caption variants. All timestamps fall within the 7,018-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"vpuSUiJHSO0":{"recap":"After 14 weeks, the inaugural Vigilante Racing League season came down to a 100-lap, 200-mile championship finale at a blistering 115-degree Michigan. Polesitter and points leader Tim Pope survived a wreck-filled night that included his own mid-race spin-and-pileup, a lead-pack crash that ended title contender Jeremiah Burke's race and got Albert Anderson III disqualified on incident points, and a late Big One that sent Jack Dixon flipping upside down through the air. Up front, Limitless Esports' 'Silent Assassin' Mike Adamson held off league commander-in-chief Alan Vaught over the closing laps to win the race, with Josh Buettner third. Pope's steady fourth clinched the league's first championship, while Buettner locked up second in the standings over Burke. Ricky Whittenburg charged from 21st to ninth — 'driving it like he stole it,' per the booth.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Alan Vaught","Josh Buettner"],"moments":[{"t":1724,"title":"Green flag on the championship finale","summary":"Pope and Burke lead the field to green side by side for 100 laps at a 115-degree Michigan with the inaugural VRL title on the line.","tags":["timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2247,"title":"Vaught takes his first lead of the night","summary":"The 33 of Alan Vaught powers to the point for the first time as the pack runs nose to tail — first through tenth covered by about half a second.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2507,"title":"The 82 becomes a saving machine","summary":"Mike Everedge loops the 82 twice in a handful of laps and drifts both spins straight without bringing out a caution.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3985,"title":"Buettner smacks the wall fighting for the lead","summary":"Championship hopeful Josh Buettner holds the 84 against the wall while racing near the front and tumbles all the way back to 18th.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4055,"title":"Klafka charges 22 spots","summary":"Eric Klafka's 88 rips the inside line from the back of the grid, up 22 positions and drag-racing the leaders off turn two.","tags":["eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4152,"title":"Pope spins and stacks up the field","summary":"The points leader snaps loose — the booth blames netcode off Zach Wheeler's near-touch — and the chain reaction collects Kuehl, Berube and Hutchinson and damages Oxendine, while Austin Paul ninjas through untouched.","tags":["timothy-pope","zach-wheeler","kelly-keel","alex-berube","justin-hutchinson","josh-oxendine","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4521,"title":"Hutchinson breaks loose and collects the Ripper","summary":"Justin Hutchinson loses it on cold tires running the high line and slides down into Jack 'the Ripper' Dixon to bring out another yellow.","tags":["justin-hutchinson","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5485,"title":"Burke's title bid ends in the wall","summary":"Running with the lead pack, Jeremiah Burke's Mardi Gras 753 gets loose and scrapes the wall, and the scattering mayhem snags Kilgore, Berube, Jeff Green and teammate Albert Anderson.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","russ-kilgore","alex-berube","albert-anderson","jeffrey-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5665,"title":"America's Driver DQ'd on incident points","summary":"Albert Anderson hits the 13-incident-point limit and is disqualified — 'he's in every wreck on the track' — moments after the booth had declared him just fine.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5842,"title":"The Big One — trucks upside down","summary":"A late-race melee flips Jack Dixon's 07 through the air multiple times — 'like a figure skater... actually more like a gymnast' — while netcode turns Rob Green's Kid Rock 91.","tags":["jack-dixon","rob-green"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5957,"title":"Anderson owns it in the booth","summary":"Fresh off the DQ, Anderson joins the broadcast, vows to beat the daylights out of his basement punching bag with a stiff drink, and promises the 12 will be up front next season.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":6787,"title":"Adamson wins it, Pope takes the crown","summary":"The Silent Assassin holds off Alan Vaught over the final lap to win the finale, with Buettner third, as Tim Pope cruises home fourth to clinch the inaugural VRL championship.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2541,"quote":"Good gracious, man — that guy is a saving machine.","context":"Mike Everedge drifts the 82 out of a second spin without wrecking","gold":3},{"t":3247,"quote":"Sorry — Ted Nugent might have shot some and run across the track, I mean what the heck, maybe a raccoon. Sorry guys, got excited there for a second.","context":"Adam Turner apologizes for screaming over a mid-pack scattering","gold":3},{"t":5519,"quote":"Broadcaster curse — we just talked about Anderson being just fine... I don't know. He's dead.","context":"Albert Anderson wrecks again seconds after the booth said he was okay","gold":4},{"t":5842,"quote":"This is going to bring out another yellow — this is a big one, upside down trucks!","context":"The late-race Big One erupts with the 91 involved and trucks flipping","gold":5},{"t":5887,"quote":"Jack Dixon going for a wild ride out there, flipping multiple times — looking like a figure skater out there flipping through the air... actually, more like a gymnast.","context":"Calling Jack Dixon's airborne flips in the Big One","gold":4},{"t":6843,"quote":"Ricky Wittenberg was driving it like he stole it, man.","context":"Praising the 55's charge to ninth right after the checkered flag","gold":3},{"t":7147,"quote":"He's probably in Ohio shooting a deer or wrestling a cow or something with his bare hands — that's what they do up there, they're tough.","context":"Zach Wheeler's interview connection drops mid-question","gold":4},{"t":8026,"quote":"My results were self-induced today... I just ran out of talent at some point.","context":"Jeremiah Burke owning his race-ending spin in the post-race interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 1 (inaugural) finale, 100 laps / 200 miles at Michigan, aired live Dec 22, 2021. Auto-captions garble names heavily: Buettner also appears as Bittner/Bettner/Bitner (Buettner used, most frequent); league leader Alan Vaught and admin/car-owner Lori Vaught appear as both Vaught and Vaughn; Jorge Rincon's surname is uncertain (Francone/Rencon/Renkan/Rincon all heard); Alex Berube's middle nickname (4J/Forge/Foursey/Forshay) is unresolved — he is called a Quebec native. Ricky Whittenburg is the season sponsor (DND Race Graphix, Keller Williams Johnson City TN) and drove the 55; captions spell it Wittenberg. Lori Vaught fields the 007 admin truck but per the booth doesn't actively drive. Dale Adamson (#46, Mike's son) was announced for next season and did not race. Trevor Robertson sat out ill. Full finishing order read on air: Adamson, Vaught, Buettner, Pope, Wheeler, Kilgore, Oxendine, Paul, Whittenburg, Everedge for the top 10. Final points: Pope champion, Buettner second, Burke third.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"vq9Pcl_y05g":{"recap":"Alan Vaught put the No. 33 on the pole for the Phoenix Classic and controlled most of the 150-lapper, at one point the only driver to crack the 27-second bracket while stretching his lead to well over a second in clean air. The second half turned chaotic: Greg Klein's No. 92 slapped the wall with bits and pieces flying in a multi-truck pileup, and the night's signature Big One sent Mike Everage's No. 82 flipping onto its roof while Craig Goodenough speared the barrels. Vaught surrendered the lead by pitting under a late caution, restarted outside the top 10 with about 18 laps to go, and carved back to the front on fresh tires. On a one-attempt green-white-checker he held off Tim Pope by three tenths — with trucks wrecking across the line behind them — for his first win of the season. Josh Bittner survived last-lap bumper pressure from Jeremiah Burke to complete the podium, with Burke fourth after climbing 20 spots.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Josh Bittner"],"moments":[{"t":1168,"title":"Massive dog-pile launch through the dog leg","summary":"The green flag drops mid-lineup-rundown and the field immediately goes three and four wide through the dog leg and turns three and four as polesitter Vaught clears the pack.","tags":["jess-vaught","dustin-eaton","josh-bittner","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1297,"title":"Ramsey's slow artistic drift into the pit wall","summary":"The 34 self-spins off turn four and takes a slow, 'artistic' slide down into the pit-lane divider wall, bringing out the first caution of the evening.","tags":["nick-ramsey"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1565,"title":"Kuehl loops it on the apron — race stays green","summary":"On the restart the 01 spins and collects the 23, but both trucks are so far down on the apron that iRacing never throws the caution and the field races on.","tags":["kelly-keel","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2652,"title":"The booth's orangutan and Cannonball Run detour","summary":"During a long green run the booth spirals from a fear of orangutans into Clyde from Every Which Way But Loose and full Cannonball Run trivia, complete with a fun fact on Manis the orangutan actor.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2812,"title":"Pileup out of two during the green-flag stops","summary":"Ramsey spins again off turn two and hits the barrels at a good clip mid pit-cycle; the stack-up behind snags Player, Ochoa, Eaton, and Goodenough and leaves four trucks with mandatory-repair meatball flags.","tags":["nick-ramsey","andrew-player","dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough","edson-ochoa","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3625,"title":"Kelly Kuehl's steering gives out","summary":"Already nursing a wounded truck, Kuehl loses the steering, drives straight up the racetrack, and pounds the far outside wall — the accumulated damage finally catching up in a miserable night.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4766,"title":"Klein's wall-slammer scatters the field","summary":"The 92 gets super loose off the dog leg, snaps back hard into the outside wall with bits and pieces flying everywhere, and a pinball of action collects a half-dozen trucks including the 43, 19, 3, 16, and 29.","tags":["greg-cline","albert-anderson","john-curtis","jack-dixon","jess-vaught","dave-mayberry","mike-adamson","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5067,"title":"The Big One: Everage flips onto his roof","summary":"Burke rejoins from deep in the apron into a four-wide and turns the 82 sideways; Everage goes for a flight across the desert on his roof, Goodenough hammers the barrels, Kuehl gets plowed into, and Burke apologizes on the radio.","tags":["mike-everage","jeremiah-burke","craig-goodenough","kelly-keel","shawn-mcdonald","chandler-paul","dustin-wade"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5468,"title":"Net code hooks Pope sideways","summary":"A tangle the booth calls 'net code all the way' clips the 7 sideways across the track, dragging the 43 and 18 into the mess and leaving the 10 with major damage.","tags":["timothy-pope","john-curtis","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6009,"title":"Leaders roll the strategy dice","summary":"Under a late caution, leader Vaught and the lap-85 pitters trade track position for fresh tires while Burke, Pope, Bittner, and others stay out — setting Vaught up to restart outside the top 10 with about 18 to go.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6295,"title":"Vaught's fresh-tire charge to the front","summary":"Restarting deep in the field on new tires, Vaught slices through three-wide chaos, takes third off Bittner within a handful of laps, and closes on the leaders as the clock runs down.","tags":["jess-vaught","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6962,"title":"One-shot GWC: Vaught wins by three tenths","summary":"On the single green-white-checker attempt Burke shoves Pope at the launch, Vaught breaks free and clear, and he takes the white and the checkers by three tenths for his first win of the season — as trucks wreck across the line behind him.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","josh-bittner","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1747,"quote":"It's kind of shaped like a bagel that you dropped on the floor and it's kind of dented on one side.","context":"The booth sizing up Phoenix's oddball layout","gold":4},{"t":2255,"quote":"That's why everybody watches NASCAR, right? It's like WWF on wheels.","context":"The booth on why fans crave the carnage","gold":4},{"t":2608,"quote":"We're going to have to have a safety briefing — we can get vests that say safety third.","context":"Joking about the drivers' real-life Phoenix meetup shenanigans","gold":3},{"t":4133,"quote":"Jump on up to our chopper camera, 'cause the chopper camera never lies.","context":"Cueing the replay of a restart wreck","gold":3},{"t":5067,"quote":"Oh, big wreck — oh, this one — oh, we got trucks in the air! 82 on his roof!","context":"Calling Mike Everage's flip in the late-race Big One","gold":5},{"t":6774,"quote":"It is short track with a mile and a half and superspeedway consequences on the wrecks — you get some good pileups.","context":"Summing up Phoenix after a string of late cautions","gold":4},{"t":7393,"quote":"I was watching a big purple truck eat my bumper — I think he knew what I had for breakfast today.","context":"Josh Bittner's podium interview on Jeremiah Burke's last-lap pressure","gold":4},{"t":7703,"quote":"She purred like a kitten all night long, and that's what helped me get back to the front.","context":"Winner Alan Vaught on his new I9 power plant engine package","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 8 race at Phoenix (1-mile), 150 laps, confirmed in-booth after brief season-number confusion; VRL's next stop is Bristol. Auto-caption surname guesses are uncertain: the winner's name (vot/vought/fought/javot) is rendered here as Vought but could be Vaught; Bitner may be Bittner; Zachary Henion is a rough guess from henin/henon/henen/Howen variants; Andrew Cason from cin/cson/Conan; David Feit from 'David fight'; Scott Howe from 'Scott how'; Jorge Rincon from ringcon/Ranon/ranan. Lori is the race director (not a broadcaster). Ricky Wittenberg (DND RaceGrafix) was absent tending to a family medical situation and received multiple on-air well-wishes. Earl Evans sat out most of the night to be with his kids. Full finishing order was read out ~[2:12:18]-[2:16:04]; spotlight driver interview went to 12th-place Zachary Henion.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"vTPKkxF5gT8":{"recap":"Tim Pope opened the Charlotte playoff round with a victory after mastering tire wear through long green runs and surviving two late restarts. The 133-lap World 200 ran caution-free past the halfway-distance pit window before contact between Chandler Paul and Edson Ochoa triggered the first yellow, ending a stretch in which fuel mileage and tire conservation had separated strategies. Later cautions for a Paul-Dion Jones crash and a large restart wreck involving Sean McDonnell and John Gallagher repeatedly erased the advantages built during the final green-flag pit cycle. Pope cleared Larry Dickerson on the last restart with seven laps remaining and held him off to the finish, while hard charger Jeremiah Burke completed an Allstar Racing sweep of positions two through five.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Larry Dickerson","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1754,"title":"Vaught and Bittner start the playoffs","summary":"Alan Vaught leads Josh Bittner and the 30-truck field to green after a Memorial Day tribute and parade laps.","tags":["jess-vaught","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2035,"title":"Bittner takes the early lead","summary":"Vaught drifts up and checks slightly, allowing Bittner's preferred high line to carry him into first during the opening tire-saving stint.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2594,"title":"First green-flag stops begin","summary":"Zachary Henin, Greg Klein, Dion Jones, Kevin Hunt, Goodenough and Coffin are among the early pitters as fuel and tire strategy begin to diverge.","tags":["zachary-henin","greg-cline","dion-jones","kevin-hunt","craig-goodenough","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":2823,"title":"Henin cycles to the lead","summary":"After pitting around lap 26, Henin uses the short-pit advantage to take first as the opening green-flag cycle concludes.","tags":["zachary-henin"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3571,"title":"Second pit cycle starts near halfway","summary":"David Feit begins the next sequence around lap 58, followed by Dobson, Henin, Klein and others as the race remains caution-free.","tags":["david-fite","greg-dobson","zachary-henin","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3689,"title":"Paul and Ochoa end the long green run","summary":"Chandler Paul and Edson Ochoa tangle through the quad oval, sending Paul into the outside wall for the first caution near halfway and giving most of the field a timely pit stop.","tags":["chandler-paul","edson-ochoa"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4178,"title":"Restart crash catches Curtis and Robertson","summary":"John Curtis gets loose in turns three and four and shoots into Trevor Robertson, then across Michael Everage; Austin Paul is also caught as the field scatters moments after the restart.","tags":["john-curtis","trevor-robertson","mike-everage","austin-paul"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5396,"title":"Final green-flag stops unfold","summary":"Everage and Burke begin the final pit sequence before Vaught, Dickerson, Anderson and the remaining leaders follow, setting up a tire-and-track-position fight for the last 30 laps.","tags":["mike-everage","jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","larry-dickerson","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":5977,"title":"Paul-Jones crash erases the strategy gaps","summary":"Dion Jones gets a run below Chandler Paul through the quad oval, but their lines converge and both hit the wall; Goodenough, Kevin Hunt and Coffin take secondary contact.","tags":["dion-jones","chandler-paul","craig-goodenough","kevin-hunt","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6363,"title":"McDonnell crash brings one more yellow","summary":"On cold tires, Sean McDonnell pushes toward the wall and John Gallagher cannot avoid his rear quarter, turning McDonnell and collecting Robertson, Curtis, Dobson and others.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","john-gallagher","trevor-robertson","john-curtis","greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6720,"title":"Pope clears Dickerson on the final restart","summary":"With seven laps left, Pope gets the stronger launch and moves ahead of Dickerson while Burke pushes his teammate into second.","tags":["timothy-pope","larry-dickerson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6929,"title":"Pope holds on at the white flag","summary":"Dickerson looks high on the final lap but cannot reach Pope, who wins the playoff opener ahead of Dickerson and 28th-starting Burke.","tags":["timothy-pope","larry-dickerson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7213,"quote":"The tracks tend to line up to where I'm good at them. I practice a little bit more. I'm hungry.","context":"Jeremiah Burke explains his playoff-time surge","gold":4},{"t":7272,"quote":"We got second, third, fourth, and fifth, so it just shows what a good team we got around us.","context":"Burke celebrates Allstar Racing's four-truck result","gold":4},{"t":7514,"quote":"I'm really good at saving tire. I'm happy right now, but man, I'm just kind of bummed out.","context":"Larry Dickerson balances satisfaction with disappointment after finishing second","gold":4},{"t":7538,"quote":"It's like my third or fourth race this year I let slip through my fingers.","context":"Dickerson reflects on another near-win","gold":5},{"t":7610,"quote":"That's a big advantage, having the team we do. We can all sit here and talk during the race and strategize.","context":"Dickerson describes the value of Allstar Racing's coordination","gold":4},{"t":7775,"quote":"You've got to crack the throttle a little bit, let it rotate, and ease back into it.","context":"Tim Pope explains his tire-saving technique","gold":5},{"t":7785,"quote":"Get in too fast or too much, you'll slide the right front and burn it up. It's all about finesse.","context":"Pope identifies the key to winning Charlotte","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The complete 30-driver finishing order is read after the interviews. The opening green-flag run lasted a little over 60 laps, with the first caution arriving at roughly halfway. Jeremiah Burke gained 25 positions from 28th to third. The broadcast describes Charlotte as playoff race one but the seasons map has no entry for this video, so no season number is asserted. ","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"VW-Fvzn5qt8":{"recap":"Race #5 of the Vigilante Racing League brought the trucks to Las Vegas Motor Speedway for 133 laps, with Craig Goodenough winning the pole and controlling much of the first half. Six cautions kept reshuffling the field, capped by a back-straightaway Big One with about 30 to go that collected Dave Mayberry, Mike Adamson, Scott Rooney, Kyle Vaught and others after Goodenough got into the fence. Jeremiah Burke, who started 21st after a poor qualifying run, took fuel-only on the first caution to open up his strategy, beat Alan Vaught off pit road on the final stop, and aero-blocked his way to a roughly 0.85-second victory for his first win of the season. Vaught settled for second with Dustyn Eaton third, while Russ Kilgore and Trevor Robertson rounded out the top five. Goodenough, the class of the field early, was swept up in the big wreck and faded to 15th.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Alan Vaught","Dustyn Eaton"],"moments":[{"t":1661,"title":"Three wide from the drop of the green","summary":"Goodenough clears out front while Anderson, Vaught, and Dixon go three wide behind him on the very first lap.","tags":["craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","jess-vaught","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1893,"title":"Gallagher and Bittner in the fence","summary":"Gallagher turns down on Bittner before he's clear and both go into the fence for the first caution on lap 10.","tags":["john-gallagher","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2468,"title":"Plyler pounds the fence, race stays green","summary":"Three wide with McAdam and Dickerson ends with Plyler taking a big hit in the fence and McAdam driving through the grass — and the race stays green.","tags":["john-mcadam","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4170,"title":"Canales stalls on track and gets creamed","summary":"Joe Canales stops dead against the turn-two wall — the booth suspects a hardware disconnect — and gets hit hard, with Hunt bouncing off Kyle Vaught in the scramble; the caution traps most of the field a lap down.","tags":["joe-canales","kevin-hunt","kyle-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4616,"title":"Fight nearly takes flight","summary":"Whittenburg hits the fence off turn four, then David Feit and Kelly Cole meet in the middle — Fight gets air under the truck and nearly goes on his lid while Dixon takes a shot in the driver's door.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","david-fite","jack-dixon","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5013,"title":"Bryant runs down Dickerson for the lead","summary":"Side by side off the restart, Dillon Bryant drives it to the bottom and beats Larry Dickerson to the stripe for the race lead as Dickerson brushes the wall.","tags":["dylan-bryant","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5278,"title":"Caution during the commercial break","summary":"Andrew Cothran and Greg Dobson come together during the side-by-side break — 'true NASCAR fashion' — with Cothran getting the raw end of the deal but locking the brakes to keep from sliding into traffic.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5440,"title":"The stream fights for its life","summary":"Major network issues hit the broadcast during the late battle for the lead — 'a frame every 4 seconds' — until the booth turns off home devices and fixes it just in time for the Big One.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5863,"title":"Burke goes three wide for the lead","summary":"On fresher tires, Jeremiah Burke jumps out of line, drops to the apron, and takes the lead three wide over Whittenburg and Goodenough with 30 to go — the move that sets up the win.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5886,"title":"The Big One on the back straight","summary":"Goodenough gets into the fence fighting three wide for the lead, Anderson gets crossed up, Rooney hooks in front of Kyle Vaught, and Mayberry noses hard into the tire pack — the Big One with about 30 to go.","tags":["dave-mayberry","craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","scott-rooney","kyle-vaught","mike-adamson","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6158,"title":"Final restart: Burke checks out","summary":"With 24 to go, Burke launches to a big advantage while Whittenburg is left in the dust on old tires and Robertson takes over second.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","ricky-whittenburg","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6909,"title":"Burke holds off Vaught for win #1","summary":"From the 21st starting spot, Jeremiah Burke aero-blocks Alan Vaught over the closing laps and takes the checkered flag by about 0.85 seconds for his first win of the season; Dustyn Eaton comes home third.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1673,"quote":"You can't win it on lap one, but you can throw it away. — Yeah, tell that to Albert Anderson.","context":"Anderson goes three wide for the lead on the opening lap","gold":4},{"t":2896,"quote":"It's almost like we knew — and no, it's not a replay, it's not a tape delay, this one's live for real, folks.","context":"Leaders hit pit road the instant the booth predicts green-flag stops","gold":3},{"t":3067,"quote":"Good enough gets to the inside of Jeremiah Burke like he's tied to a tree.","context":"Goodenough on fresh tires blowing past lap traffic in the green-flag cycle","gold":4},{"t":3601,"quote":"We don't care what position it is, folks — if they're fighting for a spot, we want to see it.","context":"Booth covering the battle for 22nd place","gold":4},{"t":4898,"quote":"Mayberry's in the grass — I wonder if he was trying to text us in the chat. He's probably trying to cool his tires down.","context":"Mayberry wanders through the grass under caution","gold":3},{"t":5353,"quote":"At least we're here for the restart — I don't think Fox would have pulled that off. Don't sue us, Fox, just playing.","context":"A caution flies during the commercial break","gold":4},{"t":5897,"quote":"Big time impact I think for Dave Mayberry, others involved — the big one here at Las Vegas Motor Speedway!","context":"Calling the multi-truck Big One on the back straightaway with 30 to go","gold":5},{"t":6079,"quote":"Caution number six of the night — cautions breeding cautions here at Vegas.","context":"Yellow flies again right after the Big One","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption surname guesses: 'Allen VA/vot/bot' rendered as Vaught (wife Lori and son Kyle share the surname per the winner interviews); 'good enough' as Goodenough (#89); 'Joe canel/caneles' as Canales; 'Andrew cin/gothan' as Cothran; 'Andrew player/cler' as Plyler; 'Kelly Co/cool' as Cole; 'David Feit', 'Jorge Rincon', and booth analyst 'Chris Goans' (captions: gones/goes) are lower-confidence guesses. Podium and full finishing order were read out on air, so winner/podium are solid. The broadcast suffered network dropouts roughly 1:30:40-1:36:10, so caution five (Mike Everage in trouble, ~1:32:50) is only lightly covered. The cold-open highlight reel (~0:08:59-0:10:03, names like Lockwood/Muska, Michigan) is promo footage from another event and those names were excluded from the driver list. Derrick Welch (3rd in points) missed the race and is included as a mentioned driver only.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"wlkH-9tqtjo":{"recap":"Tim Pope won the 85-lap Brickyard Brawl from pole after combining dominant long-run speed with two-lap-fresher tires in the decisive closing run. The first 32 laps and opening green-flag pit cycle ran clean before three-wide contact among Michael Everage, Dustyn Eaton and Ricky Whittenburg produced the first caution. Alan Vaught erased Pope's large advantage by undercutting the final green-flag stop and led until Pope set up a pass with four laps left, but later cautions for Kyle Vaught and a multi-truck crash involving John Gallagher and Dave Mayberry forced the sole green-white-checkered attempt. Pope cleared Vaught on the overtime restart and won under green while Vaught held off Mike Adamson for second; a separate crash behind them after the white flag did not interrupt the finish.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Alan Vaught","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1474,"title":"Pope launches from the pole","summary":"Tim Pope leads John Osborne and the 38-truck field across the yard of bricks to begin the 85-lap race.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2443,"title":"Opening green-flag stops begin","summary":"Zachary Henin and David Feit start the first pit cycle near lap 19; the field completes the sequence cleanly apart from Jacob Young's speeding penalty.","tags":["zachary-henin","david-fite","jacob-young"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit"},{"t":3206,"title":"Three-wide squeeze brings the first yellow","summary":"Michael Everage moves down while three wide with Dustyn Eaton and Ricky Whittenburg, squeezing all three into the wall and forcing Eaton to tow on lap 33.","tags":["mike-everage","dustin-eaton","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3368,"title":"Osborne wins the pit-road race on two tires","summary":"John Osborne takes only right-side tires and exits ahead of Pope, Vaught and Craig Goodenough, but the imbalance soon costs him positions after the restart.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","timothy-pope","jess-vaught","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4011,"title":"Pope earns the halfway bonus","summary":"With no scheduled stage caution, Pope is the leader at halfway and continues to build a substantial advantage during the long green run.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead"},{"t":4856,"title":"Pope retakes command after the second cycle","summary":"Osborne briefly leads after the next green-flag stops, but Pope needs only a few corners to reclaim first while Vaught works his way into second.","tags":["timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5694,"title":"Vaught's undercut erases Pope's lead","summary":"Vaught pits earlier in the final green-flag cycle and passes Pope while the leader blends back onto the track, trading tire age for crucial track position.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5902,"title":"Mayberry and Vaught trigger a late caution","summary":"Kyle Vaught is turned across Dave Mayberry's nose with 10 laps remaining but completes a full spin and narrowly avoids the pit-wall barrier.","tags":["kyle-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6440,"title":"Pope retakes the lead with four to go","summary":"After Vaught initially clears him on the restart, Pope uses his slightly fresher tires to set up the pass and move back ahead.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6495,"title":"Gallagher crash forces overtime","summary":"Mayberry's damaged steering leaves him unable to hold the truck after Gallagher slips low; Gallagher is turned across the track and a large crash produces the final caution before overtime.","tags":["dave-mayberry","john-gallagher","joe-canales","dustin-wade"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6881,"title":"Pope wins the green-flag overtime sprint","summary":"Pope clears Vaught on the only green-white-checkered attempt and takes the white flag. A crash involving Trevor Robertson, Goodenough and Greg Klein unfolds behind them, but the leaders race to the finish with Pope first, Vaught second and Adamson third.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","mike-adamson","trevor-robertson","craig-goodenough","greg-cline"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":5973,"quote":"I didn't want to cause a wreck or get caught up in a wreck, and so we just backed off a little bit. I knew I'd be better on the long run.","context":"Spotlight driver Stoney Benfield explains his patient run to ninth","gold":4},{"t":7516,"quote":"I have not been on a podium in a while, and man, I feel—I'm speechless, believe that one.","context":"Mike Adamson celebrates finishing third","gold":4},{"t":7722,"quote":"I tried to do a little undercut at the end, give myself a chance, do something different.","context":"Alan Vaught explains how he took the lead from Pope during the final pit cycle","gold":5},{"t":7734,"quote":"Doing a restart with him on three fresh tires and Tim Pope, it's probably just a no-go.","context":"Vaught describes defending against Pope on the late restarts","gold":4},{"t":7847,"quote":"I just like a pure racing event, and that's what tonight felt like. It felt like old-school racing.","context":"Vaught praises the race's balance of speed and strategy","gold":5},{"t":7978,"quote":"I was able to get a good run on Jess there one time and got back around.","context":"Tim Pope summarizes the winning pass","gold":4},{"t":8015,"quote":"The tires, yeah, I think that helped a little bit. I was able to get it to rotate a little bit more than he was.","context":"Pope credits his fresher tires for the decisive advantage","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The broadcast reads the complete 38-driver finishing order. Twenty-six trucks finished on the lead lap. Jack Dixon suffered an early connection failure and is classified 38th. The seasons map has no entry for this video, so no season or round is asserted. the booth's recurring 'Dustin with a Y' nickname refers to him. Caption spellings are normalized through the roster, including Joe Canales, Darby Maroth, Jorge Rincon and Zachary Henin.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"WvIR4zNrAYY":{"recap":"The Season 3 finale at Phoenix put four title contenders — Alan Vaught, Tim Pope, Jeremiah Burke, and Andrew Player — into a 150-lap night shootout, and it delivered wall-to-wall chaos. Polesitter and league owner Alan Vaught dominated the first half and survived a black flag thanks to a perfectly timed caution, while Pope's championship bid ended mid-race with a wreck and a disconnect. With about ten laps to go, Burke and Vaught collided battling for the lead, sending Burke hard into the wall, and Vaught's dying engine forced him down pit road during the green-white-checkered chaos. That left Andrew Player to cruise home eighth and claim the championship for Team Orangutan, while Mike Adamson stole the race win for Limitless Motorsports ahead of Jonathan Osborne and Greg Klein.","winner":"Mike Adamson","podium":["Mike Adamson","Jonathan Osborne","Greg Cline"],"moments":[{"t":1033,"title":"Green flag: Vaught bolts, Dixon sends the dog leg","summary":"Polesitter Alan Vaught rockets to the early lead as Jack Dixon dives the dog leg on lap one; Ricky Whittenburg survives a wild ride and loses a stack of spots.","tags":["jess-vaught","mike-adamson","jack-dixon","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1904,"title":"Lap-20 pileup: Fite turned, six trucks collected","summary":"David Feit gets turned in traffic and five or six trucks pile in behind him — Reeves, Endicott, Coffin, and Chandler Paul all snagged — bringing out caution number two.","tags":["david-fite","austin-reeves","russ-endicott","andrew-cauthan","chandler-paul","robert-jordan","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2943,"title":"Oxendine hooked hard into the turn-four wall","summary":"Josh Oxendine's truck snaps right after a tap from Beamer and slams the outside wall; Jordan, Player, Fite, and Austin Paul have nowhere to go behind him.","tags":["josh-oxendine","matt-beamer","robert-jordan","andrew-player","david-fite","austin-paul"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3991,"title":"The Big One — carnage at the halfway restart","summary":"On the restart after the break, Beamer wrecks and the field stacks in with trucks up on two wheels — while a lucky caution saves black-flagged leader Vaught from going a lap down serving his penalty.","tags":["matt-beamer","jess-vaught","jonah-long","earl-evans","mike-everage","george-rincon","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4435,"title":"Chan the Man turned by the 18 — 'a homicide'","summary":"Chandler Paul gets spun by Andrew Player's 18, drawing a caution, radio chatter about anger, and the chat verdict 'I think we just witnessed the homicide.'","tags":["chandler-paul","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5480,"title":"Osborne spins: parking lot on the backstretch","summary":"Jonathan Osborne spins across the track — possibly on cold tires — and the backstretch turns into a parking lot, collecting Mayberry, Eaton, and Pope.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dave-mayberry","dustin-eaton","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5746,"title":"Burke's launch of the century","summary":"Jeremiah Burke rips the restart of the night, flying down through the apron and around Andrew Player — a move so good Player compliments him under the next caution.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5782,"title":"Pope's title bid ends in a rage-quit","summary":"Championship contender Tim Pope gets together with David Emig's 2 after a rough night, comes out angry, and manually disconnects — one of the title four is done.","tags":["timothy-pope","david-emig"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6334,"title":"Everidge goes flying","summary":"A bump from the 49 turns Beamer, and Michael Everidge goes airborne over the wreck — 'a close your eyes moment' — before landing back on all four wheels.","tags":["matt-beamer","mike-everage","david-kelly"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6769,"title":"Burke and Vaught collide for the championship","summary":"Battling side by side for the lead with ten to go, Burke pinches down as Vaught drifts up — contact sends Jeremiah Burke hard into the wall and cripples both title favorites in one blow.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7034,"title":"GWC chaos: Burke pinballed, Vaught's engine toast","summary":"On the first green-white-checkered attempt Burke pinballs through an accordion wreck that sends Austin Reeves for a wild ride, while Vaught — engine toast — crawls to pit road, handing the title to Player.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jess-vaught","austin-reeves","dustin-eaton","robert-jordan","earl-evans"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7312,"title":"Adamson takes the checkers, Player takes the crown","summary":"Mike Adamson holds off Osborne and Klein in the final two-lap shootout for his first win of the season, while Andrew Player cruises home eighth, dodging wreckage to clinch the Season 3 championship.","tags":["mike-adamson","jonathan-osborne","greg-cline","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":460,"quote":"Sit back, buckle up, throw on those drinking helmets and throw that inhibition out the window, because we are going championship racing here tonight.","context":"Alan Brown's opening welcome to Championship Wednesday","gold":4},{"t":1175,"quote":"Earl Evans says he's going to take a shot of rum for every crash tonight — you all watch out for the 13 out there.","context":"booth reads Earl's drinking-game pledge from chat, early in the race","gold":4},{"t":4012,"quote":"Oh my goodness, carnage! Jess Vaught — talk about having a rabbit's foot shoved somewhere in that roll bar.","context":"the Big One erupts just as Vaught's black-flag penalty gets erased by the caution","gold":3},{"t":4074,"quote":"Siri, play Three Wooden Crosses — because they look like there's some deaths on this highway right there.","context":"surveying the wreckage after the Big One","gold":4},{"t":5680,"quote":"Somebody's gonna have to get turnt, somebody's gonna have to get learned — I can't wait to see who gets the bad end of that deal.","context":"previewing the championship shootout in the closing laps","gold":5},{"t":6421,"quote":"This is more like the Dallas freeway right now — cell phone in one hand, pistol in the other, and your beard between your legs, driving with your knees.","context":"describing the late-race mayhem after Everidge went airborne","gold":4},{"t":6769,"quote":"Contact between the front two! Hard into the wall goes Jeremiah Burke — championship contenders getting into each other!","context":"the title-deciding wreck between Burke and Vaught with ten to go","gold":5},{"t":7362,"quote":"Winning this race is Mike Adamson... Andrew Player, just out there surviving, wins this VRL championship!","context":"the checkered flag call","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Race winner and champion are distinct: Mike Adamson won the race; Andrew Player (finished 8th) won the Season 3 title as best finisher of the championship four. Caption-name uncertainties: #1 is consistently 'David fight' (best guess Fite); #82 is introduced as 'Michael Edwards' but called 'Everidge' the rest of the night (went with Everidge); #14 Eaton is 'Dustin with a Y' per the booth (rendered Dustyn); #55 is rendered 'Wittenberg' (league spelling likely Whittenburg). Lori Vaught served as race control from the booth. The lap-75 midway caution was a built-in break with no stage points. Post-race, league owner Alan Vaught announced next season will run the NASCAR Cup schedule in trucks, with an All-Star event around Jan 9/11 and the Clash on Feb 1.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"wvkMzHmWq8I":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant's Skulloseum Showdown began from pole and ended with 167 laps led, but the 261-lap Bristol finish was anything but a straight-line domination. The upper groove accumulated treacherous marbles, and the loose trucks produced 14 cautions while split pit calls repeatedly moved Bryant back into traffic. Dustin Riehle and later Kelly Kuehl took turns controlling restarts through strategy, while the attrition mounted around them. Michael Everage's spin developed into a hard pileup that ended Dustin Wade's night, and a later three-wide squeeze sent Trevor Robertson around before Jeremiah Burke was blasted upside down. Craig Goodenough, Albert Anderson, Chris Goans and Jack Dixon were among other drivers caught in separate incidents as nearly every restart tested the field. Bryant recovered from a black flag for entering the wrong side of pit road, cycled back to the front, and still had Jonathan Osborne and John McAdam close enough to challenge late. The final caution created the race's only green-white-checkered attempt. Bryant controlled the launch, Osborne secured second, and McAdam finished third after being unable to repeat his earlier pressure. Bryant later described the upper lane as so slick that a small mistake could become a crash, making his command of the preferred groove the defining achievement.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Jonathan Osborne","John McAdam"],"moments":[{"t":1527,"title":"Bryant launches from pole","summary":"Pole-sitter Dillon Bryant gets a clean jump and immediately begins opening a gap over Jack Dixon and John McAdam.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jack-dixon","john-mcadam"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1827,"title":"Goodenough spins into Klein","summary":"Craig Goodenough loses the rear while running the extreme high line and Greg Klein has nowhere to go on the backstretch.","tags":["craig-goodenough","greg-cline"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2437,"title":"Anderson's spin catches Bittner","summary":"Albert Anderson gets loose above the groove and Josh Bittner is collected as the field tries to miss the spinning No. 99.","tags":["albert-anderson","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3086,"title":"Riehle leads after split strategy","summary":"Dustyn Eaton stays out on the strategy split and controls the restart while Bryant falls back into traffic after pitting.","tags":["dustin-eaton","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3161,"title":"Everage and Wade trigger a hard pileup","summary":"Michael Everage spins after contact in traffic, Dustin Wade arrives with nowhere to go, and John Gallagher delivers another heavy impact that ends Wade's race.","tags":["mike-everage","dustin-wade","john-gallagher"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3348,"title":"Robertson spins; Burke goes airborne","summary":"A three-wide squeeze involving Dave Mayberry and John McAdam starts a multi-truck accident; Trevor Robertson spins and Jeremiah Burke is blasted upside down.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry","john-mcadam"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3826,"title":"Kuehl controls a single-file restart","summary":"After a run of back-to-back cautions, race control switches the field to single-file and Kelly Kuehl leads them back to green.","tags":["kelly-keel"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6259,"title":"Goans spins into Dixon","summary":"Chris Goans loses the rear entering the corner and Jack Dixon cannot avoid him, with Jorge Rincon, Scott Rooney, and others caught in the secondary crash.","tags":["chris-goans","jack-dixon","george-rincon","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7211,"title":"Bryant survives the lone overtime restart","summary":"Bryant jukes the field on the only green-white-checkered attempt; Osborne takes second while McAdam cannot repeat his earlier challenge.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7299,"title":"Bryant completes the Bristol domination","summary":"Dillon Bryant takes the checkered flag after leading 167 laps, with Jonathan Osborne second and John McAdam third.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne","john-mcadam"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1504,"quote":"We've always got something to shoot for.","context":"Ricky reacts to Bristol's history of heavy caution counts.","gold":2},{"t":3229,"quote":"There's something going on with the setup or the track or the tires.","context":"The booth explains the unusually loose Bristol trucks.","gold":2},{"t":5893,"quote":"The dog seems to be the happiest person at Bristol tonight.","context":"The booth spots Dave Mayberry's sleeping canine co-pilot.","gold":5},{"t":7299,"quote":"Your winner, Dylan Bryant. Jonathan Osborne is second, and John McAdam brings it home in third position.","context":"The live checkered-flag call.","gold":5},{"t":7959,"quote":"If you slip up a little bit too much, you'll most likely crash.","context":"Bryant describes the icy upper groove in his winner interview.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The official finish call and post-race results explicitly identify Bryant, Osborne, and McAdam as the podium. The event was scheduled for 257 laps but the winner interview states Bryant led 167 of 261, consistent with an overtime extension. Roster overrides are applied to Chris Goans and Dustyn Eaton. The captions repeatedly call the No. 10 driver Andrew Cawan/Cawin; roster history maps those spellings to Andrew Coffin, though that identification deserves owner review. The captions alternate Andy Player and Andrew Player; this distill uses roster entry Andy Player for the participant explicitly shown as No. 13.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"wxQ2m1LASJM":{"recap":"The Viva Las Vegas 150 packed a 41-truck field under the lights at Las Vegas, and the traffic bit early and often: a three-wide tangle sent Todd Smith's 66 for a wild ride and drew the first caution before lap five, and a lap-52 pileup triggered by Jeffrey Johnson's botched pit entry collected so many trucks that officials briefly disabled driver chat over the 'anger and hatred' on the radio. Alan Vaught edged Greg Klein to win the halfway stage break, but a long green-flag run to the finish turned the second half into a fuel-mileage chess match as the race-long leaders had to pit from the front with under 15 laps to go. Mike Everidge inherited the lead only to run out of gas with two laps left, and Andrew Player — running a camo Veterans Day scheme while fighting off COVID — sputtered across the line on fumes to become the season's seventh different winner in seven races. Greg Klein and Albert Anderson, who both ran dry right at the stripe, completed the podium, with Ricky Whittenburg fourth and Jonah Long fifth.","winner":"Andrew Player","podium":["Andrew Player","Greg Cline","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":1408,"title":"Green flag on 41 trucks in Vegas","summary":"The huge truck field takes the initial green side by side under the Las Vegas lights, with polesitter Andrew Coffin leading them down into turn one.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","todd-smith","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1478,"title":"Three-wide bites early: the 66 goes for a ride","summary":"Three wide for the lead on lap four ends in contact that sends Todd Smith for a wild bumpy ride and snags up George McCone, Trevor Robertson and more for the first caution.","tags":["todd-smith","andrew-cauthan","trevor-robertson","robert-jordan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2090,"title":"Accidental pit maneuver wrecks the 74","summary":"Quarter panels meet and the 74 of Robert Jordan goes sideways; Russ Kilgore can't slow down in time and collects the 83 of Charlie Harkes on the way through.","tags":["robert-jordan","russ-kilgore","mike-everage","charlie-herkis"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2581,"title":"Cars everywhere: the backstretch Big One","summary":"A bobble three wide on the backstretch puts Chris Zofeld in the wall and sends Cody Tarrant, Tony Polk and a pile of trucks for hard and wild rides on lap 23.","tags":["chris-zofeld","cody-tarrant","tony-polk","dave-mayberry","mike-sobanovski","robert-jordan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2686,"title":"The booth books a driver brawl at Binion's","summary":"Sensing anger on the driver radios, the booth spends a caution scheming a pay-per-view driver fistfight downtown at Binion's Horseshoe, complete with collection hats and Adam's yacht fund.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3176,"title":"Lap-52 pileup gets driver chat disabled","summary":"Jeffrey Johnson slips coming back up the track on pit entry and triggers a massive pileup — Mike Adamson and Robert Chipman get squeezed into the wall, six trucks catch meatball flags, Russ Kilgore disconnects, and officials shut off driver chat over the 'anger and hatred.'","tags":["jeffrey-johnson","mike-adamson","robert-chipman","russ-kilgore","earl-evans"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4061,"title":"Alan Vaught takes the halfway stage","summary":"A frantic two-lap sprint to the lap-50 competition break ends with Alan Vaught holding off Greg Klein, Jonah Long, Albert Anderson and Kelly Kuehl for the stage bonus points.","tags":["jess-vaught","greg-cline","jonah-long","albert-anderson","kelly-keel"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4106,"title":"Dion Jones's figure-skating save of the night","summary":"Sandwiched on the stage-break restart, Dion Jones rotates the 4 truck a full 30 degrees toward the infield and gathers it back up without wrecking — the booth scores it a 9.5 and nominates it for iRacing save of the week.","tags":["dion-jones","andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4457,"title":"Jonah Long spins; Dustin Wade threads the needle","summary":"A pool-ball checkup on the restart sends the pink orangutan 5 of Jonah Long for a wild ride, and Dustin Wade jukes left-right-around to somehow stay clean.","tags":["jonah-long","jonathan-osborne","jeff-ottinger","dustin-wade"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4871,"title":"Netcode chaos: the 57 tumbles on the frontstretch","summary":"Russ Endicott's 57 gets turned and goes for a tumble all over his roof in what the booth calls the weirdest netcode fake-physics reaction they've ever seen; Jack Dixon and the recently interviewed Dion Jones get swept up too — broadcaster curse confirmed.","tags":["russ-endicott","greg-cline","jack-dixon","dion-jones"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6268,"title":"Everidge runs dry from the lead","summary":"After leading the fuel-mileage endgame, Mike Everidge's 82 runs out of gas with two to go and Andrew Player, nursing his own tank, sweeps by into the lead.","tags":["andrew-player","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6291,"title":"Player sputters home for win number seven-of-seven","summary":"White flag out with no cautions left: Andrew Player's truck is sputtering and spitting but makes it across the line for the win — the seventh different winner in seven races — while Greg Klein and Albert Anderson run out of fuel right at the stripe to finish second and third.","tags":["andrew-player","greg-cline","albert-anderson","mike-everage"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2708,"quote":"We have the collection hats, and these guys fight, and we take the money, and we go spend it in Vegas.","context":"The booth plans a driver-brawl fundraiser at Binion's Horseshoe","gold":3},{"t":3233,"quote":"That 58 machine, man, he has just been turned into some squeezed peanut butter.","context":"Robert Chipman pinned into the wall in the lap-52 pileup","gold":4},{"t":3314,"quote":"Driver chat has been disabled due to the anger and hatred going on out there.","context":"Officials mute the driver radio after the lap-52 pileup","gold":4},{"t":3726,"quote":"There's some moments where sometimes you need a new pair of pants, and that might be one of them.","context":"Watching the replay of a full-send near miss into a checked-up field","gold":3},{"t":4173,"quote":"Figure skating here for the four of Dion Jones.","context":"Replay of Dion Jones's 30-degree rotation save","gold":3},{"t":6302,"quote":"He is sputtering, he is spitting, but he is going to make it down and across the line — Andrew Player picking up the race win here tonight at Las Vegas!","context":"The fuel-starved 18 crosses the stripe on fumes to win","gold":5},{"t":6338,"quote":"You better tech that car — he's got some fuel in the roll bar.","context":"The booth jokes the winner somehow still had fuel pressure","gold":4},{"t":6422,"quote":"This is a case where a gambler lost, but a gambler also won.","context":"Post-race verdict on Everidge running dry while Player's gamble paid off","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Title says 'Viva Las Vegas 150' but the race was 100 laps (NASCAR trucks at Las Vegas, night race). Auto-captions garble many names heavily; proper spellings are best guesses. The 14 is called both 'Justin Eaton' (once, in the starting rundown) and 'Dustyn Eaton' (many times) — Dustin used as best guess. The 1 truck is called 'David fight' twice and 'David White' once in the finishing rundown — actual name uncertain. The 20 is called both 'Jeffrey Johnson' and 'Ethan Johnson.' Greg Dobson is a past-season VRL driver who appeared only in YouTube chat tonight, not in the field. Robert Chipman (58, finished 18th) won the random-draw driver of the day. Full finishing order was read out at ~2:01:35-2:05:43. Next race: Dover; sponsor reads for DND Race Grafix and Keller Williams of Johnson City TN bookend the broadcast.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"wyURXlW7U3k":{"recap":"Greg Klein stole the VRL All-Star Race at a revived North Wilkesboro, a 200-lap no-points truck brawl in which polesitter Ricky Whittenburg took Brayton Laster's $25 dare and started from the tail of the field. Trevor Robertson was the class of the field for most of the night, stretching out a four-second lead and winning the lap-100 stage before Tim Pope ran him down for a door-to-door fight over the lead. The long green-flag runs gave way to late chaos: a restart Big One flipped defending champion Andrew Player onto his roof, Dave Mayberry's spin collected four more trucks on the front stretch, and contact in the Pope-Robertson duel spun Pope and forced a green-white-checker. After the white flag, Mike Adamson's dive under Robertson wrecked both leaders, handing Klein — who scraped the wall just once all night — his second win of the season ahead of Albert Anderson, with Jeremiah Burke sliding across the line backwards to claim third.","winner":"Greg Cline","podium":["Greg Cline","Albert Anderson","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1021,"title":"Polesitter takes the dare","summary":"Pole winner Ricky Whittenburg accepts Brayton Laster's $25 challenge to surrender P1 and start the All-Star Race from the tail of the field.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","brayton-laster"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":1368,"title":"Lead battle ends in the grass","summary":"While dueling Robertson for the lead, Alan Vaught slides completely off into the infield grass and drops to the tail with no caution — then answers with the fastest lap of the race, a sub-19.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":1791,"title":"Shot-every-yellow Earl visits the booth","summary":"Earl Evans joins the broadcast doing a shot every caution and explains a lightning strike knocked out his power and cost him the Monday qualifier — 'Bill Gates controls the lightning now.'","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2771,"title":"Endicott finds the angled wall","summary":"Contact between the 57 and 84 sends Endicott into the jutting outside wall, and John Gallagher gets collected behind them with an estimated '87 G's' impact.","tags":["russ-endicott","josh-bittner","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3227,"title":"Robertson runs away with the stage","summary":"In his own ZIP code out front, Trevor Robertson cruises to the lap-100 stage win after stretching his lead past four seconds.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4015,"title":"McDonnell gets octopused","summary":"A bump from Osborne sends Sean McDonnell across the ice-slick grass and into the inside guardrail, which grabs the 23 and won't let go — a long tow and an on-radio apology follow.","tags":["shawn-mcdonald","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4670,"title":"Mayberry crash traps Ricky a lap down","summary":"Mayberry pounds the wall mid pit cycle; the caution hands Andrew Player a freebie stop and the lead while trapping the hard-charging Whittenburg a lap down — heartbreak for the challenge run.","tags":["dave-mayberry","ricky-whittenburg","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4900,"title":"The Big One — Player on his roof","summary":"Restart chaos: the 53 goes around, defending champion Andrew Player flips onto his roof, Whittenburg gets plowed, and Bittner's motor expires in the melee.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","andrew-player","jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg","russ-endicott","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5305,"title":"Mayberry's front-stretch pileup","summary":"Mayberry spins down the front stretch and collects McDonnell, Kelly, Osborne and Laster; McDonnell disconnects for the night and Mayberry adds 'the 400th whiskey dent' to his truck.","tags":["dave-mayberry","shawn-mcdonald","david-kelly","jonathan-osborne","brayton-laster"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5510,"title":"Pope vs Robertson, six to go","summary":"Pope restarts like he was 'shot out of a gun' and runs the dominant 64 door-to-door in a breathless side-by-side duel for the race lead.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5565,"title":"Netcode heartbreak forces a GWC","summary":"Door contact — and a dose of netcode — kicks Pope's truck loose out of the lead fight; Vaught gets squeezed in the aftermath, setting up VRL's single green-white-checker attempt.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5790,"title":"White-flag wreck decides it all","summary":"Adamson's last-gasp dive under Robertson wrecks both leaders after the white flag; Greg Klein sweeps through to steal the win as Jeremiah Burke crosses the line backwards to grab the final podium spot.","tags":["greg-cline","mike-adamson","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":790,"quote":"Basically think of your Saturday night dirt track — and they just paved it.","context":"Sizing up North Wilkesboro before the green flag","gold":3},{"t":1908,"quote":"Bill Gates took him out — Bill Gates controls the lightning now.","context":"Earl Evans lost power to a lightning strike and missed the qualifier","gold":4},{"t":1996,"quote":"Man, Trevor Robertson just absolutely in his own ZIP code right now.","context":"Robertson four seconds clear during stage one","gold":4},{"t":4015,"quote":"Oh Sean McDonald — oh man, and he gets octopused. That's gonna be a long tow time.","context":"McDonnell hung up in the inside guardrail after contact","gold":4},{"t":4650,"quote":"He who hath the latest pit strategy shall have the freshest tires at the end.","context":"Mock-biblical wisdom during the final green-flag pit cycle","gold":3},{"t":4905,"quote":"Oh contact! 53 going around — wow, that's a big one! Oh, the 18 up on his roof!","context":"Calling the restart Big One that flipped Andrew Player","gold":4},{"t":5828,"quote":"It's going to be Jeremiah Burke, backwards, crossing to close out that podium — what just happened?","context":"The checkered flag falls on the green-white-checker chaos","gold":5},{"t":6298,"quote":"I just got done swallowing a handful of blood pressure pills, so my pressure should start coming down here soon.","context":"Albert Anderson opening his second-place interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner clearly stated: Greg Klein, his second win of the season. Full top 10 as read: Klein, Anderson, Burke, Kelly Kuehl, Dustyn Eaton, Andrew Player, Austin Paul, Alan Vaught, Jonathan Osborne, Trevor Robertson. Laster's first name is garbled across captions (Brighton/Brayton/Braden/Brayden) — Brayton is a best guess. Booth repeatedly says 'Dustin with a Y', implying the spelling Dustyn. 'Shane the Man' (#72, spotting for the Goodwiser team tonight) real name unknown. Race admins credited as 'Lori and Jess' (captions render 'Lori Vault', likely Lori Vaught). Dave Mayberry is also the league sponsor's realtor (Blue Fox Properties) and separately offered $25 to any Monday-qualifier driver who won. The random-draw prize went to 12th-place finisher Tim Pope. Dillon Bryant and Larry Dickerson were announced as joining Albert Anderson's All-Star Racing team next season. Event format: 200 laps, no points, stage caution at lap 100, one green-white-checker attempt. Josh Kelleher and Greg Thompson did not race (chat guest and spotter respectively); Dustin Wade registered but did not grid.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"wZ9l87pwpBI":{"recap":"VRL's first visit to the Red Bull Ring ran all 45 laps without a full-course caution, forcing 27 starters to solve the unfamiliar road course through pace, incident avoidance and two green-flag pit cycles. Pole-sitter Josh Bittner cleared the opening braking zone, while Alan Vaught spun into the gravel and was struck by Kelly Kuehl as he waited to rejoin. Alex Forget-Bérubé charged roughly a dozen places from the rear, and Jeremiah Burke erased Bittner's early advantage before the first fuel window. Bittner short-pitted around lap 14; Trevor Robertson stayed out longer after managing his tires onto Burke's bumper, then briefly inherited the lead before the cycle returned Bittner to control. Burke tried the undercut in the final stint, but the decisive contest became Bittner versus Robertson when they exited the last stops side by side. Bittner used his momentum to clear the former leader with 13 laps remaining. Robertson then disconnected while running second, with both the broadcast and Robertson's chat message attributing it to weather-related packet loss. Bittner won by roughly three seconds over Burke. Behind them, Zachary Self survived contact with Jonathan Osborne and a penultimate-corner attack that spun Eric Klafka to retain third. Burke later revealed that a bathroom trip had cost him heavily during the first stop; Bittner called the clean run his toughest iRacing race.","winner":"Josh Bittner","podium":["Josh Bittner","Jeremiah Burke","Zachary Self"],"moments":[{"t":1701,"title":"Bittner controls the opening corner","summary":"Pole-sitter Bittner clears the first braking zone cleanly and immediately opens a gap over Burke as the field checks up behind him.","tags":["josh-bittner","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1777,"title":"Vaught spins on the opening lap","summary":"Alan Vaught loops the No. 33 into the gravel and is then struck by Kelly Kuehl while waiting to rejoin, forcing Vaught to use an early fast repair.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1809,"title":"Berube charges from the rear","summary":"Alex Berube gains roughly a dozen places in the opening laps and continues a recovery that ultimately carries him from the rear of the grid to eighth.","tags":["alex-berube"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":2278,"title":"Burke closes onto Bittner's bumper","summary":"Burke erases most of Bittner's early advantage and begins applying pressure while both leaders keep their incident counts low.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":2991,"title":"Bittner short-pits the first cycle","summary":"Bittner is the first unaffected contender to make a scheduled stop, entering around lap 14 to gain clean track and flexibility in the 15-lap fuel windows.","tags":["josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3117,"title":"Robertson pressures Burke before their stops","summary":"Robertson's tire management carries him to Burke's rear bumper, and the two remain on track longer than Bittner before Burke pits and Robertson inherits the lead.","tags":["trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":3395,"title":"Pope completes the opening pit cycle","summary":"Pope finally pits from the lead on lap 17, allowing the first cycle to settle with Bittner back in control ahead of Robertson and Burke.","tags":["timothy-pope","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"pit_stop"},{"t":4638,"title":"Burke short-pits the final stint","summary":"Burke stops at lap 30 to gain fresh tires and an undercut while Bittner, Robertson and Pope remain on track a little longer.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4989,"title":"Bittner beats Robertson out of the cycle","summary":"Robertson exits pit road side by side with Bittner, but Bittner uses his momentum to clear the former leader and take command with 13 laps remaining.","tags":["josh-bittner","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5057,"title":"Packet loss ends Robertson's winning bid","summary":"Robertson disconnects while running second and challenging for the win, giving Bittner a gap of more than six seconds and dropping Robertson deep in the order.","tags":["trevor-robertson","josh-bittner"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":"technical"},{"t":5631,"title":"Contact intensifies the fight for third","summary":"Osborne gets into Self under braking and Pope subsequently contacts Osborne, but Self keeps third while Klafka and Pope remain in pursuit.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","zachary-self","timothy-pope","eric-klafka"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":6278,"title":"Bittner wins; Self survives for third","summary":"Bittner completes the final corner and wins over Burke; moments later Klafka bumps Self in the penultimate corner, spins himself and leaves Self with the final podium spot.","tags":["josh-bittner","jeremiah-burke","zachary-self","eric-klafka"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":6278,"quote":"Across the line, picking up the win here today at the Red Bull Ring!","context":"The live victory call for Bittner.","gold":2},{"t":6487,"quote":"You don't understand—I am sweating so much right now.","context":"Self reacts after narrowly holding off Klafka for third.","gold":5},{"t":6662,"quote":"That first pit stop I had to go to the bathroom. I got out of the rig and went to the bathroom and came out 14 seconds behind Josh.","context":"Burke reveals the unusual reason his first pit stop cost so much time before his second-place recovery.","gold":5},{"t":6830,"quote":"That was certainly the toughest race I think I've ever done on here.","context":"Bittner describes the challenge of the unfamiliar road course after taking the win.","gold":5},{"t":6879,"quote":"Being able to come out here and run 45 laps without spinning my truck out or running horribly off-road into one of the sand pits, it just felt amazing.","context":"Bittner reflects on executing a clean caution-free race.","gold":5},{"t":7035,"quote":"For it to stay green-flagged the whole way, I think it was great to see the drivers.","context":"Bittner praises the field's caution-free road-course performance.","gold":2}],"sourceLimitations":"The live finish, podium interviews and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Bittner, Burke and Self. The race ran all 45 laps without a full-course caution. Robertson was a leading contender until the broadcast and Robertson's own chat message confirmed a packet-loss disconnect caused by bad weather; he reconnected and finished 23rd. The spoken grid appears to miscount the 27 named starters as 28, while the final rundown explicitly lists 27 finishers; all 27 named participants are included. Simon Cobrasregis and Jacob Schaffet follow the roster's canonical spellings.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"XE5D9MK-88I":{"recap":"VRL opened its new season with the Clash at the Coliseum, a no-points exhibition on the quarter-mile LA Coliseum bullring and the league's first-ever try at heat racing. Alan Vaught, Andrew Player, Jack Dixon, and Jeremiah Burke each won a heat to set a 24-truck, 150-lap feature that devolved into a caution-plagued demolition derby, headlined by a roughly ten-truck pileup with trucks literally climbing on top of each other. Vaught's dominant 33 spun out of the lead late and tumbled to 16th, throwing the front of the field into chaos. Jeremiah Burke's 753 survived a green-white-checker that ended with the field frozen by a final-lap caution to take the win, with quadriplegic driver Jonathan Osborne charging up 11 spots to second and Canada's Jack \"the Ripper\" Dixon third.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Jonathan Osborne","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1248,"title":"Parking lot on the Heat 1 restart","summary":"Heat 1's restart goes sideways — the 90 slams the inside wall, trucks stack up behind him, and the booth declares \"we got ourselves a parking lot.\"","tags":["daniel-baker","dustin-wade","dave-mayberry","albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":1474,"title":"Racing with his mouth","summary":"The booth spotlights quadriplegic driver Jonathan Osborne, who drives the 81 with a mouth-controlled joystick — and still talks smack on the radio while doing it.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3106,"title":"Synchronized swimmers","summary":"The 753, 82, and 99 all spin in unison putting power down off the final turn in the last heat — Kim Krauss radios that three of them went around at exactly the same time.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","mike-everage","kim-krauss"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3267,"title":"WWE dogpile in the corner","summary":"A restart dogpile heading into the turn looks like a WWE fight spilling into the corner of the ring, though everybody keeps the wheels rolling.","tags":["mike-everage","chandler-paul","eric-klafka"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3964,"title":"Feature lap-one gridlock","summary":"A hard bump from the 72 to the 81 triggers a chain reaction that blocks the entire quarter-mile on the feature's opening lap — Greg Klein left doing an Austin Powers back-and-forth to get turned around.","tags":["chandler-paul","jonathan-osborne","greg-cline"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4493,"title":"Defending champ wrecked out","summary":"Last season's champion Andrew Player gets wrecked (\"holy moly\") after winning his heat, one of the night's biggest casualties.","tags":["andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4715,"title":"Mayberry goes four wide","summary":"Dave \"Hot Rod\" Mayberry tries to sneak four wide through the turn and spins — \"this is comical,\" admits the booth as radios light up.","tags":["dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6155,"title":"The Big One — trucks climbing trucks","summary":"Roughly ten trucks go sideways at once in the night's signature wreck — \"a wrecking yard out there\" with trucks literally climbing on top of each other, Mike Adamson in the middle of it again.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6663,"title":"Vaught spins from the lead","summary":"Dominant heat-one winner Alan Vaught loses the rear tires putting power down while leading, blocking the whole track; a late caution freezes him back in 16th.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7380,"title":"Osborne rattles the leader","summary":"Osborne taps then flat shoves the leading 753 of Burke hard into the outside wall, handing Jack Dixon the lead in the closing laps.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jeremiah-burke","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7728,"title":"Frozen-field finish","summary":"The one-attempt green-white-checker ends with the field frozen by a caution the play-by-play man never saw — Jeremiah Burke wins the Clash over Osborne and Dixon.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":8242,"title":"Blame it on the wheelchair","summary":"In his runner-up interview, Osborne jokes he's blaming every wreck he caused tonight on still getting used to his new wheelchair.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":875,"quote":"This is a little meet and greet, right? Like, hi, my name is Greg Klein, I'm about to meet your bumper in the rear end.","context":"Previewing the no-points Clash before the green flag","gold":4},{"t":1262,"quote":"Oh, and thought he saved it — but not quite, and we got ourselves a parking lot.","context":"Calling the Heat 1 restart pileup","gold":4},{"t":3130,"quote":"It's like synchronized swimmers out there, just trying to put the power down.","context":"Three trucks spinning in unison in the final heat","gold":3},{"t":3349,"quote":"You don't need to use your brakes if you've got a guy in front of you with a tailgate — you just use him up.","context":"Everidge leaning on the 99's bumper for the transfer spot","gold":4},{"t":3988,"quote":"It's like the Austin Powers thing, you know, where he's stuck in the tunnel — he's going back and forth, back and forth to turn around.","context":"Greg Klein trying to get turned around in the lap-one feature gridlock","gold":4},{"t":6442,"quote":"If you call Martinsville a rhythm track, this track — you have to be able to do a samba while listening to a waltz.","context":"Describing the chaos of the quarter-mile Coliseum","gold":4},{"t":6795,"quote":"They should rename this thing the Dash and Crash.","context":"Sizing up the 30-lap shootout after a boatload of cautions","gold":4},{"t":7761,"quote":"I didn't have the heart to tell you — they froze the field and I didn't want to interrupt your mojo.","context":"The booth reveals the race actually ended under caution mid-call","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Heat 1's winner was never explicitly announced, but the 33 of Alan Vaught led at the end of it and started the feature on pole, so all four heat winners are inferred as Vaught, Player, Dixon, and Burke. Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: Vaught ('just bought'/'Jazz fought'), Fite ('David fight'), Riehle ('Dustin really'), Klafka ('Eric clapka'), Krauss (also captioned 'Kraus'/'Krause'). 'Dustin with a Y' Eaton implies an alternate first-name spelling (possibly Dustyn). The finish came under caution — the field was frozen mid-final-lap of the one-attempt green-white-checker, so Burke's win was official but anticlimactic. Lori ran race control and the winner thanked 'Jess and Lori' as league organizers. Exhibition race only — no points on the line.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"xeXp6rcOPBQ":{"recap":"The Winter Classic season came down to the DND Race Grafix 100 Finale at Indianapolis Motor Speedway, and the #33 of Alan Vaught closed it in style — taking the white flag with Trevor Robertson's #6 mounting one final charge down the backstretch and holding on to win the race and clinch the Season 7 championship in the same moment. Robertson settled for second on the night and congratulations in the post-race interviews, while the booth confirmed Anderson and Pope rounded out the top of the final standings. The broadcast closed with the league announcing the Season 8 format: no stage breaks, straight points, and a five-race championship showdown for the first time.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Trevor Robertson"],"moments":[{"t":1440,"title":"Green at Indy — Vaught leads the finale","summary":"Alan Vaught leads the field to green in the No. 33 and begins opening an early advantage through the first corners at Indianapolis.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2611,"title":"Wittenburg spins at pit entry — the lane jams","summary":"Ricky Whittenburg loses the No. 55 entering pit road, blocking the narrow entrance and bringing out the race yellow the booth had warned could happen.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4808,"title":"Vaught closes back onto Robertson at lap 60","summary":"After the green-flag stops spread the field, the booth highlights Trevor Robertson's No. 6 and Alan Vaught's No. 33 running close, with Vaught edging back toward Robertson's bumper and waiting on a mistake.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":7038,"title":"White flag — Robertson's last charge falls short","summary":"The white flag waves with the #33 of Vaught leading down the backstretch as Trevor Robertson makes one final attempt to run him down for the race and the title.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":7887,"title":"Race winner AND season champion — the 33 takes it all","summary":"Victory lane doubles as a coronation: Alan Vaught is announced as the race winner from Indianapolis Motor Speedway and the Season 7 champion in the same breath.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":8001,"title":"Champion's mic drop","summary":"Vaught on Robertson's charge: catching him was one thing — passing him after burning up the tires would have been a whole other deal.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2624,"quote":"coming on into entries gets all Loosey Goosey and Spins out and that's going to cause an absolute cluster there at the entrance of pit Lane and the yellow is out","context":"Ricky Whittenburg's pit-entry spin blocks the narrow lane and triggers the yellow.","gold":4},{"t":7038,"quote":"about to claim a winner winner chicken dinner as the 33 at javot makes his way down the backstretch","context":"The white-flag call as Alan Vaught leads Trevor Robertson down the backstretch.","gold":4},{"t":8001,"quote":"catching me is one thing getting past me after you burnt your tires up to catch me that's a whole another deal","context":"Alan Vaught, fresh champion, on Robertson's final-lap charge.","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Hand-extracted from the transcript by the archive owner-side scan (winner/champion explicitly called on tape at 2:11:27 and 2:16:09); not a full agent distill — moments beyond the finish sequence not cataloged.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"xjRrth3U3SA":{"recap":"Dillon Bryant capped the penultimate race of the VRL Truck Series season — the Round 2 playoff cutoff at virtual Martinsville — by starting fourth, taking the lead on lap 73, and leading 128 laps en route to the win, locking himself into the championship round at Phoenix. Pole-sitter Craig Goodenough dominated the opening stint, but a long green-flag run forced him to pit under green and an apparent penalty left him three laps down in 21st. A caution-filled middle stage — seven yellows in all, including a quarter-distance pile-up triggered when Mike Adamson locked up and collected the field — kept scrambling the order, and Trevor Robertson's spin with 16 to go proved decisive: Bryant, who admitted he was about eight laps short on fuel, got his stop under yellow while chief rival Tim Pope had just pitted under green. Bryant beat new Outcast Racing teammate Larry Dickerson by 1.3 seconds for the team's first 1-2, with John McAdam holding off a hard-charging Stony Benfield for third.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Larry Dickerson","John McAdam"],"moments":[{"t":1569,"title":"Eaton pancakes the wall on lap 1","summary":"Just a lap into the race, Dustyn Eaton slams the outside wall off turn two, keeps his foot in it, and gives up spots to Dillon Bryant — an early wound for one of the fastest trucks in the field.","tags":["dustin-eaton","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2286,"title":"Curtis spins, chain reaction brings caution one","summary":"John Curtis comes around on lap 38 — likely too much rear brake — and triggers a chain reaction that leaves Kevin Hunt and Dion Jones facing the wrong way.","tags":["john-curtis","kevin-hunt","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2524,"title":"Three-wide restart gamble goes wrong","summary":"Albert Anderson dives to the inside on the restart, making it three wide into turn one — 'you really just can't get that done here at Martinsville' — and Scott Rooney, John Osborne, and Andrew Player get swept up in caution number two.","tags":["albert-anderson","scott-rooney","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2767,"title":"The pile-in at quarter distance","summary":"The biggest wreck of the night: Mike Adamson locks the left front, spins after tagging Kyle Vogt's 16, Jeremiah Burke finishes the spin, and the freshly restarted field barrels in — Kevin Hunt, Ricky Whittenburg, Trevor Robertson, and Dave Mayberry all involved in caution three.","tags":["mike-adamson","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke","kevin-hunt","ricky-whittenburg","trevor-robertson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3334,"title":"Eaton wrestles the lead from Goodenough","summary":"On the single-file restart Dustyn Eaton runs down pole-sitter Craig Goodenough, battles side by side through three and four, and clears him off turn four for the lead as Goodenough's older tires 'show their ugly head'.","tags":["dustin-eaton","craig-goodenough","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3446,"title":"Bryant takes the point on lap 73","summary":"On fresher rubber, Dillon Bryant quickly disposes of Dustyn Eaton for the lead on lap 73 — the pass that starts his 128-lap run to the checkered flag.","tags":["dylan-bryant","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3671,"title":"Dickerson shot out of a cannon","summary":"Larry Dickerson, on lap-39 tires, clears Jeremiah Burke and then goes the long way around the outside of Craig Goodenough to crack the top five — the booth says he's been 'shot out of a cannon' since his stop.","tags":["larry-dickerson","jeremiah-burke","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3732,"title":"Goodenough's night unravels on pit road","summary":"The dominant pole-sitter is forced to pit under green with no caution in sight, then returns to his stall for an apparent penalty — cycling from the lead battle to 25th and ultimately three laps down.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4429,"title":"McAdam spins the tires, restart stack-up","summary":"On the lap-119 restart John McAdam spins the tires coming up to speed, Jorge Rincon's 28 gets into Larry Dickerson, and the chain reaction brings out caution number six.","tags":["john-mcadam","george-rincon","larry-dickerson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5568,"title":"Chaos just outside the top 10","summary":"Anderson, Cole, Burke, and Eaton go at it three wide — Anderson nearly loses it, Burke uses Kelly Cole's truck to break a spin, and the booth can only ask 'what is going on here just outside the top 10, it's chaos'.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5925,"title":"Robertson's spin flips the race to Bryant","summary":"Running fifth, Trevor Robertson loses it on his own with 16 to go and collects John Curtis — terrible timing for him, perfect timing for leader Dillon Bryant, who was on pit road about eight laps short on fuel and gets his stop under the yellow.","tags":["trevor-robertson","john-curtis","dylan-bryant"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6364,"title":"Bryant seals it as Benfield bangs the 47","summary":"On the final lap Stony Benfield gets into the back of John McAdam battling for third, but out front it doesn't matter — Dillon Bryant wins by 1.3 seconds over teammate Larry Dickerson for an Outcast Racing 1-2, punching his ticket to Phoenix.","tags":["dylan-bryant","larry-dickerson","john-mcadam","stony-benfield"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1661,"quote":"Go faster, Pastor!","context":"Chat's rallying cry for pastor-driver Stony Benfield, read on air — it became the running gag of the whole night","gold":4},{"t":2697,"quote":"That's awesome — I think Steve Austin might have beat him to that.","context":"After chat reveals Stony Benfield once wanted to be a wrestler called 'Stony Stone'","gold":3},{"t":2879,"quote":"Gotta hold the brake, folks, hold the brake.","context":"Replaying the quarter-distance pile-in as trucks kept barreling into the frozen field","gold":3},{"t":2958,"quote":"Lori's going to need a bigger notebook tonight.","context":"Chat jab at the chief official, read and endorsed by the booth as the cautions stacked up","gold":3},{"t":3587,"quote":"Live by the rear brake, die by the rear brake.","context":"After Mike Adamson's wild save off turn four — the booth's tech theme of the whole night","gold":4},{"t":4200,"quote":"Everybody on the racetrack will be pissed off at somebody else on the racetrack before this race is over with.","context":"Returning from break mid-race, summing up short-track racing at Martinsville","gold":4},{"t":6036,"quote":"Pace truck's driving out of there before these guys are done wrecking — he just apparates through the 43.","context":"Replay of the late Robertson caution, with the virtual pace truck ghosting through Curtis's wreck","gold":3},{"t":6375,"quote":"Started fourth but he's going to finish first — off turn four, checkered flag, Bryant wins it!","context":"The finish call as Dillon Bryant takes the win by 1.3 seconds","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Several surnames are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Allen Vogt' and 'Kyle Vogt' (captioned VA/vot/bot/F), 'Jorge Rincon' (Ren Con/ranone/ran cone), 'Kelly Cole' (consistently captioned 'Kelly cool' — surname could genuinely be Cool), 'Darby Maroth' (the booth itself said it was gambling on that name), 'Craig Goodenough', 'Andrew Coffin', and 'Greg Dobson'. Booth is a single play-by-play voice addressed as Steve on HBR TV; one chat greeting to 'Steve and Annie' suggests a possible co-host, but only one commentator is evident on tape. Lori is the chief race official and Jess a league admin — not drivers. Points standings were unofficial pending post-race review. Greg Klein was classified 32nd, 200 laps down — did not take the green flag. Full stated results beyond the podium: Benfield 4th, Anderson 5th, Dixon 6th, Rancone 7th, Pope 8th, Robertson 9th, Allen Vogt 10th.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"XllA3wqt-Mk":{"recap":"Chris Goans earned his first VRL Premiere Series victory at Dover after a long strategic race in which Craig Goodenough appeared dominant for most of the night. The first caution came during green-flag stops when Colin Decker and Kyle Vaught collided at pit entry, and a later netcode incident turned Dillon Bryant into the wall on a restart. Goodenough regained control and carried the lead deep into the final run, but a heavy outside-then-inside wall impact left his steering damaged and allowed Goans to close and pass. Goodenough held on for second, while Mike Adamson completed the podium.","winner":"Chris Goans","podium":["Chris Goans","Craig Goodenough","Mike Adamson"],"moments":[{"t":1055,"title":"Goodenough wins an ultra-tight pole","summary":"Craig Goodenough takes pole in a qualifying session where roughly a tenth of a second covers much of the front of the grid.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon","josh-bittner","timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"qualifying"},{"t":1228,"title":"Goodenough clears Dixon at the start","summary":"Goodenough launches cleanly and clears outside-row starter Jack Dixon while the field quickly settles into a single-file tire-saving run.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jack-dixon"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1403,"title":"Gaines' PC problem ends his night","summary":"Jason Gaines blinks out, appears to strike the inside wall, and retires after suffering the same computer problem that had affected a prior race.","tags":["jason-gaines"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"technical"},{"t":2169,"title":"Pit-entry collision brings the first caution","summary":"During the first green-flag stop cycle, Colin Decker does not realize Kyle Vaught is entering pit road and the two collide, leaving Vaught backwards against the wall and creating a scoring scramble.","tags":["colin-decker","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2995,"title":"Netcode turns Bryant into the wall","summary":"Dillon Bryant is sent around beside John Osborne even though the replay shows a visible gap between the trucks, a clear netcode incident that badly damages Bryant's race.","tags":["dylan-bryant","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3589,"title":"Klein crowds Dixon into the wall","summary":"Greg Klein gets loose beneath Jack Dixon and forces Dixon into the outside wall, costing Dixon pace but not immediately ending his race.","tags":["greg-cline","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3868,"title":"Pope stretches the fuel window","summary":"Tim Pope runs roughly 43 laps before stopping, temporarily leading as a group of drivers tries to offset strategy and catch a timely caution.","tags":["timothy-pope","greg-dobson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4724,"title":"Final green-flag stops begin","summary":"Goodenough pits from the lead and Goans follows one lap later, setting the order for the long run to the finish.","tags":["craig-goodenough","chris-goans","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4838,"title":"Goodenough hits both walls","summary":"While closing quickly on traffic, Goodenough clips the outside wall and then the inside retaining wall; he continues, but the post-race interview confirms serious wheel damage.","tags":["craig-goodenough","kyle-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5215,"title":"Goans takes the lead from wounded Goodenough","summary":"Goans closes on slightly fresher tires, gets underneath the damaged Goodenough, and completes the pass for the lead with only a handful of laps remaining.","tags":["chris-goans","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5426,"title":"Goans claims his first Premiere win","summary":"Chris Goans reaches the checkered flag with a comfortable advantage for his first Premiere Series victory; Goodenough finishes second and Mike Adamson third.","tags":["chris-goans","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2397,"quote":"It's unfortunate timing. And now all this is all messed up right now.","context":"Kyle Vaught explains the pit-entry crash and scoring confusion","gold":3},{"t":3141,"quote":"Might have been just a bit of netcode, but it wasn't much.","context":"The booth examines the gap between Bryant and Osborne","gold":3},{"t":3867,"quote":"If you do what the leader does every time, you're just going to follow the leader to the checkered flag, right?","context":"The booth discusses offset strategy during the long green run","gold":3},{"t":5798,"quote":"The wheel was sitting to the right at about three o'clock, so I was just trying to survive at that point.","context":"Craig Goodenough explains the effect of his wall damage","gold":4},{"t":5987,"quote":"This was a blast tonight. I love this place.","context":"Chris Goans celebrates his first Premiere Series win","gold":4},{"t":6008,"quote":"I'm just glad we were in a position to be able to take advantage of his misfortune.","context":"Goans credits his positioning after Goodenough's damage","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The post-race call explicitly identifies this as Chris Goans' first VRL Premiere Series win; roster_overrides.json supplies the canonical spelling. Tom Barish appeared on the 32-truck grid but the booth later stated he did not start, so the drivers array contains the 31 actual starters. The Bryant-Osborne wreck is described as netcode because multiple replay angles showed no physical contact. Goodenough confirmed in his interview that the late double-wall impact caused wheel damage and worsening steering.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"XT1_1zw_jPk":{"recap":"Talladega's regular-season finale built its pressure gradually, then released nearly all of it in the closing run. Jonah Long complicated the lead pack while racing two laps down, and Albert Anderson used a push from Jeremiah Burke to capture the stage. The longer green stretch also exposed the fuel window when Robert Jordan ran dry. Then the race changed character. Cody Tarrant was launched beyond the racing surface in a crash that also sent Chandler Paul airborne. Later, Anderson flipped onto his roof after a push went wrong at the front, and the Good Wiser crash collected a larger group that included Tim Pope. David Feit added another violent image when contact turned into a blowover. A late caution forced green-white-checkered overtime and put strategy beside survival. Alan Vaught, recovering from earlier trouble and staying out on fuel, received a sustained push from Pope on the final run. Vaught reached the checkered flag first, Pope finished second, and Burke took third. Austin Reeves went airborne in the incident behind them as the caution froze the field. The official finishing order settles the podium, while the checked-in source leaves the final playoff-point calculation outside this race story. What the tape proves is a patient fuel play, a committed drafting partnership, and a finish decided amid one last Talladega eruption.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Tim Pope","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":921,"title":"Flamethrower candle ritual on a hot mic","summary":"During qualifying, pit reporter Adam Turner forgets to mute and is caught lighting his booth candles with a flamethrower, explaining he needs 'candles and velvet' because broadcasting is his art.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":1930,"title":"Riley spun hard into the inside wall","summary":"An unsquared push from Albert Anderson sends the No. 37 of Dustin Riehle spinning rear-first into the inside wall early on; heavy damage but the race stays green because it happened off the racing line.","tags":["dustin-reilly","albert-anderson","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2955,"title":"Jonah Long races the leaders two laps down","summary":"Two laps down after early damage, Jonah Long drafts up to the lead pack and drops down in front of Albert Anderson — 'what a move by Jonah Long' — trying to claw a lap back the hard way.","tags":["jonah-long","albert-anderson","david-emig"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4075,"title":"Burke shoves Anderson to the Stage 1 win","summary":"Jeremiah Burke delivers the final push that gets Albert Anderson the stage win at the halfway competition caution, while David Feit spins behind them as the 4 and 123 tangle.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","david-fite","dion-jones","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4205,"title":"Robert Jordan runs dry at the stage break","summary":"Robert Jordan runs out of fuel coasting at 75 mph into turns three and four — 'absolute heartbreak' — after apparently missing his fuel box on the previous stop.","tags":["robert-jordan"],"heat":2,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4850,"title":"Tarrant launched out of the stadium","summary":"The first yellow of the night is a violent one: the 37 and 57 tangle, birthday boy Chandler Paul gets 'aerial show time,' Ricky Whittenburg escapes through the grass, and Cody Tarrant flies clean out of the end of the grandstands.","tags":["cody-tarrant","chandler-paul","ricky-whittenburg","dustin-reilly","russ-endicott","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5710,"title":"Race leader Anderson flips onto his roof","summary":"Controlling the race on the bottom lane, Albert Anderson gets turned in a push gone wrong from the Team Tang trucks and lands on his roof — then, 'like a cat,' ends up back on his wheels. The 123 takes major damage and Team Tang's night unravels.","tags":["albert-anderson","dustin-eaton","dustin-wade","john-gallagher","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6461,"title":"Dixon found parked backwards — booth blames aliens","summary":"Under caution, Jack Dixon is discovered facing backwards on track with no replay showing why. The booth cycles through theories — aliens, a cocktail from Canada, 'a momentary lapse of talent' — before Dixon reveals his monitor died mid-race.","tags":["jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6805,"title":"THE BIG ONE wipes out the Good Wiser charge","summary":"With about 15 to go, a teammate push between the 64 and 28 goes wrong and triggers a seven-plus-truck pileup — 'this is the big one' — collecting the entire Good Wiser team, Tim Pope, and more, moments after the booth praised their race.","tags":["andrew-player","george-rincon","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","mike-everage","tony-polk","andrew-cauthan","austin-paul"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7265,"title":"Fite sandwiched into a blowover","summary":"Running third with under 10 to go, David Feit gets pinched between two trucks and goes flipping upside down into the grass as the 83 and 22 make contact right in front of Alan Vaught.","tags":["david-fite","charlie-herkis","matt-beamer","jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7760,"title":"Six to go: wreck forces overtime","summary":"Contact between the 7 and 28 spins the 81 to the apron, the 123 gets loose, and the 18 crosses the track to bring out the yellow — sending the finale to a green-white-checkered with meatball flags all over the roster.","tags":["russ-kilgore","george-rincon","jonathan-osborne","andrew-player","david-emig","austin-paul","john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":8195,"title":"Green-white-checkered: Vaught steals the finale","summary":"Three-wide, three-deep to the white flag with wrecks erupting mid-pack, league owner Alan Vaught holds the bottom with a Tim Pope push and wins the regular-season finale over Pope and Burke — while Austin Reeves goes 'a couple hundred feet in the air' at the line and Mayberry's win-and-in bid dies in fourth.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry","austin-reeves","josh-oxendine","albert-anderson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":956,"quote":"I gotta surround myself in candles and velvet when I do these races because this is art to me.","context":"Adam Turner caught on a hot mic lighting his booth candles with a flamethrower during qualifying","gold":4},{"t":4780,"quote":"That thing has been magnetized or something, because we've been seeing people up in it all night long.","context":"On the outside wall after yet another truck brushed it","gold":3},{"t":4916,"quote":"Cody went out of the end of the grandstands. He's gone. He gone.","context":"Cody Tarrant launched airborne out of the stadium in the first big wreck","gold":4},{"t":5606,"quote":"Throw a beach blanket over the top 15 right here, they're all right on top of each other.","context":"The pack running three-wide and nose-to-tail before the leaders wrecked","gold":3},{"t":6534,"quote":"We'll just call that a momentary lapse of talent.","context":"Jack Dixon found facing backwards on track under caution with no replay explaining why","gold":4},{"t":6815,"quote":"We got contact, ourselves a big pile up — this is the big one! Every truck we just talked about involved in that one.","context":"The seven-plus-truck crash with 15 to go that wiped out the Good Wiser team","gold":4},{"t":8185,"quote":"It is time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet and throw inhibition out the window — it is time to go green white checkered racing.","context":"Setting up the overtime restart that decided the regular-season finale","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-caption garbling is heavy; several proper names are best-guess: 'Dustin really' rendered as Dustin Riehle (never spelled on tape), 'David fight' as David Feit (his cheering family in chat used the surname Decker, so his real surname is uncertain), Charlie Herkes spelling uncertain (hircus/herkis/harkes variants), and Jorge Rincon appears under many garbles (only clearly said twice). 'Dustin with a Y' suggests Eaton's first name is spelled Dustyn. Tony Polk is sometimes garbled as 'Tony Pope' — distinct from Tim Pope. Winner and full finishing order were read out clearly on air. The final playoff cutoff was NOT settled on the broadcast: Alan Vaught said Mike Adamson 'might be one spot out' pending official points, while Jonah Long said in chat he was out. Race admin Lori (Vaught's wife) handled race control. Broadcast was AAA Broadcasting, aired live 2022-12-14, sponsored by Blue Fox Properties. Kelly Kuehl, Greg Klein, and Robert Chipman were mentioned but did not race tonight.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"xxnA6duW23g":{"recap":"Tim Pope controlled much of the Homestead playoff opener, winning the scheduled halfway stage over Alan Vaught after the pair traded the lead through the first green-flag pit cycle. The second half initially stayed green despite a hard Dion Jones-Kyle Vaught crash, but contact between Jonathan Osborne and Jack Dixon finally produced the race's first natural caution and opened a late strategy scramble. Kelly Kuehl's short-service gamble put him on the front row, Pope's restart contact sent Alan Vaught tumbling through the order, and an immediate Osborne spin collected Vaught and several playoff contenders before Jeremiah Burke took command on the next restart. A final Trevor Robertson crash set up a nine-lap shootout in which Burke repeatedly beat Pope to clean air, then drove away when Pope got loose coming to the white flag; Burke won over Sean McDonnell and Pope.","winner":"Jeremiah Burke","podium":["Jeremiah Burke","Sean McDonnell","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1309,"title":"The playoff opener begins with instant trouble","summary":"Pope leads from the pole while Chandler Paul, Coffin, Kyle Vaught, Mayberry, and others encounter spins or contact in the opening corners; the race remains green.","tags":["timothy-pope","chandler-paul","andrew-cauthan","kyle-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2160,"title":"Vaught wrestles the lead from Pope","summary":"As lap-25 pit stops begin behind them, Vaught works the low lane and edges ahead of Pope, who immediately fights back on the outside with worn tires.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":2236,"title":"The first green-flag stops cycle through","summary":"Pope pits, Vaught and Robertson follow a lap later, and Anderson collects temporary laps led before making the last major stop of the cycle.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":3030,"title":"Pope wins the halfway stage","summary":"Pope navigates lapped teammate Whittenburg in the closing laps and beats Vaught to the stage line; Robertson, Burke, and McDonnell complete the top five.","tags":["timothy-pope","ricky-whittenburg","jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","jeremiah-burke","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":"stage_finish"},{"t":3371,"title":"Vaught loses ground on the stage restart","summary":"Pope and Vaught resume side by side, but Vaught appears to miss a shift or lift entering Turn 1 and falls back toward Robertson as the pack fans out three wide.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":3461,"title":"Jones and Kyle Vaught hit the inside wall","summary":"Dion Jones and Kyle Vaught tangle and strike the inside barrier hard; Jones has major steering damage and accepts responsibility on the radio, but green-flag racing continues.","tags":["dion-jones","kyle-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3887,"title":"Osborne and Dixon trigger the first natural caution","summary":"Osborne builds a run along the wall, becomes locked together with Dixon, and spins the No. 07 across the track, finally bringing out a yellow late in the race.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":3995,"title":"Kuehl gambles to win the race off pit road","summary":"Kuehl takes fuel only or right-side tires and leapfrogs the field, emerging ahead of Vaught, Robertson, Pope, Burke, Bittner, Long, Anderson, and McDonnell for the restart.","tags":["kelly-keel","jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","jonah-long","albert-anderson","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4245,"title":"Pope turns Vaught sideways in the restart battle","summary":"After Vaught clears Kuehl, Pope reaches Vaught's quarter panel and gives the No. 33 a nudge; Vaught saves the truck but bleeds positions from the lead group to 13th.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","kelly-keel"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"contact"},{"t":4299,"title":"Osborne's spin collects playoff contenders","summary":"Osborne gets loose exiting Turn 2 and spins across Vaught's path, triggering a pileup that also catches Kyle Vaught, Dixon, Adamson, Mayberry, Taylor, and others.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","kyle-vaught","jack-dixon","mike-adamson","dave-mayberry","mike-taylor"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4776,"title":"Robertson crashes to create a nine-lap shootout","summary":"Robertson drifts up in front of a charging Dickerson and spins into a multi-truck accident involving Kuehl, Osborne, Mayberry, and Whittenburg, erasing Burke and Pope's developing lead fight.","tags":["trevor-robertson","larry-dickerson","kelly-keel","jonathan-osborne","dave-mayberry","ricky-whittenburg","jeremiah-burke","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":5398,"title":"Burke wins the playoff opener","summary":"Burke protects the lead through the final restart, opens a gap when Pope gets loose coming to the white, and takes the checkered flag; McDonnell wins the side-by-side fight for second over Pope.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","shawn-mcdonald","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3324,"quote":"It depends on if he has Jack Link's.","context":"Jack Dixon answers the booth's question about what Canadians call Bigfoot","gold":5},{"t":3853,"quote":"He's driving his truck like he stole the thing and has a pistol and a hostage on board.","context":"The booth describes Jonathan Osborne's aggressive charge","gold":5},{"t":5470,"quote":"These guys are so good, if you're off, you're 15th. Some leagues, if you're off, you're running fifth.","context":"Ricky Whittenburg describes the depth of the VRL field","gold":5},{"t":5869,"quote":"I love short tracks. I like beating and banging.","context":"Runner-up Sean McDonnell looks ahead to Martinsville","gold":4},{"t":6175,"quote":"The big thing there was track position. If you can get clean air, I knew if I could get five laps in the lead, it was going to be really hard to pass me.","context":"Winner Jeremiah Burke explains the decisive advantage","gold":5},{"t":6197,"quote":"I just needed to beat them on these restarts every time and drive as hard as I can.","context":"Burke explains his late-restart plan against Pope and Vaught","gold":5},{"t":6208,"quote":"My hands hurt. That has to have been as hard as I've driven recently.","context":"Burke describes the physical intensity of the win","gold":5},{"t":6303,"quote":"Super clean at the beginning, got a little Western at the end there.","context":"The booth sums up the race's dramatic change of character","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 6, Round 18 at Homestead-Miami Speedway according to seasons_map.json; this was the opening race in the round-of-12 playoffs, with eight drivers advancing after the round. The 100-lap event used 60% fuel, four total tire sets, one fast repair, a 13-incident penalty threshold, and further penalties every six incident points. A planned stage caution followed lap 50, which Pope won over Vaught; the first natural caution came later from the Osborne-Dixon contact. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Burke-McDonnell-Pope podium and reads the complete 25-driver starting grid and finishing order. Caption variants are normalized to roster spellings including Alan Vaught, Sean McDonnell, Josh Bittner, Andrew Coffin, and Ricky Whittenburg; Dustyn Eaton is retained as the established archive spelling despite repeated on-air emphasis that Dustin is spelled with a Y. All timestamps fall within the 6,915-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"XYzyyWEHTik":{"recap":"VRL's long-awaited season opener at Homestead-Miami — 33 trucks, 100 laps, a 107-degree track and cash on the line — opened in chaos, with the field wrecking before lap 1 was complete and 'the Big One' leaving trucks destroyed everywhere barely a dozen laps in. After the admins switched to single-file restarts, the race settled into a long green-flag chess match of tire management and 60%-fuel pit strategy. Bluegrass Brawl winner Alex Forget-Bérubé led much of the middle stages in the #19 Canadiens truck, surviving a spectacular sideways save, but his tires faded late and Trevor Robertson's #6 Gorilla Glue machine swept around the outside for the lead with under ten laps to go. Robertson won the opener on fumes — one more lap, he said, and he'd have run out of fuel — with pit-strategy gambler Josh Buettner second and a fuel-dry Forget-Bérubé third. Tim Pope claimed pole and the race's fastest lap (33.44) on his way to fourth.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Josh Buettner","Alex Forget-Bérubé"],"moments":[{"t":1361,"title":"Green flag, instant carnage","summary":"Cold tires and opening-night nerves: the #63 gets into the back of the #4 at the start, collecting Isaac Wilson's #93 and the #14 before the field even completes lap 1.","tags":["john-herzig","alexander-gray","josh-oxendine"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2032,"title":"The Big One","summary":"Trucks destroyed everywhere on the first real green run — the #88 goes around, the #51 of Adamson claims responsibility, and much of the field hits pit road on a track the booth calls a cheese grater.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2087,"title":"Buettner mows the lawn","summary":"Josh Buettner dives the #84 down through the grass and threads past the Big One's carnage untouched, setting up his run to second.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":2440,"title":"Triple seven at the wall","summary":"Battling for third, the #7 and #77 get together — 'make that a triple seven' — with both trucks nearly riding up into the wall before hanging on.","tags":["russ-kilgore","zachary-self"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2697,"title":"Whittenburg hunts the leader","summary":"Side by side for the lead: Whittenburg's #55 keeps forcing the inside line on Forget-Bérubé, who holds him off lap after lap with outside-lane speed.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2719,"title":"187 murdered on the server","summary":"187 Cuz disconnects mid-race and the booth declares him 'murdered by a bad internet connection.'","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":3397,"title":"Buettner's 27-second gamble ends","summary":"After stretching a 27-and-a-half-second lead on his stay-out strategy, Buettner finally pits and the field streams past — a dice roll that won't be judged until the checkers.","tags":[],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4158,"title":"Wall tag hands Wheeler the lead","summary":"The #19 brushes the wall, Zach Wheeler pounces for the lead, and the fight behind them goes three wide — 'wow, almost four wide there for a second.'","tags":["zach-wheeler","trevor-robertson","russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4387,"title":"The save of the night","summary":"On five-lap tires the #19 snaps sideways for an entire corner — Forget-Bérubé gathers it up and misses Rincon's #28. The booth calls it an amazing save.","tags":["george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4614,"title":"The 19 takes it back","summary":"Forget-Bérubé times his run around a lapped car and dives inside Wheeler into turn 1 to reclaim the lead.","tags":["zach-wheeler"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4915,"title":"Robertson's three-wide money move","summary":"Three wide with the #88 and #7, Trevor Robertson rides the outside to strip the lead from a fading Forget-Bérubé with about eight laps to go — the pass that wins the opener.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5335,"title":"Checkered flag on fumes","summary":"Robertson takes the white and brings it home 'with some flair' — both he and third-place Forget-Bérubé ran the tank dry, with the #19 out of fuel exiting turn 4 and unable to do a burnout.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2032,"quote":"There it is — there's trucks destroyed everywhere back here. That's the big one!","context":"the lap-13 mega-wreck erupts behind the leaders","gold":4},{"t":2134,"quote":"This is chess, it's not checkers, is what we like to say.","context":"sizing up the field's diverging pit strategies","gold":3},{"t":2719,"quote":"187 Cuz got murdered on the server... 187 got murdered — murdered by a bad internet connection.","context":"a driver named 187 Cuz disconnects mid-race","gold":4},{"t":4387,"quote":"Oh what a save by the 19! He got loose and his car was sideways for a minute and he caught it. That was awesome.","context":"Forget-Bérubé's sideways save on cold tires","gold":4},{"t":4695,"quote":"When you're shooting dice in Waco, you'll roll snake eyes every time, that's for damn sure.","context":"riffing on the #020 of Snake Eyes running laps down","gold":3},{"t":4857,"quote":"The Quebec Cannon got a little competition coming up from behind — now that's what we're going with, I like that.","context":"coining Forget-Bérubé's nickname as Robertson closes in","gold":3},{"t":5035,"quote":"It's time to start mirror driving, it's time to start pulling out all the stops and throwing blocks — we're talking about money now, boys!","context":"eight laps to go with Robertson leading a charging pack","gold":4},{"t":5644,"quote":"When the good Lord gives us unlimited fuel and tires, we take that unlimited fuel and tires — every single caution we get.","context":"runner-up Josh Buettner explaining his strategy in the post-race interview","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Auto-captions garble names heavily. The #19's name is rendered a dozen ways (alex 4j/4g berube, for jay barubas, ford shave ruby); best reconstruction is French-Canadian 'Alex Forget-Bérubé' (Forget pronounced 'for-zhay'), but the exact form is uncertain. 'Buettner' vs 'Bittner' both used in-booth — Buettner chosen. The booth itself was unsure if the #37 is 'Reel or Riley' (Dustin Reel used). Early on they attributed the #29 ghost-hood paint to Jeff Snyder, later clarified: #29 = Dave Mayberry 'Hot Rod', Jeff Snyder = #999. Snake Eyes (#020), 187 Cuz, and The Ringer (#88) are known only by handles. Final results were read from live timing and called unofficial (e.g. Everidge's 9th was hedged). First ~10 minutes of the stream are pre-race music with stray caption fragments. Fastest lap (33.44, Tim Pope) was announced as unofficial. Race payout: $25/$15/$10 plus $5 fastest lap.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"y3ZEmEYG3VQ":{"recap":"The Vigilante Racing League closed its season with a 200-lap All-Star exhibition at the freshly revived North Wilkesboro, inverting the grid so league champion Andrew Player and the season's winners had to climb from the rear on a hot, abrasive track with only three spare sets of tires. The night delivered mayhem in bunches — a restart pileup swept up half a dozen trucks, and the Big One sent Austin Reeves' No. 6 flying over the pit wall before he somehow landed on all fours and drove away. Alan Vaught's No. 33 went a lap down with an unscheduled green-flag stop, answered with the fastest lap of the race on fresh tires, and carved all the way back to the point. Shrugging off a joking YouTube-chat bounty on his PC, Vaught held off Trevor Robertson on worn tires over the final laps to win, with Jack 'the Ripper' Dixon edging Mike Adamson by a nose for third. The booth called it one of the most exciting races they had ever broadcast.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Trevor Robertson","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1325,"title":"Green at last after the inversion fiasco","summary":"Manually inverting the grid black-flags half the field and even catches the flagman napping before the green finally flies — Dustyn Eaton wins the jump from the front row and takes the early lead.","tags":["dustin-eaton","andrew-cauthan"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2057,"title":"Anderson sends Hot Rod spinning","summary":"The league's two biggest bickerers meet again — Albert Anderson snags Dave Mayberry's quarter panel and sends him around on the front stretch, and the booth begs for a fight about it.","tags":["albert-anderson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2373,"title":"Osborne bounces off Anderson into the leader","summary":"Three-wide off turn four, Osborne pushes up into Anderson, bounces off him 'like a force field' hard into the inside wall — collecting race leader Dustyn Eaton and Jack Dixon with heavy damage.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2487,"title":"Ricky's shifter breaks mid-interview","summary":"In-race interview: Whittenburg admits his downshift button broke last week and now the upshift won't work either — 'I'm having all kinds of problems' — as the booth suggests unplugging it and plugging it back in.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":2824,"title":"Vaught-Burke championship rematch","summary":"Vaught and Burke go back at it side by side for the lead — a rerun of what the booth called the hardest racing they had ever seen from the season championship.","tags":["jess-vaught","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2922,"title":"Vaught's gamble: lap down, fastest lap","summary":"An unscheduled green-flag stop drops the 33 a lap down, but on four fresh Goodyears Vaught rips the fastest lap of the race (18.95) and starts the long climb back through the field.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3372,"title":"Restart mayhem: a huge gaggle of trucks wrecked","summary":"Adamson spins the tires on the restart and pounds the outside wall, triggering 'absolute mayhem' behind him — Dion Jones, Mayberry, Dixon and Kelly Kuehl all swept into the big pileup.","tags":["mike-adamson","dion-jones","dave-mayberry","jack-dixon","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4936,"title":"THE BIG ONE: Reeves flies over the pit wall","summary":"Mayberry's engine lets go, Anderson gets loose off turn four, and the front stretch becomes a parking lot — Austin Reeves' No. 6 goes flying and tumbling over the pit wall, hangs in the fence, lands on all fours and incredibly drives away; Oxendine gets turtled and Dion Jones is done for the night.","tags":["austin-reeves","albert-anderson","mike-adamson","greg-cline","josh-oxendine","dion-jones","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5458,"title":"A case of beer to unplug the leader's PC","summary":"The YouTube chat puts a bounty on the 33 — Kyle Vaught offers to go turn off Jess's PC for a case of beer, and the booth gleefully warns Jess about the 'insider threat' during his mid-race interview.","tags":["jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6145,"title":"18 to go: parking lot in turn one","summary":"Player and Anderson spin together off turn four and the entry of turn one fills with wrecked trucks — meatball flags for Player, Mayberry, Whittenburg, Oxendine, Anderson and Burke, and Oxendine's engine pops soon after.","tags":["andrew-player","albert-anderson","ricky-whittenburg","josh-oxendine","jeremiah-burke","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6501,"title":"Vaught wins the All-Star on old tires","summary":"White flag out and the 33 holds off Trevor Robertson on ancient tires to take the All-Star win from the back of the grid, with Jack the Ripper Dixon nipping Mike Adamson by a nose for the final podium spot.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","jack-dixon","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1237,"quote":"All right, now I want to see some hatred and anger, come on!","context":"Adam Turner begging for pre-race fireworks during the grid inversion","gold":3},{"t":2320,"quote":"I want to be in the grandstands or in pit lane eating a hot dog — I don't want to be racing here.","context":"Asked which lane a driver would want on these restarts","gold":3},{"t":2877,"quote":"We're not gonna have much paint left on these trucks, and that's going to be just fine.","context":"Blessing the old-school beating and banging at the throwback track","gold":3},{"t":4946,"quote":"It's a parking lot! There's guys upside down on the front stretch — we're gonna need a bambulance for the six!","context":"The Big One erupts and Austin Reeves sails over the pit wall","gold":5},{"t":5028,"quote":"It's probably a 7.5 on the landing there, but still able to walk away from it.","context":"Judging Reeves' airborne flight like a gymnastics routine","gold":4},{"t":5686,"quote":"Jess, I hope you got your one hand on a pistol there, because I think someone's coming after and trying to sabotage your PC.","context":"Relaying the YouTube-chat beer bounty to the race leader mid-interview","gold":4},{"t":6491,"quote":"I can't believe Jess out there on those old ass tires — he's still holding on to this lead out there.","context":"Vaught defying tire wear in the closing laps","gold":4},{"t":7164,"quote":"That man should be locked up, like, tonight — he should be incarcerated. I think I still got an old set of handcuffs around here.","context":"Albert Anderson (interviewed) on 30-year best friend and chat menace Russ Endicott","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"All-Star exhibition closing the VRL season (Season 5 teased in the winner interview: Coliseum, Bristol dirt, Chicago Street Course, Indianapolis Road Course, Charlotte Roval). Grid was inverted by hand by league admin Lori (race control, not a driver; garbled once as 'Gloria'). Name spellings are best guesses from auto-captions: winner's surname heard as Vaught/Vaughn/'just fought' (family Kyle and Taylor Vaught appear in chat); 'David Feit' (#1) is rendered 'David fight' throughout so spelling is unverified; 'Dustyn Eaton' is the booth's 'Dustin with a Y' distinguishing him from Team Tang teammate Dustin Wade, exact spelling unheard; Andrew Coffin (#10) also garbled as cotton/coth/Carson; Ricky Whittenburg spelled 'Wittenberg' in captions. Full 21-truck finishing order read on air at ~2:06:07: Vaught, Robertson, Dixon, Adamson, Osborne, Reeves, Wade, Anderson, Coffin, Fite, Eaton, C. Paul, Klein, Kuehl, Oxendine, Player, Burke, Whittenburg, A. Paul, Mayberry, Jones. Chat regulars (Russ Endicott, Earl Evans, Rebecca Smith, Kyle Vaught, Matt Beamer, Richard Gray, Greg Dobson, Edith Anderson) are viewers, not drivers. Broadcast dated by booth mentions of the FAA NOTAM outage and Jeff Beck's passing (Jan 2023).","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Yb3KPQFpmko":{"recap":"Tim Pope started from pole, but the Gen 4 cars barely reached turn one before a four-wide crash launched Jacob Young and damaged several contenders. Andrew Player's apparent brake failure caused the next caution, and Pope then lost the car from the lead on a restart, triggering a violent multi-car pileup. Alan Vaught, who had started 25th, charged through the field and repeatedly traded the lead with Josh Bittner while the race mixed long green runs with sudden bursts of chaos. Jonathan Osborne and Scott Martin brought out another yellow, Albert Anderson survived contact with Jorge Rincon, and Andrew Coffin went upside down in a massive lap-50 accident. Vaught took command through the final green-flag cycle and appeared ready to cruise home until Craig Goodenough's contact with Anderson and David Vaught sent Goodenough airborne with six laps left. The first overtime restart was waved off by another pileup. On the final attempt, Jeremiah Burke turned Bittner just after the white flag, collecting Trevor Robertson and much of the pack. Alan Vaught escaped to win, while Coffin and hard charger Dave Mayberry threaded through the wreckage to complete an improbable podium.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Andrew Cauthan","Dave Mayberry"],"moments":[{"t":1444,"title":"Four-wide turn one detonates the opener","summary":"The Gen 4 field goes four wide on cold tires; Nick Ramsey snaps loose, Mike Adamson and Jeremiah Burke are collected, and Jacob Young is launched in the secondary impact.","tags":["nick-ramsey","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke","jacob-young","dustin-reilly"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2388,"title":"Player's brakes disappear","summary":"Andrew Player suddenly slows and dives for the apron with an apparent brake or pedal failure, clipping another car and bringing out the second caution.","tags":["andrew-player"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":2683,"title":"Pope's leader snaps into a death machine","summary":"Tim Pope's car violently hooks right just after a restart, collecting Albert Anderson, Mike Everage, Kyle Vaught, Ricky Wittenberg, and others in a field-wide scramble.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","mike-everage","kyle-vaught","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3105,"title":"Bittner crosses Vaught back for the lead","summary":"Alan Vaught appears to complete the pass, but Josh Bittner catches the sliding rear end and executes a late crossover to continue their side-by-side lead fight.","tags":["josh-bittner","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3561,"title":"Osborne and Martin take the grass route","summary":"A wall-induced bottleneck catches Jonathan Osborne and Scott Martin, sending both through the infield and producing another caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","scott-martin"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3870,"title":"Anderson and Rincon crash without a yellow","summary":"Albert Anderson slides across Jorge Rincon's nose on the restart and both hammer the inside wall, yet drive away while the race stays green.","tags":["albert-anderson","george-rincon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4146,"title":"Coffin goes upside down in the Big One","summary":"Jonah Long and Andrew Coffin tangle at speed, Coffin flips, Austin Paul is launched, and Edson Oloa arrives into a sprawling Auto Club pileup.","tags":["jonah-long","andrew-cauthan","austin-paul","edson-ochoa"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4537,"title":"Five-wide restart launches Vaught's charge","summary":"The field fans from four to five wide as Albert Anderson attacks and Vaught surges from deep in the pack toward eventual control of the race.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":5546,"title":"Goodenough is launched with six to go","summary":"Craig Goodenough taps Anderson, David Vaught arrives into Goodenough, and the No. 89 is lifted into the air to erase Alan Vaught's two-second advantage.","tags":["craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5810,"title":"First overtime launch collapses immediately","summary":"Anderson spins the tires, Edward Smith and Andrew Player collide behind him, and Tim Pope is swept into the chain reaction before the leaders complete a lap.","tags":["albert-anderson","edward-w-smith","andrew-player","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6166,"title":"Burke turns Bittner under the white flag","summary":"Jeremiah Burke bumps Josh Bittner while racing for the win, spinning both and collecting Trevor Robertson as the rest of the field erupts down the backstretch.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","josh-bittner","trevor-robertson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6199,"title":"Vaught wins while Coffin and Mayberry escape","summary":"Alan Vaught drives clear of the final-lap Big One; Andrew Coffin dives beneath the carnage for second and Dave Mayberry survives from 32nd to claim third.","tags":["jess-vaught","andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1444,"quote":"We're already going to have our first caution — the 17 goes airborne!","context":"The field crashes seconds after the initial green","gold":5},{"t":2696,"quote":"Oh no, it's a death machine! Oh my goodness — just carnage everywhere.","context":"Pope's car snaps across the field on the restart","gold":5},{"t":4146,"quote":"The three's in the air, the 10 is upside down! Oh my goodness, that was a big one!","context":"Coffin and Austin Paul are launched in the lap-50 pileup","gold":5},{"t":4537,"quote":"We're going four wide — five wide behind him! That was tight!","context":"The pack fans across Auto Club on the restart","gold":5},{"t":5668,"quote":"Everybody get ready to have all those amplifiers turned on up to 11.","context":"The booth prepares for a one-attempt overtime shootout","gold":4},{"t":5788,"quote":"It is time to buckle up, strap on those drinking helmets, and throw inhibition out the window!","context":"The first overtime restart approaches","gold":5},{"t":6166,"quote":"Contact made — oh no! There goes the six, the 53 — oh my goodness!","context":"The leaders trigger the final-lap Big One","gold":5},{"t":6221,"quote":"It was just absolute chaos down the backstretch — everybody fighting for whatever they can.","context":"The booth replays the race-deciding pileup","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 7, Round 4 at Auto Club, 85 laps in the Gen 4 car. The winner, podium, and full finishing order are explicitly stated after the race. Andrew Coffin's captions repeatedly render his surname as 'cin/caon'; the canonical archive spelling is used. Dave Mayberry gained 29 positions in the No. 29 and is explicitly named hard charger.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"yBTOk0FMKEo":{"recap":"VRL wrapped its third season with championship night at Talladega — 94 laps and 250 miles in the Xfinity cars, with Alan Vaught's driver title and Limitless Motorsports' team championship already mathematically locked up. Albert Anderson snatched the pole from Vaught in the final seconds of qualifying, and the race ran caution-free until about five laps to go, decided instead by green-flag pit cycles and fuel saving with Greg Klein leading much of the final run. The night's only caution — a multi-car wreck that spun Jeremiah Burke and Anderson just as half the field dove for pit road — set up a one-attempt green-white-checkered with Cult of Chaos lined up second through fifth. A white-flag stack-up collected Ricky Whittenburg and Chandler Paul, but Austin Paul, shoved to the stripe by Tim Pope, won the drag race to the line for Cult of Chaos's first win of the season ahead of Pope and Jack 'the Ripper' Dixon. Champion Vaught, caught in the late carnage, finished ninth to close a season in which he averaged a third-place finish.","winner":"Austin Paul","podium":["Austin Paul","Tim Pope","Jack Dixon"],"moments":[{"t":1514,"title":"Anderson steals the pole in the final seconds","summary":"Albert Anderson snatches pole position away from champion Alan Vaught at the end of qualifying, with the top five separated by about three hundredths of a second.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":1824,"title":"Green flag on the championship finale","summary":"Anderson and Vaught bring the 22-car field to the green side by side for 94 laps at Talladega, and the pack immediately goes three wide.","tags":["albert-anderson","jess-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":2947,"title":"Pit road rush hour — black flags fly","summary":"The first green-flag stop cycle turns chaotic: speeding black flags for Burke, Everidge and Jones, while pole-sitter Anderson clips the commitment cone and sits through a 49-second stop that costs him the lead lap.","tags":["albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","mike-everage","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3798,"title":"Poke Salad Tony's classy lapper move","summary":"Lapped and alone in no-man's land, Tony Poke radios the leaders that he'll hug the yellow line, then drops to the apron to wave the pack by — the booth salutes the class move.","tags":["tony-polk","timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4650,"title":"Cawthon hammers the inside wall","summary":"An off-center shot from the 48 sends Andrew Cawthon spinning into a hard single-car impact on the inside wall — heavy damage, but race control lets it stay green.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","jack-dixon"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5280,"title":"Anderson begs race control for a caution","summary":"A lap down and desperate, Anderson pleads over the radio that there's grass and debris all over the trioval — the booth cracks that there are no styrofoam cups in simulation land.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6011,"title":"McCabe goes for a wild ride","summary":"McCabe drifts up into the 57 off the yellow line and gets sent spinning through the inside grass with the 57 and the 4 collected — and still no caution flies.","tags":["chad-mccabe","russ-endicott","dion-jones"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6091,"title":"Beating and banging for the lucky dog","summary":"Kilgore takes a trip through the grass and trades hard contact with race-winning contender Vaught as the fight for the lucky dog boils over inside the lead pack.","tags":["russ-kilgore","jess-vaught","dave-mayberry"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6503,"title":"The Big One with five to go","summary":"As half the field dives for pit road on fumes, Mayberry hits the commitment cone, Burke and Anderson spin, and the 82 and 57 get knotted up — the night's ONLY caution after roughly 89 green laps, forcing a green-white-checkered.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson","mike-everage","chad-mccabe","russ-endicott"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6959,"title":"Drinking-helmet time: one-shot GWC","summary":"Fuel-gambling leader Greg Klein takes the field down for the one and only green-white-checkered attempt with Cult of Chaos stacked second through fifth behind him.","tags":["greg-cline","chandler-paul","austin-paul","ricky-whittenburg","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7003,"title":"White-flag stack-up wipes out the Cult","summary":"Whittenburg gets too big a push from Kuehl on the outside, comes down across teammate Chandler Paul and stacks up the pack at the white flag — no caution, leaving five cars with a shot at the win.","tags":["ricky-whittenburg","chandler-paul","kelly-keel","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7049,"title":"Austin Paul wins it for Cult of Chaos","summary":"Tim Pope glues himself to the No. 3's bumper and pushes Austin Paul past Klein as Whittenburg arrives with a full head of steam — nose to tail across the line, Cult of Chaos finally reaches victory lane in the season finale.","tags":["austin-paul","timothy-pope","jack-dixon","greg-cline","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":2734,"quote":"Earl's just riding around out there, he's probably eating potato chips or a quarter pounder with cheese.","context":"Earl Evans lapping alone with nobody to race after his pit-start penalty","gold":4},{"t":3075,"quote":"Man, this is rush hour traffic down there in Houston, everybody trying to find their lane.","context":"the mad scramble of the first round of green-flag pit stops","gold":3},{"t":5292,"quote":"Begging and pleading, but there's no styrofoam cups here in simulation land.","context":"Albert Anderson lobbying race control for a debris caution","gold":4},{"t":6035,"quote":"People need some new change of drawers out there right now, I guarantee.","context":"the field barely threading through Chad McCabe's wild ride","gold":3},{"t":6959,"quote":"It is time to buckle up, strap on that drinking helmet, and throw inhibition out the window.","context":"launching the one-shot green-white-checkered to end the season","gold":5},{"t":7084,"quote":"Well cock-a-doodle-doo, how do you do, Cult of Chaos!","context":"the call as Austin Paul takes the checkered flag","gold":5},{"t":7129,"quote":"He just comes straight on down and takes out his teammate and pretty much the rest of the field — good night.","context":"replaying the white-flag stack-up triggered by the 55","gold":3},{"t":8819,"quote":"I'm Alan Brown, for Alan Kewins and Alan English — this is an all-Allen broadcast and we're signing off. We goin', Allens, see ya!","context":"the season-ending sign-off","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Guest commentator's surname is heavily garbled in captions (Queens / qins / kewins / Cubans / killings); 'Alan Kewins' follows the sign-off captions but the true spelling is uncertain (possibly Kuehns). Regular booth member Adam Turner was absent (dove hunting); Lori Vaught (Jess's wife) served as race controller and league admin. 'Dustin Riehle' (always captioned 'Dustin really') and 'Andrew Cawthon' are best-guess spellings. Ricky Whittenburg is captioned 'Wittenberg' throughout. Osborne (#81, nicknamed Chachi) missed the race after reinstalling Windows; first name never stated. Randy Schweitzer (#78) disconnected before the start. The final-lap stack-up drew no caution, so the finish ran green. Full finishing order read out around 8467s: Austin Paul, Pope, Dixon, Klein, Whittenburg, Riley, Kuehl, Kilgore, Vaught, Chandler Paul, Anderson, Burke, Adamson, Everidge, Mayberry, Ottinger, McCabe, Cawthon, Poke, Evans, Endicott, Jones. Race was the Season 3 finale (broadcast Wed Sept 14, 2022); Season 4 (trucks, stage racing, playoffs) announced to start Sept 28. Edith Anderson won Fan of the Season; Shelby Boone Fan of the Race; Greg Klein random-draw driver of the day, and Klein announced as departing next season due to work schedule.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"yemWp1UYu2Q":{"recap":"Alan Vaught had to drive through the Michigan field twice to earn his first win of Season 2. Starting 27th under the league's winner-balancing rule, Vaught climbed into contention during a long opening act built around green-flag stops and varied tire calls, only for a competition-caution speeding penalty to send him back into the 20s. The late race then changed character: contact involving Jeremiah Burke, Russ Endicott and Eric Klafka ended Burke's strong run, another pileup followed, and a Turn 2 stack-up appeared to create a nine-lap shootout. That restart produced one more caution, making the later five-lap dash the actual finish. Teammate Kelly Kuehl pushed Vaught clear of Jorge Rincon on the final launch, then mounted his own inside challenge in Turns 3 and 4 on the last lap. Vaught closed the lane and took the checkered flag over Kuehl and Rincon, gaining 26 positions for hard-charger honors. Kuehl said earlier trouble had left him ready to quit; Vaught reached victory lane still struggling to believe the recovery had ended in a win.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Kelly Kuehl","Jorge Rincon"],"moments":[{"t":1381,"title":"Ellis launches from pole","summary":"John Ellis clears Kelly Kuehl at the green before Mike Adamson attacks for the lead and the field quickly forms multiple lanes.","tags":["john-ellis","kelly-keel","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1964,"title":"Everage spins but the race stays green","summary":"Michael Everage is turned in a single-truck incident, avoids the wall, and continues without a caution as the opening run rolls on.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"spin"},{"t":2449,"title":"Burke inherits the lead through pit strategy","summary":"An early stop lets Jeremiah Burke cycle to the front while most of the contenders complete the first green-flag pit sequence.","tags":["jeremiah-burke","albert-anderson","mike-adamson"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4100,"title":"Competition caution ends the long opening act","summary":"The scheduled yellow flies as Russ Kilgore begins lap 66, bringing the varied fuel and tire strategies back together.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"caution"},{"t":4399,"title":"Ottinger hits the wall after the restart","summary":"Dion Jones's old tires cause a major check-up and Jeffrey Ottinger is sent into the wall amid three-wide traffic.","tags":["dion-jones","jeff-ottinger"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5885,"title":"Burke and Endicott collide","summary":"Lapped Russ Endicott makes contact with Jeremiah Burke and Eric Klafka, ending Burke's strong run and drawing a frustrated attempted swipe under caution.","tags":["russ-endicott","jeremiah-burke","eric-klafka"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6257,"title":"French and Adamson trigger another yellow","summary":"Justin French and Mike Adamson make contact in tight traffic, and John Ellis takes responsibility over the radio for the ensuing pileup.","tags":["justin-french","mike-adamson","john-ellis"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6729,"title":"Turn 2 pileup sets up a nine-lap shootout","summary":"A check-up behind Pope's aggressive entry snowballs into a crash involving Albert Anderson, Chandler Paul, Russ Kilgore and others.","tags":["timothy-pope","albert-anderson","chandler-paul","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7030,"title":"Vaught leads the final restart","summary":"Vaught gets a strong launch with nine laps remaining and Rincon slots behind him, but a deeper crash involving Robert Jordan and Jack Dixon produces one last reset.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","robert-jordan","jack-dixon"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7358,"title":"Vaught and Kuehl control the five-lap dash","summary":"On the final restart, Kuehl pushes teammate Vaught clear of Rincon before setting up his own challenge for the win.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":7556,"title":"Vaught blocks the last-lap bid and wins","summary":"Kuehl looks inside in Turns 3 and 4, but Vaught closes the door and takes his first win of the season over Kuehl and Rincon.","tags":["jess-vaught","kelly-keel","george-rincon"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":7556,"quote":"Jess Vaught has two corners remaining to pick up his first win on the season here tonight.","context":"The booth sets up Vaught's final defensive lap.","gold":2},{"t":7576,"quote":"His first win here tonight at Michigan, with Kelly Keel in second and George Rincon in third — what a finish!","context":"The live finish call.","gold":5},{"t":7788,"quote":"I was ready to quit. Jess was like, 'Oh, don't do that.'","context":"Kuehl explains how he recovered from an early pit-entry crash to finish second.","gold":5},{"t":8238,"quote":"I can't believe I'm sitting in victory lane right now.","context":"Vaught opens his winner interview after twice charging from the back.","gold":5},{"t":8418,"quote":"I saw a swing and a miss during caution.","context":"Vaught alludes to the frustration that followed one late incident.","gold":5},{"t":8598,"quote":"Even better than victory circle, I get to sleep in a bed tonight, guys.","context":"Vaught jokes after Lori reveals he had already been on the couch.","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"The finish call, podium interviews, and complete results rundown explicitly confirm Vaught, Kuehl, and Rincon. Vaught started 27th after the league's winner/EOL balancing rule and was credited as hard charger at plus 26; Rincon gained 16 positions. Michael Everage won the random-driver draw after finishing fifth. The race was 125 laps with one fast repair, a 13-incident disqualification limit, 70% fuel, and five total tire sets. The moment at 2:02:38 (7358s) is the actual final five-lap restart; the earlier nine-lap restart later drew another caution.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"YfhsU2Caczk":{"recap":"VRL's 200-lap throwback race at Rockingham paired vintage NASCAR paint schemes with a punishing, bumpy one-mile track and a 17-incident-point disqualification limit. Mike Adamson led early, but repeated wall contacts and wrecks shuffled the order before John Ellis emerged as the late leader through the final green-flag pit cycle. Tim Pope, on tires five laps newer than Ellis's, erased a large deficit and reached the leader with four laps remaining, but Ellis held the preferred line and resisted Pope's outside bid on the final lap for his first win of the season. Jonathan Osborne broke through Adamson's defensive line in the closing laps to finish third, with Alan Vaught fourth and Adamson fifth.","winner":"John Ellis","podium":["John Ellis","Tim Pope","Jonathan Osborne"],"moments":[{"t":1453,"title":"Adamson leads the throwbacks to green","summary":"Pole-sitter Mike Adamson launches the 200-lap Rockingham race while a field of vintage tribute schemes immediately struggles for grip on cold tires.","tags":["mike-adamson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1511,"title":"Everage makes a near-sideways save","summary":"Michael Everage breaks loose down the backstretch and slides nearly sideways across the track, but gathers the truck without triggering a wreck.","tags":["mike-everage"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":1554,"title":"Kuehl spins into Burke","summary":"Kelly Kuehl and Justin French converge on the same lane entering Turn 1; Kuehl spins and Jeremiah Burke has nowhere to go before striking the rotating truck.","tags":["kelly-keel","justin-french","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2466,"title":"Green's wall hit triggers a big backstretch crash","summary":"Rob Green catches the outside wall and collects Kuehl, sending Kuehl hard toward the inside pit wall and bringing out a yellow around lap 36.","tags":["rob-green","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2969,"title":"Pit-exit pileup bottles up the field","summary":"Contact between Russ Kilgore and Dustin Riehle at pit exit snowballs into a bottleneck that also involves Burke, Rincon, Whittenburg, Kuehl, and others.","tags":["russ-kilgore","dustin-reilly","jeremiah-burke","george-rincon","ricky-whittenburg","kelly-keel"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3989,"title":"The leader is collected amid a blinking incident","summary":"Douglas Camp gets sideways after briefly blinking, contact develops with Jeffrey Green, Tim Pope loses control, and early leader Adamson takes a hard hit before the third caution.","tags":["douglas-camp","jeffrey-green","timothy-pope","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4113,"title":"Ellis wins the race off pit road","summary":"Under the third caution, John Ellis beats Alan Vaught and Jonathan Osborne out of the pits and takes control of the race's next phase.","tags":["john-ellis","jess-vaught","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5145,"title":"Green rebounds into traffic before the competition yellow","summary":"Rob Green bounces off the wall and comes back down into traffic, involving Jack Dixon just before the scheduled competition caution at lap 123.","tags":["rob-green","jack-dixon"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5478,"title":"Kuehl and Jeffrey Green are disqualified","summary":"Kelly Kuehl and Jeffrey Green reach the 17-incident-point limit and are removed from the race after a three-wide contact sequence involving Albert Anderson and Dave Mayberry.","tags":["kelly-keel","jeffrey-green","albert-anderson","dave-mayberry"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6526,"title":"The final green-flag cycle reshapes the lead","summary":"Adamson begins the final stop sequence near lap 165; Ellis pits on lap 166 and Pope on lap 171, giving Pope a five-lap tire advantage for the run to the finish.","tags":["mike-adamson","john-ellis","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":6948,"title":"Pope clears Adamson and starts hunting Ellis","summary":"Pope passes Adamson for second with 19 laps left and begins erasing an approximately five-to-six-second deficit to Ellis.","tags":["timothy-pope","mike-adamson","john-ellis"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":7359,"title":"Ellis withstands Pope's last-lap charge","summary":"Pope reaches Ellis with four laps remaining and tries the outside on the white-flag lap, but Ellis holds on for his first win of the season as Osborne and Vaught finally clear Adamson behind them.","tags":["john-ellis","timothy-pope","jonathan-osborne","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":766,"quote":"Rockingham is a one-mile track, 200 laps. That means, English, that for you in Louisiana, that's 200 miles.","context":"Adam Turner needles Allen English during the race setup","gold":3},{"t":1666,"quote":"You know what they call this bumpy track in Louisiana? The perfect road, because that's better than anything we got around here.","context":"Allen English jokes about Rockingham's notoriously rough surface","gold":4},{"t":4597,"quote":"John Ellis is just in a totally different time zone here tonight.","context":"The booth marvels at Ellis dipping into the 23-second lap range","gold":3},{"t":7292,"quote":"Please, Lord, don't let there be a yellow.","context":"The booth imagines Ellis's thoughts as Pope closes in the final laps","gold":4},{"t":7431,"quote":"Here comes Pope down around the outside, but not in time! John Ellis picks up the first win for him of the season.","context":"The final-lap winning call at Rockingham","gold":5},{"t":8032,"quote":"I was surviving. I don't know how I got away with the zero-x, but somehow, someway, here I am finishing in sixth place.","context":"Josh Bittner describes gaining 16 positions without an incident point","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"This race is not mapped in pipeline/seasons_map.json; the metadata and broadcast title identify it only as 'VRL: Throwback Race @ Rockingham,' uploaded March 24, 2022. The broadcast explicitly calls Ellis the winner and reads Pope second and Osborne third; the winner interview is not present in the caption transcript even though the booth says it is coming. The results discussion is partially garbled, but the complete 27-driver starting grid is explicit. Kuehl and Jeffrey Green were explicitly disqualified for incident points; the booth also suspected, but did not confirm, a later Rob Green disqualification, so none is asserted. Transcript timestamps end at 2:21:51 (8511 seconds), within the 8524-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"YgFdhgb14jo":{"recap":"The Dega Domination 213 opened the VRL Premiere Series Championship 4 round at Talladega — an 80-lap, 213-mile truck race with no fast repairs — with Tim Pope and Dillon Bryant arriving tied atop the standings at 4,030 points ahead of Craig Goodenough and Chris Goans. Goodenough's title bid took an immediate hit when he was swept up in a lap-8 backstretch wreck with Pope and Albert Anderson that also knocked Scott Rooney out of the race. Polesitter Jonathan Osborne later produced the save of the night, gathering up a sideways truck at the head of the pack near lap 50, and the field stayed remarkably clean until the final green-flag pit cycle, when a massive wreck with four laps to go collected Pope, Trevor Robertson, Kelly Kuehl, Chris Goans and Tom Barish. When the pack stacked up again seconds after the green-white-checkered restart, iRacing froze the field and Dillon Bryant — carrying roughly 37 seconds of unrepaired damage — was declared the winner ahead of Andy Player, with Greg Klein shown third before revealing a final-restart penalty. Bryant left Talladega showing a roughly 23-point championship lead heading to Martinsville and Phoenix.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Andrew Player"],"moments":[{"t":1490,"title":"Green flag on Dega Domination 213","summary":"The 27-truck field takes the green with polesitter Jonathan Osborne edging Tom Barish in a clean two-by-two start, Albert Anderson rolling a Budweiser scheme on the outside.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","tom-barish","albert-anderson"],"heat":2,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":1873,"title":"The Big One strikes on lap 8","summary":"Eight laps in, three championship-round drivers tangle on the backstretch — Goodenough noses the wall hard, Pope takes front-end damage, Anderson hits hard, Bryant barely threads through, and Scott Rooney is knocked out of the race.","tags":["timothy-pope","craig-goodenough","albert-anderson","dylan-bryant","scott-rooney"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2126,"title":"Wrecked Goodenough shrugs it off","summary":"Moments after his title-hope-crushing wreck, Goodenough joins the booth smiling: 'It's all good, man. Super Speedway racing' — vowing to fix it, ride around laps down, and see what happens.","tags":["craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3425,"title":"Gallagher spins himself to save the 38","summary":"Entering pit road hot in the first green-flag cycle, Gallagher deliberately turns himself around rather than plow into the 38, sacrificing his own race position to avoid ruining somebody else's night.","tags":["john-gallagher","chris-goans"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4407,"title":"Osborne's miracle save at the head of the pack","summary":"Leading a mob of trucks, Osborne gets turned sideways, gathers it up off the apron as the field splits around him — 'that should have been massive' — drawing the caution while Bryant picks up heavy nose damage in the scramble.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","dylan-bryant","kelly-keel","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":4658,"title":"Damaged Superman holds the point","summary":"Race leader Bryant tells the booth he's carrying 38 seconds of damage after Osborne 'self cleared himself off my nose' — planning to tuck into the draft and hope the truck still cuts the air.","tags":["dylan-bryant"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":5835,"title":"Land rush: the money stop under green","summary":"With about six laps left the entire lead pack dives onto pit road at once — 'Land rush, folks. Safe. Safe so far.' — while Goodenough gambles, stays out an extra lap, and unlaps himself the old-fashioned way.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5945,"title":"Four to go: Pope's night goes up in smoke","summary":"As trucks blend off pit road, Barish washes up, Bryant lifts high, and Kill's dive underneath triggers a massive wreck that collects points co-leader Pope, chase leader Robertson, Anderson, Goans and more — Bryant escapes through the middle, and Kill apologizes to everyone on the radio.","tags":["timothy-pope","tom-barish","kelly-keel","dylan-bryant","trevor-robertson","albert-anderson","chris-goans","dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6372,"title":"Overtime lasts seconds — Bryant wins frozen","summary":"The green-white-checkered barely launches before the inside line stacks up and wrecks the pack; under the league's one-attempt overtime iRacing freezes the field and Dillon Bryant is declared the Dega Domination 213 winner ahead of Andy Player.","tags":["dylan-bryant","andrew-player","timothy-pope","albert-anderson","dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":6675,"title":"Klein's podium vanishes live on air","summary":"Pulled into the booth as the third-place finisher, Klein reveals he was just penalized for being a couple inches ahead of Bryant on the final restart, dropping him to 22nd — 'That's the Charlie Brown in the football thing right there' — and hands the interview to Mike Everidge.","tags":["greg-cline","mike-everage","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":217,"quote":"This ain't your mama's racing stream.","context":"channel stinger opening the broadcast","gold":4},{"t":2270,"quote":"You wouldn't have been talking to me. I'd been laying in the floor crying probably.","context":"Ricky on how calmly Craig Goodenough took his early wreck","gold":4},{"t":3656,"quote":"What could go wrong, Ricky? — Yeah. Whole lot.","context":"watching the roof cam as the pack runs three-wide","gold":3},{"t":4505,"quote":"This is really nothing. This is a nothing burger for an accident here at Talladega.","context":"replaying Osborne's near-catastrophic save at the front of the pack","gold":3},{"t":5839,"quote":"Oh boy. Land rush, folks. Safe. Safe so far. Safe.","context":"the entire lead pack dives onto pit road for the final green-flag stop","gold":4},{"t":6385,"quote":"That's it. It's over. They wrecked. Are you kidding me?","context":"the green-white-checkered attempt wrecks seconds after the restart","gold":4},{"t":7273,"quote":"I saw you in three or four crashes that you was able to maneuver around of like you was Houdini. So, I think you cashed those poker chips in tonight, brother.","context":"Ricky to race winner Dillon Bryant in the victory interview","gold":5},{"t":7683,"quote":"Until then, race fans, remember: stay sharp, stay fast, stay vigilant.","context":"Alan's signature sign-off closing the broadcast","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Third place is ambiguous: the booth announced a podium of Bryant/Player/Klein, but Klein reported live that a final-restart penalty (a couple inches ahead of Bryant) dropped him to 22nd, and Mike Everidge was interviewed as the third-place finisher — yet the closing results read-through still listed Klein 3rd and Everidge 4th, so podium is listed only through P2. Heavy auto-caption garbling; least-certain best-guess names: Chris Goins (Gones/Gins/Gains), Kelly Kuehl (Kill/Hill/Cole), Tom Barish (Beerish/Bears), John Schanbacher (Scholach/Schwlocker/Shenbachler/Shan Bacher), Kyle Vault (Va/Block/Calvot), Jorge Rincon (Ren Khan/Ranc/Rcon), Andrew Cowan (Cawan/Cawin), and broadcaster Alan Vaughn (heard as 'Alan Vaugh'/'Allen'/'Allan'). A 'Burke' was named in Bryant's Allstar team shoutout but is otherwise unidentified; Kevin Hunt was named only as a Team Tang teammate and may not have raced tonight. Lori (also captioned Lauri), Alan's wife, is the league admin posting on-screen messages. The finish came under the league's one-attempt overtime rule: the field was frozen when the GWC wreck occurred, so the final order was set by the freeze rather than a racing finish. This was race 1 of 3 in the Championship 4 (Talladega, Martinsville, Phoenix); it also ran as race 4 of 6 in the separate contender chase led by Trevor Robertson over Dustin Wade and Greg Klein.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"YKBbvdXXD40":{"recap":"Championship leader Dillon Bryant took the pole and had 'the fastest truck tonight, hands down' in the Paperclip Punishment 104 at virtual Martinsville, the middle leg of the VRL Premiere Series Season 12 championship round with the title four of Bryant, Craig Goodenough, Tim Pope and Chris Goans all racing ahead of the Phoenix finale. The 150-lapper turned into a demolition derby with 18 cautions that wrecked contender-championship leader Trevor Robertson (24th) and swallowed late threat Mike Adamson, who slammed the inside wall minutes after promising to 'go get me a win.' The race ended frozen under yellow when the final caution flew during the league's one-and-only green-white-checkered attempt, handing Bryant the provisional win over Tim Pope and Albert Anderson. Controversy followed instantly: Bryant was black-flagged on the final restart, leaving the result — and potentially the championship picture — pending review by race admin Lori. Alan Bach called the entire night solo, with regular partner Ricky Whittenburg out with laryngitis.","winner":"Dillon Bryant","podium":["Dillon Bryant","Tim Pope","Albert Anderson"],"moments":[{"t":1168,"title":"First caution just six laps in","summary":"Greg Dobson gets in with too much rear bias and spins the 085, and John Gallagher's 123 lands right in his lap along with Tom Beerish — the first yellow at lap 6, which the booth notes is already further than Monday night's race got.","tags":["greg-dobson","john-gallagher","tom-barish"],"heat":2,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2570,"title":"Pope runs down the leader on fresh tires","summary":"After Bryant stays out under caution, Tim Pope's fresh-tire 7 machine hunts down the leader and 'pretty handily takes that position' — the pit-cycle gamble the booth warned about all night.","tags":["timothy-pope","dylan-bryant"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":2924,"title":"Bumper cars on the restart","summary":"Craig Goodenough dives for the bottom before clearing Mike Everidge's 82 and gets launched into Tony Benfield's 75, collecting Jonathan Osborne while Scott Rooney sits on the outside with nowhere to go — 'a little bumper cars action.'","tags":["craig-goodenough","mike-everage","stony-benfield","jonathan-osborne","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3138,"title":"'That's a lot of trucks'","summary":"The seventh caution sweeps up five-plus trucks after Jonathan Osborne goes in a little hot on Mike Adamson, turning Mike Everidge and stacking up Anderson, Dobson, Beerish and Schollenbacher behind them.","tags":["albert-anderson","mike-everage","greg-dobson","tom-barish","jonathan-osborne","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4259,"title":"The Big One at the Paperclip","summary":"After Jorge Rincon launches the restart super late, the field stacks up: Benfield and Goodenough touch, Trevor Robertson loses a fender 'and it's just a pile up from there' with seven-plus trucks sideways in turn one.","tags":["trevor-robertson","stony-benfield","craig-goodenough","john-mcadam","jonathan-osborne","mike-everage"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4383,"title":"Pope threads the needle","summary":"The replay from Tim Pope's cockpit shows him slicing straight through the sideways trucks untouched — 'that's what you call threading the needle' — wreck avoidance that keeps his championship night alive.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":4674,"title":"Contender leader's night falls apart","summary":"Trevor Robertson, the contender-championship leader, aims for a gap between the 75 and 47 that isn't there — the left front is demolished and he has to tow to pit lane, on his way to a 24th-place finish.","tags":["trevor-robertson"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4781,"title":"Devil horns and a promise","summary":"Running eighth with 25 to go, Mike Adamson tells the booth 'I'm about to go get me a win' and throws up devil horns for his onboard camera before the restart.","tags":["mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":4872,"title":"99 and 89 tangle out of a podium spot","summary":"'Oh no. Oh no.' — Albert Anderson gets a piece of Craig Goodenough's left rear, they lock together and the 88 slides past; the 89 spins out of contention yet somehow lines back up second for the restart while Anderson incredibly saves his truck.","tags":["albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5252,"title":"Adamson finds the inside wall","summary":"Minutes after promising a win, Mike Adamson pounds the inside retaining wall in a late caution that starts when Tony Benfield spins under braking and collects Kelly Kuehl — the 88's contention ends and he limps home 18th.","tags":["mike-adamson","kelly-keel","stony-benfield","scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5636,"title":"Frozen at the finish","summary":"On the league's one and only green-white-checkered attempt, the 18th caution flies before Dillon Bryant can take the white flag — the field is frozen and Bryant wins the Paperclip Punishment 104 over Tim Pope and Albert Anderson.","tags":["dylan-bryant","timothy-pope","albert-anderson"],"heat":4,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5909,"title":"The black flag bombshell","summary":"In his podium interview Albert Anderson reveals Bryant was black-flagged on the final restart — Goodenough claimed Anderson was hanging back, Bryant admits he brought the field down faster on purpose, and the win goes under review by race admin Lori with roughly a 20th-place finish on the line.","tags":["dylan-bryant","albert-anderson","craig-goodenough"],"heat":5,"kind":"drama","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":743,"quote":"Lots of beating and banging. It's basically gladiators out there. It's not the coliseum, but it's very close.","context":"Alan Bach setting the scene for Martinsville before the green flag","gold":3},{"t":2558,"quote":"Mike Adamson is like Darth Vader in his cocoon here racing.","context":"Showing Adamson's new over-the-shoulder onboard camera view","gold":4},{"t":2879,"quote":"What's the team orders tonight? Anything? — Just go win.","context":"Greg Dobson deadpans the Phoenix Racing team plan mid-caution interview","gold":4},{"t":4074,"quote":"You hear Andy Player shutting off his engine. Don't tell anybody. I think he's saving gas.","context":"Catching the master strategist killing his engine under caution","gold":4},{"t":4385,"quote":"Wow. Talk about that's what you call threading the needle.","context":"Tim Pope slices untouched through the multi-truck pileup","gold":4},{"t":4786,"quote":"I don't know. I'm about to get after it. I'm about to go get me a win.","context":"Mike Adamson with 25 to go — he found the inside wall soon after","gold":4},{"t":6016,"quote":"I plan on kicking a lot of ass there next week, so it should be pretty good.","context":"Albert Anderson looking ahead to the Phoenix finale after his podium","gold":3},{"t":6497,"quote":"Stay sharp, stay fast, stay vigilante, and we'll see you next time.","context":"Alan Bach's signature VRN sign-off to close the broadcast","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"Winner is provisional: Dillon Bryant was black-flagged on the final restart and results were announced as unofficial pending review by race admin Lori (Bryant said an upheld black flag would drop him to roughly a 20th-place finish). Several names are auto-caption best guesses: 'Jorge Rincon' (#28, heard as Rcon/Rencon/Rinkcon/Vancage), 'John Schollenbacher' (#12 Coors Light, nicknamed 'the Closer'), 'Mike Everidge' (#82), 'Andrew Cowan' (#10), 'Kelly Kuehl' (#01), 'Tom Beerish' (#35). The results readout garbled 14th/15th ('14th George Vancage 15th') — the unnamed spot is likely Mike Everidge, the only driver missing from the readout. Full order as read: Bryant, Pope, Anderson, Goodenough, Gomes, Gallagher, Cowan, Milner, Klein, Player, Osborne, Eaton, McAdam, [garbled 14th/15th incl. Rincon], Rooney, Schollenbacher, Adamson, Kill, Mayberry, Benfield, Beerish, Dobson, Robertson, Wade. The booth repeatedly said Miami Homestead for the finale before correcting on-air that the championship race is at Phoenix. Regular co-commentator Ricky Whittenburg missed the broadcast with laryngitis. Race: 150 laps, 18 cautions, 25 trucks; also race 5 of 6 for the separate VRL Contender championship led by Trevor Robertson over Dustin Wade and Greg Klein.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"yWPlme5EWWs":{"recap":"Alan Vaught led from pole to checkered flag at Road America to become Season 3's first repeat winner. Jorge Rincon remained within striking distance through the first several stints, but Vaught stayed at qualifying pace to preserve his focus and pulled clear as traffic and small mistakes slowed Rincon. Jeremiah Burke recovered from an unusually early first stop, a spin on his out-lap, and several other excursions to finish third, while David Feit climbed 11 positions to fourth. With no full-course cautions available, numerous spins and hard impacts played out under green, and Vaught ultimately won by 19 seconds over Rincon.","winner":"Alan Vaught","podium":["Alan Vaught","Jorge Rincon","Jeremiah Burke"],"moments":[{"t":1901,"title":"Vaught launches from pole","summary":"Alan Vaught leads Jorge Rincon and Jeremiah Burke through Turn 1, beginning a flag-to-flag run at the head of the field.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":2585,"title":"Burke makes a very early stop","summary":"Running near the front, Jeremiah Burke pits far earlier than the other leaders as part of an alternate fuel strategy that is later compromised by a spin on his out-lap.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2700,"title":"Osborne slams the Kink wall","summary":"John Osborne crashes hard at the Kink and pits for repairs, beginning a long recovery that eventually carries him back to seventh.","tags":["jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3197,"title":"Fate and Ott spin together","summary":"David Feit and Jim Ott both lose control while negotiating Robert Jordan's off-track car; Fite remains on the pavement while Ott slides through the gravel.","tags":["david-fite","jim-ott","robert-jordan"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":3642,"title":"Ott avoids Osborne's second spin","summary":"Osborne spins directly in front of Ott, who reacts quickly enough to stop completely and avoid a collision before resuming.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":4519,"title":"Jones climbs the tire barrier","summary":"Dion Jones gets two tires into the grass under braking, rockets into the tire barrier, and comes to rest perched atop it with the nose torn away.","tags":["dion-jones"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5373,"title":"Vaught and Rincon stop together","summary":"At the halfway point, Vaught and Rincon make their second scheduled stops together while Burke's offset strategy leaves him working through traffic.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5963,"title":"Fate holds Ott in a podium fight","summary":"David Feit and Jim Ott run nose-to-tail for third with 20 laps and another pit stop remaining, continuing one of the race's closest sustained battles.","tags":["david-fite","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":7305,"title":"Final stops create a fuel question","summary":"After Vaught and Rincon complete their last stops, Burke and Mike Adamson attempt to stretch older fuel; both eventually pit, with Burke retaining third.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke","mike-adamson"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":8412,"title":"Jordan spins in front of the leaders","summary":"Robert Jordan spins while Vaught approaches late in the race, but Vaught clears the incident and continues toward the white flag.","tags":["robert-jordan","jess-vaught"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"incident"},{"t":8902,"title":"Vaught completes a flag-to-flag victory","summary":"Vaught takes the checkered flag as the season's first two-time winner, 19 seconds ahead of Rincon, with Burke completing the podium.","tags":["jess-vaught","george-rincon","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3197,"quote":"That was just an absolute kerfuffle.","context":"The booth reacts after Fate and Ott both spin while navigating Jordan","gold":3},{"t":8226,"quote":"Dude, I am tired. My foot hurts. I made every mistake in the book.","context":"Jeremiah Burke describes the physical and mental toll after finishing third","gold":5},{"t":8276,"quote":"It's a long, grueling race, and I can tell you what: I'm officially the first loser.","context":"Jorge Rincon jokes about finishing second","gold":5},{"t":8977,"quote":"I must say, for this one, probably never happen again. Really proud of this one.","context":"Alan Vaught reacts to his dominant Road America victory","gold":5},{"t":9000,"quote":"When I laid off a little bit, it seemed like I would start to make little mistakes.","context":"Vaught explains why he continued running near his qualifying pace","gold":4},{"t":10011,"quote":"George Rincon was just sitting there idling at the start-finish line, and his motor just blew up.","context":"The booth gets one final illustration of Road America's toll after the race","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"All 20 starters are taken from the complete pre-race grid and are corroborated by the final finishing-order readout. The broadcast consistently called the No. 221 driver 'David Feit'; this is retained as a transcript spelling for established driver David Feit. Guest analyst Greg Klein joined the booth during the race but is not included in the primary broadcaster list. The finish call explicitly states a 19-second gap between Vaught and Rincon. No full-course cautions were used at this road course.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"z1Q6w0WX6uw":{"recap":"Tim Pope set the pace through an exceptionally clean opening half at Darlington, leading the field to the scheduled lap-55 stage caution after 55 green-flag laps. The stage stop immediately scrambled the race when Pope had to brake for a still-closed pit road and Alan Vaught and Trevor Robertson stacked up behind him; Vaught then spun in traffic on the restart, while Robertson later took command as Pope fought accumulating wall damage. A string of late cautions and divergent tire calls reshuffled the order, but Pope launched back to the lead and controlled the final run. Pope won ahead of Robertson, and Josh Buettner completed an Ain't Dead Yet sweep of the podium after last-lap contact sent Jonathan Osborne spinning out of third.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Trevor Robertson","Josh Buettner"],"moments":[{"t":1337,"title":"Darlington bites on lap one - but nobody lifts","summary":"George McCone rotates nearly all the way around and Jeremiah Burke also gets crossed up in the opening traffic, yet both save their trucks and the race stays green.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3047,"title":"Fifty-five green laps at the Lady in Black","summary":"Pope reaches the scheduled halfway caution after the entire opening stage runs green, a striking display of control from a 24-truck field at Darlington.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3118,"title":"Closed pit road triggers a stage-stop stack-up","summary":"Pope checks up when pit-entry lights remain red, and Alan Vaught and Trevor Robertson pile into the queue behind the leader before anyone reaches a pit box.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3394,"title":"Vaught gets ping-ponged on cold tires","summary":"Running second just after the stage restart, Vaught gets loose in turns three and four, takes a touch at the right-rear, and spins through traffic as Ricky Whittenburg is swept into the scramble.","tags":["jess-vaught","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3932,"title":"Robertson pounces as Pope pounds the wall","summary":"Repeated Darlington stripes finally cost Pope momentum; Greg Klein, Mike Adamson, and Jonathan Osborne rush past while Trevor Robertson takes over the lead.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","greg-cline","mike-adamson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4089,"title":"McCone and Evans bring out the late yellow","summary":"George McCone and Earl Evans run out of room side by side, with McCone turned against the outside wall and the field sent to its decisive final tire stop.","tags":["earl-evans"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4437,"title":"Adamson's no-tire gamble jams the restart","summary":"Mike Adamson stays out for track position, but the fresh-tire runners swarm him; Robertson surges back to the lead as the traffic bottlenecks behind the 88.","tags":["mike-adamson","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4544,"title":"Player spins and the escape lane disappears","summary":"Andrew Player is turned after Mike Taylor moves off the wall; Dustyn Eaton and Jeremiah Burke both dive low to avoid him, only to pinball into one another and extend the wreck.","tags":["andrew-player","mike-taylor","dustin-eaton","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4838,"title":"Pope launches back to the point","summary":"Pope times the restart from the outside and clears Robertson into turns one and two, restoring an Ain't Dead Yet one-two-three at the front.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":4947,"title":"Coffin's wall bounce collects Mayberry and Burke","summary":"Andrew Coffin four-wheel-slides into the outside wall and rebounds directly into Dave Mayberry and Jeremiah Burke, with Dustyn Eaton also clipped in the heavy multi-truck crash.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5533,"title":"Podium sweep sealed in a last-turn spin","summary":"Pope takes the white flag with Robertson secure in second while Buettner attacks Osborne for third; contact sends Osborne spinning across the track and lets Buettner complete the team's podium sweep.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3303,"quote":"Now I've got a cake with a file in it - it's called a bastard file.","context":"The booth extends its running gag about rescuing absent commentator Adam Turner","gold":4},{"t":5167,"quote":"I'd rather climb somebody for second.","context":"The booth defines the old racing art of 'climbing' a rival on the last lap","gold":4},{"t":5568,"quote":"Timothy Pope comes back across the line winning this race with Trevor Robertson on his tail.","context":"The winning call as the battle for third spins behind the leaders","gold":4},{"t":6711,"quote":"This one was great. It had just the right amount of drama and contact and cautions in it.","context":"The booth sums up an unexpectedly clean Darlington night","gold":3}],"sourceLimitations":"Adam Turner was the scheduled third booth member but was absent. The transcript and post-race interviews explicitly confirm Pope as winner, Robertson second, and Buettner third. The grid contained 24 drivers; Lori Vaught served as race control and is not included as a driver.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ZAiqx96e168":{"recap":"Race 2 of VRL Season 11 brought nearly 40 trucks to a sun-baked virtual Atlanta Motor Speedway for 133 laps of pack racing. Pole sitter Jason Gaines controlled the early stages before Allen Vaught and Albert Anderson took turns at the point through a surprisingly tame middle run. The closing 40 laps became a caution-fest — nine yellows in all, capped by a turn-two Big One with 22 to go that swept up Kelly Cole, Albert Anderson, Craig Goodenough and more. From 13th on the grid, Dustyn Eaton surged forward late with pushing help from John Gallagher, who had started 40th and led in the closing laps himself. At the stripe Eaton beat Scott Rooney by 0.002 seconds — a photo finish so close the booth admitted they had no idea who won — with Gallagher third.","winner":"Dustyn Eaton","podium":["Dustyn Eaton","Scott Rooney","John Gallagher"],"moments":[{"t":1828,"title":"Lap 1: Coffin spins the field into an instant caution","summary":"Three-quarters of a lap into the race, Andrew Coffin turned down 'like there was nobody there' and spun in turns 3-4, collecting Dave Mayberry and sending Anthony Williams and Chris Klein sliding through the grass.","tags":["andrew-cauthan","dave-mayberry","chris-klein","anthony-williams"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2658,"title":"Howen hammers the fence and the pack piles in","summary":"Battling Ricky Whittenburg for 10th, Zachary Howen's 7-Eleven truck got in the fence off turn 4 on its own, then got run over by the pack — Sean McDonnell got in there and Mike Everage took a huge hit from behind.","tags":["zachary-henin","shawn-mcdonald","mike-everage","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2912,"title":"Dobson's gamble: first to worst in one lap","summary":"Greg Dobson stayed out under yellow to inherit the lead, then didn't fire off on the restart and plummeted from first to 36th in about a lap, later running 4 mph off qualifying pace with an apparent problem.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3426,"title":"Vaught takes the point from Gaines","summary":"Around lap 44 Allen Vaught completed the pass on dominant pole sitter Jason Gaines, kicking off a long stretch of the two swapping the race lead back and forth.","tags":["jess-vaught","jason-gaines"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":3721,"title":"Anderson pounces for the race lead","summary":"After stalking the leaders for 50 laps, Albert Anderson's Country Time No. 99 jumped out front, clearing Jason Gaines and Allen Vaught to lead the field.","tags":["albert-anderson","jason-gaines","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4176,"title":"Vaught's aggressive halfway block nearly backfires","summary":"Off the first green-flag stops, Allen Vaught threw a very aggressive block on Albert Anderson that almost bit him — Anderson took the lead anyway, and Jeremiah Burke was nearly 'the meat in the sandwich' between Welch and Vaught in the dog leg.","tags":["jess-vaught","albert-anderson","jeremiah-burke","derek-welch"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5075,"title":"Lap-92 Turn 4 melee sweeps the front-runners","summary":"Greg Klein caught the apron below the red line and shot up into Jeremiah Burke's No. 53, which took a big piece of the SAFER barrier; Dustyn Eaton got a piece of it while Albert Anderson just squeaked through.","tags":["greg-cline","jeremiah-burke","dustin-eaton"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":5906,"title":"The Golden Horseshoe: Anderson's second great escape","summary":"After narrowly threading through his second big wreck of the night, the booth crowned Albert Anderson with a 'Golden Horseshoe' — he restarted 17th on fresh tires with 30 to go and a real shot.","tags":["albert-anderson"],"heat":3,"kind":"funny","subkind":""},{"t":6420,"title":"The Big One in Turn 2 with 22 to go","summary":"Just as Gallagher rocketed to the lead on the restart, Kelly Cole went around off contact with Chris Klein and the melee was on — Whittenburg, Mayberry, Kyle Vaught, Albert Anderson, Craig Goodenough and John McAdam all swept up in the night's biggest wreck.","tags":["chris-klein","ricky-whittenburg","dave-mayberry","jess-vaught","albert-anderson","craig-goodenough","john-mcadam"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":7077,"title":"Gallagher leads from 40th on the grid","summary":"With 12 to go, John Gallagher — who rolled off dead last in 40th — held the race lead in the No. 123, setting up the frantic final-lap scramble.","tags":["john-gallagher"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":7390,"title":"0.002 seconds: Eaton edges Rooney at the stripe","summary":"Side by side to the white flag and all the way around the final lap, Dustyn Eaton held off Scott Rooney in a drag race off turn 4 to win by two one-thousandths of a second — so close the booth had no idea who won until the graphic came up.","tags":["dustin-eaton","scott-rooney","john-gallagher"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1471,"quote":"Paint scheme on that car looks angelic — feel like I'm looking towards the light in my near-death experience. It's very bright.","context":"Kevin Hunt's blinding-white truck rolls out for qualifying","gold":4},{"t":2385,"quote":"Unless you got Zack Millett in third who doesn't care and he's just going to push you through first.","context":"Steve derails Chris's careful 'don't push the pusher' drafting lesson","gold":3},{"t":4792,"quote":"Clean air is king — doesn't matter what kind of race car you're in, if you're out in front you got all that air on the nose of your machine.","context":"Greg Klein stuck behind leader Allen Vaught late in a run","gold":3},{"t":5325,"quote":"I don't even think you can put fuel in the roll cage to make it from here.","context":"Booth doing fuel math with 40 laps remaining","gold":3},{"t":5906,"quote":"Well, Albert Anderson with a golden horseshoe up his ass — let's see if it pays off here.","context":"Anderson threads through his second big wreck of the night untouched","gold":4},{"t":6556,"quote":"The one that you came to the dance with left early, so you either look for a new partner or just dance by yourself... trust no one.","context":"Chris on Vaught losing drafting partner Kelly Cole to the Big One","gold":4},{"t":6868,"quote":"Cautions breed cautions... everyone's checked out, they're aggression level 10, scratching and clawing for every inch of track position.","context":"Working caution number nine with 16 laps to go","gold":3},{"t":7418,"quote":"At the stripe, Eaton wins it by two one-thousandths of a second over Scott Rooney and John Gallagher — oh, what a finish! I had no idea who won!","context":"The photo-finish call at the checkered flag","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Race finished under green; margin of victory 0.002s stated on air, full finishing order read at ~2:13:12. Nine cautions total. Several proper names are best guesses from garbled auto-captions: 'Allen Vought' (heard as VA/bot/vot/fought/Vault), 'Kelly Cole' (heard as 'Kelly Co'/'Kelly cool' — could be Co/Coe), 'Zachary Howen' (results read it as 'henin'), 'Joe Canales' (canel/caneles), 'George Rencone', and co-commentator 'Chris Gon' (heard as gon/gones). Lori Vought is credited in the field but stated on air to be in an admin-only role. The pre-show montage (~13:30-14:34) appears to be highlights from a different race (Michigan is mentioned) featuring names like Tim Muska, Lockwood, Reynolds and De Merit — excluded from the driver list. Zack Millett mentioned as the usual co-host but not in the booth or field tonight. Broadcast is the Track Limits network; race streamed 2025-02-27, VRL Season 11, next round at COTA West.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"Zf-l5QoA4EA":{"recap":"Tim Pope led the Charlotte 200 from pole and spent much of the caution-free 133-lap race locked in a strategic duel with points leader Alan Vaught. The field completed repeated green-flag pit cycles without a speeding penalty, while tire conservation and a difficult Turn 4 pit entry determined who could remain in contention. Vaught lost time and acquired handling damage while avoiding Earl Evans and the spinning Russ Kilgore, then attempted to recover the race with an earlier final stop. Pope stayed out several laps longer, used his fresher final tires to set successive fastest laps, caught and passed Vaught with 11 laps left, and pulled away to win ahead of Vaught and Jim Ott.","winner":"Tim Pope","podium":["Tim Pope","Alan Vaught","Jim Ott"],"moments":[{"t":1529,"title":"Pope controls the Charlotte start","summary":"Pole-sitter Pope launches clear of Airson, while Kilgore follows into second and the 23-car field begins the 133-lap race under the lights.","tags":["timothy-pope","jason-airson","russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"start"},{"t":1923,"title":"Kilgore saves a wild Turn 4 moment","summary":"Kilgore catches the outside wall, gets sideways, and bounces through the grass, but lands the car cleanly and keeps the race green despite losing several positions.","tags":["russ-kilgore"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":"save"},{"t":2730,"title":"The first green-flag cycle begins","summary":"Pope, Vaught, Airson, and Ott stop together around lap 38; Pope narrowly wins the race off pit road and later reassumes the lead after Adamson and Welch complete their longer runs.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson","jim-ott","mike-adamson","derek-welch"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":2985,"title":"Vaught closes onto Pope's bumper","summary":"After the first pit cycle, Vaught erases Pope's advantage through traffic and reaches the leader's rear bumper as the two principal contenders begin their long strategic duel.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":4014,"title":"The leaders pit together a second time","summary":"Traffic prompts Pope to pit and Vaught, Airson, and Ott follow; Vaught gains slightly during the exchange and cycles ahead of Pope once the field sorts out.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jason-airson","jim-ott"],"heat":4,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":4434,"title":"Evans collects Kilgore without a caution","summary":"Evans bounces off the wall and loses control into Kilgore, sending the No. 7 spinning and badly damaging both cars; Evans reaches the 13-incident disqualification limit, but the race remains green.","tags":["earl-evans","russ-kilgore"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":4645,"title":"Vaught's avoidance gives Pope the lead","summary":"Vaught slows to miss Kilgore's incident, drifts into the wall, and loses roughly two seconds as Pope drives back into first; Vaught later says the contact made his car noticeably tight.","tags":["jess-vaught","russ-kilgore","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"lead_change"},{"t":5120,"title":"Vaught tries the final-stop undercut","summary":"With about 24 laps left, Vaught pits before Pope in an effort to erase the damage-induced deficit; Pope remains on track for several more laps before taking his final tires.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"moment","subkind":"strategy"},{"t":5294,"title":"Dobson crashes hard after the final cycle","summary":"Dobson loses the car exiting Turn 2, strikes the outside wall, and then hits the angled inside barrier nearly head-on, ending his competitive run without producing a caution.","tags":["greg-dobson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":"crash"},{"t":5371,"title":"Pope's fresh tires erase the undercut","summary":"Pope sets successive fastest laps after his later stop, quickly clears Ott, and cuts Vaught's advantage from more than a second to less than half a second.","tags":["timothy-pope","jim-ott","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"charge"},{"t":5507,"title":"Pope passes Vaught with 11 to go","summary":"Pope uses his fresher tires to sweep past Vaught through Turns 3 and 4, retaking the lead before steadily stretching the margin.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":5862,"title":"Pope completes a flag-to-flag strategic win","summary":"Pope takes the checkered flag about four and a half seconds ahead of Vaught, with Ott another four and a half seconds back in third; Adamson wins a final-lap fight with Burke for fifth.","tags":["timothy-pope","jess-vaught","jim-ott","mike-adamson","jeremiah-burke"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":947,"quote":"Don't let the squirrel find a nut.","context":"The booth gives its colorful key to keeping the loose Xfinity car under control","gold":5},{"t":3045,"quote":"I'm super impressed that all those guys were able to make it onto pit road without incident and without getting a black flag for speeding.","context":"The booth praises the field after the first green-flag stop cycle","gold":4},{"t":6183,"quote":"I was down around 60 percent on two of the long green-flag stops, and I just didn't have the rotation.","context":"Third-place Jim Ott explains how hard he used the right-front tire","gold":4},{"t":6268,"quote":"Tim, he's class of the field almost on most weeks, and I was just happy and excited that I was there.","context":"Runner-up Alan Vaught reflects on challenging Pope","gold":5},{"t":6610,"quote":"Put the hammer down those last few laps. I tried to run him back down and was able to catch him there.","context":"Winner Tim Pope describes his final-tire charge","gold":5},{"t":6644,"quote":"I was going to go at 15, but since he pitted earlier, I decided to pit a few laps earlier.","context":"Pope explains how Vaught's undercut adjusted his planned stop","gold":4},{"t":6745,"quote":"That cat's an alien.","context":"The booth marvels at Pope's ability to learn tracks and win","gold":5},{"t":6758,"quote":"Once we took that green, it stayed green the entire way, all 133 laps.","context":"The broadcast sums up the caution-free race","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Season 3, Round 6 at Charlotte Motor Speedway according to seasons_map.json. The Charlotte 200 ran 133 laps and 200 miles in Xfinity cars with 70% fuel, four total tire sets, one fast repair, and disqualification at 13 incident points. The broadcast explicitly confirms the Pope-Vaught-Ott podium, reads the complete 23-driver starting grid, and later gives the complete finishing order. The race ran caution-free from green to checkered even though the Evans-Kilgore and Dobson crashes were substantial. Jonathan Osborne earned hard charger by advancing from 20th to ninth. Canonical roster spellings are used for Jason Airson, David Feit, Tony Polk, Alan Vaught, and Russ Endicott despite frequent caption variants. All timestamps fall within the 7,304-second metadata duration.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ZGhpUqhmw54":{"recap":"Larry Dickerson drove from 16th on the grid to win the Championship Round at virtual Phoenix Raceway, claiming both the race and the VRL title aboard his #69 'Screaming Eagle' truck. Polesitter Tim Pope dominated the opening 50 laps until mysterious nose damage picked up during the first caution sent him tumbling as deep as 22nd, and Craig Goodenough took command through the midsection. The title fight flipped with 18 laps to go when championship leader Dillon Bryant got loose off Turn 2, hit the wall and triggered a multi-truck melee in the dogleg that collected John Curtis and Kelly Kuehl, leaving Bryant 19th. From there Dickerson controlled a string of late restarts, holding off Goodenough and a hard-charging Pope — who completed a 'miraculous comeback' to third — for the win and the championship. Five cautions slowed the 150-lap, Veterans Day-themed event, which opened with a silent pace lap in tribute.","winner":"Larry Dickerson","podium":["Larry Dickerson","Craig Goodenough","Tim Pope"],"moments":[{"t":1770,"title":"Silent lap for Veterans Day","summary":"Before the green, the field runs an extra pace lap in complete silence to honor Veterans Day, with tribute paint schemes across the grid.","tags":[],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3250,"title":"Vaught steals the lead on pit road","summary":"Alan Vaught's 14.28-second stop and quicker pit lane time beat Tim Pope's 14.78, cycling the #33 into the race lead during green-flag stops.","tags":["jess-vaught","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":""},{"t":3594,"title":"Mystery nose damage derails Pope","summary":"Dominant polesitter Tim Pope comes to the restart with front-end damage picked up under yellow and starts sliding backward through the field.","tags":["timothy-pope"],"heat":4,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":3669,"title":"Rooney slams the Turn 2 wall","summary":"Scott Rooney gets loose, overcorrects, tank-slaps and pounds the wall hard off Turn 2 — and the race somehow stays green.","tags":["scott-rooney"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3713,"title":"Goodenough takes command through the dogleg","summary":"Craig Goodenough sets up Alan Vaught into Turn 3, shortcuts the dogleg perfectly and drives off with the lead he would hold for the race's midsection.","tags":["craig-goodenough","jess-vaught"],"heat":3,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":4410,"title":"Marof's engine lets go, Osborne has nowhere to go","summary":"Darby Marof's engine expires and leaves him crawling on the bottom; Jonathan Osborne never sees him in time and plows in, ending the #81's night.","tags":["darby-maroth","jonathan-osborne"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4654,"title":"Burke's restart free-fall","summary":"Race leader Jeremiah Burke inexplicably falls off the pace on the restart and sheds positions four-wide; even on replay the booth can't find a violation.","tags":["jeremiah-burke"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":5726,"title":"Caution traps the leader mid-pit-cycle","summary":"Goodenough finally commits to his last stop with 25 to go and the yellow flies moments later, handing early-stopper Trevor Robertson the lead and reshuffling the title fight.","tags":["craig-goodenough","trevor-robertson","timothy-pope"],"heat":3,"kind":"drama","subkind":""},{"t":6106,"title":"Melee in the dogleg — Bryant's title bid ends","summary":"Championship leader Dillon Bryant gets loose off Turn 2, tags the wall, bounces off Goodenough and turns perpendicular in the dogleg, collecting John Curtis and Kelly Kuehl while barely missing teammate Larry Dickerson.","tags":["dylan-bryant","craig-goodenough","john-curtis","kelly-keel","larry-dickerson"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":6476,"title":"Pope storms back into the top three","summary":"With nine to go, a wounded Tim Pope drives under Trevor Robertson into Turn 3 to complete his climb from 22nd back into podium contention.","tags":["timothy-pope","trevor-robertson"],"heat":4,"kind":"pass","subkind":""},{"t":6800,"title":"Three to go: Pope shoves Dickerson at the restart","summary":"On the final restart Pope launches into the back of Dickerson coming to the stripe, then wages a side-by-side war with Goodenough for second as Dickerson escapes.","tags":["larry-dickerson","timothy-pope","craig-goodenough"],"heat":4,"kind":"restart","subkind":""},{"t":6877,"title":"Dickerson wins the race and the championship","summary":"Larry Dickerson holds off Goodenough's last deep dive into Turn 3 and takes the checkered flag for the win and the VRL title, with Pope completing a miraculous comeback in third.","tags":["larry-dickerson","craig-goodenough","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":1517,"quote":"'Your belly's ready'? Am I reading that right? I already ate dinner so I'm good, but hello back.","context":"greeting a chatter's garbled username during qualifying","gold":3},{"t":3526,"quote":"Usually I'm pretty good about that, but... pretty well medicated right now, so let's see what's going on here.","context":"chat asks why the caution flew and the booth confesses","gold":3},{"t":5092,"quote":"Still with the race lead — he's more than good enough right now.","context":"punning on race leader Craig Goodenough's name","gold":4},{"t":5379,"quote":"It's kind of like playing poker — you got to know when to hold 'em and when to fold 'em.","context":"on Goodenough timing his final pit stop","gold":3},{"t":6401,"quote":"Race car spelled backwards is still race car, but race car upside down is expensive.","context":"reading a chatter's joke under a late caution","gold":4},{"t":6766,"quote":"You put him within a truck length of a championship, no matter what he's driving, he's got a shot.","context":"on battered Tim Pope before the final restart","gold":4},{"t":6899,"quote":"Checkered flag waves — Dickerson wins the race and the title!","context":"the championship-winning call at the line","gold":5}],"sourceLimitations":"Solo broadcaster identifies himself only as 'Steve' with HBR TV (captions render it 'hbr TV'/'hbtv'/'hbrr TV'; channel metadata says 'tln'). Several surnames are best guesses from garbled captions: 'Alan Vaught' and 'Kyle Vaught' (captions: vot/bot/VA/fought/Thon), 'George Rencone' (Ren con/ranone/rayone), 'Kelly Kuehl' (Kelly Co), 'David Feight' (pronounced 'fight' per race control correction), 'Darby Marof' (Maro/Marth/Maria). Captions sometimes call Craig Goodenough 'Greg'. Jason Gaines' truck number is captioned both 83 and 93. Lori V served as race control (credited 33rd, not officially classified); Albert Anderson skipped the race to travel and did not compete. 'Justin Eaton' in the caption of the final results is Dustyn Eaton. The booth's 'seven of Justin elire' reference is real-world Xfinity champion Justin Allgaier, not a league driver. Full top-five per results read: Dickerson, Goodenough, Pope, Whittenburg, Gallagher.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"},"ZMVC4gqvlWA":{"recap":"Trevor Robertson charged from 25th to win Season 5's Charlotte round after a race shaped by tire conservation, stage strategy, and several restart incidents. J.R. Hollingsworth won the midpoint stage and remained a contender through the final run, while a late caution for contact between Albert Anderson and Timmy Bates produced a 20-lap shootout on mixed tire ages. Hollingsworth led late, but contact with Robertson during the closing battle cost him two positions and put Robertson ahead for the white flag. Tim Pope chased Robertson to the line but finished second, with Hollingsworth recovering for third.","winner":"Trevor Robertson","podium":["Trevor Robertson","Tim Pope","J.R. Hollingsworth"],"moments":[{"t":1114,"title":"Klein takes a surprise pole","summary":"Greg Klein earns the pole, one of his best qualifying efforts, with Tim Pope alongside for the start.","tags":["greg-cline","timothy-pope"],"heat":2,"kind":"moment","subkind":"qualifying"},{"t":2132,"title":"Osborne and McDonnell spin to the grass","summary":"John Osborne and Sean McDonnell make contact while fighting for position; McDonnell spins through the infield but blends back into traffic without a caution.","tags":["jonathan-osborne","shawn-mcdonald"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":2324,"title":"Cold tires send Wade into the wall","summary":"Dustin Wade loses the rear on cold tires exiting Turn 4 and hits the outside wall hard, drawing the first incident caution during green-flag pit stops.","tags":["dustin-wade"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3135,"title":"Hollingsworth wins the stage","summary":"J.R. Hollingsworth takes the competition-caution stage over Tim Pope and Greg Klein, with Alan Vaught and Mike Adamson completing the top five.","tags":["j-r-hollingsworth","timothy-pope","greg-cline","jess-vaught","mike-adamson"],"heat":3,"kind":"moment","subkind":"stage"},{"t":3528,"title":"Restart stack-up destroys Robertson's charge","summary":"A checkup at the stage restart turns Alan Vaught into Trevor Robertson and spins Jonah Long as well, forcing Robertson to recover again after he had climbed roughly 20 positions.","tags":["jess-vaught","trevor-robertson","jonah-long","ricky-whittenburg"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":3997,"title":"Bittner and Endicott collide","summary":"Josh Bittner turns across Russ Endicott, who is launched into a violent impact and comes to a sudden stop near the pit-road barrier, prompting another caution.","tags":["josh-bittner","russ-endicott"],"heat":5,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4606,"title":"Bates spins after Anderson contact","summary":"Albert Anderson carries momentum under Timmy Bates in the tri-oval; Bates comes down across Anderson's nose and spins through the infield, creating the late caution everyone had anticipated.","tags":["albert-anderson","timmy-bates"],"heat":4,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""},{"t":4992,"title":"Robertson leans on Hollingsworth for the lead","summary":"With three laps left, Robertson and Hollingsworth make contact side by side; Hollingsworth saves the truck but drops behind both Robertson and Pope.","tags":["trevor-robertson","j-r-hollingsworth","timothy-pope"],"heat":5,"kind":"pass","subkind":"battle"},{"t":5016,"title":"Robertson completes the comeback","summary":"Trevor Robertson holds a three-tenths advantage through the final lap and wins after starting 25th, with Tim Pope second by a narrow margin and J.R. Hollingsworth third.","tags":["trevor-robertson","timothy-pope","j-r-hollingsworth"],"heat":5,"kind":"finish","subkind":""},{"t":5039,"title":"Rincon and Bittner tangle at the finish","summary":"Behind the leaders, Josh Bittner gets into Jorge Rincon during the run to the checkered flag, capping the race with one last incident.","tags":["george-rincon","josh-bittner"],"heat":3,"kind":"wreck","subkind":""}],"soundbytes":[{"t":3415,"quote":"I'm just planning on staying close enough to this front group while I save tires, and trying to out-pit and just out-long-run everybody else.","context":"Trevor Robertson explains his plan during the stage caution","gold":4},{"t":3582,"quote":"Vaught goes for the tumble spin in the dryer.","context":"The booth describes Alan Vaught's stage-restart crash","gold":3},{"t":4038,"quote":"He stuck the landing. I give it a 10.","context":"The booth reacts to Russ Endicott's violent airborne crash","gold":4},{"t":4932,"quote":"Getting spicy, boys. It's almost over with here.","context":"The booth watches Robertson and Hollingsworth fight for the win","gold":3},{"t":6304,"quote":"I ran hard but tried to save tires at the same time, if that makes any sense. I just had the speed at the end.","context":"Trevor Robertson explains his recovery and winning pace","gold":4}],"sourceLimitations":"The podium and winner are explicit in the finish call and post-race rundown. The field is reconstructed from the full starting-grid readout and contained 30 trucks. The transcript alternates Mike/Michael Adamson; the roster contains a canonical Mike Adamson entry, which is used here. The start-list caption describes Albert Anderson as having an 'AOL'; context indicates an end-of-line penalty, not a separate entrant.","resultConfidence":"reported-on-tape"}};
